hadiths[2600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4403","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abdullah bin Abi Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, his name is: Abdullah bin Uthman bin Aamir bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Sa’d bin Taym bin Murrah bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fihr"
"4404","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh al-Madaini told us, Shababah told us, Salih bin Musa al-Talhi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Ishaq, On the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is pleased with If he looks at a person from the fire, let him look at Abu Bakr, and his name, as his family gave him: is Abdullah bin Uthman bin Amir bin Amr. Where he was born, the name Atiq prevailed over him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4404 - Saleh is weak and the chain of transmission is dark"
"4405","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Wasil Al-Mutawa’i told me about Bikind. My father told me, Muhammad bin Ismail told me, Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, we told him. Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli heard Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Abdi speaking, on the authority of Harun bin Saad, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya, he heard Ali “swearing that God Almighty had sent down the name of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, from heaven as a truthful one” had it not been for the place of Muhammad ibn Sulaiman. Al-Sa’idi, out of ignorance, would have ruled this chain of narration to be authentic, “and it has a witness from the hadith of Al-Nazzal bin Sabra, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4405 - If it were not for the ignorance of Muhammad bin Suleiman Al-Saeedi, the sheikh of Ishaq Al-Saluli, I would have ruled it authentic."
"4406","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqi told us, my father told me, Ishaq bin Yusuf told us, Abu Sinan told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, Al-Nazzal bin Sabra told us: We agreed with Ali, may God be pleased with him, who had a good soul, and he was joking, so we said: Tell us about your companions. He said: All The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, are my Companions, so we said: He told us on the authority of Abu Bakr, and he said: “That is a man whom God called a truthful one on the authority of Gabriel and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4406 - Hilal bin Al-Alaa Munkar Al-Hadith"
"4407","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told me, Muhammad bin Katheer Al-San’ani told us, Muammar bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was taken on a journey to Al-Aqsa Mosque, he began talking People did so, and some people apostatized. Those who had believed in him and believed him, and they heard about this to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and they said: Do you have the right to Your friend claims that he was taken on a journey to Jerusalem tonight. He said: Or did he say that? They said: Yes. He said: If he had said that, then he would have told the truth. They said: Or do you believe him that he went to the Holy House tonight and came before In the morning? He said: Yes, I believe him in what is beyond that. I believe him in the news of heaven in the morning or in the morning. That is why he was called Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4407 - True"
"4408","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdul Hamid told me, Muhammad bin Zakaria told me, Ibn Aisha told me, my father told me, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: “Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, was the minister of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He used to consult him in all his affairs, and he was a second time in Islam, and he was a second time in Al-Ghar, and he was a second time in Al-Arish on the day of Badr, and he was a second time In the grave, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not introduce anyone to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4408 - Its narrators are unknown"
"4409","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Abu Ayyub Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Muqri told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Waqidi, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Akhi Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “He died Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, on Tuesday night, the eighth of Jumada al-Awwal, thirteen years old, and he was sixty-three years old at that time. He was sick for fifteen days, and the reason for his illness was that he bathed on a cold day, so he had a fever for fifteen nights and did not go out to pray. Omar, may God be pleased with him, used to lead the people in prayer while he was in his house that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had reserved for him, and he came to Uthman’s house today. He recommended that Asma bint Umays wash him, his wife. She was weak, so she sought the help of Abd al-Rahman, and he was shrouded in two garments, one of which should be washed. It is said: In three garments, he was carried on the bed of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, which was the bed of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on which she used to sleep. Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was carried to him, and Omar prayed over him in the mosque between the grave and the pulpit, and he was buried in the house with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him at night, and his head was placed between the shoulders of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4409 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4410","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Abu Ubaid Al-Qasim bin Ismail narrated to us, Ubaid Allah bin Saad narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, Saif bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, said: “The reason for Abu Bakr’s death was the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and is still His body ran until he died.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4410 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4411","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Abdullah bin Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath told me, Abdul-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth told me, my father told me, on the authority of My grandfather, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, “One day a man gave as a gift to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, a sheet of khazirah, and with him was a man who was said to have Al-Harith Ibn Kalada has it, and he has knowledge. When they ate from it, Ibn Kalada said: It contains the poison of the Sunnah, but by the One in whose hand my soul is, not a year has passed. Until they died on one day, the New Year.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4411 - It is mursal"
"4412","So Abu Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me, about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, al-Sari bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi said: “What can be expected from this worldly world, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was poisoned, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was poisoned, and he was killed.” Omar bin Al-Khattab was killed, Othman and Ali were killed, Al-Hasan was poisoned, and Al-Hussein was killed.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4412 - The secret is abandoned"
"4413","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid al-Hafiz narrated to me in Hamdan, Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Amr bin Ziyad told us, Ghalib bin Abdullah told us. Al-Qarfasani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Habib bin Abi Habib, said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to Hassan bin Thabit: “I said in Did Abu Bakr do anything? He said: Yes. He said: “Speak until I hear.” He said: I said:
 [Simple Sea]
 And the second of the two was in the cavernous cave, and... the enemy surrounded it as it ascended the mountain.
 And the love of the Messenger of God, they knew... of the creatures, he did not make any substitute for it.
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4413 - Amr bin Ziyad fabricates the hadith"
"4414","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Jawhari told us, in Baghdad, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Al-Khalil bin Zakaria told us, Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked about Ibn Abbas, or was he asked who was the first to convert to Islam? He said: “Did you not hear Hassan, may God be pleased with him, say:
 [Simple Sea]
 If you remember an insult from a trustworthy brother...then remind your brother Abu Bakr of what they did.
 The best of mankind is the one who is most pious and just... after the Prophet, and he fulfills what they are burdened with.
 “The second, the next, the one whose scene is praiseworthy...and the first of the people among them to believe the Messengers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4414 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4415","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Al-Humaidi told me, Sufyan told me, Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, asked me: How much did you shroud the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? So I said: “In three garments.” He said: “In them they shrouded me.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4415 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4416","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told me, Abdul-Rahman bin Salih Al-Azdi told us, Abdul Rahim told us Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who told him that Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, when When he was about to die, he said: How much did you shroud the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? So I said: “In three new Yemeni white dresses, without a shirt or turban.” He said: “Wash this dress of mine, and in it is a deterrent of saffron.” And a hardship, so make it with two new garments.” So I said: It is a creation, and he said: “The living has more right to the new than the dead. Indeed, it is a period of respite.” Abd al-Rahim said: Hisham bin Urwa told me, he said: Othman bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Urwa, “that Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, prayed over him in The mosque, and was buried at night next to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the room of Aisha, may God be pleased with her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4416 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4417","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi Al-Maamari told me, Ja’far bin Musafir told me, Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Abi Nu’aym, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, ruled for two years and seven months in his caliphate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4417 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4418","The distinguished ruler Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, dictating, Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darstawayh told me Al-Farisi, Yaqoub bin Sufyan told us, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told us, Muhammad bin Muhajir told us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the first time he was sent, and he was In Mecca, and he was at that time disdainful, I said: What are you? He said: “I am a prophet.” I said: What is a prophet? He said: “Messenger of God.” I said: God sent you? He said: “Yes.” I said: What did he send you on? He said: “To worship God, to break idols, and to uphold ties of kinship.” I said: “Yes, what He sent you with, so who followed you in this?” He said: “Slave and free,” meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. Amr used to say: You saw me when I was a quarter of Islam. He said: So I converted to Islam and said: Do I follow you, O Messenger of God? He said: “No, but follow your people. When you are informed that I have left, follow me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And he continued Abu Salam, for his narration, included Damra bin Habib, Abu Talha al-Rasibi, and Shaddad bin Abdullah Abu Ammar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4418 - True"
"4419","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: And he told me Muawiyah bin Salih, Abu Yahya, Damra bin Habib, and Abu Talha told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, who said: Amr bin Absa told me May God be pleased with him. He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was staying in Ukaz. I said: O Messenger of God, who followed you in this matter? He said: “Two men, Free and Abd, followed me against him, Abu Bakr and Bilal.” He said: So I converted to Islam at that time. As for the hadith of Abu Ammar"
"4420","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Shaddad told us Ibn Abdullah Abu Ammar, who had met a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Abu Umamah said: O Amr ibn She frowned. How can you claim that you are a quarter of Islam? He mentioned the hadith in its length"
"4421","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Abu Bakr was our master, the best of us, and he loved us.” To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It is true according to their condition, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4421 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4422","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Bayhaqi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, said: Ibrahim bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf told me that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf was With Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and that Muhammad bin Maslama broke Al-Zubayr’s sword, then Abu Bakr got up and addressed the people and apologized to them, He said: By God, I was never keen on the leadership day or night, nor was I desirous of it, nor did I ask God Almighty for it, secretly or publicly. But I am afraid of the temptation, and I have no comfort in the emirate, but I have undertaken a great matter for which I have no strength and no ability except through the strengthening of God. Glory be to Him, I wish that the people who were most powerful for it were in my place today, so the Muhajireen accepted from him what he said and what he apologized for. Ali, may God be pleased with him, said On the authority of him and Al-Zubayr: We were only angry because we were delayed from consultation, and we see Abu Bakr as the most deserving of people after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Indeed, he is the owner of the cave, and the second of two, and we know of his honor and pride. “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so.” “By praying with the people while he was alive.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4422 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4423","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Buhturi Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Husayn bin Ali Al-Ja’fi told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, the Ansar said: From us. A prince, and among you is a prince. He said: Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, came to them and said: O community of Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He has commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer,” so which of you would be willing to precede Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him? The Ansar said: We seek refuge in God lest we advance Abu Bakr. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4423 - True"
"4424","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Muhammad bin Abi told us Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “They beat the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Until he fainted, then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, stood up and started calling out and saying: Woe to you! Will you kill a man who says, “My Lord is God?” They said: Who is this? They said: This is Ibn Abi Quhafa, the insane. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4424 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4425","Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Sa’id bin Ufayr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Malik al-Madliji, who is the nephew of Suraqa bin Jasham, that his father told him that he heard Suraqa bin Jasham says: “The messengers of the infidels of Quraysh came to us, making blood money for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and for whoever killed them in every This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4425 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4426","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Many, on the authority of Qais Al-Harithi, who said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, preceded him, and Abu Bakr seconded him, and a third Omar, then a trial befell us, and God pardons whomsoever He wills.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4426 - True"
"4427","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha'arani informed us, Yusuf ibn Adiy and Nu`aym ibn Hammad told us, they said: Abd told us God Ibn Al-Mubarak, Omar Ibn Saeed Ibn Abi Husayn Al-Qurashi informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them he says: When Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was laid on his bed, and people surrounded him, praying for him, and I was among them, then Ali bin Abi came A student, may God be pleased with him, said: I had thought that God Almighty would place you with your two companions, and that is because I often listened to the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Abu Bakr and Omar and I went, and Abu Bakr and Omar and I entered, and Abu Bakr and Omar and I went out.” And I thought that God would place you with them. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4427 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4428","Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Adl Al-Saidalani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Saeed bin Maslamah Al-Qurashi told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and one of the His hands were on Abu Bakr, and the other was on Omar, and he said: “This is how we will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4428 - Saeed bin Maslama Al-Qurashi is weak"
"4429","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqiqi told us, about Hamdan, Umair bin Madaris told us, Abdullah bin Nafi’ Al-Sayegh told us, Asim bin Omar told us, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The first from whom the earth will split, I will be.” Then Abu Bakr, then Omar, then I will come to the people of Al-Baqi’ and they will split from them, and I will disperse among them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4429 - Asim bin Omar is the brother of Abdullah Dhafouh"
"4430","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to me, Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti narrated to me, Abu Nu’aym and Khallad bin Yahya narrated to us, they said: Mas’ar narrated to us, on the authority of my father Awn Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me and to Abu Bakr: “With one of you Gabriel, and with the other Michael, and Israfil, a great king who witnesses the fight and is in the ranks. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4430 - True"
"4431","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Uthma told us, Musa bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Huwayrith told me that Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mutim told him that he heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, addressing the people, and he said: “While I I was experiencing the heart of a full moon when a strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen, then it went away, then a strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen, except... The one that was before it, then it went away, then a strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen, except the one that was before it, so it was the first wind. Gabriel descended with a thousand angels with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the second wind was Michael descending with a thousand angels from The right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr was on his right, and the third wind was Israfil, who descended with a thousand angels on the The easy way of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. While I was in the easy way, when God Almighty defeated His enemies, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, carried me on His horse galloped past me and I fell on my heel, so I called upon God Almighty and He held me back. When I sat on top of it, I stabbed the people with this hand until I “This man was stained with blood.” He pointed to his armpit. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4431 - Rather, it is a strange reprehensible act"
"4432","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Hafiz told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas Al-Asqalani told me, Muhammad told me Ibn Ismail Ibn Abi Fudaik Al-Madani, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Abdullah Ibn Atiya Al-Saadi, on the authority of Abd Al-Aziz Ibn Al-Muttalib Ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah ibn Hantab, said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked at Abu Bakr. Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “These are hearing and sight.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4432 - Hassan"
"4433","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Musa bin Umair told us, he said: I heard Makhoul says: A man asked him about the saying of God Almighty: {For God is his master, and Gabriel, and the righteous of the believers} [Al-Tahrim: 4] He said: Tell me Abu Umamah, as he said: “Allah is his master, and Gabriel, and the righteous of the believers are Abu Bakr and Omar.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4433 - Musa bin Umair Wah"
"4434","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, and Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jawhari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Fudayl bin Marzuq Al-Rawasi told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Yatha’, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you befriend Abu Bakr, you will find him ascetic in this world. Desiring the Hereafter, and if you take care of Omar, you will find him strong and trustworthy. Do not take the blame of a blamer from God Almighty, and if you take care of Ali, you will find that he is a guide. “A Mahdi will lead you on the path.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman witnessed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4434 - Weak"
"4435","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir bin Shazan told us, Sharik bin Abd told us. By God, on the authority of Uthman bin Umair, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: They said: O Messenger of God, if only you would remain in power over us? He said: “If he appoints a caliph over you and you disobey him, torment will be inflicted upon you.” They said: “If you had appointed Abu Bakr over us,” he said: “If “Shall I appoint him as your successor over you? You will find him strong in the command of God but weak in his body.” They said: “If you had appointed Omar as your successor over us.” He said: “If I should appoint him as your successor over you.” You will find him strong and trustworthy. The blame of a scoundrel does not take him in God. They said: If you had appointed Ali as your successor over us, he said: “You will not do it, and if you do “You will find him a guide, a Mahdi, who will follow you on the straight path.” “Uthman bin Umair, this is Abu Al-Yaqzan.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4435 - Othman Abu Al-Yaqzan is weak"
"4436","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghdadi informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Alaf informed us, in Egypt, Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, Sufyan informed us Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And consult them in the matter} [Al Imran: 159], He said: “Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4436 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4437","Abu Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told me, Ash’ath bin Abd al-Malik al-Hamrani, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who among you has seen a vision?” Then a man said: I saw as if a scale had descended from the sky, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abu Bakr, and Omar and Abu were weighed. Bakr, and Abu Bakr preferred, and Omar and Uthman were weighed, and Omar preferred, then the scales were lifted, and we saw hatred in the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He stated, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” This was witnessed by the hadith of Sa’id bin Juman, on the authority of the ship that
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4437 - Ash’ath bin Abdul Malik, this is trustworthy, but what he used as evidence"
"4438","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jumhan, on the authority of Safina, the slave of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, then he went to His companions said: “Which of you saw a vision tonight?” He said: One day he prayed and said: “Which of you has seen a vision?” Then a man said: I saw, O Messenger of God, as if a scale had been lowered from the sky, and you were placed on one side of the scale, and Abu Bakr was placed on the other side. So I swung at Abu Bakr, so I got up and Abu Bakr left his place, so Omar Ibn Al-Khattab was brought and placed on the other side, so Abu swayed him. Bakr, so Abu Bakr was removed, and Othman was brought and placed on the other side, so Omar gave the upper hand to Othman, then Omar and Othman were raised and the scale was raised. He said: Then the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed, and then he said: “The succession of the Prophethood is thirty years, and then you will be king.” Saeed bin Jumhan said: Safina said to me: “Keep the two years of Abu Bakr, ten of Omar, twelve of Uthman, and six of Ali, may God be pleased with them all.” These narrations were attributed with an authentic chain of transmission traced back to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4438 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4439","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Musa bin Harun Al-Bardi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Harb, Al-Zubaidi told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amr Ibn Aban Ibn Uthman Ibn Affan, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with him On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tonight I see a righteous man. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, consorted with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and Omar was called to Abu Bakr and Othman was called to Omar.” Jabir said: “When we rose from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, we said: The righteous man.” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and as for what was mentioned about their rank to one another, they are the rulers of this matter with which God sent His Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4439 - True"
"4440","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Balawayh told me - from the origin of his book - Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Mu’in told us, Hushaym told us, On the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Sulayman bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “The caliphate is in Medina and the kingdom is in the Levant.” It is true.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4440 - Suleiman bin Abi Suleiman and his father are unknown"
"4441","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Al-Mukhtar bin Nafi’ told us, Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God have mercy on Abu Bakr. “He gave me his daughter in marriage, and took me to the Hijrah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4441 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4442","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Saqr told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Maan bin Issa told us, Ubaid Allah told us Ibn Omar Ibn Hafs, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered in the year of the conquest, he saw women He smeared the horses’ faces with wine, so he smiled at Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and said: “O Abu Bakr, what did Hassan bin Thabit say?” Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, recited it:
 [abundant sea]
 My structure is useless if you don't see it... it makes my shoulders tingle like a pain
 They make haste with the helpless...the women smear them with wine,
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Enter from where Hassan said.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4442 - True"
"4443","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani and Abu Sa`id al-Thaqafi told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hadrami told us, Dirar bin Surad told us, a partner told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ubaida Al-Salmani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you,” so Abu Bakr came out. He greeted him and then sat down. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4443 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4444","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Muslim Imran bin Maysara told us, Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Salam bin Harb, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Dalani, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Gabriel took me by the hand.” So he showed me the gate of Paradise through which my nation will enter. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, I wish I were with you so that I could see it. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Are you not the first of my nation to enter it?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4444 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4445","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, who said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: When Khadija, may God be pleased with her, died, Khawla bint Hakim came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Won’t you get married? He said: “Who?” She said: If you want a virgin, and if you want a married man, he said: “And who is the virgin?” And who is the clothes? She said: As for the virgin: she is the daughter of the most beloved of God’s creation to you, Aisha bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and as for the married woman, Sawda bint Zam’a. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4445 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4446","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, narrated to us in a whisper, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq He said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: Which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “Abu Bakr, then Omar, then Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4446 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4447","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik told us, Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Arwa Al-Dawsi, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, appeared, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to them.” “For God who supported me through you” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4447 - Asim bin Omar Wah"
"4448","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hafs bin Omar told us, Mas’ar bin Kadam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Rab’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “I intended to send men to the horizons who would teach people the Sunnahs and duties, just as Jesus, son of Mary, sent the disciples.” He was told: So where? Are you from Abu Bakr and Omar? He said: “I am indispensable to them, for they are part of religion like hearing and sight.” This is a hadith narrated alone by Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni, on the authority of Mas’ar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4448 - Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni narrated it alone on the authority of Mas’ar, but it is weak."
"4449","Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Talhi told me, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Munjab bin al-Harith told me, Husayn told us Ibn Omar Al-Ahmasi, narrated by Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, who said: When it was revealed to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {Indeed, those They lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of God. These are those whose hearts God has tested for piety.} [Al-Hujurat: 3] Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: “So I vowed to myself that I would not speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except as a secret brother.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4449 - Husayn bin Omar Wah"
"4450","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail. Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, how is reconciliation after This verse: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it} [An-Nisa: 123] So for every evil that we have done, We will recompense for it. He said: “May God forgive you, O Abu Bakr,” he said. Three times: “O Abu Bakr, aren’t you sick, aren’t you sad, aren’t you camping, aren’t you afflicted by calamities?” I said: Yes, he said: “It is what you will be rewarded for in this world.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4450 - True"
"4451","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani, and Abu Muhammad Abd told us. Allah bin Ishaq Al-Baghawi, in Baghdad, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi in Marw. They said: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Al-Harith Al-Wasiti, Abu Ismail Hafs bin Omar Al-Ayli told us, Mas’ar bin Kadam told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Follow the example of those after me, my father.” Bakr and Omar, and they were guided by the guidance of Ammar, and they adhered to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4451 - True"
"4452","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar and Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq, Al-Adl, in Baghdad, told us: Thana Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Suyuti, Yahya bin Abdul-Hamid told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, and Mas’ar bin Kadam, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Imitate those who After me, Abu Bakr and Omar, and they followed the guidance of Ammar, and adhered to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd.”"
"4453","Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Abdullah told me, Muhammad bin Abdoos bin Kamil told me, Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, Waki’ told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Abd. Al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Imitate those who After me, Abu Bakr and Omar, and follow the guidance of Ammar, and when Ibn Umm Abd tells you, believe him.”"
"4454","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Hilal, the client of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Follow those after me, Abu Bakr and Omar.”"
"4455","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Hamdoun bin Khalid told us, Ali bin Othman Al-Nufaili told us, Ishaq bin Issa bin Al-Tabbaa’, Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Imitate those after me, Abu Bakr and Omar, and follow the guidance of Ammar, and adhere to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd” this “hadith for the sake of what was narrated in the virtues of the two Sheikhs, and he established this chain of narration, on the authority of Al-Thawri and Mas’ar Yahya Al-Hammani and also established it, on the authority of Mas’ar and Waki’, and Hafs bin Omar Al-Aili, then he fell short in his narration, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah Al-Humaydi and others. He established the chain of narration, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, Ishaq bin Isa bin Al-Tabba’, so the authenticity of this hadith was proven by what we mentioned, even if they did not narrate it, and they We found witness to it with an authentic chain of transmission, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud.”"
"4456","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Yahya bin Salamah bin told us. Kuhayl, my father told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Follow the example of those after me, Abu Bakr and Omar, and be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and adhere to the covenant of Ibn Masoud.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4456 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4457","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Wahib told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, the preachers of the Ansar rose Then the man from among them started saying: O community of immigrants, whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, employed a man from among you, he would pair with him a man from among us. We think that this matter will be followed by two men, one of you and the other of us. He said: Then the Ansar’s preachers continued on this matter, so Zayd ibn Thabit, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one of the immigrants, and the Imam will be one of the immigrants, and we are his supporters as we were. Supporters of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, stood up and said: “May God reward you with goodness, O community of Ansar,” and he remained steadfast. Your speaker.” Then he said: “If you had done otherwise, we would not have made peace with you.” Then Zayd ibn Thabit took Abu Bakr by the hand and said: This Your friend, so they pledged allegiance to him, then they set off. When Abu Bakr sat on the pulpit, he looked at the faces of the people and did not see Ali, so he asked about him, and he said: People from The Ansar brought him, and Abu Bakr said: The cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he circumcised him. Did you want to sever the disobedience of the Muslims? He said: No Thathrib, O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he pledged allegiance to him. Then he did not see Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, so he asked about him until they brought him. He said: The cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his disciples, you wanted to tear apart the Muslims’ disobedience, so he said something like his saying: No, O Thareb. The successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he pledged allegiance to him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4457 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4458","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak Al-Zahid told us, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Balawi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-San’ani told us, Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was taken to the mosque. Al-Aqsa started talking about that, and some people who had believed in him and believed him apostatized, and some polytheists sought out Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. God bless him, so they said: Do you have a message to your friend who claims that he was taken on a journey to the Holy House that night? He said: Did he say that? They said: Yes. He said: If he said that, then he would have told the truth. They said: Or do you believe him that he went to the Holy House tonight and came before In the morning? He said: Yes, I believe him in what is beyond that. I believe him in the news of the sky in the morning or in the evening. That is why he was named Abu Bakr. Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” “For Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Sana’ani is truthful.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4458 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4459","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, said: Bilal called the noon prayer, and the shouting came before the Banu Amr bin Awf, for it had occurred among them. So evil that they threw stones at each other, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them and said: “O Abu Bakr, if the prayer is established, then come forward and join the people.” He said: Yes, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. This is how they only agreed on that during the illness of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who ""He died in it""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4459 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4460","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Abi Uthman al-Tayalisi told us, Nasr bin Mansour told us Al-Marwazi, Bishr bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Banu Al-Mustaliq sent me to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to whom shall we give our alms after you? He said: So I came to him and asked him, and he said: “To Abu Bakr.” So I came to them and informed them, and they said: Go back to him and ask him. If he told Abu Bakr, A new virgin, to whom? So I came to him and asked him, and he said: “To Omar.” So I came to them and informed them, and they said: Go back to him and ask him. If it happened to Omar, then to Who? So I came to him and asked him, and he said: “To Uthman.” So I came to them and informed them, and they said: Go back to him and ask him, for if something happened to Uthman To whom? So I came to him and asked him, and he said: “If something happens to Uthman, then curse you forever.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4460 - True"
"4461","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Asadi al-Hafiz told me, in Hamdan, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told me, Amr ibn Ziyad, Ghalib al-Qurqasani narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Habib, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to Hassan ibn Thabit: “Did you say anything about Abu Bakr?” He said: Yes. He said: “Speak until I hear.” He said: I said:
 [Simple Sea]
 And the second of the two was in the cavernous cave, and... the enemy surrounded him as he ascended the mountain.
 And the love of the Messenger of God was known to them... among the creatures, he did not treat anyone unjustly with it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4461 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4462","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of my father Al-Sha’atha’ Al-Kindi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Tayeb, said: Abu Sufyan bin Harb came to Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and said: What is the matter with this? What is the matter with the fewest and most humiliated of Quraysh - meaning Abu Bakr -? By God, if you wish, I can fill it with horses and men. Ali said: “You have always been hostile to Islam and its people, O Abu Sufyan. It will not harm him at all. Indeed, we found Abu Bakr worthy of it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4462 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"4463","Ahmed bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Yusuf bin Muhammad, the chief tailor, told us, Muhammad bin Khaled Al-Hubli told us, Kathir bin Hisham Al-Kalabi told us, Jafar bin Burqan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: We were with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the delegation of Abd al-Qais came to him, and some of them spoke idle words. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to Abu Bakr, and said: “O Abu Bakr, did you hear what they said?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and I understood him. He said: “Then answer them.” He said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, answered them with an answer and was honest. The answer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Bakr, God has given you the greatest satisfaction.” Then some of the people said to him: What The greatest satisfaction, O Messenger of God? He said: “God will appear to His servants in the Hereafter in general, and He will appear to Abu Bakr in particular.”"
"4464","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki’ informed us, about Abi Al-Umays, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had been a successor... “He would have succeeded Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4464 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4465","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father and Ahmad bin Mani’ told me, they said: Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ayyash, told us by Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Whatever Muslims see as good is good in the sight of God, and whatever Muslims see as bad.” It is bad in the sight of God, and all the Companions decided to appoint Abu Bakr as successor, may God be pleased with him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings it out, and there is a more reliable witness than him, except that there is a message in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4465 - True"
"4466","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, the Muhajireen and Ansar gathered at the shed of Banu Sa’idah in pledge of allegiance to Abu Bakr, so I went to Umm Salamah and said to her: “The people have pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4466 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4467","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Muzaki told me about Marw, Abdullah bin Ruh al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Shuaib bin Maymun, on the authority of Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: It was said to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him: Will you not become a successor? On us? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has never appointed me as a successor, but if God intends good for the people, He will bring them together after me for their good, as “He gathered them together after their Prophet for their good.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4467 - True"
"4468","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Yahya bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Abu Bakr was appointed to us, and he was the best caliph.” “May God have mercy on us and be kind to us.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4468 - True"
"4469","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Radi God, on their authority, said: We walked around a room in which Abu Bakr was afflicted with the pain in which he had been arrested. He looked at us carefully and said: “Aren’t you satisfied? What should I do? We said: Yes, O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4469 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4470","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahz bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, may God be pleased with him, “that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, when he sent the armies towards the Levant, Yazid bin Abu Sufyan, Amr ibn al-Aas, and Shurahbil ibn Hasnah. He walked with them until he reached Thaniyat al-Wada’, and they said: O successor of the Messenger of God, you will walk. And we are riding “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4470 - Sent"
"4471","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “I entered upon Abu Bakr during his caliphate.”"
"4472","With its chain of transmission, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The money of the two Bahrains came to us during the caliphate of Abu Bakr.”"
"4473","Al-Walid bin Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad told us. Al-Muharbi, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn and Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis came to Abu Bakr May God be pleased with him, so they said: “O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4473 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4474","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I fought during the caliphate of Abu Bakr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 4474 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"4475","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu Qalaba told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Zaid told us, Aslam told us. Al-Kufi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Tayeb, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, said: “We were with Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq and he cried, so we said: O successor of the Messenger of God, What is this crying? """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4475 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4476","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ubayy told us, and Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, they said: Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered together and appointed Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4476 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4477","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Usama told us, Abdullah bin Abi Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather He is Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Rusafi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to me. Al-Harbi, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, they said: “Umar bin Al-Khattab bin Nufayl bin Abdul-Uzza bin Riyah bin Abdullah bin Qurt ibn Razah ibn Adiy ibn Ka’b ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fahr - one word, they said: - And his mother was Hintama bint Hashim ibn Al-Mugheerah bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzoum, and her mother was Al-Shifa bint Abd Qais bin Adi bin Saad bin Taim, nicknamed Abu Hafs. The day of Abu Bakr’s death, may God be pleased with them both, which was Tuesday, was replaced by the remaining eight of Jumada al-Akhira.”"
"4478","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Ibrahim bin Saeed told me, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: “Abu Bakr died and Omar, may God be pleased with them, succeeded him after two years, three months and two years.” And twenty days from the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4478 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4479","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Shayban bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Nahwi told us, on the authority of Asim, On the authority of Zirr, he said: I went out with the people of the city on the day of Eid, and I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, walking barefoot, an old man, bald, a left-handed man. He walked for a long time, supervising the people as if he were on an animal with raindrops, saying: “Servants of God, emigrate, but do not emigrate, and let each one of you fear the rabbit.” He picks it up with pebbles or throws it with a stone, and eats it, but to make those who draw spears and arrows sharp for you.” The ruler said: “And the reason was Calling him the Commander of the Faithful”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4479 - True"
"4480","What Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Iskandarani, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz asked Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah: For whatever was written by the successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the era of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, then Omar would first write from The successor of Abu Bakr, so who was the first to write from the Commander of the Faithful? He said: Al-Shifaa told me, and she was one of the first emigrants, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, wrote to the governor of Iraq to send Two handsome men came to him, asking them about Iraq and its people. The governor of Iraq sent Balayd bin Rabi’ah and Adi bin Hatim, and when they came In Medina, they stopped their two camels in the courtyard of the mosque, then they entered the mosque, and they found Amr ibn al-Aas. They said: Ask permission for us, O Amr. On the Commander of the Faithful, and Amr said: You, by God, have given him the right name. He is the Commander and we are the believers. So Amr jumped up and entered upon Omar, the prince of the believers. The believers, and he said: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful. Omar said: What seemed to you about this name, O Ibn Al-Aas? My Lord knows that you will come out of what You said, he said: Labid bin Rabi’ah and Adi bin Hatim came and stopped their mounts in the courtyard of the mosque, then they entered upon me and said to me: Ask permission for us. O Amr Ali, Commander of the Faithful, by God they have perfected your name. We are the believers and you are our commander. He said: “So the decree carried him away from that day.” Al-Shifa was the grandmother of Abu Bakr bin Suleiman.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4480 - True"
"4481","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ayyub Al-Tai told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab said: When Omar came to the Levant, a ford occurred to him, so Omar dismounted from his camel and took off his socks, or he said: his loincloth, then he took hold of his reins. He mounted his mount and entered the ford, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, you have done a great deed before the people of the land. You took off your socks, presented your saddle, and went through the ford. He said: Then Omar touched Abu Ubaidah’s chest with his hand, and said: “Oh, if only someone else could say it.” O Abu Ubaidah, you were the least of people, so God honored you with Islam. No matter how much you seek glory in anything else, God Almighty will humiliate you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4481 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4482","And Abu Bakr told us, I am Abu Al-Muthanna, Musaddad told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, Muslim Al-Awar told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I fought with Omar. Damascus, may God be pleased with him. We stayed at a certain place, and Dihqan came asking for evidence of the Commander of the Faithful until he came to him. When Dihqan saw Omar, he prostrated, and Omar said: “What is this prostration?” He said: This is what we do to kings. Omar said: “Prostrate to your Lord who created you.” He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have prepared food for you. So come to me, he said: Omar said: “Are there any pictures of non-Arabs in your house?” He said: Yes. He said: “We have no need of your house, but go and send us a quantity of food, and do not add to it.” He said: So he went and sent. He brought him food and he ate from it. Then Omar said to his servant: “Do you have any of that wine in your medicine?” He said: Yes, he said: “Then send it for us.” So he brought it and poured it into a vessel, then he smelled it and found that it was unpleasant, so he poured water on it, then he smelled it and found that it was bad. He rejected the wind, so he poured water on him three times, then drank it, then said: “If there is something suspicious in your drink, do this with it.” Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not wear brocade or silk, and do not drink from vessels of silver and gold, for they are for them.” This world, and for us in the Hereafter.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4482 - They left the one-eyed Muslim"
"4483","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Shababah bin Siwar told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, strengthen the religion with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4483 - True"
"4484","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Saeed bin Suleiman told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Oh God Islam was strengthened by Omar. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it,” and its witnesses were authentic, on the authority of Aisha bint al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them both. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4484 - True"
"4485","Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Al-Majishun bin Abi told us Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O God, honor “Islam is due to Omar ibn al-Khattab in particular.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. On the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah: “O God, strengthen Islam by the two men most beloved to You.” Mujalid bin Saeed was the only one to say it, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi and did not I mentioned to Mujalid what happened before his narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4485 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4486","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Hatim Al-Ijli Al-Hafiz told us, Omar bin Muhammad Al-Asadi told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Oh God, strengthen Islam through Omar bin Al-Khattab or Abu Jahl bin Hisham.” So God made the call of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He handed it over to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and he established the rule of Islam over it and demolished idols with it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4486 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4487","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told me, Asim bin Ali told me, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “By God, we were not able to pray visibly at the Kaaba until Omar converted to Islam.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4487 - True"
"4488","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Hudhayfah told us: We told us: Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Islam in the time of Umar was like a man approaching “It only increases in proximity. When Omar was killed, he was like a man running away. He only increases in distance.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4488 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4489","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khorasani, Al-Adl, told us in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Jafi told us, Al-Fadl told us Bin Jubayr Al-Warraq, Ismail bin Zakaria Al-Khalqani told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The first one whom the truth will embrace on the Day of Resurrection will be Omar, and the first one whom the truth will shake hands with on the Day of Resurrection will be ‘Umar. The Resurrection is Omar, and the first one to be taken by the hand and taken to Paradise will be Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4489 - Topic"
"4490","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We have been proud since the time of Umar’s conversion to Islam.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4490 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4491","Abdullah bin Kharash told us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when Omar converted to Islam: “Gabriel came to me and said: The people of heaven rejoiced about Omar’s conversion to Islam.” True.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4491 - Abdullah bin Kharash was deemed weak by Al-Daraqutni"
"4492","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, and Abu Muhammad bin Saad Al-Hafiz narrated to us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us. Al-Abdi, Al-Nufaili told us, Khaled bin Abi Bakr bin Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck Omar bin Al-Khattab’s chest with his hand when he converted to Islam three times. And he says: “O God, remove the hatred from his chest and replace it with faith.” He says that three times: “This is an authentic hadith with a straight chain of narration. He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4492 - Al-Bukhari said Khalid bin Abi Bakr Al-Amri has evil deeds."
"4493","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Sulaiman al-Faqih, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zahid, and Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, they said: Thana Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, said: Omar fought the polytheists in the mosque of Mecca, and he continued to fight them since the morning, until the sun was about His head, he said: He became tired and sat down, then a man with a red cloak and a black shirt, with a good face, came in to see him, and he came until he relieved them, and he said: What do you want from this man? They said: No, by God, except that he was a boy. He said: What a fine man he chose for himself a religion, so they called it, but he did not choose it for himself. Do you think the Banu Adi will be satisfied? That Omar would be killed? No, by God, the Banu Adi will not be satisfied. He said: And Omar said on that day: “O enemies of God, by God, if we had reached three hundred, we would have expelled you.” From her, I said to my father afterward: Who is that man who turned them away from you that day? He said: “That is Al-Aas bin Wa’il, Abu Amr bin Al-Aas.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4493 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4494","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati, Yahya bin Abdul-Hamid told us, my father told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr Abi Omar. Al-Khazzaz, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: “When Omar, may God be pleased with him, converted to Islam, the polytheists said: Today is the middle of the day.” Some of us said: “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4494 - True"
"4495","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Musharrah bin Haaan, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If there were a prophet after me, it would be Omar bin Al-Khattab.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4495 - True"
"4496","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan, Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Muammar bin Suleiman told us, Ubaid Allah told us Ibn Omar, that he heard Abu Bakr Ibn Salim narrating, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “In my sleep, I saw that I was given a cup full of milk, and I drank from it until I was full, until I saw it in a vein between the skin and the flesh. So there was something left over, so I gave it to Omar ibn Al-Khattab. They said: O Prophet of God, this is knowledge that God has given you. So you were filled with it, so you got something left over. I gave it to Omar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: “You are correct.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4496 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4497","Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “If the knowledge of Omar were placed on the pan of a scale, and the knowledge of the people was placed on the other, Omar’s knowledge would prevail.”"
"4498","Mas’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, “Umar was a master of the Lord. And He made us read the Book of God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4498 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4499","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, Ubayy told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Al-Layth bin Saad, and Yahya bin Ayyub told us, they said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “There were hadith scholars among the nations, but if there is anyone among my nation, then it is Umar ibn al-Khattab.” This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4499 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4500","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Shihab told us, Muhammad bin Wasi’ told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a light sermon, and when he finished his sermon He said: “O Abu Bakr, stand up and deliver the sermon.” So Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, got up and delivered the sermon, but he stopped short of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When Abu Early in his sermon, he said: “O Umar, get up and deliver the sermon.” Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, got up and delivered the sermon, but he stopped short of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and without Ubayy. Bakr, may God be pleased with him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4500 - Interrupted"
"4501","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Ghaz, Ibn Ajlan, and Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Ghudayf bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: A young man passed by Omar, and Omar said: What a good boy. He said: Then Abu Dharr followed him and said: O boy, ask forgiveness for me. He said: O Abu Dharr, I ask forgiveness for you. And you are the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Ask forgiveness for me. He said: No, or tell me. He said: You passed by Omar, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: What a good boy, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God put the truth on the tongue of Omar and in his heart.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4501 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4502","Abu Al-Hussein Abdul-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad told us Al-Farawi, Abdul-Malik bin Qudamah Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, came while the prayer was still in progress, and three people were sitting, one of whom was Abu Jahsh al-Laythi. He said: Get up and pray with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then two stood up, but Abu Jahsh refused to stand up, so Omar said to him: Pray, O Abu Jahsh, with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: I will not get up until a man who is stronger than me in arms and more powerful than me comes to me and knocks me down, then pushes my face into the dirt. He said: Omar: So I got up to him, and I was stronger in arms than him, and more powerful than him, so I knocked him down, then I pushed his face into the dirt, and Othman came upon me. So he detained me, and Omar bin Al-Khattab went out angry until he went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw him and saw the anger in His face, he said: “What is the matter with you, Abu Hafs?” He said: O Messenger of God, I came to a group of people sitting at the door of the mosque, and prayer had been performed, and among them was Abu Jahsh al-Laythi, so the two men got up and repeated Hadith,Then Omar said: By God, O Messenger of God, Othman did not help him except that he entertained him for a night, and he wanted to thank him for it, so he heard him. Othman, and he said: O Messenger of God, do you not hear what Omar tells us with you? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Omar is pleased with God’s mercy, I wish you had brought me the head of the evil one.” So Omar got up and then he continued. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and said: “Come on, Omar, where did you want to go?” He said: I wanted to bring you the head of the evil one, so he said: “Sit down until I tell you that the Lord is indispensable to the prayer of Abu Jahsh al-Laythi. Indeed, God is in heaven.” The world is angels out of humility who will not raise their heads until the Hour comes. When the Hour comes, they raise their heads and then say: Our Lord, we have not worshiped You. Your worship is true.” Then Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said to him: What do they say, O Messenger of God? He said: “As for the inhabitants of the lower heaven, they say: Glory be to Him who is the King and the Kingdom, and as for the inhabitants of the second heaven, they say: Glory be to the Ever-Living, Who does not He dies, so say it, O Umar, in your prayer.” He said: “O Messenger of God, so what about what you taught me and commanded me to say in my prayer?” He said: “Say this once.” And this time, what he commanded was that he said: I seek refuge in You with Your forgiveness from Your punishment.I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from Your Majesty. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4502 - Strange denial"
"4503","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Omar bin Muhammad told me that Salem bin Abdul God Ibn Omar told him, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “I never heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab say about anything: I do not think Such and such, unless it was as he thought. While Omar ibn al-Khattab was sitting, a beautiful man passed by him and said to him: My assumption was wrong or you are on the right track. Your religion in pre-Islamic times, and you were their soothsayer.” He said: “I have never seen a Muslim man greeted like today.” Omar said: “I resolve that you will not You told me? He said: I was their priest in pre-Islamic times? He said: What is surprising about what has brought you? “He mentioned a long hadith that had no support.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4503 - The hadith in Sahih Al-Bukhari with this chain of transmission is complete"
"4504","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani Abu Abdullah told me, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Al-Ala’ Al-Zubaidi told me, Amr bin Al-Harith Al-Zubaidi told me, Abdullah bin Salem Al-Ash’ari told me, Muhammad bin Al-Walid told me Bin Amir Al-Zubaidi, Rashid bin Saad told us, that Abu Rashid told them, returning it to Maadi Karib bin Abdul Kulal that Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, said: We traveled with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, on his last journey to the Levant, and when he approached it, he was informed that There was a plague there, so it was said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, you should not attack him, just as if he had fallen while you were there, you would not have been able to He left it and returned, heading toward the city. He said: While we were walking at night, he said to me: Get out of the way. So he turned away, and I turned away. So he alighted from his mount, then put his head on the arm of his camel, and he fell asleep, but I could not sleep. Then he went and said to me: What do I have to do with them? Avert me from my sins. Damascus, then he rode off, and I did not ask him anything. Even if I thought that I was mingling with people, I said to him: Why did you say what you said when you woke up from your sleep? He said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Seventy thousand will be sent from between the wall of Homs and the olives in the red dirt. They will have a reckoning.” If God brings me back from this journey of mine, I will certainly bear with my children, my family, and my wealth until Hums descends. He returned from that journey. And he was killed, may God be pleased with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4504 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"4505","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, in Kufa, Ubaid bin Hatim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Dawud bin Rashid narrated to us, Al-Haytham bin Adi narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, wrote to Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas: “Take for the Muslims a house A migration and a place of jihad.” So Saad sent a man from the Ansar called: Al-Harith bin Salamah, and he went to the place of Kufa for them today. So Saad brought it down to the people, and he outlined our mosque and wrote the lines in it. Al-Sha’bi said: In Kufa there was a planting of lavender and wormwood. And chrysanthemums, and anemones. In pre-Islamic times, the Arabs called it the virgin’s cheek - so they adopted it and wrote to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, who wrote: “Leave him,” so the people turned to Kufa.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4505 - Al-Haytham bin Adi has fallen"
"4506","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i informed us, Muhammad ibn Maslamah informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sharik informed us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: “Kufa is the dome of Islam, and the land of affliction.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4506 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4507","Abd Al-Baqi bin Qani’ Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hammad told us, Al-Hasan bin Yusuf Al-Maruzi told us, Baqiya told us, Buhair bin Saad told us, On the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, that His mistress came to dye his beard, and he said: “I only want you to extinguish my light as so-and-so extinguishes his light.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4507 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4508","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jawhari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Abdullah bin Dawud Al-Wasiti told us, Abd al-Rahman, my nephew, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of his uncle Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab said One day, Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them both, said: O the best of people after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr said: Are you not You said that because I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The sun has not risen over a man is better than his life.” This hadith is with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4508 - The hadith is semi-mawdoo’"
"4509","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: “The most virtuous of people are three: Al-Aziz, when he looked at Joseph and said to his wife: Honor his resting place, and the woman who saw Moses, peace be upon him, and said to her father: O father, hire him, and Abu Bakr when he succeeded Omar May God be pleased with them both. Al-Hakim said: “May God be pleased with Ibn Masoud. He did well in bringing them together, and this chain of transmission is authentic.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4509 - True"
"4510","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abdul-Ala bin Hammad Al-Narsi told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ma`dan ibn Abi Talha al-Imari, who said: “Umar, may God be pleased with him, was injured on Wednesday For the remaining four nights of Dhul-Hijjah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4510 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4511","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Yahya bin Subayh told us. Al-Khorasani, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha Al-Yamari, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him He said on the pulpit: “I saw in a dream as if a rooster gave me three pecks - so I said: I am a foreigner - and I have made my affairs up to these people.” The six about whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested while he was satisfied: Othman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. And Saad bin Abi Waqqas, so whoever is appointed successor is the caliph.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4511 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4512","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Shabib told us. Al-Ma’mari, Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Hasab told us, Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: “Abu Lu’lu’a was owned by Al-Mughirah bin Shu`bah was making mills, and Al-Mughirah was using it every day for four dirhams. Then he met Abu Lu’lu’ Umar and said: O Prince Believers, Al-Mughirah has become too much for me, so speak to him to ease my burden, so Omar said to him, “Fear God and be good to your master.” He said: And from the intention Omar was told to meet al-Mughirah and talk to him about relieving his burden. He said: Abu Lu’lu’ah became angry. His name was Fayrouz, and he was a Christian. He said: Let the people go. All of them were fair to him except me. He said: Then he became angry and determined to kill him, so he made a dagger with two points. He said: He sharpened it and poisoned it. He said: And Omar grew old. Omar did not say “Allahu Akbar” when the prayer was being held until he had spoken and said: “Straighten your rows.” Then he came and stood in the row following Omar’s example in the morning prayer. When the prayer was performed, Omar spoke and said: Straighten your rows, then he said the takbir, and when he said the takbeer he leaned on his shoulder and placed his face on another place, and he made his face in I attacked him, and Omar fell. He said: Thirteen men went with him, but seven of them scattered, and six of them died, and Omar, may God be pleased with him, endured. On his behalf, he was taken away and the people surrounded him until the sun was about to rise. He said: Then Abd al-Rahman bin Awf called out, O people, prayer, prayer, and he panicked. Prayer. He said: Then Abdul Rahman came forward and led them in prayer, and recited the two shortest surahs in the Qur’an. He said: When he left, the people went to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: He called for something to drink to see the extent of his wound, and wine was brought and he drank it. He said: Then he went out and Adam did not know Is it Umm Nabeeth? He said: So he called for milk, and it was brought. He drank it, and it came out of his wound. They said: There is no harm in you, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: «If “Killing was wrong, so I was killed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4512 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4513","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, that He heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: When Omar bin Al-Khattab departed from Mina during the last Hajj, he made a vow with Batha’a, then heaped Batha’a in a heap, then He spread his garment over her, then he lay down and extended his hands to the sky, and said: “O God, my age has grown, my strength has weakened, and my flock has spread. So take me to you, neither wasting nor neglecting.” Then he came in Dhul-Hijjah and addressed the people, saying: “O people, I have established for you the Sunnahs. And I have imposed upon you the duties, and I have left you upon the clear ones - and he struck one hand over the other - unless you turn toward the people to the right and to the left.’ So what? Dhu al-Hijjah passed until Omar, may God be pleased with him, was killed, and I heard Saeed bin al-Musayyab say: “Abu Lu’lu’a, the one who killed Omar, was stabbed twelve times.” A man of Omar, and six of them died, and six of them dispersed, and he had with him a knife with two edges, so he stabbed himself with it, killing her.”"
"4514","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Jallab narrated to me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr narrated to me, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Zaydah narrated to us, On the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Umar lived for three days after he was stabbed, then he died and was washed and shrouded.”"
"4515","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Amer, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I entered upon Omar when he was stabbed and said: Give good tidings of Paradise, O Commander of the Faithful. You converted to Islam when the people disbelieved. You struggled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the people failed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and he was satisfied with you, and he did not differ in your opinion. You have two caliphs, and you were killed as a martyr. He said: “Accide against me,” so I responded to him. He said: “By God, besides Whom there is no god, if only I had anything on the earth.” Of yellow and white, I would have ransomed him from the terror of the rising.”"
"4516","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Wahib told us, Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, “Indeed, Omar was prayed for in the mosque, and Suhaib, may God be pleased with him, prayed for him.”"
"4517","Abu Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Husayn bin Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Qasim my brother told us, Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Sufyan. Al-Thawri, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: When Omar was killed, Ali and Othman hastened to pray over him, and Suhaib said to them: “To you. On my behalf, I have been in charge of your affairs more than praying for Omar, and I am praying with you the prescribed prayer, so Suhaib prayed over him.”"
"4518","Mukhlid bin Ja’far Al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad bin Jarir told us, Al-Harith bin Muhammad told us, Muhammad bin Sa’d told us, on the authority of Al-Waqidi, “Omar was satisfied God, on his authority, performed Hajj on people ten consecutive Hajj, including one Hajj in the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and nine in his caliphate, and that he was buried next to Abu Bakr in the house of Aisha, may God be pleased with them, and his caliphate lasted ten years, five months, and twenty-nine days.”"
"4519","Abu Saeed Al-Thaqafi and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Maamari told us, Al-Walid bin Shuja’ told us, Muhammad bin Bishr, Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah, Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, and our sheikhs narrated that Omar bin Al-Khattab May God be pleased with him, when he was stabbed, he said to Abdullah: “Go to Aisha and extend peace to her, and say: Omar says to you: If it is not It will harm you and not be difficult for you, for I would like to be buried with my companion, and if that would harm you and be difficult for you, then by my life he has been buried in this. Al-Baqi is one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the mothers of the believers, who is better than Omar.” Then the Messenger came to her, and she said: That is It will not harm me or make me difficult. He said: “So bury me with them.”"
"4520","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Qasim bin Abi al-Zinad told us, Hisham bin Saad told me, on the authority of Amr bin Othman bin Hani, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: “I looked into the grave - the grave of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar - from Aisha’s room, may God be pleased with her, and I saw red gravel on her.”"
"4521","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Bishr bin Al-Walid Al-Qadi told us, Abu Yusuf Al-Qadi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Umar, may God be pleased with him, died when he was sixty-three years old.”"
"4522","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “If Umar is a fortified fortress, he will enter Islam is in it, but does not come out of it. When Omar was struck, the fort was cut short, Islam comes out of it, and does not enter it, when the righteous are mentioned. So he greeted them with 'Umar."
"4523","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jafar Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that Ali entered upon Omar while he was lying down, and said: “May God’s peace be upon you,” then He said: “There is no one more beloved to me than to meet God with what is in his record than this record.” Al-Hakim said: “What of the Shura news is authentic? It was published after the death of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, and is linked to the news of the Saqifat of Banu Sa’idah."
"4524","Abu Sahl bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us, dictating, Abu Qalaba told us, Ubi told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who said: “A voice was heard. On Mount Tabala when Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was killed: poetry
 [Long Sea]

 Let whoever weeps over Islam, weep over Islam... for my doom is about to come, and the covenant has not been brought forward.
 And it has managed the world, and its goodness has been managed... and it has been filled with it by one who was certain of the promise.
 “So they looked and saw nothing.”"
"4525","Abu Sahl bin Ziyad told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Ashhal bin Hatim told us, Ibn Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Atika bint Zaid bin inherited Amr bin Nufail Omar, may God be pleased with him, and she said: (Poetry) """"
 [light sea]

 Judy's eyes are filled with tears and lamentations...do not dictate to the imam of the cross.
 So I was saddened by the longing for the knight with him... Why the day of commotion and reprimand
 The infallibility of religion, the helper over time, and the relief of the anxious and distressed.
 Say to the people of affliction and misery, “Die... when you made us drink of Manun, a cup of peoples.”
 Atika also said:
 [Long Sea]

 So Fayrouz pained me like no other... with the rich whiteness of Munib’s book
 Kind to others, harsh to transgressions... My brother, trustworthy in the deputies, is responsive.
 “Whenever he says, his words do not lie. His actions are quick to good deeds and are not fixed.”
 The hadith of Al-Thawri is included in the two Sahih books, but I have mentioned here some letters with a sound chain of transmission that are useful and strange.”"
"4526","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi and Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Jallab told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabah told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Omar, the client of Afra, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Omar said to the companions Al-Shura: “To God belongs a dirham, if the most upright people twisted it, how could He make them follow the truth, even if it was carried around the neck by the sword?” He said: So I said: You know that. From him and do not give him your guardianship? He said: “If I leave, then someone better than me has appointed me as successor, and if I leave, then someone better than me has left as my successor.”"
"4527","Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Al-Mansur, Commander of the Faithful, told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Yazid Al-Riyahi told us, Harun bin Ismail Al-Khazzaz told us, Qurrah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, he said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The camel says: Oh God, I absolve myself from the blood of Othman, and my mind was lost on the day Othman was killed, and I denied myself and they came to me to pledge allegiance, so I said: By God, I am ashamed before God to pledge allegiance to a people who killed a man. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Am I not ashamed of whom you are ashamed?” And from Him are the angels.” And indeed, I am ashamed before God to pledge allegiance while Othman was dead on the ground and had not yet been buried. So they left, and when he was buried, the people returned. So they asked me to pledge allegiance, and I said: Oh God, I am sorry for what he has done. Then a resolve came and I pledged allegiance. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, It was as if my heart had cracked, and I said: O God, take it from me to Uthman until you are satisfied. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4527 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4528","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Uthman bin Affan bin Abi Al-Aas bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams Ibn Abd Manaf Ibn Qusayy Ibn Kilab, and Umm Uthman: Arwa bint Krayz, and Umm Arwa: Umm Hakim, and she is Al-Bayda, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They differed regarding the nickname of Othman, so it was said: Abu Abdullah, and it was said: Abu Amr.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4528 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4529","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told me, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, Abu Dawud told me, Ibn Abi al-Zanad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aban Bin Othman, he said: I heard Abu Abdullah Othman bin Affan, and I heard Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari saying: I heard Othman Bin Saeed Al-Darimi says: I heard Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah saying: “Uthman bin Affan was nicknamed Abu Amr, and Abu Abdullah was killed in Al-Hijjah in the year thirty-five.”"
"4530","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told me, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashhab told me, Abu Hilal told me, on the authority of Qatada, “Uthman bin Affan was killed when he was ninety or eighty-eight years old.”"
"4531","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Uthman bin Affan was killed on Friday for twelve. Thirty-five years of Dhul-Hijjah remained, and his caliphate was twelve years.”"
"4532","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of my father Abdullah, the servant of Shaddad ibn al-Haad, said: “I saw Uthman ibn Affan on the pulpit on Friday, wearing a thick, expensive, Adani garment. Four or five dirhams, a keffiyeh scarf with torn flesh, a long beard, and a handsome face.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4532 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4533","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Suleiman told us, Abu Ubayd Allah Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb told us, My uncle told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The first stone that the Prophet carried May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to build the mosque, then Abu Bakr carried another stone, then Othman carried another stone, and I said: O Messenger of God, don’t you see what How can these people help you? He said: “O Aisha, these are the caliphs after me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, but it was known for its weak chain of transmission. From the narration of Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Atiyya, “For that reason he was abandoned.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4533 -: Ahmed bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb Munkar Al-Hadith"
"4534","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told me, he said: “And it was pledge of allegiance to Othman, may God be pleased with him, on the twelfth of Muharram in the year twenty-four.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Takhris Al-Dhahabi] 4534 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it in Al-Takhris"
"4535","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yasar He said: “The pledge of allegiance to Othman, may God be pleased with him, came. Abdullah said: “They did not avoid announcing it to the One Above.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4535 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4536","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Shayban bin Farukh told us, Talha bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ubaida bin Hassan, on the authority of Ataa Al-Kikharani, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, while we were in the house of Ibn Hashfa with a group of immigrants, including Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with them, and he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let every man of you rise to his level.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose to Uthman and embraced him, and said: “You are my guardian in this world and the hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4536 - Rather, it is weak"
"4537","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, with Al-Tabaran, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr bin Maysarah told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam bin Aws Al-Ansari, Abu Ubadah Al-Zarqi told me, Zaid bin Aslam told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed Uthman on the day he was besieged in a place. Funerals, and he said: I adjure you by God, O Talha, remember the day you and I were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in such-and-such a place. And none of his companions were with him except me and you, so he said to you: “O Talha, there is not a prophet except that he has a companion from his nation with him in Paradise, and that Othman is my companion and with me in Paradise.” Then Talha said: “By God, yes.” Then Talha said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4537 - Qasim Al-Bukhari said this, his hadith is not authentic"
"4538","Abu Abdullah bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Kulaib bin Wael, he said: Habib bin Abi Mulaika told me, he said: A man came to Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, and said: Did Othman witness the Pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. He said: So he witnessed Badr. He said: No. He said: “So he was among those whom Satan led astray?” He said: Yes, so the man got up and some of the people said to him: This man now claims that you had an affair with Uthman. He said: He also says: He said: Answer me. The man said: Did you understand what I told you? He said: Yes, I asked you, did Othman witness the Pledge of Ridwan? You said: No, and I asked you: Did he witness a full moon? So I said: No, and I asked you: Was he among those whom Satan led astray? So I said: Yes, and he said: As for the Pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: “Uthman set out for the need of God and the need of His Messenger,” and he was struck with an arrow for himself, and he did not strike for anyone except him, and as for those who turned away on the day the two groups met, it was Satan who caused them to slip. With some of what they earned, and God has certainly pardoned them. Indeed, God is Forgiving, Forbearing. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4538 - True"
"4539","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Suleiman Al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hawalah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “That On the Day when you will attack a man wearing a cloak, who pledges allegiance to the people of Paradise.” So I attacked Othman, may God be pleased with him, while he was wearing a cloak. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4539 - True"
"4540","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Hisham bin Abi Al-Damaik told us, Al-Hussein bin Ubaid Allah told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi told us Hazim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there lightning in Paradise? He said: “Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Othman will move from one house to another, and Paradise will shine for him.” If he is Al-Hussein bin Ubaid Allah This was preserved on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, so it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4540 - The topic"
"4541","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, Musa and Muhammad told us, And Ibrahim, Banu Uqba, said: Abu Umna Abu Hasana told us, saying: I witnessed Abu Hurairah and Uthman confined in the house, and I asked his permission to enter. Speaking, Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be a trial, a disagreement - or a disagreement - and a trial.” He said: We said: O Messenger of God, what do you command us to do? He said: “You should look after the prince and his companions,” and he pointed to Uthman. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4541 - True"
"4542","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba He said: Abu Alqamah, the servant of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, told me: Kathir bin al-Salt told me, he said: Uthman bin Affan fell asleep in The day he was killed, he woke up and said: “If the people had not said that Othman wished for strife, I would have told you. He said: We said: May God bless you.” So he spoke to us, for we do not say what people say. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this dream of mine, and he said: “You are a witness with us.” “Friday” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4542 - True"
"4543","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abu Sahlah, the servant of Uthman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him On her authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Invite for me - or I wish I had - a man from my companions.” She said: I said: Abu Bakr? He said: “No.” I said: Omar? He said: “No.” I said: Is your cousin Ali? He said: “No.” I said: Othman? He said: “Yes.” She said: Then Othman came and said: “Arise.” He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began to walk to Othman, and Othman’s color changed. He said: Then, when the day came, we said: Won’t you fight? He said: No, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrusted me with a matter, so I am patient with myself over it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4543 - True"
"4544","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Musa bin Dawud Al-Dhabi told us, Al-Faraj bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Uthman: “Allah will clothe you with a shirt, but if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off.” This is an authentic hadith with a high chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4544 - How is he in good health and what is his position on Faraj bin Fadala?"
"4545","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, that He said: “The name of Abu Sarh is Al-Hussam bin Al-Harith bin Habib bin Khuzaymah.” Al-Hakim said: “And when Abdullah bin Saad took control of Egypt, he followed Among them is Amr ibn Sawad al-Sarhi, the companion of Abdullah ibn Wahb, and as for al-Walid ibn Uqba ibn Abi Muait, he was born during the lifetime of the Messenger of God. God and was carried to him, so he was deprived of his blessing, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4546","Tell us about the authenticity of what you mentioned, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Fayyad bin Zuhair told us. Al-Ruqiy, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Kallabi, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Uqba, he said: “When he opened The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the people of Mecca bring their children, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped their heads. And he prayed for them, so my father took me out to him, and I was good-natured, so he did not wipe my head, nor did he touch me, and nothing prevented him from doing so except that My mother created me with good nature, but he did not touch me for good nature.” Ahmad ibn Hanbal, may God be pleased with him, said: “It was narrated that he converted to Islam.” On that day, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt disgusted with him and did not touch him, nor did he supplicate for him, and creation is not prevented from supplicating. There is also no crime for a child in He did something else, but he prevented the blessing of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, due to God Almighty’s prior knowledge of it, and God knows best.”"
"4547","Abu Zakaria al-Qasim bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja al-Suddi told us, Dawud bin Rashid told us, Al-Haytham bin Adi told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told me, Tariq bin Shihab Al-Ahmasi told me, he said: Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, used On his authority is Al-Walid bin Uqba bin Abi Muait, and his maternal brother was in charge of Kufa and its land, and therein was Saad bin Abi Waqqas, so he took precedence over Saad. So he made him sit with him, not knowing his knowledge. Then Abu Wahb said: What brought you forward? He said: “I brought a worker.” He said: For what? He said: “On your deeds.” He said: By God, I don’t know whether I was foolish after me, or whether I was foolish after you? He said: “By God, I have not been foolish after you, nor have you been foolish after me, but the people have gained influence over you because of their authority.” So he said: You are right. Then Saad said: He narrated to me the story of a hyena, and he bought with a man’s flesh if his helper were to witness it today, O hyenas of evil. Al-Haytham said: And when Uthman was deposed Al-Walid bin Uqba, on the authority of Kufa, and Sa’id bin Al-Aas as its governor. Al-Haytham said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When Sa`id ibn al-Aas came forward and said: “Wash the pulpit so that I may ascend on it or it may be purified.” So the pulpit was washed until Sa`id ibn al-Aas ascended.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4547 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4548","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam Al-Misri told us, my father and Shuaib told me Ibn Al-Layth, they said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Rabi’ah Ibn Laqit Al-Tajibi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Hawwalah Al-Asadi, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever is saved from three has been saved.” They said: What, O Messenger of God? He said: “My death, and the killing of a caliph who was steadfast in the truth and was given it, and who was the Antichrist.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4548 - True"
"4549","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani informed me, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, a partner told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Najiya, who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mill Islam will return after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it will be the same as those who perished, even if they remain. Their religion will last for seventy days.” Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: O Prophet of God, with what has passed or with what remains. He said: “No, but with what remains.” This is a hadith. “Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, and it contains a clear explanation of the killing of Uthman, as I mentioned, from the date of the killing in the year thirty-five.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4549 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4550","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Al-Walid bin Uqba bin Abu Muayt bin Amr bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams, he was Othman’s maternal brother, and their mother was Arwa bint Kuraiz bin Rabi’ah bin Abd. Shams, and her mother, Umm Hakim, Al-Bayda, daughter of Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, paternal aunt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was killed. He greeted Uqba bin Abi Muait on his return. Al-Walid was a man in the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was nicknamed Abu Wahb."
"4551","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Saeed bin Abdullah Al-Jurjisi narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us. Bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amr bin Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Tonight I see a righteous man. Abu Bakr has intercourse with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar has intercourse with Abu Bakr, and Othman was assigned to Omar.” When we got up from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we said: As for the righteous man, he is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for what was mentioned about their relation to one another, they are the rulers of this matter with which God sent His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Al-Darimi said: So I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Muhammad bin Harb, with the chain of transmission of this hadith, and the people narrate it, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, but it is Amr.” Ibn Aban, and Aban Ibn Uthman did not have a son called Amr.”"
"4552","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of my father Al-Ash'ath, on the authority of Murrah ibn Ka'b, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning a sedition to which he admitted, then a masked man in a garment passed by him. He said: “This is the Day upon guidance.” So I stood up to him, and behold, it was Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, so I turned to face him. So I said: Is this? He said: “Yes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4552 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4553","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Damrah bin Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Ibn Shudhab, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Kathir, the client of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, who said: Uthman, may God be pleased with him, came To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a thousand dinars when he prepared the army of hardship, so Uthman emptied it in the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So the Prophet made May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he turns it around and says: “Whatever he does after this day is of no harm to Uthman.” He said it repeatedly, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4553 - True"
"4554","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mihran al-Razi told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that Uthman spoke in the morning and said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him in a dream that night, and said: “O Uthman, break your fast with us.” Then Uthman became fasting and was killed that day, may God be pleased with him. “This is a hadith.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4554 - True"
"4555","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Ja’fi told us, Al-Fadl bin Jubayr Al-Warraq told us, Khalid bin Abd told us By God, Al-Tahan Al-Muzani, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, approached, and when he approached him, he said: “O Othman, you will be killed while reciting Surat THE HEIFER (al-Baqarah): Then some of your blood will fall on: {So Allah will suffice you for them, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing} [Al-Baqarah: 137], and you will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a ruler over every despised person. The people of the East and the West will envy you, and you will intercede for the number of Rabi’ah and Mudar.” Al-Hakim said: “I have mentioned the supporting reports in this chapter in The book about the killing of Uthman, may God be pleased with him, so why is it appropriate to mention it at the end of it in this place, for this is sufficient, as for What the innovator claimed was that she helped the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, to kill him, for it is a lie and a falsehood, and it has been repeated repeatedly. News other than that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4555 - A complete lie"
"4556","Abu Al-Qasim Ali bin Al-Mu’mal bin Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Yunus Al-Qurashi told us, Harun bin Ismail Al-Khazzaz told us, Qurrah told us Ibn Khalid Al-Sadusi heard Al-Hassan, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abbad, who said: I witnessed Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the Day of the Camel saying: This, O God, I will be healed. To you is the blood of Othman, and my mind was lost on the day Othman was killed, and I denied myself and they wanted me to pledge allegiance, so I said: By God, I am ashamed of I swear to God that I pledge allegiance to a people who killed a man. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Am I not ashamed of the one whom the angels are ashamed of?” And I Because I was ashamed before God to pledge allegiance while Othman was dead on the ground and not yet buried, so they left. When he was buried, the people returned to me and asked me for the pledge of allegiance. So I said: Oh God, I am sorry for what he did. Then came a resolve, so I pledged allegiance. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, and it was as if my heart had been torn apart. So I said: Oh God, take from me for Othman until you are satisfied.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4556 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4557","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Bashar bin Musa Al-Khafaf told us, Al-Haatibi Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: On the Day of the Camel, I went out to look at the dead. He said: Then Ali and Al-Hasan bin Ali stood up, Ammar bin Yasser, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, and Zayd bin Suhan were looking around at the dead. He said: Then he saw Al-Hasan bin Ali killed, strangled on his knees. His face, then he turned his heart to his back, then he shouted, then he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. The Quraysh rejoiced, by Allah, and his father said to him: Who is he? Son? He said: Muhammad bin Talha bin Ubaidullah. He said: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. By God, he was a good young man, then he sat down depressed. Sad, then Al-Hasan said to him: O father, I was forbidding you from this path, but so-and-so and so-and-so prevailed over you in your opinion. He said: It was that My son, I wish I had died twenty years before this. Muhammad bin Hatib said: So I got up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, we are coming. Medina, and people asked us about Othman, what do you say about him? He said: So Ammar bin Yasser and Muhammad bin Abi Bakr spoke, and they said: And they said, so Ali said to them: “O Ammar, and O Muhammad, you say that Othman He took influence and mistreated the woman, and by God I punished you, so you mistreated him, and you will come to a just arbitrator who will judge between you.” Then he said: “O Muhammad Ibn Hatib: When you come to Medina and are asked about Uthman, say: By God, he was among those who believed and did righteous deeds, then they feared and believed, then they feared And do good, and God loves those who do good, and in God let the believers put their trust.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4557 - Bashar bin Musa Al-Khafaf is weak"
"4558","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Khalil Al-Asbahani told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Khattimi Al-Qadi told us, in Al-Ray, Al-Musayyab bin Abd told us. The King, Marwan bin Muawiya told us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Amr bin Sufyan, who said: Ali addressed us on the Day of the Camel, and he said: Where are the people’s fans? He said: We said: They are squatters around the camel. He said: Then he said: “As for what follows, this emirate was not entrusted to us by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Therein is a covenant whose traces will be followed, but we saw it for ourselves. Abu Bakr was appointed as successor and he remained and remained steadfast, then Omar was appointed as successor and remained And he was upright, then time struck with its course.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4558 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4559","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Ali bin Qadim told us, Abu Israel told us, about the ruling, he said: “Eighty Badrians and two hundred and fifty of those who pledged allegiance testified with Ali from Siffin under the tree.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4559 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4560","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Ali bin Qadim told us, Abu Israel told us about the ruling, he said: “He witnessed with Ali Siffin,” etc
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4560 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4561","Al-Shaybani, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulaiman Al-Razi told us, I often heard Abu Al-Nadr say: I heard Raba’i bin Harash He says: I set out for Hudhayfah in Al-Mada'in. The night before, people walked to Othman, and he said: O my son, what have your people done? He said: What condition are you asking about? He said: Whoever left among them came to this man, so I named for him a man from among those who left, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever left group, and exchanged the emirate, he met God and had no argument before Him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4561 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4562","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Qahtaba Al-Sanabihi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, I heard Maymun ibn Mihran mention that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “I would not be pleased if I took my sword to kill Uthman, and I have The world and what is in it”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4562 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4563","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Najda al-Qurashi told us, Ali bin Abdul Hamid told us, Yaqoub bin Abdullah al-Qummi told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antarah, on the authority of his father, said: I saw Ali, may God be pleased with him, in the cayenne and he was on his bed, and Aban bin Uthman was with him, so he said: “Indeed, I hope that your father and I will be among those whom God Almighty said: {And We have removed from their breasts any hatred as brothers upon beds facing one another} [Al-Hijr: 47] """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4563 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4564","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Umayyah bin Muslim Al-Qurashi informed us of equality. My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Mughraa, I heard Muhammad Ibn Ishaq Ibn Bashhar mentioning, on the authority of his sheikhs, that Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan was the wife of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, I sent a messenger to Abdullah bin Abi Rabia, brother of Ayyash bin Abi Rabia, informing him of the killing of Othman, and I sent him With his shirt in which he was killed, and his clothes stained with his blood, when the Messenger responded to him, he went out to the people, and ascended the pulpit, and told them By killing him, he spread his shirt on the pulpit, and wept, and the people wept with him, and he composed this saying: “
 [Long Sea]

 There has come to me a matter in which the people are distressed... and there is a long, long weeping in the eyes.
 And in it is the enjoyment of a modest life...and in it is genuine plucking of the noses.
 The affliction of the Commander of the Faithful, and this... is returned to her. She smells the mountains, they disappear.
 A group attacked him in the city... two groups of them were murderers and traitors.
 I will make Abu Amr cry with every Muhannad... and white for her in the shields, Halil
 And there will be no sleep until the people are imprisoned by force... and the cruel deceivers are cured of the people.
 And I will not live in a town as long as I live... I will travel there as a tail, and you will be killed.”
 He said: He went out with those who were with him, and when he approached Mecca, he fell from his mount and died.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4564 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4565","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm told us, Al-Hussein bin Abi Al-Ahwas Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Balkhi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mughra’a, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: What I have heard of Uthman’s elegies, may God be pleased with him, is better than the words of Ka’b ibn Malik: “
 [Long Sea]
 So he folded his hands and then closed his door...and he was certain that God was not heedless.
 And he said to the people of the house, “Do not kill them.” May God forgive everyone who did not fight.
 So how did you see God pouring upon them...enmity and hatred after communication,
 And how have you seen goodness, turning away from it... from the people as moving winds turn away?
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4565 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4566","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta Al-Asbahani told us, Suleiman bin Daoud told us. Al-Shazakouni, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked about Uthman: “What Was it on the middle of his ring? He said: He had the sincerity of his intention on his seal. Oh God, grant me life a happy life, and make me die a martyr. By God, he lived happily and died a martyr.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4566 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4567","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told me, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Abdah bin Suleiman, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Husayn Al-Harithi, who said: Ali bin Abi Talib came to Zayd bin Arqam, may God be pleased with them both. He returned and there were some people with him, so Ali said: “Be still or be silent, for by God, you will not ask me about anything unless I inform you.” Then Zaid said: I adjure you. God, you killed Othman? So Ali knocked on me for an hour, then said: “By the one who split the seed and cured the breeze, I did not kill him, nor did I order his killing.” Harun said: Abu told us Usama, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Qatada, said: “I saw Al-Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, brought out of Uthman’s house wounded.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4567 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4568","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Muhammad bin Talha told us, Kinana Al-Adawi said: “I was among those who besieged Othman.” He said: I said: Muhammad bin Abi Bakr killed him? He said: “No, Jablah bin Al-Ayham, a man from the people of Egypt, killed him. He said: And it was said: He was killed by Kabirah Al-Sakouni, so he was killed at the right time, and it was said: He killed him Kinana bin Bishr al-Tajibi, and perhaps they participated in his killing, may God curse them.” Al-Walid bin Uqba said:
 [Long Sea]
 Indeed, the best of people after their Prophet is... the one killed at Al-Tajibi who came from Egypt.”
 By al-Tajibi, he means the killer of Uthman, may God be pleased with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4568 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4569","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Abu told me Saydan Ubaid bin Tufayl said: Rabi’ bin Harash told me, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, that he proposed to his daughter Omar. He returned him, and this was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When Omar went to him, he said: “O Omar, shall I direct you to a better circumcision for you than Othman? Is Othman better for him than you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Give me your daughter in marriage, and I will marry my daughter to Othman.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"4570","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Mandah Al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Issa bin Al-Musayyab Al-Bajli told us, Abu Zur’ah told us, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, bought Paradise from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, twice: He sold the right where he dug a well. Aid, and where he prepared the army of hardship “with a valid chain of transmission, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4570 - Issa bin Al-Musayyab was deemed weak by Abu Dawud and others."
"4571","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Furat Al-Qazzaz, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umair Ibn Saeed said: Ali wanted to march to the Levant to Siffin, and the Nakha’s gathered until they entered Al-Ashtar’s house, so he said: “Is there anything in the house except Myeloid? They said: No. He said: “This nation sought the best of its people and they killed him - meaning Uthman - and we fought the people of Basra with a pledge of allegiance.” We interpreted it from him, “And you are marching against a people over whom we have no pledge of allegiance, so let every man look where he puts his sword.” This is a hadith, even if it is not It has a complicated chain of narration. “The chain of narration is authentic in this matter.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4571 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4572","I heard the judge, Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Jarrahhi, and Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Al-Muzaffar Al-Hafiz, saying: We heard Abu Hamid Muhammad bin Harun al-Hadrami says: I heard Muhammad bin Mansour al-Tusi saying: I heard Ahmad bin Hanbal say: “He did not come to any of the Companions of the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, among the virtues that came from Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad al-Dawri said: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in say: “The name of Abu Talib is Abd Manaf” - Al-Hakim said: “And this is how Ziyad bin Muhammad bin Ishaq, and there have been reports that Abu Talib’s nickname was his name, and God knows best” - I heard Abu Abbas say: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad says: I heard Yahya bin Maeen say: “The mother of Ali bin Abi Talib: Fatima bint Asad bin Hashim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4572 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4573","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Fatima bint Asad bin Hashem was the first Hashemite to be born of a Hashemite, and she was a great notable during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She died during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he prayed upon her. Ali’s name was a lion, and for that reason he says:
 [The sea of rage]
 “I am the one my mother called me Haidara.”"
"4574","Bukayr bin Muhammad al-Haddad al-Sufi told me, in Mecca, al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib al-Maamari told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Jabla told us. Al-Bahili, my father told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Saeed Al-Qurashi, he said: We were sitting with Saeed bin Al-Musayyab when Ali bin Al-Hussein passed by us, and I did not see a Hashemite. He had never been a more devout worshiper of God than him, so Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab rose up to him and we stood with him, so we greeted him and he responded to us, and Sa`id said to him: O Abu Muhammad, Tell us about Fatima bint Asad bin Hashim, mother of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them. He said: Yes, my father told me, he said: I heard Amir The Believers Ali bin Abi Talib says: When Fatima bint Asad bin Hashim died, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shrouded her in his shirt and prayed. On her, and he said “Allahu Akbar” on her seventy times, and he descended into her grave and made my day in the sides of the grave, as if he was enlarging it and leveling it, and he came out of He buried her in her grave with tears in her eyes, and he dug in her grave. When he went, Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said to him: O Messenger of God, I saw you. You did something to this woman that you had never done to anyone. He said: “O Umar, this woman was my mother who gave birth to me. My father A student was doing something, and he was having a banquet, and he used to gather us over his food, and this woman was giving a share of it all. So I will return there, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, told me about my Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, that she is one of the people of Paradise, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, told me God Almighty commanded seventy thousand angels to pray over her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4574 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4575","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, and Ahmad bin Ja`far al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, Bukair bin Mismar told us, he said: I heard Amer. Ibn Saad says: Muawiyah said to Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with them: What prevents you from cursing Ibn Abi Talib? He said: So he said: I do not curse what I mentioned three things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him, because I have one of them more beloved to me than Red camels. Muawiyah said to him: What are they, Abu Ishaq? He said: I do not curse him as I mentioned when the revelation came down to him, so he took Ali and his two sons and Fatima and put them under his garment, then said: “My Lord, indeed These are my family.” And I do not curse him as I mentioned when he succeeded him in the Battle of Tabuk, which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded. Then Ali said to him: You left me behind with the boys and women. He said: “Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there will be no prophethood after me?” and I will not revile him. I did not mention the Day of Khaybar. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will give this banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God will grant victory to His hands.” We asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Where is Ali?” They said: It is Armad, so he said: “Call him.” So they called him and he spat in his face, then gave him the standard, so God granted him victory. He said: No, by God, he did not mention him. Muawiyah literally until he left Medina “This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it in this context, and they all agreed on Narrating the hadith of brotherhood and the hadith of the banner.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4575 - On the condition of a Muslim only"
"4576","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Handali told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Yahya told us Ibn Hammad, and Abu Bakr Muhammad Ibn Balawayh told me, and Abu Bakr Ahmad Ibn Ja’far Al-Bazzar told me, saying: Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad al-Hafiz told us. Al-Baghdadi, Khalaf bin Salem Al-Mukhurami told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Amash, he said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, On the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage and descended on Ghadir Khumm He ordered a group of people to stand up and say: “It is as if I had been called and responded. Indeed, I have left among you two weighty things: one of them is greater than the other, the Book of God Almighty. And my family, see how you succeed me in them, for they will not separate until they return to the basin.” Then he said: “Indeed, God Almighty is my master. And I am the master of every believer.” Then he took Ali’s hand, may God be pleased with him, and said: “Whoever I am the master of, this is his guardian. Oh God, protect him who is his guardian.” And he returned whoever had been hostile to him.” He mentioned the hadith in its length. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in its length. The hadith of Salamah bin Kuhail witnessed it, on the authority of Abu Tufayl. It is also authentic according to “Their condition”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4576 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4577","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Dalaj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated, Al-Azraq bin Ali narrated to us, Hassan narrated to us. Ibn Ibrahim Al-Kirmani, Muhammad Ibn Salamah Ibn Kuhayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Ibn Wathilah, that he heard Zayd Ibn Arqam May God be pleased with him, he says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, camped between Mecca and Medina, at the trees of five large piles of bones, and the people swept up what Under the trees, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went in the evening and prayed, then he stood up to deliver a sermon, and he thanked and praised God, and mentioned and preached. He said: What God willed that he should say: Then he said: “O people, I leave behind you two matters. You will not go astray if you follow them, and they are: the Book of God. “And my family, my family.” Then he said: “Do you know that I have more right to the believers than they do to themselves?” three times. They said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.” And the hadith of Buraydah Al-Aslami is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4577 - They were not narrated by Muhammad bin Salamah bin Kuhail, and Al-Saadi has distorted them."
"4578","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, and Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim told us Al-Ghifari, and Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amri told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, and Ahmad bin Yusuf told us, they said: Abu Nu’aym, Ibn Abi Ghaniyeh told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Buraydah Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, he said: I went with Ali to Yemen, and I saw a frown on his face, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned Ali and looked at him, and I saw the face of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed and said: “O Buraida, am I not more worthy of the believers than they are on their own selves?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.” He mentioned the hadith: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4578 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4579","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, my father and Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, they said: Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us. Al-Dhabi’i, on the authority of Yazid Al-Rashk, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a detachment, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, appointed Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, as his guardian. Ali went on in secrecy and had an affair with a slave girl. They denied this to him, so four people entered into a contract. From the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if we met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, we would tell him what Ali had done. Imran said: And it was When Muslims come from a journey, they start with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and look at him and greet him, then they depart to their journey. The group arrived and greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then one of the four stood up and said: O Messenger of God, did you not see that Ali did such-and-such? So he turned away from it, then the second stood up and said something like that, so he turned away from it, then the third stood up and said like that, so he turned away from it, then he got up Fourth, he said: O Messenger of God, did you not see that Ali did such-and-such, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, approached him with anger on his face. He said: “Whatever you want from Ali, Ali is from me, and I am from him, and the guardian of every believer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4579 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4580","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, “Ali bin Abi A student, may God be pleased with him, converted to Islam when he was ten years old.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4580 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4581","Abu Ishaq al-Muzaki and Abu al-Hussein al-Hafiz told me, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: “Ali greeted Ali when he was ten or sixteen years old.” This chain of narration. Better than the first, and I only put that forward because I rose above it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4581 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4582","Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Zahid, the owner of Tha’lab in Baghdad, told me. Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told me, Zakaria told me. Ibn Yahya Al-Masry, Al-Mufaddal Ibn Fadalah narrated to me, Samak Ibn Harb narrated to me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: “Perhaps Ali has four qualities that no one else has: He is the first Arab and non-Arab to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is the one whose standard “With him in every march, and he who was patient with him on the Day of Judgment, and it is he who washed him and took him into his grave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4582 - It contains Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Waqar and he is accused."
"4583","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Sukari told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Urni told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Divided, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, presented the banner to Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the day of Badr. He is twenty years old. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"4584","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amri told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Absi, they said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abbad Ibn Abdullah Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “I am the servant of God, and the brother of His Messenger, and I am the greatest friend. He will not say it after me.” Except he is a liar. I prayed seven years before the people, before anyone from this nation worshiped him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4584 - A false hadith, so consider it"
"4585","Shuaib bin Safwan, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Hibba bin Juwayn, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I worshiped God with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seven years before anyone from this nation worshiped him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4585 - This is false"
"4586","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Suhayb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: Abu Dharr and Nu’aym, Abu Dharr’s cousin, set off, and I was with them in search of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was The mountain was hidden, so Abu Dharr said: O Muhammad, we have come to you to hear what you say and what you call for, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I say no. There is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God.” So Abu Dharr and his companion believed in him and I believed in him, and Ali was in need of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He sent him there. A revelation was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Monday, and he prayed for Ali on Tuesday: “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4586 - True"
"4587","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abdul Rahman bin Bayhas Al-Mala’i told me, Ali bin Abbas narrated to me, on the authority of Muslim Al-Mulai, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was informed on Monday, He greeted Ali on Tuesday.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4587 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4588","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hammad Al-Murtadi told me, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Salih, the owner of the prayer hall, told us, Ali bin Salih told us, Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, who said: “Ali, may God be pleased with him, was killed. On Friday, the seventeenth night before the month of Ramadan, in the year forty, and his caliphate was five years minus three months, he killed him. Abd al-Rahman bin Muljim al-Muradi, on the day he was killed, was sixty-three years old, or sixty-four.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4588 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4589","I heard Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari, saying: I heard Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, saying: I heard Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, He says: “Ali bin Abi Talib ruled for five years, and he was killed in the year forty of the emigration of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was sixty-three years old.” A year ago, he was killed on a Friday, the twenty-first of the month of Ramadan, and he died on a Sunday and was buried in Kufa.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4589 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4590","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, he told me Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, that Abu Sinan al-Du’ali told him that he had visited Ali, may God be pleased with him. In a complaint he complained about, he said: So I said to him: We feared for you, O Commander of the Faithful, regarding this complaint of yours. He said: But I, by God, do not I feared for myself because of him, because I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the truthful and trustworthy, saying: “You will be struck here with a blow.” And a blow here - and he pointed to his temples - and its blood will flow until your beard is dyed, and its owner will be the most wretched of it, just as he was barren. “The camel is the most miserable of Thamud.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4590 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4591","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh al-Sahmi told us, Sa`id bin Ufayr told us, Hafs told me Ibn Imran Ibn Abi Al-Rassam, on the authority of Al-Sari Ibn Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I came to Damascus intending to invade, so I came to Abdul-Malik To greet him, and I found him in a dome on a mattress near the pillar, and under him were two blankets. So I greeted him, then I sat down, and he said to me: O Ibn Shihab, Do you know what happened in the Holy House on the morning that Ali bin Abi Talib was killed? So I said: Yes, and he said: Come on, so I got up from behind the people until I came behind the dome, and he turned his face to me, so he looked down at me and said: What happened? So I said: “Not a single stone was removed from the Holy House without blood being found underneath it.” He said: “There is no one left who knows this except me, and no one else has heard me.” “None of you.” I did not speak to him until he died.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4591 - And the news is mursal"
"4592","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told me, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Sulami told me, my uncle Muhammad told me Bin Hassan, Al-Hasan bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Saad Al-Qurashi, who said: “Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, was appointed successor He was thirty-five years old, and he was fifty-eight years and months old. When the season arrived in the year thirty-five, Abdullah bin Abbas was sent to The season of the year thirty-five, and the year thirty-seven, and the year thirty-eight, and the season arrived, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, was busy with the fighting. So the people came together to confront Shaybah ibn Uthman al-Hajabi, and he testified with the people. When it was forty years old, Ali was killed on a Friday, seventeen years ago. From the month of Ramadan, in the year forty, and he was sixty-three years old.” Al-Hakim said: “So we looked and found clear proof of these dates. With an authentic chain of narration”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4592 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4593","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Sari bin Yahya Al-Tamimi told us, Qubaysah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Najiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The mill of Islam revolves over thirty-five or thirty-six days. If they perish, then in the way of those who perished, and if their religion remains for them, then for seventy years.” Omar said: O Messenger of God, with what remains or with what has passed? He said: “With what remains.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"4594","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us: Dictating in Sha`ban of the year four hundred and two, he said: “There was a difference of opinion. The narrations at his time, so it was said: He was sold out four days after the killing of Othman, may God be pleased with him, and it was said after five, and it was said after three, It was said that the pledge of allegiance was made on Friday for the remaining five days of Dhu al-Hijjah, and it was said that the pledge of allegiance was given shortly after the killing of Othman in the house of Amr bin Muhammad al-Ansari, one of the sons of Amr bin Mabdhul, and the most correct narration is that he abstained from pledging allegiance until Uthman was buried, then pledged allegiance on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him openly, and the first one to pledge allegiance to him was Talha, and he said: This pledge of allegiance will be broken.”"
"4595","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi narrated to us, Waddah bin Yahya Al-Nahshali narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us. Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid Al-Nakha’i, who said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, was sold out on the pulpit of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Khuzaymah bin Thabit said while he was standing in front of the pulpit: “
 [Long Sea]
 If we pledged allegiance to Ali, it would suffice us... Abu Hassan, because we fear temptations.
 We found him to be the most worthy of people because...he was the most knowledgeable of the Quraysh with the Book and the Sunnahs.
 And indeed, the dust of Quraysh cannot be broken through... If one day it comes upon the body...
 And in it is that which is in them of all goodness...and in it is that which is in it of all that is good.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4595 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4596","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Al-Ala’ bin Salih told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rashid, who said: When Ali’s pledge of allegiance came to Hudhayfah, he said: “I will not pledge allegiance after him unless I become destitute or lose.” Al-Hakim said: “This is The reports contained in the pledge of allegiance to the Commander of the Faithful are all authentic and unanimously agreed upon. As for the statement of those who claimed that Abdullah bin Amr was the father of Masoud Al-Ansari, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Ansari, and Usama bin Zaid stayed away from I pledged allegiance to him, for this is the statement of the one who denies the reality of those conditions, so listen now to their reality.”"
"4597","Abu al-Qasim al-Hasan bin Muhammad al-Sakouni told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, a partner told us, On the authority of Abu Al-Sayrifi, on the authority of Abu Qubaisah, Omar bin Qubaisah, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: I saw Ali, may God be pleased with him, on a shabby saddlebag. With Al-Rabdha, and he was saying to Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein: “What do you have to do with Tahanan Hunayn the maid? By God, I have struck this matter back to stomach. So I found no choice but to fight the people, or to disbelieve in what was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4597 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4598","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us about the authenticity of his condition, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Bishr bin Shuaib bin Abu Hamzah Al-Qurashi, my father told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Hamzah bin Abdullah bin Omar told me that, while he was sitting with Abdullah Ibn Omar, when a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, by God, I have been keen to be like you. I follow your example in the matter of dividing people, and I shun evil as much as I can. Indeed, I am reading a decisive verse from the Book of God that has taken hold of my heart, so tell me. About her, did you see what God Almighty said: {And if two parties of the believers were killed, then make peace between them; but if one of them wrongs the other, So fight the one who transgresses until she complies with the command of God; but if she complies, then make peace between them with justice, and be fair. Indeed, God loves those who are just.} [Al-Hujurat: 9] Tell me about this verse. Abdullah said: What do you have to do with that? He left me, and he moved on until his darkness disappeared from us, and Abdullah bin Omar came to us and said: “I did not find anything in myself regarding this matter.” The verse: “I did not find in myself that I had not fought this transgressing group as God Almighty commanded me.” This is a big chapter that was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar is a group of major followers, but I presented the hadith of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and I confined myself to it because it is authentic. “According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4598 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4599","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad told us. Al-Dashtaki, Amr bin Abi Qais Al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, may God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with a group of some of his companions, so I and a man from the Ansar went ahead of us to the enemy, so I carried On a man. When I approached him, he said “Allahu Akbar,” so I stabbed him and killed him, and I saw that he had only done that to save his blood. When we returned, he preceded me to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, there is no knight better than yours. We were confronted by a man and he overtook me to him, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and he did not stop him. That is when he killed him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Osama, what did you do today?” So I said: I attacked a man, and he said “Allahu Akbar”, and I saw that he did so to save his blood, so I killed him. He said: “How can it be, after Allah is the Greatest? He turned his heart, so I said what he said. He continued to say to me on that day, “I will not fight a man who says, ‘God is greater than what he has forbidden me,’” until he met him, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said hello"
"4600","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ja`far ibn Nasr narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’a’a, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4599 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4601","So Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, Muslim told us Al-Mala'i, on the authority of Khaythamah bin Abdul Rahman, said: I heard Saad bin Malik, and a man said to him: Ali is falling for you, because you left him behind, so he said Saad: By God, it is an opinion I had, but my opinion was wrong. Ali bin Abi Talib was given three things, because if I was given one of them, he would be dearer to me. Of this world and what is in it, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him on the day of Ghadir Khumm, after thanking God and praising him: “Do you know that I Am I more deserving of the believers? We said: Yes. He said: “O God, whomever I am his master, then Ali is his master, and the guardian of whoever supports him, and he who antagonizes him who antagonizes him.” And he was brought on the Day of Khaybar while he was He became blind until he could see, so he said: O Messenger of God, I am blind. So he spit in his eyes and prayed for him, but he did not blink until he was killed, and Khaybar was conquered against him and he was taken out. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his uncle Al-Abbas and another mosque, so Al-Abbas said to him: You will take us out, and we are your clan and your general, and you will live there. Aliyah? He said: “I did not bring you out and put it to rest, but God brought you out and put it to rest.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4601 - Al-Hakim remained silent about his correction"
"4602","So Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Dawud bin Rasheed told us, Al-Haytham bin Adi told us, on the authority of Mujalid, Ibn Ayyash, and Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: “When Uthman was killed and Ali, may God be pleased with them both, was pledged allegiance, he delivered a speech. Abu Musa, while he was in Kufa, forbade people from fighting and engaging in sedition, so Ali removed him from Kufa, from Dhi Qar, and Ammar sent him Ibn Yasir and Al-Hassan Ibn Ali dismissed him, and he employed Qardhah Ibn Ka’b, and he continued to work until Ali came from Basra months later and dismissed him. Then, when he went to Siffin, he succeeded Uqba bin Amr Aba Masoud Al-Ansari, who had come from Siffin.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4602 - Al-Haytham bin Adi is abandoned"
"4603","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari and Abu Masoud Al-Badri entered upon Ammar while he was mobilizing the people, and they said to him: “What did we see? I have done something from you since you converted to Islam that is more objectionable to us than your haste in this matter.” Ammar said: I have not seen anything from you since you converted to Islam. I hate for you to delay you in this matter. He said: So Ammar dressed them in a uniform, and went out to pray on Friday.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4603 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4604","So Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Salem Bin Saleh bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Labid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Maslamah, who said: I said: Oh Messenger of God, what should I do if the worshipers disagree? He said: “You go out with your sword to the free woman and strike her with it, then you enter your house until a fatal death comes to you, or a sinful hand.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4604 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4605","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Ibrahim bin Jafar Al-Ansari told me, Sulayman bin Muhammad, from the descendants of Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Ansari, told me on the authority of Saad bin Zaid bin Saad Al-Ashli, that he presented as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sword from Najran, and when he came to him, he gave it to Muhammad bin Maslama, and he said: “Strive with this for the sake of God, and when you break people’s throats, hit the stone with it, then enter your house, and lie down until it kills you.” A wrong hand, or a decisive death will come to you.” Al-Hakim said: “For these reasons and similar reasons, the retreat of the one who has withdrawn from fighting has come With Ali, may God be pleased with him, and fighting those who fought him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4605 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4606","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Musa told us, meaning Israel bin Musa said: I heard Al-Hasan saying: “Talha and Al-Zubayr came to Basra, and the people said to them: What has come to you? They said: We ask for the blood of Othman. Al-Hasan said: Oh, Glory be to God. Did the people not have minds to say: By God, Othman did not kill anyone but you? He said: When Ali came to Kufa, and the people had no sense, they said: O man, by God, we do not guarantee you.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4606 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4607","So Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Yusuf, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Mus’ab, he said: Musa Ibn Uqba told me, he said: Alqamah Ibn Waqqas Al-Laythi said: When Talha went out Al-Zubayr and Aisha were asking for the blood of Othman, may God be pleased with them all. Aisha was the people’s fiancée, and they were her followers, so they turned away. Those with them of the same race looked down on Urwa bin Al-Zubayr and Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, so they turned them away. He said: And I saw Talha, the most beloved of his gatherings. He left it, while stroking his falsehood with his beard. He said: So I said to him: O Abu Muhammad, I see you. And your favorite gathering is the one where you are stroking your beard over your head. If you hate this matter, then leave it, for he will not force you to do it. Uhud, he said: “O Alqamah bin Waqqas, do not blame me. Yesterday we were one hand against everyone else, but today we have become two mountains of iron, crawling along.” ""One of us to his friend""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4607 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4608","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri narrated to me, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to me, Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to me, Humaid Al-Taweel narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: God protected me from something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Khosrau died. He said: “Who did they leave behind?” They said: His daughter. He said: Then he said: “A people will not succeed if they have a woman in charge of their affairs.” He said: When Aisha came, she mentioned the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so God protected me through him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4608 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4609","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, I am Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hisham, And Qais, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I wish I had been bereaved of ten like Al-Harith ibn Hisham, and that I had not continued my journey with Ibn Al-Zubayr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4609 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4610","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ward, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned the emergence of Some of the mothers of the believers, and Aisha laughed, so he said: “Wait, O Humayra, lest it be you.” Then he turned to Ali and said: “If you are appointed by command her to do anything, so be kind to her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4610 - Abdul Jabbar did not go out to him"
"4611","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me from the origin of his book, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told me, Abdullah bin Salih told us Al-Azdi, Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Al-Asbahani told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim Al-Makki, on the authority of Amra bint Abdul Rahman, who said: When Ali walked to Basra. He went to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bid her farewell. She said: “Walk in God’s protection and in His protection, for by God Indeed, you are upon the truth: and the truth is with you: and had it not been that I hate to disobey God and His Messenger: then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded us to acknowledge Our homes, I would have walked with you: But by God, I will certainly send with you someone who is better than me and dearer to me than myself. Ibn Umar. These three hadiths All of them are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4611 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4612","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri narrated to us, Ismail bin Musa Al-Suddi narrated to us, Abd al-Salam bin Harb narrated to us, Ismail bin Abi narrated to us. Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: Al-Zubair came to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, asking him for permission to fight, and Omar said: “Sit in the Your house, for you have invaded with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: He repeated that to him, and Omar said to him on the third or the following day: “Sit in Your house. By God, I find at the edge of the city that you and your companions are going out and wreaking havoc on the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4612 - True"
"4613","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: When Aisha, may God be pleased with her, reached some of the homes of Banu Amir, dogs barked at her, and she said: What water is this? They said: Al-Haw'ab. She said: I don't think I'm anything but returning. Al-Zubair said: Not yet. Go forward and the people will see you, and God will reconcile matters between them. She said: What? I think I am only returning. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “How about one of you when the dogs of the Haw’ab barked at her?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4613 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4614","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra bin Yarim, and Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: When we left Mecca, the daughter of Hamza, and she called: O uncle, O uncle, so I took her hand and gave it to Fatima. I said: Without you, your cousin’s daughter. When we came to Medina, we quarreled there. Me, Zaid, and Ja’far, so I said: I took her and she is my cousin. He said: Zaid is my brother’s daughter, and Ja’far said: My cousin’s daughter and her paternal aunt is with me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ja’far: “You resemble me in character and character,” and he said to Zaid: “You are our brother and our protector,” and he said to me: “You From me and I from you, give her to her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is a mother.” So I said: Will you not marry her, O Messenger of God? He said: “She is my breastfeeding brother’s daughter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with these words. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of my father. Ishaq, briefly on the authority of Al-Bara’
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4614 - True"
"4615","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, and she said to me: Is the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, reviled among you? So I said: God forbid, or Glory be to God, or a word similar to it. She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever curses Ali has “He cursed me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Bukayr bin Uthman Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, with additional wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4615 - True"
"4616","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Hafiz narrated to us in Hamdan, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ishaq al-Taymi narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waqiq narrated to us, Bukair ibn al-Qaq narrated to us. Othman Al-Bajli said: I heard Abu Ishaq Al-Tamimi say: I heard Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali say: I performed Hajj when I was a boy, so I passed In Medina, and behold, the people were one group, so I followed them, and they entered upon Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard her saying: O Shabib b. A quarter, then a rude man answered her: At your command, my mothers. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is insulted in your club? He said: How did that happen? She said: Ali bin Abi Talib. He said: We say things that we want to protect the world from. She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever reviles Ali has reviled me, and whoever reviles me has reviled God Almighty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4616 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4617","Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Shaybani informed us of the origin of his book. Ali bin Saeed bin Bashir Al-Razi, in Egypt, told us Al-Hasan bin Hammad told us. Al-Hadrami, Yahya bin Ya’la told us, Bassam Al-Sayrifi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Tha’labah, on the authority of Abu Dharr Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever obeys Ali He has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys Ali has disobeyed me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4617 - True"
"4618","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tamim al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told me, Abu Asim told me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Ma’mal, Abu told me Bakr bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of his father, who said: A man from the people of the Levant came and insulted Ali in the presence of Ibn Abbas, but Ibn Abbas counted him. He said: “O enemy of God, you have harmed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. {Indeed, those who harm God and His Messenger, may God curse them in this world and the hereafter, and He has prepared For them is a humiliating punishment.} [Al-Ahzab: 57] If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were alive, I would have harmed him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4618 - True"
"4619","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zur’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, and we told him Ahmad bin Ja`far al-Bazzar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Aban Ibn Salih, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Maqil Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Nayyar Al-Aslami, on the authority of Amr Ibn Shas Al-Aslami, who was one of the people of Al-Hudaybiyyah, said: We went out with Ali, may God be pleased with him, to Yemen, and he exhausted me during his journey until I found in Myself, when I came, I made his complaint known in the mosque until it reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So I entered the mosque one morning. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among some of his Companions. When he saw me, he showed me his eyes. He said: He fixed his gaze on me until I sat down. He said: “Oh Amr, by God, you have harmed me. I said: I seek refuge in God lest I harm you, O Messenger of God. He said: Yes, whoever harms Ali has harmed me. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4619 - True"
"4620","Abdan bin Yazid bin Yaqoub Al-Daqqaq told us, from the origin of his book, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Abu Nu’aym Dirar bin Surad told us, Muammar bin Suleiman told us, he said: I heard my father mentioning, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said To Ali: “You will clarify for my nation that about which they differed after me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4620 - Rather, it is, in my opinion, a harmful situation"
"4621","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa from the origin of his book. Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, he said: Ibn Abi Gharza, and Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Fitr bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him. He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his sandal broke, so Ali stayed behind to fix it. He walked for a little while and then said: “Indeed, among you is someone who fights.” “On the interpretation of the Qur’an just as I fought for its revelation.” Then the people looked forward to her, and among them were Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, Abu Bakr said. Bakr: I am he. He said: “No.” Omar said: “I am him.” He said: “No, but the one who wears the sandal” - meaning Ali - so we came to him and gave him good tidings, but he did not raise it. He shook his head as if he had heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4621 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4622","Abu Qutaibah Salem bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami told me, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, my uncle Abu Bakr told us, Ali bin Thabit Al-Dahhan, Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasira, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called me and said: “O Ali, there is among you an example of Jesus, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him. The Jews hated him to the point of They astonished his mother and the Christians loved him until they put him in a position that he was not in.” He said: And Ali said: “Except that he will perish in a place of rain.” He confuses me with what I am not, and he is a hateful and slanderer, who is driven by my affairs to slander me. Indeed, I am not a prophet, nor has anything been revealed to me, but I act according to a book. God, and the Sunnah of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as much as I am able, so whatever I have commanded you to do in terms of obedience to God Almighty, it is incumbent upon you to obey me in whatever you like or You hated it, and I did not command you to disobey me or others. There is no obedience to anyone in disobeying God Almighty, but obedience only in what is right.” “Sahih chain of narration.” And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4622 - Al-Hakam bin Abdul Malik and Hah Ibn Ma’in"
"4623","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ahmad bin Sahl told us The jurist, in Bukhara, Abu Ismah Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil Al-Bukhari told us, Affan and Suleiman bin Harb told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Abi al-Tufayl, I think it is on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said to me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O Ali, you have treasure in Paradise, and you are the one with its two horns, so do not follow one look with another, for you will have the better of it.” “The Hereafter is not yours.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4623 - True"
"4624","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Umair told us, Aamir bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf Dawud ibn Abi Awf, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Tha’labah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “O Ali, whoever separates from me has separated from God, and whoever separates from you, O Ali, has separated from me” with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4624 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"4625","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Hafs Omar bin Al-Hassan Al-Rasibi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali “Master of the Arabs” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by Umar bin Al-Hasan, and I hope that it is truthful. If it were not for that, I would have ruled It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it has evidence from the hadith of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4625 - I think that it is he, meaning Omar bin Hassan Al-Rasibi, who wrote this"
"4626","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Qari told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Nasih told us, Al-Hussein bin Alwan told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Call for me the master of the Arabs.” So I said: Oh Messenger of God, are you not the master of the Arabs? He said: “I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.”"
"4627","There is another witness to it from the hadith of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Call for me the master of the Arabs.” Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said. On her behalf: Are you not the master of the Arabs, O Messenger of God? He said: “I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4626 - Posted by Ibn Alwan"
"4628","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha Al-Qannad told us, Al-Thiqah Al-Ma’mun told us, Ali bin Hashim bin Al-Barid, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Sa’id Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Abu Thabit, the servant of Abu Dharr, who said: I was with Ali, may God be pleased with him. May God protect him on the Day of Camel. When I saw Aisha standing, some people entered me as people enter, so God revealed that to me at the noon prayer, so I fought. With the Commander of the Faithful. When he finished, I went to Medina and went to Umm Salamah and said: By God, I did not come to ask for food or drink, but I A slave of Abu Dharr, and she said: Welcome, so I told her my story, and she said: Where were you when hearts flew their rain? I said: To where God revealed that about me at noon. He said: Well done. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Ali is with the Qur’an.” “And the Qur’an is with Ali. They will not separate until they come to the basin.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and Abu Sa’id al-Taymi is a trustworthy person. Safe, but they did not expel him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4628 - True"
"4629","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Al-Mukhtar bin Nafi’ Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Hayyan told us Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God have mercy on Ali, O God, turn the truth with him where it is.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4629 - Mukhtar bin Nafi’ has fallen"
"4630","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hani, Al-Adl told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, about Abdullah bin Amr bin Hind Al-Jamali said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: “When I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He gave it to me, and if I remained silent, he would start it with me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4630 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4631","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ja`far, narrated by Awf, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, who said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had doors A street in the mosque. One day he said: “Close these doors except the door of Ali.” He said: Then some people spoke about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up. He greeted God, praised God, and praised Him, then said: “As for what follows: I have been commanded to block these gates except the gate of Ali,” and your speaker said about it, By God, I did not block anything or open it, but I was ordered to do something and I followed it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4631 - True"
"4632","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Isfaraini told me, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Al-Baraa told me, Ali bin Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Madini, my father told us, Suhail bin Abi Saleh told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Ali bin Abi Talib was given three qualities, because having one of them is dearer to me than being given red camels. It was said: And what are they, oh? Commander of the Faithful? He said: “He married him to Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he lived in the mosque with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it was permissible for him to do anything therein.” It is permissible for him, and the banner is on the Day of Khaybar.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4632 - Rather, Al-Madani Abdullah bin Jaafar is weak"
"4633","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Al-Nufaili told us, Zuhayr told us, Abu Ishaq told us, Othman said, Ali bin Hakim Al-Awdi and Amr bin Awn Al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Qatham Ibn Al-Abbas: How did Ali, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inherit from you instead of you? He said: “Because he was kind to him, and we were kind to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4633 - True"
"4634","I heard the chief judge, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Saleh Al-Hashimi, saying: I heard Abu Omar Al-Qadi saying: I heard Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi saying: This statement of Qutham was mentioned to him, and he said: “The heir inherits only by lineage or loyalty, and there is no disagreement among the people of knowledge that the cousin does not He inherits with the paternal uncle. It has been shown by this consensus that Ali inherited knowledge from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the exclusion of them, and with the validity of what the judge mentioned.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4634 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4635","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Ali used to say during the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God says: {And if he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?} [Al Imran: 144] By God, we will not turn back on our heels after God has guided us. Whether he dies or is killed, I will fight for what he fought for until I die. By God, I am his brother, his guardian, his cousin, and the heir of his knowledge. Who has more right to him? ""from me""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4635 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4636","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Yahya bin Salamah told us. Ibn Kuhayl, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said In a sermon he delivered during the Farewell Hajj: “I will kill the giants in a battalion,” and Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him: Or Ali? He said: “Or Ali bin Abi Talib»
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4636 - Ismail bin Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhail and his father were abandoned."
"4637","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahim Al-Harawi told us, in Ramla, Abu Al-Salt Abdul-Salam bin Salih told us, Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I am a city “Knowledge and Ali is its gate, so whoever wants the city, let him go to the gate.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And Abu Al-Salt is trustworthy.” Safe. For I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub in history saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I asked Yahya bin Ma’in about my father. Al-Harawi prayed, and he said: “Trustworthy.” So I said: Wasn’t it narrated on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, “I am the city of knowledge”? He said: It was narrated by Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Faidi, and he is trustworthy and trustworthy. I heard Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl, the jurist al-Qabbani, the imam of his time in Bukhara, saying: I heard Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz He says: He was asked about Abu al-Salt al-Harawi, and he said: Yahya ibn Ma’in and we were with him entered Abu al-Salt and greeted him, and when he left, I followed him. So I said to him: What do you say, may God have mercy on you, about Abu Al-Salt? He said: “He is truthful.” So I told him: He narrates the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “I am the city of knowledge, and Ali Its gate, so whoever wants knowledge, let him come to it through its gate.” He said: This and that Al-Faidi narrated, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, as Narrated by Abu Al-Salt
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4637 - Rather, it is subject"
"4638","He told us correctly, what Imam Abu Zakaria mentioned, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Al-Hussein bin Fahim, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Al-Dharais told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Faidi told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I am the city of knowledge, and Ali is its gate. So whoever wants the city, Let him come to the door.” Al-Hussein bin Fahm said. Abu Al-Salt Al-Harawi told us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah. Al-Hakim said: “So that the beneficiary of this may know.” Know that Al-Hussein bin Fahm bin Abdul-Rahman is trustworthy, trustworthy and a memorizer.” This hadith is supported by the hadith of Sufyan Al-Thawri with a chain of transmission. That's right
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4638 - Ahmed bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Harrani This is a liar and a charlatan."
"4639","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali, the jurist and imam al-Shashi al-Qaffal, spoke to me in Bukhara, and I asked him. An-Nu’man ibn al-Harun al-Baladi told me, In a country, from the origin of his book, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Harrani told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bahman al-Taymi, said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “I am the city of knowledge, and Ali is its gate. Whoever wants knowledge, let him come to the gate.”"
"4640","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad bin Salamah and Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qatabani told us, and Abu Al-Hasan told me Ahmad bin Al-Khidr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Umayyah Al-Qurashi, with the name of the driver, Ahmed bin Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Halwani told us, they said: Abu Al-Azhar told us, and Abu Ali Al-Muzaki told us, On the authority of Abu Al-Azhar, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at me and said: “O Ali, you are a master in this world, a master in the hereafter, your beloved is my beloved, and my beloved Beloved of God, and your enemy is my enemy, and my enemy is the enemy of God, and woe to whoever hates you after me.” Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, “and Abu Al-Azhar Their consensus is trustworthy, and if trustworthy is specific to a hadith then it is authentic according to their origin.” I heard Abu Abdullah Al-Qurashi say: I heard Ahmad b. Yahya Al-Halwani says: “When Abu Al-Azhar came from Sana’a and reminded the people of Baghdad of this hadith, Yahya bin Mu’in denied it. When it was the day of his session, he said at the end of the session: “Where is this Naysaburi liar who narrated this hadith on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq? Then Abu Al-Azhar stood up and said: Here I am. Yahya bin Ma’in laughed at his statement and his standing in the gathering, so he brought him closer and closer to him, then He said to him: How did Abdul Razzaq tell you this, and he did not tell anyone else about it? He said: I know, O Abu Zakaria, that I came to Sana’a while Abd al-Razzaq was absent in a village of his far away, so I went out to him while I was ill. When I reached him, he asked me about the matter of Khurasan, so I told him about it and wrote about it, and I left with him to Sana’a. When I bade him farewell, he said to me: Your rights are obligatory upon me. I am telling you a hadith that no one else has heard from me. So, by God, he narrated this hadith to me, verbally, and Yahya ibn al-Khattab confirmed it. A certain person and apologized to him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4640 - Munkar is not far from the situation"
"4641","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Suleiman Al-Baransi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Yahya bin Ya’la told us, Bassam told us Al-Sayrifi, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Tha’labah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him, to Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever obeys you He has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys you has disobeyed me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4641 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4642","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, with Marwa, Ishaq told us, Al-Qasim bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Ya’la Al-Aslami told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He wants to live my life, die my death, and reside in the eternal Paradise that my Lord promised me, so let Ali bin Abi Talib be my guardian, for he will not “He will bring you out of guidance, and will never lead you into error.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not bring it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4642 - It is closer to the situation"
"4643","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Hafiz told us, in Hamadan, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Fasawi told us, Ishaq bin Bishr Al-Kahili told us, a partner told us, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We did not know the hypocrites except by their denial of God.” and His Messenger, and neglecting prayers, and hating Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4643 - Rather, Ishaq bin Bishr is accused of lying"
"4644","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali, the jurist and imam of Shashi, told me in Bukhara. Al-Nu’man bin Harun Al-Baladi told me, Abu Ja’far Ahmad bin Abd told me. Allah bin Yazid Al-Harrani, Abdul Razzaq told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Bahman He said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was holding the hyena of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, as he said: “This is the prince of righteousness, the killer of immorality, saved by him who helped him, abandoned by whoever let him down,” then he extended In his voice: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4644 - Indeed, by God, it is fabricated"
"4645","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Sufyan Al-Tirmidhi told us, Surayj bin Yunus told us, Abu Hafs told us Al-Abar, narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Fatima, may God be pleased with her, said: O Messenger of God, You married me to Ali bin Abi Talib, and he was poor and had no money. He said: “O Fatima, are you not satisfied that God Almighty has looked at the people of The land, so two men chose, one of them was your father, and the other was your husband.” Abu al-Salt Abd al-Salam bin Salih told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us on the authority of Muammar, On the authority of Abu Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Fatima said: You married me to a family member who had no money. He mentioned something similar, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4645 - Rather, it is subject
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4645 - Rather, it is subject"
"4646","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Hussein bin Hassan Al-Ashqar told us, Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali: {It is only you A warner, and to every people there is a guide.} [Al-Ra’ad: 7] Ali said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the warner, and I am the guide.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4646 - Rather, the ugliness of God who created it is a lie"
"4647","Mukarram bin Ahmad bin Mukarram Al-Qadi told us, Ja’far bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hussein Al-Ashqar told us, Ja’far bin Ziyad Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was angry, he would not “None of us dares to speak to him other than Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4647 - Al-Ashqar was trustworthy, and Ibn Adi accused him, and Ja’far spoke about it."
"4648","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri told me, in Baghdad, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Awwam Al-Riyahi told us, Abu Zaid Saeed bin Aws told us Al-Ansari, narrated by Auf, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, who said: A man said to Salman: How intense is your love for Ali? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Whoever loves Ali has loved me, and whoever hates Ali has hated me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4648 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4649","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Isbahani told us, Sharik told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Al-Aswad bin Amir and Abdullah bin Numayr told us, they said: A partner told us, On the authority of Abu Rabi’ah Al-Iyadi, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has commanded me to love four My friends, and he told me that he loves them.” He said: We said: Who are they, O Messenger of God? And we all would love to be one of them. He said: “But Ali is one of them.” Then he remained silent. Then he said: “Ali is one of them,” then he remained silent. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4649 - Muslim did not narrate to Abu Rabi’ah"
"4650","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me. Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ayyub Al-Saffar and Humaid bin Yunus bin Yaqoub Al-Zayyat reported, saying: Thana Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ayadh bin Abi Taybah, my father told us, Yahya bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I was serving the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a grilled chicken was presented to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Oh God, bring me the most beloved of your creation to eat with me from this bird.” He said: So I said: Oh God, make him a man from the Ansar, so Ali came. May God be pleased with him, so I said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is on a need. Then he came, and I said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is on a need. Then he came, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Open.” So he entered, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What kept you from me?” So he said: This is The last three times, Anas came to me, claiming that you were in need. He said: “What made you do what you did?” So I said: O Messenger of God, I heard your supplication, so I would love for him to be a man from my people. Then the Messenger of God said: “Indeed, a man may love his people.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated on the authority of Anas by a group of his companions, in excess of thirty people, then the narration was authentic.” On the authority of Ali and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri and Safina, and in the hadith of Thabit Al-Bunani on the authority of Anas, an increase in words
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4650 - Ibn Iyad I do not know him"
"4651","As the trustworthy Al-Ma’mun Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Aliya bin Khaled Al-Sakouni, in Kufa, from the original of his book, Ubaid bin Kathir Al-Amiri told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Dubais told us, and Abu Al-Qasim told us, Muhammad told us Bin Abdullah bin Suleiman Al-Hadrami, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban bin Saleh told us, they said: Ibrahim bin Thabit Al-Basri Al-Qassar told us, said: Thabit Al-Bunani said that Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, was complaining, so Muhammad bin Al-Hajjaj came to visit him among his companions, and the conversation continued until They mentioned Ali, may God be pleased with him, and Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj snubbed him, and Anas said: Who is this? They made me sit, and they made him sit, and he said: O son of al-Hajjaj, do I not see you criticizing Ibn Abi Talib, the one who sent Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the truth? I was the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before him, and every day a boy from the sons of Ansar, that day was my day, and the mother of Ayman, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came with a bird and placed it in the hands of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Umm Ayman, what is this bird?” She said: I caught this bird and made it for you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You and to me.” This bird eats with me.” He knocked on the door, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Anas, look who is at the door.” I said: Oh God. Make him a man from the Ansar. So I went and saw Ali at the door. I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is on a need. So I came until I got up. From my position, I did not wait until he knocked on the door and said: “O Anas, look who is at the door.” So I said: Oh God, make him a man from the Ansar. So I went and saw Ali at the door. I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is on a need, so I came until I took my place, and it was not long before he was struck. The door, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Anas, go and enter it, for you are not the first man to love his people who is not one of the Ansar.” So I went and brought him in, and he said: “O Anas, bring him the bird.” He said: So I placed it in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they all ate. Muhammad bin Al-Hajjaj said: O Anas, was this in your presence? He said: Yes, he said: “I make a covenant with God that I will not disparage Ali after this position, and I do not know of anyone who disparages him without making his face white for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4651 - Ibrahim bin Thabit has fallen"
"4652","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jaafar ibn Hamdan al-Quta’i informed us of Baghdad from the origin of his book. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, My father told me, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, Abu Balaj told us, Amr bin Maymun told us, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas, when Nine people came to him and said: O Ibn Abbas, either stay with us or leave us alone among these people. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Abbas: Rather, I will stand with you. He said: And he will be healthy on that day before he becomes blind. He said: So they began and talked, but we do not know what they said. He said: Then he began to shake off his garment and said: Oops and Oops. They found a man who had ten virtues that no one else had. They came across a man to whom the Prophet said, “Pray.” May God bless him and grant him peace: “I will certainly send a man whom God will never disgrace, who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger will love.” So a man looked forward to her. He said: “Where is Ali?” They said: He was grinding in the mill. He said: “And none of them would grind.” He said: Then he came while he was gray-haired and could hardly see. He said: So he blew on him. His eyes, then he shook the banner three times and gave it to him, so Ali brought Safiyya bint Huyay. Ibn Abbas said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent And he greeted so-and-so with Surat Al-Tawbah, so he sent Ali to succeed him and took it from him.And he said: “No one will do it except a man who is from me and I from him.” Ibn Abbas said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his cousins: “Which one of you?” Will he be loyal to me in this world and the hereafter?” He said: And Ali was sitting with them, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, approached one of them and said: “Which of you will be my friend in this world?” And the afterlife? They refused, so he said to Ali: “You are my guardian in this world and the hereafter.” Ibn Abbas said: Ali was the first of the people to believe after Khadija. May God be pleased with her. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his garment and placed it on Ali, Fatima, Hassan, and Hussein, and said: “{He only wants May God remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and purify you with a thorough purification} [Al-Ahzab: 33]. Ibn Abbas said: “And Ali saw himself, so he put on a garment The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he slept in his place.” Ibn Abbas said, “The polytheists were accusing the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he came Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, while Ali was sleeping. He said: And Abu Bakr thought that he was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he said: O Prophet God, so Ali said to him: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set off towards Bir Maimun and overtook it. He said: So Abu Bakr set off and entered with him. laurel,He said: And Ali, may God be pleased with him, started throwing stones just as the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw stones while he was starving, and he wrapped his head in The garment did not take him out until morning, then he uncovered his head, and they said: You are a mean person, and your companion was not starving, and we threw him away, and you You are starving and we have denounced that.” Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the Battle of Tabuk and took the people with him. He said: Then Ali said to him: Should I go out with you? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “No.” Then Ali cried and said to him: “Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses except that there is no prophet after me? I will go unless you are my successor.” Ibn Abbas said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You are the guardian of every believing man and believing woman after me.” Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, blocked the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali, so he used to enter the mosque from the side, which is his way and not He has a different path.” Ibn Abbas said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever I am his master, his master is Ali,” Ibn Abbas said. Abbas: God Almighty told us in the Qur’an that He was pleased with the people of the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts.Did he tell us that he was angry with them after that? Ibn Abbas said: And the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Omar, may God be pleased with him, when He said: Give me permission to behead him. He said: “And you were a doer, and how do you know? Perhaps God had looked at the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want: “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.” The only master, Abu Ya’la Hamza bin Muhammad al-Zaidi, may God be pleased with him, told us On his authority, Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Mahrawih Al-Qazwini Al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Hatim Al-Razi, saying: “It was astonishing for them to They find the virtues from the narration of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4652 - True"
"4653","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Saleh, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said on the day of Badr to me and Abu Bakr: “On the right hand of one of you is Gabriel, The other is Mikael, and Israfil is a great king who witnesses the fight and is in the ranks.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4653 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4654","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, On the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar Abu Tuwala Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Muhammad bin Ka’b. Ibn Ajra, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: Ali Ibn Abi Talib complained about the people to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he stood up among us as a preacher, and I heard him say: “O people, do not complain about Ali, for by God, he is the most fearful in God’s essence and in his For the sake of God” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4654 - True"
"4655","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Al-Khalil Al-Qushayri told us, Kathir bin Yahya told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Which of you will take care of me in this world and the hereafter?” So he said to each of them: “Will they take care of me in this world and the hereafter?” He said: No, until he passed by most of them, and Ali said: I take care of you in this world and the hereafter, so he said: “You are my guardian in this world and the hereafter.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4655 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4656","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “We were talking about the people of Medina having killed Ali bin Abi Talib. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4656 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4657","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Sa’id bin Muhammad al-Warraq told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hazour said: I heard Abu Maryam Al-Thaqafi saying: I heard Ammar bin Yasser, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says to Ali: “O Ali, blessed is he who loves you and believes in you, and woe is he who hates you and lies about you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4657 - Rather, Saeed and Ali are abandoned"
"4658","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told me, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, I am a young man, and a judgment is coming to me about which I have no knowledge. He said: Then he put his hand on my chest and said: “O God, make his tongue firm and guide his heart.” I did not doubt the ruling or the ruling after “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4658 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4659","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa, Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Ibrahim bin Musa told me, Issa bin Yunus told us, Al-Ajlah told us, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, who said: While I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from The people of Yemen, so he began speaking to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informing him. He said: O Messenger of God, three people came to Ali, may God be pleased with him. They were disputing about a child. They had intercourse with a woman during one period of purity, so he said: Two people had a good heart for this child, then he said: You are partners. You are quarreling. Indeed, I am casting lots among you. For whomever lots are drawn for, he will have the child, and he must pay two-thirds of the blood money for his two companions. So he cast lots among them, and it was drawn for one of them. So he pushed the boy to him and said: “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed until his molars became visible.” Or, he said: his molars."
"4660","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Ajlah told us this, and he added to it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I don’t know about it except what Ali said.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” The hadith was further confirmed by the narration of Ibn Uyaynah, and Abu Ishaq Al-Subai’i followed Al-Ajlah in his narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4659 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4661","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told us, he said: My grandfather Muawiyah ibn Amr, Zaida told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I walked with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted a woman and she slaughtered a sheep for us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let a man from the people of Paradise enter.” So Abu Bakr entered. May God be pleased with him. Then he said: “Let a man from the people of Paradise enter.” Omar, may God be pleased with him, entered, then he said: “Let a man from the people of Paradise enter.” Paradise, O God, if You wish, make him exalted.” He said: Then Ali bin Abi Talib entered, may God be pleased with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4661 - True"
"4662","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Hatim Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Muaddeb told us, Saif bin Muhammad told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, On the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The first of you Coming to the basin, the first of you to embrace Islam is Ali bin Abi Talib.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4662 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4663","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, said: “The first to embrace Islam was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission,” “But the disagreement regarding this letter is that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq was satisfied May God bless him and grant him peace. He was the first of the men to become a Muslim, and Ali bin Abi Talib converted to Islam before he reached puberty.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4663 - True"
"4664","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Kathir bin Yahya told us, Abu Awanah Daoud told us. Ibn Abi Awf, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Ziyad, that he heard Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Nawfal say: Abu Saeed Al-Khudri told us May God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon Fatima, may God be pleased with her, and said: “You and I and this sleeper - meaning Ali - and they are - Meaning, Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein - they will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4664 - True"
"4665","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, Malik bin Dinar narrated to us, saying: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr and said: O Abu Abdullah, who was the bearer of the banner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He looked at me and said: It is as if you are easy-going. So I got angry and complained to his fellow reciters, so I said: Aren’t you surprised by Saeed? I asked him who was the bearer of the standard of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked at me and said: You are of a gentle mind. They said: You asked him. He was afraid of Al-Hajjaj, and he took refuge in the house. So I asked him now, and he said: “The one who carried it was Ali, may God be pleased with him.” This is how I heard him. From Abdullah bin Abbas: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” There is evidence for this hadith from the hadith of Zanfal al-Urfi, and it contains a length of film. Take him out
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4665 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4666","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Shihab bin Abbad told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Al-Hasan told us Ibn Hayy, on the authority of Abu Rabi’ah Al-Ayadi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Paradise longs for three Ali And Ammar and Salman: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4666 - True"
"4667","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us in Nishapur, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Uqba bin Qubaysah, my father told me, Ammar bin Saif told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I asked my Lord Almighty not to marry anyone from my nation, nor to marry unless he was with me in Paradise and He gave me.” This hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4667 - True"
"4668","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Amr bin Al-Husayn Al-Uqaili narrated to us, Yahya bin Al-Ala’ al-Razi narrated to us, narrated to us Hilal bin Abi Humaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin As’ad bin Zurarah, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It was revealed to me in Ali has three things: He is the master of the Muslims, the imam of the pious, and the leader of the green-haired. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4668 - I consider it fabricated"
"4669","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Issa Al-Subaie informed me, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Jizzi told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan Al-Ashqar told us, Saeed told us Ibn Khathim Al-Hilali, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Yasar Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talha, he said: We performed Hajj and passed on to Al-Hasan Ibn Ali. In Medina, and with us was Muawiyah bin Hudayj, and it was said to Al-Hasan: This is Muawiyah bin Hudayj who insulted Ali, so he said: Ali, so he was brought, and he said: “Are you the one who insulted Ali?” He said: What you did, so he said: “By God, if you meet him - and I do not think you will meet him on the Day of Resurrection - you will find him standing over the basin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He will defend from him the banners of the hypocrites, with a staff of thorns in his hand.” The truthful and trustworthy, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to me, and he who slanders will be disappointed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4669 - Rather, it is reprehensible and false"
"4670","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah, and Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Nadr told us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: A messenger said to me God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O Ali, shall I not teach you some words that, if you say them, God will forgive you for the fact that He will forgive you: There is no god but God the Most High. The Great, there is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4670 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4671","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaybah told us, he said: Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: By the one by which I swear, if Ali Because of the closest of people to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We visited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the morning before, and he was saying: “Ali has come?” Ali came? Repeatedly, Fatima, may God be pleased with her, said: It is as if you sent him on a need. She said: Then he came after that. Abu Salamah said: So I thought he had it for him. A need, so we left the house and sat at the door, and I was one of the closest to the door, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell upon him and made He left and spoke to him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested on that day, and Ali was the closest person to people in covenant with him. “This is an authentic hadith.” chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4671 - True"
"4672","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, and Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Arara, they said: Harami bin Amara told me, Al-Fadl bin Amira told me, Maymun Al-Kurdi told me, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, that Ali was satisfied On his authority, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taking my hand while we were on the streets of Medina, we passed by a garden and I said: O Messenger of God, What a better garden. He said: “For you in Paradise there is better than this.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4672 - True"
"4673","Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Aziz bin Muawiyah Al-Basri told us, Abdul-Aziz bin Al-Khattab told us, Nasih bin Abdullah Al-Muhallimi, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: I entered with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to visit Ali. Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, visited him while he was sick, and Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, were with him. They moved around until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down. May God bless him and grant him peace. One of them said to his friend: I see him as nothing but perished. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He will not die unless he is killed.” And he will not die until he is filled with rage.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4673 - A weak chain of transmission"
"4674","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Humaid told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Zayd al-Ahwal told me, on the authority of Uqab ibn Tha`labah, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari told me, regarding the caliphate of Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Ali bin Abi Talib to fight the transgressors, the unjust, and the renegades.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4674 - It is not valid"
"4675","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Yunus al-Qurashi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin al-Khattab told us, Ali bin Ghurab bin Abi Fatima told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabatah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying to Ali bin Abi Talib: “You will fight the transgressors, the unjust, and those who deviate from the roads, the rivers, and the Shafaat.” Abu Ayyub said: I said, O Messenger of God, with Who are these people fighting? He said: “With Ali bin Abi Talib.”"
"4676","Abu Hafs, Omar bin Ahmad Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail Bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Awdi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Indeed, among what the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entrusted me is that the nation You will betray me after that: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4676 - True"
"4677","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan. Al-Taymi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: “As for you, you will meet after me. Effort. He said: Is my religion safe? He said: “In safety with your religion.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4677 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4678","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, I am Abu Muslim, Ibrahim bin Bashar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ayan, on the authority of Abi Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: Abdullah bin Salam came to me, and I put my foot in stitches, and I want Iraq, so he said: Do not come to Iraq, for if you go to it, sword flies will strike you with it. Ali said: “By God, it has The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it to me before you. Abu Al-Aswad said: So I said to myself: “Oh God, I have never seen a fighting man like today.” He speaks to people like this: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4678 - Ibn Bashar is disgraceful and Ibn Ayan is unsatisfactory"
"4679","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Ubayy told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Khuthaym al-Muharbi narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir Radi On his authority, he said: Ali and I were companions in the expedition of Dhu al-‘Asharah, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, camped there and stayed there, we saw Some people from Banu Mudlij were working in a spring of palm trees that they owned, and Ali said to me: O Abu Al-Yaqzan, can you bring these people and see how they are? Do they work? So we came to them and looked at their work for an hour, then we fell asleep, so Ali and I went and lay down in trees of palm trees in a patch of dirt. So we slept, and by God, nothing woke us up except the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, moving us with his foot, and we were disturbed by that knock. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Abu Turab” because of the dirt he saw on him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not tell you about the two most wretched of people?” We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Uhimar Thamud is the one who hamstrung the she-camel, and the one who harms you, O Ali, for this - meaning his horn - until you get wet.” This is from the blood - meaning his beard -” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not include it with this addition, rather they agreed on the hadith of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, “Qom Aba Turab”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4679 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4680","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan told us, Al-Harith bin Mansour told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jarry bin Kulayb Al-Amiri said: When Ali marched to Siffin, I hated fighting, so I went to Medina, and I entered upon Maimuna bint Al-Harith, and she said: “Who are you from?” I said: From the people of Kufa. She said: “From which of them?” I said: From Bani Amir. She said: Welcome to welcome, and close to close. Are you coming, what has brought you? He said: I said: Ali marched to Siffin and I hated fighting, so we came here. She said: “Did you pledge allegiance to him?” He said: I said: Yes, she said: “Go back to him and be with him, for by God he did not go astray, nor will he go astray.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4680 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4681","Da’laj bin Ahmad al-Sijzi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz bin Muawiya told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq al-Ja’fi told us, Abdullah bin Abd Rabbuh Al-Ijli, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Looking at Ali is worship.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and its evidence is on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud is correct
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4681 - The topic"
"4682","Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us, Saleh bin Muqatil bin Saleh told us, Muhammad bin Abdul bin Utbah told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Salem, Yahya bin Issa Al-Ramli told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Looking at Ali’s face is an act of worship,” followed by Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4682 - And this is a topic"
"4683","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Qari told us, Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair Al-Dhabi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Consideration To the face of the Most High is worship.”"
"4684","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asmah, the two Al-Adlan, told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Mu’la bin Rashid told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, On the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, proposed to Ali, may God be pleased with him, or Kulthum, and he said: Marry her, and Ali said: I am destining her for my nephew Abdullah bin Jafar, so Omar said: Marry her, by God, what Among the people there is one of the people who observes the same things as I do, so Ali married him to her. Then Omar Al-Muhajireen came and said: Don’t you congratulate me? They said: By whom, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: By Umm Kulthum, daughter of Ali and daughter of Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every lineage and cause will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection, except what was of my own cause and lineage, so I wanted it to be between me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “And his lineage and cause are recognized.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4684 - Interrupted"
"4685","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Ahmad bin Salamah and Muhammad bin Shazan told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, They said: Abdul Razzaq told us, I am Al-Numan bin Abi Shaybah, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd bin Yatha’, on the authority of Hudhayfah Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you give it to Abu Bakr, he is ascetic in this world, desiring the Hereafter, and in his body. Weakness, and if you entrust it to Umar, then he is a strong and trustworthy one, who does not fear in God the blame of a scoundrel. And if you entrust it to Ali, then he is a guided guide who will establish you on a straight path.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4685 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4686","On the authority of Hayyan Al-Asadi, I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “The nation will betray you after me, and you live on My religion, and you will be killed for my Sunnah. Whoever loves you will love me, and whoever hates you will hate me, and this will be dyed from this” - meaning his beard from His head - “correct”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4686 - True"
"4687","Abu al-Tayyib Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Dhuhli narrated to me, Ja`far ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Hafiz narrated to me, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, a partner narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Zar’ah, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahb, said: A delegation from the people of Basra came to Ali, and among them was a man from the Kharijites called Al-Jaad bin Na'ja, so he thanked and praised God, and sent blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said: Fear God, O Ali, for you are dead, so he said Ali: “No, but I will be killed. A blow to this one will turn this one into disarray.” He said, and Ali pointed to his head and beard with his hand, “A judgment fulfilled, and a promised covenant, and he who slanders will be disappointed.” Then he criticized Ali for his clothing, and said: “If only I had worn better clothing than this,” then he said: “Indeed “This dress of mine is far from arrogant for me, and I am more worthy of Muslims to imitate me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4687 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4688","Professor Abu Al-Walid Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Siwar bin Abdullah Al-Anbari told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: My father said: Tell us Al-Harith bin Makhshi said that Ali was killed on the morning of the twenty-first of Ramadan. He said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Ali say, while he was giving a sermon, and he mentioned He praised Ali, saying: “He was killed on the night the Qur’an was revealed, the night Jesus was taken captive, and the night Moses was arrested.” He said: And Al-Hasan bin Ali prayed for him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4688 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4689","Abu Al-Walid narrated to us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Ansari narrated to us, Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ruh, on the authority of Mawla For Ali, “Al-Hassan prayed over Ali and said the greatest for him four times.”"
"4690","Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Nakhai told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hatim told me, my father told me, Amr bin Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat told me. Ibn Nasr said: I heard Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi saying: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Muljim al-Muradi was in love with a woman from the Kharijites.” From Taim Al-Rabab, called Qattam, so he married her and gave her three thousand dirhams in charity, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, was killed in that.” He said Al-Farazdaq:
 [Long Sea]
 I have never seen a foal with a smooth leg... like a colt colt without a tambourine.
 Three thousand male and female slaves...and he struck Ali with the determined sword.
 There is no dowry more expensive than Ali’s, even if it is expensive... and no lethality less than that of Ibn Muljim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4690 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4691","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Awn Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Abdul Aziz bin Al-Khattab told us, Ali told us Ibn Ghurrab, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When Ibn Muljam struck Ali with that blow, Ali advised him and said: “He has struck me, so do well.” To him, and make his bed for him. If he lives, then death or retaliation, and if he dies, treat him, for I will dispute with him before my Lord Almighty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4691 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4692","Al-Walid told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf told us, Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya said: When they brought Ibn Muljim to Ali, he said: “Do to him what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did to a man appointed for him. He ordered him to be killed and burned with fire.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4692 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4693","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Ahmad bin Sayyar Al-Imam told us, Rafi’ bin Harb Al-Laythi told us, Hakim bin Hakim told us. Zaid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, said: “I saw the killer of Ali bin Abi Talib being burned with fire among those who had spears.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4693 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4694","Ahmad bin Balwayh Al-Aqsi told me, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abbad bin Yaqoub told us, Nuh bin Darraj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Asmaa Al-Ansariyyah said: “No stone was lifted at Iliya on the night Ali was killed except that foul blood was found underneath it.” Al-Hakim said: “The narratives differed regarding the age of the Commander of the Faithful when he was killed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4694 - Noah is a liar"
"4695","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: I am Bishr bin Musa, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Jaafar told us. Bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: “Ali, may God be pleased with him, was killed when he was fifty-eight years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4695 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4696","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Ali told me Bin Omar bin Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, saying: I heard Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, in the year he died When I entered the year of eighty-one, he said: “This is my sixty-five. I am older than my father’s age. My father died when he was sixty-three years old, and he died when he was sixty-three years old. Hanafi school of thought in that year.” Al-Hakim said: “As for the duration of the caliphate of the Commander of the Faithful Ali, may God be pleased with him, it was according to what the Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. “Peace be upon him”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4696 - It contains Al-Waqidi"
"4697","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, My father, Saeed bin Jumhan, told me about the ship of Abu Abd al-Rahman, the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The caliphate of the Prophethood is thirty years.” Saeed said: “Abu Bakr lasted two years, Omar bin Al-Khattab ten years, and Othman bin Affan two years.” “Ten years, and Ali six years.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4697 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4698","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Amr bin Abdullah Al-Awdi told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, On the authority of Musa bin Mutair, on the authority of Sa`sa`ah bin Suhan, he said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, addressed us when Ibn Muljim beat him, so we said: O prince Believers, he appointed a successor over us, and he said: I leave you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left us. We said: O Messenger of God, appoint a successor over us. He said: “If God knows there is good in you, He will grant you your choice.” Ali said: “So God knew what was good about us, so He appointed Abu Bakr over us, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 4698 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"4699","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, in Marw, Muhammad bin Yunus bin Musa Al-Qurashi told us, Na’il bin Najih told us, Fitr bin Khalifa told us, On the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: Sa’sa’ bin Suhan entered Ali’s house and said: O Commander of the Faithful, who do you appoint as successor over us? He said: “If God knows there is good in your hearts, He will leave over you the good for you.” Sa’sa’ah said: “Then God knows there is evil in our hearts, so He will leave it to us.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4699 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4700","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Ja’d told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq speaking, on the authority of Amr Al-Asam, he said: I said to Al-Hasan bin Ali: These Shiites claim that Ali Messenger before the Day of Resurrection. He said: “They lied, and by God, these are not his followers. If we had known that he would be sent, we would not have married his wives or We divided his money.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4700 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4701","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdul Ghaffar bin Dawud Al-Harrani told us, Musa told us Ibn Ayan, on the authority of Adi Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: They said to my father: O Mahdi, peace be upon you. He said: “Glory be to God, did I not forbid you from this?” “The Mahdi is only one whom God Almighty and Majestic has guided.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4701 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4702","Saeed bin Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Nakha’i told me, Abdan al-Ahwazi told me, Ali bin al-Mundhir told me, Muhammad bin Fudayl told me, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wael, that Abdullah bin Al-Kawa, Shabib bin Rubi’i and people with them “secluded Ali after he departed from Siffin to Kufa, when He denounced them for insulting Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them. Then those who came after them among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disagreed with him. And they revolted against him, so Ali came out to them and argued with them and returned without fighting.” And in the hadith of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, with additional words, including Ali’s belief, “I will not make you live in a town until I have met God Almighty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4702 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4703","Abu Sa`id al-Nakhai told me, Abdan al-Ahwazi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, I am Amer bin al-Samat, on the authority of Abu al-Jahhaf, On the authority of Muawiyah ibn Tha`labah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: “Whoever separates from me has separated By God, whoever separates from you has separated from me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4703 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4704","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya, who said: A man from among those who were dear to Ali called out while he was praying the dawn prayer, and said: {And it has been revealed to you and to those of Before you, if you associate, your work will surely be nullified and you will be among the losers.} [Az-Zumar: 65]. Then Ali answered him while he was in prayer: """" {So be patient indeed, for He has promised God is Truth, and let not those who do not believe think lightly of you.} [Al-Rum: 60] “These are hadiths with authentic chains of narration and not with a chain of transmission, so I was judging them based on what The drawing was done with it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4704 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4705","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us: Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, Othman bin Omar, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Sharik bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: In my house, it was revealed: {God only desires to remove uncleanness from you, O People of the House} [Al-Ahzab: 33] She said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for Ali and Fatima And Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, and he said: “These are my family.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4705 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4706","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, and Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, they said: Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Abu Ammar told me, Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ told me, he said: I came to Ali but did not find him, so Fatima said to me: Go. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to invite him. He came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they entered and I entered with them. He called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, and each one of them sat on his thighs, and brought Fatima and her husband closer to his lap, then he wrapped a garment over them. And he said: {Allah only desires to remove uncleanness from you} [Al-Ahzab: 33] Ahl al-Bayt and to purify you with a thorough purification. Then he said: «These are my family, O God. “My family has more right.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4706 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4707","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, and Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, they said: Bishr bin Ahmad told us. Al-Mahboubi, Bamrou, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, Musab bin Shaybah told us, on the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, who said: The Mother of the Believers, Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told me: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the morning, wearing a cloak of water. Black hair, then Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came and took them with him, then Fatima came and he took her with them, then Ali came and took him with them. Then he said: “{Allah only desires to remove uncleanness from you, O People of the House, and to purify you with a thorough purification} [Al-Ahzab: 33] “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4707 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4708","Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Al-Nahwi wrote to me, mentioning that Al-Hasan bin Arafa told them, saying: Ali bin Thabit Al-Jazari told me, saying: Bukayr bin Mismar, client of Amer bin Saad, I heard Amer bin Saad say: Saad said: The revelation came down to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he brought Ali, Fatima, and their two sons under his garment, then said: “Oh God, these are my family and my household.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4708 - Ali and Bakir spoke about it"
"4709","Abu Al-Hasan Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah Al-Hazami told me, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr al-Mulaiki told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib, On the authority of his father, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw mercy descending, he said: “Pray for me, pray for me.” Safiyyah said, “Who, O Messenger?” God? He said: “My family is Ali, Fatima, Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein.” So they were brought and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, threw his cloak over them, then raised his hands and said: “O God, these are the descendants of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,” and God Almighty revealed: “God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House.” And He purifies you with a thorough purification} [Al-Ahzab: 33] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” The narration was authentic on the condition of the two sheikhs that he taught them Praying for his family just as he taught them to pray for his family.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4709 - Al-Maliki is going to have hadith"
"4710","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Zuhair bin Harb told us, Abu Salamah Musa bin Ismail told us, Abd told us Al-Wahid bin Ziyad, Abu Farwa told us, Abdullah bin Issa bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila told me that he heard Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila says: Ka’b bin Ujrah met me and said: Shall I not give you a gift that I heard from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, he said: So give it to me. He said: We asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we said: O Messenger of God, how is the prayer upon you, Ahl al-Bayt? He said: “Say, O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Abraham and the family of Abraham. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. O God, bless Muhammad and his family. Muhammad, just as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” He narrated this hadith with its chain of transmission and wording, word after letter. A letter from Imam Muhammad bin Ismail al-Bukhari, on the authority of Musa bin Ismail in al-Jami’ al-Sahih. I only included it so that the beneficiary may know that The family and the entire family. Abu Farwa and Urwa bin Al-Harith Al-Hamdani were among the closest followers in Kufa.”"
"4711","Abu Bakr told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Muslih Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi told us, Jarir told us Ibn Abdul-Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hassan Ibn Abdullah Al-Nakhai, on the authority of Muslim Ibn Subaih, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of God and my family, and they will not separate until they return to me at the Basin.
 This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4711 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4712","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz al-Asadi told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Dezil told us, Ismail told us Ibn Abi Uwais, my father narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, and other companions of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O sons of Abdul Muttalib, I have asked God for you three things: He strengthens your leadership, guides the lost of you, and teaches the ignorant of you. I asked God to make you honorable, merciful, and merciful. If only a man was kind. Between the Rukn and the Maqam, he prayed and fasted, then he met God, and he who hated the family of Muhammad entered Hell. “This is a good and authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4712 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4713","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Talid bin Sulayman told us, Abu al-Jahhaf told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked at Ali, Fatima, Al-Hasan, and Al-Hussein, and said: “I “War to whoever fights you, and peace to whoever makes peace with you.” This is a hasan hadith from the hadith of Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Hanbal, on the authority of Talid ibn Sulaiman. For I did not find any other narration from him. “And there is a witness to it, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4713 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4714","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Malik bin Ismail told us, Asbat bin Nasr Al-Hamdani told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi, on the authority of Subaih, the client of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said to Ali And Fatima, Al-Hassan and Al-Hussein: “I am at war with whomever you fight, and I am at peace with whomever you are at peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4714 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4715","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Abar told us, Ishaq bin Saeed bin Arkoun Al-Dimashqi told us, Khalid bin Da’laj Abu Amr Al-Sadusi, I think it is on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The stars are a safety for the people of the earth from drowning, and my family are a safety for my nation from disagreement. If an Arab tribe violates them, they disagree.” “So they became the party of Satan.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4715 - Rather, it is subject"
"4716","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih and Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anbari informed us, saying: Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Hisham bin Yusuf al-San’ani told us, Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us, and Muhammad bin Ali, the Bukharian writer, told us, In Bukhara, they said: Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, Abdullah bin Suleiman told me Al-Nawfali, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Love God for the blessings He nourishes you with, and love me for the love of God, and love my family for the love of me.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4716 - True"
"4717","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Bukayr Al-Hadrami, Muhammad Ibn Fudayl Al-Dhabi told us, Aban Ibn Ja’far Ibn Tha’lab told us, on the authority of Ja’far Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abi Nadra, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no one, Ahlul Bayt, hates us except “Allah will admit him to Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not take him out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4717 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4718","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Isbahani told us, Ahmed told us Bin Mahdi bin Rustum, Al-Khalil bin Omar bin Ibrahim told us, Omar bin Saeed Al-Abh told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Urwa, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My Lord promised me that among my household, whoever of them acknowledges monotheism, and I will deliver the message.” That he should not torture them.” Omar bin Saeed Al-Abh said: “Saeed bin Abi Orouba died on a Thursday, and this hadith was narrated on the day On Friday, he died seven days later in the mosque, and some people said: May God reward you with goodness for a man of rejection and affliction, and some people said: May God reward you. Good friend of the Sunnah and the community. You have fulfilled what you heard. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4718 - Rather, it is objectionable and not valid"
"4719","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told me, in Baghdad, Musa bin Harun told us, Qutayba bin Sa`id told us, Hatim bin Ismail told us, about Bukayr bin Mismar, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: When this verse was revealed: {We will call upon our sons and your sons and our women And your women, and ourselves, and yourselves} [Al Imran: 61] The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called upon Ali, Fatima, Hassan, and Hussein, may God be pleased with them, He said: “Oh God, these are my family.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4719 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4720","Ahmad bin Jaafar bin Hamdan Al-Zahid told me, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Ibrahim Al-Qaratisi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ahmasi told us, Mufaddal bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, who said: I heard Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, say: He was standing at the door of the Kaaba. Whoever knows me, then I am the one who knows me, and whoever denies me, then I am Abu Dharr. I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Indeed, the example of my family is among you.” Like Noah’s Ark for his people, whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever left it drowned.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4720 - Mufaddal bin Salih Wah"
"4721","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he greeted me: “An angel descended from heaven and asked God’s permission to greet me. He had not descended before her, so he gave me good news that Fatima is the mistress of the women of Paradise.” Abu Maryam Al-Ansari followed him, on the authority of Al-Minhal
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4721 - True"
"4722","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Jizzi told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hussein Al-Arni told us, Abu Maryam told us Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zurr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “An angel descended from heaven, and he asked God for permission to greet me, as he had not descended before, so he gave me good news that Fatima is the mistress of the women of Paradise.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"4723","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Isbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Isbahani told us, we told him Ismail bin Amr Al-Bajli, Al-Ajlah bin Abdullah Al-Kindi told us, on the authority of Habib bin Thabit, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me: “The first to enter Paradise will be me, Fatima, Al-Hasan, and Al-Hussein.” I said: Oh. Messenger of God, so those who love us? He said: “From behind you.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4723 - The hadith is objectionable"
"4724","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Yazid, the judge in Baghdad, told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abi Al-Awam Al-Riyahi told us, Yazid bin Harun, I am Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and put his foot between me and Fatima, may God be pleased with her, and taught us what to say if We went to bed, and he said: “O Fatima, if you are in your position, glorify God thirty-three times, praise God thirty-three times, and say ‘Allahu Akbar’ four times.” And thirty.” Ali said: “By God, I have not abandoned it yet.” Then a man said to him: There was something in his mind about it, not even on the night of Siffin. Ali said: “Not even on the night of Siffin.” “Siffin” is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4724 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4725","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Fatima, may God be pleased with her, and I was with him. She took a gold chain from her neck and said: This was given to me by Abu Hassan. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Fatima, would you be pleased for people to say: Fatima is the daughter of Muhammad, and in your hand is a chain of fire.” Then he left. He did not sit down, so Fatima went to the chain, bought a boy, and freed him. This reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Praise be to God who He saved Fatima from the Fire.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not take her out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4725 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4726","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Othman Al-Adami told us, in Baghdad, Saeed bin Othman Al-Ahwazi told us, Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Sadoosi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Imran Al-Qaisi, Muawiyah Ibn Hisham told us, Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, and Abdullah Ibn Ghanam, they said: Abu Kurayb told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ali bin Muhammad bin Khaled Al-Mutraz, Ali bin Al-Muthanna Al-Tusi told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Amr bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fatima maintained her chastity, so God made her descendants sacred to Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4726 - Rather, it is weak"
"4727","Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Aqsi informed us of the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abu Muslim, the leader of the Al-A’mash, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The prophets will be sent on the Day of Resurrection riding animals to bring the believers from among their gathered people, and Salih will be sent to... His she-camel, and I will send her steps on Buraq at her furthest end, and Fatima will be sent in front of me.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4727 - Abu Muslim did not go out to him"
"4728","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi informed us, in Baghdad, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz, in Kufa, And Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, and Abu Al-Hussein bin Mati, in Kufa, and Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl, they said: Ibrahim bin Abd told us. Allah Al-Absi, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Bakkar Al-Dhabi told us, Khaled bin Abdullah Al-Wasiti told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, On the authority of Ali, peace be upon him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will call out from behind the veil: O people of Everyone, lower your gaze from Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, until you pass by: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4728 - No, by God, but rather fabricated"
"4729","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Hubayra’s daughter came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in her hand was a gold ring or gold rings. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began striking In her hand, Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and complained to her about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had done to her. Thawban said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered to see Fatima and I was with him, and she took a gold chain from her neck and said: This is a gift to her. Abu Hassan came to me with the chain in her hand, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Fatima, would you be pleased for people to say: Fatima is the daughter of Muhammad.” And in your hand is a chain of fire? “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and did not sit down, so Fatima went to the chain and bought a boy with it, and freed him, and that was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God who saved Fatima from Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4729 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4730","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, and Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym told us, in Kufa, we told him Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza, they said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Salem told us, Hussein bin Zaid bin Ali told us, on the authority of Omar bin Ali, on the authority of Jafar Bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali Bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To Fatima: “Indeed, God becomes angry because of your anger and is satisfied when you are pleased.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4730 - Rather, Hussein bin Zaid is a denier of hadith"
"4731","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali, the jurist Al-Shashi narrated to us, Abu Talib Ahmad bin Nasr Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ali bin Saeed bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad Ibn Yaqoub, Muhammad Ibn Ismail Ibn Raja’ Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Juma Ibn Umair, he said: I entered with my mother on Aisha, and I heard her from behind the veil asking her about Ali. She said: “You are asking me about a man, and by God, I do not know a man who loved To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than Ali, and there is no woman on earth more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than his wife.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4731 - Jamil bin Umair is accused"
"4732","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Othman bin Umair told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal Bin Amr, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “I have never seen anyone who was like him.” Words and a conversation from Fatima to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever she entered upon him, he welcomed her, and he stood up to her and took her by the hand. So he kissed her and made her sit in his seat.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4732 - Indeed, it is true"
"4733","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Sayegh told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Abi Al-Hussein told us, Ali bin Thabit Al-Dayan told us, Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace be upon him: “Fatima is the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise, except for Maryam bint Imran.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Muslim was alone in narrating the hadith of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best women of the worlds are four.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4733 - True"
"4734","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us, in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farawi told us, Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fatima is only a burden on my part. Whatever makes her expand makes me happy, and whatever makes her feel holds me down.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4734 - True"
"4735","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Shazan Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Ja’far bin Ziyad Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, who said: “The most beloved of the women to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Fatima. “And among the men is Ali” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4735 - True"
"4736","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Hamdani told us, Abd al-Mu’min bin Ali al-Zaafrani told us, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, that he entered upon Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “O Fatima, by God, I have never seen anyone more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than you, and by God, no one among the people has ever been more beloved.” “Your father, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more beloved to me than you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4736 - Strange and strange"
"4737","Abu Al-Hussein bin Abi Amr Al-Sammak told me, and Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, saying: Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi told us, Yahya bin Saeed the Umayyad told me, my father told me, Yazid bin Sinan told me, Urwa bin Ruwaym told me, he said: I heard Abu Thalabah Al-Khushani, may God be pleased with him, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned from a campaign or a journey, he would come to the mosque and pray there. He prayed two rak'ahs, then he recited the prayer of Fatima, may God be pleased with her, then he went to his wives. When he returned, he left the mosque, and Fatima met him at the door. The house covered her mouth, and her eyes were crying, so he said to her: “My daughter, what makes you cry?” She said: O Messenger of God, do I not see you disheveled and disheveled, with your clothes torn off? He said: So do not cry, for God Almighty has sent your father For a matter in which there will not remain on the face of the earth a house of turrets, nor a hair, but God will bring glory or humiliation into it until it reaches where night has reached.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4737 - Yazid bin Sinan is Al-Rahawi, his weakness is Ahmad and others, and he is an insignificant obstacle that is not known."
"4738","The distinguished ruler Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, dictating the beginning of Dhul-Qa’dah in the year four hundred and two, Abu Al-Hussein told us Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram bin Akhi al-Hasan bin Mukarram al-Bazzar in Baghdad, Muslim bin Issa al-Saffar al-Askari told us, Abdullah bin Dawud Al-Khuraibi, Shihab bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa’d bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Gabriel, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, brought me a quince from Paradise, and I ate it on the night of my captivity, and Khadija became attached to Fatima, so I was like... “I longed for the scent of Paradise. I smelled Fatima’s neck.” This is a hadith with a strange chain of narration and text. Shihab bin Harb is unknown and the rest of the Its narrators are trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4738 - Posted by Muslim bin Isa Al-Saffar"
"4739","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ismail Al-Wasiti told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibrahim Qu’ays, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he traveled He was the last person to meet Fatima, and when he returned from a journey, the first person to meet him was Fatima, may God be pleased with her.”"
"4740","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Ala Al-Adami told us, in Basra, Yahya bin Hammad, Abu Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibrahim Qu’ais, so he mentioned something similar with his chain of transmission and added to it, so the Messenger of God said to her: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” The narrators of this hadith were narrated on the authority of the last of them in the Sahih, other than Ibrahim Qais. Zakaria bin Abi told us Zayed, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: While he was in his illness, which He died on it: “O Fatima, are you not content to be the mistress of the women of the worlds, the mistress of the women of this nation, and the mistress of the women of the believers?” This is an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4739 - Ibrahim Qais is weak"
"4741","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad told us, Hilal bin al-Alaa al-Ruqi told us, Husayn bin Ayyash told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Suleiman, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: Fatima, may God be pleased with her, came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to ask him servant, and he said to her: “Which you have come to ask is more beloved to you or better than him?” He said: I thought that she had asked Ali. He said: “Say: Oh God, my Lord.” Heavens, Lord of the Great Throne, Our Lord and Lord of all things, the Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Qur’an, forsake love and intentions, I seek refuge in You from the evil of You are the cornerstone of everything. You are the first, so there is nothing before you. You are the last, so there is nothing after you. You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above you. And you are the Inward One, and there is nothing besides You. Pay off our debt and enrich us from poverty.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4741 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4742","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Waddah bin Yahya Al-Nahshali told us, Abu Bakr told us Bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Fatima, may God be pleased with her, she said: The polytheists of Quraysh gathered in Al-Hijr, and the Messenger of God said: “My son, be still.” Then he went out and entered the mosque upon them, and they raised their heads. They knelt down, so he took a handful of dirt and threw it towards them, then he said: “The faces became disfigured, and not one of them befell anyone except that he was killed on the day of Badr.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4742 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4743","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin al-Qasim al-Dhuhli told me in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Faryabi told us, Sulayman bin Abdul-Rahman al-Dimashqi told us, Omar bin Saleh Al-Dimashqi, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Ayman, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married May God bless him and grant him peace, his daughter Fatima, Ali bin Abi Talib, and commanded him not to enter upon Fatima until he comes to her.” He mentioned the hadith with an authentic chain of narration, And they did not take it out
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4743 - Sent"
"4744","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim told me, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Absi told me, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told me, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, On the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Juma’ bin Umair, he said: I went to see Aisha, may God be pleased with her, with my aunt, and she was asked: Which of the people was most beloved to me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “Fatima.” It was said: Who are the men? She said: “Her husband, if what she knows of him is a regular and consistent faster.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4744 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4745","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Maryam bint Imran, and Aasiyah. Pharaoh’s wife, Khadija bint Khuwaylid, and Fatima bint Muhammad” “This hadith is in the Musnad of Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Hanbal Like this
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4745 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4746","And Abu Bakr Al-Qutay’i told us about the virtues of Ahl al-Bayt, classified by Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Hanbal. Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us. Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told me, Muammar told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam bint Imran, Asiyah, wife of Pharaoh, Khadija bint Khuwaylid, and Fatima bint Muhammad.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. His saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds” suffices. Among the women of the world
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4746 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4747","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abu Sa’id, the client of Banu Hashim, told us. Abdullah bin Jafar, Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar bin Makhrama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Al-Miswar, that he sent To him, Hassan bin Hassan was proposing to his daughter, and he said to him: Tell him, let him meet me in the dark. He said: So he met him, and the fenced one thanked God and praised him, then He said: As for what follows, by God, there is no lineage, lineage, or kinship more beloved to me than your lineage, lineage, and kinship, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Fatima is a part of me. Whatever tightens it contracts me, and whatever expands it expands me, and on the Day of Resurrection, lineages will You will be cut off without being a relative, and my cause and my son-in-law.” And you have her daughter, and if I had married you, he would have taken her. So he departed, apologizing to him. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4747 - True"
"4748","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Humaid and Ali bin Zaid told me on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was passing by Fatima’s door. May God be pleased with her for six months. When he went out for the dawn prayer, he would say: “Prayer, O People of the House. {God only desires to remove from you impurity.” Ahl al-Bayt and purifies you with a thorough purification} [Al-Ahzab: 33] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4748 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4749","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, My father told me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: Ali proposed to Abu Jahl’s daughter to her uncle Al-Harith ibn Hisham, so he consulted the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Are you asking me about what is sufficient for her?” He said: Ali, I may know what is according to it, but do you command me to do it? He said: “No, Fatima is a bitch from me, and I only think that she is sad or frightened.” Then Ali said: I will not do anything that she dislikes. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4749 - Strong transmitter"
"4750","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of my father Hanzalah, a man from the people of Mecca, said that Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, and her family said to him: We will not marry you to the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then this reached the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Fatima is a bitch of mine, so whoever harms her has harmed me.”"
"4751","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Musa bin Sahl bin Kathir told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyaani told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that was conveyed to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “Fatima is only a part of me. Whatever harmed her annoys me, and whatever annoys me, he annoys me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"4752","Ahmad bin Jaafar bin Hamdan Al-Bazzar told me, Ibrahim bin Ubaid Allah bin Muslim told me, Saleh bin Hatem bin Wardan told me, he told me My father, Ayoub told me, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madani, on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, who said: I was at the wedding of Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. When we arrived in the morning, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the door and said: “O Umm Ayman, pray for my brother.” She said: He is your brother and you may marry him. He said: “Yes, Umm Ayman.” Then Ali came, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sprinkled some water on him and prayed for him, then said: “Call Fatima for me.” She said: Then she began to stumble out of shame, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Be still, for I have married you to the most beloved of my family to me.” She said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sprinkled water on her, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned and saw blackness between his hands, and said: “Who is this?” So I said: I am Asma bint Umays. I said: Yes. He said: “You came at the wedding of the daughter of the Messenger of God?” I said: Yes, so he called for me
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4752 - The hadith is wrong"
"4753","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “I did not see anyone who was The speech and speech are more similar to those of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than to Fatima. Whenever she entered upon him, he would rise up to her, kiss her and welcome her. He took her by the hand and made her sit in his seat, and whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her, she would stand up to him, coming to him. “And she kissed his hand.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4753 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4754","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yunus ibn Muhammad told us, Dawud told us Bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Alba bin Ahmar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote There were four lines on the ground. Then he said: “Do you know what this is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best women of the people of Paradise are four: Khadija bint Khuwaylid, And Fatima bint Muhammad “the hadith” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4754 - True"
"4755","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Huywayh bin Al-Mu’amil Al-Hamdani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, I am Abd al-Razzaq bin Hammam, My father told me, on the authority of Mina bin Abi Mina, the client of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He said: Learn from me before the hadiths become mixed with falsehoods. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I am the tree and Fatima is its branch, Ali is its pollen, and Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are its fruits, and our followers are Its leaves, and the root of the tree in the Garden of Eden, and the rest of that in the rest of the Garden. Saduq, Abd al-Razzaq and his father and grandfather are trustworthy, and Mina is the freed slave of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. He met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and heard from him. “And God knows best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4755 - No human being said this except the ruler, but rather a fallen follower"
"4756","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Shabawayh, the chief jurist, told us about Marw, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith Al-Naysaburi told us about Marw, Ali told us Bin Mihran Al-Razi, Salama bin Al-Fadl Al-Abrash told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that whenever Fatima, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mentioned, she would say: “I never saw anyone who was “The truest tone of it is, unless it is the one who gave birth to it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4756 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4757","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm told us. Al-Hafiz, they said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Absi told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Bakkar Al-Dhabi told us, Khaled Al-Wasiti told us, and Abu told me Bakr Ahmad bin Jaafar bin Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Muslim Al-Basri told us, Abdul Hamid bin Bahr told us, Khaled bin Bahr told us Abdullah, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the day comes Resurrection It was said: O people of the gathering, lower your eyes, so that Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will pass by, wearing two ribbons. “Khadhrawan” said: Abu Muslim: Abu Qalaba told me, and Abdul Hamid was with us, that he said: “Hamrawan.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 4757 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"4758","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uthman, on the authority of Al-Hakam, On the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Khadija, may God be pleased with her, gave birth to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, two boys.” And four women: Al-Qasim, Abdullah, Fatima, Umm Kulthum, Ruqayyah, and Zainab.”"
"4759","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Mahrajani told us, Muhammad bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Basri told us, Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna told us, about Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I asked my mother about Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted her, and she said: “She was like the moon on the night of a full moon, or the sun as clouds when it emerged from the clouds, white and tinged with red, with hair.” Black, one of the people who most closely resembles the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, as the poet said:
 [full sea]

 A white woman pulls back her hair... and disappears into it while it is a tawny mass.
 “It is as if it were a bright day over her... and as if it were a dark night over her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4759 - Topic"
"4760","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki informed us, and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz said: Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Jaafar Al-Hashimi mentioning, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “Fatima Radi was born May God bless her, in the year forty-one from the birth of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4761","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us He said: “Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died three nights without the month of Ramadan. She was twenty-nine years old or “The time of her death differed.” It was narrated on the authority of Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali that he said: “Fatima died after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, within three months.” As for Aisha, she said, according to what was narrated about her: “She died after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “Six months,” and as for Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: In what Yazid bin Abi Ziyad narrated on the authority of him, he said: “Fatima died after The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for eight months.” Muhammad bin Omar said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “Fatima, may God be pleased with her, died after the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Six months.” Muhammad bin Omar said: “And this has been proven with us.”"
"4762","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanzali told us, Abdul Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “Fatima stayed after the death of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him for six months.” Salih bin Kaysan, Uqail, Ibn Uyaynah, Al-Waqidi, and Muhammad bin Abdullah, my nephew, followed him. Al-Zuhri and Ibn Jurayj are all like him."
"4763","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, the son of my brother Taher al-Aqiqi al-Alawi, informed us in Baghdad. My grandfather Yahya ibn al-Hasan told us, Bakr informed us. Ibn Abdul Wahhab, Muhammad Ibn Omar Al-Waqidi told us, Muhammad Ibn Omar Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali Ibn Al-Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God bless him and grant him peace God said about them: “Fatima fell seriously ill, so she said to Asma’ bint Umays: Don’t you see that I have been carried on the bed in public? Asmaa said: Not for my life, but I will make you a coffin as I saw it being made in the land of Abyssinia. She said: Show it to me. He said: So Asmaa sent to She cut out damp newspapers from the wool and placed a coffin on the bed, which was the first thing the coffin had been. Fatima smiled, and I did not see her. Smiling after her father until that day, then we carried her and buried her at night.”"
"4764","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, saying: Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, was buried One night, Ali buried her, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, did not notice her until she was buried and Ali bin Abi Talib prayed over her. May God be pleased with him.”"
"4765","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us: I am Abu Al-Abbas Al-Thaqafi. Ali bin Aqeel bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told me, Issa bin Abdullah Al-Alawi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Al-Hasan, daughter of Abi Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of her brother Ja’far bin Muhammad, who said: “Fatima, may God be pleased with her, died when she was twenty-one years old. She was born on the eve of the year forty-one from the birth of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him”"
"4766","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Hamdan Al-Warraq told us, Musa bin Dawood Al-Dhabi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ma’mal told us, On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “There were two months between the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Fatima.”"
"4767","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman al-Wasiti told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Ghassan told us: Abdullah bin Al-Mu’amil Al-Makhzoumi Al-Makki, and Muhammad ibn Al-Mu’amil informed me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him: “Fatima did not stay After the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for two months.”"
"4768","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Asadi, the Hafiz of Hamdan, told me, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told me, Ismail ibn Abi Uwais told me, Musa ibn Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with them, “ When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed away, Fatima, may God be pleased with her, used to say: He would have loved anything from his Lord that was nearer to him, and he would have loved it. The garden of eternity is his abode, and his Lord refuses to honor him when he comes to him, and his Lord refuses to greet him when he meets him.” When Fatima died, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “
 [Long Sea]
 For every meeting of two friends there is a separation... and everything short of separation is small.
 And my disappearance one after another...is evidence that Khalil will not last forever.”"
"4769","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, al-Nufaili told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told me, Muhammad ibn Musa told me, on the authority of Aoun Bin Muhammad bin Ali, and Amara bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Umm Ja’far, the wife of Muhammad bin Ali, who said: Asmaa bint Umays told me, she said: “Ali and I washed Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4770","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm, the Hafiz in Kufa, told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, my uncle Al-Qasim bin Abi Shaybah told me, Yahya bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “For every The Banu Umm is a group belonging to them, except for the two sons of Fatima, for I am their guardian and their group.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4770 - It is not correct"
"4771","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Bathaha told us, Affan told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Ali Ibn Munabbih Al-Thaqafi said: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came running to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he joined them to him and then said: “The boy “A stingy, cowardly, and sad thing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4771 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4772","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ziyad Al-Nahwi told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Bishr bin Mihran, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: Yahya ibn Umar entered Al-Hajjaj, and Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn narrated to us. Khaled Al-Hashimi in Kufa, Ahmed bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi lent us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Nahhas lent us, Saleh bin Musa Al-Talhi lent us, Asim bin Bahdala, he said: They gathered with Al-Hajjaj and he mentioned Al-Hussein bin Ali, so Al-Hajjaj said: He was not one of the descendants of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was with him. Yahya bin Yamar, and he said to him: “You lied, O prince.” So he said: “You must bring me what you said with proof and confirmation from the Book of God Almighty.” Or I will surely kill you, and he said: “And from his descendants are David, and Solomon, and Job, and Joseph, and Moses,” according to His words, the Almighty, {and Zechariah And Yahya, and Jesus, and Elias} [Al-An'am: 85] So God Almighty informed that Jesus is from the descendants of Adam through his mother, and Al-Hussein bin Ali is from the descendants of Adam. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his mother, said: “You are right, so what made you disbelieve me in a gathering?” He said: “What has God taken from the prophets?” That He might make it clear to the people and not conceal it. God Almighty said: {Then they abandoned it behind their backs and bought it for a small price} [Al Imran: 187] """" He said: So he denied it. To Khorasan
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4772 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4773","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Israel, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: When Fatima Al-Hasan gave birth, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came. He greeted me and said: “Show me my son. What have you named him?” He said: I said: I named him Harb. He said: “Rather, it is good.” When she gave birth to Al-Hussein, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “Show me my son.” Did you name him? He said: I said: I named him Harb, and he said: “Rather, he is Hussein.” Then, when she gave birth to the third, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “Show me your son.” Did you name him? I said: I named it Harb. He said: “Rather, he is a doer of good.” Then he said: “I only named them after the sons of Aaron: Shubbar, Shubayr, and Mushbar.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4773 - True"
"4774","Abdul-Ala bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman bin Al-Ash’ath Al-Sijistani told me in Baghdad, my father told me, Ahmad bin Al-Walid bin Burd of Antioch, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Makhzoumi told us, Aoun bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother Jafar, his mother, on the authority of her grandmother, Asma, on the authority of Fatima, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her one day and said: “Where My sons? She said: Ali took them away, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went and found them playing in a drinking bowl, with some leftover food in their hands. Dates, so he said: “O Ali, will you not kill my son before it is free?” and he mentioned the rest of the hadith, “This Muhammad ibn Musa is the son of a trustworthy Madinian man, This Aoun is the son of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’. He and his father are trustworthy, and Umm Ja’far is the daughter of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq. I found her to be Asma bint Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them. They are all noble and trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4774 - Rather, Muhammad is weak"
"4775","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Al-Munadi told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, Ubi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revolted against us. He said the salaam during one of the afternoon or afternoon prayers, while carrying one of his sons, Al-Hasan or Al-Hussein, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward. So he placed it at his right foot, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated with a prolonged prostration. My father said: So I raised my head from among the people, and lo, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was prostrating, and the boy was riding on his back, so I prostrated again. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, The people said: O Messenger of God, you have prostrated in this prayer a prostration that you never used to prostrate. Is there something you were commanded to do? Or was it revealed to you? He said: “All of that did not happen, but my son left me, and I hated to hasten him until he had fulfilled his needs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4775 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4776","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad bin al-Hasan told me Al-Subai’i, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are my sons. Whoever loves them loves me, and whoever loves me, God will love him, and whoever God loves He will admit him to Paradise, and whoever hates them will hate Me, and whoever hates Me God will hate him, and whoever God hates He will admit him to Hell. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4776 - This is objectionable"
"4777","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ibn Numayr told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Dinar told us. Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Masoud, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revolted against us. May God bless him and grant him peace, and with him are Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, this one is upon him and this is upon him, and he will follow this one once and that another time, until he comes to us. A man said to him: O Messenger of God, do you love them? He said: “Yes, whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4777 - True"
"4778","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abdul-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Hamani told us, Al-Hakam bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na`m, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Al-Hasan “And Al-Hussein is the lord of the youth of the people of Paradise, except the two cousins.” This hadith has been authenticated from many aspects, and I am surprised that they did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4778 - Al-Hakam bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Naam is soft in it"
"4779","Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Uthman bin Saeed Al-Marri told us, Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.” This is an authentic hadith with this addition, and they did not narrate it and witness it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4779 - True"
"4780","What Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Subaih Al-Amri told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Qattan, Mu’ala bin Abdul Rahman told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4780 - Mu’alla bin Abdul Rahman is abandoned"
"4781","Ahmad bin Qani’ bin Marzuq, the judge in Baghdad, told us. Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Harrani told us. My father told me, Musa bin Ayyan, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, saying: “I seek refuge with you with the perfect words of God from every devil and monster, and from every blaming eye.” Then he says: “This is how Abraham used to protect his sons Ishmael and Isaac.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4781 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4782","Abu Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Kamel bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: We were praying the evening prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was praying, and when he prostrated, Al-Hasan jumped up. Al-Hussein was on his back, and when he raised his head, he took them and placed them in a close position, and when he returned, he returned them again, and when he prayed, he placed one of them here. And one of them is here, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, should I not take them to their mother? He said: “No.” She flashed a light, and he said: “Come with your mother.” They continued to walk in her light until they entered. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4782 - True"
"4783","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hani ibn Hani, on the authority of Ali, who said: When Al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “What did you name my son?” I said: Harb. He said: “He is Al-Hasan.” When Al-Hussein was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What did you name my son?” I said: Harb. He said: “He is Al-Hussein.” Then when Mohsen was born, he said: “What did you name my son?” I said: Harb. He said: “He is a Muhsin.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have named the sons of these after Aaron named his sons Shubra. “And Shubayr and Mushbar.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"4784","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Omar bin Saeed bin Abi told me Husayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba ibn al-Harith, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, met al-Hasan ibn Ali May God be pleased with them both, so he joined him and said: “My father is similar to the Prophet, not similar to Ali,” and Ali laughed, “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4784 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4785","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Azhar bin Saad Al-Samman told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said that he met Al-Hasan bin Ali and said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissing your stomach.” So reveal the place where the Messenger of God kissed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him until I kiss him. He said: Al-Hasan revealed to him and he kissed him: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4785 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4786","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, He said: I heard Wahba Abu Juhayfah say: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Hasan bin Ali looked like him.” This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and there is an authentic witness to it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4786 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4787","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yazid bin Abdul-Samad Al-Dimashqi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, I am Muammar, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There was not among Ali’s sons more like the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than good.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4787 - True"
"4788","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubayd Allah bin Al-Walid told us, about Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair said: “Al-Hasan bin Ali performed twenty-five Hajj on foot, and the most important things are to be taken with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4788 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4789","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki informed us, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Zuhair bin Al-Alaa, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, who said: “Fatima, may God be pleased with her, gave birth two and a half years after Uhud. Al-Hassan for four years and six months of history.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4789 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4790","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, Abu Waqid told me, he said: “Abu Muhammad died. Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib, in Rabi’ al-Awwal of the year forty-nine, and Sa’id bin Al-Aas prayed over him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4790 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4791","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hammani told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I still love this man after I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He does what he does. I saw Al-Hasan in the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was inserting his fingers into the beard of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, put his tongue into his mouth and then said: “O God, I love him, so love him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4791 - True"
"4792","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Salih Al-Madani told us, Muslim bin Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, he said: We were with Abu Hurairah, and Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib came to us, and he greeted us, and we returned our greetings to him, but we did not Abu Hurairah knew about it, so we said to him: O Abu Hurairah, this Hassan bin Ali has greeted us, so he caught up with him and said: Peace be upon you, my master. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He is a master.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4792 - True"
"4793","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Haywah bin Shurayh told us, Abu Sakhr told me that Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt told him that Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told him, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed Hassan and hugged him to him, and made him smell him, while there was a man from the Ansar with him, and the Ansar said: I have a son who has reached the age of I never kissed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you think that if God has removed mercy from your heart, then what is my fault?” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4793 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4794","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Zamaa bin Salih, on the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came carrying Al-Hasan bin Ali on his neck. He said: Then a man met him and said: What a good ride you got on, boy. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And what a good rider he is” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4794 - It is not correct"
"4795","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Omari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abu Musa told us, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, He said: I heard Yazid bin Khumayr narrating, that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr narrating, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Al-Hasan bin Ali: People say that you want the caliphate, so he said: “The skulls of the Arabs were in my hand. They fought whom I fought, and made peace with whomever I made peace with.” I left it. Seeking the face of God Almighty, and shedding the blood of the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he blackmailed them by entreating the people of Hijaz. This is an authentic chain of narration. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4795 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4796","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrawayh Al-Saffar told us in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Zuhair bin Harb told us, Musa bin Ismail, Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl Al-Hadaani told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Imari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abu Talib Zayd bin Akhzam Al-Tai, Abu Dawud told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl told us, Yusuf bin Mazin Al-Rasibi told us, he said: A man stood up to Al-Hasan bin Ali and said: O Masoud. The face of the believers, and Al-Hasan said: “Do not scold me, may God have mercy on you, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the Umayyads addressing From his pulpit, one man after another, and that displeased him. Then you descended, “Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise,” and you descended, “Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree.” And what Do you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months that the Umayyads ruled over. So we counted that, so it is neither more nor “This is an authentic chain of narration, and the one who said this to Al-Hasan bin Ali is Sufyan bin Al-Layl, the companion of his father.”"
"4797","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us in Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Sari bin Ismail Al-Bajli told us, On the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Al-Layl Al-Hamdani, he said: I came to Al-Hasan ibn Ali when he pledged allegiance to Muawiyah, and I said: O you who blacken the face of the believers, then He mentioned it in a similar way
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4797 - Al-Sari bin Ismail Wah"
"4798","Nasr ibn Muhammad al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa`id al-Hafiz told me, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Bajli told me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq told me. Al-Balkhi, Nuh bin Darraj narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Bahi, on the authority of Sufyan bin Al-Layl, who said: When it came to the matter of Al-Hasan bin Ali and Muawiyah When I came to Medina while he was sitting with his companions - he mentioned the length of the hadith - he said: Then we discussed the call to prayer with him, and some of us said: The beginning of the call to prayer was a vision of Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim, and Al-Hasan bin Ali said to him: “The importance of the call to prayer is greater than that. Gabriel, peace be upon him, was in the sky two by two, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught him. He greeted Al-Hasan and Al-Hasan gave the call to prayer when he turned away.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4798 - Abu Dawud said Nuh bin Darraj is a liar"
"4799","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Sufyan, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Hafsa, he said: I heard Abu Hazim say: I witnessed the day Al-Hasan bin Ali died, and I saw Al-Hussein bin Ali saying to Saeed bin Al-Aas: And he stabbed him in the neck and said: Come forward, and had it not been a Sunnah, I would not have come forward to you, and there was something between them. So Abu Hurairah said: Are you fighting for Ibn Your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with soil in which you bury him, and I heard the Messenger of God say: “Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has loved me.” “He hated me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4799 - True"
"4800","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, and Abu Sa`id Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us: Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab Al-Shaarani, Abu Bakr Abdul-Rahman bin Abdul-Malik bin Shaybah Al-Hazami told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me in my Witr prayer when I raised my head and nothing remained but prostration: “O God, guide me among those whom You have guided, and grant me health among those whom You have guided.” You have recovered, and take care of me among those whom you have taken charge of, and bless for me what you have given, and protect me from the evil of what you have decreed. Indeed, you decree and you will not be decreed. Indeed, it does not humiliate those whom you have appointed. “Blessed are you, exalted be our Lord.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, except that Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Abi Kathir disagreed with Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Uqba in his chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4800 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4801","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid told us Allah bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Bazzar and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Bayhaqi said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, and Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Abi told us. Much, Musa bin Uqba told me, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Hawra, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, he said: He taught me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said these words in the Witr prayer: “O God, guide me among those whom You have guided, and bless for me what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. For you judge and you will not be judged, and he will not be humiliated by those whom you have appointed. Blessed are you, and exalted are you, our Lord.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4801 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4802","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Yahya, the son of my brother Taher al-Aqiqi al-Hasani, told us. Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, my uncle Ali bin Ja’far bin Muhammad told me, Al-Hussein bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Omar bin Ali, on the authority of his father, Ali bin Al-Hussein said: Al-Hassan bin Ali addressed the people when Ali was killed, and he thanked God and praised him, then he said: “A man was arrested this night.” The ancients did not precede him in any deed, nor did the others overtake him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give him his standard and he would fight while Gabriel was on his behalf. On his right, and Mikael on his left, he will not return until God grants victory over him, and he does not leave on the people of the earth either yellow or white except seven hundred. A dirham left over from his gifts that he wanted to buy for a servant for his family.” Then he said: “O people, whoever knows me knows me, and whoever does not know me.” He knows me, for I am Al-Hasan bin Ali, I am the son of the Prophet, I am the son of the successor, I am the son of Al-Bashir, I am the son of the Nazir, and I am the son of the preacher. To God, by His permission, and I am the son of the luminous lamp, and I am from the People of the House to whom Gabriel used to descend and ascend from us, and I I am from the People of the House from whom God has removed impurity and purified them with a thorough purification, and I am from the People of the House whose affection God has imposed on all Muslim, and He, Blessed and Most High, said to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {Say: I do not ask of you any reward for it except affection for my kin and whoever commits it. We will increase for him goodness therein.} [Al-Shura: 23] So performing a good deed is our affection, Ahl al-Bayt.
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4802 - It is not correct"
"4803","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh informed us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, he informed us Ibn Jurayj, Ja`far bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of his father, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, named Al-Hasan bin Ali on the seventh day, and that it was derived from His name is the name of Hussein.” He mentioned that there was nothing between them except the rope.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4803 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4804","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Abdullah bin Al-Jahm told us. Ja`far, on the authority of Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar, who said: “Al-Hasan ibn Ali was poisoned many times, all of which escaped until the last time he died was Therein, because his liver was failing, so when he died, the women of Banu Hashim mourned over him for a month.” Ibn Umar said: Ja’far bin Umar told us about it, on the authority of Abu Ja`far said: “The people remained weeping over Al-Hasan ibn Ali, and the markets did not stand up.” Ibn Umar said: Ubaida bint Na’il told us, on the authority of Aisha. Bint Saad said: “He punished the wives of Al-Hasan bin Ali according to the Sunnah.” Ibn Umar said: Dawud bin Sinan told us: I heard Tha’labah bin Abi Malik say: “We witnessed Al-Hasan ibn Ali on the day he died and buried him in Al-Baqi’. Even if a needle had been thrown, it would not have fallen except on a person’s head.” Ibn Umar said: He told me Maslama, on the authority of Muharib, who said: “Al-Hasan bin Ali died in the year fifty of Rabi’ al-Awwal, and he was forty-six years old. May the prayers be upon him. Saeed bin Al-Aas was crying and was ill for forty days.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4804 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4805","I am Hamza bin Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Uqabi in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Salam Al-Sawwaq told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shaiban told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq said: Allegiance was given to Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib in Kufa after the killing of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali, and he took the pledge of allegiance from His companions, so Harithah bin Mudarib told me, saying: I heard Al-Hasan bin Ali saying: “By God, I will not pledge allegiance to you except on what I tell you.” They said: What She? He said: “You make peace with whomever I made peace with, and you fight with whom I made war with.” And when the pledge of allegiance was completed, he addressed them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4805 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4806","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith narrating, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Al-Aqmar, a man from Banu Bakr bin Wa’il, who said: When Ali was killed, Al-Hasan rose up He was addressing the people, then a man from Azd stood up and said: I bear witness that I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placing him in his sack while he was He says: “Whoever loves me should love him, and let the witness inform the absent person.” And if it were not for the dignity of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would never have spoken about it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4806 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4807","Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Muhammad bin Musa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sirri, on the authority of Hisham bin Muhammad bin Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Abu Mikhnaf He said: “When the pledge of allegiance to Al-Hasan bin Ali took place, he was diligent in confronting Muawiyah and heading towards him, so he put Abdullah bin Jaafar at the forefront of it. Al-Tayyar with ten thousand, then Qais bin Saad followed him with a large army, so Muawiyah wrote to Abdullah bin Jaafar, and guaranteed him one thousand thousand dirhams. When he reached the Hijaz, he responded to that and stopped his march, and went to Muawiyah and he paid him his respects, and the army dispersed and Qais bin Saad alone, and many joined him. Whoever was with Abdullah bin Jaafar, Muawiyah wrote to him and urged him, but he did not agree to it until he made peace. Al-Hasan met Muawiyah, and the command was handed over to him. Al-Hasan and his companions headed to meet Muawiyah. Al-Hasan was wounded by an attack at the beginning of Sabat, and Sinan wounded him. Ibn al-Jarrah al-Asadi, the brother of Banu Nasr, stabbed him in the thigh with a pickaxe in a disgraceful manner. He was of the view of the Kharijites, so al-Hasan embraced him in His hand and stayed with him on the ground, and Abdullah bin Dhabyan bin Amara Al-Tamimi jumped on him and bit his face until his nose was cut and it split. He hit his head with a stone, and then he died, to the destruction of the inmates of the burning fire. Al-Hasan was carried on the bed to Al-Madain, where he descended upon Saad bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi. Al-Mukhtar’s uncle. He was Ali’s caretaker, may God be pleased with him, in Mada’in. He brought him a doctor and treated him until he was healed, may God be pleased with him."
"4808","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Musa told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan says: “Al-Hasan bin Ali received Muawiyah with battalions as large as mountains, and Amr bin Al-Aas said: By God, I see battalions that do not turn back.” Or kill her peers, so Muawiyah, who was the better of the two men, said: What do you think if these people are killed? Whose blood do I have? Who has me in their affairs? Who can have their wives? He said: So Muawiyah sent Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah bin Habib bin Abd Shams - Sufyan said: He had a company with him - so he made peace with Al-Hasan. Muawiyah handed over the matter to him and pledged allegiance to him for the caliphate on conditions and documents. Muawiyah conveyed to Al-Hasan a great sum of money, it was said: five hundred thousand. A dirham, and that was in Jumada al-Awwal in the year forty-one, but he was governor seven months and one before he handed over the authority to Muawiyah. ""ten days""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4808 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4809","Then Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan and al-Hussein bin al-Hasan told us, saying: Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Ansari told us, they told us: Ash'ath bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Al-Hasan bin Ali: “This son of mine is a gentleman, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation between two groups of Muslims through him.”"
"4810","Muhammad bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan and Suleiman bin Harb told us, they said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was addressing the people, when Al-Hasan bin Ali came and went up to him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hugged him and said: “Indeed, this son of mine is a master, and God Almighty may perhaps reconcile two groups through him.” “Two great Muslims”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4810 - Al-Bukhari included them on the authority of Abu Musa Israel, on the authority of Al-Hasan"
"4811","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Qarad Abu Nuh told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mazin said: A man came to Al-Hasan bin Ali when he pledged allegiance to Muawiyah, and he rebuked him and said: You have made the faces of the believers black, and you did it and did it, so he said: “No.” You reprimand me, for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw the Umayyads jumping on his pulpit, man by man. This was distressing for him and he was concerned. So God Almighty revealed, “Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise, and We sent it down on the Night of Destiny.” And what makes you know what the Night of Destiny is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months that will be spent after you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4811 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4812","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir Shazan told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah told us, Abu Ruq Al-Hamdani, Abu Al-Arif told us, said: We were in the forefront of Al-Hasan bin Ali, twelve thousand, our swords dripping with sharpness to fight. The people of the Levant, and Abu Al-Umar Taha was upon us. When the peace treaty between Al-Hasan bin Ali and Muawiyah came to us, it was as if our backs had been broken from anger and anger. Al-Hasan bin Ali came to Kufa, and a man from among us, nicknamed Abu Amir Sufyan bin Al-Layl, came up to him and said: Peace be upon you, O humiliator of the believers. Al-Hasan: “Do not say that, Abu Amer. I did not humiliate the believers, but I hated to kill them in pursuit of kingship.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4812 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4813","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Shaabi, said: Al-Hasan bin Ali addressed us at the palm tree when he made peace with Muawiyah, so he stood up and thanked God and praised Him, then he said: “The one who saddles the bag He met, and the most incapable of inability is immorality, and this matter in which I and Muawiyah differed is the right of a person, and he was more deserving of his right than me or It is my right, so I left it to Muawiyah’s desire to uproot the Muslims and spare their blood. And if I know, perhaps it will be a trial for you and an enjoyment for a while. I will say my word. This, and I ask God’s forgiveness for me and for you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4813 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4814","Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us in Kufa, Issa bin Mihran Al-Qaisi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa Al-Absi told us, Hammad bin Continuing, Fatima bint Al-Harith told me, on the authority of her father, that Ali used to say to Al-Hasan, may God be pleased with them both: “Take off his pants.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4814 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4815","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Zuhair bin Al-Ala told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Qatada bin Di’amah Al-Sadoosi, he said: “The daughter of Al-Ash’ath bin Qays named Al-Hasan bin Ali, and she was under him, and she bribed money for that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4815 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4816","Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Al-Fadl bin Ghassan Al-Ansari told us, Muaz bin Muadh told us, and Ashhal bin Hatim told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, that Al-Hasan bin Ali said: “I have urinated a portion of my liver, and I have been given poison repeatedly, but I have never been given anything like"
"4817","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Qahtaba told us, Al-Hussein bin Abi Kabsha told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Salam bin Poor person, on the authority of Imran bin Abdullah, who said: Al-Hasan bin Ali saw what the sleeper sees between his eyes written: “Say: He is God, One” [Al-Ikhlas: 1] So he told it to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: “If your vision comes true, then your time has come.” He said: He took a poisonous name in that year and died, may God have mercy on him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4817 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4818","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Jawhari told us in Baghdad, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Musab told us, Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Ammar Shaddad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Al-Fadl bint Al-Harith, that she entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, I saw a bad dream tonight. He said: “What is it?” She said: It is intense. He said: “What is it?” She said: I saw as if a piece of your body was cut off and placed in my lap, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw goodness. Fatima will give birth if God willing, a boy, and he will be in your lap.” Fatima gave birth to Al-Hussein, and he was in my lap, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, so I entered one day To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I placed it in his lap. Then a moment came to me, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked Two streams of tears, she said: So I said: O Prophet of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is the matter with you? He said: “Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, came to me and told me that my nation will kill this son of mine.” So I said: This? He said: “Yes, and he brought me some of his soil that was red.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4818 - Rather, it is interrupted and weak"
"4819","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Alaa, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, who said: “Fatima gave birth to Husayn after Al-Hasan for a year and ten months, and she gave birth to him for six years.” Five and a half months later, Hussein was killed on Friday, the day of Ashura, the first ten days of Muharram in the year sixty-one. He is fifty-four years old. I have mentioned these news with an explanation in the book The Assassination of Al-Hussein, and it is sufficient for whoever heard it. ""And his awareness""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4819 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4820","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Ali Al-Amiri, that he went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a meal for which they were invited. He said: He met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the imam of the people and Hussein was playing with the boys. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to take him, so the boy agreed. He fled here once, and here another time, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made him laugh until he took it. He said: Then he put one of his hands under it. the back of his neck, and the other was under his chin, so he put his mouth on his and kissed him, and said: “Hussein is from me, and I am from Hussein. God loves the one who loves Hussein, Hussein.” “A tribe from the tribes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4820 - True"
"4821","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jahhaf, on the authority of my father Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was carrying Al-Hussein bin Ali, and he was saying: “Oh God “I love him, so I love him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated with a similar chain of narration in Al-Hasan, and both of them have been preserved.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4821 - True"
"4822","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Shaddad Al-Musma’i told us, Abu Nu’aym told me, and Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Subai’i Al-Hafiz, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Muhammad told us Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Yahya, my nephew, Taher Al-Aqiqi Al-Alawi, in the book of lineage, my grandfather narrated to us, Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adami narrated to us, Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told me from the history book, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us. Amr Al-Anqazi and Al-Qasim bin Dinar said: Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, and Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Yusuf bin Sahl Al-Tamar narrated to me, narrated to us Al-Qasim bin Ismail Al-Azrami, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ibrahim Al-Bazzar told us, Kathir bin Muhammad Abu Anas Al-Kufi, Abu Nu’aym told us, Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them. He said: “God Almighty revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, I killed Yahya bin Zakariya seventy thousand, and I am a murderer.” With your daughter’s son, seventy thousand and seventy thousand.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Shafi’i, and in the hadith of the judge Abu Bakr bin Kamil: “I was killed for the blood of Yahya bin Zakaria, and I will fight for the blood of your daughter’s son. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4822 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4823","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told me, Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Fudayl bin Iyad, Malik bin Sa’ir bin Al-Khams told us, Hisham bin Saad told us, Nu’aym bin Abdullah Al-Mujmar told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I never saw Al-Hussein bin Ali without tears filling my eyes, and that is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day and found me in the mosque. in my hand and he leaned on me, so I went with him until he came to the market of Banu Qaynuqa’. He said: He did not speak to me, so he walked around and looked, then he came back and I returned with him and he sat in He entered the mosque, hid himself, and said to me: “Pray for me for Ka’a.” Then Husayn came so hard that he fell on his lap, then he put his hand into the beard of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he made the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, open Al-Hussein’s mouth and let his mouth enter his mouth and say: “O God, I love him, so love him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4823 - True"
"4824","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Samina told us, Muhammad bin Musab told us, Muhammad bin Musab told us Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Umm Al-Fadl, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me while Al-Hussein was in his lap: “Indeed, Gabriel is upon him.” May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He told me: “My nation will kill Al-Hussein.” Ibn Abi Samina summarized this hadith and others narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad bin Musab. ""Completely""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4824 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4825","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza told us, Ali ibn Qadim told us, Abdul Salam bin Harb, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: We were with Ali bin Al-Hussein, and a group of Kufans came, and Ali said: O people of Iraq, love us with the love of Islam. I heard my father saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people, do not exalt me above my value. For God took me as a servant before He took me as a prophet.” So I mentioned it to Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: “And after he took him as a prophet.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4825 - True"
"4826","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah told me, Hajjaj bin Nusayr told us, Qurrah bin Khaled, Amer bin Abdul-Wahid told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “We and the Ahl al-Bayt did not doubt “It is known that Al-Hussein bin Ali was killed with kindness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4826 - Hajjaj bin Nusayr Turk"
"4827","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, making the call to prayer in the ear of Al-Hussein when she gave birth to him.” Fatima, may God be pleased with her: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4827 - Asim bin Ubaidullah is weak"
"4828","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Hussein bin Sa’id told us. Zaid Al-Alawi, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded Fatima May God be pleased with her, and he said: “Adorn al-Hussein’s hair and give its weight in silver in charity, and give the midwife the man who has the aqeeqah.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4828 - It is not correct"
"4829","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, Ata bin عَجْلَانَ، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، عَنْ أُمِّ الْفَضْلِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: دَخَلَ عَلَيَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَنَا I breastfed Al-Hussein bin Ali with the milk of a son who was called Qutham. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave it to him and I gave it to him, and he urinated. On him, she said: So I lowered my hand towards him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not insult my son.” She said: Sprinkle him with water, Ibn Abbas: “The urine of a boy who has not eaten should be sprinkled, and he should be washed with the urine of a girl.” This hadith was narrated with chains of transmission, but they did not narrate it. As for Ismail bin Ayyash and Ata bin Ajlan, for they did not bring them out.”"
"4830","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khorasani told us in Baghdad, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Yazid Al-Riyahi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Aban, told by Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, he said: When Fatima Al-Hassan was born, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “Show me my son. What have you named him?” He mentioned the hadith
 Qatada said: “Al-Hussein was killed on the day of Ashura, a Friday.” Al-Hakim said: “We explain these news in the book The Killing of Al-Hussein, which contains It is sufficient for whoever heard it.” Al-Hakim said: “This is the last thing that diligence led to in mentioning the virtues of the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With authentic chains of transmission from what the two Sheikhs of Imams did not narrate, and I have dictated what my diligence led to regarding the virtues of the four caliphs and the people of The house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, some of which are authentic with chains of transmission, then I saw the first to organize this book in the order after them according to The dates of the Companions, may God be pleased with them all, from the beginning of Islam until the last of them who died, and God is the helper of that with His mercy.”"
"4831","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Tell me Al-Husayn bin Abdul-Rahman bin Saad bin Amr bin Muadh, brother of Abi Abdul-Rahman Al-Ashhali, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, my father’s brother Abdullah Al-Ashhali said: When Abu Al-Haysar Anas bin Rafi’ came to Mecca, and with him were young men from Banu Abd Al-Ashhal, among them was Iyas. Bin Muadh were seeking an alliance from Quraysh over their people from Khazraj, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard about them, so he came to them and sat with them. He said: “Is there anything better for you than what you have come for?” They said: What is that? He said: “I am the Messenger of God. God sent me to His servants to call them to worship God and not to associate anything with Him, and He sent down to me the Book.” Then he mentioned Islam to them, and recited the Qur’an to them. Iyas bin Muadh, who was a young boy, said: What kind of people are these? And God is better than what you have come for. He said: Then Abu al-Haysar took a handful of al-Batha’ and hit Iyas bin Muadh’s face with it, and said: Let us By my life, we have come for something other than this. Iyas remained silent, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and they left for Medina. An incident occurred. He sent a mission between Aws and Khazraj. He said: Then Iyas bin Muadh soon died. Mahmoud bin Labid said: “Then those who were present with him informed me. When he died, he told my people that they had not stopped hearing him exalting God, glorifying Him, praising Him, and praising Him until he died. He said: And they did not doubt. If he died as a Muslim, he had sensed Islam in that gathering when he heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what he heard. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4831 - Sent"
"4832","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “The death of Al-Bara’ bin Ma’rur occurred in Safar, before the arrival of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a month later, and he was the first of the leaders to speak.”"
"4833","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told me, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Al-Baraa bin Ma’rour was the first to be struck by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, in the pledge of allegiance to him on the night of Aqaba, among seventy of the Ansar, then Al-Baraa bin Ma’rur rose and thanked God and praised Him, then he said: Praise be to God who honored us with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and brought him to us. He was the first to answer, and the last to call, so we answered God Almighty. And we heard and obeyed, O community of Aws and Khazraj, God has honored you with His religion, so if you listen, obey, and support With gratitude, obey God and His Messenger. Then he sat down, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4833 - True"
"4834","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Mu’alla bin Asad Al-Ammi told us, Hammad told us, and Al-Rabi’ bin Badr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: “Khadija, may God be pleased with her, hired the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for two trips to “Every piece of bread was crushed with a cut.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4834 - True"
"4835","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalid Al-Homsi told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, my grandfather Ubaid Allah bin Abu Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: “The first woman whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married was Khadija bint Khuwaylid bin Asad bin Abd Al-Uzza, he married her in pre-Islamic times, and her father married her to Khuwaylid bin Asad.”"
"4836","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ma’shar narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “Khadija died May God be pleased with her, a year before the Hijra."
"4837","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub told me, Ibrahim bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, “that Abu Talib and Khadija bint Khuwaylid died in one year, and that happened before the emigrants.” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned to Medina three years later, and Khadija was buried in the graves, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended into her grave. She was twenty-eight years old on the day he married her.” Muhammad said: “The nickname of Khadija, may God be pleased with her, was Umm Hind, and she had a son and a daughter.” When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her, and Khadija’s mother was Fatima bint Zaida bin Al-Asam and her mother was Hala bint Abd Manaf.”"
"4838","Abu Al-Walid the Imam told me, Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Jabbar told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Musayybi told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad told me Bin Yahya bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: “Khadija bint Khuwaylid, may God be pleased with her, died. She was the daughter of “Sixty-five years.” This is an odd statement, as what I have is that she was not sixty years old."
"4839","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Yunus Al-Qurashi told me, Abu Zaid Saeed bin Aws told me, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Maqsam, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “Khadija gave birth to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two boys and four women: Al-Qasim and Abd. God, Fatima, Zainab, Ruqayyah, and Umm Kulthum.”"
"4840","Bukayr ibn Ahmad, the Sufi blacksmith in Mecca, told me. Sahl ibn Sulaiman al-Nili told us through Wasit. Mansur ibn al-Muhajir told us. Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir told us. Al-Hajjaj, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God who fed me with wine and clothed me.” Silk, and he married me to Khadija, and I was in love with her.”"
"4841","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Makhoul bin Ibrahim Al-Nahdi told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abi Rafi’, may God be pleased with him, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on Monday, and Khadija, may God be pleased with her, prayed with him, and he offered the prayer to Ali on Tuesday. So he converted to Islam and said: Leave me or I will command Abu Talib to pray. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is only a trust.” He said: So he said: Ali: Then I will pray, and he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Tuesday. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4841 - Muhammad bin Ubaidullah is weak"
"4842","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal and Zuhayr bin Harb told us, They said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ismail bin Iyas bin Afif, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Afif bin Amr, said: I was a merchant and I was a friend of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib in During pre-Islamic times, I came to do business and went to visit Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib in Mina. “Then a man came and looked at the sun when it tilted, so he stood and prayed. Then a woman came and she stood up to pray, then a boy came when the dream was over and he stood up to pray. So I said to Al-Abbas: Who is this? He said: This is Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib, my nephew. He claims to be a prophet, and nothing other than this has followed him in his affairs. The woman, this boy, and this woman are Khadija bint Khuwaylid, his wife, and this boy is his cousin Ali bin Abi Talib. He said Afif Al-Kindi: “And he converted to Islam, and his Islam was good. I wish that I had converted to Islam on that day, so that I would have a quarter of Islam.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, and he did not narrate it, and it has a reliable witness from the sons of Afif bin Amr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4842 - True"
"4843","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Yazid bin Al-Haytham Al-Daqqaq told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Musayybi told me, Abdullah bin Muadh Al-San’ani told me, Muammar bin Rashid told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she She said: The first thing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was told of revelation was the true vision in sleep. He would not see a vision without it coming to him. Like the breaking of the morning, then the open air was made beloved to him, and he would come to Mount Hira’ and bow his head while worshiping, until the truth surprised him while he was in the cave of Hira’. Then the king came to him about it and said: Read. He said: I said: “I am not a reader.” He said: “So he took me and covered me until I was exhausted, then he sent me, and said To me: {Read in the name of your Lord who created. He created man from a clot. Recite. And your Lord is Most Generous, Who taught by the pen. He taught man what he did not know.} [Al-Alaq: 2] He said: Then he returned with her trembling, until he entered upon Khadija, and said: “Hold me, hold me.” So they hugged him until the terror left him, and he said: “O Khadija, what's wrong with me? So he told her the news, and said: “You feared for me.” She said to him: No, give good news, for by God, God will never disgrace you. Indeed, you will uphold ties of kinship and be truthful. In the hadith, she carries everyone, welcomes the guest, and assists in the situations of truth. Then Khadija set off with him until she brought him Waraqah ibn Nawfal ibn Asad bin Abdul-Uzza bin Qusayy, who was Khadija’s uncle, her father’s brother, and he was a man who converted to Christianity during pre-Islamic times, and he used to write Arabic. And it is written in Arabic from the Bible, as God wills it to be written. He was an old man who had become blind. Khadija said: Yes, uncle, hear from your brother’s son. Waraqah bin Nawfal said: O my nephew, what do you see? So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him the news of what he had seen, and Waraqah said: This is the law that was revealed to Moses, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4843 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4844","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abdullah bin Abi Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi told me Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: “Khadija was the first of the women to believe in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4844 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4845","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Muhammad bin Falih told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Khadija, may God be pleased with her, was the first to believe in God and believe in His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, before Prayer is made obligatory.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4845 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4846","Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Sa’id bin Ajab Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Al-Dharis told me, Muhammad told us Ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal, on the authority of Abu al-Yaqzan Imran ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Rabia al-Saadi, he said: I came to Hudhayfah Ibn Al-Yaman, while he was in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was saying: “Khadija, the daughter of"
"4847","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar told us Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ and Abdullah bin Numayr told us, they said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The best of her wives is “Maryam, the daughter of Imran, and the best of her women is Khadija.” The two sheikhs agreed on quoting it, but I only mentioned it."
"4848","What Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abu Umar told us, and Nasr bin Ali told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, he told me. My father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I have been commanded to give Khadija the good news of a house in Paradise made of reeds in which there will be neither noise nor distress.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4848 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4849","Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told me, On the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ja`far ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was commanded to give good news to Khadija of a house in Paradise made of reeds in which there will be neither noise nor distress.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"4850","Ahmad ibn Jaafar told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Aamir ibn Salih ibn Abdullah ibn Urwa told me. Ibn Al-Zubayr Abu Al-Harith, Hisham Ibn Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was commanded to “I give good tidings to Khadija of a house in Paradise made of reeds.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: So I said to my father: Yahya bin Ma’in is attacking Aamir bin Salih. This, he said: You say what? You said: He saw that he heard from al-Hajjaj. He said: I saw that al-Hajjaj heard from a piece of wood, and this is shameful for a man to hear from someone who is younger than him or"
"4851","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger By God, this Khadija has come to you, and she has with her a vessel containing meat, food, or drink, so if she comes to you, read peace upon her from her Lord. And give her good tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds, in which there will be neither noise nor distress.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this. Driving, as for his saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: Give good news to Khadija, they agreed on the hadith of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi ""more concise"""
"4852","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, on the authority of Alba Ibn Ahmar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drew four lines on the ground. He said: “Do you know what this is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of the women of the people of Paradise are Khadija bint Khuwaylid and Fatima bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran” and I think he said: “And the wife of Pharaoh” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context."
"4853","Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: I found in my father’s book in his handwriting, Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, they said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Aisha said to Fatima, may God be pleased with her. On the authority of the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Shall I not give you good news that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Ladies, women of the family of “There are four things in Paradise: Maryam bint Imran, Fatima the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Khadija bint Khuwaylid, and Aasiya.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4853 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4854","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I have never envied a woman who has not envied Khadija, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not marry me.” Except after she died, and that is because the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave her good tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds in which there is no noise or hardship.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4854 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4855","Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not marry Khadija, may God be pleased with her, until she died.” Aisha said: “I have never seen Khadija or been more jealous for any of his wives than I was for Khadija. This is because of the many things he used to mention. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"4856","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Qais bin Unif told us, Qutayba bin Saad told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, he said: “Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and with him was Khadija, may God be pleased with her, and he said: May God send His greetings to Khadija, and she said: Indeed, God is peace, and may God’s peace and mercy be upon you. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4856 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4857","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Abi Al-Rijal said: As’ad bin Zurarah died in Shawwal at the beginning of nine months of the Hijra, and the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace It will be built on that day, peace be upon him. That was before Badr, and Banu al-Najjar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Our captain has died, so dig for us. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I am your leader.” Ibn Omar said: Abdul-Jabbar bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Amr. Ibn Hazm said: “The first to be buried in Al-Baqi’ was As’ad Ibn Zurarah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4857 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4858","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad told me Ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunaif, on the authority of his father, Abi Umamah, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik informed him, saying: I was a commander My father, after his sight went away and he would not hear the call to prayer on Friday except that he said: May God’s mercy be upon As’ad ibn Zurarah, so I said after Then: If I asked my father what would happen to him when he heard the call to prayer, he would say: May God’s mercy be upon As’ad bin Zurarah? So I said: O father, I like that you pray for Abu Umamah whenever you hear the call to prayer for Friday prayers. He said: “My son, he was the first to perform the Friday prayer for us.” Friday in Medina in the village of Harrat Bani Bayadah in Baqi’, called Al-Khadimat. I said: How many were you that day? He said: “Forty men.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4858 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4859","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Abu Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cauterized Asad bin Zurarah with a thorn.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4859 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4860","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Al-Muzaki told us, and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, told us: Qutayba bin Saeed, Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Zainab bint Nabit, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Her mother and her paternal aunt,” and their father was Abu Umamah As’ad bin Zurarah, bequeathed them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “so he gave them “A piece of gold dust with pearls in it,” Zainab said: “And I have found the jewelry or some of it.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4860 - True"
"4861","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar He said: “The first banner held by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was for Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, then the banner of Ubaidah bin Al Harith bin Abdul Al-Muttalib to Rabigh between Al-Juhfah and Qudayd."
"4862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid told me Ibn Ruman, on the authority of Urwa, and other of our scholars, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, who mentioned the hadith of the duel, and that Utbah ibn Rabi’ah was killed Ubaidah bin Al-Harith fought a duel. A threshold hit him in the leg and cut it off. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, carried him and he died in the bile.” He departed. From Badr, he buried him there.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4862 - True"
"4863","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: Utbah and Ubaidah disagreed between themselves, each one of them killing the one who struck it, and Hamza and Ali attacked each other. Utba killed him, and they took their companion Ubaidah and brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his leg had been cut off and his brains were leaking. They brought Ubaidah to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Am I not a martyr, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes.” Then Ubaidah said: If only Abu A student alive to know that I have more right to what he said than him, as he says:
 [Long Sea]
 And we will hand him over until we rush around him... and we will be distracted from our children and wives.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4863 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4864","Mukhlid bin Jafar Al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad bin Jarir Al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Wasiti told me, Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, I am Ishaq bin Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Sa’d, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: “The army of Badr was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Umair bin Abi Waqqas responded. Umair cried and the Messenger of God rewarded him.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4864 - Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri declared him weak"
"4865","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Narsi told us, Mansour bin Salamah Al-Khuza’i told us, Omar bin Ubayd Allah bin Zaid bin Haritha Al-Ansari Al-Madini, he said: My uncle Omar bin Zaid bin Haritha told me, Abu Zaid bin Haritha told me He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I looked down upon Saad bin Khaythamah.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4865 - Munkar"
"4866","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Halimi told me about Marwa, I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am a man, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, that Suleiman bin Aban told him, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Badr, he wanted Sa’d bin Khaythamah and his father all decided to go out with him, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he ordered one of them to go out, so he asked them. Ibn Al-Harith told his son Saad: It is necessary for one of us to stay, so stay with your wives. So Saad said: If it were other than Paradise, I would prefer it to you. I hope for martyrdom in this face of mine. So he shot them and Sa'd's arrow came out, so he went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Badr, and Amr killed him. Ibn Abd Wad
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4866 - Mursal and its chain of transmission is weak"
"4867","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabra told me, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to frequent a cemetery for his companions in which they could be buried, so he sought the outskirts of Medina. And its outskirts, then he said: “I was commanded to this place,” meaning Al-Baqi’, and it was called Baqi’ Al-Khabhaba, and most of its plants were gharqad. The first one to be buried there was Othman bin Mazun, may God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God placed a stone near his head and said: “This is the grave of We were distracted.” And when the immigrant died after him, it was said: O Messenger of God, where should we bury him? He says: “When we abandoned Othman bin Mad’un.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4867 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4868","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaidullah, On the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed Uthman bin Mad’un after he died.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4868 - Its chain of transmission is valid"
"4869","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Hibban bin Hilal told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When Othman bin Ma’zon died, she said His wife: Congratulations on Paradise, O Uthman ibn Maz’un. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at her and said: “How do you know?” She said: O Messenger of God, your knight and companion. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the Messenger of God, and I do not know what will be done to me.” So he took pity. The people were against Othman, and when Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Add her to our good ancestor.” Othman bin Mazun.” Then the women cried, so Omar started hitting them with his whip, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his hand and said: “Wait, oh"
"4870","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said Ja`dah bin Hubayra bin Abi Wahb bin Amr bin Aidh bin Imran bin Makhzum, and his mother was Umm Hani bint Abi Talib Hubayra ibn Abi Wahb married her to her. Hubayra says when she converted to Islam: “
 [Long Sea]
 Hind has longed for you if her question comes to you... and so are the stones, their roots and their untangling.
 If you have followed the religion of Muhammad... and your relatives have severed their cords from you.
 A day later, at the head of a rebel fort in Najran Khosrau, she set her imagination free.
 So be on the highest plateau.
 It is forbidden and its hills cannot be overcome.” Musab said: And Ja`dah is the one who says:
 [Long Sea]
 And who is the one who refuses to give up his maternal uncle to me...and my maternal uncle Ali is Dhul-Nada and Aqeel.”
 Musab said: “Hubayrah died in Najran as a polytheist, and as for Ja`dah, he married his maternal uncle’s daughter, Umm al-Hasan, the daughter of Ali, and she bore him a slave.” Allah bin Ja`dah bin Hubayra, about whom it was said that in Khurasan:
 [Simple Sea]
 “If it had not been for Ibn Ja`dah, neither Kuhnuz nor Khurasan would have been conquered until the trumpet was blown.”
 Musab said: “Ali appointed Ja’dah ibn Hubayra al-Makhzoumi as governor of Khurasan, and he departed for Iraq, then performed Hajj and died in Medina.” “He narrated a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the authenticity of what Musab mentioned.”"
"4871","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Abdul Hamid Al-Jafi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ja`dah bin Hubayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The best people are my generation, then those after them, then those after them, then the others who are worse off.”"
"4872","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of"
"4873","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria told us, Suleiman bin Dawood told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Tell me Abu Bakr bin Ayyash bin Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “Saad bin Malik prepared to go out to Badr. Then he fell ill and died, and the place of his grave was at the house of Ibn Qarith, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him his share and his reward.”"
"4874","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “Bani Hashim bin Abd Manaf, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, and Ali bin Abi Talib, witnessed Badr. And Zaid bin Haritha and Ansa, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Kabsha, and Abu Marthad, and his son Marthad.”"
"4875","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, On the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umayr ibn Ishaq, he said: “Hamzah was fighting in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with two swords and he would say: I am a lion.”"
"4876","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Abu Osama Ubayd Allah bin Osama Al-Halabi told us, Muhammad bin Imran bin Abi Laila told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Al-Asbahani, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hazour, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabatah, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The best of creation On the Day when God will gather them together, the Messengers, and the best of people after the Messengers will be the martyrs, and the best of the martyrs will be Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib.”"
"4877","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, he told me Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Makhrami, on the authority of Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, on the authority of her father, “Amina bint Wahb was the mother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. She was in the lap of her uncle Uhayb bin Abdul Manaf bin Zahra, and Abdul Muttalib bin Hashim brought his son Abdullah. Ibn Abdul-Muttalib, the father of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abdullah married Amina bint Wahb, and Abdul-Muttalib married Hala bint Uhab ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zahra, who is the mother of Hamza ibn Abdul Muttalib, was in one meeting, and he was close in age to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace and blessings be upon him and his breastfeeding brother.”"
"4878","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: A man told me, Whoever converted to Islam and was aware that Abu Jahl approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Safa, and he insulted him, insulted him, and said something hateful about him. Of the disgrace to his religion, and the weakening of it, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not speak to him,” and loyalty to Abdullah bin Jadan Al-Taymi in A place for her above Safa to hear that. Then he left and went to the Quraysh club near the Kaaba and sat with them. Hamza did not stay. Ibn Abd al-Muttalib was to return with his bow stretched out from a target of his, and when he did that he would not pass by the Quraysh camp, and the most severe of them was Shakima, and at that time he was a polytheist in the religion of his people, so the lady came to him while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had risen to return to his home. She said to him: O Amara, if you had seen what your nephew Muhammad suffered from Abu Al-Hakam just now, he found him here, and he hurt and insulted him, and reached the point of He was hated, then he left it and went to the Quraysh club near the Kaaba, and he sat with them and did not speak to Muhammad, so Hamza endured the wrath for what God wanted. Out of his dignity, he left quickly, not stopping anyone as he used to do.He wanted to circumambulate the Kaaba, intending for Abu Jahl to go there, so when he entered the mosque, he looked at him sitting among the people, and he turned toward him, until he saw He rose to his head, raised his bow, and struck him on the head with a heavy blow, and men from the Quraysh, from Banu Makhzum to Hamza, stood up to support them. Abu Jahl, and they said: We have not seen you, O Hamza, except that you have been patient. Hamza said: What is preventing me? This has become clear to me from him. I bear witness that he Messenger of God, and that what he says is true, by God I will not deviate, so prevent me if you are truthful. Abu Jahl said: Call Abu Amara. I cursed his nephew in an ugly insult, and Hamzah decided to convert to Islam, and he continued to belittle the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When Hamzah converted to Islam, I learned The Quraysh reported that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had become proud and abstained, and that Hamza would prevent him, so they stopped some of what they were eating and were eating. From him, Saad said about that when he hit Abu Jahl, and he mentioned an unstable attack, the beginning of which was when Abu Jahl tasted what you had deceived, he said: Then he came back. Hamza went to his house, and Satan came to him and said: You are the leader of Quraysh. You have followed this Sabian and abandoned the religion of your fathers. Death is better for you than what you have done. Then something similar came to Hamza.He said: What did I do? Oh God, if he is of the right mind, then place his belief in my heart, otherwise, make a way out for me from what I fell into, for he spent a night the likes of which he had never spent. And the whispering of Satan, until the morning he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My nephew, I have fallen into a situation from which I do not know the way out. And he made him do something like me, and I do not know whether it was more reasonable or not severe, so he spoke to me, for I was eager, my nephew, for you to speak to me. So he accepted. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reminded him, exhorted him, frightened him, and gave him good tidings. So God placed faith in himself, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: I bear witness that you are truthful, as the testimony of one who confirms and acquaints, so show, O son of my brother, your religion, for by God I do not like to have anything. The sun shone, and I am adhering to my first religion. He said: Hamza was among those through whom God strengthened the religion."
"4879","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Saeed bin Muhammad Abu Omar Al-Khajawani told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Qudamah bin Musa Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Ali and Hamza came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they had bathed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “How did you do?” One of them said: O Messenger of God, I covered him with a garment, and the other said: I did the same, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “If you did other than that to cover yourself.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4879 - True"
"4880","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: “Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib was fighting on the day of Uhud. In the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he says: I am the Lion of God. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4880 - True"
"4881","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Muhammad told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, they said: When Hamza was injured. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will never be afflicted with something like you.” Then he said to Fatima and his aunt Safiyya, may God be pleased with her. About them: “Give good news. Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, came to me and told me that Hamzah is written among the inhabitants of the heavens as Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. “The lion of God and the lion of His Messenger”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4881 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4882","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Haritha bin Mudarib, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Call Hamzah,” and he was the closest of them. To the polytheists, who is the owner of the red camel? Hamza said to me: He is Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and he forbids fighting, and he says: Oh My people, I see a people to whom you cannot reach and there is good among you. O my people, criticize her today for me and say that Utbah ibn Rabi’ah is cowardice, and you have already known. I am not the coward of you. So Abu Jahl heard about that and said: You are saying this. If someone else said, “You are filled with terror,” he said: “You mean, oh.” His face turned yellow, and he said: Then Utbah, his brother Shaybah, and his newborn son emerged, and they said: Who is fighting? Then a group of young men from the Ansar came out, and Utbah said: We do not want these, but who among the uncles of Banu Abdul Muttalib will compete with us? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Get up, O Hamza, get up, O Ubaida, get up, O Ali.” So Hamza came out to Utbah and Ubaidah to Shaybah. And Ali for Al-Walid, so Hamza killed Utbah, Ali killed Al-Walid, Ubaidah killed Shaybah, and Shaybah struck Ubaydah’s leg and cut it off. So Hamza and Ali rescued him until he died in the bile. “It is true according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4882 - They did not narrate it to Haritha, but Ibn Al-Madini distorted it."
"4883","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. May God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal crying over their loss. He said: “But Hamza has no weeping.” So the women of the Ansar came and cried for Hamza with him. He lay down and woke up and they were crying, so he said: “Oh, woe to them! They are here until now. They have been given a pledge, so let them return and not cry over a perishing after today.” It is authentic according to Muslim’s condition, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"4884","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Bastam Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmad ibn Sayyar and Muhammad ibn Al-Layth told us: Rafi’ bin Ashras Al-Maruzi told us, the grandson of Al-Saffar told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “The master of martyrs is Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib, and a man who spoke to an unjust imam and ordered him and forbade him and killed him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4884 - Al-Saffar does not know who he is"
"4885","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Muqri informed us in Baghdad, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Dunuqa informed us, Mu’alla ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us. Al-Wasiti, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, the uncle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a foreigner. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels washed him.” Authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4885 - Mu’alla bin Abdul Rahman Halak"
"4886","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Lahabi told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Haram bin Uthman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out looking for the daughter of Hamza Qubaisa until he stopped at the door and said: “Peace be upon you, is Abu Amara a sinner?” He said: She said: No, by God, may my mother and father be sacrificed for you. He went out heading towards you, so I think he missed you in some of the alleys of Banu al-Najjar. Didn’t he? Do you and my mother come in, O Messenger of God? He said: “Do you have anything?” She said: Yes, so he entered and Hays approached him and said: Eat by my mother and father, O Messenger of God. Congratulations and good health, for I have come with my intention. I would like to come to you and congratulate you and your command. Abu Amara told me that you were given a river in Paradise called Al-Kawthar. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: “And its vessels are greater than the number of stars in the sky, and I would love to bring it to your people.” Its chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it."
"4887","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by Hamza on the day of Uhud when he had been crucified and mutilated and said: “If Safiyya had not found I would have left him until God gathered him from the bellies of birds and wild beasts.” Then he shrouded him in a sheet, “in good condition, according to the condition of a Muslim.” And they did not take him out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4887 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4888","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, I am Abdullah bin Salih Al-Bukhari, Yaqoub bin Humaid bin Kasib told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: A boy was born to a man among us, and they said: What shall we name him? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They called him by the name most beloved to me, Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4888 - Ya’qub bin Kasib is weak"
"4889","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Yusuf bin Salman Al-Mazni told us, Sufyan told us Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, heard a man in Medina say: My grandfather brought my father to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: This is my son. So what do I call him? He said: “Call him the most beloved of people to me, Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib.” This unknown narrator was short in narrating the hadith on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah. The saying about it is the saying of Yaqoub bin Humaid, and Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz was debating with me that Al-Bukhari had narrated from him in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih, “And I refused to do so.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4889 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4890","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told me, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told me, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told me, Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told me, Rabi’ah bin Kulthum, on the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “I entered Paradise last night and looked therein and saw Ja’far flying with the angels, and Hamzah reclining on a bed.” Sahih. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4890 - Salamah bin Wahram was deemed weak by Abu Dawud"
"4891","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal crying over their loss, and he said: “But Hamza has no weeping” Hadith"
"4892","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, “In naming the one who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, and he was killed on the day of Uhud, and he was the son of Fifty-four”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4892 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4893","Ahmed bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Hadrami told us, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, On the authority of Abu Hammad al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stripped When he greeted Hamza, he cried, and when he saw someone like him, he gasped.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4893 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4894","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Khaled bin Khadash told us, Saleh Al-Marri told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked on the day of Uhud at Hamzah who had been killed and was mutilated. With it, he saw a sight that he had never seen a sight that was more painful for his heart or more horrific than it, and he said: “May God’s mercy be upon you, you have been an accessory to the womb, so you are reliable.” For good deeds, and had it not been for the sadness of those who came after you, I would have been pleased to leave you until you come from various mouths.” Then he swore while standing in his place: “By God “I will surely take the place of you with seventy of them.” Then the Qur’an was revealed while it was standing in its place and did not depart from it: “And if you punish, then punish with a likeness.” You will be punished for it, but if you are patient - it is better for those who are patient.} [An-Nahl: 126] Until he concluded the Surah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disbelieved on his oath. And he refrained from doing what he wanted
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4894 - Saleh Wah"
"4895","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When Hamzah was killed, Safiya came looking for him, not knowing what he had done. So she met Ali and Al-Zubair, and Ali said to Al-Zubair: Mention your mother, and Al-Zubair said to Ali: No, you mention your aunt. She said: What did Hamza do? So he showed her that they did not know, so she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “I fear for her mind,” so he placed his hand on her chest. He called, and she recovered and wept. Then he came and stood up to him and mutilated him, and said: “If the women had not been alarmed, I would have left him until he collected some of the birds’ crops.” And the stomachs of wild beasts.” Then he ordered the dead to be prayed over them, adding nine, and Hamza, may God be pleased with them, to pronounce seven “Allahu Akbar” over them. Then they would be raised and Hamzah would be left, then they would be given nine and he would say “Allahu Akbar” to them with seven takbeers, then they would be raised and Hamza would be left behind, then they would be given Nine times, then he would say “Allahu Akbar” to them seven times until he had finished with them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4895 - Abu Bakr bin Ayyash heard it from Yazid. I said, “They are not reliable.”"
"4896","Abu Al-Abbas and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ghayath told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw what a sleeper sees. He said: “I saw as if I was flanking a ram. It was as if the spear of my sword had broken, so I assumed that I would kill the ram of the people, and I interpreted that the spear of my sword was a man of my family. So Hamzah was killed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed Talha, and he was the standard bearer of the polytheists."
"4897","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Abdul Aziz bin Imran told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja`far Al-Mukhurami, on the authority of Abu Aoun, the client of Al-Miswar, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, he said: “Abdul Muttalib married Hala, daughter of Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zahra, and she gave birth to Hamza and Safiya.”"
"4898","Ismail bin Al-Fadl told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Abi Labiba, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is written with him in the heavens.” The seventh: Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, the lion of God and the lion of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4898 - Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Labiba wah"
"4899","Ja'far bin Al-Harith told us, Ja'far bin Muhammad Al-Faryabi told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid Al-Laythi told me, I heard Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi say: “Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib was nicknamed Abu Amara.”"
"4900","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Muharram in the year four hundred and three. Abu Al-Hussein told me Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari in Baghdad, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Abu Saleh Al-Farra told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abu Hammad Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lost On the day of Uhud, he greeted Hamza when the people fled from the fighting. He said: Then a man said: I saw him at that tree saying: I am the lion of God and the lion of God. His Messenger, O God, I disavow before You what these people brought to Abu Sufyan and his companions, and I apologize to You for what these people did to Abu Sufyan and his companions. When they were defeated, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked towards him, and when he saw his forehead, he cried, and when he saw what was done to him, he gasped and then said: “Don’t"
"4901","Ahmad bin Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah al-Masry told us, Ibrahim bin Bashar al-Ramadi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, Kathir al-Nawa’, on the authority of al-Musayyab ibn Najabah, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every prophet He was given seven companions, and I was given twelve.” Then it was said to Ali: Who are they? He said: Me, Hamza, and my two sons, then he reminded them, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4901 - Rather, it is very strong and weak"
"4902","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud Al-Zahid told me, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told me, Ahmad bin Saleh told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, said: Abdullah bin Jahsh said: “Oh God, I swear to you that I will meet the enemy tomorrow.” So they kill me, then they rip open my stomach, and cut off my nose and ears, and then you ask me about that? So I say: In you.” Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: “I hope that God will honor the end of his oath as he honored the beginning.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, had it not been sent in it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4902 - Authentic mursal"
"4903","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The first banner raised in Islam was for Abdullah bin Jahsh.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4903 - True"
"4904","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad told me Al-Abdari, on the authority of his father, said: Mus’ab bin Umair was a young and beautiful youth in Mecca, and his parents loved him, and his mother used to clothe him in the best way. He was the most fragrant of the people of Mecca, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to mention him and say: “I have never seen anything in Mecca.” He was more beautiful in character, more elegant in robes, and more generous in blessings than Mus’ab bin Umair.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4904 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4905","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya al-Shahid told me, Abdullah bin Abdul-Wahhab al-Hajabi told us, Hatim told us. Ibn Ismail, on the authority of Abdul Ala Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Qatn Ibn Wahib, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Dharr May God be pleased with him, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had finished on the day of Uhud, he passed by Mus’ab al-Ansari, who had been killed on his way, so he recited {from The believers are men who have been true to what they covenanted with God.} [Al-Ahzab: 23] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4905 - True"
"4906","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Basri told us, Abu Salih Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told us. Al-Tawil, narrated to us Maan bin Issa, on the authority of Makhramah bin Bukayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me on the day of Uhud to ask for Saad bin Al-Rabi’, and he said to me: “If you see him, extend my greetings to him, and say to him: The Messenger of God says to you: How do you find yourself? “He said: So I went around among the dead, and I struck him while he was on his last breath, and he suffered seventy wounds, between a stab with a spear and a blow with a sword. And an arrow shot, so I said to him: O Saad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is reciting his greetings to you, and saying to you: “Tell me how you find yourself?” He said: Upon the Messenger of God, peace be upon you, and upon you be peace. Say to him: O Messenger of God, find me feeling the scent of Paradise, and say to my people, the Ansar: You have no excuse. It is with God that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is sincere, while among you there is a sliver of something that blinks. He said: and his soul overflowed, may God have mercy on him. “This is a hadith.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4906 - True"
"4907","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed him: I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq, that Abdullah Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abi Sa’sa’ah told him, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who will look at what Sa’d Ibn Al-Rabi’ did for me?” So he mentioned the hadith in a similar way, and said: Then Saad said: Tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I am among the dead and I extend my greetings to him, and say To him: Saad says: May God reward you on our behalf and on behalf of the entire nation.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4907 - Sent"
"4908","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmed Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, on the authority of Aamir bin Wathilah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Nothing prevented us from witnessing Badr except that I And my father, we came, wanting the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the infidels of Quraysh seized us and said: You want Muhammad. We said: We do not want him. We want Medina, so they took from us God’s covenant and covenant that you would go to Medina and not fight with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. When we passed them We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we mentioned to him what they said and what we said to them, so what do you see? He said: “We seek God’s help against them, and we will fulfill their covenant.” So we set off for Medina, for that is what prevented us from witnessing Badr. “This is an authentic hadith.” chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4908 - True"
"4909","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim told me Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Uhud, Al-Yaman Ibn Jabir, father of Hudhayfah and Thabit bin Waqsh bin Za'oura were in Al-Atam with the women and boys, and one of them said to his companion, who were two old men, “No, father.” For you, what do we wait for? By God, none of us have anything left of his life except the thirst of a donkey. But we are the people’s duty - do we not take our swords? Then we joined the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they entered among the Muslims without knowing about them. As for Thabit bin Qash, the polytheists killed him, and as for The father of Hudhayfah, so the Muslim swords fell out against him, and they killed him without knowing him. Hudhayfah said: My father, my father. They said: By God, we did not know him. And they believed, and Hudhayfah said: May God forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to give it to him, so Hudhayfah gave it in charity. On the Muslims, this increased it in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4909 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4910","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Wahb bin Kaisan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “By God, on the morning of a Sunday morning, my father stopped drinking alcohol, then in the morning he fought until he was killed with the Messenger of God.” “God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is a witness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4910 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4911","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told me, Fayd bin Wathiq told me, Abu Amara Al-Ansari told me, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Jabir: “O Jabir, Shall I not bring you good tidings? He said: Yes, give me good tidings, may God give you good tidings. He said: “I sensed that God Almighty revived your father and placed him in His hands, so He said: He bestowed his blessings upon me.” My servant, I will give him whatever you wish. He said: O Lord, I have not worshiped you as I truly worship you. I hope that you will return me to this world, so that I may be killed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him again and said: “I have told you before that you will not return to it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4911 - Fayd bin Watheq is a liar"
"4912","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Amrawayh Al-Saffar told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hassan bin Musa Al-Asheeb told us, Abu Hilal told us, Saeed, nicknamed Abu Maslama, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: My father said to me: “O my son, I do not know. Perhaps I will be in... The first to be struck tomorrow, and that is the day of Uhud, so I advise you to do good to the daughters of Abdullah.” They met and that day was struck. “This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4912 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4913","Abu Bakr bin Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abu Maslamah told us, Abu Nadra told us, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “When the fighting of Uhud occurred, my father called me at night and said: I do not see me except that I was killed on the first day of the night. Whoever is killed from among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by God I will not let anyone be dearer to me than you after the soul of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and I owe a debt, so pay off my debt and be kind to your sisters. He said: So we arrived in the morning, and he was the first to be killed, so I buried him with another. In a grave, then I did not want to leave it with another in a grave, so I took it out after six months, and behold, it is as the day I placed it. Without his permission, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4913 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4914","Its explanation is what Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, I am Yahya bin Habib Al-Harithi, and Abdah Ibn Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, they said: Musa Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Kathir told us, he said: I heard Talha Ibn Kharash speaking, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah May God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Indeed, God Almighty does not speak to anyone except from behind a veil, and He spoke Your father struggled, so he said: “And I mentioned the hadith.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4914 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4915","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of His sheikhs said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram said: I saw in my sleep before Uhud as if I saw Mubashir bin Abdul-Mundhir, saying to me: You are coming to us in the coming days, so I said: Where are you? He said: In Paradise, we can rejoice therein as we wish. I said to him: Were you not killed on the day of Badr? He said: Yes, then I was revived and that was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the testimony, O Abu"
"4916","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Issa bin Maslamah bin Suleiman bin Abdullah bin Hanzalah bin Abi Aamer bin Abd Amr. My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “Hanzalah bin Abi Amer got married and went in with his family on the night that was the morning of a Sunday. When he prayed the morning prayer, Jamila stuck to him, so he came back and was with her. So he became estranged from it, then he joined the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4916 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"4917","Then Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed me: I am Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Saeed bin Yahya Al-Umawi told us, my father told me, he said: Ibn Ishaq said: Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When Hanzalah bin Abi Amir was killed after he and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith met, when Shaddad bin Al-Aswad insulted him With the sword, he killed him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your companion is being washed by the angels.” So they asked his companion, and she said: He went out when He heard the whispering while he was in a state of impurity, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For that, the angels washed him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4917 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4918","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Ibn Shaqiq told us Al-Mubarak, Abdul-Rahman bin Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, when he made an obligation for the people an obligation for a servant. God gave Hanzalah bin Hanzalah two thousand dirhams, so Hanzalah brought him his brother’s son, so he assigned him something less than that, and said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, you preferred this. Al-Ansari on my nephew? He said: “Yes, because I saw his father one day sharpening his sword like a camel’s sharpening.” “And he was the leader of his tribe, and he was lame, so he was killed.” And his son Khallad bin Amr, on the day of Uhud, they attacked everyone on the polytheists, and the polytheists were exposed and they were all killed, and with them was Abu Ayman, Amr’s client.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4918 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4919","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us about that, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, and it was Saad, nicknamed Abu Amr, and Liwa al-Aws was with him on the day of the ditch. An arrow was shot in the ankle and he was cut and bled. That was in the year five. From immigration"
"4920","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us about that, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs"
"4921","Abu Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Shabawayh, the chief of Marwa, told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Naysaburi told us, Ali bin Mihran told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to me, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik that he said: The one who shot Saad Ibn Muadh on the day of the ditch: Hibban bin Qays bin Al-Irqah, one of the Banu Amir bin Luayy. When he struck him, he said: Take it, and I am the son of Al-Irqah. Then Saad said: May God make your face sweat in the fire. Then Saad lived after he was struck by an arrow for about a month, until he ruled against the Banu Qurayza with a decree. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he returned to the city of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then his words exploded and he died at night, and Gabriel came to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: Who is this for whom the gates of heaven were opened and for whom the throne of the Most Gracious shook? “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Saad and found him dead.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4921 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4922","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, On the authority of Awf, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The throne shook at the death of Sa’d bin “Muadh” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and its chain of transmission is authentic, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4922 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4923","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Muhammad bin Amr, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Ammar, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and Yazid bin Abdullah bin Osama Al-Laythi, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Saad while he was He is buried: “Indeed, the throne was moved for him and the gates of heaven were opened for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4923 - True"
"4924","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He shook for the love of meeting God. The throne - meaning the bed - said: And he raised his parents on The pillars of the throne became rotten. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered his grave and was trapped. When he came out, it was said: O Messenger of God, what"
"4925","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid bin Al-Sakan Al-Ansariyya, may God be pleased with her, who said: When Saad bin Muadh died His mother shouted, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Will your tears not be quenched and your sadness go away, for your son is the first to laugh at God?” And the throne shook for him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not bring him out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4925 - True"
"4926","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, and Abu Musa told us about him. On the authority of him on the first journey, when I came, I asked Muhammad bin Yahya, and he told me about it. He said: Abdul Razzaq told us, I am Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas. May God be pleased with him, he said: When the funeral of Saad bin Muadh took place, the hypocrites said: How light his funeral was, and that was only because of his ruling on the children of Qurayza, then this was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “No, but the angels were carrying him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4926 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4927","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, I am Yazid bin Harun, I am Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah Al-Laythi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: We came from a journey, and they met us with something The allies, and the young men of the Ansar used to greet them whenever they came. They met Usayd bin Hudayr and called his wife to him, so he disguised himself and cried. She said: So I said to him: Glory be to God, you are one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you said in the previous verse, why do you cry over a woman? Then he uncovered his head and said: You are right, Amr Allah, and by Allah, I have the right not to cry over anyone after Saad bin Muadh, and the Messenger of God said May God bless him and grant him peace. What did he say? She said to him: What did he say? He said: He said: “The throne shook due to the death of Saad bin Muadh.” She said: He was walking between me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4927 - True"
"4928","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Abu Musa told me, Abu Al-Fadl bin Musawir told me, Abu Awanah, on the authority of Al-Amash, Abu Saleh told us, Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, told us: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The throne of the Most Gracious shook due to the death of Saad bin Muadh,” he said: Then a man said to Jabir: Al-Bara’ says: “The bed shook,” so he said: He was between these two. The two neighborhoods, Aws and Khazraj, are grudges. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The throne of the Most Gracious was shaken by the death of Saad bin Muadh.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4928 - True"
"4929","Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I entered Paradise and heard a recitation there, and I said: Who is this? They said: Haritha bin Al-Nu’man. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Such is righteousness. Such is righteousness.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4929 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4930","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Hisham bin Malas told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, and he told us Ali bin Hamshadh, and the pronunciation for him, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, he said: Harithah, my cousin, set out as an observer on the day of Badr, but he did not go off to fight, but an arrow struck him and killed him, so my aunt came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, if my son Haritha is in Paradise, I will be patient and seek reward. Otherwise, you will see what I will do. He said: “O Umm Haritha, there are many gardens, and Haritha is in the highest Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not They brought it out in this context that was narrated by Thabit, but they agreed on the narration of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, briefly.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4930 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4931","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told me Ibn Omar Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: Ja’far Ibn Abi Talib struck a Roman man and cut him in two halves, so he fell. One of its halves was in a vineyard, and thirty or thirty-odd wounds were found in one half of it. He migrated to the land of Abyssinia in the second migration, and with him His wife, Asma bint Umays, remained in the land of Abyssinia until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, migrated to Medina, then he migrated to While he was in Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not know which one I am more happy with, the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja’far.” He said: “And it was Ja’far.” His nickname is Abu Abdullah.”"
"4932","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Barad al-Ash’ari told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: My father, who breastfed me, told me From the Banu Murrah, he said: “It is as if I am looking at Ja’far bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On the day of Mutah, he mounted a horse of his and hobbled it, then he went on. So he fought until he was killed.”"
"4933","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told me, Zum’ah told us Bin Salih, on the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I entered Paradise last night and looked therein and saw Jafar flying with the angels, and Hamzah reclining on a bed.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4933 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4934","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “He did not wear sandals, nor did he put on shoes, nor did he ride the mounts, nor did he ride the balls, after the Messenger of God.” “May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He is better than Ja’far bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4934 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4935","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told me, Ali bin Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Madini told me, my father told me, Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw Ja’far bin “Abu Talib is an angel who flies with the angels with two wings.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4935 - Al-Madani is wah"
"4936","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Yahya al-Alawi, the son of my brother Tahir, informed us of my grandfather, Ibrahim bin Yahya bin Abbad al-Sijzi told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Al-Qasim told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “When an obituary came Jafar: “We recognized the sadness in the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4936 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4937","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr told us, Sa’dan bin Al-Walid, Baya’ Al-Sabri, told us, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting and Asma bint Umays close to him when he returned the greeting, then said: “O Asma’, this is Ja’far bin Abi Talib with Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil. Greet us individually.” “Peace be upon them,” and he told me that he met the polytheists on such-and-such day three or so days before his visit to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Four, and he said: I met the polytheists and was wounded in my body seventy-three times, between an arrow, a stab, and a blow. Then I took the standard in my hand. My right hand was cut off, then I took my left hand and cut it off, so God compensated me with two wings with which I could fly with Gabriel and Michael. I would come down from Paradise is wherever I want, and I can eat of its fruits whatever I want. So Asma’ said: Congratulations to Ja’far, for what God has bestowed upon him, but I fear not. People speak the truth, so go up the pulpit and tell him about it. So he went up the pulpit and thanked God and praised him, then he said: “O people, Ja’far is with Gabriel and Michael have two wings. May God protect him from his hands. He greeted me.” Then he told them how his situation was when he met the polytheists, so they became clear. For the people after the day when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, informed that Ja’far met them; That is why he was called the pilot in heaven.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4937 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4938",""
"4939","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Ibrahim ibn Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told us, about Yazid bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Nafi’ bin Ujair, on the authority of his father Nafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib - in the story of Bint Hamzah - he said: Ja'far said: I have more right to her, for her maternal aunt is with me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for you, O Ja'far, you resemble me in character and character. And you are from my tree, from which I come.” He said: “I am satisfied, O Messenger of God, with that. As for the slave girl, I will judge her for Ja’far, for her maternal aunt With him, the aunt is a mother, and Abu Hurairah used to say: The green shade has not shaded a face more beloved to me after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He received blessings from Jafar bin Abi Talib, based on the saying of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “You resemble me in character and character.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4939 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4940","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Awwam Al-Riyahi told me, Saad bin Abdul Hamid told us, Abdullah bin Ziyad told us. Al-Yamimi, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “We are the sons of Abd al-Muttalib, the masters of the people of Paradise: me, Ali, Ja’far, Hamza, Al-Hasan, and Al-Hussein.” And Al-Mahdi: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4940 - The topic"
"4941","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Issa Al-Subaie told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakim Al-Hiri told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hussein Al-Arni told us, Ajlah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God came from Khaybar, Ja’far, may God be pleased with him, came from Abyssinia. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him and kissed his forehead, then said: “By God, I do not know which of the two I am more happy with: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Khaybar.” Jafar” was sent by Ismail bin Abi Khaled and Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, while Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ibrahim bin Abi told us Talib, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled and Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from Khaybar. So he mentioned the hadith, “This is an authentic hadith, but it appeared with this authentic chain of transmission as a mursal message, and Ujlah bin Abdullah conveyed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4941 - Mursal"
"4942","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, on the authority of Hamdan, Hilal al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa May God be pleased with him. He said: Omar met Asma bint Umays and said: You are the best of people. If you had not migrated first, we would Better than you. We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, carrying your man and teaching the ignorant of you, so we ran away with our religion, so she said: I am not a refuge. Until he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, I met Omar and he said such-and-such, and he said: “Yes, You have two migrations: your migration to Abyssinia, and your migration to Medina. “This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4942 - True"
"4943",""
"4944","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakim told us, Ismail bin Aban told us, Abu Uwais told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “We were at Muttah with Ja’far ibn Abi Talib, and we found him among the dead, and we found him with him.” “Seventy-two surgeries.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4944 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4945","Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Amiri told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr bin Salem told us Al-Ijli, Sa’dan bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sitting Asma bint Umays was close to him. He returned the greeting and gestured with his hand, then said: “O Asma, this is Ja’far bin Abi Talib with Gabriel on him.” May the peace and blessings of God and Michael pass by and greet us, and I return their greetings to them. He told me that he met the polytheists on such-and-such a day before. He passed three or four times to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I met the polytheists and was wounded in my body by seventy-three of my attacks. A stab and a throw, so I took the banner with my right hand and cut it off, then I took it in my left hand and cut it off, so God compensated me with two wings to fly. They are in Paradise with Gabriel and Michael, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them, so I can eat of its fruits whatever I want. So Asma’ said: Congratulations to Ja’far, what he has been provided with. God is of goodness. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ascended the pulpit and told the people about it. He said: Then he made clear to the people after that what The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him about him, and he was named Ja’far al-Tayyar. Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck Ja’far on the Day of Badr with his arrow and his reward.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4945 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4945 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4946","Abu Zar’ah Ahmad bin Al-Hussein Al-Sufi told me in Al-Ray, Abu Al-Fadl Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Nasr bin Hilal Al-Dimashqi told me. In Damascus, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Ayyub bin Abi Aqal bin Zaid bin Al-Hassan bin Usama bin Zaid bin Haritha bin Sharahil bin Abd al-Uzza ibn Imru al-Qais ibn Aamir ibn Abd Wad ibn Awn ibn Kinanah, my uncle Zaid ibn Abi Aqal ibn Zaid told me, he told me My father, on the authority of his grandfather, Al-Hasan bin Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of his father, he said: Harithah bin Sharahil married a woman in Tayy, from Nabhan. So her children were Jablah, Asma, and Zaid. She died and left her children in their paternal grandfather’s lap, and Haritha wanted to carry them. Then their grandfather came and said: What we have is better for them, so they agreed until Jablah and Asma took off and succeeded Zaid, and horses came from Tihama from The Banu Fazara raided Tayy and took Zayd captive, so they took him to the market of Ukaz, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him before he was sent, and he said To Khadija, may God be pleased with her: “O Khadija, I saw in the market a boy whose description was Kate and Kate” - describing his mind, manners, and beauty - if only I had money I would have bought it.” Waraqah ordered Ibn Nawfal to buy it with her money, and he said: “O Khadija,Give me this boy with your own good deeds.” She said: O Muhammad, I see a poor boy and I fear that you will sell him or give him away, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “O Muwafaqa, I only wanted to adopt him.” She said: Yes, O Muhammad, so he raised him and adopted him, and he was called: Zayd bin Muhammad. Then a man from the neighborhood came and looked at Zaid and recognized him. He said: You are Zaid bin Haritha. He said: No, I am Zaid bin Muhammad. He said: No, rather you are Zaid bin Haritha is from the description of your father, your paternal aunts, and your maternal uncles, Kate and Kate. They exhausted their bodies and spent money in your cause, so Zaid said:
 [Long Sea]

 I yearn for my people, even if I am far away... for I am a homemaker in feelings.
 And abstain from the face that has displeased you... and do not do on earth the actions of cattle.
 Praise be to God, I am in the best family... a good choice, old after old.
 When he reached him, Haritha said:
 [Long Sea]

 I cried for Zaid and I did not know what he did... Will he live and be hoped for, or will the end of his life come?
 By God, I do not know, and I am asking... whether the plain of the earth has burdened you, or whether the mountains have burdened you.
 Oh, I wish my poetry could bring you back forever... Your return to me is sufficient for me in this world with great reverence
 The sun reminds me of its rising... and he presents to me his memory of when the child sneezed.And when the spirits stirred, the remembrance of him became agitated...how long my sorrows for him, oh Glory be to Him.
 I will work as hard as the devil on earth...and I will not get tired of wandering around or get tired of camels.
 Then my death will come upon me... and every person is mortal, even if hope deceives him.
 Harithah bin Sharahil came to Mecca with his brothers and family, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the courtyard of the Kaaba with a group of people. His companions included Zaid bin Haritha. When they looked at Zaid, they knew him and he knew them, but he did not stand up to them out of respect for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said to him: O Zaid, but he did not answer them. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Who are these people, O Zaid?” He said: O Messenger of God, this is my father, this is my uncle, this is my brother, and these are my clan. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Get up and greet them.” “O Zaid.” So he stood up and greeted them, and they greeted him. Then they said to him: Go with us, O Zaid. He said: I do not want a substitute for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Someone changed him, so they said: O Muhammad, we are giving you this boy as blood money, so name whatever you want, and we will carry him to you. So he said: “I ask you to “You bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Seal of His prophets and messengers, and I will send him with you.” So they repented, delayed, and hesitated.They said: “You will accept from us the dinars we have offered to you.” So he said to them: “Here is a feature other than this. I have left the matter up to him. If he wishes, Let him get up, and if he wishes, let him enter. They said: Is there anything left? They said: O Zaid, Muhammad has given you permission now, so go with us. He said: Far from it, far from it. I do not want the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a substitute, and I have no choice. He had no father or son, so they turned him around, befriended him, befriended him, and informed him of those behind him who had found them, but he refused and swore not to follow them. He said Haritha: As for me, I will console you with myself. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and the rest refused."
"4947","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, he said: It was When Harithah bin Sharahil lost his son Zaid, he cried for him and said:
 I cried for Zaid and did not know what he had done. Then he mentioned the poem in its entirety.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 4946 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"4948","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Bishr Al-Murtadi told us, Abdul Ghaffar bin Ubayd Allah bin Al-Zubair Al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Al-Mawsili told us. Mushahir, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, Jablah bin Harithah, brother of Zaid bin Harithah, narrated to me, he said: I came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I said: O Messenger of God, send my brother Zaid with me. He said: “Here he is. If he wants, I will not prevent him.” So Zaid said: No. By God, I do not choose anyone over you. Jablah said: So I said: My brother’s opinion is better than my opinion. Its chain of transmission is authentic. They did not narrate it, and he is a witness. For the past hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4948 - True"
"4949","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “Among those who witnessed Badr with... The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Zaid bin Haritha bin Sharahil al-Kalbi, the client of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4949 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"4950","Abu Ja`far al-Razi al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa: “He was the first to Zaid bin Haritha converted to Islam.”"
"4951","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Al-Alaa bin Amr Al-Hanafi told us, Saeed bin Maslamah told us, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed, I heard Amra bint Abdul Rahman saying: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, saying: “When Zaid bin Haritha and Jafar were killed Ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah Ibn Rawahah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat crying with them, and sadness was known in him.”"
"4952","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Urwa, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a mission to Mu’tah, and he fought Zayd ibn Harithah with a flag. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in Jumada al-Awwal of the eighth year, until he hunted the people’s spears, then Ja’far bin Abi Talib took them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4952 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4953","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Zahid told us, Sahl bin Ammar Al-Ataki told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Wael bin Dawud told us, I heard Al-Bahi narrates that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, used to say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never sent Zayd bin Haritha in an army except He commanded him, and if he had remained after him, he would have succeeded him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it."
"4954","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not blame us for loving Zaid,” meaning: Ibn Haritha. Ismail said: And I heard Al-Sha’bi say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never sent a troop with Zayd bin Haritha among them without his command over them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4954 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4955","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Aidh bin Yahya told me, On the authority of Abu Al-Huwayrith, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut’im, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said: “The best of the commanders of the brigades is Zaid ibn Harithah, I will divide them equally, and I will be fair in the flock.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4955 - in its chain of transmission by Al-Waqidi"
"4956","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us from the origin of his book, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abi Salama, and Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Zaid bin Haritha, may God be pleased with them, who said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on his way to one of the monuments, so we slaughtered a sheep for him and put it in the oven until it was cooked. We took it out and put it on our journey, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came walking along my side during the hot days of Mecca. Until, when we were at the top of the valley, we met Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl, and they greeted each other with the pre-Islamic greeting, and the Messenger of God said to him: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “What is the matter with me when I see your people hang you?” He said: By God, this is to change a resentment that was from me to them, but I see them as being astray. He said: So I went out seeking this religion until I came to the rabbis of Yathrib and found them worshiping God and associating partners with Him, so I said: This is not the religion I seek, so I left to go Upon the rabbis of Aila, I found them worshiping God and associating others with Him, so I said: This is not the religion I seek.Then one of the rabbis of the Levant said to me: You are asking about a religion in which we do not know anyone who worships God except an old man on the island. So I went out until I came. To him, I told him what I had come out for, and he said: Everyone I saw is in error. You are asking about a religion that is the religion of God and the religion of His angels. A prophet has come out in your land, or he is coming out, calling to him. Return to him and believe him and follow him, and believe in what he brought. So I returned and did not Something better yet, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slaughtered the camel that was under him, then we presented to him the table on which the barbecue was, and he said: What is this? So we said: “This is a sheep that we slaughtered for such-and-such sacrifice.” He said: “I do not eat anything slaughtered for anyone other than God.” It was a copper idol called: Asaf and Na'ila are used by the polytheists to wipe themselves with when they circumambulate. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated, and I circumambulated with him. When I passed, I wiped with him, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not touch him.” Zaid said: So we touched him, so I said to myself: I will touch him until I see what he says, so I wiped him, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Did you not prohibit it?” Zaid said: By the One who honored him and sent down the Book to him, I never received an idol until God honored him with the one he honored and sent down the Book to him.Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl died before he was sent, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the Day of Resurrection a nation alone will come.” Sahih. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and whoever ponders this hadith will know the virtue of Zaid and his progress in Islam before the call.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4956 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4957","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr told us dictation, Ali bin Sa`id bin Bashir al-Razi in Egypt told us, Ismail bin Ubaid bin Abi Karima al-Harrani told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Muhammad bin Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of his father Osama bin Zaid said: Ja’far, Ali, and Zaid bin Haritha gathered, and Ja’far said: I love you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said Ali: I love you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Zaid said: I love you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: So go. Us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: So I left and then came back, and said: This is Ja`far, Ali, and Zaid bin Haritha seeking permission. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give them permission.” So they entered and said: O Messenger of God, we have come to you to ask you, who is the most beloved of people to you? He said: “Fatima.” They said: We ask you about men. He said: “As for you, O Ja’far, your character resembles my character, and your character resembles my character, and you are mine.” And from my tree. As for you, O Ali, you are my brother and the father of my two sons, and from me and to me. As for you, O Zaid, you are my master, from me and to me, and I love the people. “To me” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4957 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4958","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Tajer told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Salih told us, Abu Uthman bin Salih told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Aqeel, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Usama, on the authority of Zayd ibn Harithah, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said, “He came to him when it was first revealed to him, and he showed him ablution and prayer and taught him Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4958 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"4959","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah bin Abu Bakr bin Hazzam and Salih bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of his father, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished Badr, he sent بَشِيرَيْنِ إِلَى أَهْلِ مَدِينَةٍ: بَعَثَ زَيْدَ بْنَ حَارِثَةَ إِلَى أَهْلِ السَّافِلَةِ، وَبَعَثَ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ رَوَاحَةَ إِلَى أَهْلِ الْعَالِيَةِ They give them good tidings of God’s conquest of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Zaid bin Haritha agreed with his son Osama when he settled the dust on Ruqayyah bint The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was said to him: That is your father when he came. Usama said: I came while he was standing before the people, saying: Utba bin Rabia, Shaybah bin Rabia, Abu Jahl bin Hisham, Nabih, Munabbih, and Umayyah bin Khalaf, so I said: O father, is this worthy? He said: Yes, by God, my son, “this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4959 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4960","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi told us, Shurayh bin Maslama, Ibrahim bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jablah bin Haritha, brother of Zaid, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If he did not fight, he would not give his weapons except to Ali or Zaid, may God be pleased with them. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4960 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4961","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told me about Bardan, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Yazid bin Abi Ubaid told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’ said: “I fought seven battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and nine battles with Zaid bin Haritha. He was commanded by the Messenger of God. “May God’s prayers and peace be upon us.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4961 - It is in Al-Bukhari in the Three Pieces"
"4962","Ahmad bin Sahl told us, in Bukhara, Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Hamid bin Yahya Al-Balkhi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not send Zayd on a mission except His command over them is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"4963","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim, the governor in Kufa, informed us. Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq al-Tamimi told us in Kufa. Al-Ala bin Amr told us. Al-Hanafi, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Abi Ishaq Al-Subaie narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Jabla bin Haritha, brother of Zayd bin Haritha, He said: “Two pieces of jewelry were given to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took one of them and gave the other to Zaid.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4963 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4964","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq in naming those who testified. Badr from Banu Salamah, then from Banu Adi bin Ghanam bin Salamah Bishr bin Al-Baraa bin Ma’rur bin Sakhr bin Khansa"
"4965","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani told us, Muhammad bin Ya’la told us, and Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ali told us Al-Zahid, and Abu Hamid Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Shuaib Al-Faqih said: Sahl bin Ammar Al-Ataki told us, Muhammad bin Ya’la told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us. Ibn Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who is your master, O Banu Salamah?” They said: Al-Jadd bin Qais, except that he was stingy. He said: “And what disease is more cured than stinginess? Rather, your master is Bishr bin Al-Baraa bin Ma’rour.” Sahih. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4965 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4966","Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Khalid told us, Rabah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Mubashir, may God be pleased with her, who said: I entered upon The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the pain in which he was seized. I said: May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. What do you accuse yourself of? I do not accuse my son of anything except the food he ate with you in Khaybar, and her son was Bishr ibn al-Baraa ibn Ma’rur who died before the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And I am not accusing anyone else. This is the time for my aorta to stop.” It is true on one condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4966 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4967","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdul Aziz bin Daoud Al-Harrani told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a Jewish woman invited the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions On a praying sheep. When they sat down to eat, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a morsel and put it in, then said to them: “Hold on, for this The sheep is poisoned.” So he said to the Jewess: Woe to you, for what did you poison me? “She said: I wanted to know that if you are a prophet, it will not harm you, and if not, that I might relieve the people of your distress.” Bishr ibn Bishr ate from it. Al-Baraa died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed her. “It is true according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not take him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4967 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4968","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us everything you mentioned, Ibn Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “He died Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi Kenaz ibn al-Husayn, ally of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib in Medina during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and it was said The one who died in Medina during the caliphate of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, in the year twelve was Marthad ibn Abi Marthad. Others said: “He was killed.” With two sides"
"4969","Al-Hussein bin Halim informed us: I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he told me Bishr bin Ubaid Allah, I heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, saying: I heard Abu Murthad Al-Ghanawi saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Do not sit on graves or pray over them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4969 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it due to its weakness"
"4970","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming who “Badr witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Murthad al-Ghanawi, an ally of Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib.”"
"4971","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Musa bin Harun told me, I heard Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri say: “Abu Murthad Al-Ghanawi died in... “In the year twelve of the Hijra, he was sixty-six years old.”"
"4972","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi’s name is Kanaz ibn Husayn ibn “Yarbu’ bin Amr bin Yarbu’ bin Kharsha bin Sa’d bin Tarif bin Jallan bin Ghanam bin Asar bin Sa’d bin Qays Aylan.”"
"4973","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub told me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Abu Yunus Al-Madani told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me Al-Hazami said: “Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi Kenaz bin al-Husayn, an ally of Hamza bin Abdul-Muttalib, died and was buried in Medina during the caliphate of Abu Bakr. May God be pleased with him in the year twelve.”"
"4974","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, I heard Bishr bin Ubayd Allah al-Hadrami, I heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, I heard Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not sit on graves. And do not pray to it.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it, and Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak was the only one to do so by mentioning Abu Idris Al-Khawlani about it. Bishr bin Ubayd Allah and Wathilah “It was narrated by Bishr bin Bakr and Al-Walid bin Yazid, on the authority of Bishr. I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’” “human talk”"
"4975","So Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Ubayd Allah, I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not sit on graves or pray toward them.” Sadaqa bin Khalid followed him."
"4976","Ahmad bin Ubaid al-Hafiz in Hamadan told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Abu Mushar told us, Sadaqa bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Bishr bin Ubayd Allah, I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, I heard Abu Marthad Al-Ghanawi, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Do not sit on graves, nor pray toward them.”"
"4977","Makki bin Bandar Al-Zanjani told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Yahya bin Khalid bin Amr bin Yahya bin Hamza Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hamza told me, my father told me, on the authority of his father, and he informed me on the authority of Abu Kabsha al-Saluli, on the authority of Abu Marthad Al-Ghanawi, may God be pleased with him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him as a guard, until when the face of morning approached, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “This is your friend, he has come to make a vow to you.” Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: “Did you get off your horse tonight?” He said: No, by God, O Prophet of God, unless he fulfills a need. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not worry if you do not work after this.” Yahya bin Hamza: “So I mentioned this hadith to Abu Amr Al-Awza’i, and Al-Awza’i told me: Hassan bin Atiyya used to narrate that. This is a Sunni virtue of Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, and the children of Yahya bin Hamza al-Dimashqi are unique in it from their fathers, from al-Awza’i. And they are all trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4977 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"4978","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, God said: “There were two knights with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr: one of them belonged to Marthad bin Abi Marthad, and the other belonged to Al-Zubair, may God bless him and grant him peace. “May God protect them”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4978 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4979","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Asim bin Omar bin Qatada said that people from Adhal and Al-Qarah, two neighborhoods of Jadaylah, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after Uhud, and they said: In our land Islam, so send with us a group of your companions who will teach us the Qur’an and teach us Islam.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent With them were six people, including: Marthad bin Abi Marthad, an ally of Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, who was their prince, and Khalid bin Al-Bukayr Al-Laythi. Ally of Bani Adi, Abdullah bin Tariq Al-Dhafri, Zayd bin Al-Dathna, Khubayb bin Adi, and Asim bin Thabit bin Abi Al-Aflah """", So they set out with their leader, Marthad bin Abi Marthad, until when they were in Al-Raji’, Hudhayl came to them. The people did not look after them in their camps except the men in They had swords in their hands, and they had covered them with them, so the people took their swords to fight, and they said: Oh God, we do not want to kill you, but we want to harm those who People of Mecca, for you is God’s covenant and covenant. As for Asim, Marthad, and Khalid, they fought until they were killed, and they said: By God, we will not accept any polytheist. A covenant or a contract at all
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4979 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"4980","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Saeed told me Ibn Malik Al-Ghanawi, on the authority of his father, that “Marthad ibn Abi Marthad witnessed the Day of Badr riding a horse called Al-Sabil,” Muhammad ibn Amr said: “Marthad al-Ghanawi was martyred between Uhud and Khandaq in Safar in the year four.” This indicates that Marthad was martyred before his father, Ubayy. Marthad, may God be pleased with them, for eight years. Abu Marthad died in his bed in Medina during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, for a year. Twelve, I tried to search for a hadith that was supported by a narration on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I did not find anything except the hadith that “"
"4981","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Yahya bin Ya’la, on the authority of Al-Qasim Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Marthad bin Abi Marthad Al-Ghanawi, who was Badr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It pleases you to be accepted.” Your prayer, let your chosen ones lead you, for they are your delegation in what is between you and your Lord Almighty.”"
"4982","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa “in naming who Jabbar bin Sakhr bin Umayyah bin Khansa bin Sinan witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4983","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, he said: “Jabbar bin Sakhr died in Medina in the year thirty He is sixty-two years old.”"
"4984","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Bazzar Al-Asqalani told us, Muadh bin Khalid told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad, Sharhabeel bin Saad told us, that he heard Jabbar bin Sakhr, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I We are forbidden from seeing our private parts.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4984 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4985","Abu Abdullah told us, with his chain of transmission, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Omar, who said: “Abu Hudhayfah’s conversion to Islam occurred before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered.” He lived in Dar Al-Arqam and was among those who emigrated two migrations.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4985 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it due to its weakness. Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “Abu Hudhayfah witnessed Badr and called his father to Stool. His sister Hind bint Utbah said to him when he called his father to stool:
 [Simple Sea]
 The cross-eyed, the foxed, the cursed bird... Abu Hudhayfah is the worst of people in religion.
 Didn’t you thank your father who raised you when you were young...until you grew up as a young man without shame?"
"4986","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Waqidi, he said: “And Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah was a tall man with a beautiful face, and his mother was Umm Safwan.”"
"4987","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, I am Wahb bin Jarir, my father told me, I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah ibn Rabi’ah was martyred on the Day of Al-Yamamah.”"
"4988","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Ma`bad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of Badr: “Whoever among you meets Abbas So let him stop it, for he left in disgrace.” Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah said: “Should we kill our fathers, brothers, and clans, and leave Abbas alone?” By God, I will strike him with the sword. Then I reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: “O Abu Hafs,” Omar, may God be pleased with him, said. On his authority: It was the first day on which I was insulted by Abu Hafs - the face of the Messenger of God’s uncle was struck with a sword. “So Omar said: Leave me so that I may strike his neck. He had hypocrites, and Abu Hudhayfah was saying: I am not safe from that word that I said, and I am still afraid until God expiates it for me. With testimony, he said: So he was killed on the Day of Al-Yamamah as a martyr, “correct according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not produce him.”"
"4989","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Salih told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jabir, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mahran, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Muawiyah entered upon Ubayy Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah found him crying, so he said: What makes you cry? Pain or eagerness for the world? He said: No, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, making a covenant with me, so I said: What is it? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perhaps a time will overtake you and they will gather a group while you are in it.” And I have gathered what he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. He acknowledged, “In the hadith, they are obscene, which is that Abu Hudhayfah Utbah bin Rabi’ah was martyred before Muawiyah converted to Islam, but he only said This is what Muawiyah said to his uncle Abu Hashim bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah on the day of Siffin.”"
"4990","Tell us that what you mentioned is correct, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Bakr bin bint Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Jadi told us, we told him Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Mu’awiyah entered upon Abu Hashim and mentioned the story with his example, “They disagreed about the name of Abu Hudhayfah.” Bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and he said: His name is Hushaym."
"4991","As Abu Ishaq bin Yahya and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub told us, they said: I am Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Abu Yunus told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, he said: “Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah, his name is Hushaym, and it was said: Abu Hudhayfah’s name is Hasal.”"
"4992","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, I heard Yahya bin Ma’in say: “Abu Hudhayfah bin Utba bin Rabi’ah’s name is Hasl. I fear that he is an illusion in it, for Al-Yaman, Hudhayfah’s father, was nicknamed Hasl, and it was said: His name is Asal.”"
"4993",""
"4994","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Harun al-Faqih told us, Muhammad ibn Nusayr told us with his chain of transmission, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sa’d, who said: “It is said that the name of my father Hudhayfah bin Utbah, Hushaym and it is also said: Divided."
"4995","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Yazid told me Ibn Ruman, on the authority of Urwah Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the cauldron to be thrown into it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood over them and said: “O people of the heart, have you found what your Lord promised to be true?” For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” Then his companions said: O Messenger of God, do you speak to dead people? He said: “They know that what your Lord has promised you is true.” When he ordered them to be withdrawn, he saw on the face of Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utba’s hatred. And his father was being dragged to the pit, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “O Abu Hudhayfah, by God, it is as if what happened to your father displeased you.” He said: By God, O Messenger of God, I have no doubt in God or in the Messenger of God, but if he was forbearing and of sound opinion, then I hoped that he would not die. Until God Almighty guides him to Islam. When I saw that it had passed, and that it happened where it happened, it saddened me. He said: So a messenger called for him. May God bless him and grant him peace. “It is authentic according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4995 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4996","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “And Qutubah bin Amer bin Hadidah witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Badr, the same day in which the following verse was revealed: “Righteousness is not that you enter houses from... Its appearance} [Al-Baqarah: 189] And his brother Yazid bin Amir bin Hudaydah, and Yazid was nicknamed Abu Al-Mundhir."
"4997","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told me, on the authority of Sheikhs from his people said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out during the season in which a group of Ansar met him, and he presented himself to Arab tribes, then they departed from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returning to their country. They believed and believed Qutbah bin Amir bin"
"4998","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Ibn Abi Sabra told me, Ishaq bin Abdullah told me, Ibn Ka’b bin Malik told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Qutba bin Amir bin Hadidah with twenty men to the neighborhood of Khath'am in Safar in the year seven."
"4999","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Ibrahim bin Mahdi told us, Abu Saeed Al-Muaddeb told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take the Qur’an from four: from Abdullah Ibn Masoud, and from Muadh, and from Ubayy, and from Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfah. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4999 - Weak"
"5000","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Muhammad bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, on the authority of his sheikhs, he said: “Salem The servant of Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah was the servant of Thubaytah bint Ya’ar al-Ansariyya, and she was a slave of Abu Hudhayfah, so he adopted him, and it was said Salem bin Abi Hudhayfah. When the Qur’an was revealed {Call them by their fathers} [Al-Ahzab: 5] it was said to Salem, the servant of Abi Hudhayfah, that he was killed as a martyr on the Day of Al-Yamamah. In the year twelve, his head was found near Abu Hudhayfah’s leg, or Abu Hudhayfah’s leg was at his head.” Musa bin Utbah said: “He is Salim bin Maqil from the people of Istakhr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5000 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5001","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram told us: Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us: Musa bin Harun al-Bardi told us: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us: Hanzala bin Abi Sufyan, that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit speaking, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I delayed one night The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after dinner, then I came, and he said to me: “Where have you been?” I said: We were listening to the recitation of a man of your companions in the mosque. I had never heard anything like his voice, nor a recitation from one of your companions. So he stood up and I stood up. He was with him until he listened to him, then he turned to me and said: “This is Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah. Praise be to God who has created such among my nation.” It is true that The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5001 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5002","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Sa’id bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Yahya bin Sa’id, that he heard Amra bint Abdul Rahman narrates that Abu Hudhayfah’s wife mentioned, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, my father told me, Suwayd bin Saeed, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that he heard Amra bint Abdul Rahman narrate, on the authority of Aisha, that my father’s wife Hudhayfah mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the entry of Salim, Abu Hudhaifa’s client, upon her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Breastfeed him,” so she breastfed him after he witnessed a full moon, and he used to enter upon her “healthy, according to the condition of a Muslim, but they did not take him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5002 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5003","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told me, My father, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jahm, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr. That he said: “Salim’s mother, the Ansariyah, made Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah, a slave for God, and that he was killed on the Day of Al-Yamamah, and she inherited a weapon.” And a horse, so Omar bin Al-Khattab sent to her: Take it, you are the people most deserving of it. She said: I have no need of it, for I had left it for God. God Almighty when I freed him, then Omar, may God be pleased with him, took him and put him in the path of God Almighty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5003 - This is not correct"
"5004","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told us, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, said: “When Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfah, was killed, they said: A quarter of the Qur’an was gone.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”"
"5005","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shuraih told us, Abu Sakhr told me, Zayd bin Aslam told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, that he said to his companions: “Wish for it.” Some of them said: I wish for it. This house is filled with gold, which I spend in the way of God and give in charity. A man said: I wish it were filled with aquamarines and gems. So spend it for the sake of God and give in charity. Then Omar said: “Wish it were.” They said: We do not know, O Commander of the Faithful. Omar said: “I wish it were.” It is full of men like Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, Muadh bin Jabal, Salem, the client of Abu Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5005 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5006","Abu Abdullah bin Battah narrated that to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm narrated to us, I am Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, he said: He narrated to me Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Rahman, from the descendants of Zaid bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of his father, who said: Zaid bin Al-Khattab used to carry the banner of the Muslims. On the Day of Al-Yamamah, the Muslims were exposed until Hanifa appeared against the men, and Zayd ibn Al-Khattab started saying: “As for the men, there are no men. Men, there are no men.” Then he started shouting at the top of his voice, “Oh God, I apologize to you for the flight of my companions, and I absolve you of what they brought.” Musaylimah and Muhkam bin Tufayl, and he began to pull the banner forward with it towards the enemy’s throat, then he struck with his sword until he was killed, may God have mercy on him. Upon him, and the flag fell, and Salem, Abu Hudhayfah’s servant, took it, and the Muslims said: O Salem, we fear that we will be attacked by you, and he said: How miserable is the bearer of the Qur’an if you come from me, and Zayd ibn al-Khattab was killed in the year twelve of the Hijra."
"5007","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Nawfal bin Musahaq, he said Ibn Umar: “The fifth of five companions in the raids on Musaylimah, and they killed others. It was said: Zayd ibn al-Khattab, Abdullah ibn Makhramah, and two others.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5007 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"5008","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me: Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab said: Omar used to be afflicted with a calamity, and he would say: “I was struck by Zayd bin Al-Khattab, so I was patient.” And Omar saw his satisfaction. By God, on his authority, he killed his brother Zaid, and he said to him: “Woe to you! You have killed a brother of mine who had never been young without mentioning him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5008 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5009","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Muhammad bin Rusta told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, Al-Waqidi told us, Omar bin Uthman Al-Habashi told us, on the authority of His fathers, on the authority of Umm Qais bint Muhsin, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and Ukkasha was forty years old, and he was killed after that.” In the year in Buzakha during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, in the year twelve, and Okasha was one of the most beautiful people.”"
"5010","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman the jurist in Baghdad told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The first group to enter Paradise Their faces were in the light of the moon on a full-moon night, then those next to them were in the brightest shining star that shone in the sky.” So Okasha bin Muhsin, and he said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them, and he said: “O God, make him one of them.” Then another person got up and said: O Messenger of God, “I pray to God to make me one of them.” He said: “Okasha preceded you to it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5010 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5011","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abdullah bin Suleiman told me, On the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, who said: “We were the advance force of two hundred knights, and over us Zayd ibn al-Khattab, and Thabit ibn Aqram and Okasha ibn Muhsin were in front of us. When we passed by them, they were killed, Sareya, Khalid, and the Muslims. Behind us, they stood over them, and Khaled ordered a dig for them and buried them with their blood.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5011 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5012","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Ma’an bin Adi Ibn al-Jadd Ibn al-Ajlan, an ally of Banu Amr Ibn Awf, witnessed Aqaba, Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and the scenes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he was killed on the Day of Al-Yamamah as a martyr during the caliphate of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5013","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, my father told us, on the authority of Salih, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, he said: “Ma’an ibn Adi was killed at al-Yamamah on the day of Musaylamah al-Kaddhab.”"
"5014","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, he said: “Abbad bin Bishr bin Waqsh was one of the Banu Abd al-Ashhal is nicknamed Abu Bishr and is called Abu al-Rabi`."
"5015","Abu Abdullah bin Battah narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad bin Omar narrated to us, he said: “Abbad bin Bishr bin Qash bin Zugha bin Za’ura bin Abd al-Ashhal was nicknamed Abu Bishr. Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Bishr bin Amara said: “He was He is known as Abu Al-Rabi’. He embraced Islam in Medina at the hands of Mus’ab bin Umair. This was before Saad bin Muadh converted to Islam, and Abbad bin Bishr witnessed Badr. He was among those who killed Ka'b bin Al-Ashraf, and he also witnessed Uhud, the trench, and the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he also witnessed on the Day of Al-Yamamah, and on that day there was tribulation and hardship, and he went to battle until he was killed on that day as a martyr. That was in the year twelve, and he was the son of Forty-five years”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5015 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5016","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “There were three Banu Abdul-Ashhal who were not One of them is better than them: Saad bin Muadh, Usayd bin Hudair, and Abbad bin Bishr. “Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr said: By God, he did not name me.” Abi Abbad said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5016 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5017","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, they said: “The name of my father Dujana Samak bin Kharsha bin Luthan bin Abd Wad bin Zaid bin Tha’labah bin Al-Khazraj, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother among them. And Utba bin Ghazwan, and Abu Dujana witnessed Badr and Uhud, and stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and pledged allegiance to him on that day. Death, and he witnessed Al-Yamamah and was among those who participated in the killing of Musaylimah, and Abu Dujana was killed that day as a martyr.”"
"5018","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj told us Bin Minhaal, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a sword on the day of Uhud. And his companions surrounded him, and he said: “Who will take this sword?” So they spread out their hands. He said: This is me. He said: This is me. Then he said: Who will take him for his rights? The people were reluctant, so Sammak Abu Dujana said: I will take him as he deserves, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him away, and he was separated from him on that day. The polytheists
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5018 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5019","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us dictation, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Al-Wazi’ bin Thawr, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, displayed a sword. On the day of Uhud, he said: “Who will take this sword by rights?” So I got up and said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He turned away from me and then said: “Who will take this sword for its own sake?” So I said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He turned away from me and then said: “Who will take this sword by rights?” Then Abu Dujana Samak bin Kharsha stood up and said: O Messenger of God, I am taking him according to his right. What is his right? He said: “That you do not kill a Muslim with it, and do not flee with it from an infidel.” He said: So he pushed him to it, and when he wanted to fight, he knew about a group. He said: I said: Let us look at him today, how he is doing? He said: So he did not do anything for him except to tear him apart and spread him thin until he came to women at the foot of the mountain who had tambourines, and among them was a woman. And she says:
 [The sea of rage]

 We are the daughters of Tariq... we walk on the tigers
 If you accept, we will embrace...and spread out our palms.
 Or contemplate our parting...an irresistible separation.
 He said: So he swung the sword towards a woman to strike her, then he stopped her. When the fight became clear to him, I said to him: I have seen all your work except... You raised the sword against the woman and you did not hit her. He said: By God, I honored the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to kill a woman with it. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5019 - True"
"5020","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa “in naming Whoever witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was from Banu Adi Tha’labah bin Anama bin Adi, and he was martyred on the Day of the Trench.”"
"5021","Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, about Haram bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Atiq, and Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Jabir, that Tha’labah bin Anama came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was He was sitting, and he greeted someone with a gold ring on his finger, but he did not respond to him. Then he greeted him, but he did not respond to him. It was said: O Messenger of God, he greets you. Alopecia three times, but she did not respond to him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you not see my face covered with an ember of fire in his hand?” So he threw the stone. Vixen with a ring
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5021 - Haram bin Othman perished"
"5022","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq “in naming those who “Bani Zurayq bin Amir witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then from Banu Al-Ajlan Rafi’ bin Malik bin Al-Ajlan Al-Zarqi.”"
"5023","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym, and Ahmad bin Salama told us, they said: Qutayba bin Saeed told us, we told him Rifa’ah bin Yahya bin Abdullah bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ah, on the authority of his father’s uncle Muadh bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ah bin Malik, who said: I prayed He came behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I sneezed and said: Praise be to God, very good and blessed praise be to Him, blessed be He as our Lord loves. He was satisfied, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, he left and said: “Who is speaking during the prayer?” So I said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: “So what did you say?” He said: I said, Praise be to God, a great, good, and blessed praise, as our Lord loves and is pleased with him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And who My soul is in His hand. Thirty-and-one angels hastened to see which of them would take it up.” Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, and we did not write it down except on his authority, so he mentioned the hadith like it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5023 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5024","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Shaarani told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, I am Abdul Aziz bin Imran, Rifa’ah bin Yahya told me, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ bin Malik, on the authority of his father, he said: When he On the day of Badr, people gathered to attack Umayyah ibn Khalaf, so I approached him and looked at a piece of his armor that had been torn off from under his armpit. He said: So I stabbed him with a sword and killed him, and I was shot with an arrow on the Day of Badr and my eye went out. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spat on it and called. “For me, none of it harmed me.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5024 - Abdul Aziz bin Imran is weak"
"5025","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ubaid. Ibn Rifa’ah Ibn Rafi’ Ibn Malik Ibn Ajlan Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ Ibn Malik, who said: The day of Badr has come. Then we lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the companions called out to one another: Is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among you? So they stood until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and with him was Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. They said: O Messenger of God, we have lost you. So he said: “Abu Hassan had pain in his stomach, so I stayed behind to see him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5025 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5026","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Al-Aswad told us, Urwa told us “in naming those who witnessed Aqaba is from the Ansar from Banu Zurayk, Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ bin Malik bin Al-Ajlan bin Zurayk, and he is a captain and he was also mentioned in his name. Whoever witnessed Badr?"
"5027","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told me, Shabab Al-Asfari told us, he said: “Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ bin Malik bin Al-Ajlan bin Amr bin Amir bin Zuraiq bin Abd Haritha, his mother, and the mother of his brother Khallad bin Rafi’, the mother of Malik bint Ubayy Ibn Salul, Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ died when Muawiyah rose up.”"
"5028","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Thabet bin Qais bin Shammas told us. Ibn Imru' al-Qais Ibn Malik, the orator of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, witnessed Uhud, the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he was killed as a martyr on the Day of Al-Yamamah."
"5029","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan Al-Asadi told us, my father told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq He said: “Thabet bin Qais bin Shammas was martyred on the Day of Al-Yamamah, and Abu Bakr presented him to the Ansar along with Khalid bin Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him."
"5030","Muhammad ibn Issa al-Attar told me about Marw. I heard Ahmad ibn Sayyar say: “The surname of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas is Abu Abd al-Rahman.”"
"5031","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abu Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent man Abu Bakr is. The man is Omar, what an excellent man is Abu Ubaidah bin al-Jarrah, what an excellent man is Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas, what an excellent man is Muadh bin Jabal, what a fine man is Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh, what a miserable man is so-and-so and so-and-so.” Seven men were named by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but Suhail did not name them for us. “Sahih on The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5031 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5032","Abu Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Ibn Aoun told us, Musa bin Anas, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “On the Day of Al-Yamamah, I came to Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas, and he was He was being mummified, so I said: Uncle, don’t you see what people are doing? So he put on his shrouds, then he went and said: Now, now, and he started saying: With spices like this, and Al-Ansari gestured to his leg like this in The faces of the people fight against the people. It is unfortunate that you have not become accustomed to your peers. This is not how we used to fight with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he fought until he was killed. “Sahih According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5032 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5033","Imam Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told me, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh Al-Warraq told me, saying: Al-Hussein bin Sufyan told us, Wahb bin Baqiya told us, I Khaled, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: Thabit ibn Qais delivered a speech at the arrival of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Medina, and he said: We prevent you from what we prevent ourselves and our children from, so what do we have? He said: “Paradise.” He said: We are satisfied. “It is true according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5033 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5034","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Attar told me about Marw, Abdan bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Baghdadi told us. He was called Al-Araj, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us. My father told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ismail bin Muhammad bin Thabit Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, that Thabit bin Qais said: O Messenger of God, I was afraid that I might have perished. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Why?” He said: God forbade us from wanting to be praised for what we did not do, and I find that I love praise. He forbade us from vanity, and I find that I love beauty. He forbade us from raising our voices above your voice, while I was loud, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Thabit, are you not satisfied with “Do you live a praiseworthy life, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: He lived a laudable life, and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musailamah al-Kadhab. “It is true according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this.” Driving” Only Muslim narrated the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah and Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the verse “Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet” was revealed [Al-Hujurat: 2], Thabit bin Qais came and mentioned the hadith briefly.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5034 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5035","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Musa bin Ismail told me, Hammad bin Salamah told me, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, “that Thabit bin Qais came on the Day of Al-Yamamah, having mummified himself and wearing his shrouds, and his companions had been defeated, and he said: O God, I disavow before you what he brought. These people, and I apologize to you for what these people have done, what a miserable thing you have become accustomed to is your peers. They stayed between us and our peers for an hour, then he took off and fought for an hour. So he was killed, and his armor had been stolen, and a man saw him as a sleeper would see, and he said: My armor is in a pot under a shroud in such-and-such a place, and he willed With wills, he asked for the shield and found it where he said: So they carried out his will “truly according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it, and the hadith of his commandments has a story.”"
"5036","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Ata’ al-Khurasani told me, he said: I came to Medina and came to the daughter of Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, and I mentioned the story of her father. She said: When God revealed to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, {Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet} [Al-Hujurat: 2] the verse, and the verse {And God does not like every Arrogant and proud} [Al-Hadid: 23] My father sat in his house crying, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost him. He asked him about his situation, and he said: I am a man. His voice was loud, and I feared that he had thwarted my work, so he said: “Rather, you will live as a praiseworthy person, and die as a martyr, and God will admit you to Paradise in peace.” When the day came Al-Yamamah with Khalid bin Al-Walid. He was martyred, and a man from among the Muslims saw him in his dream and said: When I was killed, a man from among the Muslims snatched my armor. Muslims and hid him in the farthest part of the army while he was with him, and he leaned on the shield with a twine, and placed a saddle on the twine, so he missed the prince. So tell him, and beware of saying, “This is a dream,” or you will waste it. And when you come to Medina, go and say to the successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I owe such-and-such a debt, and my servant is so-and-so who is an old slave of mine, and beware of saying, “This is a dream” and thus wasting it. He said: So he came to him and told him. He found the matter as he told him, and he came to Abu Bakr and told him, so he carried out his will, and we do not know of anyone who did so after he died. His will is none other than Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5036 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5037","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Shadhakuni told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me He said: “And Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’ bin Abd Al-Uzza bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf bin Qusayy, and Abu Al-Aas’s name was Maqsim, and his mother’s name was Maqsim. Hala bint Khuwaylid bin Asad bin Abdul Uzza bin Qusayy, and her paternal aunt was Khadija bint Khuwaylid, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married his daughter Zainab before Islam, and she bore him Ali and Umamah. Ali died when he was young, and she remained alive. Umamah until Ali bin Abi Talib married her after the death of Fatima, may God be pleased with her. Abu Al-Aas was among those who witnessed Badr with him. The polytheists, and Abdullah bin Jubayr bin Al-Numan Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them, captured him. When the people of Mecca sent him to ransom their captives, he came Concerning the ransom of Abu Al-Aas, his brother Amr bin Al-Rabi’, with money given to him by Zainab. I have mentioned above what happened between him and Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until Zainab was martyred. Listen now to the good outcome of Abu Al-Aas, his good conversion to Islam, and his move to Medina until... He died in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5038","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Yahya told me Ibn Abbad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: When the people of Mecca were sent to As a ransom for their captives, Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to ransom Abu Al-Aas with money and in it she sent a necklace that was Khadija’s. I brought it to Abu Al-Aas when he built on it. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that necklace, he felt very tender for it and said: “If you decide to release her prisoner and return to her what is hers, do so.” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so release him and return to him what is hers. For it, and Abu Al-Aas continued to adhere to his trap until, shortly before the conquest of Mecca, he went out to trade to the Levant with money from the money of the Quraysh. They sold it with him, and when he finished his trade and a caravan arrived, a convoy of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him. It was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was the one who directed the expedition to the caravan in which Abu Al-Aas held a caravan from the Levant, and they were seventy and one hundred riders.Their prince was Zaid bin Haritha, and that was in Jumada al-Awwal in the year six of the Hijra. They took the burdens in that caravan, and took them prisoner. People from the caravan, but Abu Al-Aas prevented them from escaping. When the company arrived, because of what they had befallen, Abu Al-Aas came during the night to ask for his money until he entered the Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sought protection from her and she rented to him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the morning prayer So he grew and the people grew with him
 Ibn Ishaq said: Yazid bin Roman told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Zainab, may God be pleased with her, screamed: O people, I have rewarded Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’. He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him from his prayer, he turned to the people and said: “O People, did you hear what I heard? They said: Yes, he said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I did not know of anything that had happened until I heard from him what you heard. Indeed, he is generous to the Muslims.” The closest of them.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left and went to see his daughter Zainab and said: “My daughter, honor his resting place, and he will not be alone with you.” You are not permissible for him.”
 Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told me, on the authority of Amra,On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to the company who had raided the property of Abu Al-Aas and said to them: “Indeed This man is one of us, as you know, and you have acquired wealth for him. If you do good, return to him what is his. We like that, but if you refuse. That is the reward of God, which He has bestowed upon you, and you are more deserving of it.” They said: O Messenger of God, rather, we will return it to him. He said: “Return his money to him.” To the point that a man would bring a rope, and another would bring a spear and a tool, and one of them would even bring a straw, until they returned his money to him. Then he carried it to Mecca, and gave to everyone who had wealth from the Quraysh his wealth from someone who was taller than him, then he said: Oh People of Quraysh, do any of you have any money left that he did not take? They said: No, may God reward you with good, for we have found you loyal and generous. He said: For I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger, and nothing prevented me from accepting Islam in his presence except for fear that you would think that I only wanted to take your money, so when God Almighty gave it to me To you, and I finished it. I converted to Islam. Then he left and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 Ibn Ishaq said: Dawud bin Al-Husayn told me,On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, responding to Zainab with the first marriage, and nothing happened after six years.” Then Abu Al-Aas returned to Mecca after he converted to Islam, and he did not witness a scene with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he came to Medina after that. He died in Dhul-Hijjah in the year twelve during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he left his will to Al-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam, may God be pleased with him. About him"
"5039","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, that “Dirar bin Al-Azwar, the poet, the name of Al-Azwar is Malik bin Aws bin Judhaymah bin Rabi’ah bin Malik bin Tha’labah bin Asad bin Khuzaymah, and he was Dharaar, a poet-knight who witnessed the Day of the Dove and fought so hard until all his legs were cut off, so he began to get down on his knees and fight as he stepped on it. The horse until death overcame it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5039 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"5040","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Dirar bin Al-Azwar Al-Asadi was killed on the day of Ajnadin"
"5041","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Hassan bin Ali bin Al-Bari told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak, narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ya’qub ibn Buhair, on the authority of Dirar ibn Al-Azwar, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with a sputum. From my family, so he said to me: “Milk her.” So I went to make her tired, and he said: “Do not make her tired. Leave the need for milk.” The chain of narration is authentic and it is not preserved due to any harm. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, other than this. As for his virtue, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him when he recited his poem which “"
"5042","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Omar Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Dirar bin Al-Azwar, may God be pleased with him, when he converted to Islam, came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted and proceeded to say:
 [The Converging Sea]

 I left off the cup and playing the qāyān...and wine as a prayer and supplication.
 And I encroached upon the ink in the depths...and my effort was upon the Muslims to fight.
 Jamila said, “You have scattered us...and you have dispersed your family far north.”
 O Lord, let me not be deprived of my deal... I have sold my family and my money for nothing.
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How foolish your deal was, O Dirar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5042 - True"
"5043","Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat Al-Asfri told us, he said: “Abu Kabsha died A servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year thirteen.”"
"5044","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, they said: “Abu Abu Kabsha is a slave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His name is Sulaim, and he was one of the people born in the land of Dos. Abu Kabsha witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted Badr and Uhud and all the other scenes, and he died on the first day that Omar ibn al-Khattab was appointed successor, and that was on Tuesday for eight nights. They remained from Jumada al-Awwal in the thirteenth year of the Hijra.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5044 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5045","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr. He said: “And he was among those who witnessed Badr from Banu Hashim bin Abd Manaf, Abu Kabsha, the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5046","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us all of that, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs."
"5047","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi informed us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us Ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, my father told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: “Talib ibn Umair embraced Islam in Dar al-Arqam, then he entered and left. On his mother, who is Arwa bint Abdul Muttalib, and he said: I followed Muhammad and submitted to God, Lord of the Worlds, glory be to Him, and she said: His mother has more right Whomever you support and whoever you support is your cousin. By God, if we were capable of what men are capable of, we would follow him and defend him. He said: So I said: Oh mother, what prevents you from converting to Islam and following him, since your brother Hamza has converted to Islam? She said: I will see what my sisters do, and then I will be? One of them said: I said: I ask you by God, will you not come to him and greet him and say the truth to him and bear witness that there is no god but God? She said: I I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She used to support the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In her own words, she urges her son to support him and do his job. “It is authentic and strange according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"5048","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf. Abdul-Hakim bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas said: “When Khaled bin Saeed converted to Islam and his father Abu Uhayha did to him what he did to him, he did not return from his religion, and he was bound to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his son Amr bin Saeed followed his religion. When Amr converted to Islam, he joined his brother Khaled in the land of Abyssinia. And with him was his wife Fatima bint Safwan bin Umayyah.”
 Muhammad bin Omar said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Umm Khaled bint Khalid bin Saeed, who said: “Amr bin Saeed came to us from the land of Abyssinia after my father’s arrival, and he remained there until he was taken on two ships with the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then they came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was at Khaybar in the seventh year of the Hijra. Amr testified with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Al-Fath, Hunayn, Al-Taif, and Tabuk. When the Jews went out to the Levant, he was among those who went out, and he was killed on the day of Ajnadin, as a martyr in the caliphate of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq. May God be pleased with him in Jumada al-Awwal in the thirteenth year, and Amr ibn al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, was among the people at that time."
"5049","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Bahili told us, Al-Asma’i said: “Khalid bin Saeed, Aban bin Saeed, and Amr bin Saeed were among the people of precedence in Islam, as were Uhayhah and Al-Aas. Ibn Sa`id ibn al-Aas were killed on the day of Badr as unbelievers, but Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, killed them all.” When I mentioned him in the Khaled bin Saeed"
"5050","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Hisham ibn al-Aas, his mother was Harmala bint Hisham bin Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman bin Omar bin Makhzoum»"
"5051","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, they said: “Hisham Ibn Al-Aas Ibn Wael Ibn Hashim Ibn Saeed Ibn Sahm, and his mother’s name is Harmala bint Hisham Ibn Al-Mughirah, and Hisham was a pre-Islamic person. In Mecca before his brother Amr, he migrated to the land of Abyssinia, then he came to Mecca when the Prophet’s emigrant, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached Medina. He wanted to join him, but his father and his people imprisoned him in Mecca until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the ditch, and he witnessed Medina. This is from all the signs, and he was younger than his brother Amr ibn al-Aas.”
 Ibn Umar said: Thawr ibn Yazid told me, on the authority of Khalid ibn Ma’dan, who said: “When the Romans were defeated on the day of Ajnadin, they ended up in a place It is a strait that can only be crossed by one person after another, so the Romans started fighting over it, and they advanced and crossed it, so Hisham bin Al-Aas bin Wael advanced. So he fought them for it until he was killed, and that was at the beginning of the caliphate of Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, in the year thirteen.”"
"5052","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Ubi told us, Makhramah bin Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj told us, on the authority of Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar bin Makhramah said: “Hisham bin Al-Aas bin Wael was a righteous man. One day he saw two Muslim armies facing each other.” retreating from their enemy, so he offered forgiveness and then said: O community of Muslims, these uncircumcised people have no patience with the sword, so do as you do. I will do it, he said: Then he began to enter among them and kill a group of them, and he began to advance towards the enemy’s throat while shouting: To me, O community of Muslims, To me, Hisham bin Al-Aas bin Wael, were you fleeing from the security of Paradise until he was killed, may God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5052 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5053","Hamid bin Muhammad Al-Muddhikir told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sons of Al-Aas are believers, Hisham and Amr.” Sahih according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5053 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5054","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Faryabi told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Abd Al-Dimashqi told us Al-Rahman bin Bashir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Nafi’ informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “We used to say: No one has the ability to repent. If he left his religion after his conversion to Islam and knowledge of it, then God revealed among them {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of God’s mercy} [Al-Zumar: 53] So I wrote it down with my own hand, then I sent it to Hisham bin Al-Aas bin Wa’il, who shouted it out and sat on his camel, then proceeded to Medina. “May God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5054 - Abd al-Rahman bin Bashir Munkar al-Hadith"
"5055","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, that Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abu Sabra was narrated by Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Habiba, the client of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: When On the day of the conquest of Mecca, Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl fled, and his wife, Umm Hakim bint Al-Harith bin Hisham, was a sane woman who converted to Islam. Then she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for safety for her husband. He ordered her to return him, so she went out in search of him and said to him: I came to you from The most virtuous of people, the most virtuous of people, and the best of people. I trusted you, so he trusted you. So he returned with her. When he approached Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he greeted his companions: “Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl comes to you as a believer and an emigrant, so do not curse his father, for cursing the dead harms the living, and do not He reaches the dead.” When he reached the door of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he rejoiced and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, jumped up to him, standing on his feet. Happy with his arrival
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5055 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5056","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us, Ubayy told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa said: Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl fled on the day of the conquest, heading to Yemen, and Umm Hakim bint Al-Harith bin Hisham came and she was On that day, she was Muslim and was under Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl. “So she asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask for her husband, and he gave her permission.” And he made him safe.” So she went out with a Roman for her, and he turned her away from herself. She continued wishing for him and getting close to him until she came to people from Mecca. So she cried out to them for help, and they bound him. Then she caught up with her husband, some Tihamah, who had been boarding a ship. When he sat on it, he called out “Lalat.” And Al-Uzza, and the ship’s owners said: No one will pass here calling on anything except God alone as a sincere one. Ikrimah said: By God, if he is in The sea alone is that it is on land alone. I swear to God that I will return to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Ikrimah returned with his wife. “So he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and pledged allegiance to him, and he accepted from him,” and a man from Hudhayl entered when Banu Bakr was defeated, fleeing from his wife. She blamed him, belittled him, and reproached him for running away, so he said:
 [The sea of rage]

 And if you had seen us in the service... when Safwan fled and Ikrimah fled
 And they stabbed us with sharp swords... cutting off every forearm and every skull.
 You did not say the slightest word of blame.
 Urwah said: On that day, two Muslim armies were martyred, then Quraysh, then Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl, from Banu Makhzum.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5056 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5057","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl said: When I reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: O Muhammad, this You told me that you believed in me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are safe.” So I said: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, without any partner. To him, and you are the servant of God and His Messenger, and you are the most righteous of people, the most truthful of people, and the most loyal of people. Ikrimah said: I say that and I am humbled. My head was ashamed of him, then I said: O Messenger of God, ask forgiveness for me for every hostility I have shown you or any procession in which I was placed in which I wish to show Polytheism, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O God, forgive Ikrimah for every hostility he has shown, or any procession he has placed in which he wants to repel.” On your way.” I said: O Messenger of God, show me the best of what you know, and I will teach him. He said: “Say: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad His servant and His Messenger, and you struggle in His way.” Then Ikrimah said: By God, O Messenger of God, I will not spare the expense I spent in preventing in the way of God unless I spend twice as much in the way of God, and I do not fight a fight in averting people from the path of God unless I spend twice as much in the way of God, then He worked hard in fighting until he was killed on the day of Ajnadin, as a martyr during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He used it in the year of his proof against Hawazin to confirm it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ikrimah died that day in Tabala.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5057 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5058","Abu Al-Hasan Al-Amri told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told me, Abu Yunus told me Al-Qushayri, Habib bin Abi Thabit told me, “Al-Harith bin Hisham, Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl, and Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah decided On the Day of Yarmouk, Al-Harith called for water to drink, and Ikrimah looked at him. Al-Harith said: Push him to Ikrimah, and Ayyash ibn Ayyash looked at him. Abu Rabi’ah, and Ikrimah said: Push him to Ayyash, but he did not reach Ayyash or to any of them until they died without having tasted it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5058 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5059","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah Al-Nahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me the day I came as a migrant: “Welcome to the passenger.” The immigrant, welcome the immigrant passenger, welcome the immigrant passenger.” So I said: By God, O Messenger of God, I will not leave an expense that I have spent I spent the like of it in the cause of God Almighty. “The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5059 - True, but interrupted"
"5060","Abu Abdullah Al-San’ani told me in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told me, Abdul Razzaq told me, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of my father Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw in “The dream is as if Abu Jahl came to me and pledged allegiance to me.” When Khalid ibn al-Walid converted to Islam, it was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: God has fulfilled your vision. O Messenger of God, this was Khalid’s Islam, so he said: “Let there be something else,” until Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl converted to Islam, and that was the truth. His vision is “authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5060 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5061","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Al-Muttalib bin Kathir told us, Al-Zubayr bin Musa, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw that my father was a fool of ignorance.” In Paradise.” When Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl converted to Islam, he said: “O Umm Salamah, this is him.”
 Umm Salamah said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ikrimah complained to him that when he passed through Medina, he was told: This is the son of an enemy. God is the father of ignorance, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and delivered a sermon and said: “People are minerals. Their choice in ignorance is their choice in Islam.” “If they understand, ‘Do not harm a Muslim with an infidel.’” Authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5061 - There are no weak narrators in it"
"5062","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, I am Ismail bin Ishaq, Suleiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika said: Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl used to take the Qur’an, place it on his face, cry, and say: “The words of my Lord are the Book of my Lord.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5062 - Sent"
"5063","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “As for Abu Quhafa Al-Taymi, he Othman bin Amir bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Saad bin Taym bin Murrah converted to Islam on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he died in Mecca in Muharram in the year Fourteen years of Hijra, and he is ninety-seven years old.”"
"5064","Judge Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Omar bin Salem bin Al-Jaabi, the only memorizer, told me. Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Harrani told me, My grandfather Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib, Muhammad bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Bakr came On the day of the conquest of Mecca with his father, Abu Quhafa, he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you had made the old man stay in his house, we would have come to him.” True, according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, but they did not take him out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5064 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"5065","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Maruzi told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Malik told us. Al-Fihri, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them, who said: I brought Abu Abi Quhafa, may God be pleased with them. God on his authority to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Will you leave the sheikh until I come to him?” So I said: Rather, he is more deserving of coming to you. He said: “I We will preserve it for the hands of his son with us.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5065 - Abdullah bin Abdul Malik Al-Fihri is a denier of hadith"
"5066","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, Jdi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “The name of Abu Quhafa Othman bin Aamir bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Saad bin Taym bin Murrah bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fahr Aslam On the day of the conquest, he died in Muharram in the year fourteen, and he was ninety-seven years old.”"
"5067","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Shadhakuni told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abu Quhafa Abu Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them both, died in the year seventeen, and he was one hundred and four years old.”"
"5068","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that Omar ibn al-Khattab took Abu Quhafa by the hand and brought him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when he brought him to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Change it and do not bring it black.”
 Ibn Wahb said: Omar bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, congratulated Abu Bakr, by his father’s conversion to Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5068 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5069","Abu Al-Abbas Ismail bin Abdullah told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, Azra bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought on the day of the conquest of Abu Quhafa and his head. His beard was like a thorn, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Mind his beard.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5069 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5070","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Qadi bin Al-Qadi told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Shuja’ told us, Al-Hussein bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: It is as if I look at Abu Quhafa’s beard as if it were dirty. He turned red because of his intense redness, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “If you had kept the old man in his house, we would have given him a tribute.” “For Abu Bakr”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5070 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5071","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Nasrabadhi told me, Harun bin Yusuf told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Amara bin Abdullah bin Sayyad, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was arrested He said: The news reached the people of Mecca. He said: Abu Quhafa heard the terrible shock and said: What is this? They said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. He said: It is a great matter, so who carried out the matter after him? They said: Your son. He said: I was satisfied with Banu Makhzum and Banu al-Mughirah. They said: Yes. He said: Oh God, there is no one to remove what You have raised, and there is no one to lift up what You have placed. When he was near Ras al-Hawl, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, died. He said: Then the news reached the people of Mecca, and Abu Quhafa heard the panic. He said: What is this? They said: Your son has died. He said: It is a great matter, and what happened before it was more venerable than it. He said: Who carried out the matter after him? They said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. He said: He is its author. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5071 - They did not give anything to Amara bin Abdullah bin Sayyad"
"5072","Abu Abdullah bin Battah narrated that to us with his chain of transmission, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin narrated to us Omar, on the authority of his sheikhs, said: “Nawfal bin Al-Harith died one year and three months after Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, succeeded him. Omar prayed over him and then walked with him to Al-Baqi’ until he was buried there.”"
"5073","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Yunus told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, he said: “Nawfal died. Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Abdul-Muttalib, who was nicknamed Abu Al-Harith for the past two years of the caliphate of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, in Medina.”"
"5074","Abu Ahmad bin Shuaib Al-Adl told me, Asad bin Nuh told me, Hisham bin Yahya told me, Muhammad bin Saad told me, I am Ali bin Issa. Al-Nawfali said: When Nawfal ibn Al-Harith was captured at Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Redee yourself, O Nawfal.” He said: What is mine? شَيْءٌ أَفْدِي بِهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: «افْدِ نَفْسَكَ بِرِمَاحِكَ الَّتِي بِجُدَّةَ» قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ مَا عَلِمَ أَحَدٌ أَنَّ لِي بِجُدَّةَ رِمَاحًا بَعْدَ اللَّهِ Other than me, I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. So he ransomed himself with it, and it was a thousand spears. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood between Nawfal. And Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, and before that they were partners in pre-Islamic times, negotiators in financial matters, and loving each other. Nawfal witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, conquered Mecca, Hunayn, and Taif, and Hunayn remained stationed on the day of Hunayn with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “It is as if I am watching your spears being struck in the loins of the polytheists.”"
"5075","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh told us, Hassan bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Yunus bin Yazid, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his grandfather, Nawfal bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib, that he sought help from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him regarding marriage, and he married him a woman. He looked for something but did not find it, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Abu Rafi’ and Abu Ayoub with his armor, and we pawned it from a Jewish man for thirty saa’s of barley, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave it to me, and we ate from it. Half a year, then we ate it and found it as we had entered it. Nawfal said: So I mentioned it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If you had not eaten it She will eat from it as long as she lives.” As for Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith and Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, they were killed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5076","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi informed us of the accuracy of what I mentioned, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa Ibn al-Zubayr said: “Among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Quraysh and the Ansar were three hundred and thirteen men.” He said: “And from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf: Ubaidah, al-Tufayl, and Husayn, the Banu al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and they disagreed regarding Rabi’ah. Ibn Al-Harith, and it was said that he lived after that and lived during the days of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5076 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5077","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib, on the authority of Rabi’ah, who said: It reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a people attacked him and said: To him: The example of Muhammad is like that of a palm tree that grew in a tree. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and then said: “O people, God created He created it and made them into two groups, so He placed me in the best of the two groups. Then He made them into tribes, so He placed me in the best of them. Then He made them into houses, so He placed me in The best of them in household. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the best of you in speech and the best of you in household.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5077 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5078","I read in the history of Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Barqi, Abu Ubaid Al-Qasim bin Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Kalbi regarding the saying of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “And the first blood I shed was the blood of Rabi’ah ibn Al-Harith. He was breast-feeding among the Banu Layth, and Hudhayl killed him.” Hisham said: “Rabi’ah was not killed.” He lived after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until the caliphate of Omar, and the one killed by Hudhail was someone else.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5078 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5079","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Jubayr, that Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif told him: He came to the Levant during the reign of Muawiyah, and a group of the people of the Levant met him and said: What is the relationship between you and Muawiyah? He said: So I said: A cousin. They said: Shall we not narrate to you a hadith which he narrated to us before his death, and which he had not narrated to us before that? So I said: Yes, and he said: He told us before his death that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever meets God without associating partners with Him will enter Paradise.” Musa bin Jubayr said: I told Salman Al-Aghar this hadith of Abu Umamah, and he said: I bear witness that Sa’id bin Al-Harith bin told me Abdul Muttalib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to what the Syrians narrated on the authority of Muadh, may God be pleased with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5079 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5080","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: “And of those who went out From the people of Mecca, an immigrant to the land of Abyssinia, from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Banu Umayyah ibn Abd Shams, Khaled ibn Saeed Ibn Al-Aas Ibn Umayyah Ibn Abd Shams Ibn Abd Manaf, and with him his wife, who gave birth to him in the land of Abyssinia, his son Sa’id Ibn Khalid.”"
"5081","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, saying: “The mother of Khaled ibn Sa’id ibn al-Aas is clear.” Known as Umm Khaled bint Hubab bin Abd Yalil bin Nashib bin Ghayra bin Saad bin Laith bin Bakr bin Abd Manat bin Ali Ibn Kinana Ibn Khuzaymah”"
"5082",""
"5083","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me about Mecca, Abu Yahya Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, Ahmed bin Al-Walid Al-Azraqi, Amr bin Yahya bin Saeed bin Amr bin Al-Aas told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of his uncle Khalid bin Saeed, “that Saeed bin Al-Aas Ibn Umayyah fell ill and said: Because he lifted me from my illness, the god of Ibn Abi Kabsha will never be worshiped in the interior of Mecca, so Khalid bin Saeed said “At that time: Oh God, do not raise him up, for he died in that illness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5083 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5084","So Abu Saeed Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Makhzoumi told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: “Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas was martyred on the day of Marj al-Safar.” Khalifa said: “He was in the year thirteen.” He said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died while he was in charge of Yemen.”"
"5085","So Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Salam bin Junada told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Muammar told us. Bin Hamza bin Omar bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Khaled bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed told me, my father told me, that his uncles Khaled, Our father and Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas returned from their work when they were informed of the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr said: “What? No one is more deserving of work than the workers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Go back to your works.” They said: “We will not work after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He handed over to someone, so they went out to the Levant and were killed by the last of them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5085 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5086","Abu Nu`aym Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman al-Ghafari told me about Marw, Abdan bin Muhammad bin Isa al-Hafiz told us, I heard Abdullah bin Muslim It is mentioned, on the authority of Abu al-Yaqzan, and others, “that Khalid bin Sa`id bin al-Aas converted to Islam before Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them both.” It is an illusion on the part of its speaker. I presented the narration that Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was the one who invited him to Islam until he converted to Islam.”"
"5087","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Ibn Ishaq told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, “that Khaled bin Saeed, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed him to Yemen, came after the death of the Messenger of God.” He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, waited for his pledge of allegiance for two months, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me, and then he did not remove me until he arrested him. God Almighty, and he met Ali bin Abi Talib and Othman bin Abd Manaf, and said: O Banu Abd Manaf, you have been happy about your situation. Others will follow suit. Omar conveyed it to Abu Bakr. As for Abu Bakr, he did not convey it to him. As for Omar, he conveyed it to him. Then Abu Bakr sent soldiers to the Levant, and the first one to be appointed to control a quarter of it was Khaled bin Saeed, so Omar began to say: Do you command him when he did what he did, and he said"
"5088","Abu Nu`aym al-Ghifari told us about Marwa, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, Abdan ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Hafiz told us, I heard Ahmad ibn Sayyar He says: “Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas had twenty sons and twenty daughters born to his father Saeed. As for Al-Khalid bin Saeed, he was killed on the day of Marj. Zero in Muharram in the year fourteen during the caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5089","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Ishaq bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, on the authority of his father Saeed bin Amr, on the authority of Khaled bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he had a ring in his hand. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “What is this ring?” He said: A ring that I took. He said: “So I threw it away.” So I threw it to him, and behold, it was an iron ring. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What Did you engrave it? I said: Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took it and sealed it with it until he died. It is the seal that was in his hand. “Sahih chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5089 - Yahya Al-Hamani is weak"
"5090","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban told us, Khalid bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed, I heard my father mentioning, on the authority of his uncle Khalid bin Saeed the Great, that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when He came from the land of Abyssinia with his daughter, Umm Khalid, and he brought her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing a yellow shirt, and he was amazed. The maid took off her shirt, and she understood some of the words of the Abyssinian, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, confused her with the words of the Abyssinian year after year. She was in Abyssinia, and she was beautiful and beautiful. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “I am in good condition and I behave. I am in good condition and I am in good manners.” He said: So she did well. By God, then she appeared, then she leaned towards the back of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and placed her hand on the place of the seal of the Prophethood. So her father took it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave her.” The chain of narration is correct. The two sheikhs agreed to narrate hadiths by Ishaq. Bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of his fathers and paternal uncles, and this is the mother of Khaled, the daughter of Khaled bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, whom her father bore her. When she was young, she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. After that, she accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she narrated on his authority.
 Abu Bakr bin Daoud, Abu Muhammad al-Baladhuri al-Hafiz, and Abu Sa`id al-Thaqafi told me that this was true. They said: Muhammad bin Ayyub told us: I am Sahl bin Othman Al-Askari, Junada bin Salam Al-Qurashi narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, I heard Umm Khaled bint Khaled bin Saeed bin Al-Aas Al-Akbar says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “seek refuge from the torment of the grave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5090 - But it is interrupted"
"5091","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And from the Banu Zuhair Safwan bin Makhrama bin Nawfal, whose nickname is Makhrama, and he is the brother of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, and his mother was Atika bint Awf, sister of Abd."
"5092","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Issam told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Bashir Abu Ismail told us, I heard Al-Qasim bin Safwan Al-Zuhri mentions, on the authority of his father, who was a companion, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cool yourself off by praying the noon prayer, for the intense heat From the stench of hell"
"5093","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, saying: “He was a pre-Islamist in Mecca and migrated to the land of Abyssinia and then He returned to Mecca, and Abu Jahl imprisoned him, beat him, and made him hungry and thirsty. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying for him. And Qunut” as Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Waqidi"
"5094","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, he said: Then Salama bin Hisham escaped after that, and joined the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina. That was after the ditch, and his mother said Daba'ah bint Amir bin Qardh bin Salamah bin Qusayr bin Ka'b bin Amer bin Rabi'ah:
 [The sea of rage]
 No, they are the Lord of the Sacred Kaaba... prevail over every enemy who surrenders to him.
 He has two hands in ambiguous matters... a hand with which He gives and a hand with which He bestows.
 He remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested. Then he went out with the Muslims to the Levant when Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, sent armies to wage jihad against the Byzantines, so Salamah, may God be pleased with him, was killed as a martyr at Marj al-Safar in Muharram in the year fourteen in “The Caliphate of Omar, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5095","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming the Ansar who witnessed Aqaba from Banu Sa’idah bin Ka’b bin Al-Khazraj, Sa’d bin Ubadah bin Dulaim bin Haritha bin Ubaidah bin Huzaimah, who is a captain and witnessed Badr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5095 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5096","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa “in naming who He witnessed Aqaba and from Banu Sa`idah ibn Ka`b ibn al-Khazraj, Sa`d ibn Ubadah, he was carrying the banner of the Ansar with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him on the day of Badr and other days.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5096 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5097","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Yahya told me Ibn Abdul Aziz Ibn Saeed, “Saad Ibn Ubadah Ibn Dulaim Ibn Haritha Ibn Al-Nu’man Ibn Abi Huzaymah Ibn Tha’labah Ibn Tarif Ibn Al-Khazraj Ibn Sa’idah Ibn Ka’b Ibn Al-Khazraj”
 Muhammad bin Omar said: Saad bin Ubadah was nicknamed Abu Thabit, and he was one of the seventy who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Among the Ansar on the night of Aqaba - according to the narrations of all of them - was one of the twelve captains, and he was a master of horses, and he did not witness a full moon. He was mentioned. He was preparing to go out to them and it was the Ansar’s turn to urge them to go out, so he collapsed before going out and stayed, so the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If Sa’d had not witnessed it, he would have been keen on it,” and he had witnessed Uhud, the trench, and all the sights.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5097 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5098","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Saad bin Ubadah died. He was nicknamed Abu Thabit Bahuran from the Levant for two and a half years of the caliphate of Omar, may God be pleased with him, and that was the last fifteen years.”"
"5099","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Hamwi told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, I heard Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair saying: “Saad died. Ibn Ubadah Bahuran in the year sixteen.”"
"5100","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Ma’bad bin Ka'b, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Bring out to me twelve captains.” So We brought out for him Saad bin Ubadah bin Dulaim bin Haritha bin Huzaimah bin Tha’labah bin Tarif bin Al-Khazraj bin Sa’idah, and he was Captain of Bani Sa'idah
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5100 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5101","Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Hisham bin Muhammad bin Al-Sa'ib Al-Kalbi, Abd Al-Hamid bin Aish bin Jabr told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “I heard someone from Quraysh saying at night against Abu Qubais:
 [Long Sea]
 If Al-Sa`dan submits, Muhammad will be in Mecca in the morning, not fearing disagreement from an opposing person.
 The Quraysh thought they were Saad Tamim and Saad Hudhaim, so when it was the second night they heard him say:
 O Sa'd, Sa'd of the Aws, be a supporter... And O Sa'd, Sa'd of the arrogant Khazrajites
 Respond to the one who calls for guidance and wish... May God grant him Paradise, the death of Arif.
 For the reward of God for the one who seeks guidance...is a garden of paradise with wings.
 When they woke up in the morning, Sufyan said: By God, he is Saad bin Muadh and Saad bin Ubadah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5101 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5102","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Muslim told us, Bakkar bin Muhammad told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad “that Saad bin Worship: The savagery of a people came and fell down dead, and the jinn said:
 [Fast Sea]

 We killed the master of Khazraj...Saad bin Ubadah
 And we shot him with two arrows... but his heart did not miss.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5102 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5103","Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, he said: “ Saad bin Ubadah stayed in bed without urinating, then he came back and said: I find something on my back. Soon he died, so the jinn wailed and they said:
 [Fast Sea]
 We killed the master of Khazraj...Saad bin Ubadah
 And we shot him with two arrows... but his heart did not miss.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 5103 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"5104","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan, and Muhammad bin Ghalib narrated to me, saying: Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Hammad bin Salama narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, informed him of the arrival of Abu Sufyan, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, spoke Then he turned away from him, then Omar, may God be pleased with him, spoke and he turned away from him, and Saad bin Ubadah said: O Messenger of God, by the One in whose hand is my soul. “If you had ordered us to wade into the sea, we would have waded into it, and if you had ordered us to go to their heads to Burk al-Ghumām, we would have done so.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lamented. May God grant peace to the people.” So they set off until they camped at Badr, “Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5104 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5105","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: Saad ibn Ubadah used to say: “O God, grant me glory. There is no glory except with an effect, and there is no effect except with money. Oh God, let not a little reform me, and I will not be reformed.” Accordingly, even if there was a caller calling out to a hill: “Whoever wants fat and meat, let him come to Sa’d.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5105 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5106","Abdan bin Yazid al-Daqqaq told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told me, Atiq bin Yaqoub told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abi told me. Bakr, on the authority of his uncle Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who said: “The polytheists took Saad bin Ubadah, tied his hand around his neck, and took him into Mecca. They beat him and dragged him by the forelock, and he had a long hair.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5106 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5107","Makram bin Ahmad told us, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Madaini told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Saad bin Ubadah, may God be pleased with him, that his mother died while she had to fast. He said: So I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and he ordered me to To perform the prayer on her behalf.” The two sheikhs agreed to narrate this hadith, that Umm Saad bin Ubadah died and he did not perform the prayer on his behalf, and this “It is true according to their condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5107 - Al-Madaini is weak"
"5108","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith Ibn Abd al-Muttalib Ibn Hashim. He was the breastfeeding brother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his cousin, whom Halima breastfed for several days. He was familiar with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, he antagonized him and criticized him as he criticized his companions. He remained for twenty years. angering the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would not stay behind a place where Quraysh was marching to fight the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he mentioned Characters of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He went to Mecca in the year of the conquest. God Almighty placed Islam in his heart, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received it. Before his descent, he greeted the fathers, so he and his son Jafar converted to Islam, and he went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and witnessed the conquest of Mecca. And Hunayn, Abu Sufyan said: When we met the enemy at Hunayn, I galloped from my horse with the sword in my hand, and God knows that I wanted to die without him. While he was looking at me, Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, this is your brother and your cousin, Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith, may he be pleased with him. He said: “He So I did. May God forgive him every enmity he had shown him.” Then he turned to me and said: “My brother by my life.” So I kissed his leg in the stirrup. They said: Abu died. Sufyan bin Al-Harith was in Medina after his brother Nawfal bin Al-Harith by four months minus thirteen nights, and it is said: He died in the year twenty Omar bin Al-Khattab prayed over him, and he was buried in the house of Aqeel bin Abi Talib in Al-Baqi, and he was the one who dug his own grave three days before he died. Days: “I mentioned Abu Sufyan’s conversion to Islam in the conquest of Mecca as previously mentioned.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5108 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5109","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed me, told me about al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani, I heard Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir saying: “Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abd Al-Muttalib, whose name was Al-Mughirah, died in the year twenty, and Omar Ibn Al-Khattab prayed for him.”"
"5110","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham Bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, “Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, was the most beloved of the Quraysh to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and he was harsh to him, but when he converted to Islam, he was the most beloved of people to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5110 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5111","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ammar Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abu Habba Al-Badri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith is good.” “My family” is authentic according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5111 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5112",""
"5113","Ali bin Issa told us, Ali bin Abdul Muttalib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kathir bin Al-Abbas bin Abdul Al-Muttalib, on the authority of his father, said: “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn. I saw him and no one was with him except me and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib, who was holding the reins of the mule of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was riding it, and Abu Sufyan did not give up That he hastens towards the polytheists.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5113 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5114","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari and Abu Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Faqih told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad Bin Bashar, they said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Al-Muttalib, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man had dates from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he came to him to pay for them, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, borrowed. He handed over dates from Khawla bint Hakim, so he gave them to him and said: “I had dates, but they were weak.” Then he said: “Likewise.” The faithful servants of God do this, and God does not have mercy on a nation in which the weak among them does not take his rights from the strong who are not satisfied. Abu Sufyan narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, other than this one hadith, and he did not transmit its chain of narration from Shu’bah other than Gandar. We told him Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari, I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, my father told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Samak, he said: We were with Mudarak ibn Al-Muhallab In Sijistan, I heard a sheikh speaking, on the authority of Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned him, but Abdullah bin Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his father"
"5115","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told us, he said: Among those who accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the descendants of Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, was Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “He is among the best of my family,” and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is the master of the youth of the people of Paradise.” He remained patient with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him in the middle of the morning and said: “Who? “This?” He said: Your mother’s son, O Messenger of God, and he said: “The barber shaved him and cut off a wart from his head, and the blood did not ooze from it until he died, and that was in the year On the twentieth, Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, prayed upon him, and he met the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in some way, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A man was going to Mecca for the conquest, and he converted to Islam before the conquest.”"
"5116","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq, my father Abu Yunus told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: “Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, whose name was Al-Mughirah, died in the year twenty, and Omar bin Al-Khattab prayed over him.”"
"5117","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Jabla told us, my father told me, Shu'bah reported, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, who said: We were with Mudarrak ibn al-Muhallab in Sijistan in his pavilion, and I heard an old man speaking, on the authority of my father. Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God does not sanctify a nation if the weak does not take what is due to the strong.” And he is not amused.” So, the sheikh whom he did not name was Othman bin Jabla, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he called him Ghandar, but he did not mention it. Abu Sufyan in the chain of transmission”"
"5118","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Musa and Bandar told us, they said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, we told him Shu'bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib, who said: It was for a man who was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He handed over some dates, and he came to him to collect them, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, borrowed dates from Khawla bint Hakim, so he gave them to him and said: “As for... I had dates, but they had fallen into disrepair.” Then he said: “Thus do the faithful servants of God. Indeed, God does not have mercy on a nation that does not take The weak among them has no right to enjoy it.”"
"5119","Abu Abdullah bin Abi Dahl told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Yasin told me, Muhammad bin Habib Al-Sammak told us, Abdullah bin Ziyad told us. Al-Thobani, from the descendants of Thuban, on the authority of Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Laith, the client of Muhammad bin Iyad Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Iyaad said: I was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I was young, wearing a rag, and my private parts were exposed, so he said: “Cover the sanctity of his private parts. For the private parts of a child are inviolable as the private parts of an elder, and God does not look at anyone who reveals their private parts.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5119 - Its chain of transmission is dark and its text is objectionable"
"5120","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “Among those who migrated to The land of Abyssinia with Ja`far, may God be pleased with him, from Banu Zuhra ibn Kilab, Utbah ibn Masoud, and his brother Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him."
"5121","Abu Al-Hussein Al-Hafiz informed me: I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Hafiz, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Dawud bin Rashid told us, Muhammad bin Rabia, Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, he said: When Abu Utbah bin Masoud died Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with them, cried, and it was said to him: Are you crying? He said: “My brother and companion with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the third, and the most beloved of people to me, except for Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5122","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim said: “When Utbah bin Masoud died, Omar bin Al-Khattab waited for Umm Abd, and she came and prayed for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5122 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5123","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: “Abdullah did not “Allah bin Masoud is higher in our view than his brother Utbah bin Masoud, but he died quickly.”"
"5124",""
"5125","Abdullah bin Ghanim told me, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, I heard Yahya bin Bukayr saying: “Utbah bin Masoud died in the year Forty-four” and he has one hadith."
"5126","Narrate to us the hadith mentioned by Ibn Bukayr Abu Ali Al-Hafiz, I am Ahmad bin Yahya bin Zuhair, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Harithi told us, Abu Asim told us, Abu Ma’dan Al-Manqari told us, meaning Amer bin Masoud, Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a black female slave, and she said: O Messenger of God, I have a safe slave upon me. Will you be freed from me?"
"5127","Abu Jafar Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Othman bin Saleh told us, Musa bin Aoun bin Abdullah bin Aoun bin Ubaid Allah told us. Bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud. My grandmother, Umm Abdullah bint Hamza bin Abdullah bin Utba, told me. I heard my father Hamza. Bin Abdullah says: I asked Abu Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud: What do you remember from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “I remember that he took me when I was five or six years old, and he sat me on his lap, wiped my head, and prayed for me and my descendants to be blessed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5127 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5128","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, I heard Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari say: I heard Musab bin Abd Allah Al-Zubayri says: Naeem Al-Nahham is Naeem bin Abdullah bin Khalid bin Usayd bin Abdul Awf bin Ubaid bin Awaij bin Adi bin Ka'b, who converted to Islam before the Hijra, was one of those who migrated to the land of Abyssinia. He is the one who is called Al-Nahham, but he was only told that because the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I heard a namah from the bliss in Paradise,” and the namah is the sound."
"5129","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming those who On the day of Ajnadin of Quraysh, then of Banu Adi bin Ka’b Na’im bin Abdullah al-Nahham, he said: “That was in the year thirteen.” Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, with his chain of transmission, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Omar: “Na’im al-Nahham was killed on the Day of Yarmouk as a martyr in Rajab of the year Fifteen”"
"5130","Muhammad bin Ali al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Razzaq told me, I am Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Naim al-Nahham, who said: The muezzin of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the call to prayer on a cold night, and I was under my quilt, so I hoped that God would meet me. God Almighty said, “And there is no difficulty,” and when he finished, he said: “And there is no difficulty.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5130 - True"
"5131","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Al-Tufayl bin converted to Islam. Amr followed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Mecca, then returned to his people from the land of Dus, and he continued to reside there until he migrated to Medina after Badr and Uhud and the Trench when he brought those of his people and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Khaybar who had converted to Islam with him, then he joined Khaybar. with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Khaybar, so he shared their shares with the Muslims.”"
"5132","Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Atki told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farawi told us, Abdullah bin Jafar told us. Al-Makhrami, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Aoun al-Dawsi, on the authority of al-Tufayl ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him, who said: We said: O Messenger of God, make us Your right hand, and make our emblem, O Mabrur. “So he did, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So all the emblems of the lion are to this day, O Mabrur.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and the emblem of the lion is not They will bring him out if he is not a messenger, and Amr ibn al-Tufayl ibn Amr has reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5132 - Sahih mursal"
"5133","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Amr bin Al-Tufayl bin Amr bin Tarif bin Al-Aas bin Thalabah Al-Azdi, and his father Al-Tufayl bin Amr was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he was arrested. When the Arabs apostatized, he left. He struggled until the Muslims finished with Tulayha and the entire land of Najd, then he walked with the Muslims to Al-Yamamah, with his son Amr bin Tufayl with him. Then Amr ibn al-Tufayl went out and was wounded and his hand was cut off. Then he recovered and his hand became healthy, while he was with Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, when Food was brought and he stepped aside from it. Omar said: Why did you step aside where your hand was? He said: Yes. He said: No, by God, I will not taste it until you whip it with your hand. In it, by God, there is no one among the people in Paradise except you. Then he went out in the year of Yarmouk during the reign of Omar, may God be pleased with him, with the Muslims and was killed. A martyr, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5134","Abu Abdullah told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Saad bin Ubaid bin Al-Numan bin Qais bin Amr bin Zaid bin Umayyah bin Zaid, who is called Saad al-Qari, and his nickname is Abu Zaid, and he is one of the six who compiled the Qur’an during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and was killed on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah as a martyr. In the year sixteen, and he was sixty-four years old, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5135","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “Utba bin Ghazwan bin Jaber bin Wahib bin Naseeb bin Malik bin Al Harith bin Mazen bin Mansour bin Ikrimah bin Khasfa bin Qais Aylan Bin Mudar bin Nizar"
"5136","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, in mentioning Utba bin Ghazwan, may God be pleased with him. About him, they said: “His nickname is Abu Abdullah, and it was also said that Abu Ghazwan, and he was mentioned as a tall, handsome man, and he was an early convert to Islam, and he immigrated To the land of Abyssinia, the second migration, and he was one of the archers mentioned among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was the one who saw Basra, and he died during the caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, at Ma’dan Bani Sulaym, while he was going to Basra as its governor before Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and his servant Suwayd presented Omar with his possessions and his estate.” Ibn Omar said: “But Utbah ibn Ghazwan died. In the year fifteen, and it is said that seventeen, and he was fifty-seven years old.”"
"5137","Abu Ja`far told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad: “Utba bin Ghazwan witnessed Badr with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5138","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim told me, Ubaid bin Ghannam told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, they said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr said: “Utbah bin Ghazwan died in the year seventeen, and he died at the age of fifty-seven, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5139","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Qurra bin Khalid told us, and Ahmad told us Ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Waki` told us, Qurra Ibn Khalid told us, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Hilal, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, and the wording for it, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Asad bin Musa narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Khalid bin Umair Al-Adawi, who said: Utbah bin Ghazwan addressed us, and he thanked God and praised him, then he said: “As for what follows, The world has brought forth a noise and has left a shoe, but only a sap of it remains, like the sap of a vessel being used by its owner, and you are on the move. From it to an abode that will never disappear, so move from it with the best that will come to you, for it has been mentioned to us that the stone is thrown from the brink of Hell. So he will sink into it for seventy years, and no bottom can reach it. By God, you will certainly fill it. Are you amazed when it has been mentioned to us that two shutters of From the gates of Paradise, there are forty years between them, and a day will come upon him when it will be intense with crowding. And you saw me, and I was on the seventh day with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, we have no food except the leaves of the trees, to the point that they ulcerate our throats, and I picked a clover and divided it between me and Saad bin Abi Qasas, the knight of Islam, so I girded myself with half of it, and Saad girded myself with half of it, and not one of us alive today has become the prince of Egypt. disasters, and I seek refuge in God lest I be great within myself and small with God, and there has never been a prophecy without it diminishing until it is fulfilled. “I will make her a king, and you will either be tested or you will put to the test the princes after me.” It is authentic according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5139 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5140","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Balawayh told me, and I asked him. Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abd al-Malik bin Bashir al-Nasa’i, Abu Hafs Omar bin al-Fadl al-Sulami told us, Utbah bin Ibrahim bin Utbah bin Ghazwan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Utbah bin Ghazwan said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day to the Quraysh: “Is there anyone among you other than you?” They said: The son of our sister Utbah bin Ghazwan. He said: “The son of the sister of the people is one of them.” The mention of Utbah bin Ghazwan in this hadith is strange. Very, and his virtues are many, and this is because of his virtues, and the Musnads of Utba bin Ghazwan on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, are dear, and he We wrote a hadith from that which we found very surprising, as I remember, even if Al-Ghallabi was not one of the conditions of this book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5140 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"5141","It was narrated to us by Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Ibrahim Al-Hafiz Bhamdan, Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Ghalabi told us, Abdul-Rahman told us, I am Omar bin Jablah, Omar bin Al-Fadl Al-Sulami told us, Ghazwan bin Utbah bin Ghazwan told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell.”"
"5142","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Yazid Al-Saydalani told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, My father told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yassar, who said: “Abu Ubaidah Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah bin Hilal bin Ahab bin Dabbah bin Al-Harith bin Fahr bin Malik bin Al-Nadr bin Kinanah, and his mother was Umm Ghanam bint Jabir bin Al-Adl bin Amir bin Umayrah Bin Wariah bin Al-Harith bin Fahr»"
"5143","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told us, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told us, so he mentioned this lineage and said: “The mother of “Slave of Islam”"
"5144","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, he said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said To his companions: “They wished,” so he made each man wish for something, and he said: “But I wish for a house full of men like Abu Ubaidah ibn Al-Jarrah.” They said to him: “You have not given Islam any good.” He said: “That is what I wanted.”"
"5145","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah used to say: “There were three of my friends among the Companions of the Messenger of God, and they were not my family: Abu Bakr, Omar, and Abu Ubaidah.”"
"5146","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Aidh Al-Tai, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab said: “Omar’s letter came to us: When the epidemic occurred in the Levant, Omar wrote to Abu Ubaidah: I have come across an urgent need for you. Tell me about it. Abu Ubaidah said: May God have mercy on the Commander of the Faithful. He wants the survival of a people who will not remain. He said: Then Abu Ubaidah wrote to him: I am in one of the Muslim armies, and I do not alienate myself from what befell them. When he read the letter, he recovered, and the people said: Abu Ubaidah has died. He said: No, and he had written to him with the message, so come from the land of the Jordan, for it is deep and desert, to the land of Jabiyah, for it is a desert. Nadiya, when the letter came to him with the intention, he ordered his herald to give the people permission to leave. When he came to him to ride him, he put his foot in the stitches and bent. His leg, and he said: I do not see your illness except that it has infected me. He said: Abu Ubaidah died and the epidemic returned from the people. “All of the narrators of this hadith Trustworthy, and it is a strange thing at times.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5146 - According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs"
"5147","Abu Abdullah Al-Sayyari told me in the book Al-Riqqaq by Ibn Al-Mubarak, I am Abu Al-Mawjih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am Abd Al-Hamid ibn Bahram, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam told me, on the authority of al-Harith ibn Umayra al-Harithi, who said: “Muadh took Ibn Jabal sent Al-Harith Ibn Umayrah to Abu Ubaidah Ibn Al-Jarrah, asking him how he was when he was stabbed. Abu Ubaidah showed him a stab wound that came out in the He palmed it, and he was upset about it, and he moved away from it when he saw it, so Abu Ubaidah swore to him by God that he would not like to have red camels in their place.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5147 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5148","Ali ibn al-Mu’mal ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, my father told me, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Uthmani told me, Amr ibn Khalid ibn Asim ibn Amr ibn Othman, Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahaq told me, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, who said: When Abu Ubaidah was stabbed, he said: O Muadh, pray With the people, Muadh led the people in prayer, then Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah died, so Muadh rose among the people and said: “O people, repent to God for your sins.” Sincere repentance, for Abdullah does not meet God repenting of his sin unless it is God’s duty to forgive him.” Then he said: “You People, you have been shocked by a man. By God, I do not claim that I have ever seen among the servants of God a servant who was less winking, nor more righteous, nor far away from deceit, nor He loves the outcome more strongly, and I am not more sincere to the common people than him, so have mercy on him, may God have mercy on him, then wake up in the morning to pray for him, for God will not be harsh on you. Never again.” So the people gathered, and Abu Ubaidah came out, and Muadh came forward and prayed over him until when he brought him to his grave, Muadh bin Jabal entered his grave. And Amr bin Al-Aas and Al-Dahhak bin Qais, when they put him in his bed and went out, they covered him with dirt, then Muadh bin Jabal said: “O Abu Ubaidah, I will praise you, and I will not say falsehood. I fear lest a hatred from God befall me with it. I have never been. By God, I have never known of those who remember God much, and of those who They walk on the earth frivolously, and when the ignorant address them they say: “Peace,” and among those who, when they spend, are neither extravagant nor stingy, and He is clear. “That is your standing, and by God you are one of the humble and humble people who have mercy on the orphan and the needy and hate the arrogant traitors.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5148 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5149","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Abu Ayyub Suleiman bin Dawud Al-Shadhakuni told me, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Waqidi, Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Muadh, on the authority of Malik bin Yakhamir, that he “described Abu Ubaidah and said: A man Thin, with a veiny face, with a long, thin beard, hunched over, with broad beards.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5149 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5150","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told me, Abu Mushar told me Abd al-A`la bin Mushar told me, Yahya bin Hamza told us, On the authority of Urwa bin Ruwaym, he said: “Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah died with a stallion from Jordan in the year eighteen.”"
"5151","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “And who One of Banu al-Harith ibn Fihr, Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, witnessed Badr, and he was forty-one years old.”"
"5152","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Asad bin Musa told us, Damrah bin Rabi’ah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shudhab. He said: “He made Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah set up the throne for Abu Ubaidah on the day of Badr, and he made Abu Ubaidah depart from him, so when he Abu Ubaidah inflicted wounds on him and killed him, so God Almighty revealed this verse about him when he killed his father: “You will not find a people who believe in God.” And on the Last Day they will be friends with those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, even if they are their fathers or their sons.} [Al-Mujadila: 22]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5152 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5153","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud Al-Zahid told us, Abdullah bin Qahta told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, My father told us, I heard Bashar bin Abi Saif speaking, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghaytif, who said: We entered upon Abu Ubaidah bin We saw the surgeon and his thin wife was sitting at his head, while he was facing the wall, so we said to her: How did Abu Ubaidah spend the night? Tonight? She said: He spent the night with wages, so he turned to us and said: I did not spend the night with wages, then he said: Don’t you ask me about what I said? So we said: We did not like what you said, so we will ask you about it. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever spends in the way of God For seven hundred, and whoever spends on himself and his family or visits a sick person or more, a good deed will be rewarded ten times as much, and fasting is a shield unless He breaks it, and whoever God tests with calamity in his body, it will be a disgrace to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5153 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5154","Khalaf bin Muhammad al-Bukhari told me, Muhammad bin Harith told me, Amr bin Ali told me, I heard Yahya bin Saeed say: “Abu Ubaidah died while he was Fifty-eight years old.”"
"5155","Ahmad Al-Anazi told us, Uthman bin Saeed told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim Al-Dimashqi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz said: “Abu Ubaidah al-Jarrah died in Jordan in the year eighteen, and Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with them both, prayed for him.”"
"5156","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, Omar bin Hamza told us, Salem bin Abdullah told us, That Abdullah bin Omar told them that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I have not been exposed to the emirate or loved it except that people from the people of Najran They came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they complained to him about their worker, and he said: “I will certainly send the trustworthy man over you.” Omar said: I was among those who spoke arrogantly. He hoped that he would send me, so Abu Ubaidah sent “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5156 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5157","Hamza bin Al-Abbas told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Al-Haytham bin Jamil told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not one of my companions whom I would have taken over some of his character if I had wished, except Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah.” “This is a strange messenger, and its narrators are trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5157 - Sent"
"5158","Ali ibn al-Mu’mal told me, Ubayy told me, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Uthmani told me, Amr ibn Khalid told me, Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Thabit told me, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Saad, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said to Abu Ubaidah when he directed him to the Levant: “I would like you to know your honor over me and your status with me. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is not on earth a man from among the Muhajireen or anyone else whom I would equate with you, nor does this - meaning Omar - have any status with me except him. Write down what you have
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5158 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"5159","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Salamah bin Musa bin Ismail told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha. Issa bin Talha narrated to me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Abu Bakr narrated to me He said: I was on the first day of Uhud and in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man was fighting on his behalf, and I saw him, he said: protecting him. He said: So I said: Be Talha wherever I missed what missed me. He said: Between me and the east there is a man whom I do not know, and I am closest to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted him while he was running quickly, but I would not kidnap him. Then he saw that it was Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. So we went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted all of them, and his forelock had been broken and his face had been cut, and two of the Forgiver’s rings had entered his cheeks. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: May God bless him and grant him peace: “On you is your companion.” He meant Talha, and he was bleeding and he did not look at him, so we approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I wanted what Abu Ubaidah wanted, and he asked for me and continued until I left him. His throat had grown, and he hated to disturb it with his hand. Then he hurt the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he held him tight with his fold, and he got up and took it off, and his fold came out, so he called for me and did not leave me until I left it, but he was jealous of the other, so he did the same and took it off, and its folds came out, and Abu Ubaidah was careful about the folds. “This is a hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5159 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5160","So Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, explaining this hadith, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Muhammad bin Salih told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ruman said: “Abu Ubaidah Amer bin Al-Jarrah embraced Islam along with Uthman bin Mad’un, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and their companions.” Before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Dar Al-Arqam, Abu Ubaidah migrated to the land of Abyssinia, the second migration, and Abu Ubaidah at Badr and Uhud, and he stood firm on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the people were defeated, and he was the one who removed the two rings with his folds. The forgiveness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which had entered his cheeks and caused Abu Ubaidah’s folds, may God be pleased with him, to fall out when he removed them. That is, Abu Ubaidah was the most eloquent of the doubles.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5160 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5161","Abu Zur’ah al-Razi narrated to me, Amr bin Idris al-Dhab’i told me, in Egypt, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Nusayr told us, Abu Yahya al-Waqar told us, I heard Abdullah bin Wahb, says: “The inscription on Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah’s ring was loyalty dear.”"
"5162","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: Al-Aqib and Al-Sayyid, companions of Najran, came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. وَسَلَّمَ يُرِيدَانِ أَنْ يُلَاعِنَاهُ، فَقَالَ أَحَدُهُمَا لِصَاحِبِهِ: لَا تَفْعَلْ، فَوَاللَّهِ لَئِنْ كَانَ نَبِيًّا فَلَعَنَنَا لَا نَفْلَحُ نَحْنُ وَلَا عَقِبُنَا After us, they said: Rather, we will give you what you asked, and send with us a truly trustworthy and trustworthy man. He said: So the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked forward to her. He greeted him and said: “Get up, Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.” When he stood up, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the trustee of this nation.” It was agreed upon. The two sheikhs for narrating this hadith briefly in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Al-Thawri and Shu’bah on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah Israel disagreed with them, and said: On the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Abdullah and he traced the hadith, he completed what Al-Thawri and Shu’bah had, so I brought it out. Because according to their condition it is true.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5162 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5163","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, that the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Send with us a man who will teach us the Qur’an. So he took him by the hand. Abu Ubaidah sent him with them and said: “This is the trustworthy person of this nation.” It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not mention it by mentioning the Qur’an.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5163 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5164","Abu Amr bin Ismail told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Ismail bin Sami told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Abu Al-Buhturi, who said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said to Abu Ubaidah, may God be pleased with them both: Shall I pledge allegiance to you? For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You are the trustee of this nation.” Then Abu Ubaidah said: How can I pray in the presence of a man whose command is Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believe us when he was arrested? “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5164 - Interrupted"
"5165","Muhammad bin Ya’qub al-Muqri informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Qutayba bin Sa’id told us, Kathir bin Hisham told us, Ja’far bin Burqan, Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj told us: I was informed that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “If I had caught Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, I would have appointed him as his successor and would not have consulted. If I were asked about him, I would say: I appointed you as my successor, Amen of God and the Amen of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5165 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5166","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Al-Khalil told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent man is Abu Bakr, what an excellent man is Omar, What an excellent man, Abu Ubaidah bin al-Jarrah, what an excellent man, Usayd bin Hudayr, what an excellent man, Thabit bin Qais, what an excellent man, Muadh bin Jabal, what an excellent man. “Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh” is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5166 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5167","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Rabi’ah Fahd bin Awf told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Radi On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “brothered between Abu Talha and Abu Ubaidah.” It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5167 - Fahd bin Awf abandoned him"
"5168","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq “in naming those who Aqaba was witnessed by Muadh bin Jabal bin Amr bin Aws bin Aidh bin Adiy bin Kaab bin Ghanam bin Saad bin Ali bin Asad bin Sarida bin Yazid bin Jashm, who was in Banu Salamah, witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and all the sights, and he died in Emmaus. The plague spread during the caliphate of Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, but the Banu Salamah claimed it because he was the brother of a man of theirs.”"
"5169","I heard Abu Al-Abbas, I heard Al-Abbas, I heard Yahya bin Ma’in say: “The surname of Muadh bin Jabal is Abu Abdul Rahman.”"
"5170","Abdullah bin Ya’qub Al-Farisi told me, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told me, Ibn Bukayr told us, I heard Malik bin Anas say: “Muadh bin Jabal He died when he was twenty-eight years old, and he was the imam of the scholars at that time.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5170 - This is wrong"
"5171","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Muadh bin Jabal told us Bin Amr bin Aidh bin Adi bin Kaab bin Amr bin Ada bin Saad bin Ali bin Asad bin Sardah bin Yazid bin Jashm “He witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5171 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5172","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim Al-Hazami told me, Muhammad bin Falih told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, he said: “Muadh Ibn Jabal Ibn Amr, one of the Banu Salamah Ibn Al-Khazraj, nicknamed Abu Abd al-Rahman. He died in the year eighteen in the plague of Emmaus, and he was the son of Thirty-eight years”"
"5173","So Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib said: “Isa, son of Mary, was raised when he was thirty-three years old, and Muadh bin Jabal died when he was thirty-three years old, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5174","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, I am Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyeh told him, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, who said: “Muadh bin Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and it is known that In his age, he is thirty-two years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5174 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it due to its weakness"
"5175","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told me, Yahya bin Bukayr told me, I heard Malik Ibn Anas says: “Muadh ibn Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and he was the imam of the scholars at some point.”"
"5176",""
"5177","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, I am Ibn Wahb, Malik bin Anas told me, On the authority of Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani, he said: “I entered the Damascus Mosque and saw that I was a man with bright complexions and a long silence. And when the people were with him, whenever they disagreed about something, they attributed it to him and deviated from his opinion. Then I asked about him, and it was said: Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5177 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5178","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Al-Thaqafi told us, Ali bin Saeed Al-Baghdadi told us, Damra told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ata, On the authority of his father, he said: “The grave of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, was buried in Khalid’s palace.”"
"5179","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told me, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of my father Ibn Ka’b Ibn Malik said: “Muadh Ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, was a beautiful, tolerant young man, one of the best young men of his people. He would not ask for anything but he gave it to him.” Until he owed a debt, he closed his money.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5179 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5180","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, On the authority of Qais bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he passed by Muadh bin Jabal while he was standing on the"
"5181","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa. He said: “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He appointed Mu’adh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, as his successor in charge of the people of Mecca when he set out for Hunayn, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him orders. He was granted permission to teach the people the Qur’an and to make them understand the religion. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out for Medina, and succeeded Muadh bin Jabal. On the people of Mecca.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5181 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5182","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Shadh bin Al-Fayyad told us, Abu Qahdham Al-Nadr bin Ma’bad told us, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Omar passed by Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with them, and he was crying, and he said: What makes you cry? He said: A hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The lowest hypocrisy is polytheism, and the most beloved of the servants to God, Blessed and Most High. The hidden pious ones, who, if they are absent, will not be missed, and if they testify, they will not be recognized. These are the imams of guidance and the beacons of knowledge.” Sahih. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5182 - Abu Qahdham said: Abu Hatim does not write his hadith, and Al-Nasa’i said: He is not trustworthy."
"5183","Abu Nu`aym Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Nasr al-Ghifari told us about Marwa, Abdan bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Hafiz told us, Qutaibah bin Saad, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Yazid bin Umair, who said: When Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, was present at the death, and it was said to him: Hosanna, O Abu Abdul Rahman. He said: “Sit me down, for knowledge and faith In their place is whoever seeks them and finds them. He says that three times, so they sought knowledge four times: with Uwaimir Abi Darda, and with Salman Al-Farisi, with Abdullah bin Masoud, and with Abdullah bin Salam, who was Jewish and converted to Islam, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “He will be the friend of ten people in Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5183 - True"
"5184","Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi told us, Ubaid bin Tamim told me, Al-Awza’i told me, about the worship of Ibn Nasi, on the authority of Ibn Ghanam, I heard Abu Ubaidah and Ubadah ibn al-Samit while we were with Abu Ubaidah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Muadh bin Jabal is the most knowledgeable of the ancients and the last after the prophets and messengers, and God boasts of him to the angels.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5184 - I consider it fabricated"
"5185","Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal said that Muadh bin Jabal spun to his right, then said: “I have not done this since I converted to Islam and accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5186","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, I am Ibn Wahb, Othman bin Ata told me, on the authority of his father, that Muadh bin A mountain, may God be pleased with him, rose up in the army that was on it when the epidemic occurred, and said: “O people, this is the mercy of your Lord, and a supplication. Your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.” Then Mu’adh said while delivering the sermon: “O God, grant the family of Mu’adh their fullest share of this.” Mercy.” So while he was like that, he came and it was said: Your son Abd al-Rahman was stabbed. Then when he saw his father Muadh, he said: Abd al-Rahman says: Oh Father, {The truth is from your Lord, so do not be of those who doubt} [Al-Baqarah: 147]. He said: Muadh says: “{You will find me, God willing, among the patient ones} [Al-Saffat: 102],” so he died. From Friday to Friday, all of Mu'adh's family, then he was the last of them."
"5187","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told me, Musa bin Ali told me Ibn Rabah Al-Lakhmi, on the authority of his father, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, addressed the people and said: “Whoever wants to ask about the Qur’an, let him come.” Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and whoever wants to ask about what is lawful and forbidden, let him come to Muadh ibn Jabal, and whoever wants to ask about money, let him come to me. For God Almighty made me a treasurer.”"
"5188","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, Farwa bin Nawfal al-Ashja’i told me, he said: Ibn Masoud said: “Indeed, Mu’adh was a servant of God, obedient to God, and upright.” So I said to myself: Abu Abd al-Rahman made a mistake. Rather, God Almighty said: “Indeed, Abraham was a nation obedient to God” [An-Nahl: 120] the verse. He said: Do you know what a nation is? What is qanit? So I said: God knows best. He said: “The nation who knows what is good, and is obedient and obedient to God and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And so was Muadh bin “A mountain that was a teacher of goodness and was obedient to God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Abdullah, with a chain of transmission at the end.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5188 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5189","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, I heard Firas narrates, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Indeed, Mu’adh was an obedient servant,” he said: Then a man from Ashja’, called Farwa bin Nawfal: That was Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him. Abdullah said: “Whoever forgets has forgotten. We liken him to Abraham.” Abdullah was asked about the nation, and he said: “The teacher of goodness, and the obedient one who is obedient to God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abdullah said: “He forgot who He forgot. Indeed, we likened him to Abraham.” Abdullah was asked about the nation, and he said: “The teacher of goodness, the obedient one, obedient to God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5189 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5190","So Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sakouni told me in Kufa, Ubaid bin Ghannam bin Hafs bin Ghayath Al-Nakhai told me, my father told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was arrested and they appointed Abu Bakr as his successor, he was pleased with him. May God bless him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Muadh to Yemen, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them both, appointed Omar to appoint him for the season. Then he met Mu'adh in Mecca and he had a slave with him, and he said: Who are these people? He said: “These were given to me as gifts, and these were given to Abu Bakr.” Then Omar said to him: “I think you should bring them to Abu Bakr.” He said: He met him from Tomorrow, he said: “O Ibn Al-Khattab, you saw me yesterday as I was going down to Hell and you were taking my custody, and I saw nothing but your obedient person.” He said: So he brought them to Abu Bakr, and said: “These were given as gifts to me and these to you.” He said: We have delivered your gift to you, so Muadh went out to Prayer, then they were praying behind him, and Muadh said: “To whom are you praying?” They said: To God Almighty, and He said: “You are His, so He freed them.” It is true according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5190 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5191","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Al-Hasan bin Sahl Al-Majwiz told us, Abu Asim told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi told us, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, addressed the people and said: “Whoever wants to ask about the Qur’an, let him come to Ubayy bin Ka’b, and whoever wants to ask about permissible and forbidden, let Muadh bin Jabal come, and whoever wants to ask about the obligatory duties, let Zayd bin Thabit come, and whoever wants to ask about “The money, let it come to me, for I am its custodian.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5191 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5192","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, that Al-Hassan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Muammar, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, he said: Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, was a forgiving, forgiving young man. He was the best of the youth of his people, and he did not hold anything back. He continued to be condemned until he drowned all his money in debt. “Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. His fines,” and if they had left anyone for the sake of another, they would have left Mu’adh for the sake of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sold to them “And he handed over his money until Mu’adh arrived with nothing.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5192 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5193","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, I am Al-Hussein bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Qattan in Raqqa, Amr bin Bakr Al-Saskiki told us, Mujasha bin Amr Al-Asadi told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal that His son died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to him to condole him: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, to Muadh bin Peace be upon you, for I praise God for you, besides whom there is no god. As for what follows, may God reward you greatly, inspire you with patience, and grant us sustenance. And beware of gratitude, for our lives, our wealth, our families, and our children are among the best gifts of God Almighty, the Most Blessed, and His hidden burdens. Enjoy it in bliss and happiness, and receive it from you with a great reward. Prayers, mercy, and guidance. If you seek it, be patient, and do not be discouraged. Reward you and you will regret it, and know that grief does not avert anything, nor does it ward off grief, and whatever is coming down has already happened, and “peace” is strange and good except that it brings joy. Ibn Amr is not a condition of this book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5193 - This is the position of Mujasha bin Amr"
"5194","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shuraih told us, I heard Uqba bin Muslim say: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali told me, on the authority of al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, he said: He took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in my hand one day, then he said: “O Muadh, by God, I love you.” So I said to him: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God. And I, by God, love you. He said: “And I advise you, O Muadh, not to fail at the end of every prayer to say: O God, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and doing good deeds.” Worshiping You “And Muadh al-Sanabihi recommended that, and al-Sanabihi recommended that to Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, and Abu Abd al-Rahman recommended to Uqba Ibn Muslim” with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5194 - True"
"5195","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Issa bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: Muadh bin Jabal was one of the best of people. He was of the best face, the best of them in character, and the most generous of their livelihood. He owed a lot of debt, and his debtors stuck with him until he was absent from them for days in his house. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made enemies of his acquaintances, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to Muadh to invite him, and his accusers came with him. They said: O Messenger of God, take for us our share of it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on whoever gives him alms.” So people gave him alms. Others refused, and said: O Messenger of God, take for us our right from him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be patient with them, O Muadh.” He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, robbed him of his money and gave it to his creditors, who divided it among them, and they received five-sevenths of their due. They said: O Messenger of God, sell him to us. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Leave him alone, for you have no way over him.” So Muadh departed to the Banu Salamah, and someone said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, if you had asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you had become destitute today, he said: What? I would have asked him. He said: He stayed for a few days, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, summoned him and sent him to Yemen, and said: “Perhaps God will grant you strength.” And he will pay your debt for you.” He said: So Muadh went to Yemen, and he did not stay there until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and he completed the year in which he performed Hajj. Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, visited Mecca, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, appointed him to perform Hajj, so they met on the Day of Tarwiyah there. So they embraced each other and consoled his companion with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then they went down to the ground talking, and Omar saw Muadh Two boys. He said: Who are these? Then he mentioned the letters that I mentioned above.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 5195 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"5196","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas bin Abd Al-Muttalib bin Hashim, nicknamed Abu Muhammad, invaded Mecca and Hunayn with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and remained with him when the people departed in defeat. He participated in the Farewell Pilgrimage with him, and he was among those who washed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and took care of his burial. Then he went out to the Levant, waging Jihad on the other hand. Jordan in the plague of Emmaus in the year eighteen of the Hijra, during the caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him."
"5197","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub. I heard Al-Abbas say: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in say: “Al-Fadl bin Abbas was killed on the day of Yarmouk in The era of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5198","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, I am Al-Thaqafi, Ubayd Allah bin Saad Al-Zuhri told us, my uncle Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ishaq said: “Al-Fadl bin Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib. His surname was Abu Muhammad and his mother was Umm Al-Fadl, and her name was Lubabah bint Al-Harith. He was killed in The succession of Abu Bakr with Khalid bin Al-Walid. His father, Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, and his brother, Abdullah bin Abbas, spoke about the virtue Ibn Abbas """"
 - As for the hadith of his father Abbas on the authority of him -"
"5199","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, he said: Yahya bin Saeed said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that Abu Ma’bad The servant of Abdullah bin Abbas told him that he heard Abdullah bin Abbas speaking, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, that he said: When It was the day of Arafat, and virtue was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people were many around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the people increased, I said: Al-Fadl will tell me about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. Al-Fadl said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pushed back and the people pushed back with him, so he made The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was holding the reins of his camel and began calling to the people: “You must be at peace.” When he reached Muzdalifah, he descended and prayed the Maghrib prayer. And the evening and the afterlife together, until when dawn came, he prayed the Fajr prayer, then he stood in Muzdalifah at the Sacred Shrine, then he pushed and the people pushed with him. He held the reins of his camel and started saying: “O people, you must be calm,” until when he reached the point of reaching a point of loss, he put something down and started saying: “You must take pebbles.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Someone other than Abu al-Zubayr narrated it, on the authority of Abu Ma`bad, and they did not narrate it. As for the hadith of his brother Abdullah bin Abbas, it is It is narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ata’ and Abu Ma’bad on the authority of Ibn Abbas in two words: “You must be at peace.” He was stoning the Jamarat, but this did not happen. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5199 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5200","Abu Al-Tayyib Al-Harbi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Muhmash bin Issam told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Amara, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Utba, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that virtue was synonymous with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the gathering. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished, he said: “O people, be calm, for righteousness is not By wasting horses and camels.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5200 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5201","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, he said: “Shurhabeel bin Hasanah It was said: His mother was under the rule of Sufyan bin Muammar bin Habib bin Wahb bin Hudhafah bin Jumah, and she migrated with Sufyan, and as for Abu Sharhabeel is Abdullah bin Al-Mutta’ bin Amr from Yemen, and Sufyan is Jamil bin Muammar, and he was called Jamil with The two hearts are part of his mind, until God said: {God has not made for a man two hearts within his belly} [Al-Ahzab: 4] and he testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Hunayn, and Shurahbil ibn Hasanah died on the Day of Yarmouk during the caliphate of Omar, may God be pleased with him, in the year eighteen.”"
"5202","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan narrated to us, Al-Hussein narrated to us, Muhammad bin Omar narrated to us, he said: “Shurhabil Ibn Hasanah and his mother Hasanah, and she is Aduliya and Abu Sharhabeel Abdullah bin Muta’ bin Amr from Kindah, an ally of Banu Zahra, nicknamed Abu Abdullah, and he is from Abyssinian immigrants, the second migration.”"
"5203","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Omar bin Zurarah told me, Ziyad bin Abdullah Al-Bakai told us, about Muhammad bin Ishaq “In naming the one who immigrated to Abyssinia: Shurahbil Ibn Hasnah. His mother Hasnah immigrated to the land of Abyssinia with Her husband is Sufyan bin Muammar bin Habib bin Wahb bin Hudhafa bin Jumah.”"
"5204","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, he said: “Shurhabil bin Abdullah bin Al-Mutta’ bin Amr bin Abdul Aziz, and his mother Hasana, who was loyal to Uthman ibn Habib, and Sharhabil ibn Hasana died in the plague of Emmaus in the year eighteen He is sixty-seven years old.”"
"5205","Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Atki told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Nuaym bin Hammad told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, about Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, that Al-Najashi “sent Umm Habibah, may God be pleased with her, to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Sharhabeel Ibn"
"5206","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Shurhabil Ibn Hassana, may God be pleased with him, was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he launched raids with him. He was one of the princes with whom Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, in the Levant.”"
"5207","Hamid bin Muhammad Al-Harawi told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, and Matar Al-Warraq told us, about Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, who said: The plague occurred in the Levant, and Amr ibn al-Aas addressed us and said: This is the plague. An abomination, so they fled from it through the valleys and paths. This reached Shurahbil ibn Hasanah and he said: “Amr lied. I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him, and Amr is more misguided than the camel of his family, but it is the mercy of your Lord and the call of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the death of the righteous before you.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5207 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5208","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told me, he said: “Abu Jandal bin Suhail bin Amr, his name is Abdullah bin Suhail bin Amr bin Abd Shams bin Nadr bin Malik bin Hasal bin Amir bin Luay: Umm Abi Jandal was a sister from the Banu Nawfal. Ibn Abd Manaf witnessed Badr and was with the polytheists. When he descended at Badr, he fled to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and was martyred on the day Al-Yamama “This is how I found out that he died in his youth, and I thought he was delusional at the time of his death.”"
"5209","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abu Jandal bin Suhail bin Amr He converted to Islam long ago in Mecca, but his father, Suhail bin Amr, imprisoned him, bound him with iron, and prevented him from immigrating. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down to He surrendered Al-Hudaybiyyah, and Suhail bin Amr came to him and judged him according to what he had judged him to do. Abu Jandal, wearing his chains, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned him to his father. Because there was peace between them, then it broke down after that, so he joined Abu Basir while he was on the stick, and a group of Muslims had gathered to him. Whenever a caravan of Quraysh passed by them, they would intercept it, kill whomever they could of them, and take whatever they could of their possessions, and it continued. Abu Jandal was with Abu Basir until Abu Basir died, then Abu Jandal and those who were with him from the Muslims came to Medina at the time of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he continued to fight with him and fight after him in the cause of God until he died in the Levant during the plague of Emmaus in the year eighteen of the year. The caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5210","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Al-Harith bin Hisham Ibn Al-Mughirah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Umar Ibn Makhzum, then Salit Ibn Muslim told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ikrimah, who said: When it was the day Al-Fath: Al-Harith bin Hisham and Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah entered upon Umm Hani’ bint Abi Talib, may God be pleased with her, and sought protection from her. They said: We are next to you, so she helped them, so Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, entered and looked at them and brandished the sword at them. So she jumped on them and embraced him, and said: Are you doing this to me from among the people in order to start me before them? So he said: Do you support the polytheists? So he left. Umm Hani said: I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have never met Ali from my mother’s son. I escaped from him. I rented two father-in-laws of mine from the polytheists and broke out against them so that he could kill them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “That was not for him.” We have rewarded whom you have rewarded, and we have protected whom you have believed.” So I returned to them and informed them, so they departed to their homes.It was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Al-Harith bin Hisham and Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah were sitting in their club, chatting in public. Al-Muzafara, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no way to them. We have secured them.” Al-Harith bin Hisham said: And I was ashamed to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sees me, and I remember seeing me in every place of the polytheists. Then I remember his righteousness and mercy, so he met him. While he was entering the mosque, he greeted me with the good news and stood until I came to him, so I greeted him and bore witness to the truth, and he said: “Praise be to God who He guided you. There was no one like you who was ignorant of Islam.” Al-Harith said: By God, I have never seen someone like you who is ignorant of Islam.
 Ibn Umar said: Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told me, Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair told me, I heard Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham He narrates, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his Hajj, and he was standing on his camel, and he was saying: “By God, you are indeed good.” “The land, and I love the land to God, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have expelled.” He said: So I said: I wish we could do so, so return to it, for it is Your birth and birth,Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I asked my Lord, Almighty and Majestic, and said: O God, you have taken me out of the land that I love most, so send me down. He loved the earth for you, so he brought me to Medina.”
 Ibn Umar said: “Al-Harith continued to reside in Mecca after he converted to Islam until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. When Abu Bakr’s letter came, Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, mobilizes the Muslims to invade the Romans. Ibn Hisham, Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl, and Suhail bin Abi Amr presented Abu Bakr ruled over Medina, so he came to them in their homes, welcomed them, greeted them, and was pleased with their place. Then they went out with the Muslims in raids to the Levant. Al-Harith bin Hisham witnessed a stallion and two soldiers, and he died in the Levant in the plague of Emmaus in the year eighteen, so he succeeded Omar bin Al-Khattab as ruler. His wife is Fatima bint al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, and she is the mother of Abdullah ibn al-Harith. Abdul Rahman used to say: “I have never seen a better companion than Omar.” Ibn Al-Khattab “Abdul-Rahman Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Hisham was one of the nobles of Quraysh.”"
"5211","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Dahqan told me about Marw, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told me, I am Abdan bin Othman, I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Al-Aswad bin Shayban, on the authority of Abu Nawfal bin Abi Aqrab, who said: Al-Harith bin Hisham, may God be pleased with him, left Mecca and was frightened. The people of Mecca were greatly alarmed, and not a single person was left who went out to pay him his respects, until when he was at the top of Al-Batha’ or wherever he wanted from there, he stopped and stood. The people around him were crying, so when he saw the people’s dismay, he said: “O people, I did not leave out of desire for myself over yourselves, nor to choose a country over Your country, but this matter happened, and men from Quraysh emerged from it, and by God, they were not from its teeth nor from its homes. By God, if the mountains of Mecca were gold and we spent them in the way of God, we would not have missed a single day of theirs. By God, if So they came to us in this world, seeking to share with them in the afterlife. Then a man feared God and went out as a fighter. So he went out as a fighter to the Levant and was martyred.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5211 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5212","Abu Omar Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Zahid, the companion of Thalab, told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Anazi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, on the authority of His father said: Al-Harith bin Hisham was one of those who witnessed Badr with the polytheists, but he was defeated among those who were defeated, so Hassan bin Thabit taunted him, saying:
 [full sea]
 If what you told me is a lie... then I will be saved from Al-Harith bin Hisham.
 He left his loved ones to fight on their behalf...and escaped with Tamra’s head and bridle.
 Al-Harith bin Hisham, may God be pleased with him, said, apologizing for his flight that day:
 [Long Sea]
 God knows I did not stop fighting them...until they killed my horse with a foamy blond hair.
 So I knew that if I fight one... I will be killed and my enemy will not be affected.
 So I turned away from them and the loved ones among them... desiring for them a punishment on the Day of Judgment.
 Then he attacked Uhud with the polytheists, and he did not continue to adhere to polytheism until he converted to Islam on the day of the conquest of Mecca, may God be pleased with him. Aisha narrated, on the authority of"
"5213","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Amer bin Salih Al-Zubairi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Hisham, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, how does revelation descend upon you? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is like the ringing of a bell, then he will be separated from me, and I have realized what he said, and he is the hardest on me, and sometimes “The angel comes to me and appears to me and speaks to me, so I understand what he says.” I do not know of anyone who said this hadith, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Al-Harith other than Amir bin Saleh “It was narrated by Hisham’s companions, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the hadith"
"5214","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Wa’il bin Dawud, on the authority of الزُّهْرِيِّ حَدَّثَهُمْ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ ثَعْلَبَةَ بْنِ صُعَيْرٍ الْعُذْرِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، «أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ He stood up as a preacher and ordered the zakat of al-fitr to be given as a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley for each person, or for each head, whether young or old. “A saa’ of dates, or a two-mode of wheat.” This is a hadith narrated by most of Al-Zuhri’s companions on his authority, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Tha’labah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, but they did not mention his father."
"5215","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told me, he said: “And Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin صُعَيْرِ بْنِ أَبِي صُعَيْرٍ الْعَدَوِيُّ وُلِدَ قَبْلَ الْهِجْرَةِ بِأَرْبَعِ سِنِينَ وَحُمِلَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَمَسَحَ وَجْهَهُ وَبَرَّكَ He was in the year of the conquest, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was fourteen years old. Abdullah bin Tha’labah died, and his nickname was Abu Muhammad, in the year eighty-nine, and he is ninety-three years old.”"
"5216","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Su’ayr, may God be pleased with him, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiped his head.”"
"5217","Abu Abdullah Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Su’ayr Al-Adhri, “He was born in the year of the conquest, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to him and he wiped his face And bless him.”"
"5218","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, he said: Among the allies of the Quraysh: Abdullah bin Adi. Ibn Al-Hamra Al-Zuhri, and his mother was Bint Shurayq bin Amr bin Wahb bin Shurayq, and his nickname was Abdullah bin Adi Abu Amr."
"5219","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Amr Abdullah bin Adi bin Al-Hamra Al-Khuza’i. He mentioned the plan to build the Kaaba. Ibn Omar said: “Abdullah bin Adi died during the caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5220","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, and Abdullah bin Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, they said: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of my nephew Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, On the authority of Abdullah bin Adi bin Al-Hamra, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stopped at the charade and said: “By God, I I know that you are the best of God’s earth and the most beloved of God’s earth to me, and had I not been expelled from you I would not have left.”"
"5221","Abdullah bin Battah narrated to us, Al-Hasan narrated to us, Al-Hussein narrated to us, Muhammad bin Omar narrated to us, saying: “And Khalid bin `Urfata bin Abraha bin Shayban bin Hasal bin Hind bin Abdullah bin Ghaylan bin Aslam bin Athrah, an ally of Bani Zuhra, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas was the ruler of Al-Qadisiyah."
"5222","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari told us, Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Muslim, the client of Khaled Ibn Arfafa, said to Al-Mukhtar: This is a lying man. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"
"5223","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, On the authority of Khaled bin Arfata, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “There will be events, strife, division, and disagreement. If you are able to be the one killed and not the killer, then do so.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5223 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5224","Ahmed bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told me, he said: “Suhail bin Amr, nicknamed Abu Yazid.”"
"5225","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Suhail bin Amr is one of the nobles of Quraysh. And their leaders, and he witnessed Badr with the polytheists, so Malik bin Al-Dakhsham captured him and said:
 [The Converging Sea]
 I took Suhail captivated, but I did not desire... anyone else from all the nations through him.
 And Khandaf knows that the boy... Suhayl is her youth if he is disciplined.
 I hit the blade until it bent... and I hated myself for the blessing.
 He said: And from his descendants is Abdullah, and he was one of the first immigrants, and he witnessed Badr and Abu Jandal, and he accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Utbah Al-Asghar”
 Ibn Omar said: Ishaq bin Hazim told me on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met Osama bin Zaid and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted his mount and made him sit in front of him, while Suhail bin Amr had his hands drawn towards him. His neck. Suhail said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca, I broke into my house, locked my door, and sent to Abdullah to Ask for protection from Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for I do not feel safe from being killed. So Abdullah went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, do you believe in him? He said: “Yes, he is secure in the security of God, so let him appear.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those around him: “Whoever meets Suhail bin Amr, do not He is drawn to him, for by my life, Suhail has intelligence and honor, and there is no one like Suhail who is ignorant of Islam.” So Abdullah bin Suhail went out to his father. So he informed him of the statement of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Suhail said: By God, he was righteous, both small and great, and Suhail used to accept and turn away in safety. He went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was a polytheist, until he converted to Islam by jiranah. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him some of the spoils. Hunayn, one hundred camels. Suhail bin Amr narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5225 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5226","Ishaq bin Muhammad al-Hashimi told us in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid al-Qatwani told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mina, on the authority of Abu Sa’id ibn Fadala al-Ansari - and he was a companion - may God be pleased with him. He said: I accompanied And Suhail bin Amr, one night Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, comforted him, and I heard Suhail saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “For one of you to remain in the cause of God for an hour is better for him than his life’s work for his family.” Suhail said: “And I will be stationed until I die and never return to Mecca.” Never.” He remained stationed in the Levant until he died there in the plague of Emmaus. This plague only occurred in the Levant in the eighteenth year of the year AH. Immigration
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5226 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5227","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us: I am Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari, Abdan bin Uthman told us, I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Jarir bin Hazim, I heard Al-Hasan speaking, saying: People attended Omar’s gate, and among them were Suhail bin Amr, Abu Sufyan bin Harb, and the sheikhs from Quraysh. So he went out and began to give the call to prayer to the people of Badr, such as Suhaib, Bilal, and Ammar. He said: By God, he was Badr and he loved them, and he had instructed With it, Abu Sufyan said: I have never seen the call to prayer like today, that these slaves are given the call to prayer while we are sitting and no attention is paid to us, so Suhail bin Amr - what a man he was not the wisest - said: “O my people, by God, I see what is on your faces. If you are angry, then get angry.” Upon yourselves, the people were called and you were called, and you hurried and you slowed down, but by God, the favor they preceded you with in what they saw is more difficult for you. This is what you are competing for from your door.” Then he said: “Indeed, these people have preceded you in what you see, and you have no way, by God, to what They preceded you to it, so consider this jihad and stick to it. Perhaps God Almighty will grant you jihad and martyrdom.” Then he shook off his garment and stood up. Then he went to Damascus. Al-Hasan said: “By God, he is right. God will not make a servant who hastened to him the same as a servant who was slower than him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5227 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5228","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hassan bin Muhammad, he said: Omar said To the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: O Messenger of God, let me remove the two turbans of Suhail bin Amr, so that he will never preach to his people again. So he said: “Leave him.” Perhaps one day he will make you happy.” Sufyan said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, the people of Mecca fled, so Suhail bin Amr stood at the Kaaba. He said: Whoever’s god is Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then Muhammad has died, and God is alive and does not die.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5228 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5229","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta Al-Asbahani told us, Suleiman told us Ibn Dawud Al-Shadhakuni, Muhammad Ibn Omar told us, he said: “Bilal Ibn Rabah, the client of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them both, and his nickname is Abu Abdullah. He was one of the descendants of Sirat. He died in Damascus in the year twenty and was buried near the small gate in the Damascus cemetery. He was sixty-six years old.”"
"5230","I heard Shuaib bin Talha say: “Bilal was raised by Abu Bakr, and Shuaib knows best about Bilal’s birth.”"
"5231","Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: Someone who saw Bilal told me: “He was a very thick-skinned man, tall and thin, stooped. He has a lot of hair, thin hair, and has a lot of hair, and it does not change. Bilal witnessed Badr Uhud, the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was a brother between him and Ubaidah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib.”"
"5232","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Hanafi, he said: “Bilal bin Rabah Abu Amr and Umm Bilal Hamama. He was sixty-seven years old and was buried at the Small Gate in the Damascus cemetery.”"
"5233","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq “that Abu Bakr He bought Bilal from Umayyah bin Khalaf, and he had witnessed a full moon with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was black in color. He was bought by Abu Bakr, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, on his behalf from Umayyah ibn Khalaf, Abu Bakr gave him a boy and took Bilal in his place, and his mother’s name was Hamama, and they all converted to Islam. His nickname was Abu Abdullah. He died in Damascus in the year twenty, or it is said, eighteen.”"
"5234","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, I heard Ismail bin Abi Khaled mentions, on the authority of Qays bin Mudrak bin Awf Al-Ahmasi, who said: I passed by Bilal while he was in the mosque, and I said: O Abu Abdullah, what makes you sit? He said: “I am waiting for the sun to rise.”"
"5235","Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad ibn Sulaiman informed me, I heard Muhammad ibn Ismail saying: “Bilal ibn Rabah Abu Abdul Karim, It is said: Abu Abdullah, and it is said: Abu Amr, the client of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him."
"5236","Abu Ishaq told us, I am Al-Thaqafi, Ubayd Allah ibn Saad told us, Ya’qub told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Bilal ibn Rabah, his mother Dove, and his sister is Oprah. It is said: Omar bin Abdullah Al-Madani is the client of Oprah."
"5237","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, Amr ibn Maimun told us, that Bilal’s brother belonged to the Arabs and claimed that he was one of them, so he proposed to a woman from The Arabs and they said: If Bilal is present, we will marry you. He said: Then Bilal came and said: “I am Bilal bin Rabah, and this is my brother, and he is a person of bad character.” And religion, so if you want to marry him, then marry him, and if you want to invite him, then invite him.” They said: “Whoever’s brother we will marry, then marry him.” It is true. The chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it, and this brother of Bilal has a narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5237 - True"
"5238","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Ja’fi told us, Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The first to demonstrate his Islam were seven: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he prevented him.” God bless his uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, God Almighty protected him with his people, and as for the rest of them, the polytheists took them. So they clothed them in iron armor and made them stand in the sun, and there was not a single one of them who did not go to them whenever they wanted, except for Bilal, for he was easy on his soul. In the name of God Almighty, and he treated his people in disgrace, so they gave him children, and they began to circumambulate him around the streets of Mecca, and he began to say: “Uhud Uhud,” with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5238 - True"
"5239","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us Ahmad bin Abdullah, Ahmed bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Bahr bin Nasr narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah Al-Majishun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “Abu Bakr is our master, and he freed our master,” meaning Bilal, “it is true, but they did not take him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5239 - True"
"5240","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ahmad Al-Thaqafi told us, Qutaibah told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: He mentioned Omar Fadl told Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them both, and he began to describe what was in it, then he said: “This is our master Bilal, one of the good deeds of Abu Bakr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5240 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5241","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, freed seven of those who were being tortured for the sake of God Almighty. Glory be to Him, among them are Bilal and Aamer bin Fuhayrah.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5241 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5242","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, al-Hakim told me, on the authority of al-Haqal ibn Ziyad, on the authority of al-Awza’i, Abu told me Ammar, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best of Sudan are three: Luqman and Bilal The dormitory of the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “with a valid chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"5243","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Amara bin Zazan told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are four races: I race against Arabs, Salman races against horses, Bilal races against Abyssinians, and Suhaib races against them.” By the Romans, “Ummara ibn Zazan was the only one to do so, on the authority of Thabit.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5243 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5244","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Wasiti told me, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Hussam bin Misk, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What an excellent man Bilal is. He is the master of the muezzins, and no one follows him except a muezzin, and the muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection.” Hussam was unique in his name.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5244 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5245","Abu Al-Abbas bin Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, I am Al-Hussein bin Waqid, told us Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: One morning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Bilal and said: “O Bilal, Why did you race ahead of me to Paradise last night? I heard your rattle in front of me, so I came upon a noble, square, golden palace, and I said: Who is this?"
"5246","Ibrahim bin Firas al-Faqih told me in Mecca, Bakr bin Suhail al-Damiati told me, Abdullah bin Saleh told me, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, may God be pleased with him, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he was staying in Ukaz. So I said: Who is with you on this matter? He said: “Two men: Abu Bakr and Bilal. So I converted to Islam, and you saw me while I was a quarter of Islam.” The chain of transmission is correct, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhees Al-Dhahabi] 5246 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"5247","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us He said: “Bilal, may God be pleased with him, died in the year twenty.”
 Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told me, Musab bin Abdullah told me, he said: “Bilal bin Rabah died in the Levant. In Damascus in the year twenty"
"5248","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Nasawi told me about Marwa, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith told us, Ammar bin Al-Hasan told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: “The first and second obstacles were witnessed by the Ansar, then by the Banu Abd al-Ashhal, Abu al-Haytham ibn Al-Tayhan, and his name is Malik, an ally of theirs, and he is a captain. He witnessed Badr and there was no outcome."
"5249","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, Abu Al-Haytham Bin Tayhan, his name is Malik bin Bali bin Amr bin Al-Haf bin Quda’ah, an ally of Banu Abd Al-Ashhal, and he said: And Abu Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan As'ad bin Zurarah was one of the first of the Ansar to convert to Islam in Mecca, and one of the first to meet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before their people. They presented the city with that, and Abu al-Haytham witnessed Aqaba with the Muslim Ansar, and he was one of the twelve captains, there is no disagreement. among themselves in this matter, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayhan and Uthman ibn Maz’un, and Abu al-Haytham testified “Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the other scenes were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5250","Saeed bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Saleh bin Kaysan, who said: “Abu Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan died during the succession of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.” In the city »"
"5251","Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habibah told us: I heard the sheikhs, the people of the house, meaning the Banu Abd al-Ashhal, saying: “Abu al-Haytham died. Ibn al-Tayhan, in the twentieth year of Medina.”"
"5252","Muhammad bin Yazid, Al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Hilal bin Bishr told us, Abu Khalaf Abdullah bin Issa told us, about Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his house one day At noon, he saw Abu Bakr sitting in the mosque, and he said: “What kept you out, Abu Bakr, at this hour?” He said: The one who brought you out took me out, O Messenger of God. Then Omar came and said: “What brought you out, O Ibn Al-Khattab?” He said: Who brought you out, O Messenger of God? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat talking to them and then said: “Do you have any strength? So you two go to this palm tree - and he gestured with his hand to the houses of the Ansar - and get food, drink and shade, God willing? We said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off and they went with him and mentioned the hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5252 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5253","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Saeed bin Amir bin Hudhaym bin Salman bin Rabi’ah bin Saad bin Jumah, and Umar had some of the soldiers of the Levant in charge of him, and he died while doing his work. In the Levant in the year twenty"
"5254","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abdullah told us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, that Omar, may God be pleased with him, said to Sa’id bin Amir bin Hudhaym: What is the matter with the people of the Levant? Do they love you? He said: I take care of them and care for them, so he gave him ten thousand and he returned them, and said: I have servants and horses, and I am well, and I want my work to be charity. On the Muslims, and Omar said: Do not do it, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me money less than that, so I said: Similar to what you said, and he said to me: “Then God has given you money that you did not ask for and did not indicate to yourself, so take it, for it is the provision that God has given you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5254 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5255","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Anas bin Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, nicknamed Abu Yazid, an ally of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he died in the year twentieth in the month of Rabi’. The first, and there was twenty-one years between him and his father in age. I mentioned above Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, and after him his son Marthad. And this grandson, and they are all among the Companions, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5255 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5256","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Rais told me about Marwa, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith told us, Ammar bin Al-Hasan told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: “And Usayd bin Hudayr bin Samak bin Atik bin Rafi’ bin Imru’ al-Qais bin Zaid bin Abd Al-Ashhal, nicknamed Abu Yahya, died in the year twenty."
"5257","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abu died Yahya Usayd bin Hudayr, in the twentieth year. He had witnessed Aqaba, then he was a captain. Omar bin Al-Khattab prayed over him in Medina and was buried. In Al-Baqi’, he has two nicknames: Abu Yahya and Abu Hudayr, and his father is Hudayr Al-Kateb. Usayd did not comment."
"5258","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, “And Usayd bin Al-Hudayr told us بْنِ سِمَاكٍ يُكَنَّى أَبَا يَحْيَى وَيُقَالُ أَبُو الْحُصَيْنِ وَيُقَالُ: أَبَا بَحْرٍ، وَكَانَ أُسَيْدٌ شَرِيفًا فِي قَوْمِهِ فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، وَالْإِسْلَامِ يُعَدُّ Of their wise men and those with their opinions, and he was one of the scribes, and his father Al-Hudayr the scribe was like that before him, and he was the chief of the Aws on the day Baath, and Hudair was killed that day, and Usayd bin Hudair was one of the seventy Ansar who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Aqaba in the narration of all of them, and one of the twelve captains, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother between Usayd bin Hudayr and Zaid bin Haritha, and Usayd did not witness Badr. He and other senior companions, including the captains and others, stayed away from Badr, because they did not think that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, faced neither war nor fighting. Usayd witnessed Uhud and was wounded seven times on that day, and remained steadfast with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “peace and blessings of God be upon him when the people were exposed, and he saw the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5258 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5259","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Usayd bin Hudayr told us, that he used to recite on the back of his house and he was good. The voice said: While I was reading, something like clouds covered me, and the woman was in the house, and the horse was in the house, so I was afraid that the woman would fall. So I left, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read, for he is an angel who has listened to the Qur’an.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Because Sufyan bin Uyaynah sent it on the authority of Al-Zuhri.
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5259 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5260","Muhammad ibn Salih, Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal, and Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to me. They said: Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani narrated to us, Sa’id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, I am Yahya bin Ayyub and Ibn Lahi’ah. They said: Amara bin Ghaziyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Othman, on the authority of his mother. Fatima bint Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “Usayd bin Hudayr was one of the most virtuous people, and he used to say: If only I were as I would be in one of three conditions: I would be among the people of Paradise, and I would not doubt that when I read the Qur’an and when I heard it, and when I heard The sermon of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if I witnessed a funeral, I had never witnessed a funeral, so I spoke to myself only in the direct object, And it did not reach him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5260 - True"
"5261","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Hisham bin Ali and Ishaq bin Al-Hassan told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a dark night. They left, and the staff of one of them lit up, so they walked in its light, and when they separated, the staff of the other lit up.” It is true according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5261 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5262","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Ammar bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Husayn, and he told me عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ مُحَمَّدٍ الصَّيْدَلَانِيُّ، ثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ أَيُّوبَ، أَنَا يَحْيَى بْنُ الْمُغِيرَةِ السَّعْدِيُّ، ثَنَا جَرِيرٌ، عَنْ حُصَيْنٍ، عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of his father, who said: Usayd Ibn Hudair was a righteous, laughing and pleasant man, while he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He talked to the people and made them laugh. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stabbed him in the side and said: You have caused me pain. He said: “Take retaliation.” He said: “O Messenger of God! You have to wear a shirt, but I did not have a shirt on. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his shirt and embraced him, then began to kiss his cheek and said: May my father be sacrificed for you. You and my mother, O Messenger of God, wanted this. “This is the wording of the hadith of Jarir on the authority of Husayn. The hadith of Warqa’ is brief and has a correct chain of narration. He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5262 - True"
"5263","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Qutaibah told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us. Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent man Usayd bin Hudayr “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5263 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5264","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me about what I read to him from the beginning of his book. He said: I am Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad, and Ahmed joined us. Bin Al-Husayn Al-Lahabi, Muhammad bin Talha Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Husayn bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Muadh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudair, that he groaned, and he was our leader, so he led us in prayer sitting, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned to him and they said: Oh Messenger of God, Usayd is our imam, and he is sick, and he prayed with us sitting, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So pray behind him sitting, for The imam is to be followed, so if he prays sitting, they pray behind him, sitting.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5264 - True"
"5265","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Muhammad bin Amr. Ibn Alqamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, who said: We came from a journey, and we met Dhu al-Hulayfah, and he was the servants of the Ansar. They will meet them. When they come and meet Usayd ibn Hudair, they call his wife to him, and he disguises himself and weeps. She said: So I said to him: Glory be to God, you From the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you have preceded, why do you cry over a woman? So he uncovered his head, then said: You have spoken the truth for the life of God, and by God it is right that I should not cry over anyone after Saad bin Muadh. The Messenger of God said: May God bless him and grant him peace. What did he say? I said to him: What did he say? He said: “The throne shook due to the death of Saad bin Muadh.” Aisha said: Usayd bin Hudayr walked between me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5265 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"5266","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Iyad bin Ghanam bin Zuhayr was from The nobles of Quraysh.” Ibn Qays al-Ruqayyat mentioned him and said:
 [light sea]
 Iyaad and what Iyadh bin Ghanam...he was among the best of women.
 He was the first to pass the road to the Romans."
"5267","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Nadr bin Salamah Al-Jaudi told us, Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, He said: Muhammad bin Omar Al-Waqidi told me, on the authority of his sheikhs, that they said: “Iyad bin Ghanam bin Zuhair bin Abi Shaddad bin Rabi’ah bin Hilal bin Uhayb bin Dabbah bin Al-Harith bin Fahr “He converted to Islam before Al-Hudaybiyyah and witnessed Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted him, and Umm al-Hakam, the daughter of Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, was with him. When Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah attended his death, he left Iyad as his successor. He was next to him, and Iyadh was a righteous man. When he was reported to Omar Abu Ubaidah, he expressed his sympathy and compassion for him, and said: Let no one tighten your corset. He asked whose work he appointed as successor, and they said: Iyad ibn Ghanam, so he confirmed it and wrote to him: Indeed, I have appointed you as your guardian as long as Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah did. So, do what God has a right for you, so Iyadh died on the day he died, and he had no money nor did anyone owe him a debt, and he died in the Levant in the year twenty. He is sixty years old
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5267 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5268","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Iyad bin Ghanam died in the year twenty.”"
"5269","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi informed us about what they agreed upon, Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Amr bin Ishaq told us Bin Ibrahim bin Al-Alaa bin Zuraiq Al-Homsi, Ubi told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, Al-Fadl told us Ibn Fadalah, narrating it to Aidh, Aidh narrating it to Jubayr bin Nufayr, that Iyad bin Ghanam Al-Ashri had an encounter with the owner of a house when it was opened. Then Hisham bin Hakim came to him and spoke harshly to him. Hisham stayed for several nights, then Hisham came to him apologizing, and said to Iyad: Did you not know that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people who will be most tormented on the Day of Resurrection will be the people who will be most tormented in this world.” Then Iyad said to him: Oh. Hisham: Indeed, we have heard what you have heard, and we have seen what you have seen, and we have accompanied those whom you have accompanied. Have you not heard, O Hisham, Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And he said: “Whoever has advice given to someone in authority should not speak to him publicly, but let him hold his hand and let him be dissatisfied with it. If he accepts it, He accepted it, otherwise he would have fulfilled what he owed and what is his.” And indeed, O Hisham, you are the one who dares to dare against the authority of God, so why not? You were afraid that the authority of God would kill you, and you would be killed by the authority of God. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5269 - Ibn Zuraiq is weak"
"5270","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Azhari told us, Al-Hussein bin Ishaq Al-Tustari told us, Azhar bin Nuh told us, Amr bin Al-Walid told us, He said: I heard Muawiyah bin Yahya Al-Sadfi, saying: Yahya bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghanam, who said: A messenger told me One day, God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Iyad, do not marry an old woman or a barren woman, for I will outnumber you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5270 - Muawiyah bin Yahya is weak"
"5271","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Al-Baraa bin Malik bin Al-Nadr bin Damdam bin Zaid bin Haram bin Jundub bin Amir bin Ghanam bin Adi bin Al-Najjar, and his mother: Umm Sulaym bint Malhan, who is the brother of Anas bin Malik through his father and mother, witnessed Uhud and the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was brave and had a distinguished reputation in war.” It was reported on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab wrote, “Do not use Al-Baraa ibn A king over an army of the Muslims, for it is one of the destructions that will come upon them.”"
"5272","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Azhar bin Saad told us, Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Thumama ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “He entered upon his brother Al-Baraa’ while he was lying down, placing one of his legs on On the other hand, his voice rejoiced, and he said: Do I fear that I will die in my bed, when you have been alone in killing a hundred of the infidels, apart from those whom the people joined me in? “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5272 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5273","Abu Mu'in Muhammad bin Issa Al-Attar told me about Marw, Abdan bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Rahman told us. Ibn Ma'n, Muhammad Ibn Ishaq reported on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Anas, he said: I heard Anas Ibn Malik say: Al-Bara' Ibn Malik was a man. He had a good voice, and he used to say to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during some of his travels. While he was standing, he approached women, and the Messenger of God said to him: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Beware of bottles.” He said: Then he stopped. Muhammad said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, hated for women to hear his voice.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5273 - True"
"5274","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, Al-Adl, informed me, and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, saying: Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Ayli told me, dictating to me. He said: Salama bin Ruh told me, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “How many weak and humble people of Dhul-Tamrain, if they had sworn an oath to God, He would have fulfilled their oath among them. Al-Bara’ bin Malik, for Al-Bara’ met a crowd of The polytheists, and the polytheists have caused pain among the Muslims.” So they said: O Baraa’, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you swore to God will surely bless you, so swear on your Lord.” He said: “I swear to you, O Lord, when you have given us their shoulders.” Then they met at the licorice bridge. So they felt pain among the Muslims, and they said to him: O Baraa’, swear on your Lord. He said: I swear on you, O Lord, when you gave us their shoulders. And you joined me with your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so they gave up their shoulders, and Al-Bara’ was killed as a martyr. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5274 - True"
"5275","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Azhar bin Jamil told us, Omar bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “When the Day of Aqaba was in Persia and the people had gathered, Al-Bara’ bin Malik got up and rode his horse while it was marching, then he said To his companions: “Wretched is that which you have accustomed your peers to, so he attacked the enemy, so God granted victory to the Muslims, and Al-Bara’ was martyred on that day.” He said Abu Imran Musa bin Harun: “Al-Bara’ was martyred on the day of Tuttar, and she was from Persia. Al-Bara’ bin Malik was martyred in the year one of And twenty years after the Hijra”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5275 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5276","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told me, Abu Khalifa Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah Muammar. Ibn Al-Muthanna said: “Al-Numan Ibn Amr Ibn Muqrin Ibn Amer Ibn Bakr Ibn Hajin Ibn Nasr Al-Muzani”"
"5277","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Sulayman told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, “Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin Al-Muzani was killed while he was the leader of the people in the year twenty-one.”"
"5278","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama told us, he said: Shu`bah narrated to me, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: “I brought Ibn Umar the funeral corpse of Nu’man bin Muqrin, and he placed his hand on his face, and made He cries.” Abu Abdullah bin Atiyya added to it with his chain of transmission, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, and said: Ibn Muqrin bin Aidh bin Mija bin Hujar Ibn Nasr Ibn Habashiyah Ibn Ka’b Ibn Abd Ibn Thawr Ibn Hadmah Ibn Latim Ibn Uthman Ibn Muzainah, and his nickname was Abu Amr. He and six of his brothers witnessed the trenches with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Numan was one of those who carried one of the Messenger of God’s brigades. May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5279","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Imran told us Al-Juni, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, consulted Al-Hurmuzan in Isfahan, Persia, and Azerbaijan, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, Isfahan is the head, and Persia and Azerbaijan are the wings, so if you cut off One of the wings, then the head belongs to the wing, and if you cut off the head, the two wings fall off, so start with Isfahan, so Omar bin Al-Khattab entered the mosque, Then he saw Al-Numan bin Muqrin praying, so he waited for him until he finished his prayer, and he said to him: I am your employer. He said: As for a collector, no. An invader, yes? He said: You are an invader, so he released him and sent to the people of Kufa to reinforce him and join him. Among them were Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, Al-Ash'ath bin Qais, Amr bin Ma'di Karib, and Abdullah bin Amr, so Al-Nu'man came to them and showed them And between them was a river, so Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah sent a messenger to them, and their king, the one with the eyebrows, consulted his companions and said: What do you think? I’m sitting. Do they have the appearance of war or the appearance and splendor of a king? So he sat in the form of a king and rejoiced on his bed.He placed the crown on his head, and around him were two blankets with brocade garments, earrings, and bracelets. Then Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah came and took With his two fingers, and the spear and shield in his hand, and the people around him spread out on a carpet of his, so he began to stab him with his spear, so he pierced it so that they would fly, and he said The one with the eyebrows said to him: O Arabs, you have been afflicted with extreme hunger and hardship, so you left. If you wish, we will meet you and return to your country. Then Al-Mughirah spoke and thanked God and praised Him, and said: We Arabs used to eat carrion and dead things, and people used to trample us, and we did not We trampled upon them, so God sent a messenger from us, in honor among us, and he spoke truthfully to us, and that He had promised us that here it would be opened for us. We have found everything that we promised to be true, and I see her here in a uniform and appearance, and I do not see those with me going to take him. Al-Mughirah said: So she said For myself: If you gathered your leggings and jumped up, then I sat with him on the bed, when I found him inattentive, and they rebuked me and started urging him, so I said: Do you think that if I was foolish, then this is not done to messengers, and we do not do this to your messengers when they come to us. He said: If you wish. You cut ties with us, and if you wish, we cut corners with you. I said: Rather, we cut corners with you, so we cut corners with them.We lined them up and they lined up, each seven in a chain, and five in a chain, so that they would not flee. He said: They shot us so that they hastened over us. He said: Al-Mughirah told Al-Nu’man: “The people hastened towards us, so carry us.” He said: “You are one of virtues, and I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” But I “witnessed that if the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not fight at the beginning of the day, he would delay the fighting until the sun had set, the winds had blown, and the Victory,” then Al-Nu’man said: O people, three tremors shook. As for the first tremor: Let the man relieve himself, and as for the second: So let the man look at his weapon and his sword. As for the third: I am pregnant, so bear. If anyone is killed, let no one blame anyone else. And if I am killed So do not turn away from me, for I am calling upon God with an invitation, so I decided upon every one of you when he believed in it, and he said: O God, grant Nu’man today as a witness. He supported the Muslims and conquered them, so he protected the people and waved his banner three times, then he was carried and it was the first to fall, may God be pleased with him, so I mentioned I gave him my will, and I did not blame him, and I knew his whereabouts. So when we killed a man from among them, his companions would turn away from us, dragging him, and the one with the eyebrows fell from the His martyred mule, his stomach split open, and God granted victory to the Muslims.So I brought an-Na`man and in it was an agar, so I brought him water and poured it on his face and washed the dirt off his face. He said: Who is this? I said: Maqil bin Yasar. He said: What did the people do? So I said: May God grant them victory, and he said: Praise be to God, write about this to Omar, and he was relieved, so the people gathered to Al-Ash’ath bin Qays, and he said: So we went to the mother of his son and said: Has he made a covenant with you? She said: No, except for an evildoer who has a book in it, so she read it: Then, if so-and-so is killed, then so-and-so, and if so-and-so is killed, then so-and-so. Hammad said: Then Ali bin Zaid told me, and Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi told us that he came to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and said: What did Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin do? He said: He was killed. Then he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. Then he said: What did so-and-so do? I said: He was killed, O Commander of the Faithful, and others we do not know. He said: I said: We do not know them, but God knows them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5279 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5280","Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Al-Thawri, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd bin Muqrin, on the authority of Suwaid bin Muqrin, said: We were seven Banu Muqrin during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We had a servant, and one of us slapped him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Free him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5280 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5281","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Rusta Al-Asbahani told us, Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Shadhakuni told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, He said: “Qatada bin Al-Numan bin Yazid bin Amr bin Sawad bin Zafar, and Zafar’s name is Ka’b bin Al-Khazraj bin Amr, and he is the Prophet. Ibn Malik Ibn Aws, and Qatada was nicknamed Abu Amr, and he was the grandfather of Asim and Yaqoub, the sons of Omar Ibn Qatada, and Asim Ibn Omar was from Scholars through biographies and other things
 Qatada bin Al-Numan witnessed Aqaba with seventy of the Ansar, and he was one of the archers mentioned among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He witnessed full moon and Uhud, and his eye was swollen on the day of Uhud, and his pupil ran down his cheek. Then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger"
"5282","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “The name Al-Hadrami, the father of Al-Ala’ Abdullah bin Attab bin Jubayr bin Rabi’ah bin Malik bin Awif bin Malik bin Al-Khazraj, and he was an ally in the war. Ibn Umayyah, but he was called Al-Hadrami because he came from Hadhramaut, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed him to Bahrain. Then Omar appointed him as governor of Bahrain, and he died there, so he appointed Abu Hurairah al-Dawsi in his place, but Al-Ala’ ibn al-Hadrami died. In Bahrain in the year twenty-one.”"
"5283","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq. Ibn Jarih reported, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told me, that Muhammad bin Al-Aswad bin Khalaf told him that his father Al-Aswad, He told him that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledging allegiance to people on the day of the conquest. He said: So he sat near the house of Samurah. Al-Aswad said: Then I saw the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he sat down, and people, young, old, and women, came to him and pledged their allegiance to him on Islam and the martyrdom, so I said: What is Islam? He said: “Belief in God.” I said: What is the testimony? He said: “A testimony that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5283 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5284","Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He took Hussein and kissed him, then he turned to them and said: “The boy is stingy, cowardly, ignorant, and sad.”"
"5285","Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, he said: “Muhammad bin Al-Aswad bin Khalaf bin Abd Yaghuth Al-Qurashi is counted among the Meccans.”"
"5286","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, “That Khaled bin Al-Walid died in the year twenty-one in Homs.”"
"5287","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Khaled bin Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzoum, and his mother: Lubabah bint Al-Harith bin Hazan Al-Hilaliyya, sister: Maimunah bint Al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Khaled was nicknamed Abu Sulaiman. Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, appointed him to rule Edessa and Harran. And Ar-Rabbah, and he remained there for a year, and sought pardon, and He pardoned him, so he came to Medina and resided there in his house until he died in Medina in the year two. ""And twenty"""
"5288","Abdullah bin Ghanim Al-Saydalani told me, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, I heard Yahya bin Bukayr saying: “Khalid bin Al-Walid He is called Abu Suleiman.”"
"5289","Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us: I am Abd al-Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: It was said: According to Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him: Women from the Banu al-Mughirah gathered in the house of Khalid ibn al-Walid, crying, and we hate to They will harm you, so if I forbid them, then Omar said: “They do not have to shed one or two tears of theirs unless there is licking or clawing.” “By licking” means: slapping, and by “lagging” it means: “screaming.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5289 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5290","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salama al-Ghazi told me, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Saleh told me, al-Layth told me, Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, departed from the parties, Khalid ibn al-Walid stayed at the party’s house, and sent To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his conversion to Islam. Tell us about the authenticity of what Al-Zubaidi mentioned about Khalid bin Al-Walid’s conversion to Islam before Khaybar."
"5291","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ubaid bin Abdul Wahid, I am Muhammad bin Al-Sirri, Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Sulaym, On the authority of Salih bin Yahya bin Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace on the Day of Khaybar, so he sent me to proclaim: Prayer is comprehensive, and no one will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5291 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5292","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Muhammad bin Fulayh told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, who said: “The conquest of Khaybar took place in the year six months,” but the narration is contrary to this."
"5293","Al-Hussein bin Ali told us: Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Rashid, the servant of Habib ibn Abi Aws, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Aws, Amr ibn al-Aas narrated to me from his narration, he said: I went out deliberately To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I met Khaled bin Al-Walid. That was before the conquest and he was coming from Mecca. I said: Where do you want, O Abu? Solomon? He said: By God, the mark has been straightened, and the man is a prophet. Go and embrace Islam. Until when? He said: “So we presented Medina to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and Khaled bin Al-Walid came forward and converted to Islam and pledged allegiance, then I approached, pledged allegiance, and left.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5293 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5294","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, in a section selected by Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal, on the authority of Ali bin Bahr bin Bari, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, my father told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Wahshi bin Harb bin Wahshi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq directed Khalid ibn al-Walid to fight the people of apostasy, and he was spoken about that, but he refused to turn him away and said: I heard the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He mentioned Khalid bin Al-Walid and said: “Yes, Abdullah, a brother of the clan, and a sword from the swords of God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5294 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5295","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal. He said: My father told me. Wahb bin Jarir told us. He said: Tell me. My father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he mourned the people of Mu’tah, he said: “Then one of the swords of God, Khaled Ibn Al-Walid, took the banner, and God gave him victory.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5295 - True"
"5296","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned the people of Mu’tah on the pulpit, then he said: “Then Major General Khalid bin “Al-Walid, and it is a sword from the swords of God.” This is a high, authentic, and strange hadith from the hadith of Ayyub, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5296 - Ayoub did not hear from Anas"
"5297","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Tha’labah told us, Abu Ismail Al-Muaddeb told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not harm Khaled For it is a sword from the swords of God, which he poured upon the disbelievers.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5297 - Mursal, which is more similar"
"5298","Abu Al-Abbas Ismail bin Abdullah told us, I am Abdan Al-Ahwazi, Abu Al-Sakin Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Tai told us, we told us Imran bin Zuhar bin Hisn, he said: Humayd bin Munhab told me, he said: My grandfather Aws bin Haritha bin Laam said: “There was no one more hostile to To the Arabs from Hormuz. When we finished with Musaylimah and his companions, we went to the direction of Basra, and we met Hormuz in Kazma in a crowd. Great, so Khaled appeared to him and called for excrement, so Hormuz appeared to him, so Khaled bin Al-Walid killed him, and he wrote about that to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq So he ransomed him and plundered him, and his cap amounted to one hundred thousand dirhams, and when the Persians honored a man, they would make his cap worth one hundred thousand dirhams.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5298 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5299","Ali bin Issa told me, Ahmad bin Najdah, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Hushaym told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of his father, Khalid bin Al-Walid lost his cap on the day of Yarmouk, and he said: They searched for it, but they did not find it. Then they searched for it and found it, and behold, it was A beautiful skullcap. Khalid said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah and shaved his head, and the people moved the sides of his hair, so I preceded them to His forelock and I put it in this hood, and if I witnessed a fight while she was with me, I was granted victory?
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5299 - Interrupted"
"5300","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najood, on the authority of Abu Wael said: Khalid bin Al-Walid wrote to Rustum, Mahran, and the council of Persians: “Peace be upon whoever follows guidance. As for what follows, we invite you to Islam. If you refuse, then pay the tribute out of hand, and you are negligent. But if you refuse, then with me are people who love to kill in the cause of God."
"5301","Then Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Mus’ab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “He died. Khaled bin Al-Walid in Medina in the year twenty-two.”"
"5302","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Khalid bin Al-Walid died in the Levant. It was said: “In Homs, in the year twenty-one.” Yahya bin Bukair said: “He died in the city in the year seventeen or eighteen.”"
"5303","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa: “In naming Whoever witnessed Badr from Asad bin Abdul-Uzza Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah is an ally of them.”"
"5304","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Haatib bin Abi Balta’ah was nicknamed Abu Muhammad.”"
"5305","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Haatib bin Abi Balta'ah was nicknamed Abu Muhammad and he was in what was said of Lakhm. Then he was one of Banu Rashidah and he witnessed Badr and the Trench, and all the scenes were with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him to Al-Muqawqis, the owner of Alexandria, and among what was mentioned was The aforementioned archers were among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He died in Medina when he was sixty-five years old, and Othman bin Affan. He was a merchant who sold food. He had a good body, a thin beard, and he bent down towards the palace as long as his fingers were long."
"5306","Abdullah bin Hamawayh Al-Saidalani told me, and Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, saying: I heard Yahya bin Bukair saying: “Hatib died. Ibn Abi Balta’ah in the year 30, and Othman Ibn Affan prayed over him. He was nicknamed Abu Muhammad.”"
"5307","Abu Nasr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Omar Al-Khafaf told me, Muhammad bin Al-Mundhir bin Saeed Al-Harawi told us, Abu Al-Zubayr Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Muslim Al-Makki said: Harun bin Yahya bin Harun bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib bin Abi Baltaa told me. Al-Madani said: Abu Rabi’ah Al-Harrani told me, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He heard Hatib ibn Abi Balta’ah al-Madani say: He saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at Uhud while he was in difficulty and in the hands of Ali ibn Abi. He was looking for a shield that had water in it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was washing his face with that water, and Hatib said to him: Who did this to you? He said: “Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas smashed my face, and struck my forearms with a stone he threw at me.” I said: I heard a shouter shouting on the mountain, “Muhammad has been killed.” So I came to you and my spirit was gone. I said: Where is Utbah heading? He pointed to where he was heading, so I went on until I found him and struck him. With the sword, I beheaded him, then descended, took his head, robbed him, and his horse, and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he handed it over to me. He prayed for me and said: “May God be pleased with you” twice.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5307 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5308","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told us, On the authority of Jabir that a servant of Hatib came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining to Hatib, and he said: O Prophet of God, let Hatib enter the Fire, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have lied. They will never enter it, while Badr and Al-Hudaybiyyah were witnessed.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5308 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5309","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Musa bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Al-Harith Al-Harrani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah, that He told him that his father had written to the infidels of Quraysh in a letter while he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he had witnessed Badr, so he called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him and Ali and Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them, and he said: “Go until you meet a woman who has a letter, so bring it to me.” So they went until They came to her and said: Give us the letter that you have. They told her that they would not leave until they had removed every garment on her. She said: Have you not Two Muslim men said: Yes, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that you have a letter. When she was certain that she had not escaped from them, She removed the book from her head and gave it to them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called a woodcutter to read the letter to him. He said: “Do you know? This book? He said: Yes. He said: “What made you do that?” He said: My son and my relatives were there, and I was a Bedouin among you, the people of Quraysh. Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Permit me, O Messenger of God, to Hatib was killed, and the Messenger of God said, “No.” He had witnessed Badr, and you do not know, perhaps God had seen the people of Badr, and said, “Do what Whatever you wish, I will forgive you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5309 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5310","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubayy told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, said: “Ubayy bin Ka’b bin Qais bin Ubaid bin Zayd bin Muawiyah bin Amr bin Malik bin The carpenter witnessed a full moon.”"
"5311","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, “He mentioned this lineage and added to it, and the mother of Ubayy bin Ka'b Sahaila bint Al-Aswad bin Haram bin Amr bin Zayd Manat bin Adi bin Amr bin Malik bin Al-Najjar, and she is Abu Talha's paternal aunt."
"5312","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq told us: I am Ismail ibn Qutaibah, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr told us, he said: “Ubay ibn Qutaybah died. Ka`b during the caliphate of Omar ibn al-Khattab in the year twenty-two.”"
"5313","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, and he mentioned The lineage is like this, and he added that he witnessed Aqaba with seventy of the Ansar, “and he was writing down the revelation for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was The time of his death differed, so it was said that he died during the caliphate of Omar in the year twenty-two, and it was said that he died during the caliphate of Othman in the year thirty, and this “I confirm the sayings that Uthman ordered him to compile the Qur’an.”"
"5314","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, he said: My father told me, Hushaym told me, on the authority of Yunus bin Abdul, and Mubarak, On the authority of Al-Hasan, Ghani Al-Suddi narrated to us, he said: “I saw Ubayy ibn Ka’b with a white head and beard, not dyed.”"
"5315","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, Abu Nu’aym told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq said: “The people who judged among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were six: Omar, Ali, Abdullah, Ubayy, and Zaid. And Abu Musa, may God be pleased with them, “This is what he told us, and in most of the narrations and the most correct of them, Muadh bin Jabal replaced Abu Musa.”"
"5316","Muhammad bin Muzaffar told me, Abu Al-Jahm told us, Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: I heard Abu Mushar, saying: “Ubayy bin Ka’b named him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the master of the Ansar. He did not even die. They said: the master of the Muslims.”"
"5317","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “And my father died in... Caliphate of Omar in the year twenty-two”"
"5318","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Ubayy bin Ka’b died during the caliphate of Uthman in the year Thirty-two disagreements emerged at the time of the death of Ubayy ibn Ka’b.”"
"5319","So Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Mus’ab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Ubayy bin Ka’b bin Amr bin Malik bin Al-Najjar died during the Caliphate of Othman. He had a white head and beard. He was killed in the year twenty-nine, and it was said that he was Twenty-two years, and it was said that he died during the Caliphate of Uthman in the year thirty, and it was mentioned that he was nicknamed Abu Tufayl, and he had two nicknames. His death occurred in the city of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the stabbing attack against Othman appeared.”"
"5320","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told me, Abu Ja`far al-Hadrami told us, Muhammad bin al-Hasan bin Ishkab told us, Muhammad bin Kathir al-Kufi told us, about Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, said: “There was ferocity in Ubayy.”"
"5321","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Sari bin Yahya Al-Tamimi told us, Qubaysah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, speaking on the authority of his father, he said: When the people fell into the matter of Uthman, may God be pleased with him On his authority, I said to Ubayy ibn Ka’b: Aba al-Mundhir, what is the way out of this matter? He said: “The Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet. Whatever is made clear to you, act upon it, and whatever is difficult for you, leave it to the one who knows it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5321 - True"
"5322","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “made brotherhood among his companions, so he made brotherhood between Ubayy bin Ka’b and Sa’id bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl.”"
"5323","Abu Al-Nadr, the jurist, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr Al-Bajli told us, Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Qais bin Ubadah, said: I witnessed Medina, and when the prayer was performed, I went forward and stood in the first row, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, came out. God told him, so he divided the ranks, then he came forward and a light-bearded man came out with him. He looked at the faces of the people, and when he saw me, he pushed me and stood in my place. This became difficult for me, so when he left, he turned to me and said: Do not be distressed and do not make you sad. I am more difficult for you than I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, saying: “No one will stand in the first row except the Muhajireen and Ansar.” So I said: Who is this? They said: Ubayy bin Ka’b, “This is a hadith narrated alone by Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Qatada, and it is an authentic chain of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5323 - True"
"5324","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Sari bin Yahya told us, Qabaisa told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Surah was revealed to me. And I was commanded to recite it to you.” He said: I said: I named it for you. He said: “Yes.” I said to my father: Are you happy about that, Abu Al-Mundhir? He said: And what prevents me, by God Almighty and Blessed, He says: {Say: By the grace of God and by His mercy - and in that let them rejoice} [Yunus: 58] “This is an authentic hadith.” chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5324 - True"
"5325","Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the reciter and imam in Mecca in the Sacred Mosque, told us. Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Sayegh, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza told us: I heard Ikrimah bin Suleiman, He says: I recited to Ismail bin Abdullah bin Constantine, and when I reached Duha, he said to me: “Takbir, Akbar at the end of every surah, until It concludes. Abdullah bin Kathir told him that he had recited the reading to Mujahid, so he ordered him to do so, and Mujahid told him that Ibn Abbas ordered him to do so. Thus, Ibn Abbas told him that Ubayy bin Ka’b ordered him to do that, and Ubayy bin Ka’b told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to do so. Thus, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5325 - Al-Bazzi has spoken about it"
"5326","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Saeed bin Iyas. Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Abu Al-Mundhir, Which verse in the Book of God is greater in your opinion? He said: I said: {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Al-Baqarah: 255] He said: Then he struck my chest and said: “May knowledge be blessed with you, Aba al-Mundhir.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5326 - True"
"5327","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Abu Qalaba told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ja’far bin Suleiman told me, on the authority of my father Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Jundub, said: I came to Medina to seek knowledge, so I entered the mosque, and behold, there was a man and the people were gathered around him. So I said: Who is this? They said: This is Ubayy ibn Ka'b, so I followed him and he entered his house, so I knocked on the door for him, and he came out and he cursed me and cursed me, so I received him. towards the qiblah, so I said: “O God, we complain to You about them, we spend our expenses, we tire our bodies, and we carry our mounts in pursuit of knowledge. We found that they hated us, so he said: “If you delay me until Friday, so that I may speak about what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I will not be afraid.” It is a blameworthy person. When it was Thursday, I woke up and saw that the roads were deep. I said: What is the matter with the people today? They said: It is as if you are a stranger. I said: Yes, they said: The leader of the Muslims, Ubayy ibn Ka’b, died."
"5328","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, he said: Habib bin Abi told me Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “Ali made us judge, and my father made us read, and we will pray.” Some of what my father says, and my father says: I learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I will not leave it, and God, Blessed and Most High, said: {What We abrogate a verse or cause it to be forgotten.} [Al-Baqarah: 106]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5328 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5329","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, Abu Salamah, and Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, said: Omar bin Al-Khattab passed by a man and he was saying: {The forerunners, the first among the immigrants and Ansar. And those who followed them in righteousness, may God be pleased with them and they are pleased with Him} [Al-Tawbah: 100] until the end of the verse. Then Umar stopped at him and said: Go away, so when He left, and Omar said to him: Who taught you this verse? He said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b taught it to me, and he said: Go with us to him, so they went to him, and behold, he was reclining on a pillow, bowing his head, and he saluted. He returned the greetings to him, and said: O Abu Al-Mundhir. He said: “At your service.” He said: This man told me that you recited this verse to him. He said: “He is right. I received it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Omar said: Did you receive it from the Messenger of God? He said: Yes, I received it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “May God bless him and grant him peace” three times, all of which he said, and on the third time while he was angry, “Yes, by God, God has sent it down to Gabriel.” And He revealed it to Muhammad, but neither Al-Khattab nor his son took part in it. So Omar came out, raising his hands, and saying: God is great, God is great. Akbar
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5329 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5330","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, he said: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, I am Rawh bin Ubadah, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Omar bin Al-Khattab came to this verse: {Those who believe and do not mix up their faith with injustice} [Al-An’am: 82] Then Ubayy ibn Ka’b came and asked him: Which of us has not done wrong? He said to him: “O Commander of the Faithful, that is polytheism. Did you not hear what Luqman said to his son: {O my son, do not associate anything with God, for polytheism is injustice. Great} [Luqman: 13] """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5330 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5331","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told me, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin al-Muthanna, who said: “Abd Al-Rahman bin Awf bin Abdul Rahman bin Abd bin Al-Harith bin Zahra bin Kilab bin Murrah bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fihr bin Malik"
"5332","Musab bin Abdullah told me, he said: “Abdul Rahman bin Awf bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Zahra, and his mother and his brother’s mother.” Al-Aswad bin Awf: Al-Shifa’ bint Awf bin Abd bin Al-Harith bin Zahra bin Kilab, and she had emigrated before the conquest. Abdul-Rahman’s name is: Abdul-Amr, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called him Abdul-Rahman.”"
"5333","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa’d narrated to us, he said: “Abdullah died Al-Rahman ibn Awf was nine years of age from Uthman, and Uthman prayed upon him, and he was seventy-five years old.”"
"5334","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, I heard Ibrahim bin Qariz saying: I heard Ali saying: When Abd al-Rahman bin Awf died: “She reached her peace and preceded her race.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5334 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5335","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, so he mentioned this lineage and added, “And he was Abdul Rahman His nickname is Abu Muhammad, and in pre-Islamic times his name was Abdul Kaaba, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him Abdul Rahman.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5335 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5336","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: I am Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Muhammad bin Abi Nu’aym al-Wasiti told us, Ibrahim told us. Ibn Saad said: My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, who said: “In pre-Islamic times my name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of God named me “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhees Al-Dhahabi] 5336 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhis due to its weakness"
"5337","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, regarding what he read to Malik, On the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abdul Rahman: “What did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in receiving the The corner? - meaning the Black Stone -” Abdul Rahman said: I received it and left it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are correct.” Al-Hakim said: “I am not I doubt whether Urwah ibn al-Zubayr met Abdul-Rahman ibn Awf. If he heard this hadith from him, then it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and he did not He brings him out.”"
"5338","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal. He said: My father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he told us: Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Saad bin Abi Waqqas at the funeral of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He said: “Go, Ibn Awf, with your belly from the world, which you have not frowned upon at all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5338 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5339","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Abd al-Rahman: “How did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in receiving the stone?” He said: I received it and left it. He said: “You are correct, O Abu Muhammad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5339 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5340","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdul Rahman died. Ibn Awf, nicknamed Abu Muhammad, in the year thirty-two, and he is seventy-five years old.”"
"5341","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told me, Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ibrahim told me Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf fainted during his pain, so they thought that it had overtaken him. Therein, until they rose up from him and dressed him in a garment, and Umm Kulthum bint Uqba and his wife went out to the mosque seeking help in what she had been commanded to do. Of patience and prayer, they remained for an hour while he was in a trance, then he woke up, and the first thing he spoke was to say “Allahu Akbar,” and so the people of the house said “Allahu Akbar.” He followed them, then said to them: “Did I faint just before?” They said: Yes, and he said: “You are right.” He said: “Indeed, while I was in a trance, two men attacked me, one of them very harsh and rude, and they said: ‘Go, let us judge you. To the Mighty, the All-Knowing,” and he said: “Send him back, for he is among those for whom God has ordained happiness and forgiveness in their mothers’ wombs, and that he will enjoy He built it for as long as God wished.” He lived for a month after that, then he died, may God be pleased with him, and Uthman, may God be pleased with him, performed the Hajj there.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5341 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5342","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Abu Thabit told us, Yusuf bin Yaqoub al-Majishun told us, I am righteous. Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, who said: “Umayyah Ibn Khalaf said: Write me in the name you used to You write it to me, ‘Abd Amr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5342 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5343","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin al-Ja’d told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I heard Saad bin Malik, when Abd al-Rahman bin Awf died, saying: “And they brought him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5343 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5344","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Abu Ayyub told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Jafar Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Yaqoub Ibn Utbah Ibn Al-Mughirah Ibn Al-Akhnas, who said: “Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf was born ten years after the elephant.” For years, he died, may God have mercy on him, in the year thirty-two, when he was seventy-five years old. His nickname was Abu Muhammad, and he was buried in Al-Baqi’. Othman prayed over him, and he was a tall man with thin skin - meaning, thin skin - white with a reddish hue.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5344 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5345","Muhammad ibn Ya’qub al-Hafiz narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa’d narrated to us, Ya’qub narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I was informed that “Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was wounded twenty-one times on the day of Uhud, and he was injured in his leg, and he was limping from there.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5345 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5346","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, I am Yazid bin Harun, I am Humaid, on the authority of Anas, and we told us Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Humaid told me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik says: “Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came as an immigrant to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother. “Between him and Saad bin Al-Rabi’, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5346 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5347","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told me about Hamdan, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Burd told us, al-Haytham bin Jamil told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, who said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, saying to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf: The day he died, go: “O Ibn Awf, you have attained its purity and outstripped its lustre.”"
"5348","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Hisham Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: “I was informed that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf freed thirty thousand houses.”"
"5349","Abu Ja`far al-Faqih told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad: “In naming the one who witnessed Badr With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Banu Zahra bin Kilab bin Murrah: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf bin Zuhair."
"5350","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abu Bakr told me Ibn Abi Sabra, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abi Harmala, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Al-Sharid, who said: “Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf left behind a thousand camels and three thousand sheep. With Naqi', and a hundred horses grazed on Naqi', and he used to farm in Al-Jurf on twenty meadows, and he saved his family's food from that year. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf converted to Islam before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Dar al-Arqam, and before he made supplication there, and he witnessed He was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Badr, Uhud, the Trench and all the other scenes. He remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he took office. People »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5350 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5351","Muhammad bin Ya’qub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ubayd Allah bin Sa’d told us, Ya’qub told us, on the authority of his father, “Abd al-Rahman bin Awf told me He was called: the disciple of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5352","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Salih bin Ibrahim bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Miswar bin Makhrama, who said: I was riding in a caravan between Uthman and Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Awf, then Othman said: “Who is the owner of the khamisah?” Abdul Rahman said: I do, then Othman said: “Here, Miswar, whoever claims that he is better than your uncle Abdul Rahman in the first migration has lied
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5352 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5353","Ahmad bin Ali al-Muqri informed me, Abu Umayyah Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Ibrahim bin Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, my father told me, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his mother, Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Busra while she was combing Aisha’s hair, and he said: “Oh Busra, who will propose to Umm Kulthum? She said: I heard one or two men say: “Where are you regarding the leader of the Muslims, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf?” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5353 - In its chain of transmission is Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, and he is weak."
"5354","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani, Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Abu Al-Mu’alla. Al-Jazari, on the authority of Maymun bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said To the people of the Shura Council: Would you like me to choose for you and finish it? Then Ali said: I am the first to be satisfied, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says to you: “You are trustworthy among the people of heaven, trustworthy among the people of earth.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5354 - Abu Al-Mu’alla is Furat bin Al-Sa’ib, they left him"
"5355","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Suleiman Al-Baransi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told me, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, said: I told Abdullah bin Omar, and Abu Abdullah told me Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abd al-Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Jabir Al-Asadi said: I was in ihram and saw a gazelle, so I shot it and it died, and it fell on me as a result of that, so I went to Omar bin Al-Khattab I asked him, and I found next to him a man with a white, gentle face, so he was Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, so I asked Omar, and he turned around. To Abd al-Rahman, and he said: Do you think a sheep would be enough for him? He said: “Yes.” So he ordered me to slaughter a sheep. When we got up from him, he said: A friend of mine: Indeed The Commander of the Faithful did not think well of issuing a fatwa until he asked the man, and Omar heard some of what he said, so Omar beat him up at Durra, then he approached me to beat me. So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I did not say anything, but he said it. He said: Then he left me, then he said: “You wanted to kill what is forbidden and commit transgression.” With a fatwa,” then the Commander of the Faithful, may God be pleased with him, said: “Indeed, there are ten morals in man, nine good, and one bad. And that evil one spoils it.” Then he said: “Beware of the stumbling of youth.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5355 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5356","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Salamah Mansour bin Salamah Al-Khuza’i told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Ja`far al-Makhrami, Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar told me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf sold his land for forty thousand dinars, so he divided it. Among the Banu Zahra, the poor Muslims and immigrants, and the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent money from Aisha, may God be pleased with her. Then she said: Who sent this money? I said: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He said: And he told the story. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one will be kind to you after me except “Those who are patient. May God give Ibn Awf drink from the waters of Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5356 - Not connected"
"5357","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yunus bin Muhammad, and Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Azraqi told us, they said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Al-Husayn bin Awf bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to his wives: “Indeed, the one who is kind to you after me is the truthful and righteous, O God. “Give water to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from the waters of Paradise.” The hadith has been authenticated on the authority of Aisha and Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5357 - On the authority of Aisha and Umm Salamah"
"5358","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Khalid bin Yazid bin Abi Malik told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “O Ibn Awf, you are one of the rich. And you will not enter Paradise except crawling, so lend to God, and He will free your feet.” He said: “What did I lend to God?” He said: “You will disown yourself from what you are in.” He said: O Messenger. God, from all of him altogether, said: “Yes.” Then Ibn Awf came out while he was concerned about that, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to him and said: “ Gabriel came to me and said: Order Ibn Awf to entertain the guest, to feed the poor, to give to the beggar, and to start with those he supports, for if he does That was the purification of what was in it: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5358 - Khalid bin Yazid is considered weak by a group"
"5359","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Quraysh bin Anas told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of you is the best to my family after me.” The Quraysh said: Then Muhammad spoke to me. Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman: “His father bequeathed to the mothers of the believers a garden that was sold after him for forty thousand dinars.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and he has a valid witness according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5359 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5360","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, Sakhr bin Abdullah bin Harmala, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, narrated to him, he said: I entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to me: “I am telling you to do what concerns me after me, and none will be patient with you except those who are patient.” Then she said: So God gave your father drink. From the path of Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf had connected them with money, so it was sold for forty thousand.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5360 - Sakhr bin Abdullah Saduq did not go out to him"
"5361","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi, may God be pleased with him, told me: Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Hajjaj bin Rashidun al-Masri told us in Egypt, saying: Musa bin Aoun bin Abdullah bin Aoun dictated to me: “Abdullah bin Masoud bin Kahil bin Habib bin Tamer bin Makhzoum bin Sahila bin Kahil bin Al-Harith bin Taim bin Saad bin Hudhayl bin Mudarika bin Ilyas bin Mudar bin Nizar”"
"5362","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us about this, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us this, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Yazid Al-Sada’i told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Yazid Al-Sada’i told us. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, said: “Abdullah bin Masoud bin Al-Harith bin Shamkh bin Makhzoum Ibn Kahil Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Saad Ibn Hudhayl, from the allies of Bani Zuhra.” Al-Waqidi differed from them regarding this lineage, as Abu Abd told us. Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Abdullah bin Masoud bin Ghafil Ibn Habib Ibn Shamkh Ibn Far Ibn Makhzoum Ibn Sahila Ibn Kahil Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Taym Ibn Saad Ibn Hudhayl Ibn Mudarika, and he was His son's nickname is Abd al-Rahman: Abu Abd al-Rahman, and his father was Masoud bin Ghafil, who swore an alliance with Abd al-Harith bin Zahra in pre-Islamic times. Abdullah bin Masoud converted to Islam before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Dar Al-Arqam, and Abdullah bin Masoud testified at all He traveled around Badr and Uhud, the trench, and all the battlefields with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he emigrated two migrations, and he was the owner of a secret. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his siwak, his black shoes, his sandals, and his purity. He was a thin, short man with thick skin. He died In Medina in the year thirty-two, he was buried in Al-Baqi’, and on the day of his death he was said to have been sixty-odd years old.”"
"5363","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abdullah died Ibn Masoud was in Medina in the year thirty-two, when Uthman was killed. He had advised Al-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam and prayed over him. It has been said that Ammar ibn Yasser was prayed over, and he was buried in Al-Baqi’ at night. He was sixty-six years old.”"
"5364","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abdullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abu Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him Abba Abdul-Rahman, and no children were born to him.”"
"5365","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Musa bin Harun told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “The mother of Abdullah bin Masoud, Umm Abd bint Abd bin Al-Harith bin Zahra.”"
"5366","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “The nickname of Abdullah bin Masoud Abu Abd al-Rahman told us, Abu al-Abbas told us, Sa`id bin Uthman al-Tanukhi told us, al-Khasib bin Nasih told us, Sulayman bin Abi told us Suleiman Al-Qaflani, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, “that Ibn Masoud called Alqamah Abu Shibl before he was born to him,” he said: He was asked, and Alqamah narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nicknamed him Abu Abdul Rahman before he was born.” ""His"""
"5367","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Yahya ibn al-Yaman told us, al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim He said: “Abdullah bin Masoud was kind and gentle, and his mother was: Umm Abd bint Abd bin Al-Harith bin Zahra, and it is said: she was from the continent"""
"5368","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us: I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abi told us Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: “You have seen me “The sixth person on earth is a Muslim other than us.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5368 - True"
"5369","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming Whoever witnessed Badr from among the allies of Banu Zahra bin Kilab, Abdullah bin Masoud,” Urwah said: “And among those who emigrated to Abyssinia by migration.” The first was before the emergence of Jaafar bin Abi Talib Abdullah bin Masoud.”"
"5370","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sukhbra, who said: “I was with Abdullah bin Masoud, and he was a gentle man, with a tinge on him, and gentle. “The body is weak in flesh.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5370 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5371","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Masoud died in Medina, and he prayed Ali Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam”"
"5372","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother between Al-Zubayr and Ibn Al-Awwam and Abdullah Ibn Masoud.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5372 - True"
"5373","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdul Allah ibn al-Zubayr said: “Mention what Abdullah ibn Masoud advised, if something happened to him during his illness, that he return his will to By God, then to Al-Zubayr Ibn Al-Awwam and his son Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, and they are in trouble and trouble for what is now and what they have decreed, and Abd’s daughters are not to be married. God, except by their permission, and this does not apply specifically to Zainab.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5373 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5374","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told me, Abu Al-Umays told me, On the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, who said: “Abdullah used to have the Sunnah come upon him, and he would not narrate on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. One day, he spoke about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a conversation that made him depressed and made the sweat bead on his forehead and he said: “Show “This or close to this.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5374 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5375","Abu Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Ishaq Al-Subaie’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he heard Abu Musa say: “My brother and I came from Yemen. So we stayed for a while and saw nothing but Abdullah bin Masoud, a man from the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from what we saw of his entry and entry. His mother said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5375 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5376","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: I heard Hudhayfah says: “Indeed, the person whose guidance, honor, and guidance most resemble Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is Abdullah bin Masoud, from the time he goes out until the time he returns. I do not know what is in his house, and the well-preserved companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew that Ibn Umm Abd was one of the closest people to God. On the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5376 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5377","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told me: I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am Mas’ar. He said: Maan bin told me Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of his father, who said: “Abdullah, when his eyes calmed down, I heard a loud noise. Like the sound of bees until morning.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5377 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5378","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, I Jami` bin Shaddad said: I heard Abdullah bin Mirdas say: “Abdullah used to address us every Thursday on his feet, and he would speak some words while we We long for it to increase.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5378 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5379","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Habba Al-Arani said: I read in Omar’s letter to the people of Yemen and Kufa: “As for what follows, you are the head of the Arabs and their skull, and you are my arrow.” What I am shooting at, if something comes from here and here, and I sent Abdullah to you and chose him for you, and I preferred you to him over myself.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5379 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5380","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, he said: My father told me, Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Habba Al-Arni, that people came to Ali and praised Abdullah bin Masoud, and he said: “I say about him something like What they said, and the best is the one who has read the Qur’an, declared what it has permitted to be lawful, and declared unlawful what it has declared unlawful, is an expert in the religion, and knowledgeable of the Sunnah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5380 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5381","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr, who said: “I have not seen a man more knowledgeable about what God has revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, than... Abdullah bin Masoud,” and Abu Musa said: “If you say that, for he used to listen when we did not listen, and he would enter when we did not enter.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5381 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5382","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told me, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: “If you knew my sins, two men would not have stepped on my heels.” And you placed dust on my head, and I wished that God had forgiven me for one of my sins, and that I had been called Abdullah bin Ruthah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5382 - All of them are authentic"
"5383","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told me, and Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, they said: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail told us, Israel, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: I came to Syria and prayed two rak’ahs, then I said: “O God, make it easy for me to sit with a righteous person.” So I met a group of people and sat down, then one of them came and sat next to me, so I said: Who is he? Abu Al-Darda’ said, “I said, ‘I prayed to God to facilitate a good companion for me, and He facilitated it for me.’ He said, ‘Who are you from?’” I said: From the people of Kufa. He said: “Isn’t there with you Ibn Umm Abd, the owner of the sandals, the pillow, and the sanitizer, and among you is the one whom God has rewarded?” Who is Satan according to the tongue of his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and among you is the keeper of the secret of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which no one else knows? This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And the chains of transmission that preceded it are all authentic and they did not narrate them. Rather, I left out the words.” It is based on it because it is not supported, and this is supported.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5383 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5384","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, they said: Abu Hudhayfah told us, and Da’laj bin told us. Ahmad Al-Sijzi, in Baghdad, Abdul Aziz bin Muawiyah Al-Basri told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ten people in Paradise: He mentioned Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and Sa’id bin Zaid. And Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with them, said: “This is a hadith that was mentioned only by Ibn Masoud, in which Abu Hudhayfah was cited, and Al-Bukhari cited Abu Hudhayfah as evidence.” Hudhayfah, except that they did not use Abdullah bin Zalim as evidence."
"5385","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, informed us. He said: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi, while I was listening. Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurra, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Masoud was on a tree gathering for them. Then the wind blew and uncovered his legs, and they laughed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in Al-Mizan from Uhud” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5385 - True"
"5386","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, I am Ahmad bin Salamah, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Sahbani, on the authority of Kumail bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was with him. On his authority, and whomever of his companions, God willing, we passed by Abdullah bin Masoud while he was praying, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who is this?” It was said: Abdullah bin Masoud, and he said: “Indeed, Abdullah recites the Qur’an carefully as it was revealed.” Then Abdullah praised his Lord and praised Him. So he did well in praising his Lord, then he asked him, and he made the most beautiful question, and he asked him like the best question a servant of his Lord has asked, then he said: Oh God, I I ask you for a faith that will not waver, a bliss that will never fade, and the accompaniment of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the highest of the two heavens in your paradise, the paradise of eternity. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Ask and it will be given to you,” twice, so I set out to give him good tidings, and I found Abu Bakr who had preceded me. And he was the first to do good. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5386 - True"
"5387","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Warraq told us, Hamdan told us, Yahya bin Ya’la Al-Muharbi told us, Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have accepted for my nation what has been approved for it.” Ibn Umm Abd” This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And it has a defect from the hadith of Sufyan Al-Thawri, so Muhammad ibn Musa bin Imran Al-Faqih, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and as for the hadith of Israel
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5387 - Sent"
"5388","So Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Israel, all of them, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have satisfied for my nation what Ibn Umm Abd has approved for it.”"
"5389","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein informed us, al-Mu’affa ibn Sulaiman al-Harrani informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ma’in informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If I were “I would have appointed Ibn Umm Abd as my successor over them without consulting anyone.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5389 - Asim bin Damra is weak"
"5390","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever loves “Whoever reads the Qur’an fresh as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Umm Abd read.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5390 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5391","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa, Al-Adl, told me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told me, he said: Tell me My father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I was sitting with Omar when a thin man came to him, and he started looking at him and his face lit up. Then he said: “How is he filled with knowledge? How he was filled with knowledge” - meaning Abdullah bin Masoud -. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5391 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5392","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: He was told: Tell us about the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “About which of them?” He said: Tell us on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud. He said: “He taught the Qur’an and the Sunnah, then he finished and that was sufficient for him.” He mentioned the rest of the hadith as “authentic according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5392 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5393","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me: I am Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Ma’mal bin Sufyan told us, Ismail bin Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, in this verse: {And do not drive out those who call upon their Lord. In the morning and the evening they seek His face.} [Al-An'am: 52] He said: “I camped with five of the Quraysh, myself and Ibn Masoud among them, and the Quraysh said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If you expel these people from you, you will make these people nearer to us.” Then it was revealed: {And do not expel those who call upon their Lord in the morning. And the evening, they seek His face} [Al-An'am: 52] to his saying {With the thankful} [Al-An'am: 53] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5393 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5394","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf, Al-Adl, informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, I am Ja’far bin Aoun, I Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Jafar bin Amr bin Harith, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abdullah bin Masoud: “Read.” He said: He recited and it was revealed to you. He said: “I would love to hear it from someone else.” He said: So he opened Surat An-Nisa until he conveyed: {So how if we come from every nation? As a witness, and We have brought you as a witness against these.} [An-Nisa: 41] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was confused, and Abdullah stopped, and the Messenger of God said to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He spoke.” He praised God at the beginning of his speech, praised God, and sent blessings upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and bore witness to the truth. And he said: We are satisfied with God as our Lord, and with Islam as our religion, and I have accepted for you what God and His Messenger are satisfied with. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have satisfied for you what “Ibn Umm Abd is not satisfied with you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5394 - True"
"5395","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amri told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, He said: A brother was mentioning the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not mention Ibn Masoud, so I said to him: I see you do not mention Ibn Masoud. He said: “That one.” “A man over whom I have no preference.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5395 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5396","Maymoon bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi, their master, told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah, he said: “Abdullah was likened to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his guidance, guidance, and character.” Ibrahim said: “Alqamah was He is likened to Abdullah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"5397","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Amr bin Wabisa Al-Asadi, on the authority of his father, said: I was in Kufa in my home, when I heard at the door of the house, peace be upon you. He entered, and I said: And peace be upon you. He entered, and when he entered, he was Abdullah bin Masoud. I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, what time? Visit this? - That was in the afternoon - he said: The day had been long for me, so I remembered who I was talking to. He said: So he started talking to me about the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted me and I was talking to him, then he started talking to me and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be a trial, and the one who sleeps in it is better than the one who sleeps in it.” He who lies down, and he who lies down in it is better than one who sits, and he who sits in it is better than one who stands, and he who stands in it is better than one who walks, and he who walks is better than one who rides, They killed them all in the fire. I said: O Messenger of God, when is that? He said: “Those are the days of the Harj.” I said: When are the days of the Harj? He said: “When a man does not trust his companion.” I said: What do you command me to do if I reach that time? He said: “Brace yourself and your hand, and enter your house.” I said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if he enters my house? He said: “Then enter your house.” I said: What do you think if he enters my house? He said: “Then enter your mosque and do like this, or hold him on the elbow with his right hand, and say: My Lord, God, until you die in that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5397 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5398","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yusuf bin Adi told us, Jarir told us, On the authority of Mughirah bin Abi Razin, he said: It was said to Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib: Which is greater, you or the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “He is older than me, and I was born before him.”"
"5399","So Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me, in Mecca, my grandfather told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: “Al-Abbas was older than The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the age of three, came to my mother and was told: Amina had given birth to a boy, so she took me out when I woke up, holding my hand until We entered her, and it was as if I was looking at him rubbing his feet while sitting alone, and the women started talking to me and saying: Kiss your brother. He said: And Al-Abbas died. “In the year thirty-four, he is eighty-eight years old.”"
"5400","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of His sheikhs, “Al-Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib bin Hashim bin Abd Manaf was the paternal uncle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His mother was Nataila bint Khabab bin Kulayb bin Malik bin Amr bin Amer bin Zaid Manat bin Amer Al-Khazrajiya, and Al-Abbas was nicknamed Abu Al-Fadl, and Al-Fadl was He is older than his son, and Al-Abbas was three years older than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Abbas testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The conquest of Mecca, Hunayn, Taif, and Tabuk greeted him, and stayed with him on the day of Hunayn among his family while the people discovered him. Ibn Umar said: Thana Khaled bin Al-Qasim Al-Bayadhi, Shu’bah’s client Ibn Abbas told me, saying: “Al-Abbas was moderate in the channel, and he used to tell us, on the authority of Abd Al-Muttalib is that he died while he was more steadfast than him, and Al-Abbas died on a Friday of the fourteenth of Rajab in the year thirty-two. During the caliphate of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, he was eighty-eight years old, and he was buried in Al-Baqi in the Bani Hashim cemetery.”"
"5401","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Umm Al-Abbas bin Abd Al-Muttalib Natila bint Khabab bin Kulayb bin Malik bin Amr bin Amr bin Al-Nimr bin Qasit, Al-Abbas was born three years before the elephant ""Years"""
"5402","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl told me Bin Dukayn, Zuhair told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, who said: “Abbas freed seventy people upon his death. Owned"
"5403","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, from the origin of his book, Abu Imran Musa bin Harun Al-Hafiz told us, Ishaq bin Rahuwayh, and Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, and Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, They said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. He said: I am Wahb bin Jarir. He said: My father told me. He said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq say: Hussein told me. Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, a servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “I was a servant of Abbas. Ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and I had converted to Islam, and Umm al-Fadl had converted to Islam, and al-Abbas had converted to Islam, and he was concealing his Islam out of fear of his people. Abu Lahab had left Badr behind, and Al-Aas ibn Hisham was sent in his place. He had a debt from him, so he said to him: Stop this invasion from me. I leave to you what you have to do, so he did, and when the news came, and God suppressed Abu Lahab, and I was a weak man, carving these cups in a room, By God, I was sitting in the room, sculpting my cups, and with Umm al-Fadl, when the immoral person Abu Lahab was dragging his feet, I saw him. He said: At a tree. The room was with his back to my back, and the people said: This is Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith, and Abu Lahab said: Come to me, my nephew.Then Abu Sufyan came and sat with him, then people came and stood up to them, and he said: O son of my brother, how was the situation of the people? He said: Nothing, by God, if we meet them and give them our shoulders, they will kill us however they want, and take us prisoner however they want, and I swear by God as long as I blame People. He said: Why? He said: I saw white men on dull horses. No, by God, they are not fit for anything, and nothing can do for them. He said: So I raised the roof of the room. So I said: By God, those are the angels. Then Abu Lahab raised his hand and struck me in the face, and I revolted. He carried me and struck the ground with me until he puddled on me. My chest, so Umm al-Fadl stood up and stopped, and raised a pillar from the room and hit him with it, causing a disgusting grief to linger in his head, and she said: O enemy of God, you have weakened him, if you saw his master absent from him and he stood up humiliated. By God, he only lived for seven nights until God struck him. With the lens, it killed him. His two sons left him for two or three nights to bury him until it stank. Then a man from the Quraysh said to his sons: Aren’t you ashamed? Your father's house stinks? They said: We fear this ulcer. The Quraysh feared the plague as they fear the plague, so a man said: Go, I will be with you. He said: By God, they did not wash it except by throwing water on it from afar.Then they took him up and threw him at the top of Mecca against a wall, and they threw stones at him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5403 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5404","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, he said: My father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubair said: “Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, had converted to Islam and lived as a water-carrier and did not emigrate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5404 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5405","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Osama Abdullah bin Osama Al-Halabi told us, and Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed told us Bin Al-Sammak, in Baghdad, Issa bin Abdullah Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm Al-Hafiz told me, in Kufa, Musa bin Aaron, they said: Muhammad bin Imran bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila told us, Muawiyah bin Ammar Ad-Dahni told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: My maternal uncle, Djed bin Qays, carried me, and I cannot throw a stone, on the seventy, riding from among the Ansar who came to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us and his uncle Abbas was with him. He said: “O uncle, take care of your uncles for me.” So he said: “O.” Muhammad: Ask of your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish. He said: “As for what I ask of you for myself, you withhold from me the same thing from which you withhold your property and yourselves.” They said: What do we have if we do that? He said: “Paradise.” These narrations are all with one word and in the hadith of Musa bin Imran, and no one heard it except from him. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.” And the Abbasids, may God be pleased with them, in the advancement of Abbas’s Islam, did not have a more authentic hadith than this hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5405 - True"
"5406","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Omar Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Jabbar bin Omar Al-Atardi told us, Yunus bin Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Al-Hussein bin Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Abu Rafi’ told me, he said: “We were... Al-Abbas: We had entered Islam, and we were concealing our Islam. I was a servant of Abbas and I carved cups. When the Quraysh went to the Messenger of On the day of Badr, God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made us expect news, so he gave us the Khuzai guarantee of the news, and we found within ourselves strength. We were pleased with the news that came to us about the appearance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, I am sitting in the row of Zamzam carving cups. Umm al-Fadl was sitting with me, and we were pleased with the news that had come to us about the appearance of the Messenger of God, and we were informed of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when The wicked Abu Lahab came, dragging his feet. God had oppressed him, and he was ashamed of the news that had come to him, until he sat on the floor of the room and said: People: This is Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith. He came and the people gathered around him, and he said to him: Abu Lahab, come to me, my nephew. So he sat in front of him. He said: Tell me about the people. He said: Yes, by God, what are these people? If we meet the people and give them our shoulders, they can put weapons among us wherever they want. By God, despite that, as long as I blamed the people, we met white men on bright horses, and by God, nothing remained. He said: I raised the roof of the room and said: That’s it. By God, the angels. He said: Abu Lahab raised his hand and struck my face with an ugly blow. I revolted at him, and I was a weak man, so he tolerated me and hit me. He covered me with the earth and poured blessings on my chest, and he struck me. Umm al-Fadl rose to one of the pillars of the tent and took it, saying: I weakened him if he was absent. His master, and you hit him on the head with a pole, and put him in a terrible turmoil, so he started dragging his feet in humiliation, and God threw him with a spear. By God, he only stayed for seven days until he died. His three sons left him in his house, and they did not bury him until it stank. The Quraysh feared this. The lens protects itself from the plague, until a man from the Quraysh said to them: Woe to you, are you not ashamed if your father’s house stinks and you do not bury him? They said: We fear the infection of this ulcer. So he said: Go, and I will help you with it. By God, they did not wash it except tossing it with water from afar. As they approached him, then they carried him to the top of Mecca, and they leaned him against a wall, then piled stones on him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5406 - Hussein bin Abdullah bin Ubaidullah is wah"
"5407","Abu Ahmad Al-Tamimi told me, Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: Ziyad bin told us Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Husayn bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Abu Rafi’ said: “I was a servant of Al-Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib, and Islam had entered the Ahl al-Bayt, so al-Abbas converted to Islam, Umm al-Fadl converted to Islam, and she converted to Islam, and al-Abbas He feared his people and hated their discord, and he used to conceal his Islam.” Abu Ahmad did not add anything more to this chain of transmission in this text, and he said This was sent to us of the news that indicates the progress of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib’s conversion to Islam before Badr, so he converted to Islam. And listen now to the one that contradicts it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5407 - Hussein bin Abdullah Wah"
"5408","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Hammad Al-Qabbani told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Sirri, and Saleh bin Muhammad told us. Al-Razi, they said: Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, he said: Ibn Shihab said, Anas told him Ibn Malik, that some men from the Ansar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission, and they said: Give us permission and we will leave it to our sister’s son, Abbas. His ransom, and he said: “By God, you do not leave a dirham.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5408 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5409","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: When the people of Mecca came to ransom their captives, Zainab bint The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the ransom of Abu Al-Aas, and she was sent with it with a necklace that Khadija had brought to Abu Al-Aas when he built Upon her, when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw her, he was very tender towards her, and said: “If you decide to release her prisoner and respond to her... What is hers, so do.” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and they replied to him what is hers. He said: Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, I was a Muslim, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I know about your Islam, so if it is as you say, then God will reward you, so redeem yourself and your two brothers’ sons: Nawfal Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Abd Al-Muttalib, and Aqeel Ibn Abi Talib Ibn Abd Al-Muttalib, and your ally is Utbah Ibn Amr Ibn Jahdam, brother of the Banu Al-Harith bin Fihr “He said: What is that with me, O Messenger of God?” He said: “So where is the money that you and Umm al-Fadl buried? You said to her: If I get the money, then this money goes to Banu al-Fadl, and Abdullah and Qutham?” “He said: By God, O Messenger of God, I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. This is something that no one knew except me and Umm al-Fadl, so count for me.” O Messenger of God, you did not get twenty ounces of money from me that I had. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do it.” So Abbas ransomed himself. And his two nephews and his ally, and God Almighty revealed: {O Prophet, say to those of the prisoners in your hands that God knows what is good in your hearts. He will give you better than what has been taken from you, and forgive you; and God is Forgiving, Merciful.} [Al-Anfal: 70] So he gave me the place of the twenty uqiyah in Islam. Twenty servants, each of them had money in his hand to use, along with what I hope for forgiveness from God Almighty. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5409 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5410","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abdullah bin Amr bin Abi Umayyah told us, Ibn Abi Umayyah told us Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to venerate Al-Abbas as a son “And his father in particular, God singled out Al-Abbas for it from among the people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5410 - True"
"5411","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, I Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Al-Abbas is from me and I am from him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5411 - True"
"5412","Abu Qutaibah Salim bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami informed me, in Mecca, Musa bin Harun told us, Abdul-Quddus bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Kabir told us. Bin Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, Al-Hasan bin Anbasa Al-Warraq told us, Ali bin Hashim bin Al-Barid told me, Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi told me Rafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Rafi’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Abu, you are favored by God.” Until you are satisfied” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5412 - True"
"5413","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Ubayd Allah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, On the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, said: One day I was in the mosque, and Abu Jahl came and said: God has mercy on me if I see Muhammad prostrating. That he stepped on his neck, “So I went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until I entered upon him and informed him of what Abu Jahl had said, so he left.” He was angry until he came to the mosque. Then he hurried on before entering the door and storming through the wall. I said: This is an evil day. So I took precautions, then I followed him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and was reciting: Recite in the name of your Lord who created. He created man from a clot of clots. When he reached the matter of Abu Jahl, he said: {No. Indeed, man is transgressed if he sees that he has become wealthy} [Al-Alq: 7]. A man said to Abu Jahl: O Abu Al-Hakam, this is Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. Abu Jahl said: Don’t you see what I see? By God, He has blocked the horizon of the sky for me. “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached the end of the surah “He prostrated.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5413 - It contains Abdullah bin Saleh, but not Umdah, and Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, but he is abandoned."
"5414","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us in others, they said: Abdullah told us Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, Yahya Ibn Ma’in told me, Ubaid Ibn Abi Qurra told me, Al-Layth Ibn Sa’d told me, on the authority of Abi Qabil, on the authority of Abi Maysarah, Mawla Al-Abbas, said: I heard Al-Abbas, may God be pleased with him, say: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and he said to me: “Look into The sky.” I looked, and he said: “Do you see anything in the sky?” I said: Yes, he said: “What do you see?” I said: Al-Thuraya, and he said: “But he will rule this nation according to the number of your descendants.” This is a hadith that was unique to Ubaid bin Abi Qurrah, on the authority of Al-Layth. And our imam, Abu Zakaria, may God have mercy on him, if he had not pleased him, he would not have narrated a hadith like this on his behalf.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5414 - This is not correct"
"5415","Ali bin Hamshah Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamzah Al-Zubairi told us, Ismail bin Qays bin Saad bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out at a time when The heat descended, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up to wash himself. Then Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib stood up and covered him with a garment of wool. He said: Easy: I looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the side of the cloak, and he was raising his head to the sky and saying: “O God, protect me.” “Al-Abbas and his son from the Fire” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5415 - Ismail bin Qais bin Saad is weak"
"5416","Mukarram ibn Ahmad al-Qadi told me, in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham told me, Ismail ibn Abi Uwais told me, Muhammad ibn Talha, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Haritha bin Al-Numan told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Haritha, he said: When Safwan bin Khalaf bin Umayyah Al-Jumahi came and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Abu Wahb, upon whom did you descend?” He said: On Al-Abbas. He said: “I descended upon the Quraysh who loved the Quraysh the most.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5416 - True"
"5417","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Khazzaz told us, Abu Zuhar bin Husayn’s uncle, on the authority of his grandfather Humaid bin Munhab, who said: I heard my grandfather Khurraym bin Aws bin Haritha bin Lam, may God be pleased with him. He says: I migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his departure from Tabuk, so I converted to Islam, and I heard Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib say: Oh Messenger of God, I want to praise you, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say, ‘May God not open your mouth.’” He said: Then Al-Abbas said:
 [The Laying Sea]
 Before her, I slept in the shadows and in... a warehouse where the paper is scattered.
 Then the country fell, there was no human being... you, no moth, no leech.
 Rather, it is a sperm that rides on a ship and has... bridled an eagle and caused its occupancy to sink.
 It is transferred from crucifixion to uterus... If a world passes, a plate appears
 Until your dominant house contained... Alia's penthouse with the pronunciation underneath it.
 And when you were born, the earth shone... and your light illuminated the horizon.
 We are in that light and in... the light and the paths of guidance we penetrate.”
 This is a hadith whose narrators were unique to the Bedouins from their fathers, and narrators like them are not fabricated.”"
"5418","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, Yunus told me, about Al-Zuhri, Kathir ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me. Al-Abbas said: I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Hunayn, so I and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib joined the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we did not separate from him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Upon him, he greeted a white mule of his that Farwa bin Naama al-Jadami had given him as a gift. When the Muslims and the infidels met, the Muslims turned away. They retreated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began running with his mule ahead of the infidels. Al-Abbas said: I am holding the reins of the mule of the Messenger of God. She, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, kept her hands, wanting not to rush, while Abu Sufyan was taking the passengers of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “That is, Abbas, call, O companions of Al-Samura.” So I called them and he said: By God, it is as if I had compassion for them when they heard my compassionate voice. The cows on their calves, so they said: Oh, here you are! Oh here you are! He said: So fight them and the infidels, and the call to the Ansar is saying: O people! The Ansar, O people of Ansar. Then the invitation was restricted to the Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, and they said: O the Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, oh the Ansar. Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked at their fight as he was riding his mule like one who was being attacked, and the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “This is when the battle became heated.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took pebbles and threw them in the faces of the infidels. Then he said: “They have been defeated, by the Lord of Muhammad.” So I went to look, and lo and behold, the fighting was as it was in what I saw. By God, it was nothing but the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his pebbles, and I still see them standing at night and looking after them. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5418 - Narrated by Muslim"
"5419","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad bin Talha told us Al-Taymi, Abu Suhail bin Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is Al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet. He was the best of the Quraysh and was kind to them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"5420","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Daoud Al-Zahid told us, saying: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Ahmed told us Ibn Salih Al-Masry, Muhammad Ibn Talha Al-Taymi told us, Abu Suhail Ibn Malik told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas May God be pleased with him. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out preparing an army. He looked at Al-Abbas and said: “This is Al-Abbas, the uncle of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “I will give the best hand from the Quraysh and deliver it to her.”"
"5421","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa. He said: Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Israel. On the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man mentioned Abu al-Abbas, so he approached him and slapped him. Al-Abbas, so they gathered together and said: By God, we will strike Al-Abbas just as he struck him. This was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he delivered a speech and said: “Who? The most honorable people in the eyes of God? They said: You, O Messenger of God. He said: “Al-Abbas is from me, and I am from him. Do not curse our dead or harm the living thereby.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5421 - True"
"5422","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, On the authority of Uqba bin Abdul Ghafir, he said: Abdullah bin Abbas entered upon Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, and the bellies of the Quraysh were warmed by him. So Muawiyah asked him about their fathers until he said: What do you say about your father, Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib? He said: “May God have mercy on Abu Al-Fadl. He was, by God, the uncle of the Prophet of God, and the apple of the eye of the Messenger of God, the master of uncles and brothers-in-law, the grandfather of the grandfathers. His fathers were the best, and his grandfathers were the best. He had knowledge of matters. He was beautified by a dream, and he was endowed with understanding. He used to earn his way every day. Muhannad, and every dissenter wins his opinion, the furrows faded when his virtue was mentioned, and the lineages diverged when he mentioned His clan, the owner of the house, the waterer, his lineage and kinship, and why wouldn’t that be the case? How could this not be so? “The one who orchestrated his policy was the most generous of those who managed, and the most understanding of those who emerged from the Quraysh and rode.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5422 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5423","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Musa bin Sahl bin Kathir told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Bahrain with eighty thousand, but no money came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more money than that before, nor After that, he ordered it to be spread out on a mat, and prayer was called. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, leaning over the money, standing, and the people came. And he began to give them, and at that time there was no number or weight, and it was only a quantity, so Al-Abbas came and said: O Messenger of God, I have given my ransom. And the ransom of Aqeel on the day of Badr, and Aqeel had no money, “Give me some of this money.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take it.” So he urged Khamisah. It was on him, then he went to leave, but he was not able to, so he raised his head to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, raise Ali, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and said: “As for one of the things that God promised, He has fulfilled for me, and I do not know the other. Tell those in Your hands are among the captives. If God knew what was good in your hearts, He would give you better than what was taken from you and forgive you. This is better than what was taken from me, and I do not know. What is done with forgiveness?” Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Harith told us. Al-Ahwazi, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, that Al-Ala Ibn Al-Hadrami sent money from Bahrain to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned the hadith along the lines of: “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5423 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5424","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: Musa bin Dawood Al-Dhabi told us, Al-Hakim bin Al-Mundhir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr al-Khathami, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali bin al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, who said: Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was wearing a robe, and had two braids, and he was white. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him, he smiled and said: Al-Abbas: O Messenger of God, what made you laugh? May God make your age laugh? He said: “I liked the beauty of the Prophet’s uncle.” Al-Abbas said: What is beauty in men? He said: “The tongue.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5424 - Sent"
"5425","Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Shuaib bin Amr told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Al-Abbas was in Medina, and the Ansar asked for a garment to wear, but they did not find a shirt that would fit him except The shirt of Abdullah bin Ubayy and they clothed him with it. Jabir said: Al-Abbas was a prisoner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr, but he was only taken out Forcedly, he was carried to Medina, and Abdullah bin Abi clothed him with his shirt. Therefore, “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shrouded him in his shirt as a reward.” “For what he did to Al-Abbas” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5425 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5426","So Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd. God said: “When Al-Abbas was captured, there was no shirt for him that could cover him except the shirt of Ibn Ubayy.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"5427","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Abu Ishaq Muhammad bin Harun bin Isa Al-Hashimi told us, Musa bin Abdullah bin Musa Al-Hashimi, Ya’qub bin Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard my father saying: I entered upon Abu Ja’far Al-Mansur and saw him. A pile, so I started looking at its beauty. He said: My father Muhammad bin Ali had a pile, and he told me that his father, Ali bin Abdullah, had it. Jummah, and he told me that his father Abdullah bin Al-Abbas had a Jummah, and Al-Abbas had a Jummah, and he told me “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He had a crown, and Hashim bin Abd Manaf had a crown.” So I said to my father: I am amazed at its beauty, and he said: “That is the light of the caliphate.” He said: My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: “When God wanted to create a creation for the Caliphate, He wiped His hand on its forelock, so it would not fall on it.” “The narrators of this hadith are from the last of them, all of them are Hashemites known for their honorable origin.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5427 - Its narrators are Hashemites who are not reliable"
"5428","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Ibrahim told us Al-Iskandarani, in Egypt, Abu Yahya Al-Dareer told us Zaid bin Al-Hasan Al-Basri, Abdul Rahman bin Zaid bin Aslam told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, that he said to Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, may God be pleased with them both: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “We will add more to the mosque,” and your house is close to the mosque, so give it to us and we will add more to it in the mosque, and allocate for you a plot wider than it. He said: No. Shall I do? He said: Then I will force you to do so. He said: That is not yours, so put between you and me someone who will judge with the truth. He said: And who is he? He said: Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman. He said: So they came to Hudhayfah and told him the story. Hudhayfah said: I have news about this. He said: What is that? He said: David the Prophet, may God’s prayers be upon him, wanted to add to the Holy House, and there was a house near the mosque for an orphan, so he asked for it. He refused, so David wanted to take it from him, so God Almighty inspired him to protect the houses from injustice to my house. He said: So he left it. Al-Abbas said to him: So there is something left? He said: No. He said: So he entered the mosque, and behold, there was a gutter belonging to Al-Abbas in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him so that the rainwater would flow from it into the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Omar raised his hand and took out the gutter, and said: This gutter does not It was flowing into the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Abbas, and the one who sent Muhammad, told him the truth, he is the one who put the gutter in this The place, and you took it away, O Omar, and Omar said: Put your feet on my neck to bring it back to the way it was. So Al-Abbas did that, then he said: Al-Abbas I have given you the house, so you can increase it in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Omar increased it in the mosque, then he allocated Abbas a house wider than it. With Al-Zawra’ “This is a hadith that we wrote down, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, and Abu Ali was the memorizer of it, and he did not write it down except with this chain of transmission and the two sheikhs, may God bless him and grant him peace By God, they did not use Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid bin Aslam as evidence, and I found evidence for him from the hadith of the people of the Levant."
"5429","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi, may God have mercy on him, told us: Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abu Amira Issa bin Muhammad bin Al-Nahhas told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Shuaib Al-Khurasani told us, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Khurasani, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him When he wanted to add more to the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a dispute arose over the house of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, so he mentioned the hadith. In a similar way"
"5430","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa Ibn Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Razin, on the authority of Abi Razin, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said to Abbas: Ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He asked him, and he said: “I would not use you to wash away people’s sins.”
 With his chain of transmission on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said to Al-Abbas: Ask the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for us about veiling, and he said: “I will give you what it is.” “Better for you than to give water to you to comfort her, but not to comfort her.” Both hadiths have an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5430 - True"
"5431","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Ismail bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Hajjayyah Ibn Adiy, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul-Muttalib asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him And peace be upon him, about hastening his charity before it was due, “He granted him permission for that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5431 - True"
"5432","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Ismail bin Qutaibah, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, they said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Rabi’ah, he said: Al-Abbas came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was angry, and he said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: O Messenger of God, what do we have to do with the Quraysh? He said: “What do you have to do with them?” He said: They meet each other with bright faces, but when they meet us, they meet us otherwise. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry until A vein formed between his eyes, and when it cleared, he said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, faith does not enter the heart of a man until he judges for the sake of God.” And to His Messenger,” he said: Then he said: “What is the matter with men who harm me regarding Al-Abbas, the man’s uncle, similar to his father?” This hadith was narrated by Ismail bin Abi Khaled. On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad and Yazid, “And if they did not narrate it, then it is one of the pillars of the hadith among the Kufans.”"
"5433","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak Al-Zahid told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Yahya bin Saeed, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, when the Quraysh meet each other, they meet them with good news, and when they meet us, they meet us with faces we do not know. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became very angry and said: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the heart of a man of faith will not enter until He loves you for the sake of God and for His Messenger.” I have mentioned about the virtues of Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, may God be pleased with them, as part of the virtues of the family of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. peace be upon him, and I explained the reasons for this hadith by mentioning Al-Muttalib ibn Rabi’ah and those who omitted it from the chain of transmission, so that made no need to repeat it in the hadith. this place"""
"5434","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that he said: “To Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib: ‘The best of this nation and the heir of the Prophet and his uncle.’”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5434 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5435","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Ias told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard the narration of Abu Salih. He said: Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib sent me to Othman, may God be pleased with them both. So I went to him, and behold, he was feeding the people lunch, so I called him and he came and said: “The most beautiful of faces, O Abul-Fadl.” He said: “And your face, O Amir.” The believers, and he said: “I did not do anything more than that your messenger came to me while I was having lunch, so I fed them, then I came.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5435 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5436","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Amr bin Thabit said: A man entered Al-Hussein bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, while he was eating, and he said: “Come and eat.” He said: I have eaten. He said: “With whom?” He said: According to Ibn Abbas, he said: “As for his father, he was the master of Quraysh.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5436 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5437","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Aziz told us, Salama bin Rawh told me, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Abdullah bin Tha’labah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has advised me to do this.” Relatives, and he ordered me to start with Al-Abbas.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5437 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5438","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, Sa’ida bin told me Ubayd Allah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Dawud ibn Ata’ Al-Madani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: Umar ibn Al-Khattab drew water in the year The ashes were given to Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, and he said: “Oh God, this is the uncle of your Prophet Al-Abbas. We turn to You with him, so give us water.” They continued until he gave them water to drink. God, he said: Then Omar addressed the people, and said: “O people, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to see for Abbas what a child sees for his father. He glorifies him, honors him, and honors his oath. So, O people, follow the example of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his uncle Abbas, and take him as a means to God. Glory be to Him in what has been revealed to you.”"
"5439","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Muzani told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Al-Arqam Ibn Abd Yaghouth bin Uhayb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra, his mother: Amra bint Al-Arqam bin Hashim bin Abd Manaf, who was blind. Before his death, he died in the year thirty-five.”"
"5440","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, and he mentioned the lineage of Abdullah bin Al-Arqam. He said: “He was a scribe for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them.”"
"5441","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Bayhaqi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salama told us Al-Majjishun, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Abi Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A man wrote, and he said to Abdullah bin Al-Arqam: “Answer on my behalf.” He wrote his answer, then read it to him, and said: “You are correct.” And you have done well, O God, grant him success.” When Omar’s guardian was consulting with him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5441 - True"
"5442","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Al-Arqam bin Abd Yaghouth was in charge of the treasury during the time of Umar and was a leader during the rule of Uthman until his death, and he had many companions.”"
"5443","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana'ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ayoub ibn Musa, On the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If The prayer has been established, and one of you takes the excrement, so let him begin with the excrement.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"5444","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “On naming someone He witnessed Badr and Aqaba, from Banu Jashm bin Al-Harith and Zayd bin Al-Harith, and they are the twins Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abd Rabbuh bin Tha`labah, and he was the one who was shown the call to prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him and ordered him to do so.”"
"5445","Abdullah bin Hatim told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told me, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Zaid is the one who made the call. He is called ""Abu Muhammad"""
"5446","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubayy told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa “among those who witnessed Badr, and Al-Aqaba are from Banu Jashm bin Al-Harith and Zayd bin Al-Harith, and they are the twins Abdullah bin Zaid bin Abdul His Lord is Ibn Tha'labah Ibn Zayd Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Al-Khazraj, and his brother Harith Ibn Zayd, and Abdullah Ibn Zayd is the one who was shown the call. “By prayer”"
"5447","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Zaid bin Abdul Rabbo bin Tha’labah bin Zaid bin Al-Harith, and his nickname was Abu Muhammad, and Abdullah bin Zaid witnessed in The seventy of the Ansar on the night of Aqaba according to the narration of all of them, and he witnessed Badr, Uhud, the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He had with him the banner of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj in the Battle of Conquest, and he was the one who was shown the call to prayer that was discussed by jurists. “Islam with acceptance” and it was not included in the two Sahih books due to the differences between the transmitters regarding its chains of transmission. “The best narration concerning it is the narration of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he Some of our imams imagined that Sa`id had not joined Abdullah bin Zaid, but this is not the case, for Sa`id bin al-Musayyab was among those who entered between Ali and Othman was in the mediation, but Abdullah bin Zaid died at the end of the caliphate of Othman.” The hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, is well-known. It was narrated by Yunus bin Yazid, Muammar bin Rashid, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, Muhammad bin Ishaq and others. As for the narrations of the Kufans in This chapter is based on the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila. Some of them said: On the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal or Abdullah ibn Zayd. Among them are those who said: Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, and as for the descendants of Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of their fathers, on the authority of him, it is not straight. The chains of narration. Abdullah bin Zaid narrated this hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5448","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Bishr bin Musa narrated to us, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, and Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abdul Rabbo, who was shown The call is that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, this gift of mine is charity and it belongs to God and His Messenger, so his parents came They said: O Messenger of God, he was our livelihood. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned him to them. Then they died and their son inherited them after that.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5448 - There is a transmission"
"5449","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: And Abu Al-Darda’ Uwaimir bin Zaid bin Qays bin Khanasa bin Umayyah bin Malik bin Amir bin Adi bin Kaab bin Al-Khazraj bin Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj It was said: The name: Abu Al-Darda’ is Amer, but it was shortened, so it was said: Uwaimir, and his mother: Mahabba bint Waqid bin Amr bin Al-Aznabah bin Aamir bin Zayd Manat ibn Malik ibn Tha’labah ibn Ka’b, and Abu al-Darda’ was, as mentioned, the last person whose home was Islam, and he was still attached to an idol of his. He put a handkerchief on him, and Abdullah bin Rawaha was inviting him to Islam, but he refused, so Abdullah bin Rawaha came to him. He had a brother during the pre-Islamic period before Islam, and when he saw him leaving his house, he disagreed with him, so he entered his house and brought his wife to her house while she was combing the hair. He nodded and said: Where is Abu Darda? She said: Your brother just went out and entered his house, where the idol was, and he had the cross, so he took it down and began to revere it slowly, while he was secretly trembling from the sound of it. All the names of the devils, except that everything that is called with God is false. Then he went out, and his wife heard the sound of the one coming as he struck that idol. She said: You have destroyed me, O Ibn Rawaha. So he went out on that and nothing happened until Abu Darda came to his house and entered and found The woman was sitting crying out of pity for him, so he said: What is the matter with you? She said: Your brother Abdullah bin Rawaha entered upon me and did what you see, so he became angry. He became very angry, then he thought to himself and said: If there was any good for this man, he would have defended himself, so he set off until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and Ibn Rawaha was with him, so he converted to Islam. It was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at Abu Darda and the people were utterly defeated. On the day of Uhud, he said: “What a fine knight Uwaimir,” but he meant “unquotable.” Ibn Umar said: I heard someone mentioning that Abu al-Darda’ did not testify. Uhud, and he was among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he witnessed many scenes with him. Ibn Umar said: Abu Umar died. Al-Darda' in Damascus in the year thirty-two during the caliphate of Uthman ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5449 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5450","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, Muhammad ibn Bishr told us, Matar told us, Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjumani told us, he said: I saw an old man in Damascus who was called To him: Abu Ishaq Al-Ajrab, a client of Banu Habbar Al-Qurashi. He said: “I saw Abu Al-Darda’ Uwaimir bin Qais bin Khanasa, the companion of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was pale, short-haired, and dyed his hair yellow. I saw on him a small, scarred skullcap, and I saw on him a turban that he had thrown over his head. His shoulders.” Al-Abbas said: I heard a man who was with me say to him: How long have you seen him? He said: I saw him more than a hundred years ago. He said: And he was wearing socks and sandals. He said: “Someone came to my father Ishaq. One hundred and twenty years.”"
"5451","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Abu Dharr Jundub ibn Junada, and it was said that Yazid ibn Junada, died in Al-Rabadha in the year thirty-two, and they disagreed about who prayed over him, so it was said: Abdullah bin Masoud, and it was said: Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli.”"
"5452","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi informed us, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us Zaida, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, Mujahid narrated to us, he said: Abu Dharr said to a group of people with him: “Indeed, what you see of people has attended me. Death, and if I had a garment sufficient to shroud me or my companion, I would not be shrouded except for that, and I implore you not to let a man among you shroud me. A corporal, or a captain, or a prince, or a post.” And the people were nobles. Hajr al-Madri, and Malik al-Ashtar, was among a group of them a man from The Ansar, and all the people came to a house, except for the Ansari, and he said: I will shroud you in this garment of mine and in two garments on my waistcoat. My mother knitted them for me so that I could enter ihram for them, so Abu Dharr said: “It is enough for me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5452 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5453","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told me, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin Al-Muthanna, he said: “Abu Dhar al-Ghifari Jundub bin Junada bin Sufyan bin Ubaid bin Haram,” Ibn Salam said: “And his name is said: Yazid.”"
"5454","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Abu Dharr Jundub bin Junada bin Qais bin Amr bin Su’air bin Haram bin Ghaffar, and his mother: Ramla bint Waqi’ah bin Ghaffar, and as for what was mentioned of His name: Yazid, as it was narrated that “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him by that.”"
"5455","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Dharr: “How are you, Yazid?” in a hadith Long"
"5456","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Asim and Saad bin Amir told us, they said: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed Al-Qaseer, Abu Jamrah told me, he said: Ibn Abbas said to us: Shall I not inform you of Abu Dharr’s conversion to Islam? He said: We said: Yes, he said: Abu Dharr said: I was a man from Ghifar, and we were informed that a man had gone out in Mecca claiming to be a prophet, so I said to my brother: Go to this man and speak to him and bring me his news. So he went and met him, then came back, and I said: What do you have? He said: By God, I saw a man who enjoined good and forbade evil. He said: So I said to him: He did not cure me of the news. He said: So I took a sock. Then I went to Mecca, and I did not know him, and I hated to be asked about him, and I drank from Zamzam water while I was in the mosque. He said: Then Ali passed by me and said: It was as if the man was a stranger. I said: Yes. He said: So he went to the house, and I went with him. He did not ask me about anything, nor I told him. He said: Then when I got up in the morning, I went to the mosque to ask about him, and no one was telling me anything about him, so Ali passed by me and said: As for Does a man still know his home? He said: I said: No. He said: Go with me. He said: What brought you to this town? I said to him: If you keep secret from me, will I tell you? He said: I will do so.I said to him: We have heard that a man has left here claiming to be a prophet, so I sent my brother to speak to him, but he returned and did not recover from the news. So I wanted to meet him. He said: If you are guided, this is my face, so follow me and enter where I enter, for if I see anyone I fear for you. I went to the wall to fix my sandals and you go. He said: So he went and I went with him until he came in, and I went with him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Oh Messenger of God, offer me Islam. He offered me Islam, so I converted to Islam in my place. He said: Then he said to me: “O Abu Dharr, conceal this matter. And return to your country, and when our appearance reaches you, come.” He said: So I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will shout it before them. So he came to the mosque and Quraysh were in it, and said: O people of Quraysh, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. So they said: Go to this Sabi, so they got up and I was struck to death, then Al-Abbas overtook me, so he fell on me, then he turned to them and said: Woe to you. You are killing a man from the Banu Ghifar, and your store and passage are on Ghifar, so leave me, so when the next morning I came back, I said as I said. Yesterday, they said: Go to this Sabi, so Al-Abbas caught up with me, so he leaned on me and said: Like what he said yesterday.The first conversion to Islam of Abu Dharr was: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” As for a hadith explained in Abu Dharr’s conversion to Islam, a hadith “Levantine”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5456 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5457","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ahmed bin Ibrahim al-Qurashi told us, in Damascus Muhammad bin Aid al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, Abu Tarfa Abbad bin Al-Rayyan Al-Lakhmi told me, he said: I heard Urwa bin Ruwaym Al-Lakhmi Al-Ash’ari saying: Amer bin Ludin Al-Ash’ari told me, and he was with Abd al-Malik bin Marwan. He said: I heard Abu Laila Al-Ash’ari say: Abu Al-Ash’ari told me: Dharr said: The first thing that called me to Islam was that we were a strange people, and the Sunnah struck us, so I carried my mother and my brother, and his name was Anis, to Our in-laws are the best in Najd. When we settled with them, they honored us. When a man from the neighborhood saw that, he walked to my uncle and said: You know that Anis He opposes you to your family. He said: Then his heart sank, so I left in the parish of Iblī, and I found him sad, sad, and crying.So I said: What made you cry, uncle? So he informed me of the news, and I said: May God withhold from that, for we fear indecency, even though time has disturbed us, and some evil has troubled us. We started with him, and there was no way to meet, so I endured with my mother and my brother until we landed in the presence of Mecca, and my brother said: I am a man who defends the water. With poetry, and he was a poetic man, so I said: Do not do it, so the confusion came out with it until Jurayj ibn al-Sammah pushed him to his ram, and God bless Jurayj On that day, I felt better than my brother, so they argued to Khaba, and she preferred my brother over Jurayj, and that was because Jurayj proposed to her to her father, and she said: An old man. I had no need for him, so I envied him, so we added his grove to our own, and we had an attack. He said: Then I came to Mecca and started with Safa. Then, behold, the men of Quraysh were upon it, and I have heard that there was a Sabian or an insane person there.Or a poet, or a magician, so I said: Where is this that you claim? They said: Here he is, where you can see, so I turned to him, and by God, I would not have escaped from them even an inch until they poured every bone, stone, and stone on me. So they covered me with my blood, and I came to the House and entered between the curtains and the building and fasted there for thirty days, neither eating nor drinking except from Zamzam water, until it was On a moonlit night, two women from Khuza’ah came and circumambulated the Kaaba, then they mentioned Isaf and Na’ila, and they were two. They worshiped them, so I put my head out from under the curtain and said: Hold one of them against its owner. They got angry and then said: By God, if only Our men were present while I spoke of this, then they left, and I went out following their tracks until they met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What? You,Where are you from? Where did you come from? What brings you here? So they told him the news, and he said: “Where did you leave the Sabian?” They said: We left him between the curtains and the building, and he said to them: “Did he say anything to you?” They said: Yes, and I continued until I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then I greeted him at that time, and he said: “Who are you?” And who are you from? Where are you from? Where did you come from? What brings you? So I set out to tell him the news, and he said: “Where have you been eating and drinking?” So I said: From Zamzam water, and he said: “But it is delicious food.” And with him was Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he said: O Messenger of God, permit me to I would give him dinner. He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out walking, and Abu Bakr took my hand until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stopped. At Abu Bakr’s door, then Abu Bakr entered his house.Then he brought some raisins from the Taif raisins, and he started throwing them to us, one by one, and we ate from them until we were filled with them, so the Messenger of God said to me: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O Abu Dharr,” so I said: “At your service.” He said to me: “Indeed, a piece of land has been allocated to me, and it has wealth, and I do not consider it to be Tihama, so go out to your people and invite them to what you have entered into.” He said: So I went out until I came to my mother and brother and informed them of the news, and they said: We have no desire for the religion into which you entered. So they embraced Islam, then we left until we came to Medina. I informed my people and they said: We have believed you. Perhaps we will meet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us, we met him. Ghafar said to him: O Messenger of God, indeed... Abu Dhar taught us what you taught him,We have submitted and bear witness that you are the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Aslam and Khuza’ah came forward and said: O Messenger of God, we have We submitted to Islam, and entered into what our brothers and allies entered into. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I submit to Islam, may God make her safe, and forgive, forgive.” May God reward her.” Then Abu Bakr took my hand and said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service, O Abu Bakr. He said: Have you been deifying him in Your ignorance? I said: Yes, you saw me standing in the sun, and I would continue praying until its heat hurt me. Then I fell back as if I was invisible, so he said to me: Where were you heading? I said: I do not know except where God directed me until God brought Islam to me.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5457 - Its chain of transmission is valid"
"5458","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Lakhmi told us, Bishr told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Sadaqa bin Abd told us. By God, on the authority of Nasr ibn Alqamah, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ibn Aidh, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: Abu Dharr used to say: “You saw me a quarter “Islam, no one converted to Islam before me except the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Bilal.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5458 - True"
"5459","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abdullah bin Al-Rumi told us, Al-Nadr bin Muhammad told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zumil Samak bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Malik bin Marthad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: “I was a quarter Three people converted to Islam before me, and I was the fourth. I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. I bear witness that no There is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. I saw joy in the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5459 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5460","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, Al-Nadr told us Ibn Muhammad, Ikrimah Ibn Ammar told us, Abu Zumail told us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Marthad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “The fool is not less, nor is the green shade, the one with a more sincere dialect, nor more loyal than Abu Dharr, similar to Jesus, son of Mary.” Then Omar stood up. Ibn Al-Khattab said: O Messenger of God, so we know that for him. He said: “Yes, so inform him about it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not “They narrate it.” It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr and Abu Darda
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5460 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5461","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hamani told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and he told me Abu Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi, Abu Qalaba told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-A’mash, on the authority of Othman bin Qais Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Harb Al-Dili, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The green shade does not remain. I am not the least bit ashamed of a man who has a more sincere dialect than Abu Dharr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5461 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5462","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Bilal Ibn Abi al-Darda’, on the authority of Abi al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The green trees have not remained dark, nor have they diminished.” “A fool is the one who has a more truthful dialect than Abu Dharr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5462 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5463","The narration has been authenticated in some aspects, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “The hardest of people The affliction of the prophets, then the scholars, then the example, and the example.”"
"5464","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf, the jurist, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad, the ascetic reader, told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ narrated to us, Rabi’ah bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Dharr Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Dharr, how are you if you are in scum?” He interlaced his fingers. I said: O Messenger of God, what do you command me to do? He said: “Be patient, be patient, be patient. Treat people according to their morals, and differ from them in their deeds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5464 - Ibn Yazid did not bring him out"
"5465","Abu Al-Hussein Abdul-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram, the son of my brother Al-Hasan bin Mukarram Al-Bazzar, informed us in Baghdad: I am Abdul-Warith bin Ibrahim Al-Askari, Saif bin Miskin Al-Asawari told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Muntasir bin Amara bin Abi Dhar Al-Ghafari, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “As the time approaches, the wearing of tylas will increase, and trade will increase. And the wealth increased, and the owner of wealth increased his wealth, and immorality increased, and boys ruled, and women increased, and the Sultan became a neighbor, and he floated in Measure and balance, and a man raising a dog puppy is better for him than raising a child of his own. The elder is not respected, and the young is not shown mercy, and he is plentiful. Children of fornication, to the point that a man would cheat on a woman on the side of the road, and the likes of them at that time would say: If you both kept away from the way, And they wear sheep skins over the hearts of wolves. Their example in that time was the flatterer. “This is a hadith that was narrated alone by Saif bin Miskin, on the authority of Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah and Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah are trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5465 - Saif bin Miskin Al-Asawari is weak"
"5466","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist, told us, Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Al-Haytham bin Jamil Al-Antaki told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Majjal, on the authority of Sadaqa bin Abi Imran bin Hattan, who said: I came to Abu Dharr and found him in the mosque hiding in a black cloak alone. So I said: O Abu Dharr, what is this unit? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Alone is better than a bad companion, and a good companion is better than loneliness.” Good is better than silence, and silence is better than the dictates of evil.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5466 - It is not valid"
"5467","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hamani told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr bin Attiya, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, who said: I was with Abu al-Darda’ and a man from the city came and asked him, So he told him that Abu Dharr was going to Al-Rabdah, so Abu Darda said: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return, if only Abu Dharr cut off a limb for me. Or I somehow hybridized it after I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The greenness is not more shaded, nor is the dust lessened, than a man with a more sincere tone.” From Abu Dharr
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5467 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"5468","Abu Dharr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba bin Al-Raqqashi told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Abu Amir told us and he is righteous. Ibn Rustum Al-Khazzaz, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Samit, who said: Umm Dharr said: By God, Uthman did not lead Abu Dharr. But the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the building reaches a level, get out of it.” Abu Dharr said: When the building reaches a level. He went on to go beyond Abu Dharr’s departure to the Levant and mentioned the rest of the hadith in its length: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” The hadith explained in this chapter is the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Haram ibn Jandal Al-Ghafari. I left it out due to the wording in it and its length. Also, I limited myself to the two authentic chains of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5468 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5469","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Abu Dharr died in Al-Rabdha in the year two Thirty, and Abdullah bin Masoud prayed for him, and Abdullah bin Masoud also died, and Abdullah bin Masoud’s prayers for him are not far away.” It was narrated with another chain of transmission that he was among the group of the people of Kufa who stood to pray for him."
"5470","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibrahim bin al-Ashtar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Dhar She said: When I heard Abu Dharr’s death, I cried, and he said to me: What makes you cry? So I said: Why should I not cry when you die in a desert on the ground, and I do not have a garment that can cover you for me, nor for you, and it is necessary for your bier? He said: So give good news, and do not cry, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No two or three children will die between two Muslim women.” So they will think and see the Fire forever.” And I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying to a group of people I am among: “Let a man among you die of want. From the earth a group of believers will witness it. And there is not one of that group who did not die in a village or a group. So I am that man, by God. I did not lie, nor did I lie so that I could see the road. So I said: How is it? The Hajj has gone, and the road was cut off. He said: Go and see the road. He said: So I was trying hard. To the dune, then I come back and nurse him. While he and I were like that, I found men in their condition as if they were marble. You found them. Their mounts, - Ali said: I said to Yahya bin Sulaym: They run or hide, he said: With the dal -, She said: So I waved my dress, so they hastened to me until They came to me and said: Who is he? I said: Abu Dhar. They said: The companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, so they ransomed him with their fathers and mothers, and hastened to him until they entered upon him, and he said to them: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said to a group of people, including me: “If a man among you dies in a desert on earth, a group of believers will witness it.” He is not one of those. A group of people is a man unless he perishes in a village or a group. By God, I have never lied nor have I lied. You hear that if I had a garment that would be enough for me I was not shrouded except in a garment for me or for her. I adjure you by God, then I adjure you by God, lest a man should shroud me. Among you was a prince, or a corporal, or a post, or a captain, and not one of those people did not go away. What he said was a young man from the Ansar, so he said: I I will shroud you, uncle, I will shroud you in this robe of mine, and in two garments on my handkerchief from my mother’s yarn. He said: You, so shroud me. So the Ansari shrouded him in the group. Those who attended him, rose over him, and buried him in a group, all of them Yemeni.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5470 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5471","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me. He said: “Habib bin Maslamah bin Malik al-Akbar bin Wahb bin Tha’labah bin Wa’ila bin Amr bin Shayban bin Muharib bin Fahr He was honorable and had heard from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was called: “the beloved of the Romans because of his frequent visits to them.” He said: And Shurayh ibn Al-Harith:
 [Long Sea]
 Except for everyone who claims to be a beloved, even if it seems... his chivalry will sacrifice the beloved of Banu Fihr.
 Hammam leads the horses until it is as if... he is treading on the gravel of the coal-steeler.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5471 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5472","Sheikh Abu Bakr Al-Imam told us, I am Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, we told us Abu Bakr Al-Ghassani, on the authority of Atiya bin Qays and Rashid bin Saad, who said: The Romans marched to Habib bin Maslamah, who was in Armenia, “ So he wrote to Muawiyah requesting him, so Muawiyah wrote to Uthman about that, so Uthman wrote to the Emir of Iraq, ordering him to provide a friend. So he supplied him with the people of Iraq, and he appointed Salman bin Rabi’ah Al-Bahili over them. They set off seeking the relief of Habib, but they did not reach them until he met him. And his companions were the enemy, so God granted them victory. When Salman and his companions came to Habib, they asked them to share in the spoils, and they said: We provided you with support, and the people of the Levant said: You did not witness the fighting, and you have nothing with us. Habib refused to join them, and he and his companions retreated to Their spoils, so the people of the Levant and the people of Iraq disputed over that, to the point that there was almost a dispute between them over that, so some of the people of Iraq said: If You kill Salman, we will kill your beloved, and if you leave for Ibn Affan, we will leave.” Abu Bakr Al-Ghassani said: “And I heard that it is the first “Animosity occurred between the people of the Levant and Iraq.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5472 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5473","Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Ibrahim al-Adl told me, Muhammad ibn Imran al-Nasawi told me, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb told us, he said: I heard my father He says: “Habib bin Maslamah’s nickname: Abu Abd al-Rahman.”"
"5474","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abdul Rahman bin Thabit bin Thaban told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Yazid ibn Haritha, on the authority of Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: “I witnessed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the fulfillment of a third.”"
"5475","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us, by Rayy, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaman, on the authority of Aamer bin Abdullah bin Yahya, “Abu Dharr Al-Ghifari and the people used to call him Habib bin Maslamah.” Beloved of the Romans because of his great struggle against the Romans.”"
"5476","Abdullah bin Ghanim told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told me, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, he said: “Habib bin Maslamah died. In Armenia in the year forty-two, when he was fifty years old.”"
"5477","Ahmad bin Al-Hasan Al-Bazzar told us, Ibn Azhar bin Raqqa Al-Masry told us, Abu Aslam Muhammad bin Mukhlid Al-Ru’ayni told us, Suleiman told us Ibn Abi Karima, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Qanaa Ibn Yahya, on the authority of Habib Ibn Maslamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Visit stupidity.” Increase your love"
"5478","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Bishr bin Musa, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, he said: Abu Hubayra told me, on the authority of Habib bin Maslamah Al-Fihri, and he was the one who answered the call, that he was ordered to lead an army, and it led paths, and when the enemy came, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No group of people gather and some of them pray, and some believe, but God answers them.” Then he said: He thanked God and praised Him, then said: “Oh God, spare our blood, and make our wages the wages of the martyrs.” While they were doing that, the rain descended. The prince of the enemy, and he entered upon Habib from his tent.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5478 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5479","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And who bore witness? At Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Banu Zuhra, and among their allies was Al-Miqdad bin Amr bin Tha’labah bin Malik bin Zam’a. Bin Thumama bin Matrud bin Amr bin Rabi’ah bin Zuhair bin Nimr bin Tha’labah bin Malik”"
"5480","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming “Whoever witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was from Bani Zuhra, and from their allies, Al-Miqdad bin Amr.”"
"5481","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told me, Shabab Al-Asfari told us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said: “Lineage Al-Miqdad to Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghuth bin Wahb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra adopted him, and it is called Al-Aswad bin Abi Qais bin Abd Manaf"
"5482","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us that this was true, Abu Al-Zinba’ Ruh bin Al-Faraj Al-Misri told us, Saeed bin Ufair told us, he said: “I was a friend of Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad during the pre-Islamic period, and he made a bloody affliction among them. He fled to Kindah and made an alliance with them, then he made a affliction with them. So he fled to Mecca and made an alliance with Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghouth, and for that reason he was attributed to him.”"
"5483","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad, nicknamed Abu Ma’bad, died in the year thirty. He was about seventy years old. He used to dye his beard. He died at Al-Jurf. He was carried on the necks of the men, and Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, prayed over him, and he was buried in Al-Baqi’."
"5484","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Al-Miqdad bin Amr bin Tha'labah bin Malik bin Rabi'ah, and he mentioned to Quda'ah. He was nicknamed Abu Ma'bad, and he was an ally of Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghouth. Al-Zuhri in pre-Islamic times, so he adopted him, and he was called: Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad. When the Qur’an was revealed: {Call them to their fathers} [Al-Ahzab: 5] it was said To him: Al-Miqdad bin Amr, and Al-Miqdad migrated to the land of Abyssinia, the second migration in - the narration of Ibn Ishaq -, and he witnessed Al-Miqdad was at Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was one of the archers mentioned among the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Ibn Umar said: Musa bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of his paternal aunt, Karimah bint Al-Miqdad, that she described her father To them, she said: “He was a tall, tall man, with a large belly, and the hair on his head was the yellow of his beard, and it is a good quality that is neither great nor light. Eyes with brows drawn together, he became more attentive. She said: Al-Miqdad died at Al-Jurf, three miles from the city, so he was carried on the necks of men and buried. In Medina, and Othman bin Affan prayed over him. That was in the year thirty-three, the day he died, when he was seventy years old or so. “Ibn Umar said: Muhammad told me, on the authority of Asim bin Omar and Abdullah bin Jaafar, about brotherhood, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “is my brother among Al-Miqdad.” And Jabr bin Atik
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5484 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5485","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Umayyah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad came to Mecca and said: “I will swear by the most honorable of its people.” So Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghouth, so he was called Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, but he is Miqdad bin Amr Al-Bahrawi, not Ibn Al-Aswad Al-Kindi."
"5486","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Israel, about Mukhaariq, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: I witnessed a scene from Al-Miqdad, because being its owner was dearer to me than what was done to it, because he came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying against the polytheists, said: By God, O Messenger of God, we do not say as the people of Moses said to Moses: {Go You and your Lord, so fight. Here we sit} But we fight on your right, and on your left, and in front of you, and behind you. “Then I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “And he greeted him and shined for that, and that pleased him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5486 - True"
"5487","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, I am Ubaid bin Sharik, Abdul Wahhab bin Najda Al-Houti told us, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told us, On the authority of Hariz bin Uthman, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Maysarah al-Hadrami told me, Abu Rashid al-Hubrani told me, he said: I saw al-Miqdad bin The black guard of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting on a coffin of the money changers in Homs. He was better on the coffin than his bones. The invasion, so I said to him: God has excused you, and he said: “Surat Al-Ba’uth refused us: {Go forth, light and heavy} [At-Tawbah: 41]. The rest of us said: «Surat Al-Bu’ath, Surat Al-Tawbah. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. I mentioned it in the first of the virtues of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him. The hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud The first to spread Islam were seven: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Ammar, and his mother. Sumaya, Suhaib, Al-Miqdad, and Bilal.”"
"5488","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, On the authority of Abdullah, Ismail bin Ali Al-Hattabi told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid told me Al-Narsi, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me May God bless him and grant him peace. When I returned, he said to me: “How do you find yourself?” I said: I continued until I thought that those with me were my guardians, and by God I will not act on two men after them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5488 - True"
"5489","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “Whoever testified Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj bin Amr bin Malik bin Aws Abu Abbas bin Jabr bin Amr bin Zaid bin Jashm bin Haritha bin Al-Harith”"
"5490","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “Abu Abbas bin Jabr bin Amr bin Zayd bin Jashm bin Haritha witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5491","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Isa informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, he said: I read to Ya’qub: “Who Abu Abbas bin Jabr, whose name is: Abd al-Rahman bin Jabr, witnessed Badr."
"5492","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abu Abbas Abdullah bin Jabr bin Amr bin Zaid Al-Ansari died in the year thirty-three.”"
"5493","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Yunus told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir said: “Abu Abbas Abd al-Rahman bin Jabr died in the year thirty-four, and he was seventy years old.”"
"5494","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar said: “Abu Abbas bin Jabr and Khunais bin Hudhafa al-Sahmi were among the great companions, may God be pleased with them, and Abu witnessed 'Abs attended Badr, Uhud, the trench, and all the other scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was among those who killed Ka'b bin Al-Ashraf. Ibn Al-Ashraf said. Omar: Abdul Majeed bin Abi Abbas, from the descendants of Abi Abbas bin Jabr, told me: “Abu Abbas died in the year thirty-four, and he was the son of Seventy years old, and Uthman prayed upon him, and Abu Burdah bin Niyar, Qatada bin Al-Numan, Muhammad bin Maslamah, and Salama bin Salama bin Waqsh”"
"5495","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Abdul Majeed bin Abi Abs Al-Ansari, from the descendants of Abi Abs “He used to pray the prayers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then he would go out to Banu Haritha, so he went out one dark, rainy night and lighted his stick for him until he entered the house of Banu Haritha.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5495 - Sent"
"5496","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Umayyah Al-Qurashi told me about the driver, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Salman bin Al-Numan told us. Al-Shaybani, Yahya bin Al-Ala told us, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Abs bin Jabr Al-Ansari frowned at the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, over food he had prepared for them. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take off Put your shoes on when eating, for it is a beautiful Sunnah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5496 - Yahya and his sheikh were abandoned"
"5497","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jarrahhi, the justice of Marwa, told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Atiya told us. Al-Marwazi, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdah bin Al-Hakam bin Muslim bin Bastam bin Abdullah told us, servant of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Abu Moaz, the grammarian, Al-Fadl bin Khaled Al-Bahili, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, On the authority of Anas, he said: “The two men furthest from the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Abu Lubabah bin Abd al-Mundhir and his family in Quba. And Abu Abbas bin Jabr, and his residence was in Bani Haritha. They used to pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the afternoon, then they would go to their people. They did not pray for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to hasten his prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5497 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5498","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Abu Talha Zaid bin Sahl bin Al-Aswad bin Haram bin Zaid Manat bin Adi bin Malik bin Al-Najjar witnessed Badr and he was one of the archers. Those mentioned are among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was said that he was a man with a square Adam, and he died in Medina in the year thirty-four, and he prayed Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, was upon him, and he was seventy years old at that time."
"5499","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa “in naming those who testified Pledge of Aqaba, then Badr was witnessed by the Banu Amr bin Malik bin Al-Najjar Abu Talha, who was Zayd bin Sahl bin Al-Aswad bin Haram bin Amr bin Zaid Manat »"
"5500","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Muslim told us, Ziyad al-Bakai told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ja`far. Bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Ali bin Al-Hussein, may God be pleased with them, in the hadith of digging, he said: “Abu Talha Zayd bin Sahl used to dig.”"
"5501","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Abu Talha Al-Ansari Zaid bin Sahl"
"5502","Ahmed bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, he said: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad, and I was listening, Sa`id bin Wasil told us, we told him Shu’bah, on the authority of Yahya bin Subaih, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is my uncle, so whoever of you wishes Let his uncle come out.” Meaning, Abu Talha, the husband of Sulaim’s mother, he said: In “Al-Karam,” he said this: I heard Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya, He says: I heard Abu Abbas Al-Daghuli saying: I heard Al-Hafiz Salih Jazrah saying: Your Excellency Al-Razi said to me: “If you enter Neyshabur You will be greeted by an old man with a good face, good clothes, good riding, good speech, so know that he is Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuli, so let him be the first. You ask about him the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yahya bin Subayh, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: He ruled that the first time I entered Neyshabur, a man met me. With this description, I asked about him, and they said: This is Muhammad bin Yahya, so I greeted him, and he responded, so I followed him until he came down, so I said: The sheikh brings out his books to me, so he took out parts and said: Wait for me to go out for the noon prayer. When he went out, he called the call to prayer, established the prayer, and sat in the His mihrab, so I read to him what I had written, then I said to him: What hadith has benefited me, please, Al-Razi on the authority of the Sheikh, so he said: Bring me, and I said: Saeed narrated it to you. Ibn Amir, Shu`bah told us, and I mentioned the hadith, so he smiled and then said to me: “O boy, who would vote for something like this that you voted for? And he reads like what you read, does he know that Saeed bin Amer does not narrate anything like this? I said: Yes, Saeed bin Wasil told you. He said: Yes, Saeed bin Wasil told us.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5502 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5503","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told me, in Kufa, Muteen told us, Muhammad bin Al-Alaa Abu Kurayb told us, Qabisah told us, we told him Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, and Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The voice of Abu Talha in “An army is better than a thousand men.” He did not write it with this chain of transmission, and its narrations on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy. Rather, this text is known from the hadith of Ali bin Zaid bin Judaan, on the authority of Anas
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5503 - Its narrators are trustworthy according to Muslim’s conditions"
"5504","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Ali told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, I am Ali bin Abdullah. Al-Madini and Ibrahim bin Bashar said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jud’an, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A voice Abu Talha in the army is better than any group.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5504 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5505","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Abd told me. Allah ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said on the day of Uhud: “Whoever kills an infidel will have his plunder,” so Abu Talha was killed on that day. Twenty men “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5505 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5506","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, Abi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “Abu Talha fasted for forty years after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not breaking his fast except on the day of breaking the fast or the day of sacrifice.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5506 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5507","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Bahz bin Asad told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Talha said: “I do not conspire against two people, nor do I disparage them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5507 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5508","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd and Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “that Abu Talha read this verse: {Go forth, light and heavy} [At-Tawbah: 41] and he said: We called upon God, and God commanded us, and we called upon old men and young men to prepare me, and his sons said: May God have mercy on you, for you have fought during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, Abu Bakr and Omar, and we are fighting on your behalf now. So he invaded the sea, and he died. They asked for an island to bury him, but they were not able to. He did not change it until seven days later, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5508 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5509","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, we told him Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Humaid Al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that Abu Talha used to throw in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would raise his back from behind him to see where his arrow was falling,” so Abu Talha would reach across his chest to protect it. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Thus, O Prophet of God, may God make me your ransom. Let us move without moving. This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"5510","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “In naming The seventy who witnessed Aqaba, he said: Among the Banu Salem bin Awf bin Amr bin Awf bin Al-Khazraj, Ubadah bin Al-Samit bin Qays bin Asram bin Bahz bin Tha’labah bin Ghanam bin Salim, a captain who witnessed Badr, and all of the scenes were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5511","I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh saying: I heard Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Sufyan bin Uyaynah says: “Ubadah bin Al-Samit Badri is a Uhadi, Aqbi, Shajari, and he is a captain.”"
"5512","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed me, and al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, saying: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal say: “Ubadah ibn al-Samit Badri is one of the calcaneal peduncle"
"5513","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid told us, Ubayy told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “in naming those who witnessed Aqaba and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” he said: “And from Bani Awf, then from Bani Salem bin Jafar Ubadah bin Al-Samit, he is a captain and he witnessed Badr.”"
"5514","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, Bishr ibn Musa told us, al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubadah ibn The silent one, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to give alms, and he said: “O Abu Al-Walid.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5514 - Interrupted"
"5515","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Farahadani told us, Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, Abdah bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Al-Mukhadji, who said: “It was said to Ubadah bin Al-Samit: O Abu ""The newborn"""
"5516","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmed bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Makhoul, said: “Ubadah ibn al-Samit and Shaddad ibn Aws lived in Bayt al-Maqdis, and Ubadah was nicknamed Aba Al-Walid"
"5517","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Yunus bin told me Bukair, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Ma’abad bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, Salamah told me, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father Ka'b bin Malik said: “We went out during the Hajj in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Aqaba, and the captain of Banu Awf bin Al-Harith Ubadah bin Al-Samit”"
"5518","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ibrahim bin Na’ila Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid bin Ubaidah told us, Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata' bin Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of his father, that Muawiyah said to them: O people Ansar, what is the matter with you that you do not come to me with your brothers from Quraysh? Ubadah said: “The need.” He said: So what about the waste? He said: “We spent it on the Day of Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5519","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Damra bin Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ata’. He said: “The graves of Ubadah ibn al-Samit and Omar ibn Abdullah are in Bayt al-Maqdis.”"
"5520","Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Hafiz told me, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Abu Mushar told us, Abbad Al-Khawas told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Amr al-Sibani, on the authority of Abu Salam al-Aswad, said: “Whenever I came to Jerusalem, I would descend upon Ubadah ibn al-Samit.”"
"5521","Abdullah bin Ghanim told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told me, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, he said: “Ubadah bin He fasted in the Levant in the land of Palestine in Ramla in the year thirty-four, and he was seventy-two years old.”"
"5522","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Abbas, the martyr, may God Almighty have mercy on him, told me, Ahmed bin Ali bin Razin told us, Muhammad bin Amrawih told us, we told him Al-Haytham bin Adi said: “Ubadah bin Al-Samit died in Jerusalem, and was buried there in the year thirty-four. He was seventy-two years old. year”"
"5523","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad bin Mubarak al-Ghuri told us, Yahya bin Hamza, Burd bin Sinan narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Qubaysah bin Dhu’ayb, on the authority of his father, that Ubadah bin al-Samit disapproved of Muawiyah told him: “I will not make you live in a land.” So he went to Medina, and Umar said to him: “Whatever brought you to me, God will not conquer a land where you are not Therein are you and people like you.” So depart, leaving no authority for Mu’awiyah over you."
"5524","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abu Usama and Waki’ told us, On the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: “He had fought six battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Conquests” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5524 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5525","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Junada ibn Abi Umayyah al-Dawsi, who said: “I came into contact with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and he had understood the religion of God.”"
"5526","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Husayn bin Muhammad told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Yashkari, On the authority of Abu al-Ash`ath, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us not to fear, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5526 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5527","Abu Amr bin Ismail told me, Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Mahrajani told me, Ahmad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Najdah told me, Abu Al-Mughirah, Bishr bin Abdullah bin Bashhar told us, Ubadah bin Nasi told me, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was busy, so when a man came and had converted to Islam at the hands of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would give him to a man. From us to teach him the Qur’an, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, handed over to me a man who was with me in the house, and I was reading the Qur’an to him and he saw that I had the right to it. Indeed, he presented to me a bow that I had never seen more finer than it, nor more tender than it, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What do you see? O Messenger of God, about it, and he said: “A burning ember between your shoulders, which you have tied or hung.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5527 - True"
"5528","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Masisi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Waqid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that he entered upon Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Amirs will follow you after me who will make you know what you deny. And they deny you what you know, so whoever among you realizes that, there is no obedience to him who disobeys God.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated by Zuhair bin Muawiyah and Muslim bin Khaled Al-Zanji, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim With increases in it"
"5529","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa, Al-Adl, told me, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Muafia bin Suleiman Al-Harrani told us, Zuhayr told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid, and similar to it, and as for the hadith of Muslim bin Khaled “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5528 - Abdullah bin Waqid was the only one to narrate it, and he is weak"
"5530","So Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Mahan Al-Khazzaz told us, in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Muslim bin told us Khalid, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his father, that Ubadah bin Al-Samit stood in the middle of the house of the Commander of the Faithful, Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Muhammad Abul-Qasim, saying: “Men will take care of your affairs after me.” They make you know what you deny, and they deny you what you know, so there is no obedience to whoever disobeys God, so do not blame yourselves, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed Muawiyah is one of those people.” Uthman did not review it literally. “This hadith was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs regarding the mention of Ubadah ibn The one who is silent about Othman bin Affan, complaining of a brief text.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5530 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5531","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, a partner told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Nimr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Mukmal, on the authority of Azhar Ibn Abdullah, who said: “Ubadah Ibn al-Samit came as a pilgrim from He went to the Levant and performed Hajj, then he came to Medina and came to Uthman ibn Affan, aggrieved. He mentioned the hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5531 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5532","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “He was the first to One of the immigrants who came to the city was Abu Salama, and the first to come to it after Abu Salama was Amer bin Rabi’ah.”"
"5533","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Amer bin Rabia bin Malik bin Amer bin Rabia bin Hujair bin Salman: He mentioned lineage back to Ma’ad bin Adnan, and he was an ally of Al-Khattab bin Nufayl, and when Amer bin Rabi’ah swore an alliance with him, Al-Khattab adopted him, and he was called: Amer bin Al-Khattab until God Almighty revealed his mention: {Call them by their fathers} [Al-Ahzab: 5] So he joined his father and returned to his lineage.
 Ibn Umar said: Muhammad bin Salih told me, on the authority of Ibn Roman, who said: Amer bin Rabi’ah converted to Islam long ago, before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, settled in Al-Arqam, and before he made the supplication there, Amer bin Rabi’ah migrated to the land of Abyssinia, the two migrations, and with him his wife. Laila bint Abi Hathamah Al-Adawiya, sister of Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah. “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother between Amer bin Rabi’ah, and more Ibn Al-Mundhir Ibn Shurayh Al-Ansari.” Aamir Ibn Rabi’ah was nicknamed: Abu Abdullah, and he witnessed Badr, Uhud, and the Trench. And all the scenes are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He died after Uthman, may God be pleased with him, was killed. He had stayed home and did not People feel that his funeral has been taken out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5533 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5534","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, I am Ja’far bin Aoun, I am Yahya bin Saeed. Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, said: When people started attacking Uthman, my father got up during the night, then prayed and said: “O God, protect me from temptation because of what You have protected the righteous among Your servants with, for he did not leave or wake up in the morning except with his funeral.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5534 - True"
"5535","Abu Zur’ah al-Razi told me, Abu Sufyan Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Muawiyah al-Utbi told me, in Egypt, my father told me, Sa’id bin Ufayr told me. He said: “Amer bin Rabi’ah Al-Adawi died in the year thirty-three, and it was said that in the year thirty-two.”"
"5536","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Muhammad bin Omar bin Khalid al-Harrani told us, Ubi told us, Abdullah bin Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of Urwa, “Among those who migrated to Abyssinia who left the first time before Ja’far and his companions from the Banu Adi ibn Ka'b Amer bin Rabi'ah, from the people of Yemen, witnessed Badr."
"5537","Ahmed bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ahmed bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Saad bin Suleiman told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, Amr told us Bin Yahya, Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amer bin Rabi’ah, who said: “Badr was on the morning of the sixteenth of Ramadan.” Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab narrated, on the authority of Amer bin Rabi’ah - two hadiths, the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on one of them. -: “If you see a funeral, stand up for it” and the second hadith"
"5538","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Jabbar, in Homs, Al-Harith bin Ubaidah, narrated to us by Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aamir ibn Rabi’ah, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he passed by a funeral. Then a Jewish man said: O Muhammad, speak about this funeral. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, so the Jew said: I bear witness. He spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the People of the Book speak to you, say: We believe in God and His angels and His books.” And his messengers: “This is a hadith known to be narrated by Al-Harith bin Ubaidah Al-Rahawi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and we wrote it in the last version of Yunus, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri.”"
"5539","Abu Al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, in Nishapur, Al-Qasim bin Abdullah bin Mahdi told us, my uncle told us, a man named him Abu Al-Qasim bin Mabur, Zayd bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem said: Abdullah bin Omar said: When a funeral was being prepared Rafi’ bin Khadij and mentioned the hadith"
"5540","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us about this lineage, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Omar bin Khalid al-Harrani told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Omar bin Khaled al-Harrani told us, My father, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Nawfal bin Urwa bin Al-Zubair told us."
"5541","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told me, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, and Abu Bakr ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah told me Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, my father, may God have mercy on him, and Abdullah Ibn Saeed told me, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of His father said: “When it was the Day of Yarmouk, it was said to Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam, O Abu Abdullah.”"
"5542","Abu Bakr bin Abi Ja`far Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: “Umm Al-Zubayr: Safiyya The daughter of Abd al-Muttalib, and her mother: Hala bint Uhayb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra, and her mother: Aaliyah bint Abd al-Muttalib bin Abd hypocrisy"
"5543","Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qadi told me, and Hammad ibn Ahmad al-Qadi told us, saying: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah saying: Abu Usama told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: “Al-Zubayr converted to Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he was killed when he was sixty-odd years old.”"
"5544","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, “Talha and al-Zubayr reached all One of them is sixty-four.”"
"5545","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Al-Zubayr was killed while he was He was sixty-seven years old, and his nickname was Abu Al-Taher.”"
"5546","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, I am Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: He said Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, then Nafi bin Jubayr bin Mutim told me, saying: I heard Al-Abbas saying to Al-Zubayr: “O Abdullah, here is your order.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to raise the flag.”"
"5547","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, They said: Bukair narrated to us, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr. He said: Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam converted to Islam, and he is the son of Eight years, and he emigrated when he was eighteen years old. Al-Zubayr’s uncle used to hang Al-Zubayr in a mat, smoke fire over him, and say: Return to Disbelief, so Al-Zubair said: “I will never disbelieve.”"
"5548","Mukhlid ibn Ja`far al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad ibn Jarir told me, Amr ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ayli told me, Abu Usama told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, said: Al-Zubayr embraced Islam and migrated to the land of Abyssinia, both migrations together, and he did not remain behind in a campaign that he conquered. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “was a brother between him and Ibn Masoud,” and he was a man who was neither tall nor tall. Short, thin beard, dark in colour, hairy"
"5549","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Al-Zubayr went To Medina, so Amr bin Jarmuz followed him while he was heading towards Medina and killed him in a siege in Wadi al-Sibbaa, so God absolved Ali of his blood. And his companions, but Amr bin Jarmuz killed him in Rajab in the year thirty-six, and the Banu Majashi, the Arabs had led them to hide al-Zubayr. That is why Jarir says:
 [Long Sea]
 After Al-Zubair, she wore the clothes of a woman who had her period and had not washed off the blood.”"
"5550","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Sakin bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hafs bin Khaled, a sheikh told me, who came to us from Mosul, and said: I accompanied Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, may God be pleased with him, on some of his travels, and he became impure. In a barren land, he said: “Cover me.” So I covered him, then I suddenly turned to him and saw him covered with swords, so I said: By God, I have seen you. Effects that I had never seen on anyone. He said: “Did you see that?” He said: “By God, there is no surgery in it except with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the path of God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5550 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5551","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, he said: It was A whiff from Satan that Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had been taken, so he heard about that Al-Zubayr, who was eleven years old, so he came out with a sword. Drawn until he stood before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: I wanted to strike whoever took you, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him and his sword, and it was the first sword drawn in the path of God Almighty."
"5552","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, I am Ibn Wahb, Abu Sakhr told me, on the authority of My father Muawiyah al-Bajli is Ammar al-Dahni, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “It was the first A battle in Islam at Badr. We had only two knights with us: a horse for Al-Zubayr and a horse for Al-Miqdad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5552 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5553","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Zubayr, he said: “By God, what The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out on a campaign that he conquered, and there was no expedition that I was not in.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5553 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5554","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told us, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, said: “It was with Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam on the day of Badr. A yellow turban worn with pride, so the angels descended upon them as yellow turbans.”"
"5555","Mukhlid bin Jaafar told me, Muhammad bin Jarir told me, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told me, he said: “The inheritance of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam was divided into forty thousand. A thousand dirhams"
"5556","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, and Abu Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us: Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, we told him Qutaibah bin Saeed, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: “Al-Zubayr’s inheritance was divided into forty thousand thousand dirhams.”"
"5557","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Halwani told us, Atiq ibn al-Zubayr told us, Abu Ya`qub ibn Al-Zubayr bin Habib bin Thabit bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr said, To his father: O father, tell me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so that I can narrate on your behalf, for all the sons of the Companions narrate on the authority of his father, so he said: O my son, no one accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a companion except that I accompanied him with a companion similar to it or better than it, and I knew That your mother Asma bint Abu Bakr was under me, and that your paternal aunt Aisha was the daughter of Abu Bakr, and you learned that my mother is Safiya bint Abd Al-Muttalib, and that my maternal uncles are Hamza bin Abdul-Muttalib, Abu Talib, and Abbas, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is my maternal uncle’s son. You knew that my aunt Khadija bint Khuwaylid was under it, and that her daughter Fatima was the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you knew that Khadija’s mother was Habibah bint Asad bin Abd al-Uzza, and you have learned that the mother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Aminah bint Wahb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra. I was with him in the best company, praise be to God, and I heard him say: “Whoever says against me what I did not say?” Let him take his seat in the Fire.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5557 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5558","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubayr.” So it was said to him: O Abu Abdullah, do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it to someone other than you? He said: No, by God, I do not know. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5558 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5559","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Abu Abdullah Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar Al-Zubayri told us, Abu Ghaziyah Muhammad bin Musa, Abdullah bin Musab told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of her grandmother, Asma Daughter of Abu Bakr, she said: Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam passed by a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Hassan was reciting to them some of his poetry. While they were inattentive to what they were hearing from him, Al-Zubayr sat with them and said: “Why should I see you not listening to what you are hearing from the poetry of Ibn Al-Fura’ih? He will present it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he will listen well to him, bestow his reward upon him, and will not distract him from anything.” Hassan said:
 [Long Sea]
 He established the covenant of the Prophet and his guidance... his disciples, and words are equivalent to deeds.
 He adhered to His method and way... He is loyal to the Guardian of the truth, and the truth is more just.
 He is the famous knight and the hero who arrives when it is a glorious day.
 And if a man's mother was Safiyya... and if there is a lion in her house, it will be disgraceful.
 He has close kinship with the Messenger of God... and from supporting Islam there is great glory.
 How many calamities did Al-Zubayr inflict with his sword... on behalf of the Chosen One, and God gives and abundantly.
 If she uncovers her war leg, he stuffs it...with white, racing to death, fluttering away.
 There is nothing like it among them, nor was there before it... and eternity will not exist as long as it withers.
 Your praise is better than the deeds of good company...And your action, O Ibn Al-Hashimiyya, is better.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5559 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5560","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, who said: Uthman was afflicted with nosebleeds during the year, until he gave orders and refrained from performing Hajj, then a man from Quraysh entered upon us. So he said: He left behind, so he said: “And they said that?” He said: Yes. He said: “And who is he?” So he remained silent, then another one came in and said: Leave him as a successor, so he mentioned something similar to what the first one mentioned, so Othman said: “Al-Zubayr?” He said: Yes, then Othman said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if there was no good for them I would not know, and I love them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5560 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5561","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl, told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, I am Jafar bin Aoun, I am Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Bahi, on the authority of Urwa, said: Aisha said to me: “O my son, your father is one of those who responded to God and the Messenger after They were afflicted with ulcers.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"5562","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Jarudi told us, Abdullah ibn Sa`id al-Kindi told us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nadr bin Mansour al-Anazi, Alqamah bin Ulatha al-Yashkari told me, he said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard I was heard from within the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he said: “Talhah and al-Zubayr are my neighbors in Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. """"
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5562 - Incorrect"
"5563","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Abi Al-Qadi told us, we told us Ali bin Hakim, Sharik bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he said: “No “Insult the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for their atonement is death.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5563 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5564","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Khazim told us, Hisham told us Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me on a cold morning. So I came to him while he was with some of his wives in his quilt, so he put me into the quilt and we became three. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5564 - True"
"5565","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told me, Abu Nu’aym Dirar bin Surad told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us. Al-Darawardi, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muslim Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Zubayr Ibn Al-Awwam said: A man from the Ansar attacked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the anus of a free woman. He said: “O Zubayr, give me water.” Then he sent Water to your neighbor.” Then Al-Ansari said: O Messenger of God, if he is your cousin. Then the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, colored and he said: “O Zubair, water, then withhold the water until it reaches the wall, then send it to your neighbour.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted Zubair his right. Al-Zubair said: I believe this verse was revealed in my disputes: {But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what is disputed between them} [An-Nisa: 65]. The verse: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” I do not know of anyone who established this chain of narration, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who mentions Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his brother, and he was in distress."
"5566","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmed bin Al-Miqdam told us, Othman told us Ibn Ali, Hisham Ibn Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, he said: When it was the Day of the Camel, Al-Zubayr called his son Abdullah and advised him, and he said: “O My son, this is a day on which the oppressor or the oppressed will be killed. By God, if I kill, I will surely kill an oppressed person. By God, I have not done it nor will I do it. Look, O my children, for I will not leave anything more important than this, which is one thousand and two hundred thousand.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5566 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5567","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, about Ibn Shihab said: “Al-Zubayr left on the day of the camel defeated, but Ibn Jarmuz, a man from Banu Tamim, overtook him and killed him.”"
"5568","Ismail bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi told me, Abd al-Aziz bin Imran told us, he said: I am Saeed bin Abdul Aziz Al-Sulami, on the authority of his father, who said: When Al-Zubayr left on the Day of the Camel, he started saying: “
 [full sea]
 And I knew, if only my knowledge were of benefit to me...that life is near death.”
 Then it was not suspected that Ibn Jarmuz killed him."
"5569","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khalid told us, he said: I heard Al-Fadl bin Dukain saying: “Talha and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam were killed in Rajab in the year thirty-six.”"
"5570","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of his sheikhs, they said: Al-Zubayr left on the Day of the Camel, that was Thursday, the first ten days of Jumada al-Akhira, of this year, after the incident with a horse called: Dhu al-Khimar, heading towards Medina, was killed in Wadi al-Siba’ and was buried there. It was reported on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that he said: “My father was killed on the Day of the Camel.” He was four years older than sixty.” Ibn Umar said: I heard Mus’ab bin Thabit bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr say: “Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam witnessed Badr, who was twenty-seven years old.”"
"5571","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: I am Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah, Abdullah told us Al-Malik bin Qarib Al-Asma’i said: I heard Abdullah bin Aoun say: These good people were completely killed. Then he cried and said: Al-Zubayr has come. On his killer and he defeated him, so he said: I remind you of God, so Al-Zubayr stopped him until he did that repeatedly, then when he betrayed Al-Zubayr and hit him, Al-Zubayr said: “May God kill you. You remind me of God and then forget Him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5571 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5572","Abd Al-Baqi bin Qani’ told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hammad Al-Barbari told us, Abu Al-Sakin Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Tai told us, Omar bin Zahr bin Husayn narrated to us, saying: My grandfather Humayd bin Munhab told me, saying: “I performed Hajj in the year in which Othman was killed, and I met Talha. Al-Zubayr and Aisha, may God be pleased with them, were in Mecca, and when they walked to Basra, I walked with them, and Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, walked. To them until they met, and that was the Day of the Camel, so they fought fiercely, and seventy men were seized by the snout of the camel on that day - and he mentioned the hadith. He was very tall and said at the end - Al-Zubayr turned away defeated, but Ibn Jarmuz, a man from Banu Tamim, overtook him and killed him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5572 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5573","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Othman bin Khazraz of Antioch told us, Rabi’ah bin al-Harith told us, he told me Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Abed, Ismail bin Abi Hazim told us, he said: Ali said to Al-Zubayr: Do you not remember the day you and I were in a people’s shed? From the Ansar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to you: “Do you love him?” So I said: What is stopping me? He said: “But you will revolt against him and fight him while you are an oppressor.” He said: Then Al-Zubayr returned.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5573 - The hadith contains consideration"
"5574","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Abu Asim, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Malik Al-Raqqashi told us, on the authority of his grandfather Abdul Malik, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad Al-Dili, He said: I witnessed Al-Zubair go out to seek Ali, and Ali said to him, I adjure you by God: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “You are fighting him while you are He is an oppressor.” He said: “I did not mention.” Then Al-Zubayr went away. “This is an authentic hadith,” on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad. He narrated from him. Yazid bin Suhayb al-Faqir and Fadl bin Fadalah in one chain of narration
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5574 - True"
"5575","Abu Amr Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Matar al-Adil al-Ma’mun told us that from the origin of his book. Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Siwar Al-Hashimi, Munjab bin Al-Harith told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ajlah told us, my father told me, on the authority of Yazid Al-Faqir. Munjab said: And I heard Fadla bin Fadala, he narrated it all, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad Al-Dili, who said: I witnessed Ali and Al-Zubayr, when Al-Zubayr returned to His animal was tearing through the rows, so his son Abdullah showed it to him and said: What is the matter with you? He said: Ali mentioned to me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You will fight him while you are unjust to him,” so I will not fight him. He said: And why did you come to fight? You have only come to reconcile people, and may God reconcile this matter to you. He said: I swore not to fight. He said: Then free your servant Girgis. He stood until He reconciled with the people. He said: Then he freed his servant, Girgis, and he stood and the people’s affairs differed, so he went on his horse. “It was narrated that Al-Zubayr’s confession to Ali, may God be pleased with him, From them with that other than these aspects and narrations.”"
"5576","Abu Al-Walid, the Imam, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Qattan bin Bashir told us, Jafar told us. Bin Sulaiman, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, my grandfather told me, on the authority of Abu Jarwa Al-Mazini, who said: I heard Ali, Al-Zubayr, and Ali saying to him: I adjure you by God, O Zubayr. Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “You are fighting me and you are unjust to me”? He said: Yes, but I forgot"
"5577","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khaled bin Yazid Al-Arni told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muhammad al-Raqqashi, on the authority of his grandfather Abd al-Malik ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu Jarwa al-Mazini, who said: I heard Ali, as he was appealing to al-Zubayr, saying to him: I appealed to you by God, O Zubayr. Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “You are fighting me and you are unjust to me.” He said: Yes, but I forgot."
"5578","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muteen told us, Omar bin Muhammad Al-Asadi told us, my father told me, Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Abbas. Ibn Duraij, on the authority of Muslim Ibn Nazir, who said: We were with Ali, may God be pleased with him, and Ibn Jarmuz came to ask for permission, and Ali said: Shall I kill you? Is Safiya’s son proud? Give him permission and give him good tidings of the Fire. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Every prophet has a disciple, and Al-Zubair is my disciple and the son of my cousin.”"
"5579","So Sheikh Abu Kamil bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, On the authority of Zurr ibn Hubaysh, he said: It was said to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him: The killer of al-Zubayr was at the gate, so Ali said: Congratulations to the killer of ibn Safiyat al-Nar, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.”"
"5580","Abu Bakr bin Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, in Kufa, Abu Ja`far Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hamza bin Aoun Al-Masoudi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Asadi, Sufyan Al-Thawri and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, who said: I was sitting with Ali, and he came With the head of Al-Zubayr and with him his killer, then Ali said: To the one who gives the call, give good news to the killer of Ibn Safiya of Hellfire. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “For every A prophet and disciple, and the disciple of Al-Zubayr” These hadiths are authentic, on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali, even if they did not narrate it with these chains of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5580 - These are Sahih hadiths"
"5581","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail, the jurist about irrigation, told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Talha Al-Taymi, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha told us, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, who said: “Ali bin Abi Talib, and Al-Zubayr, Talha bin Ubayd Allah and Saad bin Abi Waqqas were called “one-year-old.” Ibrahim said: “because they were born in one year.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5581 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5582","Abu Taher Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Juwayni told me, Abu Bakr bin Raja bin al-Sindi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: “Atika bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl inherited Al-Zubayr, and her wife was, Her share of the inheritance amounted to eighty thousand dirhams, and she said in her eulogy:
 [full sea]

 Ibn Jarmuz greedily betrayed Faris... on the day of the meeting, but he was not willing.
 O Amr, if you had alerted him, you would have found him... not reckless, like a finger or a hand.
 Your mother bereaved of you if you overcame a knight... in the past of his goings and lunches.
 “How many times has he fought, but your cruiser did not deter him from it, O Ibn Faqa’ al-Fadfad?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5582 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5583","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khaled Al-Harrani told us, My father, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he said: Talha bin Ubayd Allah bin Uthman bin Amr bin Ka’b. Ibn Saad Ibn Taym Ibn Murrah, who was in the Levant, spoke to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his arrow, so he struck it for him with his arrow, and said: And do it. O Messenger of God? He said: “And your reward from the day of Badr.”"
"5584","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Jabir Al-Sindi told us, Abdullah bin Shabib Al-Muzani told us Ibrahim bin Yahya Al-Sijzi, my father told us, on the authority of Hazim bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The mother of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the mother of Uthman, the mother of Talha, the mother of Ammar ibn Yasir, and the mother of Abd converted to Islam.” Al-Rahman bin Awf, Umm Al-Zubayr, and Saad and his mother embraced Islam in life.”"
"5585","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Muhammad bin Fulayh told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab said: Talha bin Ubaid Allah bin Uthman bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Saad bin Tamim bin Murrah came from the Levant after the Prophet returned. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him from Badr. He spoke to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about his share. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “You have your share.” He said: And be rewarded, O Messenger of God. He said: “And you will be rewarded.”"
"5586","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, narrated by Makhramah bin Sulaiman Al-Walabi, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha, who said: Talha bin Abdullah said to me I attended the market of Busra, and I saw a monk in his cell saying: Ask the people of this season, is there one of them from the people of the sanctuary? Talha said: I said: Yes, I did. He said: Has Ahmed appeared yet? He said: I said: Who is Ahmed? He said: Ibn Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib, this is the month in which he emerges, and he is the last of the prophets. He left the Sacred Mosque, and he migrated. To palm trees, Harra, and swim, so be careful not to run to it. Talha said: Then what he said fell into my heart, so I left quickly until I reached Mecca, so I said: Was it an event? They said: Yes, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amin prophesied, and Ibn Abi Quhafa followed him. He said: So I went out until I entered upon Abu Bakr and said: Did you follow this man? He said: Yes, so go to him, then go to him and follow him, for he is calling to the truth. So Talha told him what the monk said: So Abu came out Bakr married Talha, so he brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Talha converted to Islam.The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him of what the monk said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, explained it. When Abu Bakr and Talha converted to Islam, Nawfal bin Khuwailid bin Al-Adawiya took them and tied them together with one rope, and Banu Taim did not prevent them. Nawfal bin Khuwaylid was He is called the most powerful of the Quraysh, and that is why Abu Bakr and Talha were called the Qarnayn, and Talha bin Ubayd Allah did not witness Badr, and that is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. Wajh and Sa`id bin Zaid were spying out news of the caravan, so they left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had finished fighting those who He met him from the polytheists, and they met him in the shade and in a veil on the veil, departing from Badr, but he witnessed Uhud and other than that. Scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was among those who remained steadfast with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud when the people took power, and pledged allegiance to him on Death, and Malik bin Zuhayr shot the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on that day, and Talha with his hand avoided the face of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He hit his pinky finger and it was paralyzed. He said: He felt pain when the shot hit him.He mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he had said: In the name of God, he would have entered Paradise.” And the people were looking at him and Talha was struck. On that day, a man from the polytheists struck him twice on his hard head: one blow while he was facing it, and one blow while he was turning away from it, and he was Dirar bin Al-Khattab Al-Fihri says: I, by God, hit him that day.
 Ibn Omar said: “Talha was nicknamed Abu Muhammad, and his mother was the difficult one, the daughter of Abdullah Al-Hadrami, and Talha was killed on the day of the camel. Marwan bin Al-Hakam, and he had a son called Muhammad, and he is called Al-Sajjad, and he was nicknamed Talha. He was killed with his father Talha on the day The camel, and Talha was a pre-Islamic man."
"5587","Ibn Umar said: Ishaq bin Yahya told me, on the authority of his grandmother, Sa`dah bint Awf al-Marriya, the mother of Yahya bin Talha, who said: “Talha was killed.” Ibn Ubaid Allah, and in the hand of his treasurer were one thousand dirhams and two hundred thousand dirhams, and his assets and properties were valued at thirty thousand thousand dirhams, and he was in He mentioned a reward with money, clothing and food, and he was killed on the day he was killed when he was sixty-two years old.” Ibn Umar said: Asad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid bin Al-Muhajir, said: “Talha was sixty-four years old on the day he was killed.”"
"5588","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Junaid, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Imran, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha told me, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, who said: “Talha bin Ubaidullah is white, he looks to red, he is square, he is close to being short, he is broad-chested, broad-shouldered, when he turns around, everyone turns around. “He had large feet, a beautiful face, he had long hair when he walked, and he never changed his hair.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5588 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5589","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me: I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Abbad bin Al-Walid Al-Anazi told us, Hibban told us, Sharik bin told us Al-Hubab, Utbah ibn Sa’sa’a ibn al-Ahnaf told me, on the authority of Ikrash, who said: We were fighting Ali with Talha and with us Marwan. He said: Then we were defeated. He said: Marwan said: “I will not know how to take revenge on Talha after today.” He said: So he shot him with an arrow and killed him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5589 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5590","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ashhal bin Hatim told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Nafi’ said: “Talha bin Ubayd Allah was killed by Marwan bin Al-Hakam.”"
"5591","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Yahya bin Sulaiman Al-Ja’fi told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, said: “I saw Marwan bin Al-Hakam when Talha bin Ubaid Allah was shot at that day, and he fell to his knee and still remained... He glorified Allah until he died.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5591 - True"
"5592","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Umayyah Al-Tarsusi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Aishi told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Hammad told us. Al-Talhi, Talha bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in his hand A quince, so he threw it to me, or, he said: he threw it to me, and said: “Don’t take it, Abu Muhammad, for it hardens the heart.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5592 - True"
"5593","Muhammad bin Zafar Al-Hafiz told me, and I asked him. Al-Hussein bin Ayyash Al-Qattan told me, Al-Hussein told me, Yahya bin Ayyash told me. Al-Qattan, Al-Hussein bin Yahya Al-Marwazi told us, Ghalib bin Hulays Al-Kalbi Abu Al-Haytham told us, Juwayriyah bin Asma told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Sa`id, my uncle told me, he said: When the Day of the Camel came, Ali called out to the people: “Do not shoot anyone with an arrow, do not stab anyone with a spear, and do not hit anyone.” With a sword, and do not seek the people, for this is the station of whoever succeeds in it, he will live on the Day of Resurrection.” He said: So we agreed, then the people said All in all: O retaliations of Uthman. He said: And Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, our imam, was in front of a large number of people with the standard. He said: Then Ali called him and said: So he came to us offering His face, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful. They say: O the revenges of Othman. So Ali extended his hands and said: O God, destroy the killers of Othman today. With their faces.” Then Al-Zubayr said to the bracelets he had with him, saying: “Throw a volley at them,” as if he wanted the fight to break out, so when he saw His companions did not wait for the army to break out, and they attacked, but God defeated them. Marwan bin Al-Hakam shot Talha bin Ubaidullah with an arrow, severing his leg. Next to his horse, the horse seized him until he caught up with him and slaughtered him. Then Marwan turned to Aban bin Uthman, who was with him, and said: I have had enough for you. One of your father's killers
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5593 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5594","Al-Walid told me, Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abdah told us, Al-Hassan bin Al-Hussein told us, Rifa’ah told us Ibn Iyas al-Dhabi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: We were with Ali on the Day of the Camel, and he sent to Talha ibn Ubaid Allah that the Qunni had come to him, and Talha had come to him. He said: I called you to God. Have you heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He says: “Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him”? He said: Yes. He said: Why are you fighting me? He said: I did not mention. He said: Then Talha left.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5594 - Al-Hasan is Al-Arni, not trustworthy"
"5595","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Suleiman Al-Narsi told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Musab, Musa bin Uqba told me, he said: I heard Alqamah bin Waqqas say: When Talha, Al-Zubayr, and Aisha went out to ask for blood Othman, may God be pleased with them, attacked those with them of the same race, and belittled Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Harith bin Hisham sent them back. He said: I saw him, and he loved the gatherings he vacated, while he was stroking his beard for his falsehood, so I said To him: O Abu Muhammad, I see you, and I love the gatherings with you. Leave them while you are stroking your beard over your falsehood. Do you hate this? Today, leave him alone, and no one will force you to do so? He said: “O Alqamah bin Waqqas, do not blame me. We were one hand against everyone else, so today they have become two mountains, one of us crawling to his friend. But he was of me in the matter of Uthman, may God be pleased with him, which I do not see as an expiation for him, except for my blood to be shed in pursuit of his. I said: Why did Muhammad ibn Talha Do you take it out and you have a small child? Leave it to him. If it is something that will be left behind in your estate? He said: He knows, I hate to see someone who has intention in this matter, so I reject him. So I spoke to Muhammad bin Talha about being backward, and he said: I hate to Ask the traveler about my father
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5595 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"5596","Abu Hafs Ahmad bin Labid, the jurist, told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Saleh Al-Harrani told us, Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Sulayman bin Isa bin Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “Talha was the predecessor of the Prophet in four days: she was with... The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave birth to Aisha, the daughter of Abu Bakr, and her sister, Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Abu Bakr, was with Talha, and she bore him Zachariah. And Yusuf and Aisha, and Zainab bint Jahsh was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Hamnah bint Jahsh was with Talha bin Ubaid Allah. She bore him Muhammad, and he was killed on the Day of the Camel with his father. Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan was the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was Her sister, Al-Rifa’ah bint Abi Sufyan, was under Talha bin Ubaid Allah, and Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah was under the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Her sister was a relative of the daughter of Abi Umayyah, the daughter of Talha bin Ubayd Allah, and she bore him Maryam bint Talha.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5596 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5597","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Al-Hasan bin Hammad Al-Warraq told us, Al-Muharbi, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, sat Talha on the Day of the Camel and wiped the dirt off his head, then He turned to Al-Hasan bin Ali and said: “I wish I had died thirty years before this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5597 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5598","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan the butcher on Al-Safa told me, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, Musa ibn Ismail told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, said on the Day of the Camel: When he saw the dead and the heads falling: “O Hassan, what good can one hope for after this?” He said: “I forbade you from this before we got into it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5598 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5599","I heard Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Amr Al-Jurashi, saying: I heard Yahya bin Yahya, saying: I heard Sufyan bin Uyaynah says: I asked Amr bin Dinar: O Abu Muhammad, did Talha and Al-Zubayr pledge allegiance to Ali? He said: Hassan bin Muhammad told me - and I have never seen anyone more knowledgeable than him - “that they went up to him and pledged allegiance to him while he was in an upper room, then they came down.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5599 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5600","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Azhari told me, Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Ghallabi told us, Al-Abbas bin Bakkar told us, Suhail bin Abi told us Suhail Al-Tamimi, on the authority of his father, said: Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, passed by Talha bin Ubaid Allah while he was being killed, and he stopped by him and said: “ This, by God, is as the poet said:
 [Long Sea]
 A boy whose wealth brought him close to his friend...when he became wealthy and poverty kept him far away.
 “It was as if a chandelier was stuck in his forehead... and there was hair on one cheek and the full moon on the other.”"
"5601","Ali bin Al-Mu’mal bin Al-Hasan bin Isa told us, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Jandal bin Waqiq told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Mazni told us, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Ansari, on the authority of Thawr bin Majza’ah, said: I passed by Talha bin Ubaid Allah on the Day of the Camel and he was paralyzed at the last breath, so I stopped Then he raised his head and said: I see the face of a man as if it were the moon. Who are you? So I said: From the companions of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali. He said: Extend your hand and I will pledge allegiance to you. So I extended my hand and he pledged allegiance to me, and his soul was relieved, so I came to Ali. So I told him what Talha had said, and he said: “God is the greatest, God is the greatest. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth. God refused to let Talha enter Paradise.” Except that I pledged allegiance to his neck.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5601 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5602","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abbad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr Ibn Al-Awwam, who said: It was upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of Uhud, Daraan got up to the rock but was unable to do so, so Talha sat underneath him until he sat on the rock. Al-Zubayr said: So I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Talha made it obligatory.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5602 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5603","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Talha made it obligatory.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"5604","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ibrahim bin al-Mundhir al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Talha told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, that Talha slaughtered camels and dug a well on the day of Dhul-Qard, so he fed them and gave them drink. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Talha al-Fayyad.” So he was named Talha al-Fayyad. It is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5604 - True"
"5605","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Sulayman bin Isa bin Musa bin Talha told us. Ibn Ubayd Allah, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of Musa Ibn Talha, on the authority of his father, Talha Ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me On the day of Uhud he greeted Talha al-Khair, on the Battle of the Tribe Talha al-Fayyad, and on the day of Hunayn Talha al-Jawaad.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5605 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5606","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Abu Shaybah. Ibrahim bin Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, a woman of Muhammad bin Talha narrated to me, She said: When Muhammad bin Talha was born, we brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What did you name him?” So we said: Muhammad, and he said: “This is my name and his nickname is Abu Al-Qasim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5606 - Abu Shaybah is wah"
"5607","Abu Bakr ibn Balawayh told me, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi told me, he said: I heard Musaab al-Zubayri say: “Muhammad ibn Talha ibn The servants of God were his mother: Hamnah the daughter of Jahsh.”"
"5608","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told me, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Bashar bin Musa told us, Al-Haatibi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Muhammad Ibn Hatib said: When we finished fighting the camel, Ali, Al-Hussein Ibn Ali, Ammar Ibn Yasir, Sa’sa’a Ibn Suhan, and Al-Ashtar rose up. And Muhammad bin Abi Bakr was going around looking for the dead, so Al-Hasan bin Ali saw a dead man with a blow on his face, so he put him on his back and said: “I To God we belong, and to Him we shall return. The Quraysh fled, by God.” Then his father said to him: “What is it, my son?” He said: “Muhammad bin Talha,” and he said: “To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return, if what I taught was to a righteous young man,” then he sat down, depressed and sad."
"5609","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Muhammad bin Al-Dahhak bin Othman Al-Hazami, on the authority of his father, he and Muhammad bin Talha were with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them, and Ali forbade He killed him, and said: “Whoever sees the one with the black robe, let him not kill him - meaning Muhammad -.” Then Muhammad said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On that day: O mother, what do you command me? She said: “I think that you should be like the best of the sons of Adam, that your hand be restrained.” So he restrained his hand and a man from Banu Asad ibn Khuzaymah, called Talha, killed him. Ibn Mudlij from Bani Munqidh Ibn Tarif, and it is said: Shaddad Ibn Muawiyah Al-Absi killed him, and it is said: Rather, Issam Ibn Mas’ar Al-Basri killed him. There are many hadiths about him, which say about his killing:
 [Long Sea]
 And his stature is disheveled with the signs of his Lord... he is little harmless in what the people see as a Muslim.
 I struck him with the spear from under his uniform...and he fell down, crushed by the hands and mouth.
 I pricked his shirt with my teeth... and turned it away from the back of a tattooed side.
 You crucified him in the drive of the horse... like the animal of Kizam in front of the saw.
 Ham reminds me of when I stabbed him...so please recite Ham before proceeding.
 There is a sin on anyone else, unless he is not a follower of Ali... and whoever does not follow the truth is wronged.
 He said: Then he said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, when he saw him struck down: “This man struck him in the head.”"
"5610","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman al-Wasiti told us, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha, my uncle Issa bin Talha told me, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, who said: He said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him: I was the first to So he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with him was Talha bin Ubayd Allah. Suddenly, Talha was overcome by cold, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I resemble a wetsuit from him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “You have to be with your companion.” So we left him and came to him, and behold, his forgiveness was granted. It stuck to his cheeks, and between him and the East there is a man who is closest to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So, he is Abu Ubaidah bin So I went to remove the wound, and Abu Ubaidah said: I ask you by God, O Abu Bakr, have you not left me? So I left it, and he pulled it, and Abu Ubaidah’s ring was removed. He said: So I went to remove the other ring, and Abu Ubaidah said to me something like: That's when he pulled out the other ring, then pulled out Abu Ubaidah's other thania, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for your companion... “It made Talha obligatory or obligatory.” It is authentic according to Muslim’s condition, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5610 - No, by God"
"5611","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ishaq bin Yahya told me, about Issa bin Talha bin Ubayd Allah said: I entered upon the Mother of the Believers and Aisha bint Talha and she was saying to her mother Asmaa: I am better than you. And my father is better than your father. He said: Then her mother insulted her and said: You are better than me. Then the Mother of the Believers Aisha said: Shall I not judge between you? She said: Yes, she said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Abu Bakr, you are freed.” God is from the Fire.” She said: From that day on, he was called Ateeq, and he had not been called Ateeq before that. She said: Then Talha bin Ubayd Allah entered and said: “You, O Talha, are among those who have died.” It is authentic according to Muslim’s conditions, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5611 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5612","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, with Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, al-Salt bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Abi Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wants to look at a martyr walking on the face of the earth Let him look at Talha bin Ubayd Allah.” Al-Salt bin Dinar was the only one to mention it, and it is not a requirement of this book.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5612 - Al-Salt Wah"
"5613","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi narrated to us, narrated to us Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Habiba, Talha’s client, said: I entered upon Ali with Omar bin Talha after he had finished with the companions of the camel. He said: So he welcomed him and treated him with kindness. He said: “I hope that God will make me and your father among those. God Almighty said: {And We removed from their breasts what He set us as brothers on beds facing each other} [Al-Hijr: 47] “And he said: “O my nephew, how is so-and-so, how is so-and-so?” He said: And he asked him about the mothers of his father’s children. He said: Then he said: “We did not seize your lands this year except for fear that he would plunder them.” People, O so-and-so, go with him to Banu Qurayza and order him to give him his produce this year and give him his land.” Two men sitting together said On one side, one of them was Al-Harith Al-A'awd: God is more just than that, that we should kill them and have them be our brothers in Paradise. He said: “A people far away.” The earth of God and crush it, then who is he? It was not me and Talhah, my nephew. If you have a need, come to us.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5613 - True"
"5614","Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Balkhi told me about Baghdad from the origin of his book. Abu Ismail Muhammad ibn Ismail told us Al-Tirmidhi, Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Sulayman bin Isa bin Musa bin Talha bin Ubaidullah Al-Qurashi told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of Musa Bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, proposed to Umm Aban bint Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams. She refused, and it was said to her: Why? She said: If he enters, he enters with might, and if he leaves, he leaves with might. The matter of his hereafter has distracted him from the matter of his world, as if he were looking at His Lord with his eyes, then Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam proposed to him, but she refused, so she was told: Why? She said: It is not for his wife to mention it in her neck. Then Ali proposed to her, but she refused. It was said to her: Why? She said: His wife has nothing to do with him except to fulfill his needs, and he says: Kate and Kate, and he was and he was. Then Talha proposed to her and she said: Truly my husband. They said: How is that? She said: I know his creatures. If he enters, he enters laughing, and if he leaves, he exits smiling. If I ask, he gives, and if I remain silent, he begins, and if I work He gave thanks, and if I sinned, he forgave. When he had started with it, Ali said: “O Abu Muhammad, if you give me permission to speak to Umm Aban?” He said: Speak to her. He said: So he took the cup of straw and then said: “Peace be upon you, O dear soul.” She said: And peace be upon you. He said: “The Commander of the Faithful proposed to you, but you refused.” She said: That was it. He said: “And Al-Zubayr, the cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to you.” And one of his disciples, but you refused.” She said: And that was it. He said: “I and my relative from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to you, but you refused.” She said: And that was it. He said: “By God, you have married us with a good face and a generous hand, giving such and such.”"
"5615","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim Al-Harbi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, my grandmother Sa’da bint Awf Al-Muriya told me, she said: “Talhah came to me and I found him sad,” so I said: “What’s wrong with me, I see you so sad.” Face, do you doubt anything about our matter? He said: “No, by God, I have not liked anything about your business, and what a good companion you are, but I have accumulated money.” She said: “Then send it to your household.” And your people, so divide among them.” She said: “So he did, so I asked the treasurer: How much did he divide?” He said: “Four hundred thousand, and his earnings every day were a thousand dirhams.” He said: His name was Talha al-Fayyad.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5615 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5616","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya informed me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Omar bin Muhammad Al-Asadi told us, my father told us, we told him Salih bin Musa al-Talhi, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the war had ended, he was proud The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Talha was silent, and Samak bin Kharsha Abu Dujana was silent and did not speak, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “You saw me on the day of Uhud and there was no creature on earth near me except Gabriel on my right and Talha on my left.” A poem was said about that:
 [Long Sea]

 And the Talha of the Day of Shaab made Muhammad sad... for an hour that was distressing and distressing for him.
 He protected him with his palms from the spears and they were cut off... His fingers were cut off under the spears and they became paralyzed.
 He was the imam of the people after Muhammad... He established the millstones of Islam until they became stable."
"5617","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Hassan bin He remained steadfast in Talha and did not spare anyone:
 [The Laying Sea]
 He stood when the Prophet greeted, and when... all the servants turned away and were revealed.
 He defends himself from the attack of the Prophet... and the enemy has approached him and they have retreated.
 His face was covered in blood... for fear that it would be said that their revolt was compassionate."
"5618","Tell us correctly what Hassan bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, Ubaidullah bin Ahmed Al-Balkhi said in Baghdad, Abu Ismail told us. Al-Sulami, Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Isa bin Musa bin Talha told us, my father told me, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of his sister, Umm Ishaq bint Talha, who said: I heard my father saying, “I have been disgraced on the day of Sunday throughout my body, even in my memory.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5618 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"5619","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abdullah bin Aamer bin Rabi’ah, whose father had witnessed Badr, told me: “Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, used the Ibn Mad’un was in charge of Bahrain, and he was the maternal uncle of Hafsa and Abdullah Ibn Omar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5619 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5620","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Ayyub told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Qudamah bin Musa, on the authority of Aisha bint Qudamah, said: “Qudamah bin Mad’un died in the year thirty-six, and he was sixty-eight years old.” A year old, and he did not change his age.” Ibn Umar said: “He is Qudama bin Mad’un, and Qudama migrated to the land of Abyssinia for the second migration. Beneath it was Safiyya bint al-Khattab, the sister of Omar ibn al-Khattab, and he witnessed the front of Badr, Uhud, the trench and all the scenes along with it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5621","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, who said: The polytheists captured Hudhayfah and his father before Badr and wanted to kill them, so they attacked them. God's covenant and covenant not to help them, so they swore to them and they sent them. They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed them, saying: We have We swore to them, and if you wish, we could fight with you. He said: “We will fulfill their pledge to them, and we seek God’s help against them.”"
"5622","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Halimi informed us: I am Abu Al-Mujih, I am Abdan, I am Abdullah, I am Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He said Urwa, “Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman was one of the Banu Abs, and he was an ally among the Ansar. His father was killed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Uhud, the Muslims on that day made a mistake about him and considered him to be one of the polytheists, so Hudhayfah began saying: My father, my father. They did not understand him until they killed him, so he ordered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sacrificed.”"
"5623","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Hudhayfah bin Husayl bin Jabir bin Rabi’ah bin Amr bin Jarwa and Jarwa is Al-Yaman, the son of Hudhayfah, but he was called Al-Yaman because he He caused bloodshed among his people, so he fled to Medina and allied himself with Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and his people called him Al-Yaman because he was allied with Al-Yamaniyya. He witnessed Hudhayfah, his father Husayl, and his brother Safwan were Uhud. As for his father, some Muslims killed him on that day, and they thought he was one of the polytheists. So Hudhayfah gave his blood money to the Muslims in charity, and as for Hudhayfah, he witnessed his battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after Badr, and lived until The first caliphate of Ali, may God be pleased with him, was in the year thirty-six, and some of them claimed that he was in Al-Mada’in in the year thirty-five after the killing of Uthman. In forty nights.”"
"5624","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Ismail, Qutaibah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Hudhayfah died. In the year thirty-six, and it was said: He died forty days after Uthman."
"5625","Mukhlid ibn Ja`far al-Baqarhi informed me, and Muhammad ibn Jarir told us, he said: “This statement is wrong, and I suspect that its owner either did not He knows the time in which Uthman was killed, or he was not good at calculating it, and that is because there is no disagreement among all the scholars that Othman was killed in Dhul-Hijjah in the year thirty-five AH, and a group of them said: He was killed for the twelve nights that remained of his life. If Uthman was killed in Dhul-Hijjah and Hudhayfah lived for forty nights after him, then that will be in the year that follows.”"
"5626","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Musa told us, Saad bin Aws told us, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya said: When Hudhayfah was present at the time of death, and he had lived for forty nights after Uthman, he said to us: “I advise you to fear God and obey the Amir “The Believers, Ali bin Abi Talib”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5626 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5627","Abu Ishaq Al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Rabi’i bin Harash said: “A man came to Hudhayfah and said: O Abu Abdullah.”"
"5628","Abu Ishaq told us: I am Muhammad ibn Ishaq, I am Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, I am Jarir, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: When Hudhayfah was brought with his shroud, and it was attributed to Ibn Masoud, he said: A new shroud was brought, and he said: “What do you do with this, if it is “Your friend is righteous, God will change him, and if he is other than that, God will strike his face with it on the Day of Resurrection.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5628 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5629","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Mas’ar bin Kadam, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, on the authority of al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, on the authority of Abu Masoud al-Ansari, who said: Hudhayfah fainted at the beginning of the night, then He woke up and said: “What night is this?” I said: The highest magic. He said: “God forbid we seek refuge in Hell” two or three times, then he said: “Buy me two garments and shroud me in them, and do not go to extremes.” Ali, if your friend is satisfied with him, he will wear better than them, otherwise he will quickly rob them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5629 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5630","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, I am Israel, On the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Gabriel came to me He, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Indeed, Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “May God forgive you.” And to your mother, Hudhayfah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5630 - True"
"5631","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Sayrifi told us, Ali bin Abbas told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, and Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, was asked on the authority of Ibn Masoud, and he said: “He read the Qur’an.” Then he stopped at his doubts and made lawful what was lawful and made unlawful what was unlawful.” He was asked about Ammar and said: “A believer forgets, and when he is reminded, he is reminded.” And he was asked. On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “He was the most knowledgeable of people about the hypocrites,” and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"5632","As Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, I am Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid al-Hazzami, my father told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, said: “Khabab bin Al-Art bin Jandala bin Sa’d bin Khuzaimah bin Ka’b bin Sa’d is an ally of the Banu Zuhra, and it was said that he was the client of Banu Zuhra."
"5633","As Ibrahim bin Firas, the jurist in Mecca, told us, Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Yahya bin Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: “Khabab bin Al-Art was the mawla of Banu Zuhra, and it was said: the mawla of Thabit bin Umm Anmar.”"
"5634","As Ahmad bin Yaqoob Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Khabab bin Al-Art is a servant Thabit ibn Umm Anmar, and Thabit the client of Al-Akhnas ibn Shariq Al-Thaqafi, and it was said: Khabab the client of Utbah ibn Ghazwan.”"
"5635","As Ahmad bin Ali bin Al-Muqri told me, Abu Issa Al-Tirmidhi told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Yazid Al-Sada’i told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: “Khabab bin Al-Art is the client of Utbah bin Ghazwan,” and “the most correct of these sayings is the saying Al-Zuhri, the narration to him is authentic.”"
"5636","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I am Ismail bin Utbah. Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us. Muhammad bin Fudayl bin told us. Ghazwan, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Kurdous say: “Khabab bin Al-Art converted to Islam the sixth of six years, so it was one-sixth of Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5636 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5637","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara: I am Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz, Khaled bin Salem told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, On the authority of Waki` ibn al-Jarrah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Maadi Karib, he said: “Khabab ibn al-Art is nicknamed Abu Abdullah.”"
"5638","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa “in naming Whoever witnessed Badr said: Khabbab bin Al-Art.”"
"5639","Abu Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Azhari told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Abdullah al-Madini told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zuhri, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal He said: “Khabab bin Al-Art died in the year thirty-seven, and he was the first of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him, to be buried by Ali in Kufa. And he was the first to send blessings upon him after the return of the Commander of the Faithful from Siffin.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5639 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5640","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khorasani, Al-Adl, in Baghdad, told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, “on the authority of his father Khabab He was a servant of Banu Zuhra, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5640 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5641","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Talaq bin Ghannam Al-Nakhi told us, Muhammad bin Ikrimah, on the authority of his father, Abdullah bin Khabbab bin Al-Art told me, he said: People were burying their dead in Kufa until Khabbab came For them, and when he became heavy, he said to me: “O my son, bury me with the back, for if you buried me with the back, it would be said: A man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was buried.” Peace and blessings of God be upon him. When Khabab died, he was buried with the back. He was the first to be buried with the back, so people buried their dead with the back."
"5642","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Khabab bin Al-Art bin Jandala bin Saad bin Khuzaymah bin Ka'b bin Saad, from the Banu Sa'd bin Zayd Manat. It was reported that he was taken captive in Mecca. Umm Anmar bint Siba’ al-Khuza’i bought it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between Khabab and Jabr bin Atik, and he testified. Khabab visited Badr, Uhud, Khandaq, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Khabab died in the year thirty-seven in the year On that day, he was seventy-three years old.”"
"5643","Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ told us, Ibrahim bin Ahmad bin Omar Al-Waki’i told us, Hassan bin Ibrahim told us, Muhammad bin Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Khabab, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was He was lying under a tree, with his hand under his head, and I said: O Messenger of God, do you not pray to God for these people whom we feared would They turn us away from our religion, so he turned his face away from me three times. I told him all of this and he turned his face away from me. The third time he sat down and said: “O People, fear God and be patient. By God, if a man was one of the believers before you, then a saw would be placed on his head and he would be cut in two, and he would not recoil. About his religion, fear God, for God is your Conqueror and Maker.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5643 - True"
"5644","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Haritha bin Mudharib, on the authority of Khabab, who said: “I feared that he would take away our rewards with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what befell us after him.” “From this world.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5644 - True"
"5645","I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh saying: I heard Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah saying: I heard Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubairi says: “Ammar bin Yasser bin Aamer bin Malik bin Kinanah bin Qais bin Al-Husayn bin Al-Wathim bin Tha’labah bin Amr Bin Haritha bin Malik bin Anas bin Zaid”"
"5646","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ammar was Ibn Yasir, his father and his mother, the people of the House of Islam, and Banu Makhzum were torturing them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Patience, O The family of Yasser, your promise is Paradise.” He said: “The name of Ammar bin Yasser’s mother was Sumayyah bint Muslim bin Lakhm.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5646 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5647","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Muqri informed me, Abu Issa Muhammad ibn Issa al-Tirmidhi told me, Shuraih ibn Yunus told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali, who said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, said to Ammar: “O Abu Al-Yaqzan.”"
"5648","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abd al-Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Jabal, on the authority of Abu Ka’b al-Harithi, that he entered upon Uthman, may God be pleased with him, and a tall, bald man came in front of him. He had hairs on his head, so I said: Who is this? They said: “Ammar bin Yasser.”"
"5649","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah said: “I saw Ammar bin Yasser on the day of Siffin, a tall man with a spear in his hand.”"
"5650","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Al-Harith bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Kulayb bin Manfa’ah, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw Ammar bin Yasser in the sweeper, black and frizzy, and he was reciting this verse: {And among His signs is that He created you. of dust, then, behold, you are human beings spreading apart.” [Al-Rum: 20]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5650 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5651","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told me, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Shu’bah. On the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Salamah saying: I saw Ammar bin Yasser on the day of Siffin, a tall old man, taking a spear in his hand. And his hand was trembling, so he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have fought for this with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, three times, and this is the fourth time.” Then He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they beat us until we reach the level of the palms of Hajar, I would know that we are on the truth and they are on falsehood.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5651 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5652","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told me, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of my father Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming one of the allies of Banu Makhzum, Ammar bin Yasser, who witnessed Badr.”"
"5653","Abu Ja`far told us, Al-Miqdam bin Dawud Al-Ru’ayni told us, Khalid bin Nizar told us, on the authority of Omar bin Qais, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah. He said: “Abu Salamah and Umm Salamah emigrated, and Ammar bin Yasser went out with them, and he was an ally of them.”"
"5654","Muhammad ibn Yaqoub al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi told me, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`d al-Zuhri told me, Ya`qub ibn Ibrahim told us, on the authority of His father said: We have heard that Ammar bin Yasser said: “I was a relative of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was no one closer in age to him than me.”"
"5655","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told us, On the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina the first time he came to it, and Ammar bin Yasser said: “What is the matter with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace, “We must make a place for him. When he wakes up from what he says, he can take shade in it and pray in it.” So Ammar gathered stones and leveled it. Quba Mosque is the first mosque built, and Ammar built it"
"5656","Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak told us, Al-Hussein bin Abi Ma’shar told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abd The Most Gracious said: “The first to build a mosque and pray in it was Ammar bin Yasser.”"
"5657","Abu Abdullah bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, and Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Mukhurami narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aoun, who narrated to me Muhammad bin Salih, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, in naming those whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had brotherhood among them from among the immigrants and Ansar, they said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between Ammar bin Yasser and Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman.”
 Abdullah bin Jafar said: “If Hudhayfah did not witness Badr, then his conversion to Islam was ancient, and they all said: Ammar bin Yasser witnessed.” “Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Nafi’ told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: “I saw Ammar bin Yasser on the day of Al-Yamamah on a rock.” And he started shouting: O community of Muslims, are you fleeing from Paradise? I am Ammar bin Yasser. Are you fleeing from Paradise? I am Ammar bin Yasser, come to me, and I will look at his ear that has been cut off, and it is shaking, and he is fighting the hardest.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Abi Ubaidah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Lu’lu’a,Umm al-Hakam’s servant, daughter of Ammar bin Yasser, said: When was the day on which Ammar bin Yasser was killed while the banner was being carried by Abu Hashim. Ibn Utbah, and the companions of Ali, may God be pleased with him, were killed that day until it was afternoon, then Ammar Ibn Yasir came forward and saw Abu Hashim He offers it, and the sun has tended to set, and Ammar has a sacrifice of milk waiting for the setting of the sun to break his fast, so he said: When the sun set and he drank the sacrifice I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Your last provision from this world is a flow of milk.” He said: Then he approached and fought until he was killed, and he was Ibn Ninety-four years
 Ibn Umar said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, he said: Khuzaymah bin Thabit witnessed The camel did not draw a sword, and he witnessed Siffin and said: I will never go astray by killing Ammar, so I will see who will kill him, for I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “The transgressing group will kill you.” He said: When Ammar was killed, Khuzaimah said: Misguidance has come to him. Then he approached. The one who killed Ammar was Abu Ghadiya al-Muzani. He stabbed him with a spear and he fell, so he fought until he was killed. At that time, he was fighting when he was four years old. Ninety. When he fell, another man fell on him and hurt his head.So they began to quarrel, each of them saying: I killed him. Amr bin Al-Aas said: “By God, they will not quarrel except in Hell.” Amr said: By God, he is that, and by God, you know him, and I wish I had died twenty years before this.
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aoun, he said: Ammar came when he was ninety-one years old, and he was He was earlier in the country than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and three people came to him: Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani and Omar bin Al-Harith. Al-Khawlani, and Sharik bin Salamah, and they all came to him, and he said: “By God, if you had struck us until you reached the palms of Hijr, we would have known.” “I am upon the truth and you are upon falsehood,” so they all attacked him and killed him. Some people claimed that it was Uqba bin Amir who killed him, and it is said: Nay, Omar bin Al-Harith Al-Khawlani killed him. Ibn Omar said: “What is unanimously agreed upon regarding Ammar is that he was killed with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them both.” In Siffin in Safar in the year thirty-seven, when he was ninety-three years old, and he was buried there in Siffin."
"5658","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Rabi’ah bin Kulthum told us, My father told me, he said: I was by the reeds in the house of Abdul-Ala bin Abdullah bin Amer. The caller said: This is Abu Ghadiya. Al-Juhani asked for permission, and Abdul-Ala said: Bring him in. He was brought in wearing pieces of cloth, and suddenly there was a tall man, one of the men, as if he were not one of the men. This nation. When he sat down, he said: “We used to consider Ammar bin Yasser among our best.” He said: “By God, I was in the Quba Mosque when he was saying - He mentioned a word: “If I had found helpers against him, I would have trampled him until I killed him.” He said: “So when it was the day of Siffin, the first of the battalion came walking on foot.” Until he was between the two rows, he stabbed a man with a spear and struck him, so the one who had been forgiven retreated and struck him, and then he saw the head of Ammar bin Yasir,” he said: He says: A servant of ours: I have never seen a man more clearly misguided than him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5658 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5659","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-San’ani told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told me, I am Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, on the authority of his father, he told him, he said: When Ammar ibn Yasir was killed: Amr entered Ibn Hazm attacked Amr Ibn Al-Aas, and said: Ammar was killed, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The transgressing group will kill him.” So Amr got up in fear until he entered upon Muawiyah, and Muawiyah said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: Ammar bin Yasser was killed. He said: Ammar was killed, so what? Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The transgressing group will kill him.” So Muawiyah said to him: We killed him. He only killed him. Ali and his companions? They brought him until they threw him between our spears or, he said: our swords, “correctly according to their terms, and they did not take him out in this manner.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5659 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5660","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Ata’ bin Muslim Al-Halabi told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash He says: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami said: We witnessed Siffin, and when we met each other, these people would enter the other’s army, and the other would enter the army. These people, I saw four walking: Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, Abu Al-Awar Al-Sulami, Amr bin Al-Aas and his son, so I heard Abdullah Ibn Amr says to his father Amr: We have killed this man, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something about him: He said: Which man? He said: Ammar bin Yasser. Do you not remember the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built the mosque? We were carrying brick by brick, and Ammar was carrying For two daughters, for two daughters. Then he passed by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, carrying two daughters for two daughters, and you were among those present. He said: “As for you The transgressing group will kill you, and you are the people of Paradise.” Then Amr entered upon Muawiyah and said: We killed this man, and the Messenger of God said about him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, what he said, so he said: Be silent, for by God you are still passing your urine. We killed him. Ali and his companions killed him. They came. with it until they threw it among us
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5660 - As you can see, it is an error"
"5661","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that two men came to Amr bin Al-Aas, disputing over Ammar's blood. Ibn Yasir and plundered him, so Amr said: Leave him alone, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, make the Quraysh passionate about Ammar. He killed Ammar and robbed him in the Fire.” Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak was the only one to mention it, and he is trustworthy and trustworthy, on the authority of Mu’tamir, on the authority of his father. If it is preserved, then it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “But the people narrated it, on the authority of Mu’tamir, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5661 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5662","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: Ammar bin Yasser asked permission to go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was with him, and he said: “Give permission to him.” When he entered, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Welcome to the perfumed and perfumed one.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5662 - True"
"5663","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahwi told us in Baghdad, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir told us, Qubaisah ibn Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha bin Mudarib, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, wrote to us: “Indeed, I have sent Ammar bin Yasser to you. A prince, and Abdullah bin Masoud, a teacher and a minister, and they were among the nobles among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the people of Badr, so listen, and they I have appointed Ibn Masoud over your Bayt al-Malik, so listen and learn from them and imitate them. I have given you preference to Abdullah over myself.” Sahih subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5663 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5664","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi and Muhammad bin Musa Al-Saydalani told me, saying: Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb and Ya’qub Al-Dawraqi told us, They said: Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar bin Muawiyah al-Dahni, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Ibn Sumayyah was never offered two matters without taking the more appropriate of them.” It is true on the condition of the two Sheikhs if it is Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad heard it from Abdullah bin Masoud, but they did not narrate it. “And it has a continuation from the hadith of Aisha, may God be pleased with her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5664 - True"
"5665","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Abdul Aziz bin Siyah told us, On the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ammar was not given a choice between two things.” Unless he chose the more guided of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5665 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5666","Ibrahim bin Asmah, Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, about Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Ammar and his family while they were being tortured, so he said: “Give good news to the family of Ammar and the family of Yasser. “Then your promise is Paradise” is true according to the condition of a Muslim, and they did not expel him from it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5666 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5667","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, Salamah bin told me Kuhail, I heard Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Ashtar, on the authority of Khalid bin al-Walid, who said: There was something between me and Ammar. So I complained about him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever reviles Ammar will be reviled by God, and whoever is hostile to Ammar.” “May God bring him back.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5667 - True"
"5668","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Abdullah told us. Bin Wahb, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, I heard Ammar bin Yasser, in Siffin, on the day he was killed, and he He calls out: “Paradise has been brought close to me, and I have married the beautiful fair-eyed. Today we meet our beloved Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who has made a covenant with me that another has added to you from “This world is a stream of milk.” It is true according to their condition, but they did not produce it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5668 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5669","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Muhammad bin Kathir told us, They said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, that Ammar bin Yasir was brought a drink of milk, and he laughed, and it was said To him: What makes you laugh? He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The last drink I drink when I die is this.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5669 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5670","Muhammad bin Salih told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of al-Ashtar, who said: I heard Khalid Ibn al-Walid saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me In secret, Ammar bin Yasser was with me. We attacked people, among them the people of a household, who had mentioned Islam. Ammar said: These people have united, but they did not She paid attention to what he said, and what happened to them happened to people. He said: Then Ammar made a promise to me that if I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. When he saw that he did not support him, he turned away with tears in his eyes. He said: So he called me and said: “O Khaled.” Do not revile Ammar, for whoever reviles Ammar will be reviled by God, and whoever hates Ammar will be hated by God, and whoever despises Ammar will be reviled by God,” he said. Khaled: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of God, for by God, nothing prevented me from answering him except that you made him foolish. Khaled said: “There is nothing I fear more than “Ammar bin Yasser made fools of me at that time.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it. This is how it was narrated by Masoud bin Saad Al-Jufi’i and Muhammad bin Fudayl. Ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Ubayd Allah Al-Nakhai, as for the hadith of Masoud Ibn Saad"
"5671","So Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Issa Al-Dahqan told us, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Jizzi told us, Abu Ghassan Malik bin told us. Ismail, Masoud bin Saad told us, and as for the hadith of Muhammad bin Fudayl"
"5672","So Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mil bin Al-Hasan told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan. Ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of al-Ashtar, on the authority of Khalid Ibn al-Walid, he said: A messenger sent me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We attacked them, and we defeated them. Ammar bin Yasser said: They hid themselves from us by claiming monotheism, so I did not pay attention to them. His saying, and he mentioned the hadith similarly. Al-Hakim said: “I presented the hadith of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Ashtar, that he is one of the members of Abu Dawud, and he found it from the hadith of Amr ibn Marzuq, on the authority of division
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5670 - True"
"5673","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, I am Shu’bah, Salamah bin told me Kuhail, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Ashtar, on the authority of Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: It happened between me and Ammar. Ibn Yasir spoke, so I complained about him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Khaled, who can insult Ammar? God will revile him, and whoever is hostile to Ammar, God will be hostile to him, and whoever despises Ammar, God will despise him.” Narrated by Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, Shu’bah differed in its chain of transmission, for he said: On the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Khaled ibn al-Walid."
"5674","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin told us Hawshab, Salama bin Kuhail told me, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, he said: There was a conversation between me and Ammar bin Yasser, so I spoke harshly to him. So Ammar went off to complain about me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Khaled came complaining about me, so he began to be harsh to him, and he only increased his harshness, and the Prophet prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. So Ammar cried and said: O Messenger of God, don’t you see him? He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head and said: “Whoever is hostile to Ammar, God will hate him, and whoever hates Ammar, God will hate him.” Khaled said: “So I went out, and there was nothing dearer to me than the satisfaction of Ammar, so I met him as I was satisfied.” The hadith of Al-Awwam bin Al-Hawshab. This hadith is authentic in its chain of transmission, on the condition that it The two sheikhs because of their agreement regarding Al-Awwam bin Hawshab and Alqamah that Shu’bah had better memory than him, as he said: On the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Ashtar, “and the two chains of narration are authentic.”"
"5675","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhail told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Imran ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of al-Ashtar, he said: Khalid ibn al-Walid started with us without me asking him. He said: It did not happen to me. Never was he more important to me than Ammar, when the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with some of his companions and appointed me over them. There was Ammar among the people, so we encountered a people among whom was a Muslim family. Ammar and some Muslims spoke to me about them and said: Let Their way, I said: No, by God, I will not do it until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sees them and gives his opinion of them. Ammar became angry with me, so when I came and asked permission to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was asking me to inform me and I was speaking to him. So Ammar asked for permission, so he gave him permission and Ammar entered. He said: O Messenger of God, have you not seen Khalid doing such and such and doing that? So I said: O Messenger of God, by God, had it not been for your council, Ibn Somaya, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ammar, come out.” So Ammar came out crying and saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not help me. He greeted Khaled, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Didn’t you answer the man?” I said: The only thing preventing me from answering him was to humiliate him, so he became angry. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, whoever hates Ammar will be hated by God, and whoever reviles Ammar will be reviled by God, and whoever despises Ammar will be reviled by God.” God despises him.” So I left the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I continued to ask Ammar until he asked forgiveness for me."
"5676","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Usama told us, Muslim Abu Abdullah Al-A'war, on the authority of Habbat Al-Arni, said: We entered with Abu Masoud Al-Ansari to Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, asking him about the temptations. He said: Go with the Book of God wherever it goes, and look at the group in which Ibn Sumayyah is, and follow it, for he goes with the Book of God wherever it goes. He said: So we said to him: Who is Ibn Sumayyah? He said: Ammar, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to him: “You will not die until the transgressing group kills you, drinking the drink of sacrifice.” “It will be the last of your sustenance from this world.” This is a high, authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5676 - True"
"5677","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh al-Anbari told us, Ubayy told us, Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, said: Amr ibn Al-Aas said: “I hope that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die on the day he died while loving man, never to enter Hell.” They said: “We used to see him loving you, seeking your help, and using you.” He said: “And God knows best about my love, but It is enough for him, as we saw him loving a man. He said: Who is that? He said: “Ammar bin Yasser”: They said: That is your murderer on the day of Siffin. Al-Hasan heard it from Amr bin Al-Aas, and he learned it in Basra without a doubt.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5677 - But it was sent"
"5678","Abu Amr Uthman bin Muhammad al-Daqqaq told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Abu al-Walid told us, about Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah say: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of Siffin, an old man who had become very tired. The spear was in his hand, and his hand was trembling. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with this three times. And this is the fourth, “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they had struck us until they reached the palms of desert with us, we would have known that our reconciler is on the truth, and that they are on the right.” Misguidance.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"5679","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yahya bin Halim told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khaythamah ibn Abi Sabrah al-Ja’fi, who said: I came to Medina and asked God to facilitate a good companion for me. So Abu Hurairah explained it to me and said to me: “Who are you from?” So I said: From the land of Kufa I came to seek knowledge and goodness. He said: “Is there not among you Saad bin Malik who answered the call, and Abdullah bin Masoud? The companion of the purification of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his sandals, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, the companion of the secrets of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ammar ibn Yasir. The one whom God protected from Satan on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Salman, the author of the two books? Qatada said: “And the two Books are the Gospel and the Criterion.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5679 - The hadith is authentic"
"5680","Abu Ali al-Hafiz and Harun bin Ahmad al-Jurjani told me, saying: Ismail told us, Ali bin al-Hasan bin Sulaym al-Hafiz told us. Al-Asbahani, Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr Ibn Sharhabeel, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Ammar was filled with faith to the point of his being.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs: If Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub memorized it, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, “then Abu Ali, the memorizer, told me, he said: We broke Muhammad.” Ibn Ishaq, Abu Musa told us, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, on the authority of a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5680 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5681","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Fudayl bin Marzuq told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, that he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was feeling unwell, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Shall I not teach you a ruqyah with which Gabriel performed the ruqyah for me?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Teach him, ‘In the name of God, I perform ruqyah for you, and God will heal you from every disease that harms you. Take it and let it comfort you.’” Sahih, subject to one condition. Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5681 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5682","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Ismail bin Mujalid, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Hammam ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and nothing was with him except Five slaves, two wives, and Abu Bakr “according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.”"
"5683","Abd al-Baqi ibn Qa’i al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawar al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa’id ibn Sulaiman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd narrated to us. Al-Rahman bin Abdul-Malik bin Abjar, my father told me, on the authority of Wasil bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Ammar bin Yasser addressed us and informed us He summarized, so we said: O Abu Al-Yaqzan, you have conveyed the message and stated it concisely. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, it is long. Prayer and shortening the sermon is a good thing from the jurisprudence of a man, so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. In this context """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5683 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5684","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Muhammad bin Aban al-Wasiti told us, Abu Shihab told us Al-Hannat, Amr bin Qais and Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, that a man had sexual intercourse with Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she was with Ali, may God be pleased with him, and Ammar bin Yasser said to him: “Be silent, shameful and shameful. Will you harm the beloved of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him?” “Sahih” according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5684 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5685","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Muzaki informed me of Marw, Abd al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Khalid, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha She said: “Look at Ammar bin Yasir, for he will die on his Fitrah unless a lapse of pride overtakes him.” Authentic chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5685 - True"
"5686","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Hushi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, I am Waki’, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: Abdullah said: “I do not know of anyone who went out in sedition, seeking the face of God Almighty and the Hereafter.” Except for Ammar bin Yasir” with an authentic chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5686 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5687","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Asim ibn Bilal al-Dhabi, the martyr, told me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Razin told me, Ali bin Khashram told us, Abu Mukhlid Ata bin Muslim told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, he said: We witnessed Siffin with... Ali, may God be pleased with him, and we have appointed two men, so if one of the people is negligent he attacks them, and he does not return until his sword is stained with blood, so he said: Excuse me, by God, I had not returned until my sword had fallen upon me. He said: And I saw Ammar and Hashim bin Utbah running between the two rows. Ammar said: “O This Hashem, by God, they will change his command and let his soldiers down.” Then he said: “O Hashim,” Paradise is under the stars. Today he threw “Beloved Muhammad and his party, O Hashem, one-eyed, and there is no good in one-eyed man who does not overcome misery.” He said: Hashem shook the flag and said:
 [The sea of rage]

 A one-eyed man who wants a place for his family... He has dealt with life until he is bored
 It must fail or fail,
 He said: Then he went to a valley in one of the valleys of Siffin. He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, and I saw the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, following Ammar as if he were They have knowledge
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5687 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5688","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad told us Bin Omar, he said: “Abdullah bin Budayl bin Warqa’ bin Abdul-Uzza bin Rabi’a bin Jazi bin Amer bin Mazen bin Adi bin Amr Ibn Rabi’ah witnessed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the conquest of Mecca, Hunayn, and Tabuk, and was killed with Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the day of Siffin."
"5689","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ubadah bin Ziyadah Al-Asadi told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Azrami, Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Yazid bin Rukana, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: I saw Abu Amra al-Ansari on the day of Siffin, and he was Badriyya Aqbiyya Ahady, and he was fasting and twisting from thirst. And he was saying to a servant of his: “Woe to you! He sprayed me and the boy sprinkled him.” Then he shot an arrow and it moved weakly until he shot three arrows, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God and whether it reaches or falls short, that will be one of the arrows that will give him light on the Day of Resurrection.” Resurrection.” He was killed before sunset."
"5690","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Utbah Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Qabisa bin Uqba, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, on the authority of Hashim bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The Muslims will appear on the Arabian Peninsula, and the Muslims will appear against Persia, and the Muslims will appear.” The Muslims will defeat the Romans, and the Muslims will prevail against the one-eyed Antichrist.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5690 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5691","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman al-Jahshi, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who said: “He was the standard-bearer of Ali ibn Abi Talib on the day of Siffin.” Hashim bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas, and he is the one who says:
 [The sea of rage]
 A one-eyed man who wants a place for his family... He dealt with life until he became bored,
 ""It must either fail or fail."""
"5692","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Al-Walid bin Shuja’ Al-Sakouni told us, Khalid bin Hayyan told us, Ja’far told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Zufar bin Al-Harith, said: I was Muawiyah’s messenger to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, in the Battle of Siffin, and she said Aisha: “Who among the people was killed?” So I said: Ammar bin Yasser. Aisha said: “That leader whose religion people follow.” She said: And who? I said: Hashim bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas, the one-eyed man. She said: “That is a man whose animal almost slipped.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5692 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5693","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Battah told me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Rusta al-Isbahani told me, Dawud ibn Sulaiman al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad bin Omar said: As for “Hashim the one-eyed, he is the son of Utbah bin Abi Waqqas who converted to Islam on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he was one-eyed, so he was cut off.” He was appointed on the day of Yarmouk, and he was the son of my brother Saad bin Abi Waqqas. He witnessed Siffin with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and he was at that time. On the foot"
"5694","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “And Khuzaymah bin Thabit bin Al-Fakih bin Tha’labah bin Sa’idah bin Amir bin Ghayyan bin Amir bin Khatma bin Jashm, and he is of The two testimonies are called Abu Amara, the bearer of the banner of the Khutmah on the day of the conquest.”"
"5695","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Khuzaimah bin Thabit bin Al-Fakih bin Tha’labah bin Sa’idah bin Amir bin Ghayyan bin Amir bin Khatma, and he is the one with two testimonies. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave his testimony with the testimony of two men.” And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, reported that he saw in a dream as if he had prostrated on The forehead of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay with him until he prostrated on his forehead. Ibn Ishaq said: He was killed with Ali. May God be pleased with him in Siffin after the killing of Ammar bin Yasser."
"5696","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq said: “Khuzaimah ibn Thabit, the one with two testimonies, testified with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, in Siffin and was killed on that day in the year seven.” Thirty years after the Hijra, and Khuzaymah had two brothers, one of whom was called Dahraj, and the other was called Abdullah.”"
"5697","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Bakkar told us, Abu Ma’shar Al-Madani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit said: My grandfather was sufficient with his weapons on the Day of Jamal and on the Day of Siffin until Ammar bin Yasir was killed. When he was killed Ammar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ammar will be killed by the transgressing group.” He said: So he drew his sword and fought until he was killed.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5697 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5698","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Suhayb bin Sinan Ibn Malik Ibn Abd Amr Ibn Aqeel Ibn Amir, and his father Sinan Ibn Malik was a worker for Chosroes on the Ublāh, and their homes were In the land of Mosul, in a village on the banks of the Euphrates, next to Al-Jazira and Mosul, the Romans raided that area, and Suhaib, who was a boy, was taken captive. Young, his uncle said:
 [The sea of rage]
 I praise God, the boy Nimri... the Romans and my family insulted him because of the Prophet.
 - He said: And the Prophet is the name of the village in which his people were -, So Suhayb grew up in the Romans, and a dog bought him from them, then she brought him to Mecca. So Abdullah bin Jud’an Al-Taymi bought him, freed him, and lived with him in Mecca until Abdullah bin Jud’an died and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent. “And he greeted”
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Abi Ubaidah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Ammar bin Yasser said: “I met Suhayb bin Sinan at the door of a house.” Al-Arqam, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said to him: What do you want? He said to me: What do you want? So I said: I wanted to enter upon Muhammad, and hear his words. He said: And I want that, so we entered upon him, and he proposed to us Islam, so we accepted Islam, then We stayed like that all day until evening, then we went out while we were hidden.
 Ibn Omar said: Asim bin Suwayd from Banu Amr bin Awf told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, who said: “Another came.” The people in the migration to Medina were Ali and Suhaib bin Sinan, and that was in the middle of Rabi’ al-Awwal, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Quba did not Yaram after that, and Suhaib witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the sights with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, according to the words of all of them.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abu Hudhayfah - a man from Suhayb’s descendants - told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “Suhayfah died in Shawwal in the year thirty-eight He was seventy years old in Medina, and was buried in Al-Baqi’. His nickname was Abu Yahya.”"
"5699","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr, he said: “Suhayb is nicknamed Abu Yahya, who is Suhaib bin Sinan al-Nimari, from Nimr bin Qasit, and he was captive and fell into the land of the Romans. It was said: “Suhayb al-Rum reached He was seventy years old, and he used to dye his hair with henna. He died in Medina in Shawwal in the year thirty-eight, and was buried in Al-Baqi’."
"5700","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: When Suhaib left as an immigrant, the people of Mecca followed him, so he folded his quiver and took out forty arrows from it, and said: “You will not reach me until I put an arrow in each of you, and then I will go to the sword, and you will know that I am a man, and I have left behind two Qurans in Mecca.” They are yours.”
 He said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas - and the like -, and it was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {And among the people is he who does evil. himself, seeking the pleasure of God.} Then when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him, he said: “Abu Yahya made a profit from the sale.” He said: And he recited to him the verse: “It is true.” On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5700 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5701","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Omari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, My father told me, Muhammad bin Amr told us, Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said to Suhaib: What I found that you were indifferent to Islam except three things: You treated Abu Yahya in private, and God Almighty said: “We had not given him any name before” [Maryam: 7]. He said: Yes, he said: And you do not keep anything without spending it. He said: Yes, he said: And you will be called to Nimr bin Qasit, and you are one of the emigrants. Among those whom God has bestowed upon him, Suhaib said: As for the saying: “I have given the nickname Abu Yahya, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called me Abu Yahya,” and as for the saying: “I do not withhold anything without spending it,” God Almighty says: “And whatever thing you spend, He will replace it with it.” And He is the Best of Providers” [Saba: 39]. As for the saying: I am being called to Nimr bin Qasit, the Arabs take one another captive, so a group of people took me captive. After I knew my family and my birth, the Arabs sold me for the black of Kufa, so I took their language, and if I were of dung, I would not belong to anyone but it. He said: You are right
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5701 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5702","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Hamid bin Ziyad bin Saifi told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Suhaib Ibn Sinan said: “I did not put the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, between me and the enemy, and I was only to his right, in front of him, or to his left.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5702 - True"
"5703","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulayman Al-Wasiti told us, Abd told us Allah bin Al-Mubarak, Abd al-Hamid bin Saifi, a descendant of Suhaib, told me on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Suhaib, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) was eating dates, so I started to eat some dates with ash in my eyes, so he said: “Do you eat dates with ash in your eyes?” So I said: I am only eating on my healthy part, which does not have ulcers. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5703 - True"
"5704","Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Matar, the ascetic justice, told me, and I asked him. Abu Habib al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah Al-Talhi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Musa bin Talha bin told us. Ubayd Allah, Abu Hudhayfah Al-Husayn ibn Hudhayfah ibn Suhayb told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Suhayf, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said, regarding the first immigrants: “They are the forerunners, the intercessors, the guides to their Lord, Blessed and Most High, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul. Indeed, they will come.” On the Day of Resurrection, weapons will be on their shoulders, and they will knock on the door of Paradise, and the keepers will say to them: Who are you? They say: We are the immigrants. Then the treasury says to them: Have you been held accountable? Then they would kneel down, spread what was on their sleeves, and raise their hands to the sky, and say: O Lord, and what shall we hold accountable? We went out and left behind our family, money, and children. God represents to them wings of gold decorated with aquamarines and rubies, and they fly. Until they enter Paradise, that is His saying: {And they say: Praise be to God who has removed from us sorrow} [Fatir: 34] The verse refers to {the lost} [Fatir: 35] “He said Abu Hudhayfah: Hudhayfah said: Saifi said: Suhayb said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They will have their stations in Paradise more knowledgeable than them.” With their homes in this world.” Strange chain of transmission and text. “I mentioned it in the virtues of Suhaib because he was one of the first immigrants, and the narrator of the hadith Its aftermath, and the hadith is for its companions, and we did not write it except on the authority of our ascetic sheikh Abi Amr, may God have mercy on him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5704 - Rather, it is a lie and its chain of transmission is dark"
"5705","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi informed us, Abu al-Zinba’ Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri told us, Yusuf ibn Adi, Yusuf bin Muhammad bin Yazid bin Saifi bin Suhaib narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Suhaib, who said: “I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “peace and blessings of God be upon him before it was revealed to him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5705 - True"
"5706","Abu Abbas Ismail bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Mikaal told us: I am Abdan Al-Ahwazi, Zayd bin Al-Harish told us, Yaqoub told us Ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, Husayn Ibn Hudhayfah Ibn Saifi Ibn Suhayb told us, my father and my paternal uncle told me, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Suhayb, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I showed the place of your migration a marshland before me, free. Either it will be migration or it will be Yathrib.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Medina, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, went out with him, and I was about to go out with him. Then two young men from Quraysh stopped me, so I started to stand up that night and not sit down, and they said: God has distracted you with his stomach, and I was not complaining, so they got up. Some of them caught up with me after I was sending mail to send me back, so I said to them: Would you like me to give you a few ounces of gold and let you go on my way, and follow me? So you followed them to Mecca? So I said to them: Dig under the sill of the door, for beneath it are the stones, and go to such-and-such person and take the two stones. I went out until I came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before he turned from it - meaning Quba - and when he saw me he said: “O Abu Yahya, he won the sale” three times, so I said: O Messenger of God, no one preceded me to you, and none told you except Gabriel, peace be upon him: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5706 - True"
"5707","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me, in Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Zayd bin Al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, regarding the words of God Almighty: {And among the people is he who sells himself seeking God’s pleasure} «It was revealed about Suhayb bin Sinan, And Abu Dharr, and the one who caught up with Suhayb on the road to Medina was Qunfud bin Amr bin Judaan.” Ibn Juraij said: Ikrimah, Ibn’s servant, claimed Abbas, “that Suhaib ransomed his family from Mecca with his money, then he left as an emigrant, and they overtook him on the road, so he gave them what was left of his money.”"
"5708","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Amr bin Al-Husayn told us Al-Uqaili, Fudayl bin Sulaiman Al-Numayri told us, Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mughith, on the authority of Ka’b al-Ahbar, Suhaib bin Sinan told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “O God, you are not a god.” We created it, and we did not create it with a Lord, nor did we have anyone before you to whom we could turn and warn you, and no one helped you in our creation so we share in you. Blessed are You and exalted.” Ka’b al-Ahbar said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to supplicate by it,” with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it."
"5709","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Hamid bin Ziyad bin Suhaib told us, my father told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Suhayb, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Do not hate Suhayb.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.”"
"5710","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, in Nishapur, Abu al-Zinba` told us, Yusuf bin Adi told us, Yusuf bin Muhammad bin Yazid told us Bin Saifi bin Suhaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Suhaib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Love Suhaib as a mother loves her child.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5710 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"5711","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Abdullah said: Suhaib was saying to us: “Come, let us tell you about our battles. As for us saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, no.” Al-Hakim: “Explanation of this hadith”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5711 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5712","What Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, Amr bin Dinar, ruler of the Al-Zubayr family, on the authority of Saifi bin Suhaib, who said: I said to Abu Suhaib: What is the matter with you that you do not narrate on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? What do your friends say? He said: That is, my son, I have heard as they heard, but what prevents me from speaking is that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever lies to me intentionally?” He was appointed on the Day of Resurrection to tie two ends of a ritual, but he will not tie it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5712 - Amr is weak"
"5713","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Aadmi al-Qari, in Baghdad, informed us, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: “When Umar, may God be pleased with him, was stabbed, he ordered Suhayb The master of Banu Jad’an was to lead the people in prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5713 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5714","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Abdoos bin Kamil told us, Abu Hayyan al-Zayyadi told us, Hisham al-Kalbi told us, he said: “Suhayb Ibn Sinan, an ally of Abdullah bin Jadaan al-Taymi.”"
"5715","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Amara bin Zazan told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There are four races: I race against the Arabs, Suhaib races through the Romans, Salman races the Persians, and Bilal races the Ethiopians.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5715 - Amara bin Zazan Wah"
"5716","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Mu’in saying: “Uwais Al-Qarni was killed.” In the hands of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, on the day of Siffin"
"5717","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila said: On the Day of Siffin, a caller from Muawiyah’s companions, Ali’s companions, called out: Is Uwais al-Qarni among you? They said: Yes, so he struck his animal until he entered with them, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The best of the followers is Uwais al-Qarni.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5717 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5718","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told me, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ruh al-Madaini told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad al-Aishi told me, he told me Ismail bin Amr Al-Bajli, on the authority of Hibban bin Ali Al-Anazi, on the authority of Saad bin Tarif, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabatah, who said: I witnessed Ali May God be pleased with him on the day of Siffin, and he said: “Who will pledge allegiance to me on death?” Or did he say: “On the fighting?” So ninety-nine people pledged allegiance to him. He said: “Where is the completion?” Where is the one I promised? He said: Then a man with a shaved head came, wearing a blanket of wool, and pledged his pledge of allegiance to death and killing. He said: It was said: This is Uwais al-Qarni, and he continued to do so. He fought in front of him until he was killed, may God be pleased with him. Al-Hakim said: “The narration was authentic about that on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him.” On his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5718 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"5719","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Asir ibn Jabir, who said: The Commander of the Faithful was Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. When the supplies of Yemen came to him, he asked them: Is Uwais bin Amir among you? Until Uwais came to him and said: You are Uwais bin Amir. He said: Yes. He said: From Murad. Then Qarn said: Yes. He said: You had leprosy, so you recovered. Of it, except for a place of a dirham. He said: Yes. He said: Do you have a mother? He said: Yes, Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Uwais bin Amir is coming against you with supplies from Yemen, from Murad and then from... There was a generation in which there was leprosy and he recovered from it, except for the place of a dirham. He had a mother with whom he was righteous. If he had sworn an oath to God, he would have fulfilled it. If you are able If he asks forgiveness for you, do it. He said: Then ask forgiveness for me. So he asked forgiveness for him. Then Omar said: Where do you want? He said: Kufa. He said: Shall I not write to its officials for you, so that they may seek good treatment of you? He said: No, because I love being in the ignorance of people. So when the next year a man from among their nobles performed Hajj, he asked Omar about Uwais: How? Did you leave him? He said: I left him with a shabby house and little possessions.He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Uwais bin Amir will come to you with supplies from the people of Yemen from Murad, then from Qarn.” He had leprosy and he recovered from it, except for the place of a dirham. He has a mother with whom he is righteous. If he had sworn an oath to God, he would have fulfilled it. If you are able to He asks forgiveness for you, so do it.” When the man came, he came to Uwais and said: Ask forgiveness for me. He said: You are the most recent of people to travel righteously, so ask forgiveness for me. He said: Did you meet Omar bin Al-Khattab? He said: Yes. He said: So he asked forgiveness for him. He said: Then the people noticed him and he went on his face. Asir said: So I covered him with a cloak, and when he saw it he was A human being said: Where did this Uwais come from? “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5719 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5720","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib Al-Dhabi told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Usir bin Jabir, who said: When the people of Yemen arrived, he made Omar, may God be pleased with him The comrades inquire and say: Is there anyone among you from a generation? Until a century came to him and said: Who are you? They said: A horn, so Omar lifted it with the reins or the reins of Uwais, so Omar handed it to him and identified it with the adjective, so Omar said to him: What is your name? He said: I am Uwais. He said: Did you have a mother? He said: Yes. He said: Do you have white hair? He said: Yes, I prayed to God Almighty, so take it away from me except the place of a dirham from my navel so that I may remember my Lord with it, so Omar said to him: Ask forgiveness for me. He said: You have the right to ask forgiveness for me. You are the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, the best of the followers is a man called Uwais al-Qarni. He has a mother, and he was afflicted with whiteness. He called on his Lord and He took it away from him, except for the place of a dirham in He said: So he asked forgiveness for him. He said: Then he entered into the depths of the people, and he did not know where he fell? He said: Then he came to Kufa, and we used to gather in a circle and remember God.He used to sit with us, and when he mentioned them, his conversation touched our hearts in a place where no other conversation takes place. So I lost him one day, so I said to someone who was sitting with us. Us: What did the man who was sitting next to us do? Perhaps he complained, and a man said: Who is he? So I said: Who is he? He said: That is Uwais Al-Qarni, so I directed him to his house, so I came to him and said: May God have mercy on you, where have you been? Why did you leave us? He said: I did not have a cloak, so he is the one who prevented me from coming to you. He said: So I threw my cloak to him, and he tossed it to me. He said: So I left him for an hour, then He said: If I had taken this garment of yours and put it on, and my people saw it on me, they said: Look at this hypocrite. He remained in the man’s mind until he deceived him. And he took his cloak, and I did not stay with it until he took it, so I said: Go so that I can hear what they say, so he put it on and we went out, so he passed by the gathering of his people. They said: Look at this hypocrite. He did not stop with the man until he deceived him and took his cloak. So I approached them and said: Are you not ashamed of why? Do you hurt him? By God, I offered it to him, but he refused to accept it. He said: Then delegations from the Arab tribes came to Omar, and the master of his people came among them. Then Omar bin Al-Khattab said to them: Is there anyone among you from a generation? And their master said to him: Yes,So he said to him: Do you know a man from the people of Qarn who is called Uwais because of such-and-such and such-and-such a thing? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, what do you remember about that or that? Omar said to him: Your mother has bereaved you. He caught him two or three times, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Indeed, a man is called Uwais. He is from such-and-such a century, and such-and-such is his cause.” When the man came, he did not He begins with someone before him, so he entered upon him and said: Ask forgiveness for me. Then he said: What do you think? He said: Omar said to me: Such and such. He said: I will not ask forgiveness from you until you grant me three. He said: What are they? He said: Do not bother me for what remains, and do not tell anyone about what Omar told you, and he forgot the third time.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5720 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5721","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Ziyad, the jurist in Al-Damghan, told us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, I am Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation, more From Rabia and Mudar.” Hisham said: Then Hawshab told me on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was Uwais Al-Qarni. Abu Bakr bin Ayyash said: So I said to a man From his people, Uwais: “How did this person achieve this?” He said: God gives it to whomever He wishes.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5721 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5722","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told me that it had passed, Abdullah bin Ali told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Sufyan Al-Thawri said: “Uwais Al-Qarni had a robe when he sat down and touched the ground, and he used to say: Oh God, I apologize to you for “Every liver is hungry, and my body is naked, and I have nothing but what is on my back and in my stomach.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5722 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5723","Abu Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, I am Yazid bin Yazid. Al-Bakri, Uwais Al-Qarni said: “Be in the command of God as if you had killed all the people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5723 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5724","Ahmad ibn Ziyad, the Damghani jurist, told us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, I am Ahmad ibn Yunus, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, a friend of ours told me. He said: A man from Murad came to Uwais al-Qarni, and he said: Peace be upon you. He said: “And upon you.” He said: How are you, Owais? He said: “Praise be to God.” He said: How is the time with you? He said: “Do not ask a man if it is evening and he does not think it will be morning, and if it is morning he does not think it will be evening, brother Murad, for death does not remain.” There is joy for a believer, brother Murad. The believer’s awareness of God’s rights leaves no silver or gold left for him. Brother Murad, the believer’s doing something God has not left a friend for him, and by God, indeed, We enjoin them to do what is right and forbid them from doing wrong, so they take us as enemies, and they find fault with that. Some of the sinners are helpers, to the point that, by God, they slander us with great crimes, and by God, that does not prevent me from speaking the truth.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5724 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5725","Ismail bin Ahmad Al-Jurjani told me, I am Abu Ya’la, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, Ataa Al-Khorasani told me: They mentioned Hajj, so they said to Uwais Al-Qarni: Did you not perform Hajj? He said: “No.” They said: Why? He said: “Then I remained silent.” Then one of them said: “I have a mount,” and another said: “I have expenses,” and another said: “I have a device.” So he accepted it from them and performed Hajj with it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5725 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5726","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim bin Abdullah bin Muawiyah Al-Sayyari, the sheikh of the people of Al-Haqiqiq in Khorasan, may God have mercy on him, informed us. He said: I Abu Al-Mawjih Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Mawjih Al-Fazari, I am Abdan bin Othman, I am Ubaid Allah bin Al-Shumayt bin Ajlan, on the authority of His father said that he heard Aslam Al-Ijli say: Abu Al-Dahhak Al-Jarmi told me, on the authority of Haram Ibn Hayyan Al-Abdi, who said: “I came to Kufa and did not I had no worries about it except Uwais Al-Qarni. I sought him out and asked about him, until I found him sitting alone on the shore of the Euphrates in the middle of the day. He performs ablution and washes his dress, so I recognized him by the adjective, and behold, he was a man of flesh, thick-skinned, hairy, with a shaved head - meaning he had no Jummah - a thick beard, wearing a cloak made of wool, and a robe of wool, without shoes, a big face, very majestic in appearance, so I greeted him, and he responded to me. He looked at me and said: May God protect you, man? So I extended my hand to him to shake his hand, but he refused to shake my hand, and said: And you, may God bless you. So I said: May God have mercy on you, Uwais, and forgive you. How are you? May God have mercy on you? Then I was choked by jealousy of my love for him and my tenderness for him when I saw his condition. I did not see until I cried and he cried.Then he said: And may God have mercy on you, Haram bin Hayyan, how are you, my brother? Who guided you to me? I said: God. He said: There is no god but God. Glory be to our Lord, if the promise of our Lord is to be fulfilled when He named me. By God, I had never seen him, nor had he seen me. Then I said: How did you know me? You knew my name and my father’s name. By God, I had never seen you before this day. He said: The All-Knowing, All-Aware informed me. My spirit has known your spirit when you spoke to my soul about yourself. Spirits have souls like the souls of the living. Believers know one another. And they converse in the spirit of God, even if they do not meet, even if they do not speak and get to know each other, even if homes separate them and homes separate them, he said: I said, Tell me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a hadith that I remember from you. He said: I did not meet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor did he I will have company with him, and I have seen men who have seen him, and he has told me of his conversation as he told you, and I do not like to open this door to My soul is to be a hadith narrator or a judge and a mufti. I have a job in my soul, Haram Ibn Hayyan. He said: So I said: O my brother, recite to me verses from the Book of God. Hear them from you, for I love you for God’s sake with an intense love, and I pray with supplications, and I command a commandment that I will keep from you.He said: Then he took my hand on the shore of the Euphrates and said: I seek refuge in God, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from the accursed Satan, in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. He said: Then he gasped. He gasped, then he cried on his place, then he said: My Lord Almighty said, “Remembrance of him,” and his speech is most worthy of speech, and his speech is most truthful, and his speech is best. The words are his words: {And We did not create the heavens and the earth and all that is between them in a changing state. We did not create them except with the truth} [Al-Dukhan: 39] until he reached {except those whom God has mercy on. Indeed, He is the Mighty, the Most Merciful” [Al-Dukhan: 42]. Then he gasped a gasp, then remained silent, and I looked at him, and I thought he had fainted. Then he said: O old man. Ibn Hayyan Your father died, and you are about to die, and Abu Hayyan died, so you will either go to Paradise or to Hell, and Adam died, and Eve died, O Ibn Hayyan, and Noah and Abraham, the companions of the Most Gracious, died, O Ibn Hayyan, and Musa, the savior of the Most Gracious, died, O Ibn Hayyan, and David, the successor of the Most Merciful, died, O Ibn Hayyan, Muhammad, the Messenger of the Most Gracious, died, and Abu Bakr, the Caliph of the Muslims, died, O Ibn Hayyan, and my brother, my guardian, and my friend, Omar Ibn Hayyan, died. Al-Khattab, then he said: And his two sons, may God have mercy on Omar, and Omar will be alive at that day, and that was at the end of his caliphate. He said: So I said to him: May God have mercy on you, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab after Hayy said: Yes, if you understand then you know what I said.And you are in the dead, and it was already, then he prayed upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and made soft supplications, then he said: This is my advice to you, O Haram bin Hayyan, the Book of God, and meeting the righteous Muslims, and may blessings and peace be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mourned myself, And I mourned you, so upon you is the remembrance of death, and they will not spare you a glance. And warn your people when you return to them, and advise all of your people, and work hard. For yourself and for you, beware lest you separate from the community and thus depart from your religion, and you do not know it, lest you enter Hell on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then he said: Oh God, This man claims that he loves me for you, and he visited me for your sake. Oh God, make his face known to me in Paradise, and admit him to me as a visitor in your abode, the abode of peace. And protect him as long as he is in this world wherever he is, and protect him from his estate and contentment with a small amount of the world, and whatever you have given him of the world make it easy for him. And make him one of those who are thankful for your blessings, and reward him with the best reward. I entrust you to God, O Haram bin Hayyan, and peace and mercy be upon you. God, then he said to me: I will not see you after today, may God have mercy on you, for I hate fame, and I love solitude because I am very sad, very sad. Concern, as long as I am alive with these people in this world,And do not ask about me, and do not seek me, and know that you are on my mind, and I have not seen you, and you have not seen me, so remember me and pray for me, for I will remember you and pray For you, God Almighty willing, go here until he takes her here. He said: I was keen to walk with him for an hour, but he refused, so I left him. He cried and I cried. He said: I started looking at his back until he entered some of the rails. I looked for him after that and asked about him, but I did not find anyone. He told me something about him, so may God have mercy on him and forgive him, and not a Friday came to me without seeing him in my dreams once or twice, or as he said.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5726 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5727","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Sharik told us, he said: They mentioned in his gathering Owais Al-Qarni, and he said: “He was killed with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, in Al-Rajjala.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5727 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5728","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Yahya bin Ma’in told me, Abu Ubaida Al-Haddad, Abu Makin told us: “I saw a woman in the Uwais Al-Qarni Mosque. She said: He and his friends were gathering in This is their mosque, they pray and read from their Qur’an, so I bring their lunch and dinner here, so that they may pray the prayers.” She said: “And it was This was their practice as long as they witnessed, until they invaded, and Uwais and a group of his companions were martyred on the battlefield in the hands of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them. “On behalf of all of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5728 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5729","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Wahhab told us Al-Thaqafi, Khaled Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jada’, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “He will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation who is more numerous than the Banu Tamim.” Al-Thaqafi said: Hisham said: I heard Al-Hasan saying: “He is Uwais.” Al-Qarni,” “Sahih chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhis Al-Dhahabi] 5729 - Al-Dhahabi said in Al-Talkhis, Sahih"
"5730","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “On naming those who He witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Banu Dubayyah Sahl bin Hunaif bin Wahib bin Ghanim bin Tha’labah bin Majdada bin Al-Harith bin Amr, and Amr, who was called “Bakhraj.”"
"5731","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khaled al-Masry told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming one of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, Sahl ibn Hunaif ibn Wahib ibn Aqim ibn Tha'labah bin Majdah bin Al-Harith bin Amr, and they claimed that he was called: Bada'a'."
"5732","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaibah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Sahl bin Hunaif Ibn Wahib Ibn Uqaym Ibn Tha'labah Abu Thabit died in Kufa in the year thirty-eight, and Ali Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, prayed for him. About them"
"5733","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad bin Al-Muaddeb told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, Othman bin Hakim told us, Al-Rabab, my grandmother, told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Hunaif, who said: I passed by a flood, so I entered, bathed in it, and then emerged from it. He was feverish, so the matter reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Tell Abu Thabit and let him give alms.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5733 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5734","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad told us Bin Omar, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, Abdullah bin Jaafar, Muhammad bin Aoun, and Saad bin Ibrahim, On the authority of Salih, on the authority of Asim ibn Omar, “On the friendship of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, between the Muhajireen and the Ansar from Banu Hashim, Ali ibn Ubayy Talib and Sahl bin Hunaif, may God be pleased with them.”
 Ibn Umar said: Sahl bin Hunaif witnessed Badr and Uhud, and remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud when the people discovered him. He pledged his allegiance to him on death, and on that day he exuded nobility on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be noble.” “Easy, for it is easy.” He said: He also witnessed the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he witnessed with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. Siffin
 Ibn Umar said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of his father. He said: “Sahl bin died Hanif in Kufa after their departure from Siffin in the year thirty-eight, and the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, prayed for him."
"5735","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdul Razzaq, I am Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, prayed over Sahl bin Hunaif, so he said takbir for him Sita, then he turned to us and said: “He is from the people of Badr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5735 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5736","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair told us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Zakaria al-Humaydi told me, Al-Ala’ ibn Katheer told me, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Mukhramah, Abu Umamah bin Sahl told me: “My father said to me: O my son, you saw us on the day of Badr, and one of us was pointing with his sword at… The head of the polytheist, so his head falls away from his body before he reaches it. “The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5736 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari"
"5737","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Masry told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali entered with his sword on Fatima, may God be pleased with them both, while she was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Take him, for you have done well with him in fighting. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you have done well in fighting. Today, Sahl bin Hunaif, Asim bin Thabit, Al-Harith bin Al-Simmah, and Abu Dujana have done well. This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it. “And therein is chastisement for whoever he thinks is better than him.”"
"5738","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Masry told us, Ahmad bin Saleh told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ دِينَارٍ، عَنْ عِكْرِمَةَ، عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: دَخَلَ عَلِيٌّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَلَى فَاطِمَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا وَهِيَ تَغْسِلُ Blood, on the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned the hadith as I dictated it. I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz say: “We did not write it connected. Except on the authority of Abu Ya’qub with his chain of transmission, and what is well-known from the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of a mursal narration, but it is known that This text is from the hadith of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather"
"5739","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sahl bin Hunaif, who said: Ali came to Fatima, may God be pleased with them both, on the day of Uhud, and he said: Hold this sword of mine, for I have fought well with it today. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you have fought well with it, then It was made good by Asim bin Thabit, Sahl bin Hunaif, and Al-Harith bin Al-Sammah.”"
"5740","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Hafiz told us, in Hamdan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told me, about Al-Zuhri, Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif told me, and he was one of the prominent Ansar who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said: “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5739 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5741","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salama Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Yahya bin Salih Al-Wahazi told me, Al-Jarrah bin Al-Minhal, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that Aamir bin Rabi’ah, a man from Banu Adi bin Ka’b, saw Sahl bin Hunaif went with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to wash himself with the kharar, and he said: By God, I have never seen anything like today, and no skin hidden. Sahl was stuck and fell, and it was said: O Messenger of God, do you have anything to do with Sahl bin Hunaif? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, summoned Amer bin Rabi’ah and became angry with him, saying: “When one of you kills his brother or friend, does he not call upon With the blessing, he washed for him.” Amer washed for him and he was relieved, and there was no harm in him. “And the washing is when a cup of water is brought to it and he puts his hands in it.” The cup all together, and he spits from the cup on his face, then he washes his right hand in it, and he washes the part from it in the cup, and he inserts his hand and washes his back, then he takes his left hand and does the same, then he washes his chest in the cup, then he washes his right knee in The mug, and his fingertips. He does this with his left leg, and enters inside his garment, then covers the mug before placing it on The ground, and he gets up from it, rinses his mouth, and spits it on his face, then pours it on his head, then throws the cup behind him.”
 The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed to narrate this hadith briefly, as Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin"
"5742","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yusuf bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that he heard his father say: Abu Sahl bin Hunaif took a bath and took off the robe that he was wearing on the day of Hunayn when he was defeated. God is the enemy, and Amer bin Rabia was watching. He said: Sahl was a white man of good character, so Amer bin Rabia said to him: I did not see Just like today, and he looked at him and was impressed by his beauty when he took off his cloak and said: There is no slave girl with a better body in her covering than that of Sahl ibn Hanif, and Sahl fell ill in his place, and his sickness became severe, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him that Sahl bin Hanif had fallen ill. And he did not smell good with you, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him, and they informed him of what had happened to Amir, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Why should one of you kill his brother? Have you not blessed him? Indeed, the evil eye is due. Perform ablution for him.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he sees “If one of you likes something, let him bless it, for indeed the evil eye is valid.” These additions are in both hadiths from what they did not narrate.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5742 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5743","Muhammad ibn Saleh ibn Hani told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Anis al-Qurashi told me, Abu Asim told me, I am Ibn Juraij, Abd told me Al-Karim bin Abi Al-Mukharif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Malik, a man from Abdul Qais, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, a client of Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of Sahl bin Hunaif said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “You are my messenger to Mecca.” So extend my greetings to them, and say to them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to do three things: Do not swear by your fathers, and when you are alone... Do not face the Qiblah, do not turn away from it, and do not clean yourselves with a bone or a camel.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5743 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5744","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “Khwat bin Jubayr bin Al-Nu’man bin Imru’ Al-Qais, who is Al-Burak bin Tha’labah Ibn Amr Ibn Awf, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, minted his shares and his reward on the day of Badr.”"
"5745","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Al-Jarrah bin Mukhlid told us, Wahib bin Jarir told us, My father told us, saying: I heard Zayd bin Aslam, narrating on the authority of Khwat bin Jubayr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Abu Abdullah.”"
"5746","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Yunus told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: “Khwat bin Jubayr Ibn Al-Numan Ibn Umayyah Ibn Al-Barak Ibn Imru’ Al-Qays Ibn Tha’labah Ibn Amr Ibn Awf Ibn Malik died in Medina in the year forty. He is seventy-four years old.”"
"5747","Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Atki told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Abdul-Aziz bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sent Khawat ibn Jubayr to the Banu Qurayzah.” On a horse of his, it is said to him: Al-Janah “is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5747 - Abdul Aziz bin Yahya is weak"
"5748","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, Abdullah bin Salih bin Ishaq told us. Ibn Salih Ibn Khwat Ibn Jubayr, he said: My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Khwat Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “What “A lot of it intoxicates, but a little of it is forbidden.” Abdullah bin Salih bin Ishaq said, on the authority of his fathers, “Khwat bin Jubayr died in the year forty.”"
"5749","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Abd told me Al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Khwat bin Salih, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabra reported, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Rifa'ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muknaf, that Khwat bin Jubayr was one of those who went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Badr. While he was in the air, a sharp stone struck him and broke his leg. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him back to Medina and struck him with an arrow.” And his reward, and it was as if he had witnessed it.” They said: He witnessed the trenches of Uhud, the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 Ibn Omar said: Salih bin Khwat bin Salih told me, on the authority of his family, they said: “Khwat bin Jubayr died in Medina in the year forty. He was seventy-four years old, and he was one of the men.”"
"5750","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Shabab bin Khayyat told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Salih bin Khawwat bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: My father, Khawwat bin Jubayr, said: I fell ill, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited me, and when I was healed. He said: “May your body be healthy, my sisters. For God Almighty is the one who has promised him.” I said: “And I have not promised God anything.” He said: “Indeed, no sick person gets sick without making a vow.” If you do anything or intend, then fulfill for God Almighty what you promised him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5750 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5751","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: His name was Abdullah Ibn Salam Al-Husayn “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him Abdullah.”"
"5752","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Battah told us, Abu Ja`far ibn Rusta told us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni told us, Muhammad ibn Umar told us, he said: Abd Allah bin Salam is nicknamed Abu Yusuf, and his name before Islam was Al-Husayn. When he converted to Islam, “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him Abdullah.” He was from the children of Israel, from the descendants of Yusuf ibn Ya’qub, peace and blessings be upon them both, and an ally of the Qawaqila from the Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj. He died Abdullah bin Salam in Medina, according to all of them, in the year forty-three during the caliphate of Muawiyah.”"
"5753","Khalaf bin Muhammad al-Karabisi told me in Bukhara, Muhammad bin Harith told us, Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: “There was loyalty Abdullah bin Salam to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he died in the year forty-three. The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Saad. Ibn Abi Waqqas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not say to anyone walking on the face of the earth that he is one of the people of Paradise except Abdullah ibn “Peace”"
"5754","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu al-Mujih told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Shaqiq told us, al-Fadl bin told us Khalid, Ubayd Allah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in the Almighty’s saying: “And a witness from the Children of Israel testified of something similar to him” [Al-Ahqaf: 10] He said: “The witness is Abdullah bin Salam, and he was one of the best scholars of the Children of Israel.”"
"5755","Imam Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad told us, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi told us Shaybah and Qutayba bin Saeed said: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mushar, on the authority of Kharsha bin Al-Hurr, who said: I was sitting in A group in the city mosque, in which there was a sheikh of good appearance, and he was Abdullah bin Salam. He said: So he began to speak to them in a good manner, and when he got up, he said: The people: Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this one. I said: By God, I will certainly follow him so that I will know where he is. His house, so I followed him, and he set off until he was almost out of the city, then he entered his house, so I asked him for permission, and he gave me permission, and said: What do you need? My nephew? I said to him: I heard people saying: such-and-such, so I liked being with you. He said: God knows best about the people of Paradise, and I will talk to you about what They said: They said that while I was sleeping, a man came to me and said to me: Get up. So he took me by the hand and I set off with him, and I saw a horse to my left. So I took it to take it, and he said to me: Do not take it, for it is the road of the people of the north. Then I saw a sharp horse on my right, and he said to me: Take it. Here, behold, I was at a mountain, and He said to me: Go up. He said: So when I wanted to go up, I fell on my mount. He said: Until I did that repeatedly. He said: Then he set off until he brought me a pillar with its top in the sky and its bottom on the earth with a ring at the top. He said to me: Climb above this. He said: I said: How? He ascended with his head in the sky. He said: Then he took my hand and descended on me, and behold, I was clinging to the ring until morning, and I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told it to him, and he said: “As for the road that you saw on your left, it is the road of the people of the north, and as for the road that is on your right, it is the road of the people of Yemen, and as for the handhold, it is the handhold of Islam, and you will not stop clinging to it until you die.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5755 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5756","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf bin Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Mughirah Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Abu Al-Mughirah Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj told us Safwan bin Amr, Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf bin Malik al-Ashja’i, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set out Peace be upon him, and I was with him until we entered the Jewish church. He said: “O Jews, show me twelve men who testify that there is no God.” Except God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. May God remove from every Jew under the firmament of the wrath with which He was angry.” He said: “So be silent.” One of them answered him, then he replied to them, but none of them answered him, so he said: “You refused, for by God I am the gatherer, I am the punisher, and I am the Prophet.” The Chosen One, have you believed or disbelieved?” Then he left and I was with him until we were almost leaving, when a man came up behind us and said: “As you are, O Muhammad, then that man said: What man do you know among you, O Jews? They said: By God, we do not know that there was among us a man more knowledgeable about the Book of God than you, nor more knowledgeable than you, nor your father before you, nor your grandfather. Before your father, he said: For I bear witness of him in God that he is the Prophet of God whom you find in the Torah. So they said: You lied, then they refuted his statement. And they said evil about him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have lied, and your words will not be accepted. As for what you mentioned above, you will praise him as much good as you have praised. But if he believes, you deny him and say about him what you said, then your saying will not be accepted. He said: So we went out as three, the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And peace be upon him, and I and Abdullah bin Salam, and God Almighty revealed therein: {Say, “Have you considered if it is from God and you disbelieve in it?” [Al-Ahqaf: 10] “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but they agreed on a praiseworthy hadith, on the authority of Anas, that is, Abdullah bin Salam’s man among you, in brief.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5756 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5757","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Salem bin Ibrahim, the owner of the Qur’an, told me, Ikrimah bin Ammar, Muhammad bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hanzala, that Abdullah bin Salam passed through the market carrying a bundle of firewood on his head, and he said: I ward off pride, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed.” “Kubr.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not mention it in mentioning Abdullah bin Salam.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5757 - Salem bin Ibrahim Wah"
"5758","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Rabia bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Yazid bin Amira, who said: When Muadh bin Jabal attended death, he was told: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, Hosanna. He said: Sit me down. Then he said: Knowledge and faith are their place. Whoever seeks them will find them. He said three things. Several times, they sought knowledge with four Rahat: Uwaimir Abi Al-Darda’, with Salman Al-Farisi, with Abdullah bin Masoud, and with Abdullah bin Salam, who was Jewish, then converted to Islam, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He lived with ten people in “Paradise.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5758 - True"
"5759","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a bowl, ate from it, and left some leftovers. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man from this group of the people of Paradise will come and eat this.” Saad said: And I had left Umayr My brother is performing ablution, so I said: It is Umair, so Abdullah bin Salam came and ate it. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5759 - True"
"5760","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Salamah bin Salamah ibn Waqsh ibn Zaghba ibn Za`ura ibn Abd al-Ashhal ibn Jumah ibn Jusham ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj ibn Amr ibn Malik bin Aws»"
"5761","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of A loop in naming the Ansar who witnessed Aqaba, then from Aws, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: “Salama bin Waqsh witnessed ""full moon"""
"5762","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “ Salama bin Salama bin Waqsh, nicknamed Abu Awf, witnessed the first and last obstacles with the seventy, according to the words of all of them, and he said All of them: Salamah witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he died in the year forty-five. He was seventy years old and was buried in the city.”"
"5763","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Shabab bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Abu Awf Salama bin Salama died. Ibn Waqsh in the year forty-five, and he was buried in Medina, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5764","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Ishaq, on the authority of Salih bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Salama bin Salama bin Waqsh, He said: We had a Jewish neighbor in Bani Abd al-Ashhal. He said: One day he came out from his house to visit us until he stopped at Bani Abd al-Ashhal. He said: Salamah: “On that day, a cloak of mine was lying on me in the courtyard of my family, and he mentioned the Resurrection, the Resurrection, the Reckoning, and the Balance. And Paradise and Hell. He said: He said that about the people of Yathrib, and the people are holders of idols and do not see a resurrection present at the time of death, so they said to him: Woe to you, do you see this? Who is so-and-so? After their death, people will be sent to Paradise and Hell and will be rewarded therein for their deeds. He said: Yes, and he who swears by it. They said: O so-and-so, woe to you, what is the sign of that? He said: A prophet sent from this country, and he pointed to Mecca with his hand. They said: When will we see him? He said: Then he looked at me, and I was the youngest of them, and he said: If this boy spends his life, he will reach it. Salamah said: “By God, he did not go.” Night and day until God, Blessed and Most High, sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was alive among us, so we believed in him, but he disbelieved in transgression. And out of envy.” So we said to him: Woe to you, O so-and-so, are you not the one about whom you told us what you said? He said: Yes, but it is not “authentic according to the conditions of Muslim,” and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5764 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5765","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth narrated to me, Zayd bin Jubayrah bin Mahmoud bin Abi Jubairah Al-Ansari from Banu Abd al-Ashhal narrated to me, on the authority of his father, Jubairah bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Salama bin Salamah bin Waqsh, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Ablution and they ate, then they went out and Salamah performed ablution, and Jabirah said to him: Did you not perform ablution? He said: Yes, but “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we left a prayer for which we had been called while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was performing ablution. So he ate, then he performed ablution, and I said to him: Did you not perform ablution, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes, but the matter is happening, and this is what happened. Mahmoud, that his grandfather Salamah was the last of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he died, unless it was Anas bin Malik, for he survived him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5765 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5766","Imam Abu Al-Walid told me, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Fudaik told me, Ibn Abi Habiba told me, on the authority of Awf bin Salamah bin Awf bin Salama bin Salama bin Waqsh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, forgive the Ansar and the sons of The Ansar, and for those loyal to the Ansar.”"
"5767","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Yazid bin Romans, and Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, and Abu Ja’far Al-Baghdadi told us, and the pronunciation is his, Abu told us Ulatha, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met a man from the people of In the desert, as he was heading to Badr, he met a spirit. The people asked him about the news of the people, but they did not find any news of him, so they said to him: Peace be upon him. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Is the Messenger of God among you? They said: Yes. The Bedouin said: If you are the Messenger of God, then tell me what is in the belly of this camel of mine? Then Salama bin Salamah bin Waqsh, who was a young boy, said to him: Do not ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I am telling you, I had a crush on her. In her womb was a lump of you, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You have disgraced the man, O Salamah.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned away. He greeted the man, but he did not say a word to him until they closed, and the Muslims received them with spirits congratulating them, then Salamah bin Salamah said: Oh Messenger of God, what are they congratulating you for? By God, if we saw old women, bald, like hanging bodies, we would burn them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, every people has a skill. “Only the nobles know it.” The chain of transmission is authentic, even if it is mursal and there is an honorable veil for Salamah ibn Salamah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5767 - Sahih mursal"
"5768","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghdadi told us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, said: Asim bin Adi bin Al-Jad bin Ajlan went out on the day of Badr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him back. And he was struck with an arrow by the companions of Badr.”"
"5769","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: And he came out Asim bin Adiy bin Al-Jadd bin Ajlan bin Dubayah, and he is from Bilai, an ally of Banu Abd bin Zayd bin Malik bin Awf bin Amr bin Awf bin Malik bin Aws went to Badr, “and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him back and struck him with his arrow.”"
"5770","And Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Asim bin Adi bin Al-Jad bin Ajlan bin Haritha bin Dubayah bin Haram bin Ja’al bin Amr bin Khuthaym bin Waddam bin Dhubyan bin هُمَيمِ بْنِ هَتَمِ بْنِ بَلِيِّ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْحَافِ بْنِ قُضَاعَةَ، وَكَانَ يُكَنَّى أَبَا عَمْرِو وَيُقَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ»
 Ibn Umar said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabrah told us, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muknaf, Aflah bin Saeed bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah, on the authority of Asim bin Adi, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he wanted to go to Badr, he left Asim bin Adi behind Quba and the people of Al-Aliyah because of something he had learned about them, so he struck him with an arrow. And reward him.” He was among those who witnessed it. Ibn Umar said: Asim bin Adi witnessed Uhud, the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and Asim was going to the palace, what is it, and he died in the year forty-five during the caliphate of Muawiyah, and he was one hundred and fifteen years old."
"5771","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ahmad bin Khabab told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Othman Al-Saluli, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Badah bin Asim bin Adi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: My brother and I bought one hundred shares of Hunayn’s arrows. This reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O Asim, two ordinary wolves did not attack the prey of a sheep that its master had lost.” He spoiled therein the love of money and honor in his possession.” The hadith is well-known by Asim, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “He is the one who:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5771 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5772","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb, that Malik told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi, on the authority of his father, “that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave permission for camel herders in Bayutah to stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then to stone the next day, then to stone on the Day of Sacrifice.” “The chain of narration is authentic. It was authenticated by Malik bin Anas and others slipped into it, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5772 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5773","So I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: In the hadith of my father Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi, narrated by Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, granted the shepherds permission to shepherd one day and graze another day.” Yahya said: This is a mistake. Rather, it is as Malik said. Yahya said: When Sufyan narrated this hadith to us, he said: Ali mentioned something in this hadith. Al-Hakim: “Abu Al-Badah bin Asim bin Adi transmitted it on the authority of his father.”"
"5774","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih narrated to us in Rayy, Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Aidh al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Badah bin Asim bin Adi, on the authority of his father, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented He entered the city on Monday for twelve nights during the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal, and he resided in the city for ten years.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5774 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5775","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, “Whoever testified The trench was Zayd bin Thabit bin Al-Dahhak bin Luthan bin Amr bin Abd Awf bin Ghanm bin Malik bin Al-Najjar, and he was among those who conveyed The dust on that day will be with the Muslims.”"
"5776","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Sa’id Abu Kharijah is called Zaid bin Thabit bin Al-Dahhak bin Zaid bin Luthan bin Amr bin Abdul Awf bin Ghanam bin Malik bin Al-Najjar. Al-Ansari, he died in the year forty-five.”"
"5777","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abu died Saeed Zayd bin Thabit bin Al-Dahhak in the year forty-five.”"
"5778","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurarah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurarah, he said: Zaid said Ibn Thabit: The incident with Baath took place when I was six years old, and it occurred five years before the migration of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Medina, when I was eleven years old, and I was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: A boy. Of the Khazraj, he recited sixteen surahs, but I did not pass in Badr or Uhud, but I passed in the Trench.”
 Ibn Umar said: Zayd ibn Thabit used to write both books, the Arabic book and the Hebrew book, and the first scene that Zayd ibn Thabit witnessed He stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the ditch when he was fifteen years old. He was among those who moved dirt at that time with the Muslims. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is a fine boy.” His eyes were overcome by him on that day, and he fell asleep. Then Amara bin Hazm came and took He took his weapon without realizing it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Raqqad, you slept until your weapon was gone.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Who has knowledge of this boy’s weapon?” Then Amara bin Hazm said: O Messenger of God, I took him and returned him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the believer to be terrorized and “His belongings will be taken eagerly and seriously.” The banner of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar was in Tabuk with Umarah ibn Hazm, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, overtook it. So he took it from him and gave it to Zaid bin Thabit, and Amara said: O Messenger of God, has something reached you about me? He said: “No, but the Qur’an is given priority, and Zayd was more absorbed in the Qur’an than you.” Ibn Umar said: Zayd bin Thabit died, and his son Ismail A young man who did not hear anything from him, “and there were disagreements about the time of his death.” Ibn Omar said: “What we have is that he died in Medina in the year forty-five. He was fifty-six years old, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam prayed for him.”"
"5779","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us of its authenticity, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baraa informed us, Ali ibn al-Madini informed us, he said: “Zayd ibn Thabit Ibn Al-Dahhak Ibn Zayd Ibn Luthan Ibn Amr Ibn Abd Awf Ibn Ghanam Ibn Malik Ibn Al-Najjar died in the year four or five. And forty"
"5780","So Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Ismail bin Musab told me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Yahya bin Kharijah bin Zaid, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Zaid bin Thabit died before When the sun sets, and it was my opinion that he should be buried before morning. Then the Ansar came and said: He should not be buried except during the day so that his funeral can be gathered for him. People, so Marwan heard the voices, so he started walking until he came to Ali, and he said: “It is my intention that he not be buried until the morning.” So when we woke up, we washed him. Three times: the first with water, the second with water and Sidr, and the third with water and camphor, and we shrouded him in three garments: one of which was cold. Muawiya clothed it for him, and we prayed over him after sunrise, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam prayed over him, and Marwan sent camels to him, and they were slaughtered. He fed the people and the women in Beijing for three days."
"5781","Imam Abu Al-Walid told us, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Are you good at Syriac?” I said: No. He said: “Then he learned it, for there come to us books.” So I learned it in seventeen days. Al-Amash said: “There used to come to him books that he did not desire.” “Only someone he trusts can look at it.” It is true, if Thabit ibn Ubaid heard it from Zayd ibn Thabit, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5781 - It is authentic if Thabit heard it from Zaid"
"5782","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar Al-Khitami, my uncle Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of my grandfather Utbah bin Al-Fakih, he said: “I said to Zayd bin Thabit, O Abu Kharijah.”"
"5783","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, said: “I witnessed the funeral of Zayd bin Thabit, and when he was buried in his grave,” he mentioned the hadith."
"5784","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musaddad told us, Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, Khaled told us Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most merciful to my nation is Abu Bakr. The most ardent of them in the matter of God is Umar, the most honest of them in modesty is Uthman, the most knowledgeable of them in the Book of God is Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and the most honorable of them is Zayd ibn Thabit. And the most knowledgeable of them about what is permissible and what is forbidden is Muadh, except that every nation has a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.” This is a chain of narration. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context, but rather they agreed with this chain of transmission on the mention of Abu Ubaidah only, and they I mentioned its reason in the book of summary.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5784 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5785","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna told us. Al-Ansari, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he took the ride of Zayd bin Thabit, and said to him: Step aside, O son of The uncle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is what we do to our elders and scholars.” The chain of transmission is authentic according to Muslim’s condition, and it was not He takes him out. One of the virtues of Zayd ibn Thabit was that he began it with the hadith of compiling the Qur’an, for it has many virtues, but the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with They had agreed to take it out, so I left it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5785 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5786","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And among the allies of Banu Nawfal bin Abd Manaf is Ali bin Muniyah, and his mother’s Muniyah, which is Muniyah bint Ghazwan bin Jabir, from Banu Mazin. His father is Umayyah bin Abi Ubaid bin Hammam bin Al-Harith bin Bakr.”"
"5787","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: “Ali bin Umayyah His father’s illiteracy and his mother’s illiteracy.”"
"5788","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shaybani told me, saying: I heard Abu Hatim Al-Sulami, saying: I heard Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj, saying: Abu Al-Marazim Ya’la ibn Umayyah al-Thaqafi, he had a companion - Muslim, may God have mercy on him, disagreed with Yahya ibn Ma’in on this matter - for I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad Ibn Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas saying: I heard Yahya saying: “The nickname of Ali Ibn Umayyah is Al-Thaqafi, Abu Al-Marazim,” and he narrated on the authority of Ali Ibn Umayyah had three of his sons: Safwan, Uthman, and Abd al-Rahman.”"
"5789","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Amr bin Abdul Rahman bin Umayyah told me that his father told him that Ya’la would be exalted. He said: I spoke to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted Abu Umayyah on the day of the conquest, and I said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to my father on the emigration, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I pledge allegiance to him.” On jihad, migration has stopped.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5789 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5790","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Ruh ibn Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq, Amr bin Dinar told us, he said: The first to chronicle books was Ali bin Umayyah, while he was in Yemen, for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said, “He came to Medina in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal,” and that people dated it to the beginning of the year, but people dated it to the beginning of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5791","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Ata’ told me Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Abdullah Ibn Safwan, on the authority of his two uncles: Ya’la and Salamah Ibn Umayyah said: We went out with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Battle of Tabuk, and with us was a companion of ours, and a man fought him, so he bit his arm and pulled it from his mouth, and his folds fell off, so he went away. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking reason. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of you should go to his brother and bite him.” Like the biting of a stallion, and after that he comes seeking reason. Go, for you have no reason.’ So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invalidated it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5791 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5792","Abu Bakr bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And who Banu Jashm bin Al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salama bin Saad bin Sarida bin Yazid bin Jashm, Muadh, Mu’awwidh, and Khallad bin Amr bin Al-Jamuh bin Zayd bin Haram bin Ka’b witnessed Badr, and Muadh killed Abu Jahl, and Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl cut off his hand, so he lived for a long time. Othman, may God be pleased with him, his mother Hind bint Amr bin Tha’labah bin Haram, and his uncle Jaber bin Abdullah Al-Ansari Uqbi Badri."
"5793","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh was injured. A catastrophe on the Day of Badr. He remained ill until the reign of Uthman, then he died in Medina in the year fourteen, and Uthman ibn Affan prayed over him and was buried. In Al-Baqi'"
"5794","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubair, “In naming those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Aqaba from Banu Haram bin Ka’b, Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh.”"
"5795","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Shazan told us, and Ahmad bin Salama told us, they said: Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abdul Aziz told us. Bin Muhammad, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent man Muadh bin “Amr bin Al-Jamouh” is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5795 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5796","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ali bin Hamshadh told us Justice, and the pronunciation for it, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us, Yusuf bin Al-Majishun narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Ibrahim bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: While I was standing in line on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and to my left, and I saw that I was between... Two Ansar boys with new teeth. I wished to be between one of their ribs, but one of them winked at me and said: Oh uncle, do you know? Abu Jahl? I said: Yes, and what need do you have of it, my nephew? He said: I was told that he curses the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I saw him my blackness would not leave his blackness until he died except One of us was in a hurry, and I was amazed at that. The other winked at me and told me the same thing. I did not want to see Abu Jahl going around among the people, so I said: They said to them: This is your companion whom you are asking about, so they attacked him with their swords and struck him until they killed him, then they departed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they told him, and he said: “Which of the two of you killed him?” So each one of them said: I killed him. He said: “Have you anointed your swords?” They said: No, so he looked at the two swords and said: “Both of you killed him and decreed his plunder to Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamuh.” The other was Muadh bin Afra.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5796 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary

 So Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi informed us, Abu Ulatha told me, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, Abu Al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa, “Khallad bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh was killed at Uhud with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5796 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5797","Abu Ja`far told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa, “Umair bin The pigeons, from the Banu Salamah, then from the Banu Haram bin Ka’b bin Ghanam bin Salamah, among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5798","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Badr: “Go to a garden as wide as the heavens and the earth,” Umayr ibn al-Hammam said. Al-Ansari: O Messenger of God, its breadth is the heavens and the earth, blah blah, no, by God, O Messenger of God, I must be one of its people. He said: “You are one of its people.” So he took out dates and began to eat, then said: If I live until I eat my dates, it will be a long life. He said: He threw away the dates he had with him, then fought them until he was killed, “Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not take him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5798 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5799","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told us, Ahmad ibn Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus ibn Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, in naming someone “One of the Banu Jashm bin Al-Khazraj bin Kharash bin Al-Sammah bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5800","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, so who testified? Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Banu Haram bin Ka’b al-Hubab bin al-Mundhir bin al-Jamuh bin Zayd bin Haram.”"
"5801","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki told me, Abu Al-Abbas bin Saeed Al-Hafiz told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf bin Ziyad told us, Abu Hafs Al-A’sha told us, Bassam Al-Sayrifi told me, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Al-Kinani, Hubab bin Al-Mundhir Al-Ansari told me, he said: “ I advised the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two things on the Day of Badr, and he accepted them from me. I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his battle. Badr came and he camped behind the water, and I said: O Messenger of God, was what you did based on revelation or according to my opinion? He said: In my opinion, my beloved. I said: The opinion is that you should leave the water behind you, so if you resort to it, you will resort to it. So accept that from me.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5801 - Munkar hadith and its chain of transmission"
"5802","So Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibn Abi told us Habibah, on the authority of Dawud ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: Opinion is what the beloveds indicated. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O beloveds, you indicated opinion.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5802 - Munkar hadith and its chain of transmission"
"5803","Abu Ishaq Al-Muzaki told me, Abu Al-Abbas bin Saeed Al-Hafiz told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf bin Ziyad Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Hafs told us Al-A’sha, Bassam Al-Sayrifi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Al-Kinani, on the authority of Hubab ibn Al-Mundhir, who said: “And Gabriel, may the blessings and peace of God be upon him, descended upon Muhammad May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Which of the two things is more beloved to you: to be in this world with your companions, or to return to your Lord in the gardens of bliss He has promised you? Of the beautiful and everlasting bliss, and whatever your soul desires, and whatever your eye delights in. So consult its companions, and they said: O Messenger of God, you will be With us is dearer to us, and you inform us of the faults of our enemies, and you pray to God to grant us victory over them, and you inform us of the news from heaven, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Why do you not speak, O beloved?” So I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, choose where your Lord has chosen for you, and he accepted that from me.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5803 - Munkar hadith and its chain of transmission"
"5804","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Abu Al-Muthanna, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma told us, Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab claim that the one who said on the day of the Saqifah: “I am its itched braid” was a man from Banu Salamah called Al-Hubab bin Al-Mundhir
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5804 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5805","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, I am Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: When Zaid bin Thabit died, Abu Hurairah said: “The rabbi of this nation died today, and perhaps God will place in Ibn Abbas is his successor.”"
"5806","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jawhari told us: I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam, Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam, Al-Shaybani narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: “Knowledge is taken from six of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It was Omar, and Abd By God, and Zaid, their knowledge resembled one another, and one of them used to borrow from one another.” He said: So I said to Al-Sha’bi: And Al-Ash’ari was among these people? He said: “He was one of the jurists.”"
"5807","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abu Hammam told us, Damra told us, he said: Ibn Shawdhab: And I heard him mentioning that he said: I heard Al-Salt bin Bahram say, while we were at a funeral, and he said: The owner of the bed told me that he witnessed Zayd’s funeral. Ibn Thabit. When he was buried, Ibn Abbas shed tears on his grave and said: “This is how knowledge goes.”"
"5808","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Abu Hammam told us, Khaled bin Hayyan told us, Ali ibn Urwa al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, that Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit witnessed a funeral, and when Zayd wanted To ride. Ibn Abbas took his stirrup and said: “Step aside, my nephew.” Then he said: “This is what is done to scholars.”"
"5809","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil ibn al-Hasan informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad informed us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, I am Muammar, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd Ibn Jud’an, that Ibn Abbas, when Zayd Ibn Thabit was buried, threw dust on him, then said: “This is how knowledge is buried.”"
"5810","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz and Abu Muslim told us that Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, said: When Zaid bin Thabit died, we sat with Ibn Abbas in the shade of a palace, and he said: “This is how knowledge goes.” “A lot of knowledge has been buried today.”"
"5811","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “And he died Abu Uhayb Safwan bin Umayyah bin Khalaf bin Wahb bin Hudhafah bin Jumah. He converted to Islam at the time of the conquest. He died in the year three And forty"
"5812","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Uthman bin Talha bin My father is Talha bin Abdul-Uzza bin Uthman bin Abdul-Dar, and his mother is bint Saeed bin Sumayyah, from Banu Amr bin Awf from the people of Quba. He converted to Islam and the conversion of Amr ibn al-Aas and Khaled ibn al-Walid at the same time, and he died in Mecca in the year forty-three.”"
"5813","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And from Banu Abd al-Dar bin Qusayy, he mentioned this lineage, and his mother was Salama bint Sa’id from Banu Amr bin Awf from the people of Quba, and he was He converted to Islam before the conquest, along with the conversion of Amr ibn al-Aas and Khaled ibn al-Walid, and he came to the city in the month of Safar in the eighth year of the Hijra. He died in Mecca in the year forty-two, when Muawiyah rose.”"
"5814","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, I am Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of His father, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entering the Kaaba, he and Osama bin Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman bin Talha. He did not enter it. “There is someone with them.” Bilal told me that he asked Othman bin Talha: Where did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? He said: “Between the two Yemeni pillars,” and Shaybah bin Uthman narrated on the authority of his uncle Uthman bin Talha."
"5815","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us from the origin of his book, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Mutarrif bin Abi Al-Wazir told us, Musa bin Abdul Malik bin Umair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shaybah bin Uthman al-Hajabi, my uncle Uthman bin Talha told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “There are three things that describe you: the friendliness of your brother. You greet him when you meet him, you make room for him in a gathering, and you call him the one you love.” His names are attributed to him: “Abu al-Mutarrif Muhammad ibn Abi al-Wazir is one of the trustworthy and ancient people of Basra. I do not know that I have mentioned him in a hadith other than This »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5815 - Abu Mutrif was deemed weak by Abu Hatim"
"5816","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: “He narrates on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhainah, On the authority of his father, this is how he narrates it, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, and it is a mistake. His father did not narrate it on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but rather Abdullah, who He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his mother’s animal.”"
"5817","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “And who Their allies were Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhayna, and Buhaynah, his mother, who was Buhaynah bint Al-Harith bin Al-Muttalib bin Abd Manaf, whom he married. Malik, who was a man from Azd, an ally of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and she bore him Abdullah bin Malik, and he was called: Ibn Thus, “We do not know of a narrator for Abdullah bin Malik among the Followers other than Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz al-Araj Abu Muhammad: The first of them is the hadith of forgetfulness. It has many methods, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he prostrated, he would keep his upper arms close to his sides.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used cupping with his beard. A sentence, and Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Baqir, may God be pleased with them, and Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Thawban narrated on the authority of ""Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhayna"""
"5818","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, Khaled bin Mukhlid Al-Qatwani narrated to us, Suleiman narrated to us. Ibn Bilal, on the authority of Ja’far Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Malik Ibn Buhaynah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to The morning prayer, and Bilal was with him. He led the prayer and passed by me and said, “You pray four morning prayers.” Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq reported, “I am Al-Hasan bin Ali.” Ibn Ziyad, Abu Hammah told us, Abu Qurrah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, and Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner."
"5819","Then Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, I am Sa`id bin Masoud, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham told us about Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhayna, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He passed by him while he was erect, praying the morning prayer in front of me. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not perform this prayer before... Dhuhr and after it, and make a separation between them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5819 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5820","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Nafi’ bin Utbah bin Malik bin Uhayb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra, and his mother is from Kinana, and her name is Zainab bint Jabir.”"
"5821","Ahmed bin Yaqoub told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Nafi’ bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas, his mother was Zainab bint Khalid bin Ubaid bin Suwayd bin Jaber bin Taym bin Aamer bin Awf bin Al-Harith bin Abd Manat bin Adi bin Kinanah, and his mother is also called Atika bint Awf, sister of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf.”"
"5822","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Omar bin Hafs told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Musa bin Abdul Malik bin Umair told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, on the authority of Nafi` ibn Utbah, he said: Some Arabs came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to greet him. They wear wool, so I stood up and said: I will come between these people and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then I said to myself: He is the savior of the people, then My soul refused to do anything but go to him. He said: I heard him say: “They will invade the Arabian Peninsula and God will conquer it. Then they will invade Persia and He will conquer it.” God, then they will attack the Antichrist, and God will conquer him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5822 - Musa bin Abdul Malik Wah"
"5823","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdul Rahman Ibn Azhar Ibn Awf Ibn Abd al-Harith Ibn Zahra Ibn Kilab, nicknamed Abu Zubayr, and his mother was Bukayra bint Abd Yazid Ibn Hashim Ibn al-Muttalib Ibn Abd Manaf witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5824","Abu Al-Hussein Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Balkhi told me in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, Ja’far bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Sa’ib, that Abd al-Hamid bin Abd Al-Rahman bin Azhar narrated to him, on the authority of his father Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of a servant when He will be afflicted by illness or fever, like an iron that has been set on fire, and its impurity goes away, but its goodness remains.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5824 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5825","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Abdullah Ibn Adiy Ibn Al-Hamra Ibn Rabi’ah Ibn Abi Amr Ibn Uhayb Ibn Alaj Ibn Abd Al-Uzza, and his mother was Bint Shariq Ibn Amr Ibn Ahab, the sister of Al-Akhnas bin Shurayq."
"5826","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And Abdullah bin Adi bin Al-Hamra Al-Thaqafi told me. His nickname is Abu Amr.”"
"5827","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalli told us, Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he told me Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that Abdullah bin Adi bin Al-Hamra told him that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing In the Hazara in Mecca, “By God, you are the best of God’s earth, and the most beloved land to God, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.”"
"5828","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And Abu Abdul Rahman Habib bin Maslamah bin Malik bin Wahb bin Tha’labah bin Wathilah bin Amr bin Sinan Al-Fihri” and it was narrated That Abu Dharr and others “called him the Beloved of the Romans because of his struggle against them.” Anaf lived for forty years, and he was not yet fifty. Companionship, he died in the year forty-three.”"
"5829","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, Saeed bin Abd told us Al-Aziz, he said: I heard Makhoul, saying: I heard Ziyad bin Jariyah Al-Tamimi, saying: I heard Habib bin Maslamah, saying: “I witnessed the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a third was voluntary.”"
"5830","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: When Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah bin Habib conquered Sijistan, and Abu Rifa`ah Abdullah bin al-Harith bin Asad bin Adi bin Malik bin Tamim bin Al-Du’ul bin Jabal bin Adi bin Abd Manat bin Ad bin Tabha, and he had a companion. “He walked in the army, and when it was night He stood up to pray, then fell asleep at the end of the night, and his companions forgot about him, so a group of the enemy came to him and slaughtered him.”"
"5831","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: “Uqba bin Al-Harith bin Amer bin Nawfal bin Abd Manaf Abu Sarwaa. Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Mulaika heard from him.”"
"5832","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Ibn Juraij told us, about Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith bin Amer, that he “married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab, Then his mother, Thuwaybah, came and said: I have breastfed you both, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that.” He mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"5833","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad ibn Amr told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, about Urwah, in naming the one who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Banu Za’ura bin Abdul-Ashhal Muhammad bin Maslamah bin Khalid bin Adiy bin Majdah bin Haritha bin Al-Harith”"
"5834","Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah Al-Bakai told us, about Muhammad bin Ishaq, in mentioning those who witnessed Badr, said: “And from the Aws, and then from their allies from the Banu Abd al-Ashhal, Muhammad bin Maslamah Bin Khaled bin Adi bin Majdah bin Haritha bin Al Harith bin Amr bin Malik bin Al Aws, he was an ally of Banu Abdul Ashhal He died in the year three and it was said: the year forty-six, and he was seventy-seven years old at that time. He was nicknamed Abu Abd al-Rahman, and he prayed Upon him is Marwan bin Al-Hakam.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5834 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5835","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Muhammad died Ibn Maslamah Al-Ansari in the year forty-three.”"
"5836","So Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibrahim bin Ja`far, on the authority of his father, said: “Muhammad bin Maslama died in Medina in the year forty-six, and he was seventy-seven years old at that time. tall and bald
 Ibn Umar said: “Muhammad bin Maslamah was nicknamed Abu Abdul Rahman. He converted to Islam in Medina at the hands of Mus’ab bin Umair before Usayd converted to Islam. Bin Al-Hudayr, and Saad bin Muadh, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between him and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and he witnessed Badr and Uhud. He was among those who remained steadfast with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud when the people departed, and he witnessed the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him except Tabuk, for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, succeeded him in Medina when he went out to it, and he was among those who killed Ka’b ibn The most honorable"
"5837","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ash'ath bin Abi Al-Sha'atha', he said: I heard Abu Burdah narrating, on the authority of Tha'labah bin Dubay'ah, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, saying: ""I do not know... “A man who will not be harmed by strife, Muhammad bin Maslamah.” So we came to Medina, and behold, a tent was destroyed, and in it was Muhammad bin Maslamah. Al-Ansari, so I asked him, and he said: I will not settle in Egypt from their lands until this strife is over from the Muslim community.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5837 - True"
"5838","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash'ath bin Abi Al-Sha'atha', on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: Hudhayfah said: “I know a man who is not harmed by strife.” So we came to Medina, and behold... Fustat was beaten, and when Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Ansari, we asked him and he said: We will not involve anything bad from their fate until the matter is cleared. As was revealed, “This is a great virtue with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"5839","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abdullah bin Musa bin Shaybah told me. Al-Ansari, Ibrahim bin Sarmah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah, on the authority of his uncle Sahl Ibn Abi Hathamah said: I was sitting with Muhammad Ibn Maslamah, and the daughter of Al-Dahhak Ibn Khalifa passed by, and he began to chase her with his gaze, and I said: Glory be to Him. By God, you are doing this, and you are the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If he throws “God’s proposal to a woman is in a man’s heart, so there is no harm in him looking at her.” This is a strange hadith, and Ibrahim bin Sarmah is not a condition of this. “The book”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5839 - Strange"
"5840","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Ibrahim bin Jafar told me Bin Mahmoud bin Muhammad bin Maslamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that Muhammad bin Maslamah, and Abu Abbas bin Jabr, and Abbad bin Bishr killed Ka’b bin Al-Ashraf, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when he looked at them: “The faces were successful.” True. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Who is Ka’b bin The most honorable? For he has harmed God and His Messenger, but they did not expel him. With complete driving that
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5840 - True"
"5841","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Makki told us, Muhammad bin Talha Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Abi Abs bin Muhammad bin Abi Abs, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Ka’b bin Al-Ashraf was, He says: Poetry, and he leaves on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and comes out in two covers. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who has Ibn al-Ashraf for me?” Has he harmed God and His Messenger? Then Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Harithi said: O Messenger of God, would you like me to kill him? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent, then he said: “Go to Saad bin Muadh and consult him.” He said: I went to Saad bin Muadh and mentioned that to him, and he said: Go, with God’s blessing, and take with you my nephew Al-Harith bin Aws bin Muadh, and through Abbad bin Bishr Al-Ashhalili, and through Abu Abbas bin Jabr Al-Harithi, and through Abu Na’il Salkan bin Qais Al-Ashhalili, he said: So I met them and mentioned that to them, and they all came to me except Silkan, and said: O son of my brother, you are trustworthy to me, but I do not like to do anything to anyone. That was something until the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, healed him. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Go with your companions.” He said: So we went out to him at night until we came to him in a fortress, and Abbad bin Bishr wrote a verse about that, explaining in verse their killing and their doctrine, and he said:
 [abundant sea]
 I shouted at him, but he did not respond to my voice...and came up from above the wall.
 So I went back to him and he said: Who is the caller? ...So I said: Your brother, Abbad bin Bishr.
 And this is our armor as a mortgage, so take it... for two months, or within a month or half a month.
 He said: People who are thirsty and hungry... and they are not deprived of wealth except poverty.
 Then he came towards us quickly...and said to us: You have come for a matter.
 And in our right hands are mourning eggs... tested with them for us to iron and burn.
 So I said to my friend, when he saw me... Swords will come to him like the slaughter of a camel.
 And Ibn Maslamah Al-Muradi embraced him... shouting at him like a roaring lion.
 He drew his sword and stabbed it... and Abu Abbas bin Jabr cut it.
 And God was our sixth guardian... with the best blessing and the most dear victory.
 And at his head came a noble group... Hud came to them of truth and righteousness.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5841 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5842","Ali bin Isa Al-Hiri told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib bin Abi Omar told me, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, I heard Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, says: Othman, may God be pleased with him, sent me with fifty horsemen to Dhu Khashab, and our prince Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Ansari, then a man came with a Qur’an around his neck and a sword in his hand, and his eyes were shedding tears, and he said: This man commands us to attack this according to what is in it."
"5843","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abu Laila Abdullah bin Sahl, one of the Banu Haritha, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who Is this evil person welcome? Then Muhammad bin Maslamah said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: “Go to him, O God, help him.” Then Muhammad bin Maslamah stood up, and Jabir said: By God, I have never seen a war between two men like it when one of them approached his friend. A tree fell between them, and one of them took refuge from his companion. When he took cover from it, his companion found what was next to him until He reached it, but they continued to twist it with their swords, so Muhammad bin Maslamah struck his sword with the spear, and his sword fell into it, and he could not It is welcome that he took out his sword, and Muhammad struck him and killed him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, given that the narrations are narrated.” With many chains of narrations that Marhab’s killer, the Commander of the Faithful, was Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, including:"
"5844","Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi did not tell us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Narsi and Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi told us, they said: Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated to us. Al-Qaisi, narrated to us by Auf bin Abi Jamila, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Buraydah Al-Aslami, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when it was revealed In the presence of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tomorrow I will give the general-general to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger will love,” so when The next day, a group of his companions attacked him. “So he called Ali while he was gray-haired. He spit in his eyes, gave him the standard, and the people rose with him.” They met The people of Khaybar were greeted before them, shaking, and then he was saying:
 [The sea of rage]

 Khaybar has learned that I am welcome... He who wields weapons is a proven hero.
 When the swords come blazing... Sometimes I stab, and sometimes I strike.
 So he and Ali differed with two blows, and Ali hit him on the head until the sword bit his molars, and the soldiers heard the sound of his blow. So he killed him, and the last of the people did not come until it was opened for the first of them. “This is a big door. I have opened it among the gates.”"
"5845","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Muhammad bin Omar told me Al-Waqidi, Abd al-Malik ibn Zaid ibn Sa`id ibn Zaid ibn Amr ibn Nufayl ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Rabah ibn Razah ibn Adi told me. Ibn Ka’b Ibn Luayy, “Amr Ibn Nufayl, and Al-Khattab Ibn Nufayl, Omar’s father, are paternal brothers.”"
"5846","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told me, Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid al-Harrani told us, my father told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, On the authority of Urwa, he said: Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl came from the Levant after “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Badr, and he spoke The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck him with his arrow and said: And your reward, O Messenger of God. He said: And your reward?"
"5847","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq in naming someone Some of the Muslims witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Banu Adiy bin Ka’b bin Fihr bin Malik. He said: “And Sa’id bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufail bin Abdul-Uzza bin Rabah bin Qart bin Razah bin Adiy bin Kaab bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fahr bin Malik, And his mother is Fatima bint Bajah from Khuza’a. He came from the Levant after the arrival of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Badr. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck Peace be upon him with his arrow. He said: And what will I do, O Messenger of God? He said: “And your reward.”"
"5848","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulaymi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Jafar bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, “Sa’id bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl was nicknamed Abu Al-Awar.”"
"5849","Khalaf bin Muhammad al-Bukhari told me, Muhammad bin Harith told us, Amr bin Ali told us, he said: “Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl Adam was He was tall and hairy, and he was nicknamed Abu Al-A'war."
"5850","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Sahl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that, “Crying was heard at the funeral of Sa’id bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl as he was leaving the city on the day Friday, so he went out to it and did not witness the Friday prayer.” Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, I am Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Thana Hushaym and mentioned it in a similar way.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5850 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5851","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, whose father was Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, had departed from the religion of his people from Quraysh, and died while Quraysh was building the Kaaba. This was five years before the revelation was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: He will be sent One nation, and Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr converted to Islam before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house of Al-Arqam, and before he called There people converted to Islam, and Saeed bin Zaid witnessed Uhud, the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not bear witness. “full moon”
 Ibn Umar said: Abd al-Malik ibn Zaid, one of the descendants of Sa`id ibn Zaid, told me on the authority of his father. He said: “Sa`id ibn Zaid died in al-Aqiq, so he carried The necks of men, and he was buried in Medina, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas and Ibn Umar descended into his pit. That was in the year fifty or fifty-one, and he was On the day he died, he was seventy-two years old.” Ibn Umar said: “And his mother was Fatima bint Ba’ja bin Umayyah bin Khuwaylid bin Al-Mu’awwidh bin Hayyan. Ibn Ghunaim”"
"5852","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Zaid bin Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Zaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of his father, “Saad bin Abi Waqqas Saeed bin Zaid bathed with the tree.”"
"5853","Abu Bakr bin Muslih al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Mahmoud bin Muhammad al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Baqiyya told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Muharib Ibn Dathar, Ibn Sa'id Ibn Zaid told me, he said: Muawiyah sent to Marwan Ibn Al-Hakam in Medina to pledge allegiance To his son Yazid, and Sa`id bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl was absent, so he began to wait for him, and a man from the Levant said to Marwan: What is keeping you prisoner? He said: Until Saeed bin Zaid comes, for he is the chief of the people of Medina, so if he pledges allegiance, the people will pledge allegiance. He said: “Then Saeed bin Zaid delayed until he took Marwan pledged allegiance, but Saeed withheld the pledge of allegiance.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5853 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5854","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Karama told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu Abdul Ghaffar, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: Sa’d washed Sa’id ibn Zaid and embalmed him, Then he came home and took a bath, then he said: “I did not take a bath from the time I washed him, but I took a bath from the heat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5854 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5855","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Nufail bin Hisham bin Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, on the authority of his father, that his grandfather Saeed bin Zaid asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his father. Zaid, and he said: O Messenger of God, Abu Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl was as you saw and as you heard, and if he had caught you, he would have believed in you, so ask forgiveness for him. He said: “Yes.” So he asked forgiveness for him and said: “For he will come on the Day of Resurrection as one nation.” As they mentioned, he was seeking religion, and he died while seeking it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5855 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5856","Abu Al-Abbas narrated to us, Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr narrated to me, that Muhammad bin Abdullah Ibn Al-Husayn told him that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab and Sa’id Ibn Zaid said: O Messenger of God, do you ask forgiveness for Zaid? He said: “Yes,” so they asked forgiveness for him. He said: “He will be resurrected as one nation.”"
"5857","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Zayd Ibn Amr Ibn Nufayl, he said: “You have seen me, and Omar is my trustee, and my mother, meaning the mother of Saeed Ibn Zaid He wants me to follow Islam, and if anyone had renounced or refused, he would have been punished for what you did to Uthman, may God be pleased with him.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5857 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5858","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Duhaim Al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i, on the authority of Omar bin Sa’id bin Shuraih, that Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, I think, on the authority of his father, that Sa’id Ibn Zaid told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ten people in Paradise will be Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Al-Zubayr, and Talha. And Abd al-Rahman, Sa`d, Abu Ubaidah bin al-Jarrah, and these are nine.” Then he remained silent and said: We ask you by God, will you not tell us who The tenth, and he said: “You called me to God by God, the father of one-eyed in Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5858 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5859","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, she said: I saw Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl standing with his back to the Kaaba, saying: “O people of Quraysh, “Today there is no one among you who follows the religion of Abraham except me.” And he was greeting the friendly woman, saying to the man if he wanted to kill his daughter: “Wait. Do not kill her, I will suffice you with her provisions.” So he took her, and when she grew up, he said to her father: “If you wish, I will give her to you, and if you wish, I will give her to you.” Its provisions are sufficient for you.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"5860","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubayr, in mentioning “Whoever of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained behind in Tabuk, Ka’b bin Malik bin Al-Qayn bin Ka’b bin Sawad bin Ghanam bin Saad, he told us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5861","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “ Ka'b bin Malik bin Abi Ka'b bin Al-Qayn bin Ka'b bin Sawad bin Ghanam bin Ka'b bin Salamah, and he is the poet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And it was said that he was nicknamed Abu Abdullah, and Ka’b witnessed Uhud and was wounded with it twelve times and inherited, but he did not witness Badr. He witnessed the trench and all the sights with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except Tabuk. He stayed away from it and was one of the three who They fell behind in the Battle of Tabuk, then he repented against them, and Ka’b ibn Malik died in the year fifty in the emirate of Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and he was at that time “Seventy-seven years old.”"
"5862","Abu Nu`aym Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafari told me about Marw, Abdan ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Hafiz told us, Zakaria ibn Abi told us Kinanah, Abd al-Rahman bin Amr told us, Yahya bin al-Muthanna al-Madani told us, Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “commanded Ka’b ibn Malik when he accepted his repentance, and that his companions should pray two rak’ahs or ""Two prostrations""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5862 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5863","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Ma’bad told me Ibn Ka'b Ibn Malik Ibn Abi Ka'b Ibn Al-Qayn, brother of Banu Salamah, that his brother was Ubayd Allah Ibn Ka'b, and he was one of the most knowledgeable of the Ansar. He told him that his father Ka’b told him - and Ka’b bin Malik witnessed Aqaba and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace - and said: “ We went out on pilgrimage from Medina, and Al-Baraa bin Ma’rur said to us: O these people, I have seen a vision, and by God I do not know whether you agree with me or not. No? He said: We said: What is that? He said: I decided not to leave this intention behind me. He mentioned the hadith in its length, and I think that I might. I narrated it in mention of Al-Bara’ bin Ma’rur, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5864","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told me in Bukhara, I am Abu Khalifa, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told me, Abu told me Ubaida Muammar bin Al-Muthanna said: “Al-Hakam bin Amr bin Mujad’ bin Hudhaym bin Al-Harith bin Nu’ayla bin Malik bin Damra bin Bakr Ibn Abd Manat Ibn Kinana”"
"5865",""
"5866","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Al-Hakam bin Amr bin Mujad’ bin Hudhaym bin Al-Harith bin Nu’ayla bin Malik bin Damrah bin Bakr bin Abd Manat bin Kinanah, And Nu'ayla, the brother of Ghaffar ibn Mulaik, accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he was arrested. Then he went to Basra and settled there, and Ziyad ibn Ubai appointed him as governor. Sufyan ruled over Khurasan until he died there in the year fifty.”"
"5867","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Tajer told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh al-Sahmi told us, Muhammad bin Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani told us, Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulayman told us, my father told me, on the authority of Abu Hajib, he said: I was with Al-Hakam bin Amr Al-Ghafari when the messenger of Ali bin Abi came to him. Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: The Commander of the Faithful says to you: You are most deserving of helping us in this matter. He said: I heard my friend, Ibn Your uncle, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the matter is like this or like this, take a wooden sword.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5867 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5868","Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman al-Ghafari told me about Marw, and Abdan bin Muhammad al-Hafiz told us. I heard Ahmad bin Shayban say: “Al-Hakam bin Amr, Rafi’ bin Amr, and Ali bin Amr accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then Ziyad assumed power over Khorasan, and this was the reason He died because he prayed for himself while he was passing through a letter that was read to him, and he received a response from Ziyad, and another from Muawiyah, so his prayer was answered, and he died. Buraydah al-Aslami had died before him, so we were all buried in the Husayn cemetery in Marw, opposite the Hammam of Abu Hamza al-Sukkari. I visited Their graves
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5868 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5869","So Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, said: Ziyad sent Al-Hakam bin Amr Al-Ghifari to Khorasan, and they captured many spoils, so he wrote to him: As for what follows, The Commander of the Faithful wrote to choose the white and the yellow for himself, and not to divide gold or silver among the Muslims, so the arbitrator wrote to him: “But After that, you wrote mentioning the book of the Commander of the Faithful, and I found the book of God before the book of the Commander of the Faithful, and I swear by God that if The heavens and the earth were a bond for a servant, so he feared God. He would make for him a way out from among them, and peace. He divided it among them, and when Muawiyah did what the arbitrator did in dividing the fae, the one who bound and imprisoned him directed at him, and he died in his chains. He was buried in it, and he said: “I am a quarrel.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5869 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5870","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, I told us Humayd and Yunus, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of al-Hasan, that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghafari to command an army, and Imran ibn Husayn met him in The emirate went around among the people and said to him: Do you know what I have come to you for? Do you not remember that when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was informed that his prince said to him: Get up and fall into the fire, so the man got up to fall into it and it overtook him. So he caught him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he had fallen into it, he would have entered Hell. There is no obedience in disobeying God.” Al-Hakam said: Yes, Imran said: It is only I wanted to remind you of this hadith: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5870 - True"
"5871",""
"5872","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “And Rafi’ ibn Amr ibn Mujad’ ibn Hudhaym ibn Al-Harith Al-Ghaffari, and he died in Basra in the year fifty.”"
"5873","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Omar bin Hafs al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “After me there will be a people from my nation who recite The Qur’an will not go beyond their throats. They will leave the religion just as an arrow leaves a target, then they will not return therein. Their marks will soar.” Abdullah bin Al-Samit: I met Rafi’ ibn Amr, the brother of Al-Hakam ibn Amr Al-Ghafari, and I said to him: What hadith did I hear from Abu Dhar such-and-such, so I mentioned to him Hadith, and he said: How do you like this? I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5873 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5874","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Mu’tamar bin Suleiman told us, Ibn al-Hakam bin Amr al-Ghifari told me, on the authority of his uncle Rafi’ bin Amr al-Ghifari, who said: I used to throw palm trees for the Ansar, and I was a boy. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me and said: “O boy, why do you throw the palm trees?” So I said: I eat. He said: “Do not throw the palm trees or anything that falls below them.” Then he wiped my head and said: “O God, satisfy his stomach.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5874 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5875","And Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Muadh bin Asad Al-Marwazi told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa, Salih bin Abi Jaafar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Ghafari, he said: I was throwing palm trees for the Ansar. So they took me and took me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: This one shoots our palm trees. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Rafi’, why do you throw away their palm trees?” I said: O Messenger of God, hunger. He said: “So whatever happens, may God satisfy you and satisfy you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5875 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5876","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Sa’id Abd al-Rahman bin Samra bin Habib bin Abd Shams, and his mother is Arwa bint Abi al-Far’ah bin Ka’b bin Amr bin Tarif bin Khuzaymah ibn Alqamah ibn Khadash ibn Ghanam ibn Malik ibn Kinanah died in Basra in the year fifty, and Ziyad prayed over him and walked in His funeral"
"5877","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman told us. Ibn Jawshan, on the authority of his father, said: I went out at the funeral of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, and Ziyad walked in front of the funeral, and some of his loyal men They walked on their heels in front of the funeral, and said: Little by little, may God bless you. He said: Then Abu Bakra joined us on some of the road to al-Mirabad. When he saw those people and what they were doing, he attacked them with force and attacked them with the whip, so he said: “Be alone, by the One who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “I saw that we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were almost throwing sand with it.”"
"5878","Ali bin Hamshadh and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he heard Al-Hasan says: Abd al-Rahman bin Samra bin Habib bin Abd Shams told us:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5877 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5879","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abdul Rahman bin Othman bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah. He is the nephew of Talha bin Ubaid Allah, and his mother is Amira bint Jadaan bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah, and he is the nephew of Abdullah bin Judaan Al-Qurashi.”"
"5880","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ishaq bin Wahb Al-Alaf told us, Ya’qub bin Muhammad told us Al-Zuhri, Muhammad bin Talha Al-Taymi told us, Othman bin Abdul Rahman bin Othman Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I converted to Islam on the day of the Conquest, “So I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5881","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Muhammad ibn Talha al-Taymi told us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman, my brother told me, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman was injured along with Ibn al-Zubayr, “so Ibn al-Zubayr ordered that he be buried in a mosque.” The Kaaba, then he ordered the horses over his grave at night to hide his tracks.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5881 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5882","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Khaled. Al-Qarizi, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Othman Al-Taymi, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a good medicine with him, and the mention of a frog is medicine, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade killing it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5882 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5883","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Uthman Bin Abi Al-Aas bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Hammam Al-Thaqafi, nicknamed Abu Abdullah. He died in the year fifty.”"
"5884","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Hamid bin Sahl Al-Thaghari told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, was at the funeral of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, and he said: We were walking lightly. He said: Then Abu Bakra rose He whipped his whip and said: “You saw us sanding with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5884 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5885","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “ Sufyan bin Awf Al-Ghamidi was from the people of Homs, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was a man of courage, help, and generosity. He who raided Hit and Anbar in the days of Ali and killed and took captive. He was among those who killed Hassan bin Hassan Al-Bakri, the brother of Al-Harith bin Hassan. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Qayla bint Makhramah. He addressed Ali, may God be pleased with him, and said in his sermon: Ghamid’s brother has He raided Hit and Anbar, and he was in charge of Sawaif in the days of Muawiyah, and Muawiyah used to magnify his affairs and say that he was in council. One on a thousand Qarihs, and Muawiyah used it after him on the Sawaifs Ibn Masoud Al-Fazari, so it was said:
 [Long Sea]

 O Ibn Masoud, establish a cross channel... as Sufyan bin Awf used to establish it.
 O Ibn Masoud, mark the city of Caesar... as Sufyan bin Awf used to mark it.
 “And Sufyan of Qurum was from the tribe of Qurm... there was a tent among the people, and there was no living person among the people to accommodate it.”"
"5886","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah was nicknamed Abu Abdullah, the governor of Kufa, and he died there in the year fifty.”"
"5887","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Azhari told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Al-Baraa told us. Al-Madini, he said: “Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah bin Abi Aamir bin Masoud bin Mu’tab bin Malik bin Amr bin Saad bin Amr bin Qais Bin Shaybah bin Bakr bin Hawazin bin Mansour bin Ikrimah bin Khasfa bin Qais”"
"5888","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Al-Hasan bin Shuja’ told me, Ahmad bin Abi Rafi’ told us, Al-Qasim bin Yazid told us Al-Jarami - and he was one of the last people of his time - on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called me Abu Jesus.”"
"5889","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah bin Abi Aamer bin Masoud bin Mu'tab bin Malik bin Ka'b bin Amr bin Saad bin Awf bin Thaqif, and his name is Qusayy bin Munabbih bin Bakr bin Hawazin bin Mansour bin Ikrimah bin Khasfa bin Qais bin Ghaylan bin Mudar bin Nizar, and his nickname was Abu Abdullah, and he was called the one who changed his mind, and he was shrewd and could not find two matters in his mind unless he found a way out in one of them. He approached the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he stayed with him until he performed the Umrah of Al-Hudaybiyyah in Dhul-Qa’dah in the sixth year of the Hijra. Al-Mughirah said: So it was The first trip I went out with him on, and I was with Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, and he kept the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, obligated, so who would he abide by? After that, Al-Mughirah witnessed the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a Thaqif delegation came and visited them and honored them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him and Abu Sufyan bin Harb to Taif, and they defeated his brigades."
"5890","Abu Ahmad Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Hashimi told us in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Yunus bin Al-Harith told us Al-Taifi, Abu Aoun Al-Thaqafi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, he sent me Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, to the people of Buhaira, then I witnessed Al-Yamamah, then I witnessed the conquests of Syria with the Muslims, then I witnessed Yarmouk, so my eye was injured on the day of Yarmouk, then I witnessed Al-Qadisiyah, and I was Saad’s messenger to Rustum, and I was assigned conquests to Omar ibn Al-Khattab. And I conquered Hamdan, and I was on the flank of al-Nu`man ibn Muqrin on the day of Nahavand, and Umar had written: If al-Nu`man dies, then the prince is Hudhayfah, and if Hudhayfah died, and Prince Mughirah died, and I was the first to draw up the Diwan of Basra, and I gathered the people to give, and I appointed Kufa to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Omar was killed, and I was in charge of it, then I handed it over to Muawiyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5890 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5891","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abdullah told me Ibn Muhammad Ibn Omar Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “When Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah cast his ring in The grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: People do not say that you descended in the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you do not tell people that your seal is in “His grave.” Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, came down and saw its location, so he took it and pushed it to him.
 Ibn Umar said: Musa al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah died in Kufa in Sha’ban in the year fifty, and he was the son of Seventy years during the caliphate of Muawiyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5891 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5892","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Zahid told us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Qahtaba ibn Marzuq al-Talhi told us, Muhammad ibn al-Talhi told us Nafi’ al-Karabisi al-Basri told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Abu Ka’b, the owner of the silk, told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Bakra, He said: “We were sitting at the door of the little boy in the mosque - meaning the gate of Ghaylan: Abu Bakra - and his brother Nafi’ and Shibl bin Ma’bad, then he came Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah was walking in the shade of the mosque, and the mosque at that time was made of reeds. He went to Abu Bakra and greeted him, and said to him: Abu Bakra: O Prince, what took you out of the Emirate’s residence? He said: I am speaking to you. Abu Bakra said to him: You are not allowed to do that, Prince. He sits in his house, and sends to whomever he wishes. So he spoke to them and said: O Abu Bakra: There is no harm in what I do. So he entered through the door of the smallest. Until a woman from Qays came to the door of Umm Jamil. He said: There was a road between the house of Abu Abdullah and the woman’s house, so he entered upon her. Abu Tomorrow: I have no patience for this, so he sent for a servant of his and said to him: Go up from my room and look through the window. So he went and looked and did not stay. If he came back and said: I found them in a quilt, then he said to the people: Get up with me, so they got up, so Abu Bakra started and looked and came back.Then he said to his brother: Look. He looked and said: What did you see? He said: I saw adultery, then he said: What is the matter with you? Look, he looked and said: What did you see? He said: I saw adultery as being forbidden. He said: I bear God's witness against you. They said: Yes. He said: So he went back to his family and wrote to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab about what he had seen. Then a terrible matter came to him, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he did not Soon he sent Abu Musa al-Ash'ari as the governor of Basra, so Abu Musa sent to al-Mughirah to stay for three days as governor. Yourself, when the fourth day comes, you and Abu Bakra and his witnesses depart. Blessed are you if you are lied to, and woe to you. If he is truthful to you, then the people set off from Abu Bakra, his witnesses, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah until they presented Medina to the Commander of the Faithful, and he said: Give me what you have, O Abu Bakra. He said: I bear witness that I saw adultery being committed. Then they presented his brother Abu Abdullah, and he testified. He said: I bear witness. Indeed, I saw adultery being committed. Then they brought Shibl ibn Ma`bad al-Bajli, and he asked him and he testified likewise. Then they brought Ziyad, and he said: What did you see? He said: I saw them in a blanket, and I heard loud breathing, and I do not know what was behind that, so Omar grew proud and rejoiced when he escaped the raiders and defeated the people. more,He said: The Commander of the Faithful, Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was the governor of Utbah bin Ghazwan of Basra, and he arrived there in the year sixteen. He died in the year nineteen, and Utba hated that and prayed to God to save him from it, so he fell from his mount on the road and died. May God have mercy on him, then what happened was the matter with Al-Mughirah.”"
"5893","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Sulaiman told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: “Egypt was conquered in the year twenty, and the Euphrates was conquered by force. It was said: It was conquered by Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, and it was Utba bin Ghazwan appointed him as his successor, and he went to Omar, and Omar ordered Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah to Basra, and he wrote to him after him, and he was one of “His matter and the matter of Umm Jamil al-Qaysiyah were not the same.”"
"5894","Al-Zubair bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told me, Muhammad bin Hammad told me, Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sirri told me, Hisham bin Al-Kalbi told me, Abd told me. Al-Rahman bin Saeed Al-Kindi said: “We witnessed the funeral of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah. When he was lowered into his pit, a man stood over her and said: Who This marmos? So we said: The Emir of Kufa, Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah. By God, he soon said:
 [Long Sea]
 I draw a land in al-Mughirah that will be known...on it are hills of jinn and mankind that will be known.
 So if you have left Haman after us... and Pharaoh, then know that the one who has the throne will do justice.
 He said: Then they came to him and insulted him. By God, I do not know which path he took. The governorship of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah of Kufa was for seven years."
"5895","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdul Hamid told me, a partner told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, I heard Jarir saying at the funeral of Al-Mughira bin Shu’bah: “Ask forgiveness for your prince, for he loved good health.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5895 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5896","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, that a man came, Then he called Abu Issa to ask permission to come to the Commander of the Faithful, Omar. Omar said: Who is Abu Issa? Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: I am. Then Omar said: Did Jesus have a father? As for the Arabs’ nicknames that you conceal, Abu Abdullah and Abu Abd al-Rahman, and a man said: “I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, calling her al-Mughirah.” Then Omar said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called her al-Mughirah. He has been forgiven for his previous and future sins, and we are in a state of solitude and we do not know what will be done to us, so we called him Abu Abdullah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5896 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5897","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Azhari told us, Abu Bakr bin Raja told us, Dawud bin Rasheed told us, Al-Haytham bin Adi told us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Sa`id, Ibn Ayyash, and Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: “Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah resided in Kufa for ten years, and he died in the year Fifty, so Muawiya annexed Kufa to Ziyad. The narrations have been authentic, that Al-Mughirah was the ruler of Kufa in the year forty-one, and he perished in the year fifty-one."
"5898","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari Al-Qadi, Ahmed bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zalim, who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah used to receive his sermon from Ali, He set up preachers who criticized him, and while he was delivering a sermon, he criticized Ali, and next to me was Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufail Al-Adawi, and he said: He hit me with his hand and said: “Don’t you see what this is saying? - Or did these people say - I bear witness that the nine are in Paradise, and if I had sworn on the tenth, I would have been truthful. We would have been with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In Hira, I, Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Saad, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and the mountain shook,” so the Prophet said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Stay firm, Hira’, for there is no one against you except a prophet, a truthful person, or a martyr.”"
"5899","Ibrahim bin Firas al-Faqih told us in Mecca, Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf al-Tanisi told us, al-Hakam bin Hisham told us Al-Thaqafi, Abd al-Malik ibn Umair narrated to me, on the authority of Warid, the servant of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, he said: We walked with One night, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck his hand on the neck of my camel, then said: “Do you have water?” I said: Yes, this is a sheet of water with me. He said: So he went down and fulfilled his need, then he came to me and said: “Do you want to do something?” I said: No. “So he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, blew his nose three times, and washed his face three times. Then he wanted to remove his arms, and there was a cloak of The wool was tight, so he was unable to remove his arms from it, so he took his hands out from under the robe, then washed his arms three times, then wiped with his head and wiped over his socks.” Then we walked and caught up with the people, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf led them in prayer. I wanted to call him to the place of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prevented me, so we prayed, then we performed the second verse: “It is strange, with a valid chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5899 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5900","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abdullah bin Hammad bin Numayr told us, Husayn told me Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I witnessed Al-Qadisiyah, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah set off, and when Ibn Rustum came to the bed, he jumped up. So he sat with him on his bed, and they were astonished, so Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said to them: “What are you afraid of about this?” Now I will stand up and return to what I was doing, and your companion will return to what he was doing.” They said: Tell us what brought you here? Al-Mughirah said: “We were misguided, so God sent among us a prophet who guided us to his religion and provided for us, and among what he provided for us was a grain that would be in this country of yours. When we ate from it and fed it to our families.” They said: We have no patience until you send us to this country. They said: Then we will kill you. They said: If you kill us we will enter Paradise, and if we kill you You entered the fire
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5900 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary due to its weakness"
"5901","Ali bin Hamshadh and Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Umayyah bin Bastam told us, Yazid bin Zurai’, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf told us, Iyas bin Muawiyah bin Qurra told me, on the authority of his father, he said: When it was the Day of al-Qadisiyah, he was sent Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah to the companion of Faris, and he said: “Send ten with me, so they were sent, and he tied his clothes over him, then he took a shroud, then set off until They came to him, and he said: “Throw me a shield.” So he sat on it, and Al-Alaj said: You Arabs have recognized the one who made you come to us. You are a people who do not find in your country enough food to be satisfied with, so take it and we will give you the food you need, for we are a Magian people, and we hate it. He killed you because you are defiling our land. Al-Mughirah said: “By God, that is not what brought us. Rather, we were a people who worshiped stones.” And idols, so if we see a stone better than another stone, we throw it and take another, and we do not know a Lord until God sends to us a messenger from Ourselves, so he called us to Islam and we followed him, and we did not come for food. We were commanded to fight our enemy who had abandoned Islam, and we did not come for food. But we have come to fight you and take your descendants, and as for the food you mentioned, we will never find food enough to satisfy us in my life. Perhaps we did not find any irrigation water at times, so we came to this land of yours and found therein abundant food and abundant water. By God, no We will give it away until it is ours or yours.” Al-Alj said in Persian: “He is right.” He said: “And you should gouge out your eye,” and his eye was gouged out the next day by an arrow that struck him “a stranger with a valid chain of transmission, and they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5901 - True"
"5902","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “He died Rukana bin Abd Yazid bin Hashim bin Al-Muttalib bin Abd Manaf in Medina at the beginning of the emirate of Muawiyah in the year forty.”"
"5903","Sheikh Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Bakr bin Qais told us: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Ammar told us, Muhammad bin Rabi’ah, Abu Al-Hasan Al-Asqalani told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Rukanah bin Abd Yazid told us, on the authority of his father that, “He wrestled with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck him down.” Rukana said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The difference between us and the polytheists is turbans over skullcaps.”"
"5904","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Amr bin died Al-Aas bin Wael bin Hashim bin Saeed bin Sahm bin Amr bin Husays bin Kaab bin Luay bin Ghalib, and his mother, Al-Nabigha, daughter Harmala bin Al-Harith bin Kulthum bin Jawshan bin Amr bin Abdullah bin Khuzaymah bin Anza bin Asad bin Rabi’ah bin Nizar, He was short and dyed black, and it was said: Al-Nabigha bint Harmala bin Sabiyah from Anza, and his brother from his mother was Urwa bin Umamah. Al-Adawi, who emigrated from Abyssinia, and his brother Hisham bin Al-Aas, was killed as a martyr on the day of Ajnadayn, and it has been said that Amr bin Al-Aas died In the year fifty-one, and God knows best.”"
"5905","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Musa bin Al-Hassan, and Abdullah bin Mihran Al-Dair told us, they said: Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ibn Al-Aas.” “Two believers: Hisham and Amr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5905 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5906","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abi Masarrat Al-Makki told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Harmala bin Imran told us, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Abu Firas, the servant of Amr bin Al-Aas, that Omar, when death approached him, He said to his son Abdullah: “If I die, wash me, shroud me, and tie my garment - or my garment - over me, for I am quarreling. So, walk quickly with me, and if you place me in the prayer place, and that is the day of Eid, either breaking the fast or Eid al-Adha, then look at the mouths of the roads. If... One day remains, and the people have gathered, so begin the funeral prayer for me, then the Eid prayer. When you put me alone, cover me with dust, for my right side is not I have more right to the dirt than my left side, so when you level the dirt on me, then sit by my grave, slaughtering camels and cutting them up, I will find peace. “How are you?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5906 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5907","Ibrahim bin Ismat Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Hilal Al-Rasibi told us, on the authority of Qatada, He said: When Amr ibn Al-Aas was about to die, he said: “Measure of my wealth.” They measured it and found it to be fifty-two mudds, so he said: “Who will take it from what is in it?” “I wish it were barren.” He said: The tide was sixteen ounces, of which an ounce was two cups. “Amr ibn Al-Aas died on the day of the breaking of the fast, and he had reached the age of ninety-four. His son Abdullah prayed over him, and he was buried in Al-Muqattam in the year forty-three. Then Muawiya appointed his brother Utbah ibn Utbah to rule over Egypt and its affairs. Abu Sufyan»
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5907 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5908","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Amr bin Al-Aas bin Wael bin Hashim bin Saeed bin Sahm, nicknamed Abu Abdullah, and his mother, Al-Nabigha, was the daughter of a captive captive from a goat. His maternal brothers are Amr ibn Uthaath ibn Abbad ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf ibn Qusayy, and Unaif ibn Abi al-Aas ibn Umayyah. Ibn Abd Shams, and there was disagreement about the time of his death.”"
"5909","Abdullah bin Abi Yahya told me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: “Amr bin Al-Aas died on the day of Fitr in Egypt in the year two Forty-three, and he was its ruler, and I heard someone mentioning that he died in the year forty-three, and I heard some scholars mentioning that He died in the year fifty-one.” The most correct thing I heard was at the time of the death of Amr ibn al-Aas:"
"5910","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Amr bin Muhammad died Al-Aas in the year forty-three, and was buried in Egypt.”"
"5911","Then Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Abu Yahya informed me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir informed me, he said: “Amr bin Al-Aas bin Wael came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year eight. He was nicknamed Abu Abdullah, and he died in Egypt on the day of Fitr. In the year forty-two, and he was its ruler.”"
"5912","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Rashid, the client of Habib ibn Aws, Amr ibn al-Aas narrated to me, from his narration, he said: I went out intending to go to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted Aslam, and I met Khaled bin Al-Walid, that was before the conquest, and he was coming from Mecca, so I said: “Where do you want, Abu Suleiman?” He said: By God, the mark has been straightened, and the man is a prophet. I will go, and by God, I will submit until when. I said: “By God, I have not come except To convert to Islam, so we went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Khalid bin Al-Walid came forward and converted to Islam and pledged allegiance, then I approached and pledged allegiance to him, then I left"
"5913","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram told us, in Baghdad, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Sa`id bin Ufayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shamasa, who said: “Amr bin al-Aas was short and weak.”"
"5914","Abd al-Samad bin Ali told us, Abu al-Ahwas al-Qadi told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told me, about Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saw Amr bin Al-Aas His gray hair had turned black, and it was like the wing of a crow. He said: “What is this, O Abu Abdullah?” He said: Commander of the Faithful, I would like for you to see a remnant in me. So Omar, may God be pleased with him, did not forbid him from that, nor did he blame him for it, and Amr bin died. Al-Aas and his age was about one hundred years.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5914 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5915","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Awana ibn al-Hakam, said: Amr ibn al-Aas used to say: “It is astonishing for someone to whom death befalls, and whose mind is with him, how can he not describe it.” When death befell him, his son Abdullah said to him: Describe death for us while your mind is with you. He said: “O my son, death is too great to be described, but I will describe to you some of it. I find myself as if there were mountains of Radwa on my neck, and I find myself as if I were in “My insides are the thorns of weapons, and I find myself as if my soul is emerging from the eye of a needle.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5915 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5916","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told me, Sa’id ibn Abi Maryam told me, Al-Layth and Ibn Lahi’ah told us, they said: Ibn Abi Habib reported, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Qays al-Tajibi, on the authority of Zuhair ibn Qais al-Balawi, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Rimthah al-Balawi, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Amr bin Al-Aas to Bahrain, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out in secret, and we went out with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fell asleep and then woke up and said: “May God have mercy on Omar.” He said: Then we remembered every human being whose name was Amr, so he fell asleep again. So he woke up and said: “May God have mercy on Omar.” Then he drowsed for the third time, then he woke up and said: “May God have mercy on Omar.” So we said: Who is Amr, O Messenger of God? He said: “Amr bin Al-Aas.” They said: What's wrong with him? He said: “I reminded him that whenever I used to call people to give charity, and he would give charity and I would be generous, I would say to him: Where did you get this from? So he says: From God, and Amr spoke the truth. Indeed, there is much good for Amr. Zuhayr said: “When the strife broke out, I said: ‘I will follow this one who has said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about it, but I did not separate from him. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5916 - True"
"5917","Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Ibrahim bin Maqil Al-Nasafi told us, Safwan bin Salih told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, On the authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Hibban ibn Abi Jablah, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not do justice to me.” And Khalid bin Al-Walid was one of his companions in his war since we converted to Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5917 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5918","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Ibn Bani Al-Muttalib bin Abd Manaf Qais bin Makhramah bin Al-Muttalib bin Abd Manaf, and his mother, Asma bint Amir, an Ansar woman.”"
"5919","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Al-Muttalib told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qays Ibn Makhramah Ibn Al-Muttalib Ibn Abd Manaf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were born May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. “In the year of the Elephant, we will be subjugated.”"
"5920",""
"5921","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Zakaria bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us The reciter, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Aqeel Zahra bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hisham, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, realized “His mother brought him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he wiped his head and prayed for him,” so he used to sacrifice one sheep on behalf of all his family."
"5922","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu al-Zanba’ Ruh ibn al-Faraj told us, Yahya ibn Bukair told us, Rishdin told us Ibn Saad, and Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Zahra Ibn Ma’abad, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah Ibn Hisham, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was holding the hand of Omar bin Al-Khattab, Omar said: By God, O Messenger of God, you are more beloved to me than everything except myself. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said hello: “Now, O Omar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5922 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5923","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Al-Munkadir bin Abdullah Ibn Al-Hudair Ibn Mahrez Ibn Abdul-Uzza Ibn Aamir Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Haritha Ibn Saad Ibn Taym Ibn Murrah The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted and listened to him.”"
"5924","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: Al-Munkadir bin Abd was God came to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, and complained to her about his need. She said: “The first thing that comes to me, I will send it to you.” Then ten thousand dirhams came to her, so she sent them to him, so he took a slave girl from her and she bore him his sons: Muhammad, Abu Bakr, and Omar. They were all mentioned for their righteousness, and the hadith was narrated from them."
"5925","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Harith bin Al-Sa’ib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever circumambulates around the Ka’bah for a week in which he does not idle, it will be like the size of a slave.” He frees her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5925 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5926","Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi Bhamdan told us from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin al-Mughirah al-Yashkari told us, al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Urni, Abdullah bin Amr bin Murrah told us, Muhammad bin Suqa told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said that “he went out one night and delayed the evening prayer until the night had passed for a while - or an hour - and the people were waiting in The mosque.” He said: “What are you waiting for?” They said: We wait for prayer. He said: “You will not stop praying as long as you wait for it.” Then he said: “It is a prayer that no one of the nations before you has prayed.” Then he raised his head to the sky and said: “The stars are a security for the people of the sky. If the stars are obliterated, then what they are promised will come to the sky, and I am a security for my companions. “So when I arrive, my companions will receive what they are promised, and my household will be a security for my nation. So when my household departs, my nation will deliver what they are promised.”"
"5927","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told me in Nishapur, Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Al-Aswad told us, about Urwa, “One of the names of the Companions of Aqaba who pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was from Banu Ghanam Ibn Malik Ibn Al-Najjar Abu Ayyub He is Khaled bin Zaid bin Kulayb bin Tha’labah.”"
"5928","Abu Sahl bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told me, in Baghdad. Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Azraq told me, Ahmad bin Al-Walid told me, Al-Walid bin told me. Muslim, Abdullah bin Lahi’ah and Al-Layth bin Saad told us, saying: Yazid bin Abi Habib told us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Tajibi, he said: They invaded us. Constantinople, and with us was Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, so we lined up in two rows. I had never seen two rows longer than them, and Abu Ayyub died. Al-Ansari in this invasion, and he “commanded that he be buried at the root of the walls of Constantinople, and that a debt be paid off, so he did so.”"
"5929","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between Abu Ayyub and Mus’ab bin Umair, and Abu Ayyub witnessed Badr, Uhud, and Khandaq. And all the scenes are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He died in the year Yazid bin Muawiyah invaded Constantinople in the succession of his father Muawiyah. In the year fifty-two, and his grave is at the base of the fortress of Constantinople in the land of the Romans. As mentioned, they visit his grave and visit it. And they draw water with it when they are parched.”"
"5930","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Musaddad told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, Ayoub told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Ayyub witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at Badr, and then no one remained behind from the Muslim invaders except him. There was only one year in it, for a young man was appointed to the army, and he sat out that year. After that, he became anxious and said: I don’t have to He was sent to work and fell ill, and Yazid bin Muawiyah was in charge of the army, so he came in to visit him and said: What do you need? He said: “My need is, if I die, mount, then run through the enemy’s land as long as you find a place to go. If you do not find a place to go, bury me and then come back.” He said: Abu Ayyub used to say: God Almighty said: {Go forth, light and heavy} [Al-Tawbah: 41], “I do not find me except light or heavy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5930 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5931","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Abu Dawud, Shu`bah told us, said: I said to al-Hakam: What did Abu Ayyub witness from the war of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them both? He said: “He witnessed with him the Day of Harura.”"
"5932","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Bakr, the muezzin at the Holy House, told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Musa Al-Lahouni told us, Yusuf bin Muhammad told us, Ibrahim bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was descending. Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was in a room, and his food was in a basket in the living room. Cats used to come from the window to take the food from the window. The basket. He complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “That ogre, so when she comes, tell her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, resolved that you should not return.” He said: So she came, and Abu Ayyub said to her: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has determined for you not to return. So she said: O Abu Ayyub, leave me alone. This time, by God, I will not leave her again. So he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. She said: That twice, then she said: May I teach you some words that, if you say them, no devil will come near your house that night, that day, and the next day? He said: Yes. She said: Read the verse of the Throne: {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Al-Baqarah: 255]. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. So he told him, and he said: “She told the truth, but it was a lie.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5932 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5933","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, I am Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyeh, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amra, on the authority of his father, that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari had a date grove in a garden in his house. So he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner [p. 520].
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5933 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5934","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, I am Abdan Al-Ahwazi, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, we told him Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of his brother Issa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that he had an oversight, So the ghouls used to come and take from him, so he mentioned the hadith in something like this: “These chains of narration, when they are combined, become a famous hadith. And God knows best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5934 - This is the best way to have hadith"
"5935","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Anas told us, Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, that Abu Ayyub came to Muawiyah and mentioned a matter to him. He said: Are you not Uthman’s companion? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us that after him an impact will befall us.” He said: What is the matter with you? He said: “He commanded us to be patient until we reach the basin.” He said: So be patient. He said: Abu Ayoub became angry and swore never to speak to him again. Then Abu Ayoub came to Abdullah bin Abbas and mentioned to him. So he left his house for him just as Abu Ayyub went out for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What do you want? He said: Four boys will be in my place. He said: I have twenty boys for you. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5935 - True"
"5936","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari came to Ibn Abbas in Basra and emptied his house for him, and said: “I will do to you what I did to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he said: “How much debt do you owe?” He said: Twenty thousand. He said: So he gave him forty thousand and twenty slaves, and said: “You have what is in the house.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5936 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5937","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan, Ibn Bukair told us, Abdullah bin Lahi’a told me, On the authority of Huyay, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that Abu Ayyub was in a gathering, and he said: Isn’t any of you able to To read a third of the Qur’an? He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them and heard Abu Ayyub, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Abu Ayyub has spoken the truth.”"
"5938","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah, and Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Simak, He said: I heard Jabir bin Samra say: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended upon Abu Ayyub, and whenever he ate food, he would send blessings to him with his grace. Then he would look at the place of the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and eat from where his hand was. One day he made food that contained garlic. So he sent it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned it. He came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, I did not see the traces of your fingers. He said: “It contained garlic.” Shu’bah said in his hadith: “Is it forbidden?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” And Hammad said in his hadith: “O Messenger of God, you sent me something that you did not eat.” He said: “You are not Like me, the angel comes to me.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5938 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5939","Abu Al-Walid the Imam told us, may God Almighty have mercy on him, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Handali told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, My father told me, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq saying: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of my father Umamah Al-Bahili, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended upon me, I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for me, I hate to be Above you, and you will be lower than me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I would rather be at the bottom when people cover us.” He said: I saw a pitcher of ours broken and its water spilled out, so Umm Ayyub and I got up with some velvet of ours, we have no quilts other than it, with which we dry the water until it reaches To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something that bothered him: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5939 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5940","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Ali bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended on me peace be upon him for a month, and I delved into all of his work, and I saw him “when the sun set - or deviated - or as he said - if he had in his hand the work of the world.” If he is asleep, it is as if he is awakened. He gets up and washes or performs ablution and prays, then he kneels four rak’ahs to complete the prayer. “And he treats them kindly and masters them.” When he wanted to set off, I said: O Messenger of God, you stayed with me for a month, and I wished you had stayed longer. From that, I delved into all of your work, and I saw you “when the sun has set or sets, and if you have in your hand the work of this world, you reject it, and you take to Prayer,” and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The gates of heaven will be opened at that hour, so the gates of heaven and the gates of Paradise will not shake. Until this prayer is prayed, I would love for something good to ascend to my Lord in those hours, and for my deeds to be taken up as the first deeds of worshippers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Talkhīsh Al-Dhahabi] 5940 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhīsh due to its weakness"
"5941","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mukhurami told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Firdous Al-Ash’ari told us, Masoud bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, That Abu Ayyub Khalid bin Zaid, who was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, camped in his house and invaded the land of the Romans, so he passed by Muawiyah, but Muawiyah killed him. Then he returned from his campaign and was cold-blooded and did not raise his head. Abu Ayyub said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us that we will see After him, a successor.” Muawiyah said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “He commanded us to be patient.” He said: “Then be patient.” Then Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, came to Basra, and Ali had ordered him May God be pleased with her, so he said: O Abu Ayyub, I want to go out to you from my dwelling just as you went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ordered his family to leave, and he gave him everything that was in the house. When it was time for him to leave, he said: What is your need? He said: What I need is my gift and eight servants who work on my land. His gift was four thousand, so he multiplied it for himself five times, and gave him Twenty thousand and forty slaves “This hadith was presented with a continuous, authentic chain of narration, and I have prepared the additions to it with this chain of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5941 - It has been presented with an authentic chain of transmission"
"5942","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Salt told us, Omar bin Miskin told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, said: I have never prayed behind your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that I heard him when he finished his prayer saying: “O God, forgive me for all my mistakes and sins, bestow upon me, give me life, provide for me, and guide me to good deeds and morals, for there is no “No one guides to its good except You, and no one turns away from its bad except You.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5942 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"5943","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Yahya bin Al-Ala told us, about Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that he took something from the beard of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “No.” “May evil be upon you, O Abu Ayyub.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"5944","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, I am Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati, Ismail bin Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, that Abdullah bin Abbas Al-Miswar ibn Makhrama disagreed about whether a person in ihram should wash his head with water without ritual impurity, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari while he was in “Some of the water from Mecca. Ask him about that.” This length of hadith is a virtue for Abu Ayyub, because Ibn Abbas and Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah returned to him in the question, and I think that The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, have included it or one of them in the Book of Purity.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5943 - True"
"5945","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, informed us, Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, Ali bin Saeed told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr told us, On the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, who said: Tufayl ibn Abdullah, the son of Aisha’s brother, said to her mother that he saw in The dream was that he met a group of Christians, and he said: You are the people, were it not that you claim that Christ is the Son of God? So he said: And you are the people. Were it not that you say: “Whatever God wills and what Muhammad wills.” He said: Then he met some Jews, and he said: You are the people, were it not for the fact that you claim that Al-Uzayr is the son of God? He said: And you are the people, were it not for the fact that you claim that Al-Uzayr is the son of God? You say what God wills, and what Muhammad wills, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and narrated to him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You narrated this.” Hadith to anyone? He said: Yes. He thanked God and praised Him, then said: “Indeed, your brother has seen what has been conveyed to you, so do not say, “What God willed” and “what Muhammad willed,” but say: “What he willed.” God is alone, He has no partner.” Hammad bin Salamah disagreed with him, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair."
"5946","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, and Abu Muslim told us, they said: Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of al-Tufayl ibn Abdullah ibn Sakhabra, Aisha’s maternal brother, He said: I saw what the sleeper sees, so he mentioned the hadith with something similar to it. “This is more worthy of the preserved than the first.”"
"5947","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us in Bukhara, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin Al-Muthanna, said: “Nubisha bin Abdullah bin Shayban bin Attab bin Al-Harith bin Husayn bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Uzza He is the Prophet of goodness, and his nickname is Abu Tarif, who lived in Basra.”"
"5948","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Mu’alla bin Rashid Al-Nabal told us. Abu Al-Yaman, Umm Asim told me, and she was the mother of the son of Sinan bin Salamah bin Al-Muhabaq Al-Hudhali, she said: Nabaishah entered upon us, and the Messenger of He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called him Nabesha Al-Khair. He entered upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he had captives with him. He said: O Messenger of God, either Be kind to them, or spare them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have done well. You will be the one seeking goodness after that.”"
"5949","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And Abu Ayyub Khaled bin Zaid bin Kulayb bin Tha’labah bin Abd Awf from Banu Tamim bin Malik bin Al-Najjar witnessed Aqaba. And Badr, and all the scenes, and he conquered Iraq, and he witnessed with Ali, may God be pleased with him, Siffin, then he went to the Levant, and entered the land of the Romans as a conqueror, and descended Constantinople »"
"5950","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Amara bin Ghaziyah told us, that Abu Ayyub Al-Azdi passed by Muawiyah, so he mentioned the hadith that was presented to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari in its length: “This is a mursal hadith, for between Amara bin Ghaziyah and Abu Ayoub and Muawiyah are supported, and the hadith of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari is connected with a chain of narration.”"
"5951","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And Jarir bin Abdullah bin Malik bin Nasr bin Tha’labah bin Jashm bin Awf bin Shulayl bin Khuzaymah bin Sakan bin Ali bin Malik bin Zayd bin Qays bin Abqar bin Anmar. He had resided during the strife in Qarqisa, then moved from there to Kufa, where he died. May God be pleased with him in the year fifty-one.”"
"5952","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari Abdullah bin Qais, an ally of the family of Utbah bin Rabi'ah bin Abd Shams."
"5953","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, He said: “Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, his name is Abdullah bin Qais bin Sulaym bin Hadhar bin Harith bin Amer bin Bakr bin Amer bin Athir bin Wael bin Najiya bin Al-Muhajir bin Al-Ash’ari, who is Nabat bin Adad bin Yashjub bin Ya’rab bin Qahtan, and the mother of Abu Musa is Tayba. The daughter of Wahb bin Atik. She had converted to Islam and died in Medina. Abu Musa had come to Mecca, so Abu Uhayha swore an alliance with Sa’id bin Al-Aas."
"5954","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari was one of those who migrated to the land of Abyssinia and resided there until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Amr bin Umayyah Al-Dhamri to the Negus. So he loaded them into two ships and brought them to him in Khaybar after Al-Hudaybiyyah.”"
"5955","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hussein Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, that Al-Ash’ari described Abu Musa, saying: “A man of light body and short stature.”"
"5956","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “He died Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari in the year fifty-two, and he is sixty-three years old.”"
"5957","And I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: “The name of my father Musa Al-Ash’ari is Abd Allah bin Qais"
"5958","Abu Zur’ah al-Razi told me, Muhammad bin Umair told me, Ibn al-Barqi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz al-Tanukhi, He said: “Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for the oldest and youngest people on the ship.” He said Abu Amer Al-Ash’ari: “I am the eldest of the people on the ship, and my son is the youngest.” Sa’id said: “Among them were Abu Amer, Abu Malik, and Abu “Moses and Ka’b bin Asim, I think they came up with Al-Abwa.”"
"5959","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us, I am Al-Hussein bin Ubaid Allah, I am Abu Ghassan, Abbad told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, I heard Al-Sha’abi, says: “Judgement is for six of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, three in Medina, and three in Kufa, then in Medina: Omar, Ubayy, Zayd bin Thabit, and in Kufa: Ali, Abdullah, and Abu Musa. Al-Shaybani said: So I said to Al-Sha’bi: Abu Musa should be added. To them he said: “He was one of the jurists,” so Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Abbas bin Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Asim, the martyr, may God be pleased with him, told me About him"
"5960","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Budin told us, Muhammad bin Amrawih Al-Harawi told us, Al-Haytham bin Adiy told us, Mujalid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, said: “The knowledge of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ended with these groups: Omar bin Al-Khattab and Ali bin Abi Talib. And Abdullah bin Masoud, Ubayy bin Ka’b, Muadh bin Jabal, Zayd bin Thabit, Abu Al-Darda’, and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari.”
 Masruq said: “The judges are four: Omar, Ali, Zayd bin Thabit, and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5960 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5961","Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, he said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari addressed us and said: “By God, if you obey God as the beginning and Abdullah bin Qais as the second, I will certainly make you accountable.” The method"
"5962","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, may God be pleased with him, Abu Dawud, I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: “No rider has ever come to Basra better for its people than Abu Musa al-Ash’ari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5962 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"5963","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Hassan bin Atiya told us, Yahya bin Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Musa al-Ash’ari said: “Ali was the first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. The purpose of narrating it was to clear the court of Abu Musa of Ali’s shortcomings. Then Ibn Abbas’s narration about him"
"5964","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, he said: I heard a black man who was with Ibn Abbas in Basra narrating hadiths, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he wrote Ibn Abbas went to him and asked him about it. Al-Ash’ari wrote to him: “You are a man of your time, and I did not narrate on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He was safe from some of it, except that I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he wanted to urinate, so he went to the floor of a wall there and said: “My son “In Israel, if someone’s urine got on someone’s urine, they would pinch him with a scissors, so if one of you wanted to urinate, he would use his urine to return it.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5964 - True"
"5965","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Badal bin Al-Muhabbar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, he heard Abu Wael say: I witnessed Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, Ammar bin Yasser, and Abu Masoud Al-Badri. Masoud and Ammar said: “We have not seen anything from you in Islam that is more hateful to us than your haste in this matter.” Ammar said: “And I have never Since you embraced Islam, I have seen something from you that is more hateful to me than your slowness in doing it.” Then they all went out to the mosque."
"5966","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Mahrez bin Hisham Al-Kufi told us, Khaled bin Nafi’ told us. Al-Ash'ari, on the authority of Sa'id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Abu Musa one night. And with him was Aisha, and Abu Musa was reading, so they stood up and listened to his reading, then they went on, and when Abu Musa came in the morning, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I passed by you, Abu Musa, yesterday, and you were reading, so we listened to your reading.” Then Abu Musa said: O Prophet. By God, if I knew where you were, I would have written to you with the words “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5966 - True"
"5967","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, I am Awf, On the authority of Abu Jamila, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurra, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: Ibn Umar said to me: “Do you know what my father said to your father?” I said: No. He said: “My father said to your father: “Are you pleased that we embraced Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that we emigrated with him, and that we struggled with him, and that we worked with him With him will it be returned to us? And that every work that we did after him, we will be saved from it, head for head. He said: Your father to my father: “No?” By God, we have striven hard after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we have prayed and fasted and done much good, and we hope for that.” He said: Then my father said to your father: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I wished that it would be returned to me, and that we would be saved from everything after that, head for head.” He said: I said: Your father is better than my father. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5967 - True"
"5968","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Anazi told me, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Hammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ma’mal, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, appointed Abu Musa to sail the sea,” while it was sailing with them. At sea at night, when a herald called out to them from above them: Shall I not inform you of a decree that God has decreed upon Himself? Whoever thirsts for God on the Day of Saifi, for it is God’s duty to give him drink on the day of the greatest thirst. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5968 - Ibn Al-Mu’mil is weak"
"5969","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Hanthali told me, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Kamil told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Lahi’ah, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, on the authority of Urwa, that Muawiyah was appointed governor of Egypt after The death of his brother Utba bin Abi Sufyan Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, in the year forty-four, and Muawiyah performed the Hajj there.
 Abu Bakr said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told me, Marouf bin Kharbudh Al-Makki told us, he said: While Abdullah bin Abbas was sitting in the The mosque, and we were in front of it when Muawiyah came and sat next to it, and Ibn Abbas turned away from it, so Muawiyah said to him: “Why do I see you turning away? Don't you know that I have more right to this matter than your cousin? He said: Why? Because he was a Muslim, and I was an infidel, no, but I am Uthman’s cousin.” He said: “My uncle is better than your cousin.” He said: “Othman was killed unjustly.” He said: - And with them is Ibn Omar. - Ibn Abbas said: “By God, this one has more right to the matter than you.” Muawiyah said: “Omar was killed by an infidel.” Othman was killed by a Muslim.” Ibn Abbas said: “By God, I refute your argument.”"
"5970","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, I am Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi, Abu Yunus told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, he said: “Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, nicknamed Abu Amr, died in the year fifty-two.”"
"5971","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yazid bin Abdul Samad Al-Dimashqi told us, Abu Al-Nadr Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Yazid told us. Al-Qurashi, Khalid bin Yazid told us, Hisham Al-Abed told me, Ubadah bin Nasi told me, and he was a worker for Abd al-Malik bin Marwan on the Jordan, he said: I passed by people who had gathered over a sheikh while he was speaking, so they separated from me, and suddenly a sheikh was speaking, saying: “O people, there are three... You have trusts. Whoever guards them is a believer, and whoever does not guard them is not a believer, if he says: I prayed and he did not pray, and I fasted and he did not fast. I took a bath from ritual impurity, but he did not take a bath.” He said: Then he from my right said: Who is this? He said: Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"5972","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Arim Abu Al-Numan Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanathili, Ziyad’s servant told me: Ziyad sent me to Hujr ibn Adi, who is said to be Ibn al-Adbar, but he refused to go. He came to him, then he brought me back the second time, but he refused to come to him. He said: So I sent to him, “I warn you not to ride the miracles of affairs. Whoever rides them will perish.” ""Her breasts""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5972 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5973","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulatha, said: “I saw Hujr bin Al-Adbar when Ziyad took him out to Muawiyah, and his feet were on one side. And he was on a camel.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5973 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5974","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Hujr bin Adiyy told us. Al-Kindi, nicknamed Abu Abd al-Rahman, had delegated to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and attended al-Qadisiyah, al-Jamal, and Siffin with Ali. May God be pleased with him. He was killed by Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan in Marj Adhra, and he had two sons: Abdullah and Abdul Rahman. They were killed by Musab bin Al-Zubayr was patient, and Hujr was killed in the year fifty-three.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5974 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5975","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muadh bin Al-Muthanna bin Muadh Al-Anbari told us, my father told me, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: “ When Hijr was sent to Muawiyah, the people were confused and said: What did Hijr do? Then news of him came to Ibn Umar while he was hiding in the market. He released his animal, jumped up, and set off, and I could hear him wailing, and he was crying.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5975 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5976","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Hujr bin Adiy said: “I will not renounce my pledge of allegiance, nor will I resign it, in the hearing of God and the people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5976 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5977","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Mufaddal bin Ghassan Al-Ghalabi told us, Yahya bin Mu’in and Hisham, Dawud bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr bin Abd al-Hadrami, who said: When Ziyad sent Hijr bin Adi to Muawiyah, he ordered Muawiyah imprisoned him in a place called: Marj Adhra. Then he consulted the people about it, saying: They started saying: Murder, murder. He said: Then Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asad Al-Bajli stood up and said: “O Commander of the Faithful, you are our shepherd and we are your subjects, and you are our pillar and we are Your baptism, if you punish, we will say: You are correct, and if you forgive, we will say: You have done well, and forgiveness is closer to piety, and every shepherd is responsible for his flock. He said: The people dispersed at his statement"
"5978","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed me, in Baghdad, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Baridi told us, Suleiman bin Abi Sheikh told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Al-Hasan Al-Shaybani, Abu Mikhnaf told us that Hadiyah Ibn Fayyad, the one-eyed man, ordered the killing of Hujr Ibn Adi, so he walked towards him with a sword. Then his senses trembled, and he said: O Hijr, didn’t you claim that you would not be afraid of death, for we will call you down? He said: “Why should I not be afraid, seeing A grave dug, a shroud spread, and a drawn sword. Indeed, by God, I will never say anything that will displease the Lord.” He said: So he killed him, and that was in Sha’ban of the year Fifty-one
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5978 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5979","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Musa bin Dawood al-Dhabi told us, Qais bin al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, Hajr ibn Adi said: “Do not wash away the blood from me, and do not release the shackles from me, but bury me in my clothes, for we will meet tomorrow.” “In earnest”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5979 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5980","Abu Ali Mukhlid bin Jaafar told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Karazi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Harmala told us Ibn Qais Al-Nakhi, Abu Zur’ah Ibn Amr Ibn Jarir told me, he said: “Jarir never came without me coming with him, and he never entered upon Muawiyah except I entered with him, and we did not enter with him except that he mentioned the killing of Hajr ibn Adi.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5980 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5981","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Baghawi told us, Ismail bin Aliyah told us, On the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Ziyad prolonged the sermon, so Hujr bin Adi said: “Prayer,” so he continued in his sermon, and said He said: “The prayer, and he struck with his hand to the pebbles,” and the people struck with their hands to the pebbles, so he descended and prayed, then he wrote about it to Muawiyah, so he wrote Muawiyah: If he sent him to me, he sent him to him, and when he came to him, he said: “Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “Am I the Commander of the Faithful?” I will not sack you, nor will I dismiss you.” So he ordered that he be killed, and when they set off with him, he asked them to give him permission, so he would pray two rak’ahs, so they gave permission. So he prayed two rak'ahs, then he said: “Do not cast iron on me, and do not wash away the blood from me, and bury me in my clothes, for I am quarreling.” He said: So he was killed. He said Hisham Muhammad ibn Sirin used to say, “If he was asked about the martyr, he mentioned the hadith of Hijr.”"
"5982","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutaybah Al-Asqalani told us, Muhammad bin Miskin Al-Yamimi told us, Abbad bin Omar told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Makhshi bin Hajr bin Adiy told us, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed them, and said: “What day? “This?” They said: A sacred day. He said: “What kind of country is this?” They said: The Sacred City. He said: “What month?” They said: A sacred month. He said: “Your blood, your property, and your honor are sacred to you, just as this day of yours is sacred to you, just as this month of yours is sacred.” As sacred as your country, this is to inform the absent witness. Do not return to being infidels after me, striking the necks of one another.”"
"5983","I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz, saying: I heard Ibn Qutaybah, saying: I heard Ibrahim bin Yaqoub, saying: “He has overtaken Hujr bin Adi Pre-Islamic times, and he ate blood during that period, then he accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and heard from him, and testified with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. Al-Jamal, Siffin, and he was killed in support of Ali."
"5984","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi informed us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Narsi told us, Amr bin Asim told us Al-Kalabi, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam, he said: I entered with Muawiyah to visit Umm The Believers Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “O Muawiyah, you killed Hujr and his companions, and you did what you did.” He mentioned the story. ""With its length"""
"5985","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun Al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, who said: Ziyad said to Imran bin Husayn: “O Abu Nujaid.”"
"5986","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, He said: “And Imran bin Husayn bin Ubaid bin Khalaf bin Abd Nihm bin Hizma bin Jahmah bin Ghadirah, nicknamed Abu Nujaid. He converted to Islam in the past. He, his father, and his sister, and he fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he remained in the land of his people, then he moved to Basra. So he lived there until he died there, and his son was born there, and Imran bin Al-Husayn died in Basra a year before Ziyad, and Ziyad died in the year five ""And fifty"""
"5987","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Nujaid Imran bin Al-Husayn bin Khalaf bin Abd Nihm Al-Khuza’i died in Basra in the year fifty-two.”"
"5988","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Yasaf said: I set off for Basra and entered the mosque, and behold, an old man was leaning against a scroll speaking, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The best people are my generation, then those after them, then those after them, then there will come people who will give testimony before they are asked for it.” So I said: Who is this sheikh? They said: Imran bin Husayn, “This is a high-level hadith that is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5988 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5989","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Fadl bin Ishaq Al-Duri told us, Abu Qutayba, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Ata’, on the authority of his father, that Ziyad, or Ibn Ziyad, sent Imran ibn Husayn as a courier, and he came and did not return with him. A dirham. He asked him, “Where is the money?” He said: “And for money did you send me?” We took it as we used to take it at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and placed it in the place we used to place it at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5989 - True"
"5990","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan told us, Hushaym told us, I am Abu Bishr, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah said: Imran bin Al-Husayn was “one of the most diligent companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in worship.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5990 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5991","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zaid, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he said: “None of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Basra preferring Imran bin Husayn
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5991 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5992","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, Musaddad told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, said: We went out with Imran bin Al-Husayn from Basra to Kufa, and not a day came when he did not recite poetry.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5992 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5993","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, I am Ibrahim bin Ata bin Abi Maimouna, on the authority of his father, that a camel belonging to Najid bin Imran bin Husayn fell, and Imran was sick, and he was hurt by it, so Imran cursed her, so Najid came out As he was returning, his she-camel was admiring him, so he was asked: What is the matter with you? He said: “Abu Nujaid cursed my camel, and it was only a short time before her neck was broken.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5993 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5994","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Al-Walid bin Shuja’ Al-Sakuni told us, Ruh told us Ibn Aslam, Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, that he said: “Know, O Mutarrif, that The angels used to salute me at my head, at the House, and at the stone door. When I was healed, that man went away. When he was healed, he spoke to him, saying: “Know, O Mutarrif, that what I used to lose has returned to me. Hush over me, O Mutarrif, until I die.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5994 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5995","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bukair Al-Adl told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hajib bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Al-Araj, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, who said: “I have not touched my private parts with my right hand since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5995 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"5996","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Sawwar bin Abdullah Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Saeed, Humaid told me, Rafi’ bin Sahban told us, that a man came to Imran bin Husayn while he was in the mosque, and said: A man divorced his wife while he was in the mosque. In a meeting three times, he said: “He committed a sin and his wife was forbidden to him.” So he went and mentioned that to Abu Musa, wanting to fault him, so Abu Musa said: “May God increase in us the likes of Abu Nujaid.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5996 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"5997","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abu Muhammad said: “Fadala bin Ubaid bin Al-Naqid bin Suhaib bin Jahjaba bin Kalfa bin Awf Al-Ansari, and his mother is the daughter of Muhammad bin Uqba bin Uhayha bin Al-Jalah died in Damascus in the year fifty-three, and his brother Ziyad bin Ubaid died there, and it is said that he died one year after him."
"5998","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Bayruti told me, Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told us, he said: “Ziyad bin Ubaid, brother of Fadalah bin Ubaid, died in Kufa, and was buried there. His nickname was Abu al-Mughirah, so Harithah bin Badr eulogized him.” He said: «
 [Simple Sea]
 God prayed over a grave and purified it... At the second hour, water is poured over it.
 Quraysh brought to him the coffin of their master... Today he is buried in generosity and firmness.
 Abu Al-Mughirah, while the world is a treacherous one...and indeed, from the deceit of the world, he is arrogant.
 You may have had knowledge for what is good... and you have had a denial for what is evil.
 And you were cheating and giving money out of abundance... even if your door was open and blocked.
 And the people after you have lost their dreams... as if birds had woven within them.”"
"5999","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin Al-Muthanna, he said: He said: “The name of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr al-Siddiq in pre-Islamic times was Abd al-Uzza, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him Abdul Rahman”"
"6000","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, He said: “Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr was nicknamed Abu Abdullah, and it was said: Abu Muhammad, and his mother was Umm Aisha, Umm Ruman bint Amer bin Uwaimir bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf converted to Islam, the mother of Ruman, and her Islam was good.
 And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about it: “Whoever likes to look at a woman from among the fair-eyed women, let him look at Umm Ruman.” She died. Umm Ruman in Dhul-Hijjah in the sixth year of the Hijra”"
"6001","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, I am Al-Maamari, he said: I heard Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah say: “The name of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr Abd al-Uzza, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him Abd al-Rahman, and he was nicknamed Abu Muhammad. He had witnessed the conquest of Damascus and Omar had sent him to war. Laila bint Al-Judi when he conquered Damascus, and he was in love with her.”"
"6002","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Sufyan told us. Umair ibn Yahya al-Ghassani said: I heard Urwa ibn al-Zubayr saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq told me that they went out to In Syria, a group of people from Mecca were competing. They came to a woman called Layla. They saw her appearance and beauty, so Abd al-Rahman returned. Ibn Abi Bakr while he was looking at her: “
 [Long Sea]

 I remembered Laila and the heavens below her... So what did Al-Judi’s daughter have, Laila and Malia?
 And I will be given a Harithiah qibla... it will be settled in Busra or it will be solved by Al-Jawabiyya.”
 When the time of Khalid ibn al-Walid came and they conquered the Levant, they afflicted it with the captivity they had afflicted, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr spoke to Khalid about it. So he wrote about that to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and Abu Bakr wrote to give it to him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6002 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6003","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Azhari informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa informed us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani informed us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid bin Jad’an, “Indeed, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr was among young men from Quraysh who migrated to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Before the conquest”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6003 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6004","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: And Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq continued to follow the religion of his people in polytheism until he witnessed Badr with the polytheists and called for a stool, and his father, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, to fight him. He mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “Enjoy yourself.” Then Abd Al-Rahman “converted to Islam during the truce of Hudaybiyyah, and his nickname was Abu Abdullah, and he died in the year fifty-three in the emirate of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan. Abd al-Rahman had a son called Abu Atiq, and his son was called Banu Abi Atiq.”"
"6005","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr said to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him: “He I saw you on the day of Uhud and I forgave you.” Abu Bakr said: “But if I had seen you, I would not have pardoned you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6005 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6006","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr died. Suddenly, and his nickname was Abu Abdullah, he died in the year fifty-three.”"
"6007","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his mother Safiya bint Shaybah, who said: I came to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and I went to her I consoled her with her brother, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, and she said: “May God have mercy on my brother. What I find most distressing in myself is that he was not buried where he died.” She said: Her brother had died in Abyssinia, so a group of Quraysh went out to him, and they carried him to the top of Mecca.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6007 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6008","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Shaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, He said: “We do not know of four people in Islam who accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fathers and children except: Abu Quhafa, Abu Bakr, and Abd. Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, and his son Abu Atiq Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6008 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6009","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr died. Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them suddenly.”"
"6010","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Musa bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: “Never attach any lie to Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr about Islam.”"
"6011","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Ibrahim Al-Asadi, Al-Hafiz Hamdan, told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Uwais, Suleiman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah, on the authority of his mother, that a woman entered Aisha’s house and prayed at the house of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and she was healthy, so she prostrated, and did not raise her head until she died, and Aisha said: “Praise be to God who gives life and causes death. Indeed, in this As an example for me, there is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr. He fell asleep in a grave, and he said, “So they went to wake him up and found him dead.” So he entered Aisha’s soul. The accusation that evil was done to him, and he was hastened and buried while he was alive, so she saw that he was an example for her, and whatever was in her soul about that went away.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6011 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6012","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr died. In the year fifty-three, he witnessed the camel with his sister Aisha, and he came to Ibn Amir to Basra.”"
"6013","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us in Nishapur, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubayy told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr died in Abyssinia on a courier from Mecca, and when Aisha, may God be pleased with her, performed Hajj She came to his grave and cried and said:
 [Long Sea]

 And we were like two sticks of scabs for a long period of time... until it was said that they would never crack.
 When we separated, Malik and I... for a long time together, we did not spend a night together.
 Then she returned to Mecca and said: “By God, if I had witnessed you, I would have buried you where you died.”"
"6014","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: “What was attached to Abdul Rahman bin Abi He became a virgin because of a lie in Islam.”"
"6015","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin al-Nadr bin Salamah al-Jarudi told us, al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he told me Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: Muawiyah sent to Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, for one hundred thousand dirhams after he refused to pledge allegiance to Yazid bin Muawiyah, so Abd returned it. The Most Gracious, but he refused to take it and said: “I would trade my religion for my world,” and he left for Mecca until he died there.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6015 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6016","Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Muzani informed me of Nishapur, and Muhammad ibn al-Adl informed me, Ibrahim ibn Sharik al-Asadi informed us, in Kufa, Ahmad informed us. Ibn Yunus, Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Bring me an inkwell and a shoulder, and I will write for you a letter after which you will never go astray.” Then he turned his back, then he turned to us and said: “Allah and the believers reject anyone except Abu Bakr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6016 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"6017","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Khuza’i told me about Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Azraqi, Dawud bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Attar told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told me, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, on the authority of Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of her father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Give your sister Aisha, So make it full of comfort, and when the hill descends, order it to enter ihram, for it is an upcoming Umrah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6017 - Its chain of transmission is strong"
"6018","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “Abdullah bin Abi Bakr was killed on the Day of Taif by a Muslim from Banu Taim ibn Murrah. He was shot with an arrow, and he died fifty days after that.”"
"6019","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, he said: “The one who was disputing food with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr in the cave was Abdullah bin Abi Bakr.”"
"6020","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Shaybani told me, Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zaghbah told me, Sa`id ibn Uqba told me, he said: “Abdullah ibn Ubayy died A virgin in the year in which Fatima, may God be pleased with her, died after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6021","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Abbas, the martyr, may God Almighty have mercy on him, told me. Abu Abbas Al-Dagholi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Karim told us, Al-Haytham bin Adi told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr was shot with an arrow on the day of Taif. So she attacked him forty nights after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he died. Then Abu Bakr entered upon Aisha and said: “Yes, daughter. By God, it is as if he had been taken by the ear of a sheep and taken out of our house.” She said: “Praise be to God who tied your heart and determined for you to Your senses.” So he went out and then came in and said: “My daughter, are you afraid that you have buried Abdullah while he was alive?” She said: “Indeed, to Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return, O father.” He said: “I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Satan.” There is no one except that he has two blames: a blame from the angel and a blame from Satan.” He said: Then a Thaqif delegation came to him, and that arrow did not stop him, so he came out to them and said: “Does any of you know this arrow?” He said: Saad bin Ubaid, brother of Banu Al-Ajlan, this is an arrow that I sharpened, shot, and butted, and I shot it. Abu Bakr said: “Then This is the arrow that killed Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, so praise be to God who honored it with your hand, and did not make it weak with his hand, for it is very hot.”"
"6022","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in two inky papyrus, which belonged to Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, and he was wrapped in them, then they were removed.” On his authority, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr had kept that garment for himself so that he would be shrouded in it if he died, then he said after He kept it: I would not keep for myself anything that God had prevented His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, from being shrouded in it, so Abdullah gave it in charity.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6022 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6023","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Othman bin Al-Haytham told us, Al-Haytham told us Ibn Al-Ash'ath, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amara Al-Ansari, on the authority of Jahm Ibn Uthman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Amr Ibn Uthman, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a Muslim reaches forty years of age, God will dispose of He suffers from three types of affliction: insanity, leprosy, and leprosy. When he reaches fifty years of age, his sins, whatever they are, are forgiven. He delayed, and he was God’s prisoner on earth, and the intercessor for his family on the Day of Resurrection.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6023 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from Al-Talkhees due to its weakness"
"6024","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Bukhari told us, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Bukhari told us Abd al-Rahman bin Shaybah, Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, he said: “We do not know In Islam, four people joined the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fathers and children, except for Abu Quhafa, Abu Bakr, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, and Abu Atiq Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman.”"
"6025","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud bin Umair bin Jud'an bin Ka'b bin Sa'd bin Taim bin Murrah, and Qunfud bin Umair was one of the nobles of Quraysh, and he was called: the drinker of gold. His mother was Hind bint Al-Harith, from Banu Ghanam bin Malik bin Abd Manat bin Ali bin Lubana. Al-Muhajir came to Basra and died there.”"
"6026","Abd Al-Baqi bin Qani’ Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Qazzaz told us, Al-Abbas bin Talib told us, Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Husayn Ibn Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Ibn Qunfud, he said: “I passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him while he was performing ablution, so I greeted him, but he did not respond to me. When he finished, he returned it to me and apologized to me, and said: “He did not prevent me from responding.” “On you, except that I hate to mention God Almighty while I am not in a state of purity.”"
"6027","Abu Nu`aym Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafari told us about Marw, Abdan ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Hafiz told us, he said: I heard Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, says: “Ka’b bin Ujrah bin Adi bin Abd al-Harith bin Amr bin Awf bin Ghanam bin Sawada, and his fathers are called Qawaqil, and he was in ihram from the Levant when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set out. He went to Hudaybiyyah, wanting to perform Umrah. His arrival coincided with the departure of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, so he went out with him, and Ka’b bin Ujrah, an ally of Banu Awf bin Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj.”"
"6028","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Anas bin Iyad told us, Saad bin Ishaq told me Ibn Ka'b Ibn Ujrah, on the authority of his father, so I said: O Abu Muhammad, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, order you to enter into ihram at the time of Hudaybiyyah? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Shave, shave.”"
"6029","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rabi’ah told us, Suleiman bin Daoud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Ka’b bin Ujrah died in Medina in the year fifty-two, and he was seventy-five years old at that time.”"
"6030","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Mu’alla bin Asad told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ka’b Ibn Ajra: “O Ka’b Ibn Ajra, I seek refuge in God from the rule of fools.” He said: O Messenger of God, and what is the leadership of the foolish? He said: “There will be princes after me. Whoever enters upon them and believes their lies, and helps them in their oppression, is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not be rejected.” Ali the basin
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6030 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6031","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, He said: “Abu Qatada Al-Harith bin Rabi’ bin Baldama bin Khannas bin Sinan bin Ubaid bin Adi bin Ghanam bin Ka’b bin Salamah bin Saad bin Ali bin Asad bin Sardah bin Yazid bin Jashm bin Al-Jarrah, and there was disagreement about his name, so Muhammad bin Ishaq used to say: His name Al-Numan bin Rubi’i, and some of them said: Amr bin Rubi’i witnessed Uhud and the trench, and the scenes after that with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him”"
"6032","Ibn Umar said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, overtook me. On the day of Dhu Qard, he greeted me and looked at me and said: “Oh God, bless his hair and skin for him,” and he said: “May your face prosper.” I said: Your face, O Messenger of God. He said: “Was Masada killed?” I said: Yes. He said: “What is this on your face?” I said: I shot an arrow, O Messenger of God. He said: “Come,” so I approached him, and he spat on him, but he never hit me, nor did he smack me.
 Ibn Omar said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “Abu Qatada died in Medina in the year four He was fifty and he was seventy years old.” Ibn Umar said: “I did not see any disagreement between Abu Qatada and the people of our country. Indeed, Abu Qatada died. In Medina, and the people of Kufa narrated that Abu Qatada died in Kufa.”"
"6033","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Yunus told me, I am Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir, he said: “Abu Qatada bin Rabi’i, one of the Banu Salamah, died in Medina fifty-four years old when he was seventy years old."
"6034","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri. I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Thawban is the client of the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He is Abu Abdullah.”"
"6035","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Thawban is the freed slave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He was originally from Yemen. He was subjected to captivity, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was against him. He was nicknamed Abu Abdullah. He died in Homs in the year Fifty-four”"
"6036","Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar al-Hafiz told us, Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Hafs al-Wasabi told us, in Homs, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa, the author of history, said: And from the news that reached us about Homs, and from among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and from the loyalists of Quraysh, Thuban ibn Bajdad, nicknamed Abu Abdullah, was a man of the tribes who was taken captive, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, freed him and said to him: “Oh Thawbaan: If you wish to join those of yours, then you are of them, and if you wish to remain steadfast, you are of us, Ahl al-Bayt, with the loyalty of the Messenger of God.” He said: Rather, I confirm the loyalty of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He died in Homs during the emirate of Abdullah bin Qart in the year fifty-four."
"6037","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, may God Almighty have mercy on him, told me that I am Ali bin Abdul Aziz, I am Ishaq bin Ismail al-Talqani, Masada bin Al-Yasa narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Khasib bin Jahdub, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shafi, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Thawban, he said: A messenger said to me God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If you swear to commit a sin, abandon it, and throw the grudges of ignorance under your feet, and beware of drinking alcohol, for God, Blessed and Most High, has not sanctified the one who drinks it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6037 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6038","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Imran bin Abdul Rahim told us, Ali bin Qarin Al-Bahili told us, Saeed bin Abdul Rahim told us Rashid, on the authority of Al-Khalil bin Murrah, on the authority of Humaid Al-Araj, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Thawban, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Supplication removes what is decreed, and righteousness increases sustenance, and a servant is deprived of sustenance because of sin befalls him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6038 - Ibn Qurayn is a liar"
"6039","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, and Makram bin Ahmed Al-Qadi told us, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, They said: Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told us, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, who told him that he heard Abu Salam, Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told me that Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him: I was standing in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, then one of the Jewish rabbis came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. So I pushed him so hard that he almost collapsed, so he said: Why? Are you pushing me? So I said: Don’t you say, O Messenger of God? The Jew said: But we call him by the name by which his family called him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The name my family gave me is Muhammad.” The Jew said: I came to ask you, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Would it benefit you if I told you?” He said: I hear with my ears, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, poked a stick he had with him and said: “Ask.” Then the Jew said: Where will the people be on the day the earth and the heavens will be changed for another earth and the heavens? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In darkness, without the gathering.” He said: Who is the first person to take leave? He said: “The poor immigrants.” He said: What will be their gift on the day they enter Paradise? He said: “Increase in the liver of the Nun.” He said: What was their food after that? He said: “The bull of Paradise, which used to eat from its outskirts, will be slaughtered for them.” He said: What is their drink on it? He said: “A river called Salsabil.” He said: You have spoken the truth, and I have come to ask you about something that none of the people of the earth knows except a prophet or one or two men. He said: “Will it benefit you if Did I talk to you? He said: I hear with my ears. He said: I came to ask you about the boy. He said: A man’s semen is white, and a woman’s semen is yellow, so when they come together they make semen. If a man’s semen is a woman’s semen, he will be male, God willing, and if the woman’s semen is superior to the man’s semen, he will become feminine, God willing.” The Jew said: You have told the truth, and indeed you are a prophet. Then he left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This man asked me about the one he asked me about. “I had no knowledge of any of it until God Almighty brought it to me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6039 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6040","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told me, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami saying: “A wise man.” Ibn Hazzam Ibn Khuwaylid Ibn Asad Ibn Abd al-Uzza Ibn Qusayy/63, nicknamed Abu Khalid, he died in the year fifty-four, and he was one hundred years old. Twenty years old. He was born thirteen years before the elephant, and he died in Medina.”"
"6041","I heard Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab, saying: I heard Ali bin Ghannam Al-Amiri, He says: “Hakim bin Hazzam was born inside the Kaaba. His mother entered the Kaaba and gave birth in it and gave birth in the House.”"
"6042","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me Al-Hazami said: “Abu Khaled Hakim bin Hazzam died in the year sixty, and he was one hundred and twenty years old.”"
"6043","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Isbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar, Al-Mundhir bin Abdullah narrated to me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Habibah, the client of Al-Zubayr, who said: I heard Hakim bin Hizam, saying: “I was born thirteen years before the arrival of the owners of the elephant, and I was wiser when Abdul Muttalib wanted to slaughter his son Abdul By God, that was five years before the birth of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 Ibn Umar said: “Hakim bin Hazzam witnessed with his father the immoral person, and his father Hazzam bin Khuwaylid was killed in the last immoral act, and Hakim was His nickname was Abu Khaled, and he had children: Abdullah, Khaled, Yahya, and Hisham, and their mother was Zainab bint Al-Awwam bin Khuwaylid bin Abd al-Uzza bin Qusayy, and it is said that the mother of Hisham bin Hakim was Malika bint Malik bin Saad from the Banu al-Harith bin Fihr, and the son of Hakim bin Hazzam, all of them were the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they converted to Islam on the day of the conquest, and they accompanied the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Hakim bin Hizam, as mentioned, was one hundred and twenty years old, and Mu’awiyah passed by him in the year of Hajj, and a mule was sent to him to drink from its milk, and that was after If he asked him what food you eat? So he said: As for Mudgh, there is no Mudgh in me. So he sent him the smear, and sent him an onion, but he refused to accept it, and he said: I did not take it from anyone. After the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something, Abu Bakr and Omar invited me to my right, but I refused to take it from them.”
 Ibn Umar said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad told us, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said to Hakim ibn Hazzam: What is the money, Abu Khalid? He said: “lack of children.”
 He said: “Hakim bin Hazzam came to the city and settled there, and built a house there, and he died in the city in the year fifty-four, and he was one hundred years old. And twenty years.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6043 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6044","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, and he mentioned Hakim bin Hazzam attributed the lineage and added to it, “And his mother was Khatah bint Zuhair bin Asad bin Abdul Uzza, and she gave birth to Hakim in the Kaaba.” She was pregnant, so labor struck her while she was in the interior of the Kaaba, so she gave birth there, and she was conceived while still breast-feeding, and the clothes that were underneath her were washed at the time. The Basin of Zamzam, and no one was born before him or after him in the Kaaba.” Al-Hakim said: “It is a difficult omen in the last letter, as it has been repeated.” The news is that Fatima bint Asad gave birth to the Commander of the Faithful Ali bin Abi Talib, may God honor his face, inside the Kaaba.”"
"6045","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam, may God have mercy on him, told us: I am Ismail bin Qutaybah, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, we told him Ali ibn Mushar, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Hakim ibn Hazzam, “did not accept anything from Abu Bakr until he was arrested, nor from Umar.” Until he was arrested, nor from Othman, nor from Muawiyah until he died.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6045 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6046","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, he said: I freed forty freedmen in pre-Islamic times, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Do I have any reward for them?” He said: “You have greeted me according to what you have done previously.” It is correct according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6046 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6047","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Asadi, Al-Hafiz in Hamadan, informed us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali told us Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, said: Hakim Ibn Hazzam freed a hundred slaves, and carried a hundred camels in During the pre-Islamic period, when he converted to Islam, he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did you see something that I used to do in the pre-Islamic period that I used to swore about? Do I have anything to do with it? Reward? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have accepted your greetings for the reward already given to you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6047 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6048","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, about Muslim bin Jundub, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, and I urged him to do so, and he said: “I do not deny Your question, O wise man, is that this money is green and sweet, but it is the dirt of people’s hands, and the hand of God is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver “Above the hand of the questioner, and the hand of the questioner is below the hands.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6048 - True"
"6049","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abid bin Buhair, on the authority of Abu al-Huwayrith, on the authority of Amara ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, who said: “You saw me on the day of Badr, and it occurred In the valley there was vapor from the sky that blocked the horizon, and when the valley was flowing with water, it occurred to me that this was something from the sky that was supported by Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And there was nothing but defeat, and the angels were present.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6049 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6050","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, Ubaid Allah bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Arak ibn Malik, that Hakim ibn Hazzam said: Muhammad the Prophet was the most beloved of people to me in pre-Islamic times, so when he prophesied and went out to Hakim bin Hazzam went out to the city of Medina during the season and found a garment for the fornicator being sold for fifty dirhams, so he bought it to give it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so he brought it to him and wanted him to take it, but he refused - Ubayd Allah said: I thought he said: “We do not accept from the polytheists, but We took it for the price.” So I gave it to him until he came to Medina, and he put it on. I saw it on him on the pulpit, but I did not see There was never anything better about it on that day. Then he gave it to Usama bin Zaid, and a wise man over Usama saw it and said: O Usama, you are wearing a suit. Dhu Yazan, he said: Yes, because I am better than Dhu Yazan, and my father is better than his father, and my mother is better than his mother. Hakim said: So I set off for Mecca. They were impressed by what Osama said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6050 - True"
"6051","Ahmed bin Suleiman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Abi Uthman Al-Tayalisi told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Abi Hatim, the owner of the food, than Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Hassan ibn Bilal, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, that the Prophet When he sent him as a governor to Yemen, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Do not touch the Qur’an unless you are pure.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6051 - True"
"6052","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Muhammad bin Salih, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, Muhammad bin Omar said: Muhammad bin Abdullah, my nephew Al-Zuhri, narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, and he narrated to me Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, and Ibn Abi Habibah narrated to me, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, regarding the one who “migrated to the land of Abyssinia, the second migration, Khalid bin Hazzam, and he was bitten by a snake on the way, and he died.”
 Muhammad ibn Umar said: Al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Asadi told me, my father told me, he said: “In it was revealed {And whoever leaves his house Migrating to God and His Messenger, then death overtakes him, and his reward has fallen upon God} [An-Nisa: 100]"
"6053","The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa and Abdul-Rahman bin Abdul-Qari, that they heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: I passed by Hisham bin Hakim bin Hazzam, and he was reciting Surat Al-Baqarah during the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “The hadith, in its length, said: “It is the basis of the arrangement of this book that Khalid ibn Hazzam was mentioned before Hakim, and that it be Hisham bin Hakim was mentioned after them, but I combined them in this place when mentioning Hakim so that it would be closer to the beneficiary’s understanding."
"6054","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Hassan bin Thabit lived in pre-Islamic times for sixty years, and his nickname was Abu Al-Walid. In Islam, he lived for sixty years, and he was Hassan bin Thabit bin Al-Mundhir bin Haram bin Amr bin Zaid Manat bin Adi bin Amr bin Malik bin Al-Najjar, poet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Umm Hassan Al-Furaiah bint Khalid bin Khunais bin Luthan bin Abd Wad. It was said that he died before forty, and it was said that he died in the year five ""And fifty"""
"6055","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Abd Al-Malik bin Saad Al-Zuhri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, my father told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Harmala Rawiyah Hassan bin Thabit, he said: “I came to Hassan,” so I said: O Abu Al-Hussam!"
"6056","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, he told me Saleh bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Asad bin Zurarah, told me The most steadfast of the men of my people, on the authority of Hassan bin Thabit, said: “By God, I am a young boy of seven or eight years of age who is wiser than what I heard when I heard a Jew, who was on the hill of Yathrib, shouting: O community of Jews. When they gathered together, they said: Woe to you, what is the matter with you? He said: The star of God has risen He will be resurrected tonight.”"
"6057","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us dictation, Abu Abbas al-Sarraj told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Khalaf al-Hadadi told me, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi told me, Salamah told me, Salamah ibn al-Fadl told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman told me. Ibn Hassan Ibn Thabit said: “Our grandfather Haram Abu Al-Mundhir lived for one hundred and twenty years, and his son Al-Mundhir lived for one hundred and twenty years. His son Thabit lived for one hundred and twenty years, and his son Hassan bin Thabit lived for one hundred and twenty years. When Hassan died, he lit a fire. He gathered his family, then he established a building. He says:
 [Long Sea]
 And if a person comes in the evening and becomes unharmed from the people, except for what he has done to Sa`id.
 He said: Then he lived after Abdul Rahman bin Hassan bin Thabit for eighty-odd years, and when death approached him, he kindled a fire and gathered his family. Then he proceeded to say:
 [Long Sea]

 And if a person attains wealth, and then does not obtain... a friend of his due to his bounty, he is ungrateful.
 Then Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Hassan bin Thabit lived after him for eighty-odd years, and when his death came, he said:
 [Long Sea]
 And if a man seeks this world, desiring it... he clings to it by the rope of delusion.”"
"6058","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zanad told me, On the authority of his father, and Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to set up a pulpit for Hassan in The mosque is being visited by a person standing and boasting on behalf of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Indeed, God supports Hassan.” With the Holy Spirit, he did not neglect or deviate from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6059","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zannad told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, something like this: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6058 - True"
"6060","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Sabrah told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Awsi told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, hated being insulted. Hassan bin Thabit then said: “Isn’t he the one who said: “
 [abundant sea]
 “For my father, my mother, and my honor... the honor of Muhammad is a protection from you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6060 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6061","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq told us, Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Qadi, Suleiman ibn Harb told us, Hammad ibn Zaid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Hazim, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, said: I saw Hassan bin Thabit, and he had a forelock that was drawn between his eyes.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6061 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6062","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Issa bin Abdul Rahman told us, Adi bin Thabit told me, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Hassan bin Thabit: “The Holy Spirit is with you.” “I did not attack them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6062 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6063","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl Al-Muzaki told me, Ahmed bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abdah bin Salman, about Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Hassan bin Thabit asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to write a satire. The polytheists, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So what about my lineage among them?” Hassan said: I will release you from them as a hair is released from dough.
 Hisham said: My father said: I went to curse Hassan in the presence of Aisha, and she said: “Do not curse Hassan, for he was defending the Messenger of God, may God bless him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.” Rather, Muslim narrated it in its length from the hadith of Al-Layth, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, and he mentioned the poem in its entirety:
 [Long Sea]

 “You satirized Muhammad and I responded to him... and with God is the reward for that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6063 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6064","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, the client of Banu Nawfal, that Abdullah bin Rawahah and Hassan bin Thabit came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. When {Tasm} was revealed [Al-Shu'ara': 1] the poets were crying while he was reciting to them: {And the poets are followed by the erring ones} [Al-Shu'ara': 224] until he reached {And they did righteous deeds} [Al-Shu’ara’: 227] He said: “You” {And remember God often} [Al-Shu’ara’: 227] He said: “You” {And they were victorious after they had been wronged} [Al-Shu’ara’: 227] He said: “You.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6064 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6065","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Hatim bin Abi told us. Saghira Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, the hadith was narrated. On the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Azib, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and it was said, O Messenger of God, that Abu Sufyan ibn Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib satirized you, so Ibn Rawaha stood up and said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to do so, so he said: “Are you the one who says, ‘God is firm?’” He said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of God:
 [Simple Sea]
 So God strengthened the good he gave you... Moses strengthened and he was given victory like they were supported.
 He said: “And God will do good to you like that.”
 He said: Then Ka’b jumped up and said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to do so. He said: “You are the one who says, ‘I am interested’.” He said: Yes. I said, O Messenger of God:
 [full sea]
 Sakina wanted to fight her Lord... so let them be defeated by those who defeat others.
 He said: “But God has not forgotten that for you.”
 He said: Then Hassan got up and said: O Messenger of God, permit me in it, and he brought out a black tongue and said: O Messenger of God, permit me if you wish. I informed him of the auction, and he said: “Go to Abu Bakr so that he may tell you the story of the people, their days, and their accounts, then speak to them and Gabriel.” With you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, Muslim narrated it in its length, and from the hadith of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6065 - True"
"6066","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Makhramah ibn Nawfal ibn Ahab ibn Abd Manaf, and he was one of those who reconciled their hearts.”"
"6067","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “He embraced Islam.” Makhramah bin Nawfal at the conquest of Mecca. He was knowledgeable about the lineage of Quraysh and its traditions, and he had knowledge of the monuments of the Holy Mosque. Makhramah Safwan, and he was nicknamed with that, and he was the eldest of his children.”"
"6068","So I heard Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari saying: I heard Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi saying: I heard Yahya Bin Abdullah bin Bukair, says: “Makhramah bin Nawfal is nicknamed Abu Al-Miswar.”"
"6069","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Tirmidhi told us, Mukhlid bin Malik told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, And Attaf bin Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, said: Al-Miswar bin Makhrama told me, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to my father: “O Abu Safwan"
"6070","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawood told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Makhramah bin Nawfal witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn, so he gave him fifty camels of the spoils of Hunayn, and Makhramah died.” In the city in the year fifty-four, and on the day he died he was one hundred and fifteen years old.”"
"6071","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Uqba, saying: “Makhramah ibn Nawfal al-Qurashi died when he was one hundred and fifteen years old. He converted to Islam on the day of the conquest, and he was one of those whose hearts were reconciled.”"
"6072","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Zuhri, he said: Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan said, and with him was Abdul-Rahman bin Azhar: Who has Makhramah bin Nawfal to do justice to me? Is there any disparagement from his tongue? Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar said to him: I will suffice for him, and that reached Makhramah, so he said: “Abd al-Rahman made me an orphan in his chambers, claiming By his strength, I am sufficient for him, so Ibn al-Barsa’ al-Laythi said to him: It is Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, so he raised a stick in his hand and struck him. He encouraged him and said: “You were our enemy during the pre-Islamic era, and you envy us in Islam, and you come between me and Ibn Al-Azhar.”"
"6073","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: When Makhramah bin Nawfal’s death was made by his daughter, who cried for him and said: “And his father was gentle and gentle, so he woke up and said: ‘Who is mourning?’” They said: Your daughter, and he said: “Come.” She came, and he said: “No one mourns like me. Say, ‘And his father. He was a right arrow. He was a strong father.’”"
"6074","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hatim bin Wardan told us, Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, said: I presented cellars to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he divided them among his companions. Then my father said to me: Go with us to him, for some cellars have come to him, so my father spoke at the door, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recognized his voice, so he came out. And he had a qiba with him, so he started saying: “I hid this for you, I hid this for you.”"
"6075","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Durastawayh Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Sa’id bin Ufair told us, and Sa’id told us Ibn Abi Maryam, Abdullah Ibn Salih, and Yahya Ibn Bukayr, the Egyptians in Egypt, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah al-Zuhri, on the authority of his father, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, introduced Islam All the people of Mecca converted to Islam, and that was before prayer was made obligatory, so that when he recited the prostration he would not be able to prostrate until he came forward. The leaders of Quraysh were Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah, Abu Jahl bin Hisham, and others, and they were at Taif in their lands, and they said: You will abandon the religion of your fathers. So they disbelieved.” Ya’qub bin Sufyan said: “We do not know of Makhramah bin Nawfal’s hadith with a chain of transmission other than this.”"
"6076","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Saeed bin Yarubu bin Ankatha bin Amir bin Makhzum, nicknamed Abu Hud, converted to Islam on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted Hunayn, “and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him fifty camels from the spoils of Hunayn.”
 Muhammad bin Omar said: I heard Abdullah bin Jaafar saying: Omar bin Al-Khattab came one day to the house of Sa’id bin Yarubu’, and he consoled him by going He looked at him and said: “Do not neglect the Friday prayer, nor the prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: “I have no leader.” He said: “We are sending to you.” With a leader,” he said: Then he sent him a boy from the captivity who said: “Sa’id bin Yarubu’ died in Medina in the year fifty-four, and it was the day he died. One hundred and twenty years old.”"
"6077","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Saeed bin Yarubu bin Ankatha bin Amer Al-Makhzoumi died in the year fifty-five, and he was one hundred and eighteen years old.”
 Musab said: In pre-Islamic times his name was Sarm, “so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, named him Saeed,” and his mother’s name was Hind."
"6078","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Ubi told us, Al-Haytham told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “Among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Aqaba from the Banu Amr ibn Sawada, Abu Al-Yusr Ka’b ibn Amr bin Abbad bin Amr bin Tamim bin Sawad bin Ghanim bin Kaab bin Salamah, from the people of Badr, witnessed Aqaba, and he was the one who was captured. Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib»"
"6079","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: “Abu Al-Yusr Ka'b bin Amr died in the year fifty-five in Medina, and he was the last of the people of Badr to die."
"6080","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abu died Al-Yusr Ka'b bin Amr bin Abbad bin Amr bin Sawad bin Ghanim bin Ka'b bin Salamah bin Saad bin Ghanim bin Asad bin Jashm Bin Al-Khazraj in the year fifty-five in Medina.”"
"6081","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Al-Yusr Ka'b bin Amr bin Abbad bin Amr bin Sawad bin Ghanim bin Ka'b bin Salamah bin Ghanim bin Asad bin Jashm bin Al-Khazraj."
"6082","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Huwaytib bin Abd al-Uzza al-Amiri, may God be pleased with him, ibn Abi Qais bin Abd Wad bin Nasr bin Malik bin Hasl from Maslamah Al-Fath, he died at the end of the emirate of Muawiyah, when he was one hundred and twenty years old. His mother was the mother of Habiba, and the mother of his brother, Rahm bin Abdul-Uzza. Zainab bint Alqama bin Ghazwan bin Yarubu bin Munqidh bin Amr bin Muhays, and Huwaytib sold a house in the city to Muawiyah. Forty thousand dinars, so the people looked forward to that and said: Forty thousand dinars is not for a man who has four children."
"6083","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told us, Daoud bin Mihran Al-Rabba’ told us, Muslim bin Khaled told us Al-Zanji, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, who said: “One day we were sitting in the courtyard of the Kaaba in pre-Islamic times. A woman came to seek refuge with the Kaaba from her husband. Her husband came and extended his hand to her, but his hand withered. I have seen this in Islam. And indeed, he is paralyzed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6083 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6084","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Ibrahim told me Ibn Jaafar Ibn Mahmoud Ibn Muhammad Ibn Salamah Al-Ashhali, on the authority of his father, said: Huwaytib Ibn Abd al-Uzza lived one hundred and twenty Years, sixty in pre-Islamic times, and sixty in Islam. When Marwan ibn al-Hakam ruled the city in his first year, Huwaytib entered upon him with sheikhs. Jallat Hakim bin Hazzam and Makhramah bin Nawfal, so they talked with him and separated, so Huwaitib came to him one day after that, and he talked to him. Marwan said to him: What is the matter with you? So he told him, and Marwan said to him: Your conversion to Islam was delayed, Sheikh, until events preceded you. Then Huwaitib said: By God, I was concerned. In Islam more than once, your father prevented me from doing all of this and forbade me, saying: You will neglect the honor of your people and the religion of your fathers for a new religion, and you will become... Follow him?! He said: Then Marwan remained silent and regretted what he had said to him. Then Huwaitib said: Didn’t Othman tell you about what he said to your father when he converted to Islam? Marwan became more and more sad, then Huwaytib said: There was not one of the elders among the Quraysh who remained in the religion of their people, until Mecca was conquered. I hate when it was opened to him from me, but the amounts,I witnessed a full moon with the polytheists, and I saw a lesson, and I saw the angels killing and taking captives between the heavens and the earth, so I said: This is a man. Forbidden, and when he mentioned that I did not see anyone, we defeated and returned to Mecca, so we stayed in Mecca, and the Quraysh surrendered one by one, so when the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah, I attended and witnessed the reconciliation, and I walked in it until it was completed, and all of that increases Islam, and God Almighty refuses except what He wants, so when We wrote the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah. I was the last witness, and I said: The Quraysh will not see anything from Muhammad except that which harms them. I was satisfied if they defended him with spears. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came for the Umrah to make up for the missed days, and the Quraysh left Mecca, I was among those who remained behind in Mecca, me and Suhail bin Amr, so that we will bring out the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the time has passed. When the three days had passed, Suhail bin Amr and I came and said: Your condition has passed, so leave our country. He shouted: O Bilal, let the sun not set on any of the Muslims in Mecca who came with us.
 Ibn Omar said: Ibrahim bin Jafar bin Mahmoud told me, on the authority of his father, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabra told me, On the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Jahm,He said: Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca in the year of the conquest, I was greatly afraid, so I left my house. I dispersed my children to places where they would be safe, and I came to the wall of Awf, and I was there, and behold, I was with Abu Dhar al-Ghaffari, and she was among me. There is a friendship between him, and the friendship is never an obstacle, so when I saw him, I ran away from him, and he said: Abu Muhammad, and I said: Here you are. He said: What's wrong with you? I said: Fear. He said: There is no fear for you. You are safe in the safety of God Almighty. So I returned to him and greeted him. He said: Go to your home. I said: May I have a way? To my house. By God, I do not see me reaching my house alive until I find myself and be killed, or someone enters my house and I am killed, and my family is in various places. He said: So gather your family in a place, and I will reach your house with you. So he reached with me, and he started calling that Huwaytib is safe so that he will not attack. Then Abu Dharr went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, saying: “Have not all the people believed except those whom you ordered to be killed?” He said: So I was reassured and returned my family to their homes, and Abu Dharr returned to me and said to me: O Abu Muhammad, until when? And until when? You have excelled in all countries, and you have missed out on much good.And a lot of good remained, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and greeted him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the most virtuous of people and the most charitable. People, and I dream of people, his honor is your honor, and his honor is your honor. He said: I said: I will go out with you, so I will go to him, so I went out with him until I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello to Al-Batha’, and with him were Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them both. I stood at his head and asked Abu Dharr how it should be said when he said hello. On him? He said: Say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. So I said it, and he said: “And peace be upon you, Huwaitib.” So I said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are the Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God who has guided you.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was pleased with my conversion to Islam, and he borrowed money from me, and I lent him forty thousand dirhams. “And I witnessed Hunayn with him.” And Al-Taif, and he gave me one hundred camels from the spoils of Hunayn.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad told me, on the authority of his father,He said: Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza sold his house in Mecca to Muawiyah for forty thousand dinars, and it was said to him, O Abu Muhammad, for forty thousand dinars. He said: “Forty thousand dinars for a man who has five children.” Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zannad said: “And on that day he will provide for himself.” Every month
 He said: Then “after that, Huwaytib came to Medina and stayed there, and he had a house there in the court of the owners of the Qur’an.” He said: “Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza died in Medina in the year fifty-four, and he was one hundred and twenty years old on the day he died.”"
"6085","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Shajara, Yazid bin Shajara al-Rahwi, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died in Byzantium in the year fifty-eight.”"
"6086","Abu al-Dhafir Ahmad ibn al-Fadl al-Kateb told us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Hamza said: I heard Yazid bin Shajara, in the land of the Romans, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Swords are keys.” Paradise »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6086 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6087","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Mansour, he heard Mujahid speaking on the authority of Yazid ibn Shajarat al-Rahwi, who was one of the princes of the Levant, and Muawiyah used to use it on the armies. One day he addressed us and said: “O people, remember the blessings of God upon you if you saw what I see of black, red, green, and white. And what is in it is that when the prayer is performed, the gates of heaven are opened, the gates of Paradise, and the gates of Hell, and the poplars are decorated and appear. So when one of them turns his face to the battle, they say: Oh God, make him firm, O God, help him, and when he turns away, they hide from him, and they say: Oh God, make him firm. Forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, so exhaust the faces of the people, so may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, for when one of you kisses, it is the first whiff of his blood. His sins will be removed from him as the leaves of a tree are removed, and two virgins will come down to him and wipe the dust from his face, and he will say to them: I am yours, and you say: We are yours, and he is clothed with a hundred garments. If they were to be circled between these two fingers - meaning the index and middle fingers - they would be sufficient to enlarge them, not of Weave the children of Adam, but from the garments of Paradise. Indeed, you are written before God by your names, your features, your adornments, your private conversations, and your gatherings. Then, when the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said: O so-and-so, this is your light, and O so-and-so, you have no light, and Hell has a coast like the coast of the sea, in which are vermin. And snakes like palm trees and scorpions like mules. So when the people of Hell cry out for relief for them, it will be said: Go out to the coast and they will come out. Then He will take the vermin by their lips and faces, and, as God wills, He will remove them and they will seek help to flee from it to Hell, and He will spread scabs over them. Then someone scratches his skin until the bone appears, and one of them says: Hey so-and-so, does this hurt you? He says: Yes, and he says: That is because you used to harm the believers.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6087 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6088","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And Maslama bin Mukhlid bin Al-Samit bin Nayyar bin Luthan bin Khazraj, nicknamed Abu Ma’an. It was said he died in Egypt, and it was said in Medina in the year sixty. He witnessed one of the And all the scenes, in which Hassan bin Thabit says:
 [The Converging Sea]
 Behold, here is my uncle, of whom I boast... Let every man show me his uncle.”"
"6089","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ibrahim bin Maysarah told us, he said: I heard a mujahid saying: “I prayed behind Maslamah ibn Mukhlid in Egypt, and he recited Al-Baqarah, but he did not omit a waw or an alif from it.”"
"6090","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And he died in it, meaning in the year sixty-two. Abu Saeed Maslama bin Mukhlid Al-Ansari in Egypt, and its prince was the first of the princes to whom Egypt and the Maghreb were united. Narration: He mentioned that “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born when he was ten years old.”"
"6091","Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb al-Mawsili told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, who am I? He said: “You are Saad bin Malik bin Uhayb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra.” So who? He said: “Other than that, the curse of God be upon him.”"
"6092","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Sa`d ibn Abi Waqqas, and he was ruled by Umar. Othman of Kufa, his mother was Hamnah bint Abi Sufyan bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf.”"
"6093","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told me, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, Hushaym told me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Samurah said: Omar said to Saad: “O Abu Ishaq.”"
"6094","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Matar told us, Ishaq bin Abi Kamil told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad said: “I heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Umair, Amir, and Uqba, brothers, and Abu Waqqas Malik bin Ahab bin Abd Manaf bin Al-Harith bin Zahra”"
"6095","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad informed us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Nuh ibn Yazid told us, Ibrahim ibn Saad, he said: “Saad bin Abi Waqqas died during the time of Muawiyah after his first Hajj, and he was eighty-three years old.”"
"6096","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ismail bin Qutaybah, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Abu died Ishaq Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who was seventy-five years old in Medina, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam, who was its governor, prayed over him.”"
"6097","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Abu Bakr told me, On the authority of Suleiman, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari said, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, he said: “My father was the last of the immigrants. ""death"""
"6098","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Bakr ibn Mismar, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, who said: “My father was a short, slender man with thick fingers, and he was nicknamed Abu Ishaq died in his palace in Al-Aqiq, ten miles from Medina, and he was carried to Medina on the necks of men.”
 Ibn Umar said: Ubaida bint Na’il told us, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, who said: “My father died in the year fifty-five, and Marwan prayed over him.” Ibn al-Hakam, who is the governor of Medina.”"
"6099","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu‘aym ibn Hammad told us, Rishdin told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab Saad “dyed his hair black.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6099 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"6100","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Salih Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, that Saad bin Abi Waqqas, when death approached him, called for a cloak of wool to be made for him and said: “Shroud me in it. For I met the polytheists therein on the day of Badr, but I was hiding it for this day.”"
"6101","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ayyub bin Sulayman bin Bilal told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, and Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who said: “Saad bin Abi Waqqas was the last of the emigrants.” ""death"""
"6102","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Ubi told us, Nuh ibn Yazid told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, said: “Saad bin Abi Waqqas was the last of the immigrants to die.”"
"6103","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Ubi told us, Nuh ibn Yazid told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, said: “Saad bin Abi Waqqas died during the time of Muawiyah after his first Hajj, and he was eighty-three years old.” He said Abu Abdullah: “Saad converted to Islam when he was nineteen years old.”"
"6104","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Umm Saad and Umm His two brothers, Umair and Amer, are Hamna bint Abi Sufyan bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams. Umair was martyred at Badr, and Amer was one of the immigrants. Abyssinia, and he used to dye his hair black, meaning happy.”"
"6105","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Wahb bin Jarir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Numan bin Rashid speaking, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: “Saad was the last of the emigrants to die.” My father said: “Saad died ten miles from The city, so he was carried on the necks of men to the city, and Marwan was its governor at that time.”"
"6106","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “The son of Saad bin Abi Qasas: Omar bin Saad was killed by Al-Mukhtar bin Abi Ubaid, and Muhammad bin Saad was killed by Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf, and he was one of Abd’s companions who was captured. Al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Al-Ash’ath, and their mother Maria bint Qais bin Maadi Karib from Kindah, and Amer bin Saad, and his mother Bahra, and Salih Bin Saad, and he was staying in Al-Hira because of something that happened between him and his brother, Omar bin Saad, and his mother, Khawla bint Umair bin Taghlib bin Wael, And Ibrahim bin Saad, and Ishaq bin Saad, and Yahya bin Saad, and Aisha bint Saad.”"
"6107","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih Bal-Ray told me, Abu Hatim told me, he said: Ibrahim bin al-Mundhir told me, Muhammad bin Talha al-Taymi told me, Ishaq bin Talha al-Taymi told me, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha told me, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, he said: “Ali and Talha were Al-Zubayr and Saad bin Abi Waqqas are said to have been born in one year. Ibrahim said: “They were born in one year.”"
"6108","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, I am Ibn Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj narrated to him, on the authority of Bishr bin Saeed, that he said: “We were sitting with Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and we were talking The hadith of the people and jihad, and the hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was included in that.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6108 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6109","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Abbas the martyr told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Razin told us, Ali bin Khashram told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Idris, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, my father told me, or my uncle told me, that Sa’ad was asked about something or a hadith and he spoke strangely. Then he said: “I would hate to tell you something in which you would add a hundred.”"
"6110","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, I am Ibn Wahb, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, he said: I accompanied Saad bin Abi Waqqas for such and such a year, but I did not hear him narrate on the authority of the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for one hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6110 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6111","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ismail bin Muhammad told me Ibn Saad, he told him, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Ibn Mismar, on the authority of Saad, he said: “I converted to Islam on the day I became Muslim, and God did not enjoin prayer.”
 Ibn Omar said: “He witnessed with him Badr and Uhud, and he remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the people took part, and he witnessed the trench. Al-Hudaybiyyah, Khaybar, and the conquest of Mecca. He had with him at that time one of the flags of the three immigrants, and he testified with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He saluted all the scenes, and he was one of the archers mentioned among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6112","Then Muhammad bin Najad told me, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, on the authority of her father Saad bin Abi Waqqas, that he said: “
 [abundant sea]

 Shall I not inform the Messenger of God that... I protected my companions with my nobility?
 With it I will drive away their enemies... with every sorrow and with every ease.
 No archer can prepare an arrow... with the Messenger of God before me.”"
"6113","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, I am Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya, Ali bin Saeed Al-Kindi told us, Abu Usama told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Saad bin Abi Waqqas came. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is my uncle, so let someone show me his uncle.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6113 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6114","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Hafs bin Maysarah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, “Saad bin Abi Waqqas was the first to shed blood for the sake of God.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6114 - True"
"6115","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Aqsi told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Ma’n told us, Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Ma’n told us My father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbi, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, who said: “The first to throw an arrow in the way of God was Sa’d ibn Ubayy Waqqas: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6115 - True"
"6116","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Hashim bin Hashim told me, about Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: “You have seen me for a third of Islam.”
 He said: Hashim bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who said: “No one became Muslim on the day that “I converted to Islam therein, and I stayed for seven nights, the third of Islam.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6116 - True"
"6117","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Al-Khasib bin Nasih told us, Abdah bin Nael told us, on the authority of Aisha Bint Saad, on the authority of her father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat in the mosque for three nights, saying: “O God, let a servant enter through this door.” He loves you and you love him.” Then Saad entered from him, saying, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6117 - True"
"6118","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Ismail told us Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I heard Saad saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O God, answer him if “He called you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6118 - True"
"6119","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi informed us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Bakr bin Mudar told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas said: “
 [full sea]
 I am the son of the one whose supplications are answered and the one who supports...the one who is chosen from among the Arabs.
 He gave it to the Prophet, seeking reward... He was singled out for it above all others who seek reward.
 And the people disagreed among themselves, and he refused...to fight the people of monotheism and the Book.
 May God grant him peace. None of them was hit by an arrow, and he was not injured.”"
"6120","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balj, on the authority of Musab Ibn Saad, on the authority of Saad, “A man slandered Ali, may God be pleased with him, so Saad Ibn Malik called upon him, and a camel or camel came to him and killed him. So Saad freed Nasmah and swore not to call upon anyone.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6120 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6121","So he narrated to us an explanation of this hadith, Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, I am Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Sirri, Hamid bin Yahya told us. Al-Balkhi in Mecca, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: I was in Medina, and while I was walking around... Market: When I reached Ahjar al-Zayt, I saw people gathered on a horseman riding an animal, and he was cursing Ali ibn Abi Talib, and the people were standing. Around him, Saad bin Abi Waqqas came and stood over them and said: “What is this?” They said: A man is insulting Ali bin Abi Talib, so Saad came forward and they released him until he stood over him and said: “Oh this, what are you insulting Ali bin Abi Talib?” Student? Wasn't he the first to convert to Islam? Wasn't he the first to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Was he not the most ascetic of people? Was he not the most knowledgeable of people? He mentioned and even said: “Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumcise his daughter?” Was he not the standard bearer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his raids? Then he faced the Qiblah and raised his hands, and said: “O God, this is insulting one of your saints, so do not separate this crowd until you show them Your ability. Qays said: By God, we had not separated until his animal had overtaken him and thrown him on his head into those stones, so his brain split open and he died. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6121 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6122","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ibrahim bin Yahya Al-Shajri told us, on the authority of his father, Musa bin Uqba told me, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told me, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: A messenger told me God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O God, direct his shot, and answer his supplication.” This is a hadith that was unique to Yahya bin Hani bin Khaled Al-Shajri, and he is “A trustworthy sheikh from the people of Medina.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6122 - Al-Shajari was the only one to narrate it, and he is trustworthy"
"6123","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Hashim bin Hashim Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: I was sitting with Saad when a man called Al-Harith bin Barsa came while he was in the market and said to him: O Abu Ishaq, I was just with Marwan and I heard him saying: This money is ours, we can give it as we please. He said: Saad raised his hand and said: “Should I pray?” Then Marwan jumped up while he was on his bed and embraced him, and said: “I implore you, O Abu Ishaq, to Whatever you pray, it is the property of God.”"
"6124","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sayrifi told us in Marw, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Makki ibn Ibrahim told us, Hashim bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad, who said: Al-Harith bin Al-Barsa’ came while he was in the market, and said to him: O Abu Ishaq, I heard Marwan claiming that God’s wealth is its wealth. He gives it to whomever He wishes, and to whomever He wishes, He withholds it. So he said to him: “Did you hear him say that?” He said: Yes, Sa`id said: Then he took Sa`d's hand and al-Harith's hand until he entered upon Marwan and said: “O Marwan, you claim that God’s money is yours. You can give him whatever you want, and whoever you want, you can withhold from whomever you want.” He said: Yes, he said: “Then I pray.” Saad raised his hands, and Marwan jumped to him and said: I adjure you by God to pray. It is the property of God. He gives it to whomever He wishes. And whoever wants to prevent it"
"6125","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi informed us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, I am Yahya Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amer, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost sleep one night and said: “I wish a man could protect me from my friends tonight.” She said: We heard the sound of weapons, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is this?” Then Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: O Messenger of God, I have come to guard you. Aisha said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept until I heard Ghateetah: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6125 - True"
"6126","Ali bin Issa told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told me, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, they said: Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, Abd told us. Al-Warith bin Saeed, Muhammad bin Juhadah told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Hussein bin Kharijah, he said: When she came The first temptation made me difficult, so I said: “O God, show me something of the truth that I can adhere to. So I was shown what the sleeper sees, this world and the hereafter, and it was There is a short wall between them, and when I was under it, I said: If I climbed this wall to see dead people, I would be braver and they would tell me. “So I landed in a land full of trees, and suddenly a group of people sat down and I said: You are the martyrs. They said: We are the angels. I said: Where are the martyrs? They said: He advanced to the ranks, so I rose to a rank that God knows best of beauty and generosity, and lo, I am in Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and lo! Ibrahim is an old man, and he says to Ibrahim: Ask forgiveness for my nation, and Ibrahim says: You do not know what they did after you. They shed their blood. And they killed their imam, so would they not do what Saad Khalili did?” I said: “By God, I have seen a vision. Perhaps God will benefit me with it. I will go and see.” In Saad’s place, I will be with him.” So I went to Saad and told him the story. He said: He was not overjoyed by it, and he said: He who was not Ibrahim Khalilah I said: “Which of the two sects are you with?” He said: I am not with one of them. He said: I said: “So what do you command me?” : Do you have any sheep? I said: No. He said: So buy if you wish, and stay in it until you are saved.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6126 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6127","Sheikh Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari, may God Almighty have mercy on him, informed us of my reading In the year 449 AH, he said: The ruler, Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Hamdawayh al-Hafiz, may God be pleased with him, said: Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr told us Ibn Khalid, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, in naming one of the Quraysh who witnessed Badr, then From the Banu Makhzum, Al-Arqam bin Abi Al-Arqam.”
 “The name of Abu Al-Arqam is Abdul Manaf bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzum, and he is from the people of Badr. He and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah and Othman bin Maz’un at the same time, and Al-Arqam was the last of the people of Badr to die.”"
"6128","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: And the Makhzoumis said: “Umm Al-Arqam bin Abi Al-Arqam Tamadur bint Hudhaym, from Banu Sahm bin Amr bin Husays.”"
"6129","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Othman bin Hind bin Abdullah bin Uthman bin Al-Arqam bin Abi Al-Arqam Al-Makhzoumi said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Uthman bin Al-Arqam, my grandfather Othman bin Al-Arqam told me that he used to say: I am the son of the seventh of Islam. My father converted to Islam on the seventh of seven, and his house was On Safa, which is the house where the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to live in Islam, and in it he called people to Islam, and some people converted to Islam there. Many times, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on Monday night: “Oh God, strengthen Islam through the two men most beloved to you, Omar ibn al-Khattab or Amr bin Hisham.” Then Omar bin Al-Khattab came tomorrow morning, and he converted to Islam in the house of Al-Arqam, and they left it and said “Allahu Akbar” and circumambulated the Kaaba. They appeared, and Al-Arqam’s house was called Dar Al-Islam, and Al-Arqam gave it in charity to his son, so I read the copy of Al-Arqam’s charity in his house: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Al-Arqam has paid for a quarter of it as long as he reaches Al-Safa. It is charity in its place in the Sacred Mosque, it cannot be sold, nor bequeathed. Shahid Hisham bin Al-Aas, and so-and-so is the client of Hisham bin Al-Aas,He said: This house continued to be a charity in which his children lived, rented, and took possession of it until the time of Abu Ja`far.
 Muhammad bin Omar said: Then my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Imran bin Othman bin Al-Arqam, who said: “I know the day that occurred on Abu Ja`far himself said that he was running between Safa and Marwah during the Hajj he performed while we were on the back of the house, so he would pass under us if he wanted to take I would have taken his hood, and he would look at us from the time the valley descends until he ascends to Safa. When Muhammad bin Abdullah came out Ibn Hassan in Medina. Abdullah Ibn Uthman Ibn Al-Arqam was one of those who pledged allegiance to him, and he did not go out with him, so Abu Ja’far complained about that to him. So he wrote to his worker in the city to imprison him and cast him in an iron, then he sent a man from the people of Kufa called Shihab bin Abd. Lord, and he wrote with him to his worker in the city to do what he ordered, so Shihab entered the prison of Abdullah bin Othman, and he was a very old man. He was eighty-some years old, and he was bored in the iron and the prison. He said: Can I save you from what you are in and sell me Dar Al-Arqam? The Commander of the Faithful wants it, and perhaps if I sell it to him, I will speak to him about it and he will pardon you.He said: It is charity, but my right to it is his, and with me are partners in it, my brothers and others, so he said: You only have to do with yourself, give us your right and you will be acquitted. So he bore witness for him, and wrote against him a letter of purchase for seventeen thousand dinars. Then he followed his brothers, and the abundance of money fascinated them, so they sold him, and it became For Abu Ja`far and for whoever cut it down, then al-Mahdi gave it to Khayzaran, the mother of Moses and Aaron, so she built it and was known by it, then it became Ja`far’s. Bin Musa Al-Hadi, then the owners of Al-Satuti and Al-Adni lived in it, then most of it or most of it was bought by Ghassan bin Abbad, son of Jafar bin Musa. As for Al-Arqam’s house in Medina in Banu Zurayq, it was an area belonging to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 Ibn Umar said: Muhammad bin Imran bin Hind told me, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Arqam bin Abi Al-Arqam was present at the death of Al-Arqam, so he recommended that Saad prayed for him, and Marwan said: “Would you imprison the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for an absent man who wanted to pray for him?” Abdullah refused. Ibn Al-Arqam was in charge of Marwan, and Banu Makhzum stood with him and a conversation took place between them, then Saad came and prayed over him. That was in the fifth year. And fifty in the city, and the number one perished when he was eighty-few years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6129 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6130","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Al-Attaf bin Khaled Al-Makhzoumi told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Arqam, and he was a Badr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sheltered in his house at Safa until Forty Muslim men gathered together, and the last of them to convert to Islam was Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them. When they were forty, they went out to The polytheists. Al-Arqam said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bid him farewell, and I wanted to go out to the Holy House, so the Messenger of God said to me: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Where do you want?” I said: The Holy House. He said: “And what will take you there?” “Is there any business?” I said: No, but I will pray in it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers then.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6130 - True"
"6131","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told us, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Nasawi told us, Abu Musab told us, Yahya bin Imran bin Uthman told us, on the authority of his grandfather Uthman. Ibn Al-Arqam Ibn Abi Al-Arqam, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Badr: “Put down what was “You have some burdens with you.” Then Abu Usayd al-Sa’idi raised the sword of al-Murziban ibn Aidh, and al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam recognized it and said: Give it to me, O Messenger of God, so he gave it to him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6131 - True"
"6132","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Bakkar told us, Abbad bin Al-Muhallabi, on the authority of Hisham bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ammar bin Saad, on the authority of Othman bin Al-Arqam bin Abi Al-Arqam Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of his father Al-Arqam May God be pleased with him, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one who climbs the necks of people on Friday, and will separate them like a neighbor throwing his reed into the fire.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6132 - Hisham bin Ziyad Wah"
"6133","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Salamah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I heard Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali, says: “Abu Al-Yusr Al-Ansari, his name is Ka’b bin Amr bin Abbad bin Amr bin Tamim bin Shaddad bin Uthman bin Ka’b. Ibn Salamah is from the people of Badr. He witnessed Aqaba, and he was the one who captured Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib.”"
"6134","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, in naming “Whoever witnessed Badr from among the Ansar was Abu Al-Yusr Ka’b bin Amr.”"
"6135","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Al-Yusr’s name was Ka’b ibn Amr, brother of Banu Salamah. He died in the year fifty-five in Medina. He was a short man with a strong stomach.”"
"6136","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abu Al-Yusr’s name is Ka’b bin Amr bin Abbad bin Amr bin Ghaziyah bin Sawad, and Abu Al-Yusr witnessed Al-Aqaba in all narrations, and he witnessed Badr when he was twenty years old, and he witnessed Uhud, and the trench and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He was a short man with a short stomach, and he died in Medina in the year fifty-five.”"
"6137","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us. Buraydah bin Sufyan Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr Ka’b bin Amr, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was pledging allegiance to people. So I said: O Messenger of God, extend your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you, and make a condition for me, for you know best the condition. He said: “I pledge allegiance to you on the condition that you worship God. And perform the prayer, pay the zakat, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6137 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6138","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, in naming “Whoever witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is Mu’tab bin Awf bin Amir bin Al-Fadl bin Afif.”
 “He is the one who is called Utib ibn al-Hamra, and his nickname is Abu Awf, an ally of Banu Makhzum, and he was an Abyssinian immigrant. The second, and they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a brother between Mu’tab ibn al-Hamra’ and Tha’labah ibn Hatib, and Mu’tab witnessed Badr and Uhud. And the trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He died in the year fifty-seven, and he was seventy-eight years old at that time. ""year"""
"6139","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin al-Mundhir al-Hazami told us, he said: “Shaddad bin Aws bin Thabit bin Al-Mundhir bin Haram, nicknamed Abu Ya’la, and he resided in Palestine, and he died in the year fifty-eight when he was ""Seventy-five years old"""
"6140","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad Al-A’war told us, he said: Abu Maashar said: “Abu Hurairah and Shaddad bin Aws perished in the year fifty-eight.”"
"6141","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Some of my friends, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: “My name in pre-Islamic times was Abd Shams bin Sakhr, so I was named in Islam Abd. The Most Gracious, but my nickname was Abu Hurairah because I was tending sheep for my family, and I found the children of a feral kitten, so I put it on my sleeve, so when I turned away from them and they heard cat noises from my lap. They said: What is this, O Abdul Shams? I said: Cat’s children. I found her. They said: So you? Abu Hurairah, but she stuck with me after that.” Ibn Ishaq said: “Abu Hurairah was a mediator in Dosas, where he liked to be among them.”"
"6142","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Sufyan bin Hamza told us. Al-Islami, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was They call me Abu Hurr, and the people call me Abu Hurairah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6142 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6143","Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told me, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told me, Asim bin Ali told us, Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to call me Abu Hurr,” and people called me Abu Kitten"
"6144","Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told me, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told me, Asim bin Ali told us, Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Because you call me a male is more beloved to me than your calling me a female.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6144 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6145","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Mandah Al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam told us, Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Muharrar bin Abi Hurairah, he said: “My father’s name was Abd Amr bin Abd Ghanam.”"
"6146","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, some people told me My friends, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: My name in pre-Islamic times was Abd Shams bin Sakhr, “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me And peace be upon Abd al-Rahman."
"6147","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Tanisi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, he said: “Abu Hurairah’s name was Abd Ghanim.”"
"6148","I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz, saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya, saying: I heard Abu Mushar, He says: “Abu Hurairah’s name is Ali bin Abdul Shams.”
 Muhammad ibn Yahya said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal say: Abu Ubaidah Al-Haddad told us: “Abu Hurairah’s name is Abdullah.”"
"6149","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, he said: “Abu Hurairah’s name is Abd Nihm bin Amer.”"
"6150","Abdullah bin Ghanim Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, he said: “Abu Hurairah died With agate, and his name is Abdullah bin Amr, and among the people are those who say: Ibn Abdul-Uzza.”"
"6151","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, he said: “Abu Hurairah is said to be the slave of Shams, and it is also said to be a slave of A greedy person, and it is said: a greedy slave, and it is said: a knife.”"
"6152","Then Muhammad ibn Yaqoub al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zangwayh told us, Ibn Aisha, he said: “Abu Hurairah’s name is Sakin. This disagreement regarding the name Abu Hurairah has been established in nine ways, the most correct of which I think is in In pre-Islamic times he was Abd Shams, and in Islam he was Abd al-Rahman. Likewise, the year of his death is disputed.”"
"6153","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hajjaj Al-A’war told us, Abu Ma’shar told us, He said: “Abu Hurairah perished in the emirate of Muawiyah in the year fifty-eight, and in that year Saeed bin Al-Aas, Aisha, and Saad bin Malik died.”"
"6154","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Al-Hasan bin It is reported that Damra bin Rabi’ah told us: “Abu Hurairah died in the year fifty-eight, and it is said: He died in the year fifty-nine, and he was eight years old.” And seventy years.”"
"6155","The chief judge, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Saleh, told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Musta’ini told us, Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Madini told us, My father told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: “Abu Hurairah died in the year fifty-seven.”"
"6156","Muhammad bin Al-Abbas the martyr told me, Hashim bin Mahboub Al-Shami told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: “Abu Hurairah died in the year fifty-five.”"
"6157","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abu died Hurairah in the year fifty-nine at the end of the emirate of Muawiyah. He was seventy-eight years old on the day he died, and Al-Walid ibn Utbah prayed over him. He was the governor of the city, and Marwan was isolated from the work of the city at that time.”
 Then Thabit bin Qais told me, on the authority of Thabit bin Mishhal, he said: Al-Walid wrote to Muawiyah informing him of the death of Abu Hurairah, so he wrote to him: “See Whoever leaves behind, pay ten thousand dirhams to his heirs, be kind to them, and do them kindness, for he was among those who supported Othman. And he was with him at home, may God Almighty have mercy on him.”"
"6158","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Hammad bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, that Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah told him that a man came to Zaid bin Thabit and asked him about something, and Zaid said to him: Take care of my father. Hurairah, for it was between me, Abu Hurairah, and so-and-so in the mosque one day, supplicating to God Almighty, and remembering our Lord. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us. May God bless him and grant him peace, until he sat down with us. He said: Then he sat down and we remained silent. Then he said: “Go back to where you were.” Zaid said: So my companion and I prayed before Abu Hurairah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made sure of our supplications. He said: Then he called Abu Kitten and said: Oh God, I ask you like these two companions of mine asked you, and I ask you for knowledge that will not be forgotten. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Amen,” so we said: O Messenger of God, and we ask God for knowledge that will not be forgotten. So he said: “Al-Dawsi preceded you with it.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6158 - Hammad bin Shuaib is weak"
"6159","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Abu Hurairah is a vessel of knowledge.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6159 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6160","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abdullah bin Salih Al-Azdi told us, Khalid bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she called Abu Hurairah and said to him: “O Abu Hurairah, what These hadiths that inform us that you are narrating on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, have you heard anything other than what we heard? Did you see anything other than what we saw? He said: “O mother, you were distracted from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the mirror and kohl, and pretending to be for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And by God, nothing distracted me from him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6160 - True"
"6161","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Mu’in told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, said: “Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, was one of the best of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6162","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sa`id al-Jamal told us, Abu Rabi’ah Fahd bin Awf told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Fayrouz Al-Danaj, said: Abu Rafi’ informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He says: “I have memorized from the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, some hadiths that I did not narrate to you, and if I had narrated to you any of them, you would have stoned me.” “By the stones.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6162 - True"
"6163","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hasan, he said: None of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated more about him than Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, and that Marwan He sent him to Medina and wanted to tell him, so he said: Narrate as we narrated. But when he refused to do so, he neglected to do so, so he sat as a scribe for him and made Abu Hurairah The scribe spoke and wrote until he finished his entire hadith. Then Marwan said: Do you know that we have written down your entire hadith? He said: “Or have you done so, and if you obey me you can erase it?” He said: So he erased it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6163 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6164","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Suleiman Al-Narsi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Amr bin Ubaid, Abu al-Za’izah, Marwan bin al-Hakam’s scribe, told us that Marwan “called Abu Hurairah and he made me sit behind the bed, and began to ask him, And I began writing until, when he was at the beginning of the year, he called for it, and made him sit behind the veil, and he began to ask him about it, and he did not add anything more or “He decreased, neither advanced nor delayed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6164 - True"
"6165","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, I am Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man said to Ibn Umar: Abu Hurairah narrates a lot on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said hello, and Ibn Umar said: “I seek refuge in God lest you be in any doubt about what he brings, but he dared and we were cowardly.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6165 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6166","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, Muadh bin Muhammad bin Muadh bin Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: “Abu Hurairah was bold to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him about “Things we don’t ask him about.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6166 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6167","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Jurashi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that he passed by Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, while he was He narrates, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever follows a funeral gets a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he gets two qirats greater than that of Uhud.” Ibn Umar said: O Abu Hurairah, see what you narrated about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Abu Hurairah rose to him until he went to Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her behalf, he said to her: O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you by God, did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, has the right to A qirat, and if he witnesses her burial, then he gets two qirats? She said: By God, yes. Abu Hurairah said: We were not distracted by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a wedding or crowd in the markets. I was only asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a word to teach me or a food to feed me. Ibn Umar said: O Abu Hurairah, you were obliging us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed us of his hadith. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6167 - True"
"6168","Abu Zur’ah al-Razi told me, Bakr bin Ahmad bin Hafs told me, Muhammad bin al-Abbas al-Saydalani told us, Abu Marwan Abd al-Malik bin Saleh Al-Qurashi, Saleh bin Qudamah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The ink is in the garment of the seeker of knowledge.” Like a creature in the clothing of a virgin slave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6168 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"6169","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, I am Ibn Wahb, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jaafar, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Umayyah Al-Damri, on the authority of his father, he said: I narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah With a hadith, but he denied it, so I said: I heard it from you. He said: “If you heard it from me, then it is written with me.” So he took my hand to his house, so he showed me one of his books from the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He found that hadith and said: “I have told you that if I “I told you about it, and it is written with me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6169 - This is objectionable and not valid"
"6170","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told us, Amr bin Uthman told us, Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: “If I heard in the hadith: He used to say, ‘He is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.’”"
"6171","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, “He sat in a gathering in which Abu Hurairah was speaking to them about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Some of them denounced him, and some recognized him, until he did it repeatedly. I knew at that time that Abu Hurairah was the best of people about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him”"
"6172","Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Faqih told me, Abu Hamid Al-Sharqi told me, and Makki bin Abdan told me, they said: Abu Al-Azhar told us, Wahb bin Jarir, my father told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq speaking, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Anas Malik bin Abi Amir, he said: I was with Talha bin Ubayd Allah, and a man came to him and said: O Abu Muhammad, by God, we do not know. This Yemeni is more knowledgeable about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him or you? He said something about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he did not say - meaning Abu Hurairah - and Talha said: “By God, there is no doubt that he heard from the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, unless we heard and knew what we did not know. Indeed, we were a wealthy people, with homes and families. We used to go to the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted both ends of the day, then we would return. Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, was poor and had no money, family, or children. His hand was only with The hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was with him wherever he went, and he had no doubt that he knew what we did not know and heard what we did not hear, and he did not accuse him. One of us said that he said something about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he did not say, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6172 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6173","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Asim bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of His father, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, going out on Friday, holding the two pillars of the pulpit, standing and saying: Tell us. Abu Al-Qasim is the Messenger of God, the truthful and trustworthy, may God bless him and grant him peace. “He continued speaking until he heard the door of the compartment opening for the imam to exit.”"
"6174","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq the Imam, saying: He mentioned Abu Hurairah, and he said: “He was one of his companions who narrated the most about him, as his narrations and the narrations of other companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became widespread.” “peace and blessings of God be upon him, with extracts from Sahih books.” Abu Bakr said: “Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated from him, with the majesty of his power, and the descent of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.”"
"6175","Ibrahim bin Bastam Al-Zaafrani told us, Saeed bin Sufyan Al-Jahdari told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, he said: I heard My father was narrating. He said: I came to Medina, and suddenly Abu Ayyub was narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. I said: He was narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah. And you are of high status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Because I narrate on the authority of Abu Hurairah is more beloved to me than that I narrate on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Imam Abu Bakr said: “Part of Abu Hurairah’s keenness for knowledge was his narration from those who narrated the least from the Prophet.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, out of his eagerness for knowledge. He narrated on the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi.”"
"6176","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir Al-Basri told us, Ubais bin Marhum Al-Attar told us, Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Yahya, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should brandish the sword against his brother, perhaps Satan is seized by his hand and falls into a pit of fire.” Abu Hurairah said: I heard it from Sahl bin Saad al-Sa’idi. He heard it from the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Abu Bakr said: “His eagerness for knowledge prompts him to hear news that he had not heard from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” From him, and he only speaks about Abu Hurairah to refute his reports, those whose hearts God has blinded, so they do not understand the meanings of the reports, or he is obstructing A Jahmi hears news about him that they see that is contrary to their doctrine, which is disbelief, so they insult Abu Hurairah and accuse him of what God Almighty has said. He kept him away from him, disguising the shepherds and the lowly, that his narrations do not support proof, or an outsider who sees the sword upon the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, and he would not see obedience to a caliph or an imam if he heard the news of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in disagreement. Their doctrine, which is misguidance,He did not find a way to refute his reports with an argument and proof. He was terrified by the incident with Abu Hurairah, or by a Qadri who abandoned Islam. And its people and the people of Islam who follow the past decrees that God Almighty has destined and decreed are infidels before the servants are gained. For her, if he looked at the narrations of Abu Hurairah that he had narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in proving predestination, he did not find any proof that he wanted to be true. His statement, which is blasphemy and polytheism, was his argument for himself that the narrations of Abu Hurairah cannot be used as evidence, or he is ignorant. He neglects jurisprudence and seeks it from someone other than his own, if he hears the news of Abu Hurairah in something that contradicts the doctrine of those who have chosen his doctrine. And his narrations are imitation without any evidence or proof. He spoke about Abu Hurairah, and he rejected his narrations that contradict his doctrine, and he uses his narrations as evidence. Disagreeing with him if his narrations were consistent with his doctrine, and some of these groups denied Abu Hurairah reports that they did not understand. It means, “I will remember some of them by the will of God Almighty.” Imam Abu Bakr, may God Almighty have mercy on him, mentioned a hadith in this context. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, whom I mentioned above, and the hadith of Abu Hurairah: A woman was tortured for a cat, and whoever prayed after Friday,And what contradicts it is the hadith of Ibn Umar, and about performing ablution from what has been touched by fire, he mentioned it, and the discussion of it is lengthy. Al-Hakim, may God have mercy on him, said: “And I Remembering, by the will of God Almighty, in this regard the narration of the great companions, may God be pleased with them all, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, from whom Zaid narrated Ibn Thabit, Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, Abdullah bin Abbas, Abdullah bin Omar, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, and Ubayy bin Ka’b, Jabir bin Abdullah, Aisha, Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, Uqba bin Al-Harith, Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, and Anas bin Malik, Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid, Abu Rafi', the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Umamah bin Sahl, Abu Tufayl, and Abu Nadra. Al-Ghifari, Abu Rahm Al-Ghifari, Shaddad bin Al-Hahad, Abu Hadrad Abdullah bin Hadrad Al-Aslami, and Abu Razin Al-Uqaili, Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, Amr bin Al-Hamq, Al-Hajjaj Al-Aslami, Abdullah bin Aqeem, and Al-Aghar. Al-Juhani and Al-Sharid bin Suwayd, may God be pleased with them all. The number of companions who narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah reached twenty-eight. As a man, as for the followers, there is none among them more distinguished, more famous, more honorable, and more knowledgeable than the companions of Abu Hurairah.Their mention in this place will take a long time due to their large number. May God protect us from disobeying the Messenger of the Lord of the Worlds and the chosen Companions. And the imams of the religion from among the followers and those after them from the imams of the Muslims, may God be pleased with them all, in the matter of the one who preserves the laws of religion for us, my father Hurairah, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6177","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, Abi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sayyar, On the authority of Jabr ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, promised us the expedition to India. I was martyred. I was one of the best martyrs, and if I return, I will be the liberated Abu Hurairah.”"
"6178","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, He said: “Abu Mahdhurah is Aws bin Ma’ir bin Wahb bin Damous bin Saad bin Jumah, and his mother is Khuza’ia,” Ibrahim Al-Harbi said: “ This is what Musab al-Zubayri said, and it was said: His name is Samurah bin Ma’ir."
"6179","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told us, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told us, he said: “Abu Mahdhurah Aws bin Ma’ir bin Ludhaan bin Rabi’ah,” said Shabab, and Abu al-Yaqzan said: “Aws bin Ma’ir was killed on the day of Badr as an infidel, and his name is My father is Mahdhurah Salman bin Samurah.” Shabab said: “And his name is called Samurah bin Ma’ir.”
 Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abu Deleted. His name is Aws bin Ma’ir bin Luthan bin Rabi’ah bin Awayj bin Saad bin Jumah, and he had a brother from his father and mother, it is said Unais was killed on the day of Badr as an infidel, and Abu Mahdhurah died in Mecca, protected by God Almighty, in the year fifty-nine, and he did not emigrate and continued to do so. residing in Mecca.”"
"6180","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Rafi’ Al-Qushayri told us, he said: I asked Abu Sa’id bin My father told the muezzin in the Sacred Mosque about his grandfather’s name, so he said: “Ma’ir bin Muhayriz.”"
"6181","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Ayoub bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Safiya A fragmented girl, that Abu Mahdhura had a lump in the front of his head. When he sat down, he sent it so that it would reach the ground, so they said to him: Why not? Do you shave it? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped it with his hand, but I was not going to shave it until I died.” So he did not shave it until he died.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6181 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6182","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told me, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid al-Makki told us, Muhammad bin Muawiyah told us, al-Hudhayl bin Bilal told us, He said: I heard Ibn Abi Mahdhurah speaking, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made for the Banu Abd al-Muttalib watering, and for Banu Abd al-Dar to protect us, and to make the call to prayer for us and our loyalists.”"
"6183","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Khaled bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, Kamil bin Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abu It is forbidden to make the call to prayer long and to make the iqamah tense.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6183 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6184","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Hanthali told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Juraij told me, he told me Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Malik bin Abi Mahdhura, that Abdullah bin Muhayriz told him: “He was an orphan in my father’s lap Mahdhura Ibn Ma'ir until he prepared him for the Levant.”"
"6185","Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Muqri informed me, Abu al-Abbas al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, He said: I heard our companions saying: On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Mu’adhdhin gave the call to prayer, “So Abu Mahdhurah carried him and threw him into Zamzam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6185 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6186","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “The name of Abu Usayd Al-Saadi Malik bin Rabi’ah"
"6187","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Abu Usayd Malik bin Rabi’ah bin Al-Badan bin Aamer bin Amr bin Awf bin Haritha bin Amr bin Al-Khazraj bin Sa’idah.”"
"6188","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Yazid Al-Sada’i told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Abi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of some of Banu Sa`idah, on the authority of Abu Usayd Malik bin Rabi’ah, and he had “witnessed full moon, and then his sight went away.”"
"6189","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Arim Abu Al-Numan told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Hazim, On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, that Abu Usayd al-Sa’idi was blinded before the killing of Othman, may God be pleased with him, and he said: “Praise be to God who gave me comfort.” Through my insight into the life of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When God wanted temptation among His servants, He withheld my gaze from it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6189 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6190","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “In the Sunnah the congregation In the year forty, Abu Usayd Malik bin Rabi’ah bin Amir bin Awf bin Al-Khazraj bin Sa’idah died, and he was the last of the people to die. Badr, and he was among those who saw the angels on the day of Badr, but his sight stopped, so he was trustworthy of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his wives.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6190 - This is an error"
"6191","Abdullah bin Ghanim Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, he said: “Abu Usayd died. Al-Saadi in the year sixty, and he is ninety-two years old.”"
"6192","Abu Abd Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, my father told me, on the authority of Al-Abbas Bin Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, he said: “I saw Abu Usayd Al-Sa’idi after his sight had gone, short, with a white head and beard. I saw his head with a lot of hair, and Abu Usayd died in the city in the year sixty, when he was ninety-eight years old, and he was the last of the people of the city to die. ""Badr""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6192 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6193","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Abi told me Dhi’ib, and Anas bin Iyaad, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, that Abu Usayd Al-Ansari came as a captive from Bahrain, so they lined up. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and looked at them and saw a woman crying. He said: “What makes you cry?” She said: My son was sold to Banu Abs, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Usayd: “You should ride, and let us bring him.” So Abu Usayd rode. So he brought it, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6193 - Sent"
"6194","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us dictation, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of his father, that it happened that young men asked Abu Usayd al-Saadi about the choice of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Ansar, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The best tribes of the Ansar are the Banu al-Najjar, then the Banu Abd al-Ashhal. Then Bani Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj built, then Bani Sa’idah, and in all the houses of the Ansar there was good.” Abu Usayd said: “If I had accepted anything other than the truth, I would have begun With my thighs, Banu Sa`idah.”"
"6195",""
"6196","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Anmati told me, he said: I heard Harun bin Abdullah, saying: “Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, nicknamed Abu Abdul-Rahman."
"6197","Sheikh Abu Bakr told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “Bilal bin Al-Harith died. Al-Muzani in the year sixty"
"6198","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani is one of those carrying a banner from the three brigades that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, held for them on the day of the conquest of Mecca. Bilal was nicknamed Abu Abdul Rahman, and he lived in the two mountains of Muzainah: Al-Ash’ar and Al-Ajrad, and he came to the city often, and he died in the year “Sixty years old, and at that time he was eighty years old.”"
"6199","Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Durastawayh Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah told us Al-Uwaisi, Humaid bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, and Bilal, the sons of Yahya bin Bilal bin Al-Harith, on the authority of their father, on the authority of their grandfather, Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, broke off the severing of ties with him, and wrote to him: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him.” Bilal bin Al-Harith, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him the minerals of the qiblah: its two valleys, its two seats, Al-Jashima, and Dhath Al-Nasab, and where the arm fits. From Quds if it is a predator,” and Muawiyah wrote"
"6200","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Bilal ibn al-Harith, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A Muslim is one who is safe from Muslims. His tongue and his hand"
"6201","Ismail bin Ali Al-Hatbi told me, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Muaddeb told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan Al-Jawhari told us, he informed us Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi, Rabia bin Abi Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, is Hajj canceled for us in particular, or for people in general? He said: “Rather, especially for us.”
 And with its chain of transmission, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged by oath with the witness.”"
"6202","Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi, the ascetic, told me, Musa bin Zakaria al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Safwan bin Al-Mu'tal bin Rahdha bin Khuza'i bin Muharib bin Murrah bin Hilal bin Falij bin Dhakwan bin Tha'labah bin Bahta bin Sulaym, and he has He lived in Basra on the way to Marbad. He died on the island, near Shamshat, and his grave is there.”"
"6203",""
"6204",""
"6205","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Saeed bin Suleiman Al-Wasiti told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, Abu Wahb narrated to us, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Safwan ibn al-Mu’tal, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to call you not to withdraw into The jar
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6205 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6206","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Safwan ibn al-Mu’tal sat with Hassan ibn Thabit So he hit him, and Safwan said when he hit him:
 [Long Sea]
 Take the sword flies from me, for I am... a boy, if I get mad, I am not a poet.
 But I protect my father-in-law and recover... from the faded, innocent, pure thrower.
 Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Safwan fled, and Hassan came to prepare with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God asked him May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he would give him the gift of Safwan, so he gave it to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, compensated him.” And peace be upon him, a wall of great palm trees and a Roman slave girl named Sirin. So Hassan sold the wall to Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan during his rule for money. Great: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6206 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6207","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Abu Hurairah Muhammad bin Firas Al-Sayrifi told us, Salam bin Qutaybah, Omar bin Nabhan told us, Salam Abu Issa told me, Safwan bin Al-Mu’talal Al-Sulami told us, he said: “We went out as pilgrims, but when we were at Al-Arj We saw a snake that was disturbed, and it soon died, and a man from among us brought out for it a piece of cloth that was defective to him, so he wrapped it in it and disappeared into the The ground and buried it, then we came to Mecca, and we were at the Sacred Mosque when a person stood over us and said: Which of you is the companion of Amr bin Jabir? We said: We do not know Amr bin Jabir. He said: Which of you is the companion of the jinn? They said: This one. He said: Either God rewarded you with good, or he was the last of the nine to die who came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “They listen to the Qur’an.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6207 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6208","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan bin Hamza told us. Al-Islami, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hamza ibn Amr Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father Hamza ibn Amr, he said: “There was the beginning of The food of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the hands of his Companions this night and this night. He said: He came to me, and I made food The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I took him to him.” Sufyan bin Hamza said: “Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami was nicknamed Abu Muhammad, he died in the year sixty-one, and he was seventy-one years old.”"
"6209","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Rusta told us, Sufyan bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hamza Al-Aslami, “Hamza was nicknamed Abu Muhammad, and he died in the year sixty-one.”"
"6210","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdul told us Allah Al-Uwaisi, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, “that Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim was killed on the day of Hurra."
"6211","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim bin Amr bin Awf bin Mabdoul bin Amr bin Ghoneim bin Mazen bin Al-Najjar, and his mother is Amara and her name is Nusayba bint Ka'b bin Amr bin Awf bin Mabdhul witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the scenes with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was an uncle. Abbad bin Tamim, and Abdullah bin Zaid was among those who killed Musaylimah the Liar on the Day of Al-Yamamah, and Abdullah bin Zaid was killed on the Day of Al-Hurra. It was the last Dhul-Hijjah of the year sixty-three in the emirate of Yazid bin Muawiyah.”"
"6212",""
"6213","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali told me, he said: “Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim is a Khazraj from Bani Mazen bin Al-Najjar, and he is the killer of Musaylimah.”"
"6214","Muhammad ibn Yusuf, the muezzin, told me, Muhammad ibn Imran told me, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb told us, he said: I heard my father saying: “Abdullah ibn Zaid is nicknamed Abu Muhammad."
"6215","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Wahib told us, Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, he said: When the time of Al-Harrah came, a man came to Abdullah bin Zaid and said: This is Ibn Hanzalah, who pledges the pledge of allegiance to people on death. He said: “I will not pledge allegiance to anyone on this matter after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6215 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6216","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Rabi’ah bin Ka'b Al-Aslami converted to Islam, and he accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the past from among the people of the Suffah. He used to serve the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not Rabi’ah ibn Ka’b continued to accompany the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina and to fight with him until he was arrested. Then Rabi’ah left Medina and went down to a well. A Muslim country, which is at a distance from Medina, and Rabia remained until the days of Al-Hurra, and it perished there. Al-Hurra was in Dhul-Hijjah in the year three ""sixty"""
"6217","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, he said: Abu told me Imran Al-Juni, Rabia bin Ka’b Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, told me: I was serving the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said to me: “O Rabia, won’t you get married?” I said: No, by God, I do not want to get married.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6217 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6218","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, he said: “Muadh bin Al-Harith Al-Qari From the Banu Al-Najjar, his nickname is Abu Al-Harith bin Al-Hubab bin Al-Arqam bin Awf bin Malik bin Al-Najjar, and he is Muadh Al-Qari, nicknamed Abu Al-Harith. He was killed on the day of Al-Harrah in Dhul-Hijjah in the year sixty-three, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6219","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Maqil bin Sinan Al-Ashja'i witnessed the conquest with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and was killed on the Day of Al-Harrah in the year sixty-three."
"6220","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “It was a stronghold Ibn Sinan Ibn Muzhar Ibn Arki Ibn Fatyan Ibn Subay’ Ibn Bakr Ibn Ashja’ witnessed the conquest with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman bin Ziyad al-Ashja’i told me, on the authority of his father, who said: Ma’qil bin Sinan al-Ashja’i had accompanied the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he carried the banner of his people on the day of the conquest. He was a young and young man, and he remained after that until Al-Walid ibn Utbah ibn Ubai sent him. Sufyan, and he was in charge of Medina, and Maqil ibn Sinan and Muslim ibn Uqba, who is known as Musharrif, met - so he said, Maqil is for Musharraf - and he was He forgot about him and talked to him until he mentioned the stronghold of Yazid bin Muawiyah - and Maqil said: “I left out of hatred to pledge allegiance to this man, and he was a judge. And the fate of my going out to him was a man who drank alcohol and committed adultery in the Sacred Sanctuary.” Then he became angry with him, and mentioned characteristics that were in him, then he said to an extravagant person: “I would love to do that with you.” Musharraf said: As for me mentioning that to the Commander of the Faithful on this day, no, by God, I will not do it. But God has a covenant and covenant with me that He will not do. My hand has power over you, and I have power over you, unless I strike the one in whom your eyes are. So when a prodigal came to the city and attacked them in the days of the heat, and it was Maqil ibn Sinan was at that time the companion of the emigrants, and a captive prodigal brought him, and said to him: O Maqil ibn Sinan, are you thirsty? He said: “Yes, may God bless the prince.” He said: Have a crystal drink for him. He said: So they took it to him and he said: Did you drink and quench your thirst? He said: “Yes.” He said: By God, do not desire anything that makes you happy after this, O Nawfal bin Musahiq, get up and behead him. So he got up to him and killed him patiently, and it was The free woman in Dhul-Hijjah in the year sixty-three, and the Ansar poet said:
 [Long Sea]

 Aren't those Ansar mourning their sorrows... and I encourage them to mourn Ma'qil bin Sinan"
"6221","Sheikh Abu Bakr told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr, they said: “Abu Muhammad al-Ash’ath ibn Qays al-Kindi from Banu al-Harith ibn Muawiyah died in Kufa, and al-Hasan ibn Ali died there after the peace treaty Muawiyah accompanied him, and Al-Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with them both, prayed over him."
"6222",""
"6223","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, he said: “Al-Miswar bin Makhramah bin Nawfal Bin Uhayb bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra, his mother was Atika bint Awf, sister of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf.”"
"6224","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Many, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah al-Daili narrated to me, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, that Ali ibn al-Hussein, narrated to him, that when they came Medina from the presence of Yazid bin Muawiyah after the killing of Al-Hussein bin Ali, may God’s peace and blessings be upon them both, Al-Maswar bin Makhramah met him He said: “I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon from his pulpit, and I was in a wet dream on that day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6224 - Narrated by meaning"
"6225","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayat told us, he said: “Al-Miswar bin Makhramah died in Mecca in the year Sixty-four, and it is said: He died in Al-Hijun. He was struck by the stone of a catapult, while he was in Al-Hijr in Mecca, so he stayed for five days, then he died, and the funeral prayer was prayed over him. Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, who was sixty-eight years old.”"
"6226","Mukhlid ibn Ja`far told me, and Muhammad ibn Jarir told us, saying: “Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah was born in Mecca two years after the Hijra, and he died. For the crescent of the month of Rabi’ al-Akhir in the year sixty-four.” And Yahya ibn Ma’in, as I spoke about him, used to say: “Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah died. “In the year seventy-three,” and this is an incorrect statement."
"6227","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zakaria Al-Faqih told us, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Zabala Al-Makhzoumi, Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Makhzoumi told me, my brother Al-Maswar bin Abdullah told me, On the authority of his father, he said: Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar ibn Makhrama told me, on the authority of her father, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed me “May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “There are dates on a plate. None of these two of you are with me.” And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died when I was eleven years old."
"6228","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us: Hatim bin Wardan told us: Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Cells were presented to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So he divided it among his companions, and my father said to me: Go with us to him, for cellars have come to him. So my father spoke at the door, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recognized him. He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) raised his voice and came out with a qiba and started saying: “I hid this for you, I hid this for you.” This hadith was narrated in the book of Muslim. “I only prepared it so that it would be known that he used to come with his father, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and that he had memorized the Misoor’s speeches of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.”"
"6229","As Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Abd Al-Warith told us. Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Qays, on the authority of Al-Miswar Ibn Makhramah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us. He greeted Arafat and thanked and praised God, then said: “As for what follows, the people of polytheism and idols used to be repelled from this place.” When the sun was on the tops of the mountains, as if they were the turbans of men on their faces, and we would pay after it had set, and they would push from “The Sacred Mash’ar when the sun is set.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “It is authentic and proven according to what I mentioned.” Al-Miswar bin Makhramah heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not as the mob of our companions imagine him to be, that he is one of those who narrate without hearing.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6229 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6230","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Al-Dahhak bin Qais bin Khalid bin Wahb bin Tha’labah bin Wathilah bin Amr bin Sinan bin Muharib bin Fahr, and his mother was Umaima bint Rabi’a is from Kinana, and she is also the mother of his sister Fatima bint Qais, the sister of Al-Dahhak bin Qais, and they are of the same father and mother.”"
"6231","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told me, Shabab Al-Asfari told us, Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Qudhami told us, about His father, on the authority of his grandfather, and Abu Al-Yaqzan and others said: “Ibn Ziyad came to the Levant, and the people of the Levant pledged allegiance to Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr except The people of Al-Jabiya, so he pledged allegiance to Ibn Ziyad, and from there there were from the Umayyads and their followers: Marwan bin Al-Hakam, and after him to Khalid bin Yazid Bin Muawiyah, and that was in the middle of Dhul-Qa'dah in the year sixty-four. Then he went to Al-Dahhak bin Qais, and they met at Marj Rahit, so they fought. Twenty days, then Al-Dahhak bin Qays and his companions were defeated. This occurred in Dhul-Hijjah in the year sixty-four, so Al-Dahhak bin Qays was killed. Qays and many people from Qays.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6231 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6232","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Al-Dahhak was Ibn Qays the Great, nicknamed Abu Unays. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested. Al-Dahhak was a boy who had not yet reached puberty.
 So Mukhlid bin Ja’far told me, and Muhammad bin Jarir told me, saying: Al-Waqidi claimed: “Al-Dahhak bin Qays did not hear from the Prophet, may God bless him. And peace be upon him. We say, and with God’s success, that the correct statement is that of Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Jarir, may God have mercy on him. It has been authenticated for him on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “peace and blessings of God be upon him.” There are narrations in which he mentioned hearing it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"6233","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani did not tell us about the origin of his book. Abu Muhammad al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Bayhaqi told us, Sunayd ibn Dawud Al-Masisi, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad bin Talha told me, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, Al-Dahhak bin Qais, who is just and satisfactory, said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There will still be a ruler from the Quraysh.” Among them are:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6233 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6234","What Sheikh Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us in dictation, Abu Khalifa Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya bin Humaid Al-Taweel told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Al-Dahhak bin Qais wrote to Qais bin Al-Haytham, when Yazid bin Muawiyah died: Peace be upon you, either. After that, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, before the Hour is a temptation like pieces of smoke, from which a man’s heart will die just as it dies.” His body, a man in the morning therein is a believer and an unbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and an unbeliever in the morning therein some people sell their religion for a small sum of this world.” And Yazid has died, and you are our brothers and sisters.” Among them:"
"6235","What Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri reported on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, who said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Dahhak bin Qays Al-Fihri. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If a man comes to the people and they say: Welcome, then welcome will be upon him on the day he meets his Lord, and when he comes The people said to him: Parched, so parched will be for him on the Day of Resurrection. Among them:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6235 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6236","What Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abu Unaysa, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Qais, who said: There was a woman in Medina who had sexual intercourse with women, and she was called Umm Attiya. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “Keep your breath down and do not become exhausted, for it is more beautiful for the face and more pleasing to the husband.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6236 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6237","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas bin Wael bin Hashim bin Saeed bin Sahm bin Amr bin Husays bin Ka’b. Abdullah bin Amr converted to Islam before His father, and from what he mentioned, was a tall man with red legs, great legs, and a white head and beard. He was blind at the end of his life. Abdullah died. Ibn Amr in the Levant in the year sixty-five, and he was seventy-two years old at that time. He was nicknamed Abu Muhammad.”"
"6238","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “The death of Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Amr bin Al-Aas, and his mother was Rayta bint Munabbih bin Al-Hajjaj bin Amer bin Hudhayfah bin Saad bin Sahm in the year sixty-five, and he was He is dyed black, and Amr ibn al-Aas was twelve years older than his son.”"
"6239","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri narrated to me, Dawud bin Rashid narrated to us, Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to me, Salem bin Abd narrated to me. Allah Al-Kala’i, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Qurashi, said: Abdullah bin Omar entered upon Abdullah bin Amr, and he had turned his beard black, and Abdullah said Allah Ibn Amr: Peace be upon you, O Shuwaib. Then Ibn Amr said to him: Do you not know me, Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: Yes, I know you as an old man. Today you are a young man. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Yellowishness is the pigment of a believer, and redness is “The pigment of a Muslim, and black is the pigment of an infidel.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6239 - Munkar Hadith"
"6240","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ismail bin Al-Hasan Al-Allaf told us, in Egypt, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Humaid bin Hani Abu Hani said that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli saying: “Three people came to Abdullah bin Amr and said: O Abu ""Muhammad"""
"6241","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, his mother was Rayta bint Munabbih bin Al-Hajjaj bin Amer bin Hudhayfah bin Saad bin Sahm bin Amr bin Husays bin Kaab bin Luay"
"6242","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take the Qur’an from four people: two men from among the immigrants, and two men from The Ansar include Abdullah bin Masoud, Salim the client of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy bin Ka’b, and Muadh bin Jabal.” He said: He singled out Abdullah. Ibn Masoud said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6242 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6243","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abdul-Malik bin told us Qadamah Al-Jumahi, Amr bin Shuaib told me in the Levant, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The mother of Abdullah bin Amr was Rayta bint Munabbih. Bin Al-Hajjaj was kind to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he came to her one day and said: How are you, Umm Abdullah? She said: Fine, and Abdullah is a man who had left this world. His father said to him on the day of Siffin: Go out and fight. He said: O father, do you command me to I will go out and fight, and it was from the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as you have heard. He said: I adjure you by God, do you know that what was from the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is that he took your hand and placed it in my hand? He said: “Obey your father Amr bin Al-Aas.” He said: Yes. He said: I command you to fight. He said: So he went out to fight, and when the war ended, Abdullah said:
 [Long Sea]
 If I witnessed the beauty of my position and my scene...in Siffin one day the wolves were white from it
 On the eve of the night, the people of Iraq came as if they were... spring clouds that had been shaken by the mountains.
 When I said, “They turned away hastily,” a battalion of them would stand firm for us, and a battalion of them would lose ground.
 So they said to us: We see that you should pledge allegiance to Ali... So we said: Rather, we see that you should compete."
"6244","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told me, Yahya bin Bukair told me, Al-Layth told me about Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr May God be pleased with them. He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and the people were terrified, so I went out with my weapon on, and looked at Salem. Abu Hudhayfah's servant, wearing his weapon, walked calmly, so I said: I will follow the example of this righteous man until he came and sat at the door of the Messenger of God. I sat with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out angry and said: “O people, what a lightness this is.” Were you unable to create this luxury as these two believing men did? This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6244 - True"
"6245","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Al-Homsi told us, Muhammad bin Himyar told us, Amr bin Qais Al-Sakouni told me, he said: “ I was having conversations with my father when a man approached, and when the people saw him, they rushed to him and said: And I was among those who started to sit with him, so I said: Who is this man? They said: This is Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas."
"6246",""
"6247","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, I am Jarir, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Akhnas bin Khalifa Al-Dhabi said: Ka’b Al-Ahbar saw Abdullah bin Amr giving fatwas to the people, so he said: Who is this? They said: This is Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, so he sent a man from his companions to him and said: Tell him: O Abdullah bin Amr, do not hesitate. A lie against God, so He will afflict you with a torment, and indeed he who fabricates a lie will be disappointed. He said: The man came to him and told him that. Ibn Omar said: Ka’b told the truth. He who slanders and does not get angry has been disappointed. He said: Then he turned the man’s heel back to him, and he said: Ask him about the gathering, what it is? And where do the souls of Muslims meet? Where do the souls of the polytheists gather? So he came to him and asked him, and he said: “As for the souls of the Muslims, they gather in Jericho, and as for the souls of the polytheists, they gather in Sana’a, and as for the first Al-Hashr, for it is a fire that drives people. They see it at night but do not see it during the day.” Ka’b’s messenger returned to him and informed him of what he had said, so he said: This is a scholar who asked him the truth"
"6248","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Asma bin Haritha bin Hind bin Abdullah bin Ghayath bin Saad bin Amr bin Amer bin Afsa, the client of Banu Haritha.”"
"6249","Saeed bin Ata bin Abi Marwan told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Asma bin Harithah Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, who said: I entered to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Ashura, and he said: “Have you been silent today, O Asmaa?” I said: No. He said: “Then fast.” I said: I have had lunch, O Messenger of God. He said: “Fast for what remains and order your people to fast.” Asma said: So I took my sandals. With my hand, I entered my saddle until I came to my people and said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to fast. They said: We had lunch. So I said: He has commanded you to fast for the rest of your day."
"6250",""
"6251","Al-Zubayr bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Hafiz told me about Istrabad, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Zaid bin Al-Harish told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad said: Ibn Al-Zabarqan, Yazid Ibn Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I did not see the names of India.” “The two sons of Haritha were nothing but two servants of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as they had been at his gate for a long time and served him, and they were in need.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6251 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6252","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Hind bin Haritha Al-Aslami witnessed Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Hind bin Haritha died in Medina during the succession of the Emir The believers, may God be pleased with him, and it was said: They were eight brothers, all of whom accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and witnessed the Pledge of Ridwan: They are Asmaa, Hind, Kharash, Dhu’ayb, Humran, Fadalah, Salamah, and Malik Banu Harithah bin Sa’id.”"
"6253","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Asam told me about the Burdan Bridge. Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Yazid bin Abi told us. Abdullah bin Ghayath, Salama bin Al-Akwa’, may God be pleased with him, narrated to us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a man who converted to Islam on the day Ashura, and he said: “Whoever eats and drinks, let him complete his fast, and whoever has not eaten, let him fast for the rest of his day.” The narration has already been mentioned that the names of He is the Messenger of that, and it was narrated that he was an Indian.”"
"6254","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham told us, Abu Hisham al-Makhzoumi told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala al-Aslami, on the authority of Yahya bin Hind bin Haritha, on the authority of his father Hind bin Haritha, may God be pleased with him, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him on the day of Ashura and said: “Order your people to fast this day.” He said: What do you think, O Messenger of God, if you find them? Have they been fed? He said: “Let them complete the last of their day.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6254 - True"
"6255","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Masqala told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar said: “Suleiman bin Surad bin Al-Jun bin Abi Al-Jun, who is Abdul-Uzza bin Munqidh bin Rabi’ah, and his nickname is Abu Mutrif He converted to Islam and accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his name was Yasar. When he converted to Islam, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him Suleiman, and he had a tooth. high and honorable among his people, and he descended on Kufa when the Muslims had descended on it and testified with the Commander of the Faithful Ali, may God be pleased with him, in Siffin, then he He went out to demand the blood of Al-Hussein bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, and under his banner were four thousand men, and Suleiman bin Surad was killed in that incident. His head was brought to Marwan ibn al-Hakam. Suleiman was ninety-three years old on the day he was killed."
"6256","I heard Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya saying: I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Bukhari says: “Al-Mukhtar bin Abi Ubaid killed this Suleiman bin Surad after Sulayman bin Surad killed Ubaid Allah bin Ziyad.”"
"6257","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, he said: “Sulaiman bin Surad killed Ubayd Allah Ibn Ziyad"
"6258","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, “Abu Shurayh Ka'b bin Amr Al-Khuza'i died in the year sixty-eight, and his name is disputed. It was said: Khuwaylid bin Amr."
"6259","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Jallab told me - may God have mercy on him - the imam of his time in Iraq, Ibrahim bin Ishaq, narrated to me. Al-Harbi, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: “Al-Numan bin Bashir bin Saad bin Tha’labah bin Khalas bin Zayd bin Malik Al-Aghar bin Tha'labah bin Ka'b bin Al-Khazraj bin Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and his mother was Amra bint Rawaha, sister of Abdullah bin Rawaha He was born to Numan Abdullah, and through him he was nicknamed Abu Abdullah.”"
"6260","Abdul Rahman bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, that Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm said: We sat with him He mentioned the first Ansar born after the arrival of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina, and he said: “Al-Nu’man bin Bashir was born after The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina a year or less than a year ago. He said: They mentioned Abdullah bin Abi Talha, and he said: “If it had been Salim’s mother was pregnant with him, and she gave birth after she came to Medina.”"
"6261","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Suleiman bin Ahmed told us, he said: I heard Abu Mushar saying: “Al-Numan bin Bashir was killed between Salamiyah and Homs, he was killed in a rage.”"
"6262","Then the chief judge Muhammad bin Saleh Al-Hashimi told me, Ali bin Muhammad Al-Madaini told us, Yaqoub bin Daoud Al-Thaqafi told us, and Maslamah bin Muharib, and others said: “When Al-Dahhak bin Qais was killed in Marj Rahit, and it was the middle of Dhul-Hijjah in the year sixty-four years during the caliphate. Marwan bin Al-Hakam. Al-Numan bin Bashir wanted to escape from Homs, where he was working, so he was afraid and called for Ibn Al-Zubayr, so the people of Homs asked for him. Homs, so they killed him and beheaded him.” The narrations in the two Sahih books have been authenticated by Al-Nu’man bin Bashir hearing from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"6263","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Omar bin Hafs told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them, said: We accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we heard him say: “Indeed, before the Hour is a trial like The dark night in which a man becomes a believer in the morning and becomes a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and becomes a disbeliever in the morning, people will sell their creation therein for a share of the world. “Easy.” Al-Hasan said: “By God, we have seen them as forms without minds, bodies without dreams, beds of fire and flies of greed, taking two dirhams in the morning.” And they go for two dirhams, and one of them sells his debt for the price of a goat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6263 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6264","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, his name is Al-Harith. Ibn Awf Ibn Usayd Ibn Jabir Ibn Abdah Manat Ibn Yashja’ Ibn Amir Ibn Laith”"
"6265","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Abu Waqid Al-Harith bin Malik, and Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, my grandfather told me, saying: I heard Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr saying: “Abu Al-Laythi Al-Harith ibn Awf ibn Usayd ibn Jabir ibn Awthrah ibn Abd Manat ibn Yashja’ ibn Amir, and he was an early convert to Islam. The Liwa of Banu Layth, Damra, and Saad bin Bakr were with him on the day of the conquest, and Abu Waqid remained after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. for a period of time, then he went out to Mecca and lived there for a year and died there.”"
"6266","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, who said: “We visited Al-Laythi during his illness in which he died, and he died and we buried him in Mecca in The cemetery of the immigrants in a trap. It was called the cemetery of the immigrants because those who had come to Medina and then performed Hajj and lived nearby were buried there. He died in Mecca, and Abu Waqid al-Laythi, Abdullah bin Omar and others were buried in this cemetery, and Abu Waqid died. Al-Laythi, in the year sixty-eight, and he is eighty-five years old.”"
"6267","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, my father told me, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us. Al-Bakri, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha told us, my uncle Musa bin Talha told me, Abu Waqid Al-Laythi told me, he said: I was sitting at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, touched his knee, and someone came to him, so he touched his ear, and the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed. And the blood flowed to his beds, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and then he said: “This is the messenger of Amer bin Tufayl, threatening me and threatening those who seek refuge with me. God Almighty sufficed him with the progeny of Ishmael and Banu Qayla, meaning the Ansar."
"6268","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hammani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Amin, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that he heard Abu Waqid Al-Laythi say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lists of the pulpits of salaries In heaven »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6268 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6269","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Zaid bin Arqam bin Zaid bin Qais bin Al-Nu’man bin Malik bin Al-Aghar bin Tha’labah bin Ka’b bin Al-Khazraj, and his nickname was Abu Amr, and he died in Kufa at the time of Al-Mukhtar bin Abi Ubaid in the year sixty-eight.”"
"6270","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: “I said To Zaid bin Arqam: O Abu Amr!"
"6271","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq said: The people went out to draw water, and among them was Zaid bin Arqam. There was only a man between me and him, so I said to him: O Abu Amr, how many raids did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? Peace be upon him? He said: “Nineteen.” I said: How many days did you raid with him? He said: “Seventeen.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6271 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6272","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Kamil Abu Al-Ala told us, he said: I heard Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja`dah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted us until we reached Ghadeer Khumm, and he ordered that a day should be made, so we could roam. One day a day came upon us that was hotter than that, so he thanked God and praised Him. And he said: “O people, no prophet was ever sent except that he lived half the life of those who came before him, and I am about to be called and answered. And I am leaving among you what after which you will never go astray, the Book of God Almighty.” Then he stood up and took Ali’s hand, may God be pleased with him, and said: “O people! Who has more right over you than yourselves?"
"6273","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, and Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani, told us: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the martyr, may God be pleased with him, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh al-Anbari told us, Ubayy told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died when I was fifteen years old.” This is how it was narrated by Ibrahim ibn Tahman, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi, and Al-Walid bin Khaled, on the authority of Shu’bah. As for the hadith of Abu Dawud,"
"6274",""
"6275","So Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shairi told us, Mahshar bin Issam told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Abbad bin Al-Walid Al-Anzi told us, Al-Walid bin Khalid bin Al-Arabi told us, Shu’bah told us, Abu Ishaq told me, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. I am fifteen years old.” This was narrated by Sa’id bin Abi Arouba and Idris bin Yazid Al-Awdi, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq.
 As for the hadith of Saeed -"
"6276","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, Khalid told us Ibn Al-Harith, Saeed Ibn Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “He died The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I was fifteen years old and had been circumcised.” The judge - may God have mercy on him - said: “Abu Ishaq and Abu Ali Sa’id disagreed. Ibn Jubayr is in the age of Ibn Abbas, and the narration of Abu Ishaq is closer to the truth. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it is Better than all the differences in his age.”"
"6277","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abu died Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Abbas, who is seventy-one years old, was born in Al-Shaab three years before the Hijra.”"
"6278","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Sulaiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “He was nicknamed Abu Al-Abbas.” Ali said: Hajjaj told us, then Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Nawfal, he said: “I said to Ibn Abbas: O Abu Abbas.”"
"6279","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Musaddad bin Mashad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus, and he Hatem bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was praying at the end of the night, so I stood up behind him, so he took me and made me stay on top of his shoes. When he came to pray, I gasped. When he left, he said: “What’s the matter with you?” I will make you my sandal and you will be humiliated.” I said: No one should wear your sandal while you are the Messenger of God. He liked it, so he prayed to God to give me more. From understanding and knowledge, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6279 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6280","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Suleiman bin Harb told us, and Abu Salama told us: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was In Maimunah’s house, she performed ablution for him, and Maimunah said to him: Abdullah bin Abbas performed ablution for you, and he said: “Oh God, grant him wisdom in religion.” And he taught him the interpretation: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6280 - True"
"6281","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Sinan Al-Rahwi told us, Al-Kawthar told us Ibn Hakim Abu Muhammad Al-Halabi, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I am the most compassionate of my nation It was recited by Abu Bakr, and the most stubborn of it in the command of God was Omar, and the most shy of it was Uthman, and the recited by Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and the most obligatory of it Zayd bin Thabit, and that Ali bin Abi Talib performed it, and that the most knowledgeable about what is permissible and forbidden was Muadh bin Jabal, and that the most correct in the dialect of Abu Dhar, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and the rabbi of this nation is Abdullah bin Abbas.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6281 - Kawthar bin Hakim has fallen"
"6282","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Harb and A’rim bin Al-Fadl told us, they said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: The meat of domestic donkeys was mentioned to Jabir, and he said: “He refused that sea - meaning Ibn Abbas - and recited {Say no “I find in what was revealed to me forbidden.” [Al-An’am: 145]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6282 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6283","Abu Abdullah told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Numayr told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: “He was Ibn Abbas is called Al-Bahr because of his great knowledge."
"6284","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, Ubayy told us, Sharik, on the authority of Mundhir al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: “Ibn Abbas was the rabbi of this nation.”
 He said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: “I have never seen someone like Ibn Abbas, and he died.” The day he died, he was the rabbi of this nation.” And Muhammad bin Ali said the day Ibn Abbas died: “Today the one who raised this nation died.”"
"6285","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: “He was Ibn Abbas was called Al-Bahr due to his abundance of knowledge."
"6286","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, Al-Minhal bin Amr told me, he said: Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas told me, On the authority of his father, he said: Al-Abbas, may God be pleased with him, ordered me to spend the night with the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I went to the mosque, and he prayed. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the last evening prayer until no one was left in the mosque except him. He said: Then he passed by me and said: “Who is this?” So I said: Abdullah. He said: “His mouth.” I said: “My father ordered me to spend the night with you.” He said: “The truth.” When he entered, he said: “Make a bed for Abdullah.” He said: So I was brought with a pillow made of sackcloth. He said: Al-Abbas asked me, “Do not sleep until you have memorized his prayers.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me. So he slept until I heard his snoring. He said: Then he sat on his bed and raised his head to the sky and said: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times, then recited This verse is from the end of Surah Al Imran until he concluded it {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth} [Al-Baqarah: 164], then he got up and urinated, then he cleaned his siwak. Then he performed ablution, then entered his prayer place and prayed two rak’ahs, neither short nor long. He said: Then he prayed, then prayed Witr. When he finished his prayer, I heard him say: “O God, place light in my sight, place light in my hearing, place light in my tongue, place light in my heart, place light on my right, and place light on my left Light, and make light before me, and make light behind me, and make above me light, and make light below me, and make light for me on the day I meet you, and make greater for me Noura: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6286 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6287","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Zainab bint Sulaiman bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, my father told me, he said: I heard my father say: He said: Abbas sent his son Abdullah to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he fell asleep. Behind him, with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a man. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned and said: “When did you come, my beloved?” He said: An hour ago, he said: “Did you see anyone with me?” He said: Yes, I saw a man. He said: “That is Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, and no human being has seen him except my blind people, unless he is a prophet, but that will be done.” At the end of your life.” Then he said: “O God, teach him interpretation, give him understanding of religion, and make him among the people of faith.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6287 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"6288","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Abu Asim told us, Shabib bin Bishr told us, Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the exit and saw a tower covered, and the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Who made this?” I said: “I am.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, teach him the interpretation of the Qur’an.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6288 - Shabib bin Bishr is gentle"
"6289","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, On the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: “If Ibn Abbas had touched our teeth, none of us would have slept with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6289 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6290","Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Ismail told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, said: Ibn Abbas got engaged while he was at the wedding ceremony, ""so he opened Surat An-Nur, and began to recite and explain,"" so I started to say: I did not see I have never heard the words of a man like him. If Persia and the Romans had heard him, I would have embraced Islam.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6290 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6291","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muslim Abi Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Yes, the interpreter of the Qur’an is Ibn Abbas.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6291 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6292","Bakr bin Abi Dharm, the governor of Kufa, told me, Al-Hussein bin Jafar Al-Qurashi told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Malik bin Saeed bin Saeed told us Al-Hasan, narrated by Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I, a companion of mine, and Ibn Abbas performed Hajj, so he started “reciting Surat An-Nur and explaining it.” My friend said: Oh, Glory be to God, what comes out of this man’s head? If I had heard this abandonment, I would have converted to Islam. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6292 - True"
"6293","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Abu Hamza Al-Thumali told us, on the authority of Abi Salih, he said: I saw from Ibn Abbas a gathering that if all of the Quraysh were proud of, they would be proud of. I saw the people gathered until The road became narrow for them, and no one was able to come or go. He said: So I entered upon him and informed him as if they were at his door, and he said to me: “Perform ablution for me,” he said. He ablutioned and sat down, and said to me: “Go out and tell them: Whoever wanted to ask about the Qur’an and its letters and what he wanted from it.” To enter.” He said: So I went out and gave them permission, and they entered until they filled the house and the room. He said: They did not ask him about anything but he told them about it. He gave them as much as they asked for or more, then he said: “Your brothers.” He said: So they left, then he said to me: “Go out and tell whoever wants to... He will ask about what is permissible, what is forbidden, and jurisprudence, so let him enter.” So I went out and told them. He said: They entered until they filled the house and the room, and they did not ask him about Nothing but he informed them of it and added something similar to it. Then he said: “Your brothers.” He said: So they left. Then he said to me: “Go out and say: Whoever wants to He will be asked about the obligatory duties and the like, and let him enter.” He said: “So I went out and gave them notice, and they entered until they filled the house and the room, and they did not ask him about Nothing but he informed them of it and added something similar to it. Then he said: “Your brothers.” He said: So they left. Then he said to me: “Go out and say: Whoever wants to He will ask about Arabic, poetry, and strange words, and let him enter.” He said: They entered until they filled the house and the room, and they did not ask him about anything except He told them about it and gave them a similar amount. Abu Salih said: If all of Quraysh were proud of that, it would be proud of them. He said: I did not see Like this for one of the people
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6293 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6294","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Sa`id ibn Masoud told us, Yazid ibn Harun told me, Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died I said to a man from the Ansar: “Come, so-and-so, let us seek knowledge, for the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, are alive.” He said: Amazingly. To you, Ibn Abbas, do you see that people need you and among the people among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who is among them? He said: “So I left that and came to ask, if the hadith was to inform me about a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had He heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I went to him and sat at his door, and the wind blew on my face. He came out to me and said: Oh cousin. Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what brings you? What do you need? “So I say: “A hadith whose narration has reached me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Then he says: “Didn’t you send it to me?” So I say: “I have the right to come to you.” He said: Then that man stayed until the people gathered against me, so he said: “This boy was wiser than me.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6294 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"6295","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ikrimah, that people apostatized during the reign of Ali, may God be pleased with him, and he burned them with fire. This was reported to Ibn Abbas. May God be pleased with them both, and he said: If it had been me, I would have killed them, according to the words of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him,” and he did not Should I burn them, because I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not punish with the punishment of God.” This was reported to Ali, may God be pleased with him. He said: Woe to Ibn Abbas, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6295 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"6296","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Abu Dawud said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, used to ask me about the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said to him: Are you asking him when we have sons like him? Then Omar said: It is from what you know. He said: So he asked them about when God’s victory and conquest came. Some of them said: God commanded us to praise Him and ask His forgiveness, and some of them said: We do not know. He said to me: O Ibn Abbas, what do you say? He said: So I said: “It is the term of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he recited the surah to the end {Indeed, he was repentant} [Al-Nasr: 3]. He said: Then Omar said: “By God, I do not know of it except what you know.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6296 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6297","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Yusuf bin Kamil told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Whenever Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, called the sheikhs from the companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called me with them. He called us one day or one night and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “On the night of Destiny is what you know, so seek it in the last ten days, in which period will you see it? Some of them said: The ninth, and some of them said: The seventh, the fifth, and the third, so he said: What is the matter with you, O Ibn Abbas, that you do not speak? I said: If you wish, I can speak. He said: I only invited you to speak. He said: I speak with my opinion. He said: I ask you about your opinion. I said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, mentioned the seven more, saying: The heavens are seven, and the earth is seven,” and He said: “Indeed We divided the earth into clefts, and caused therein to grow grain, and grapes, and trees, and olive trees, and palm trees, and orchards of herbs, and fruit, and orchards. A garden, and the earth does not produce anything that people do not eat.” Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Are you unable to say anything like what he said? This boy whose affairs are not in order? Then he said: “I had forbidden you to speak, so if I call you with them, speak.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6297 - True"
"6298","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The immigrants said to Omar ibn Al-Khattab: Call our sons as you call Ibn Abbas. He said: “That is a young man.” The middle-aged man, indeed, he has a questioning tongue and a sensible heart.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6298 - Interrupted"
"6299","Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told me in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hussein, Ibrahim bin Ikrimah bin Huyay told me, he said: “It was me, Huyay bin Ya’la, and Sa’id bin Jubayr, and I came to Ibn Abbas and was asking him. About lineage, and Hayy asks him about the days of the Arabs, and Saeed bin Jubayr asks him about fatwas, as if we were scooping from a sea.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6299 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6300","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Al-Asbahani, Abdullah bin Shaddad told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abbas said: “O Ibn Shaddad, aren’t you surprised? The boy came to me and he You took my bed for a nap. He said: This is a man at the door asking for permission. He said: I said: He did not come at this hour except for a need. “His” He said: So he came in and said: Don’t you tell me about that man? I said: “What man?” He said: Ali bin Abi Talib. I said: “What is this about?” He said: When will he be sent? I said: “Glory be to God. When He is resurrected, those in the graves will be resurrected.” He said: And he said: Don’t I see you saying as these foolish people say? So I said: “Take this man away from me, so let him not enter upon me or I will strike him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6300 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6301","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Ibn Numayr told us, Ibn Abi Ubaida told us, my father told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “I was sitting with Omar ibn al-Khattab when a letter came to him that the people of Kufa So-and-so recited the Qur’an from them, and he said, “Allahu Akbar, may God have mercy on him,” so I said: Did they disagree? He said: Ugh, and how do you know? He said: He became angry, so I came to my house. He said: He sent for me after that, and I came to him. He said: I determined that you should not come. So I came to him, and he said: I was I said something. I said: I ask forgiveness from God. I will not do anything again after that. He said: I have determined that you will not repeat to me what you said. I said: I said: It has been written to me that He recited the Qur’an such-and-such, and I said: Did they disagree? He said: And from what did you know? I said: I read {And among the people is he whose speech about the life of this world amazes you, and he calls God to witness of what is in his heart} [Al-Baqarah: 204] until it ended with {By God He does not like corruption} [Al-Baqarah: 205]. If they did that, the Companionist of the Qur’an would not be patient. Then I read: “When it was said to him, “Fear God,” pride took him. For sin, Hell is sufficient for him, and wretched is the resting place. And among the people is he who sells himself seeking the pleasure of God, and God is Most Compassionate to His servants.} He said: You have spoken the truth, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6301 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6302","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Shami told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, Abu Qubaysah Sakīn ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Mujāshi’ī, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umair told me, saying: “While Ibn Abbas was with Omar, may God be pleased with him.” On the authority of them while he was holding it in his hand, Omar said: “I see the Qur’an appearing among the people.” So I said: I do not like that, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: So he gathered He took his hand from my hand, and said: “Why did you say that?” Because whenever they recite, they recite, and whenever they recite, they disagree, and whenever they disagree, they strike each other’s necks. He said: So he sat down from me. And he left me, and I remained behind him for a day that no one knows except God. Then his messenger came to me at noon and said: Answer the Commander of the Faithful. So I went to him and he said: How? Did you say? So I repeated my article. Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “If I were to conceal it from the people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6302 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6303","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us about a habit of starting a memorization or from the book, Ahmad bin Shayban Al-Ramli told us, Abdullah bin Maymun Al-Qaddah, on the authority of Shihab bin Kharash, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: It was presented to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He handed over a mule that Khosrau had given him as a gift, and he mounted it with a hair rope, then he led me behind him, then he walked with me carefully, then he turned and said: “O Boy” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “Save God and He will protect you. Save God and you will find Him before you. Get to know God in prosperity and He will know you in hardship, and if you ask, then ask God, and if you seek help, then seek help from God. The pen has passed with what is, so if people strive to benefit you with what If God did not decree it for you, they could not do it, and if people tried to harm you with what God did not decree for you, they would not be able to do it. So if you are able Act with patience and certainty, so do it. If you cannot, then be patient, for there is much good in being patient with what you hate, and know that with patience comes victory. “And know that with distress there is relief, and know that with hardship comes ease.” This is a major and high hadith from the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, except that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not mention Shihab bin Kharash, nor Al-Qaddah in the two Sahih books, and it was narrated Hadith with chains of transmission on the authority of Ibn Abbas other than this.”"
"6304","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, may God be pleased with him, told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Mu’alla bin Mahdi told us, Abu Shihab told us, Issa bin Muhammad al-Qurashi reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me And he said: “Save God and He will protect you. Save God and you will find Him before you. Get to know God in prosperity and He will know you in hardship, and know that what has befallen you has not It would have caused you to miss, and whatever missed you would not have happened to you, and know that if the creatures had gathered together to give you something, God would not have wanted to give it to you. They were not able to do it, and if they had gathered together to avert from you something that God wanted to afflict you with, they would not have been able to do that. So if you ask, then ask. God, and when you seek help, seek help from God, and know that victory comes with patience, and that relief comes with distress, and that with hardship there is ease, and know that “The pen has flowed with what is.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6304 - Issa bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi is not approved"
"6305","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told us, Abu Tufayl told me that he saw Muawiyah, may God be pleased with him, circumambulating the Kaaba and Abdullah bin Abbas left him, and I was reciting them at their backs and listening to their words. Then Muawiyah began to touch the two pillars of the stone and say to him: Ibn Abbas: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not receive these two pillars.” So Muawiyah says: O Ibn Abbas, it is nothing. It was deserted, so Ibn Abbas began not to leave it, and whenever he placed his hand on any of the pillars, he said to him: “This is an authentic hadith.” chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6305 - True"
"6306","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Suwar told us, Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik Al-Ijli, said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, three days before his death, saying: “O God, I I repent to you for what I used to give people’s fatwas regarding matters.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is one of the virtues of Abdullah bin Abbas that he returned from A fatwa that he did not take revenge on for anything other than it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6306 - True"
"6307","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, recited this verse: “Would any of you like to have a garden of palm trees and grapes flowing from Beneath it are the rivers for him therein of all kinds of fruits} [Al-Baqarah: 266] until here {then a whirlwind struck it, in which was fire, and it was burned} [Al-Baqarah: 266] So he asked The people narrated it, and he said: “What do you think? Was revealed: ‘Would any of you like to have a garden?’ [Al-Baqarah: 266]?” So they said: God and His Messenger know best, so he became angry. Omar and he said: “Say: We know or we do not know.” Then Ibn Abbas said: I have something of that in me, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: “O my brother’s son, say, ‘No. You despise yourself.” Ibn Abbas said: It was given as an example of a deed, and Omar said: “For a rich man who did good deeds, then God sent Satan to him.” He committed sins until he drowned all his deeds, and he had a garden and it was burned when he needed it most, when the children multiplied and he reached puberty. Pride. He said: “Does any of you want to repay on the Day of Resurrection a servant whose work has become so poor that nothing will be repaid for him?” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it.”"
"6308","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Hani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Sulayman told us Ibn Harb, Hammad Ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa’ib, he said: Muharib Ibn Dathar said to me: Did you hear Sa’id Ibn Jubayr mentioning on the authority of Ibn Abbas said something about Al-Kawthar. I said: Yes, it is a lot of good. He said: Glory be to God. Say what is wrong with Ibn Abbas. I said: He said: I heard Ibn Abbas. He says: I heard Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, saying: When you revealed, “Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar,” the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is a river in Paradise, its borders are of gold, flowing with pearls and rubies, its drink is whiter than milk, and sweeter than honey.” So he said: “By God, it is true.” This is Ibn Abbas, and God is abundant in goodness. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"6309","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subai’i told me in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told me, he said: I heard Abu Nu’aym say: “Abdullah died Ibn Abbas in the year sixty-eight.”"
"6310","Muhammad ibn Yaqoub al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed us, my father informed us, Ash'ath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, that he said the takbir for Ibn Abbas four times, and said: “The rabbis of this nation have perished.”"
"6311","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Sunayd bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Ajlah bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr said: “I witnessed the funeral of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in Taif, and I saw a white bird that came until it entered under the garment. And he has not moved yet.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6311 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6312","Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Fadl bin Ishaq Al-Dawri told us, Marwan bin Shuja’ told us, on the authority of Salim bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, said: “Ibn Abbas died in Taif, so I witnessed his funeral, then a bird that had not been seen before his appearance came and entered his coffin.” So we looked and pondered whether he would come out, but it was not seen that he came out of his coffin. When he was buried, this verse was recited at the edge of the grave, and it is not known who recited it. {O reassured soul, return to your Lord, satisfied and well-pleased, so enter among My servants and enter My Paradise} [Al-Fajr: 28] “He said: And Ishmael mentioned Ibn Ali, and Issa Ibn Ali, that it is a white bird.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6312 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6313","Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Yazid, the reciter, the imam in Mecca, protected by God Almighty, told me. Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Sayegh told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Hushaim told us, Abu Hamza told us, Imran bin Ata told us, he said: “I witnessed the death of Ibn Abbas in Taif, and his guardian was Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, and he said four takbirs over him, and brought him into the grave by his feet, and laid stones over him. Three, from which we have memorized about four hundred hadiths.”"
"6314","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, he said: Ibn Waqid told us, Omar told us Ibn Uqba said: I heard Shu`bah, the client of Ibn Abbas, saying: “Ibn Abbas died in the year sixty-eight in Taif, and he was the son of Khams.” He was seventy years old, and he was dyeing his beard yellow.
 Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir said: Ibn Waqid said: Khaled bin Al-Haytham told us, saying: I heard Shu’bah, the client of Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas says: “I was born before the Hijra and we were among the people, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when I was thirteen years old.” He said: “And he died Ibn Abbas, in the year seventy-eight, and he is eighty-one years old.”"
"6315","Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Hashimi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abbad bin Bishr told us, Ali bin Badimah told us, on the authority of Mujahid He said: Yazid bin Utbah bin Abi Lahab mentioned the clouds that watered the grave of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “
 [Simple Sea]
 Three times, the sky of God poured out its mercy... with water, it passed over the grave of Ibn Abbas.
 He used to tell us this and we taught him... the knowledge of certainty, so who is aware and who is forgetful?
 Indeed, the sky narrates his mercy to the grave... This, for my life, is a matter in the hands of people.
 If the people had an opinion that they could adhere to... when they proposed, they would accuse you of Ibn Abbas.
 God has His knowledge, and any man...is there like him when delivering speeches to people?
 But they accused you of an old man from Yemen... It is not known what multiplied fifths to sixths.”"
"6316","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar told me, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dhabi told me, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, and Abdullah bin Al-Fadl bin Abbas bin Abi Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith, that Hassan bin Thabit He said: “We, the Ansar, sought to go to Omar or to Othman - Ibn Abi Al-Zannad doubted - so we went with Abdullah bin Abbas and a group of people with him. The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Ibn Abbas spoke and they spoke, and they mentioned the Ansar and their virtues, so the governor ascended.” Hassan said: “And it was a severe matter that we asked for. He said: He continued to go back to them until they rose up and excused him, except for Abdullah bin Abbas, for he said: No, by God. To the Ansar from a home. They supported and provided shelter, and he mentioned their bounty and said: This is the poet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Compassionate One. On his behalf, Abdullah continued to approach him with comprehensive words, fulfilling every need he had, and he found no choice but to fulfill our needs. He said: So we went out and had God Almighty fulfilled our need with His words, so I took Abdullah’s hand, praising him and praying for him, so I passed through the mosque the group of people who were With him, but they did not reach what he reached, so I said to Abdullah: He was the closest of you to us. They said: Yes, so I said to Abdullah: By God, it is. The youth of prophecy and his heir, Ahmad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was the most deserving of it.” Hassan said: “And I am referring to Abdullah.”
 [Long Sea]"
"6317","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah bin Ishaq Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm Al-Asbahani told us, we told him Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told me, Abdul-Hakam bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, He said: “I saw Ibn Abbas wearing a scarf made of woven fabric with scalloped edges and taking it for a thousand.”
 Ibn Umar said: Abdullah bin Ja’far narrated to me, Umm Bakr bint Al-Miswar bin Makhramah narrated to me, that Miswar bin Makhramah ascended to Then Ibn Abbas came to him in the middle of the day to visit him, and Al-Miswar said to him: O Abu Abbas, this is an hour other than this. He said: He said: “If he would like “The hours that are required for me to fulfill what is due to you are the most difficult for me.”
 Ibn Omar said: Ishaq bin Yahya told me, Abu Salamah Al-Hadrami told us, he said: “I saw the grave of Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Hanafiyyah standing over it. So he ordered him to be flattened.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6317 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6318","The Muslim judge Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Saleh bin Ali told me, Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Jariri told us, Abu Jafar Ahmad bin Al-Harith Al-Harrani told us, Ali bin Muhammad Al-Madini told us, Suhaim bin Hafs told us, he said: Abu Bakra said: “Abdullah came to us Ibn Abbas, Basra, and there is no Arab like him in body, knowledge, clothing, beauty, and perfection.” Ali Ibn Muhammad said: “Abdullah Ibn Abbas was born Ali, who is the master of his children, was born in the year forty, and it is said that he was born in the year of Al-Jamal in the year thirty-six, and he was the most beautiful and handsome of the Quraysh on earth. He prayed the most, and he was called Al-Sajjad, and after him came the Caliphate, and Abbas, who was his eldest son, and by him he was nicknamed, Muhammad, and the servants of God. Al-Fadl, and Lubabah, their mother was Zar’ah bint Musharih bin Maadi Karib bin Wali’ah, and Musharih was one of the four kings, and there are no survivors of Al-Abbas. Ubayd Allah, Al-Fadl, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abbas, and as for Lubabah bint Abdullah, she was under Ali bin Abdullah. bin Jafar bin Abi Talib, and she bore him and her son Aaqab, and Asma bint Abdullah was with Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Abbas, she bore him Hassan and Hussein, and her mother was the mother of a son.”"
"6319","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Ishaq bin Wahb Al-Wasiti told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A'mash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', who said: When Ibn Abbas's sight failed, a man came to him and said to him: If you were patient for me for seven days, you would not have prayed without Lying down, you nod. I have treated you and you will be healed, God willing. “So he sent for Aisha, Abu Hurairah, and other of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And everyone greeted, saying: Have you seen if I die on this seven days, what will you do with prayer? “Then he left his eye and did not treat it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6319 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6320","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Awf bin Malik was nicknamed Abu Abd. The Most Gracious, and it is said: Abu Amr is one of the residents of the Levant."
"6321","Then Muhammad bin Muzaffar al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim bin Khuzaym told us, Abu Zur’ah told us, he said: “Awf bin Malik al-Ashja’i was nicknamed Abu Muhammad. His house was in Homs.”"
"6322","Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad al-Yazidi told us, Abu Hassan al-Zayyadi told us, Hisham bin Muhammad bin Al-Sa'ib Al-Kalbi, who said: Auf bin Malik Al-Ashja'i was directed to by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the charity was bestowed upon him, Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq May God be pleased with him. He said: Abu Bakr said to Awf: God Almighty has revealed charity. He said: What is charity? He said: For every forty camels, there is a female she-camel. He said: So we objected, so take a she-camel. So Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, objected to her, so he took a she-camel. For his departure, and Awf said: It is for my departure, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said to him: It is greater for your reward. He said: He disobeyed her. So Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, took her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he informed him of Awf’s deed and what he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Go back to him and tell him that God has built a house for him in Paradise.”"
"6323","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i witnessed Khaybar. With the Muslims, and he had with him the banner of Ashja’ on the day of the conquest of Mecca, then Awf moved to the Levant during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. He went down to Homs and stayed until the beginning of the caliphate of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, then he died in the year seventy-three, and he was nicknamed Abu Amr.”"
"6324","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih informed us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Abi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr, Ishaq bin Rashid told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, may God be pleased with him, said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, during the Battle of Tabuk at the end of dawn while he was in his camp. So I greeted him and said: Come in, O Messenger of God? He said: “Come in.” I said: “Eat,” and he said: “Eat.” Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Six before the Hour: the first of which is the death of your Prophet. Say: “One.” I said: One. “And the second is the conquest of the Holy House. Say: Two.” I said: Two. Then he said: “And the third is two deaths that will seize you.” Like the shearing of sheep. Say: Three. I said: Three. He said: And the fourth. Money will overflow among you to the point that a man is given a hundred dinars and continues to begrudge it. Say: “Four” “I said: four” “And the fifth is a trial that will be among you. Rarely will there remain among you a house of righteousness or any place without entering it. Say: five” “I said: five.” “And the sixth is a truce that will be between you and the Banu Asfar, and they will gather for you as much as a woman’s burden, then they will betray you and come back in eighty days.” A banner, each banner twelve thousand.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6324 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6325","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us in Nishapur, Yahya bin Uthman told us, Salih al-Sahmi told us, Nu`aym bin Hammad told us, Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Jarir bin Uthman, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “My nation will split into seventy-four sects, the greatest of which is a trial against my nation, a people who measure matters according to their opinion. They make lawful the forbidden and make unlawful the lawful.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6325 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6326","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me. He said: “The first child born after the migration was Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam bin Khuwailid bin Asad bin Abdul-Uzza, and his mother Asmaa bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, and her mother is Qayla bint Abd Al-Uzza bin Abd Asad bin Nasr bin Malik bin Hasal Bin Amer bin Luay, and Abdullah, nicknamed Abu Bakr.”"
"6327","Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Saydalani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Saeed bin Suleiman told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, On the authority of Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, named Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Abdullah.”"
"6328","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us in Nishapur, Yahya bin Ayyub al-Alaf told us in Egypt, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yaqoub bin Abi Abbad Al-Makki, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “It was The date is from the year in which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, and in which Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr was born.”"
"6329","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Subaie told us about Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Jubairi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Muhammad bin A partner, Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, who said: “I was named after my grandfather, Abu Bakr, and I was given his nickname.” And he was Abdullah has two nicknames: Abu Bakr and Abu Khubayb.”"
"6330","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Abdullah told me Ibn Muhammad Ibn Yahya Ibn Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, Hisham Ibn Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, who said: The names of the daughter of Abu Bakr Radi came out. May God bless them both when she migrated to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while she was pregnant with Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, and she gave birth to him, so she brought him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it and put it in his lap and brought a date, which he sucked and then chewed. Then he put it in his mouth and rubbed it on his palate.” The first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Then the Messenger of God wiped it. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he named him Abdullah. Then he came after he was seven years old or eight years old to pledge allegiance to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Al-Zubair ordered him to do so, “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smiled when he saw him coming and pledged allegiance to him,” and he was the first to be born into Islam in Medina. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and the Jews were saying: We have captured them, so no male child will be born to them in Medina, so the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Abdullah was born, and Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab said when he heard the people of Syria saying “Allahu Akbar” when they had killed Abdullah Allah ibn al-Zubayr: Those who are arrogant for his birth are better than those who are arrogant for killing him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6330 - Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Urwa, left by Abu Hatim"
"6331","Ali bin Issa told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Maymun Al-Makki, and Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, said: Ibn al-Zubayr was mentioned by Ibn Abbas, and he said: “He was chaste in Islam, obedient to God, his father.” Al-Zubayr, his mother Asma, his grandfather Abu Bakr, his aunt Khadija, his grandmother Safiyya, and his aunt Aisha, and by God I will hold myself accountable to him. I did not hold accountable Abu Bakr or Omar for anything, but he deliberately took the praiseworthy ones, the handsome ones, and the little ones,” Abu Ali said. Al-Qabbani: “By Al-Humaidat, he means Humayd bin Zuhayr bin Al-Harith bin Asad bin Abdul-Uzza, and Tuwait bin Habib bin Asad, and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam bin Khuwailid bin Asad bin Abdul-Uzza»
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6331 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6332","Sheikh Abu Bakr told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, my father told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, said: “Ibn al-Zubayr erased himself from the Diwan when Uthman, may God be pleased with them both, was killed.”"
"6333","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told me, he told me My father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, he told me about the mail that Ibn Al-Zubayr brought Al-Mukhtar’s head, and when he saw it Ibn al-Zubayr said: Ka’b never told me a hadith without finding it to be true, except that he told me, “A man from Thaqif will kill me.” He said Al-Amash: “And he does not know that Abu Muhammad - may God forsake him - has hidden something for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6333 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6334","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Abi Al-Harith told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr “used to continue for seven days, and then the third day would come, which was Alithana.” What he means is: as if he were a lion"
"6335","Abu Al-Hussein told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Omar bin Qays, who said: “It was for Ibn Al-Zubayr had one hundred boys, and each of them spoke another language. Ibn Al-Zubayr used to speak to each one of them in his own language, and when you looked When you look at him in a matter of this world, you say: This is a man whom God did not want even the blink of an eye. And when you look at him in a matter in the hereafter, you say: This is a man who did not want “The world is in the blink of an eye.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6335 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6336","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told me, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Nafi’ bin Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz said to me: Indeed, in your heart is Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: I said: “I have never seen a person praying like him, nor one praying like him, nor I fear the essence of God like him, and no soul is more generous than him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6336 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6337","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, my father told me, Saeed bin Abi Ishaq Al-Subaie told us, Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Yazid bin Muawiyah wrote to Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr: I have sent to you a series of Silver, chains of gold, and a bundle of silver, and you swore to come to me about that. He said: Then he threw the letter down and said: «
 [Simple Sea]
 And I will not be soft for anything other than the truth...until the stone is soft for the tooth of the chewer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6337 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6338","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-Sana’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari told us, al-Qasim ibn Ma’n told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: When Muawiyah died May God be pleased with him. Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr was reluctant to obey Yazid bin Muawiyah, and he began to insult him. This reached Yazid, so he sent to He will be brought, and it was said to Ibn al-Zubayr: Make shackles of gold for you, so you can drape the garment over them, and you will fulfill his oath, and reconciliation is better. So he said: “No.” May God fulfill his oath,” then he said: “
 [Simple Sea]

 And I will not be soft for anything other than the truth...until the stone is soft for the tooth of the chewer.”
 Then he said: “By God, a blow with a sword in honor is more beloved to me than a blow with a whip in humiliation.” Then he called for himself and revealed the disagreement. To Yazid bin Muawiyah, Yazid bin Muawiyah directed to him Muslim bin Uqba al-Muzani in the army of the people of the Levant, and ordered him to fight the people of Medina. When he finished that, he walked to Mecca, he said: Then Muslim bin Uqba entered Medina, and the remnants of the Companions of the Messenger of God fled from him on that day. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he played around in it and went to extremes in killing, then he left it, and when he was on some way to Mecca he died and succeeded Husayn ibn Numayr Al-Kindi and said to him: O fool of a donkey, beware of the deceitfulness of the Quraysh, and do not deal with them except with hypocrisy. Then, Husayn continued until he came. Mecca, and Ibn al-Zubayr fought there for several days."
"6339","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Maslamah told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: I heard my father saying: Ibn Al-Zubayr sent to Al-Husayn Ibn Numayr inviting him to the stool, and he said Al-Hussein: No cowardice prevents me from meeting you, and I do not know whose victory the victory is for. If it was yours, you would have been lost behind me, and if it were mine, you would have been lost. I made a mistake in planning, and if you go back to the rest of the hadith, Ibn al-Zubayr set up a tent in the mosque, and there were women in it watering the wounded. He treats them, feeds the hungry, and caresses the wounded lion. Husayn said: A lion continues to emerge from that tent as if it were a lion. He comes out of his den, who will protect him? Then a man from the Levant said: “I am.” When the night fell upon him, he put a candle on the tip of his spear, then he struck his horse, then he stabbed Al-Fustat and it became inflamed. Fire, and the Kaaba at that time was surrounded by awnings, and on top of it was a jar, so the wind blew flames over the Kaaba until it was burned and burned. On that day, we tied the ram for which Isaac was ransomed. Muhammad ibn Umar said: Yazid ibn Muawiyah died, and Husayn ibn Numayr fled.When Yazid bin Muawiyah died, he called Marwan bin Al-Hakam to himself, and the people of Homs, and the people of Jordan and Palestine, responded to him. He directed Ibn al-Zubayr al-Dahhak ibn Qays al-Fihri came to him with a hundred thousand, so they met at Marj Rahit and Marwan that day with five thousand from the Umayyads. And their masters and followers were from the people of the Levant. Marwan said to a master of his who was unwilling: Carry on whichever side you wish. So he said: How can we bear? These are so many? He said: They are between the coerced and the enslaved. Carry upon them that you have no mother, and a good, effective appeal will suffice for you, and they will suffice you with themselves. These were slaves of dinars and dirhams, so he attacked them and defeated them, and Al-Dahhak bin Qais arrived and the army dispersed. About this, Zufar bin Al-Harith says:
 [Long Sea]

 For my life, Rahit’s affair has remained... by Marwan Sarwa’ and the incidents of captivity
 I have spent my arms, I do not give a damn about you. I... in the war, the only thing getting worse is that we continue.
 The pasture may grow on the soil... and leave the depths of souls as they are.
 In it he also says:

 Am I right? As for Bahdal and Ibn Bahdal... he will live, and as for Ibn al-Zubayr, he will be killed.
 You lied and the House of God will not kill him...And when there was a more glorious day
 And when honor is among you...a ray like the light of the sun when it sets off...He said: Then Marwan died, so he called Abd al-Malik to himself and got up, and the people of the Levant responded to him, so he delivered a sermon from the pulpit and said: From Ibn Al-Zubair? Al-Hajjaj said: I am, O Commander of the Faithful, so he silenced him, then he silenced him again, then he silenced him again, then he silenced him again and said: I am his, O Prince. Believers, for I saw in my sleep as if I had snatched up a garden and clothed it. So he set off with his head in the army to Mecca, protected by God Almighty, until He returned it to Ibn al-Zubayr, so he fought him with it. Ibn al-Zubayr said to the people of Mecca: “Take care of these two mountains, for you will not be fine.” They were honorable as long as they did not appear over them.” He said: “It was not long before Al-Hajjaj and those with him appeared in the mosque, and when it was the morning in which he was killed Ibn Al-Zubayr Ibn Al-Zubayr married his mother, Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with her. She was a hundred years old at that time, and no miscarriage occurred. She was old, but her sight and hearing did not deteriorate, so she said to her son: O Abdullah, what did you do in your war? He said: “They reached such-and-such a place.” He said: Ibn al-Zubayr laughed and said: “Indeed, there is a relief in death.” She said: O my son, perhaps you wished for me something. I would love to die until I come to one of your sides. Either you are victorious and my eyes will be pleased with that, or you are killed and I seek refuge in you.He said: Then he bade her farewell, and she said to him: My son, be careful not to give up any aspect of your religion for fear of being killed. He left her and entered the mosque. He placed two bolts on the Black Stone, hoping that it would be hit by the catapult, and Ibn al-Zubayr came and was sitting next to Zamzam, and said to him: Shall we open the Kaaba for you, so you can climb into it? Abdullah looked at him and then said to him: “You protect your brother from everything except from himself - meaning for his sake - and is the Kaaba sacred that is not For this place, by God, if they had found you hanging from the curtains of the Kaaba, they would have killed you.” He was told: “Will you not speak to them about peace?” He said: “And when this was settled?” By God, if they had found you in its belly, they would have slaughtered you all.” Then he proceeded to say: “

 I do not buy life for a sale... nor do I ascend with a ladder out of fear of death.
 I contend that he is not displaced and melaka... al-manaya, that is, he is suffixed with tayammum.”
 Then he went to the family of Al-Zubayr and preached to them: “Let none of you have his sword as his face is, and do not lower his sword and defend himself with his hand as if he were “Woman, by God, I have never met a person crawling except in the first race, and I have never suffered any wound except the pain of the medicine.” He said: While they were like that, when He entered upon them, with seventy people with him. The first one he met was the black one, and he struck him with his sword until his foot was broken.Then the lions said to him: Ah, son of an adulteress. Then Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: “Be good, O son of Ham, to the names of an adulteress.” Then he took them out of the city. Then he left the mosque and saw a people who had entered through the gate of Banu Sahm. He said: “Who are these people?” It was said: The people of Jordan, so he blamed them and said: «
 [The sea of rage]

 “I have never known a raid like a torrent... the dust of which does not settle until nightfall.”
 He said: So he took them out of the mosque, then returned, and saw a people who had entered through the gate of Banu Makhzum, so he attacked them while saying: «
 If my horn had been one, I would have been sufficient for him to drive him to death and kill him.” He said: And on the back of the mosque, among its assistants, was someone who was throwing bricks at his enemy. And others, so he attacked them, and a brick struck him in his joints until his head was shaved, and he stood up and said: “

 “It is not on our heels that our shoulders bleed... but on our feet the blood drips.”
 He said: Then he fell and two of his guardians fell on him, and they said: The servant protects his Lord and he will be protected. He said: Then he walked to him and bowed his head, satisfied. God bless him"
"6340","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Ziyad Al-Khasas told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abdullah bin Omar said to me: Look at the place where Ibn al-Zubayr is. He said: So he passed by him. He said: The boy did not do so. He said: Then Ibn Umar looked at Ibn al-Zubayr crucified, and he said: May God forgive you three times, and by God I did not know that you were fasting and steadfast. Reaching the womb, but by God, I do not hope, with the misfortune you have befallen, that God will never punish you after that. Then he turned to me and said: I heard Aba Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever does evil will be rewarded for it in this world.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6340 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6341","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Sa’id bin Muslim Al-Yashkari told us, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi He says: “Abdul-Malik ibn Marwan sent the head of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr to Ibn Hazim in Khorasan, who shrouded him and prayed over him.” He said: He said: Al-Shaabi: “He made a mistake, he should not pray on the head.”
 He said: Hisham told us, Musa told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, “When Ibn al-Zubayr was killed, his treasuries were transferred to Abd King bin Marwan for three years.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6341 - Sa’id bin Muslim Al-Yashkari. Wah"
"6342","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, may God be pleased with him, told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Aswad told us Ibn Shayban, Abu Nawfal Ibn Abi Aqrab Al-Uraiji reported, saying: Al-Hajjaj Ibn Yusuf Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them, was crucified on Aqabat Al-Madina so that the Quraysh could show this, so they either acknowledged it and began to pass by it and not stop by it, until Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab passed by, may God be pleased with him. God bless them both, and he stood over him and said: Peace be upon you, Abu Khubayb. He said it three times. I have forbidden you from that. He said it three times. You have been fasting. Tightening the ties of kinship, he said: Al-Hajjaj reached the position of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, so he took him down and threw him in the graves of the Jews. He sent to Asma bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them both, to come to him since her sight had gone, but she refused, so he sent to her: “You will come.” Or I will send to you someone who will pull you by your horns. She said: By God, I will not come to you until you send me someone who will pull me by your horns. So his messenger came. So he told him, and he said: O boy, give me my kinsman. So he handed him his mule, and he stood up and was burning until he came to her, and said to her: How did you see what God had done? By the enemy of God? She said: I saw that you spoiled his worldly life for him and spoiled your hereafter, and as for what you were taunting him in the same two senses, yes, it was mine. Two ranges, one range with which I cover the food of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from ants, and my other range is a must for women, and I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, in Thaqif there is a liar and a blasphemer.” As for the liar, we have seen him, and as for the blasphemer, you are that one. He said: So he came out. “The narrations are authentic, with Abdullah bin Al-Zubair hearing from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his entering upon him and leaving him when he was the son of Eight years, and I remember, by the will of God Almighty, in this place his reports that indicate that, for the narration is in its Musnad on the authority of the Messenger May God bless him and grant him peace, more than seventy hadiths.”"
"6343","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Al-Hind bin Al-Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma`iz said: I heard Aamir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating that his father narrated to him that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was cupping, when he finished he said: “O Abdullah, take this blood and spill it where no one can see you.” When I separated from the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I went to the blood and licked it. When I returned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “What have you done, O Abdullah?” He said: I put it in a place where I thought people would be afraid. He said: “Perhaps you drank it?” I said: Yes. He said: “Who told you to drink blood?” “Woe to you from the people, and woe to the people because of you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6343 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6344","Sheikh Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Faryabi told us, Muhammad bin Bahr al-Hujaimi told us, Sa`id bin Salem al-Qaddah told us, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever recites the Qur’an outwardly or visually will be given a tree in Paradise, even if a crow hatched under a leaf from it and then that fledgling flew and overtook it.” The old man before he cut that leaf.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6344 - Muhammad bin Bahr Al-Hujaimi is a denier of hadith"
"6345","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri told me, Abdullah ibn Nafi’ al-Zubayr, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Twice a day.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. I mentioned at the beginning of the translation that I sold it to him when he was eight years old. The Messenger of God laughed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his astonishment at him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6345 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"6346","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Waqidi told me, on the authority of Omar Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that he was told: Which of the two sons of Al-Zubayr was the bravest? He said: “None of them is anything but brave. Both of them walked towards death while seeing it.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abu Al-Qasim bin Ali Al-Qurashi told me, he said: Al-Muhallab was asked about the brave, and he said: “Ibn Al-Kalbiyyah, meaning Musab bin Al-Zubayr, one of the Banu Tamim, meaning Omar bin Ubaid Allah bin Muammar, and Abbad bin Husayn Al-Habti. He was asked: Where are you from Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr and Abdullah bin Hazim? He said: “We were only in remembrance of mankind, and we were not in remembrance of the jinn.” Ibn Umar said: “And Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him, was killed on the day On Tuesday, the seventeenth of Jumada al-Awwal, in the year seventy-three, he attacked the people of the Levant and threw a brick at him, which hit him in the face. He shivered and bled and fell, so Al-Hajjaj was informed, so he prostrated, then came until he and Tariq bin Amr stood on him, and Tariq said: Women have not given birth. “I mention who this is.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6346 - Its chain of transmission is abandoned"
"6347","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I and Omar ibn Abi Salamah were on the day of the ditch on a hill, and he was treading on me. So I looked at the fighting and bowed down to him, and he looked at the fighting. I saw my father walking around in the swamp, attacking these people once, and repeating themselves against This one time, when he came back I said: Father, I have seen you. He said: Which son, have you seen me? I said: Yes. He said: “Today the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6347 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6348","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed me, Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told me, Yahya ibn Ayyub told me, on the authority of Amara ibn Ghaziyah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, said: When Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr was killed, I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubair saying: “Whoever denies the affliction I do not deny him. It was mentioned to me that Yahya bin Zakariya was killed in connection with an adulteress who was a slave girl. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Some Basrans narrated it, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, with a chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6348 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6349","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, my father told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, said: Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr said to Abdullah Ibn Jafar: “I remember the day we received the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “He greeted me and you, so he carried me and left you.” This is a hadith by Hisham bin Urwa, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6349 - But Ismail is weak"
"6350","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadi told me, Ibrahim ibn Hamza told me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad told me Bin Yahya bin Urwa, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “I wished to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me the call. It was said: Why that? He said: “They will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. I mentioned the killing of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him, because of the audacity of Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf against God Almighty and against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his negligence towards the Two Holy Mosques and the people of The house of Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, is what the wise person is satisfied with in terms of his knowledge, so listen now to the sayings of the Companions, may God be pleased with them, and those who followed it. And their testimony to his bad faith after he killed Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Saeed bin Jubayr”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6350 - Incorrect"
"6351","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Yunus Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl said: “Dhar al-Muhribi and I disagreed regarding Al-Hajjaj. He said: A believer, and I said: An infidel.” Its authenticity is indicated by what Mujahid bin Jabr, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6352","While Abu Sahl Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us in Baghdad, Abu Omar Ahmed bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us: I heard Al-A’mash saying: “By God, I heard Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf saying: What a strange servant Hudhayl! He claims that he is reciting a Qur’an from God, and by God it is nothing but an abomination of the Bedouins. By God, if I had caught the servant of Hudhayl I would have beheaded him. “This is after he killed Abdullah bin Omar, and Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr was regretting what he had missed by killing Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, was one of the worshipers, and he cursed those who hated them and abandoned them.”"
"6353","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Anas and Sa’id Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: “Ibn Umar witnessed Badr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6353 - This is definitely wrong"
"6354","Abu Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Abu Zayd Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Tarif told us, Ja`far told us Bin Muhammad, and Hadba bin Abdul Wahhab, they said: Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Saad al-Baqal, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wael, On the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left us on the day he died, and not one of us was changed from who he was.” “On him, except for Omar and Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6354 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6355","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab bin Nufayl Al-Adawi, nicknamed Abu Abdul-Rahman, and his mother was Zainab bint Maz’un bin Habib bin Wahb bin Hudhafa bin Jumah, who used to dye his dyes with yellow, died in Mecca and was buried in Dhu Tuwa. It is said that he was buried with a trap in the cemetery of immigrants. He was buried in the year Seventy-four, the day he died, when he was eighty-four years old.”"
"6356","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Fudayl bin Marzuq told us, on the authority of Atiya He said: I said to a servant of Ibn Omar: How was the death of Ibn Omar? He said: He denounced Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf for his actions in killing bin Al-Zubayr, and he stood up to him and heard him. Al-Hajjaj said: Be quiet, old man. She became senile, and when they dispersed, Al-Hajjaj ordered a man from the Levant to hit him in the leg with his spear. Then Al-Hajjaj came in to visit him, and he said: If only I know the one who injured you. I struck his neck, and he said: “You are the one who injured me.” He said: How? He said: “The day you entered the sanctuary of God, weapons.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6356 - Attiya is weak"
"6357","Sheikh Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Al-Qadi Abu Khalifa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Suwayd Al-Dhara’ told us, Amara bin Zazan told us, he told me Makhoul, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when Al-Hajjaj set up a catapult on the Kaaba and killed Ibn al-Zubayr. Abdullah bin Umar denied that. He said something that made him uncomfortable, so Al-Hajjaj ordered him to be killed, and a man from the Levant struck him severely. When Al-Hajjaj reached his destination, he said: Ibn Umar told him: “You killed me, and now you come back to me. God is sufficient as a judge between me and you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6357 - A weak building"
"6358","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Omar came to Basra and to... Persia, a conqueror who entered it and died in Mecca in the year seventy-four.”"
"6359","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, he informed me Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, said: “My father instructed me to bury him outside the Sanctuary, but we could not, so we buried him in the Sanctuary with a trap in a grave. immigrants
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6359 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6360","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim, the Hafiz in Kufa, told me, Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told me, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told us, Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Makhrami told us, Abu Al-Malih told me, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar say: “I withheld my hand.” I did not go forward, and the one who fights for what is right is better.” Al-Hakim - may God Almighty have mercy on him - said: “The explanation of this hadith and its explanation in what Abu narrated to us. He said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar say: “I do not regret anything except that I did not fight with Ali, may God be pleased with him, the transgressing group.”"
"6361","The chief judge, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Saleh bin Ali, told me. Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Jariri Al-Bajli, my father’s companion, told us. Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Yahya, and Muhammad bin Yazid, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Al-Harith Al-Khazzaz, the client of the Commander of the Faithful Al-Mansur, joined us. The companion of Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Arabi, Ali bin Muhammad Al-Madaini told us, Ghassan bin Abdul Hamid told me, he said: It was not People complain that Ibn Umar “pledged his allegiance to Ali on the condition that he would not fight with him, and Ali was satisfied with that.”
 Abu Al-Hasan Al-Madani said: Al-Aswad bin Shayban told me, on the authority of Khaled bin Shamir, he said: I heard Musa bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah He says: “May God have mercy on Abu Abdul Rahman Abdullah bin Omar. I think he is in compliance with the covenant that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made with him.” He did not change, and by God, the Quraysh did not deceive him during their first attack, so I said: This is disgraceful to his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6361 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6362","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Jawab Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’, who said: “I and Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, presented On the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr, so we looked down and witnessed Uhud. Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “I presented it on the first day of Translation: The hadith of Yazid bin Harun, with its chain of transmission on the authority of Anas, that Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, witnessed Badr, and this chain of transmission is stronger. From him, the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, that it was shown to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was fourteen years old, but he did not allow it. It was shown to him in the ditch and he passed it, and it was the first sight. He witnessed it, and God knows best.”"
"6363","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Ibrahim Al-Asadi, Al-Hafiz Hamdan, told me. Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told me. Atiq told me. Ibn Yaqoub said: I heard Malik Ibn Anas, may God Almighty have mercy on him, saying: Ibn Shihab said to me: “Do not abandon the opinion of Ibn Umar, for he He remained after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for sixty years, and nothing of the matter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hidden from him. His companions"
"6364","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Hajjaj bin Nusayr told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman says: “Ibn Omar in his time was better than Omar in his time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6364 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6365","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Yazid bin Harun, and Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, they said: Abdullah told us Ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I have not seen anything more binding on the first matter than Abdullah Ibn Omar"
"6366","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Uthman Saeed bin Al-Hajwani told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Abu Hilal Muhammad bin Suleiman, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: “If I had testified against anyone that he is from the people of Paradise, I would have testified against Ibn Umar.”"
"6367","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Fadl told us, my father told me, On the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When Omar allotted three thousand for Usama bin Zayd, and he allotted for me Two thousand and five hundred, so I said to him: O father, why did you allocate three thousand for Osama bin Zaid, and two thousand and five hundred for me? By God, Osama did not witness a scene from which I was absent, nor did his father witness a scene from which my father was absent. He said: “You are right, my son, but I bear witness.” Because his father was the most beloved of people to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than your father, and he is more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than you.” Sahih chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it. If someone is under the illusion that this virtue is for Usama, let him know that I only narrated this hadith. For two reasons: One of them is Omar’s testimony to his son that Osama did not witness a scene without witnessing it, and this is for the virtues of Ibn Omar. The second is that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, have narrated most of what has been narrated of the virtues of Ibn Omar, based on their condition, from the chain of narrations. I am endeavoring to narrate Collecting a true chain of narration that they did not narrate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6367 - True"
"6368","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmed Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled told us, Khaled told us Ibn Mukhlid Al-Qatwani, Ubayd Allah Ibn Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “I pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah he died twice.” He said: “Umar saw the people gathered and said: Go and see what is their situation.” Then, behold, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He pledged allegiance to death, so I pledged allegiance to him.” Then I returned to Omar and informed him, and he came and I pledged allegiance to him after he had pledged allegiance. “This is for the sake of the virtues of Ibn Omar, and he did not narrate it, and Ubayd Allah bin Omar Al-Amri, may God have mercy on him, was not mentioned except with poor memory only.”"
"6369","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Saeed bin Amr Al-Ash’athi told us, Abtar told us, Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “None of us has reached the world without having She leaned towards it, and only Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them, leaned towards it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6369 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6370","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani narrated to us, Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, and Abu Al-Nadr narrated to us. Ismail bin Abdullah Al-Ajli said: Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunnis told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad said, Nafi’ told me, He said: Ibn Umar entered the Kaaba, and I heard him saying while he was prostrating: “You may know what prevents me from competing with the Quraysh in this world except... Your fear
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6370 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6371","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Musa bin Harun told us, Omar bin Muhammad Al-Asadi told us, my father told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Hanafiyyah, who said: “Ibn Umar was the best of this nation.”
 Abu Imran said: Omar bin Muhammad told us, Abi told us, Muhammad bin Aban told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Omar, Abu Hurairah, Abu Sa`id, and others “were of the opinion that none of them was in the state in which Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a different state.” Ibn Omar"
"6372","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Abbas, the martyr, may God be pleased with him, told me. Abu Hatim bin Mahboub told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Alaa, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ali bin Al-Hussein say: “Indeed, Ibn Umar is the most ascetic of the people and the most correct. the people’s opinion”"
"6373","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Musa bin Ismail told me, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf Ibn Mahran, who said: We were with Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, and Jabir said: “If it pleases you to look at The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, who did not change or change anything. So look at Abdullah bin Omar, none of us changed anything.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6373 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6374","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Ghassan told us Malik bin Ismail, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: “None of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith in which he was careful not to add or take away from Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6374 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6375","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of Abu Amr bin Hamas, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “I recited this verse {You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love} [Al Imran: 92] Then I remembered what God Almighty had given me, and I did not find anything more beloved to me than my maid, Radhiyah, so I said: She. She is free in the presence of God Almighty, so if I do not go back on anything that I have committed for God Almighty, I will marry her.” So Nafi’ married her, and she is the mother of his son."
"6376","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Anas bin Musa told me, Abd al-Samad bin Hassan told us, Kharijah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’ He said: “If I saw Ibn Umar following in the footsteps of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would say: This is crazy.”"
"6377","Abd al-Samad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qaari informed me, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told me, Abu Ubaidah told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told me, he told me Abdul-Jabbar bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Abdullah bin Omar converted to Islam before his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6377 - This is invalid"
"6378","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar May God be pleased with them both, that a man asked him about a matter, and he said: “I have no knowledge of it.” When the man turned away, Ibn Umar said: “Yes, what Ibn Omar was asked about what he did not know and he said: I have no knowledge of it."
"6379","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: And Rafi’ bin Khadij told us Ibn Rafi’ Ibn Adi Ibn Zayd Ibn Jashm Ibn Haritha Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Al-Khazraj Ibn Amr, who is Al-Nabit Ibn Malik Ibn Aws, witnessed Rafi’ Uhud, the trench, and all the scenes were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Rafi’ was an arrow in his collarbone on the day of Uhud. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “If you wish, I can remove the arrow, leave the velvet, and bear witness for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr.” Then Rafi’ left it, rejecting the words of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he did not feel anything from it for a long time, and whenever he laughed, it seemed strange. During the caliphate of Uthman, he suffered that wound and died from it.
 Ibn Umar said: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hurayr told me, from the descendants of Rafi` ibn Khadij, on the authority of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi`, on the authority of Bashir ibn Yassar said: “Rafi’ ibn Khadij died on the first of the year seventy-four when he was eighty-six years old. Ibn Umar attended his funeral, and he was nicknamed Rafi’ Abu Abdullah, and he died in Medina.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6379 - This is not correct and its meaning is not correct"
"6380","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: “Rafi’ bin Khadij Al-Harithi, nicknamed Abu Abdullah in Medina in the year seventy-four.”"
"6381","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak said: I saw Ibn Umar “standing between the two pillars of the bed of Rafi’ ibn Khadij.”"
"6382","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi told us, Ya’qub bin Muhammad told us, Rifa’ah bin Hurair told us, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rewarded him on the day of Uhud and placed him among the archers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6382 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6383","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm bin Masqala told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Salama bin Al-Akwa' and Al-Akwa''s name is Sinan bin Abdullah bin Qusayr bin Khuzaymah bin Malik bin Salman bin Aslam bin Afsa It was reported that he said: “I fought seven battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and with Zaid bin Haritha nine battles, commanding him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace
 Ibn Umar said: “And I heard that Salamah was nicknamed Abu Iyas.”
 He said: Abdul Aziz bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Iyas bin Salama, who said: “Abu Salama bin Al-Akwa’ died in Medina in the year four He was seventy and eighty years old.”"
"6384","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Salamah bin Al-Akwa’ was nicknamed Abu Sinan died in Medina in the year seventy-four.”"
"6385","Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Shabab bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Malik bin Sinan bin Tha’labah bin Ubaid bin Al-Abjar, whose name is Khudra bin Awf, and he is Abu Saeed Abi Al-Khudri Saad bin Malik.”"
"6386",""
"6387","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri is Sa’d bin Malik bin Sinan bin Tha’labah bin Ubaid bin Al-Abjar, and his name is Khudra bin Awf bin Al-Khazraj. Qatada bin Al-Numan was his maternal brother, and Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four.”"
"6388","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Al-Dahhak bin Othman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz, and Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, He said: “I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the campaign against Banu al-Mustaliq.” Ibn Umar said: “And he was fifteen years old at that time.” Ibn Omar said: Abu Sa`id also witnessed the ditch and the scenes after that."
"6389","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Saeed bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Rabih bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, he said: I appeared on a Sunday upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and my father, who is thirteen years old, made my father take my hand and say: O Messenger of God, it is the marrow of bones, even if it is Calling the muezzin, he said: And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked up at me and directed it, then he said: “Return it,” so he brought me back."
"6390","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Masqala told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar, Abdul Aziz bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, who said: “Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four.”"
"6391","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, that he used to say: “Speak, for the conversation reminds the conversation.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6391 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6392","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Rijal told us, about Amara Ibn Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: My father said to me: “I have grown old, and my friends and group have gone, so take my hand.” He said: So he leaned on me until he came to the farthest part of Al-Baqi’, a place where he would not be buried, and he said: “O my son, if I die, bury me here, and do not Don't spread a blanket over me, and don't walk with me through fire, and don't weep and mourn for me, and don't call anyone to me, and take me in a deep street, and let your walk be done. He trots away. He died on Friday, and I hated giving people the call to prayer when he had forbidden me. They would come to me and say: When will you take him out? So I say: When I am done with his device, I will take it out. He said: Then people filled Al-Baqi’.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6392 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6393","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Salih informed me, Muhammad ibn Shazan told me, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told me, Ismail ibn Ulayya informed me, about Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, said: We said to Abu Saeed: You speak to us amazing hadiths, and we are afraid that we will add or subtract, if We wrote it down. He said: “You will not write it down, nor will you make it a Qur’an, but memorize it from us as we have memorized it.” Then he said again: “Take it from us as we have learned it.” We learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6394","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abd Al-Karim bin Al-Haytham Al-Dir’aqoli told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Tabbaa’, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ali Al-Hajbi told us, my mother, who is from the descendants of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, told me that she heard Umm Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri narrated, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: When it was the day of Uhud, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, became angry in His forehead, so Malik bin Sinan, who is the father of Abu Sa’id, came to him and wiped the blood from the face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he dismissed him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever is pleased to look at the one whose blood has mixed with his blood, let him look at Malik ibn Sinan.” Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqoub, Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to me, and they narrated it."
"6395","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, may God be pleased with them both, told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr and Uthman, the sons of Abi, told us Shaybah said: Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, who said: “It was said to Jabir bin Abdullah: O Abu ""Abdullah"""
"6396","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Zuhri al-Harbi told me, Mus’ab ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah Al-Zubayri said: “Jaber bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram bin Tha’labah bin Haram bin Ka’b bin Ghanam bin Ka’b bin Salama bin Saad bin Ali bin Asad bin Sardah bin Yazid bin Jashm bin Al-Khazraj, and his nickname was Abu Abdullah.”"
"6397","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subai’i told us in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told us, he said: I heard Abu Nu’aym say: “Jabir bin died. Abdullah in the year seventy-nine.”"
"6398","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Jabir witnessed Ibn Abdullah Al-Aqaba was among the seventy of the Ansar who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time. He was one of the youngest of them at that time. He wanted to witness Badr, so his father succeeded him in charge of his sisters, and there were nine of them. He also succeeded him when he went out to Uhud and witnessed the events that followed that. The scenes »"
"6399","So Abu Al-Abbas told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “I was expressing my heart to my companions on the Day of Badr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6399 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6400","So Mukhlid bin Ja’far told me, and Muhammad bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, he said: I said to Muhammad bin Omar: The people of Kufa narrated, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “I was testing my heart on the Day of Badr for my companions,” so Muhammad ibn Omar: “This is an error in the narration of the people of Iraq regarding Jabir and Abu Masoud Al-Ansari. They consider them to be someone who witnessed Badr, and Moses did not narrate that. Ibn Uqba, nor Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, nor Abu Ma’shar, nor anyone who narrated the biography.”"
"6401","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzaki and Ali ibn Muhammad al-Qabsi informed us, saying: Al-Hussein ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Waki`, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghaseel, on the authority of Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah came to us “with his head yellow.” And his beard"
"6402","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “I entered upon al-Hajjaj and did not greet him. ""on him"""
"6403","Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Hashimi and Ali bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Ghassan Abbad bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked forgiveness for me on the night of Aqaba. Twenty-five times: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6403 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6404","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ishaq bin Issa told us, Miskin bin Abdullah Al-Harrani told us. Trustworthy, he said: I heard Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, saying: Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, he said: “He invaded The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conducted twenty-one battles, and I witnessed nineteen battles with him, and it was the last battle that the Messenger of God conquered. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6404 - True"
"6405","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Hafs bin Masqala told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani had a different surname. The people of the city claimed that he was Abu Abd al-Rahman, and others said: He was nicknamed Abu Talha"
"6406","Usama bin Zaid bin Aslam told us, on the authority of his father, and Muhammad bin Al-Hijazi Al-Hajbi, who said: “Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani died in Medina. “In the year seventy-eight, he was eighty-five years old.”"
"6407","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, he said: “Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani was nicknamed Abu Abdul Rahman died in Medina in the year seventy-eight, and he was eighty-five years old.”"
"6408","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Asma’ bint Umays was born Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib in the land of Abyssinia, and he died in the year Eighty, which is the day he died when he was eighty years old.”"
"6409","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Dawraqi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Sawwaf told us, Yahya bin Rashid, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Burdah told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abi Burdah, on the authority of Abi Musa, on the authority of Asma bint Umays. May God be pleased with her. She said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “People have one migration and you have two migrations.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6409 - True"
"6410","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, al-Hakam ibn Nafi’ told us, Ismail bin Ayyash, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, “Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr and Abdullah bin Ja’far pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When they were seven years old, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and extended his hand and pledged allegiance to them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6410 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6411","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Jafar Ibn Khalid Ibn Sarah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Jafar, who said: If you had seen me, Ubayd Allah, and Qutham playing, when he passed by us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Raise this to me,” so he carried me in front of him, and he said to Qutham: “Raise this to me,” so he put it behind him, so he called For us, Ubayd Allah was more beloved to Abbas than Qutham, and he was not freed from his uncle. He said: I said: What did Qutham do? He said: He was martyred. He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best what is good. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6411 - True"
"6412","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shaybani told us, Makki bin Abdan told us, he said: I heard Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj saying: “Abu Jafar Abdullah bin Jafar bin Abi Talib heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was ten years old.”"
"6413","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shaybani told us, Makki bin Abdan told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us: Abu The plantation of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi, Muhammad bin Abi Usama al-Halabi told us, Ali bin Abi Hamla told us, he said: “The delegation of Abdullah bin Jafar came to Muawiyah and ordered him to pay him two thousand dirhams.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6413 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6414","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Ghallabi told us, Ibn Aisha told us, he said: Ziyad, the foreigner, entered upon Abdullah. Ibn Ja`far in five blood money, so he gave him and he started saying: «
 [abundant sea]
 We asked him a lot, but he did not have anything... and he gave more than we asked for and more.
 And he did better, then he did better, then we went back... Then he did better, then I went back to him, and they went back.
 “Many times, I do not return to time without... He smiled and laughed and folded the pillow.”
 Al-Bukhari and Muslim, may God be pleased with them, agreed to hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God grant him peace when he was ten years old, and I remember the will of God Almighty in this matter explaining what they agreed upon. ""With their support"""
"6415","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abu Bakr bin Abi Khaythamah told us, Musab bin Abdullah bin Musab told us. Ibn Thabit Ibn Al-Zubayr, my father told us, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Abdullah Ibn Jafar, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “On him and grant him peace, two garments dyed with saffron, a robe, and a turban.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6415 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6416","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani told us, Muadh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Al-Ala told us, Abd told us Allah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar bin Abi Talib, said: “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding the price of “The dog and the cupping”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6416 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6417","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Bukhari told us, he said: Al-Anbari said: Ismail bin Ubayd Allah Al-Thaqafi told me, Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Marwan told me, Ibrahim bin Muhammad told me Bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of his father, that he heard Abdullah bin Jafar May God be pleased with them both, saying: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, command a man and say: “Ask God for pardon and well-being in this world and the hereafter.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6417 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6418","Abu Al-Walid the Imam told me, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told me: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, and Muhammad bin Al-Mamil told me, then Al-Fadl bin Muhammad, they said: Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Asram bin Hawshab told us, Ishaq bin Wasil Al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar Muhammad Bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: We said to Abdullah bin Jafar bin Abi Talib: Tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what Did you see him, and do not tell us about anyone else, even if he was trustworthy, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Between the navel to the knee “privacy”
 I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Charity in secret extinguishes the wrath of the Lord.”
 And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The worst of my nation are people who were born in bliss and fed with it. They eat various types of food, and they wear “And they wear many different kinds of clothing, and they ride different kinds of animals, and they speak with eloquence.”
 I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ibn Abbas came to him and said: I came to a people who were talking, but when they saw me, they fell down. They made an exception for me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And they did it?” By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of them will believe until he loves you for my love. Do you hope that you will enter Paradise through my intercession, for the Banu Abd do not hope for it? The requester
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6418 - I think it is fabricated"
"6419","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Muhammad bin Kunasa told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of her women is Maryam bint Imran. The best of her women is Khadija bint Khuwaylid.” Most of Hisham’s companions narrated it on his authority, and it is narrated in the two Sahihs like this."
"6420","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: “Wathila bin Al-Asqa’ bin Abd al-Uzza bin Abd Yalil bin Nashib bin Ghayrah bin Sa’d bin Laith. They differed as to his surname.”"
"6421","So Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas told us, the jurist in Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Salih, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I entered upon Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ and said: O Abu Al-Asqa’ told us a hadith that he heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in which there was no illusion, nothing more, or forgetfulness. He said: “Has anyone read Did you learn anything from the Qur’an tonight? So we said: Yes, and we are not its memorizers. He said: “This is the Qur’an written between your backs. You have not tried to memorize it, and you claim You add and subtract, so how about the hadiths we heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is possible that we only heard them once. “It is sufficient for you when we bring you the hadith according to its meaning.” It has been said: “His nickname is Abu Qursafa.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6421 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6422","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, he said: Maslama bin Abdul-Malik addressed us, and he said: Do not fast Ramadan while traveling, for whoever fasts it should make it up, Abu Al-Fayd said. Al-Fayd: So I met Abu Qursafa and Thathila bin Al-Asqa’ and I asked him, and he said: “If I fasted, then fasted, then fasted, then I fasted, I would not have made up my mind.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6422 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6423","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa told me, he said: “Wathila ibn al-Asqa’ was nicknamed Abu Qarasafa, he has a house in Basra, and it has been said that his nickname is Abu Shaddad."
"6424","Abu Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Duhaym Al-Dimashqi told us, Ubayy told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Marwan bin Jinnah, Yunus bin Maysarah bin Halbas told us: “I met Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ and I said: How are you, Abu Shaddad?”"
"6425","Ismail bin Ayyash, Saeed bin Khalid told me, saying: “Wathila bin Al-Asqa’ died when he was one hundred and five years old, and that was in “In the year eighty-three”"
"6426","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: “Wathila died Ibn Al-Asqa’ was eighty-three years old, and he was one hundred and five years old.”"
"6427","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muqatili, Asmaa bint Wathilah ibn al-Asqa’ told me: When my father prayed the morning prayer, he would sit facing the qiblah until The sun was rising, and perhaps I spoke to him about a need, but he would not speak to me, so I said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever prays the Fajr prayer and then recites Qul Huwa Allahu One hundred times before speaking to anyone will be forgiven.” He has committed a sin for a year.”"
"6428","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Ubayy told us, Sulaym bin Mansour bin Ammar told us, Ubayy told us, Ma’ruf told us Abu Al-Khattab, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, who said: When I converted to Islam, I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said to me: “Go and take a bath.” with water and lotus trees, and throw away the hair of disbelief from you.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over my head."
"6429","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: “Abdullah bin Abi Awfa Abu Muawiyah.”"
"6430","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Abu Awfa, and the name of Abu Awfa is Alqamah bin Khalid bin Al Harith bin Abi Usayd bin Rifa’ah bin Tha’labah bin Hawazin bin Aslam bin Afsa, his nickname is Abdullah Abu Muawiyah, and the first scene witnessed by Abdullah bin Abi Awfa was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Khaybar and the scenes after that. Abdullah bin Abi Awfa remained in Medina until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and he turned To Kufa, he settled there when the Muslims settled there and built a house there in Islam, and his sight had gone, and he died in Kufa in the year six ""Eighty"""
"6431","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Subaie told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told me, he said: I heard Abu Nu’aym say: “Abd died “By Allah, Ibn Abi Awfa, in the year eighty-seven or eighty-eight.”"
"6432","Mukhlid bin Jaafar told me, and Muhammad bin Jarir told us, saying: “It has been said that the last person to die in Kufa was among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abdullah bin Abi Awfa greeted him."
"6433","Ali bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Qadi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Saeed bin Yahya Al-Umawi told us, my father told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled said: I saw the hand of Ibn Abi hit him the hardest. I said: When did this happen to you? He said: “The day of Hunayn.” I said: Did you meet Hunayn? He said: “Yes, and before that.”"
"6434","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa: “There were one thousand and four hundred of the tree’s owners, and it was the safest price of the emigrants at that time.”"
"6435","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed, Hashraj bin Nabatah told Saeed bin Juhan, saying: I went to Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I greeted him. While his sight was obscured, he said to me: Who are you? I said: I am Saeed bin Jumhan. He said: What did your father do? I said: The Azariqa killed him. He said: May God curse the Azariqa. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that they are the dogs of hell.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6435 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6436","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told me, Muhammad bin Saad al-Awfi told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Abd al-Muhaymin bin al-Abbas bin Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi, my father told us, on the authority of his father, that “His name was Hazan, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him Sahl.”"
"6437","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, my father told me, he said: “I told Sahl bin Saad Al-Saadi: O Abu Al-Abbas."
"6438","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subai’i told me, and Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam told me, saying: I heard Abu Nu’aym say: “Sahl bin Sa’d Al-Sa’idi died in the year ""Eighty-eight"""
"6439","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Ansari, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had reached the age of fifteen year”"
"6440","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, my father told me, On the authority of Qudamah bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: “I saw Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf attacking Abbas bin Sahl bin Saad during the emirate of Ibn Al-Zubayr appeared and Sahl was wearing a yellow robe and robe. When he came, Al-Hajjaj advised Al-Hajjaj to refrain from attacking his son.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6440 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6441","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubayri told us, he told me Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I tell them on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they say: Thus and thus, and if I had come forward, they would not have heard anyone say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6441 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6442","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farawi told us, Abu Maudud told us, he said: “I saw Sahl bin Saad’s beard white and his moustache trimmed.”"
"6443","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Nasawi told us, Abu Musab told us, Abdul Muhaymin bin Abbas told us Ibn Sahl Ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he “presented the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day.”"
"6444","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hazami told us, he said: “Sahl ibn Sa’d died. Al-Saadi, nicknamed Abu Abbas, was born in Medina in the year ninety-one, and he was the last of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to die in Medina. He was a hundred years old.”"
"6445","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Abi died Hadard al-Aslami, nicknamed Abu Muhammad, in the year seventy-one and he is eighty-one years old, and the name of Abu Hadard Salama, and he is from the Banu A thin stomach from a Muslim.”"
"6446","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir told me, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us Al-Ansari, my father told us, on the authority of a servant of Anas bin Malik, who said: I said to Anas bin Malik: Did you witness Badr? He said: “You have no mother, and where can I be absent from Badr?”
 Al-Ansari said: “Anas went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he headed to Badr. He was a boy serving the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Abu Hatim said: We asked Al-Ansari: How old was Anas bin Malik on the day he died? He said: He is one hundred and seven years old.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6446 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6447","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibn Abi told me Dhi’ib, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Yazid, who said: “I saw Anas ibn Malik with a seal around his neck. Al-Hajjaj wanted to humiliate him with that.”"
"6448","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told me, Abu Nu’aym told me, he said: “Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, died. “In the year ninety-three.”"
"6449","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me. He said: “Anas bin Malik bin Al-Nadr bin Damdam bin Zaid bin Haram bin Jundub bin Amir bin Ghanam bin Adi bin Al-Najjar, and his mother was Umm Salim bint Milhan"
"6450","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Abadani told us, Ali bin Harb Al-Mawsili told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik May God be pleased with him. He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old.”"
"6451","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Qais bin Unif told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abd al-Warith bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhaib, he said: “I and Thabit al-Bunani entered Anas bin Malik, and Thabit said: O Abu Hamza.”"
"6452","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabour told us, he told me Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ma`bad ibn Hilal, said: If we used to attack Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, he would bring us something impossible. With him, he said: “I heard this from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I wrote it down and presented it to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6452 - The hadith is objectionable"
"6453","Ali bin Issa told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Samak bin Musa said: “When Anas, may God be pleased with him, entered upon Al-Hajjaj, he ordered that his neck be beheaded, then he said: O people of the Levant, do you know this? This is the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: Do you know why I went to his neck? They said: The prince knows best. He said: He was among the calamities in the first trial, and he was deceived in the after trial.
 Jarir said: Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah told me, saying: “Al-Hajjaj was taking him around in the military, so Anas wrote to Abd al-Malik: What do you think? A servant of Moses came to you. Did you harm him? So Abdul-Malik wrote to Al-Hajjaj: Leave him, let him live wherever he wants in the country, and do not let it be disturbed by him. He wrote to Anas saying that he is not for anyone. “You have inferior authority over me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6453 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6454","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, and Abu Kurayb told us: Abu Bakr bin told us Ayyash, on the authority of Al-Amash, said: Anas bin Malik wrote to Abdul-Malik bin Marwan: “O Commander of the Faithful, I have served Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him for ten years, and that Al-Hajjaj is preparing me from the area of Basra.” So Abdul-Malik said: Write to Al-Hajjaj, boy, so he wrote To him: Woe to you! I fear that no one will be kind to you. So when this letter of mine comes to you, get up and apologize to Anas bin Malik.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6454 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6455","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Maymun Abu Abdullah told me, Thabit Al-Bunani told us, he said: Anas said: “O Abu Muhammad, take it from me, for I took it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God took it from me.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of God Almighty, and you will not take it from anyone more trustworthy than me.”"
"6456","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Awf, He said: “Anas spoke rarely on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whenever he narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would say: Or as The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6456 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6457","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Ishaq bin Uthman told us, he said: I told Musa bin Anas: How much did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquer? He said: “He waged twenty-three battles, and eight battles during which he stayed for months.” I said: How many battles did Anas wage with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Eight invasions.”"
"6458","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hajjaj told us, Humaid informed us, that Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, told us He narrated a hadith, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man said: You heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he became very angry. severely, and said: “By God, everything we talk to you about, we heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he used to talk to one another, and he did not accuse ""each other""
 The mention of knowing a group of the Companions and what has come down to us of their virtues. Their mention was later than those mentioned, and the knowledge of their births and the times And when they died, may God be pleased with them, they were among them."
"6459","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat al-Asfari told us, he said: “Hamil ibn Malik ibn Al-Nabigha bin Jabir bin Ubaid bin Rabi’ah bin Ka’b bin Al-Harith bin Kathir bin Hind bin Tabha bin Lahyan bin Hudhayl Al-Hudhali has a house in Basra.”"
"6460","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, Amr bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, stood up on the pulpit and said: I remember a man who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, make a ruling regarding the fetus, and Hamal bin Malik bin Al-Nabigha Al-Hudhali stood up and said: O Prince. Believers, I was between two maids, meaning two wives, so I went out and one of them hit the other with the pillar of her umbrella, and I killed her and what was in her. Her womb. “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed that the fetus should be separated from the forelock of a male or female slave.” Then he said, “May God be great, may God grant us life, if we had not heard of this.” We decided otherwise"
"6461","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: “Abu Talib was born Aqeel, Ja`far, and Ali, each one of them ten years older than his friend in loyalty.”"
"6462","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Shabab Al-Asfri told us, Khalifa told us, he said: “Aqeel bin Abi came He sought Kufa, Basra, and the Levant, and died during the caliphate of Muawiyah.”"
"6463","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin al-Hasan, the son of my brother Abu Tahir al-Aqi, told me. My grandfather Yahya bin al-Hasan told me. Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah al-Talhi, my father told us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Hani al-Sijzi narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he narrated to me Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid bin Jabr Abi Al-Hajjaj, said: Among the blessings of God upon Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, was what God did. And he wanted good for him, because a severe crisis had befallen the Quraysh, and Abu Talib had many dependents, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He handed over to his uncle Al-Abbas: He was one of the easiest of Banu Hashim, O Abu Al-Fadl, “Indeed, your brother, Abu Talib, has many children, and he has befallen the people as you see.” “From this crisis, we will go to him and we will relieve him of his family, taking one man from his children, and you take another man and we will take care of them for him.” Al-Abbas said: Yes, so they set off until they came to Abu Talib, and they said: We want to relieve you of your family until you reveal what they are to the people. In it, Abu Talib said to them: If you leave me Aqeel, then do whatever you want. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Ali and took him to him. Al-Abbas took Ja’far and hugged him to him. Ali remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until God sent him as a prophet, so he followed him and believed him. Al-Abbas took Ja’far, and Ja’far remained with Al-Abbas until he converted to Islam and no longer needed him."
"6464","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Issa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Aqeel bin Abi Talib: O Abu Yazid, “I love you with two loves Because of your closeness to me, and out of love for what I knew of my uncle’s love for you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6464 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6465","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jarahi told us about Marwa, Yahya bin Shasawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ali told us, Ibrahim bin Rustum, told us by Abu Hamza, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he greeted him, saying to Aqeel: “I love you, O Aqeel, with two loves for you, and out of love for Abu Talib’s love for you.” Explanation of these two hadiths in the hadith Which"
"6466","Abu Umar Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Zahid told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, Yunus ibn Arqam told us, Harun bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed from a house, and with him were two blind men. Al-Abbas, Hamza, Ali, Ja’far, and Aqeel were in a land where they were working, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his blind man, “They chose from “These?” One of them said: I chose Ja’far, and the other said: I chose Ali, so he said: “I chose you both, so I chose you, so God chose Ali for me.”"
"6467","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abi Suwayd narrated to us, Abdul-Wahid narrated to us. Ibn Ziyad, Talha bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, Aqeel bin Abi Talib told me, he said: The Quraysh came to Abi Talib, and they said: Your nephew was harming us in our club and in our gathering, so he forbade him from harming us, so he said to me: O Aqeel, come to Muhammad. He said: So I went to him. So I took him out from sitting, and Talha said: A small plant grew, and he came in the afternoon due to the extreme heat, so he started looking for the raincoat and walked in it due to the extreme heat. So we went to them, and Abu Talib said: Your cousins claimed that you were harming them in their club and in their gathering, so refrain from that and flew. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at the sky and said: “What do you see this sun?” They said: Yes. He said: “I am not able to let that of you do anything from it.” Then Abu Talib said: We have not lied, Ibn My brother, come back"
"6468",""
"6469","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Maqil bin Yasar bin Abdullah bin Harraq Ibn Luayy Ibn Ka'b Ibn Abd Ibn Thawr Ibn Hadmah Ibn Latim Ibn Uthman Ibn Amr Ibn Ad Ibn Tabikha, nicknamed Abu Ali and his A plan in Basra. Maqil bin Yasar died under the command of Ibn Ziyad in the year fifty-eight.”"
"6470","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Salama told us, and Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. Al-Hanzali, Hamza bin Umair narrated, Ayoub bin Ibrahim Abu Yahya Al-Alam narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Maymun Al-Sayegh narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khaled Muhammad bin Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Ma’qil bin Yasar Al-Muzani, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me to I judge between my people, and I said: I am not a good judge. He said: “I judge between them.” I said: I am a good judge, so he said: “I judge between them, for God Blessed and Most High is with the judge as long as he does not commit intentional wrongdoing.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6470 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6471","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi and Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, they said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, he reported Imran Al-Qattan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Maqil bin Yasar Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Act upon the Book of God and do not deny any of it. Whatever of it is suspected to you, ask the people of knowledge about it and they will tell you. Believe in the Torah. And the Gospel, and believe in the Criterion, for in it is the clarification, and He is the intercessor, and He is the one who intercedes, and the granter, and the one who confirms.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6471 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6472","Sheikh Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin told us Minhaal, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Abu Imran Al-Juni narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, consulted with Al-Hurmuzan in Isfahan, Persia, and Azerbaijan, and said: “O Commander of the Faithful, Isfahan is the head.”"
"6473","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Bishr bin Maqil bin Hassan bin Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani informed me. Caliph, Muhammad bin Salam Al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Mughaffal bin Abd Nihm bin Afif Bin Suhaim bin Rabi’ah bin Adi bin Tha’labah bin Dhu’ayb bin Saad bin Adi bin Uthman bin Amr bin Ad bin Tabha”"
"6474","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani was nicknamed Abu Saeed mentioned this lineage and added to it, and his mother is Al-Atila, the daughter of Muawiyah bin Qurrah bin Muzainah, and he has a house in Basra in the presence of the mosque.”"
"6475","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qaari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Sadaqa bin Musa told us, Saeed told us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, said: “If I die, put camphor at the end of my washing, and shroud me in two garments.” And a shirt, for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did that with it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6475 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6476","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And Ka’b bin Zuhayr and Bujayr bin Zuhayr bin Abi Salma, and the name of Abi Salma is Rabi’ah bin Rabah bin Qurt bin Al-Harith bin Qatada bin Halawa bin Tha'labah bin Thawr bin Hadmah bin Latim bin Uthman bin Amr bin Ad bin Tabha came as a delegation to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they and his companions converted to Islam.”"
"6477","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hussein bin Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Abdul-Malik Al-Asadi told me in Hamadan, then Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami, Al-Hajjaj bin Dhul-Ruqaybah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Zuhair bin Abi Salma Al-Muzani told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Ka’b and Bujayr, the sons of Zuhayr, went out until they came and Al-Azzaf telegraphed, so Bujayr said to Ka’b: Be patient in the haste of this. The place until I came to this man, meaning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and heard what he was saying. Ka’b stood still and Bujayr came out. “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and offered him Islam.” So he converted to Islam and that man reached Ka’b and said:
 [Long Sea]

 Did they not deliver a good message about me... Woe to anyone else?
 On a character upon whom you have neither a mother nor a father... and upon whom you have never found a brother of yours.
 Abu Bakr gave you a drink of a generous cup... and Al-Ma’mun consumed some of it and gave you gum.
 When the verses reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he shed his blood and said: “Whoever meets Ka’b, let him kill him.” So Bujayr wrote about this to His brother reminds him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has shed his blood, and he says to him: He survived and I will not see you escape.Then he wrote to him after that: Know that no one will come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, testifying that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad Messenger of God, except before that, so when this letter of mine comes to you, submit to Islam and come. Then Ka’b embraced Islam and recited the poem in which the Messenger of God praises God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then he approached and rested his mount at the door of the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then he entered the mosque and the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with his companions at the table, a group of people gathered around him in a circle without a circle. He turned to them once and spoke to them. And to these people once, and he spoke to them, Ka'b said, so I leaned my camel at the door of the mosque, and I recognized the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by the description So I walked over until I sat next to him, then I surrendered and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are the Messenger of God of safety, O Messenger of God. He said: “And who are you?” I said: I am Ka'b bin Zuhayr. He said: You are the one you say. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and said: How? He said: O Abu Bakr. So Abu recited it to him. Bakr, may God be pleased with him:
 Abu Bakr gave you a drink of a large cup... and the commander drank some of it and chewed it.
 He said: O Messenger of God, I did not say like that. He said: “And how did you say?” He said: I only said:

 Abu Bakr gave you a drink of a generous cup...And Al-Ma'mun consumed some of it and tallow it,
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ma’mun, by God.” Then he recited the entire poem until he came to the end and dictated it to Al-Hajjaj ibn Dhul Ruqaybah until he came to the end, which is this poem:
 [Simple Sea]

 Souad said, “My heart is wet today... I am in love, and after her there is no return. I am shackled.”
 And there was no happiness in the morning when they suffered... except a low-key and scorned ostentation.
 When she smiles, the symptoms of injustice become apparent... as if the cup was full of something sick.
 The bartenders poured water on him from the water of Abtah Adha and he was covered.
 The winds drive away the filth from him and scatter him... from the side of the white pillar of Jaalel.
 He would give her respect, if she had been true to her promise... even if advice had been accepted.
 But it is a trait that has been mixed in her blood... pain, passion, disagreement, and change.
 As long as she remains in this state, she is...as the ghoul appears in her clothes.
 So do not hold on to the connection that you claimed...except as water is held by sieves.
 Arqub’s promises were an example to her...and her promises are nothing but vanities.
 Do not be deceived by what it has promised or what it has promised... except misleading wishes and dreams.
 I hope or hope that her affection will diminish... and we have no idea that we have any advice from you.
 Souad touched a land that could not reach her...Except for freed women, noble women, and correspondents
 And no one will reach it except a woman who is ungrateful...in which is both abandonment and transgression.
 From all the freshness of the palm tree, if it sweats... it is exposed to the tamper of signs. Unknown
 The tick walks on it and then slips on it... including frankincense and sticky skin.
 A carnage that slandered unjustly... and its elbow was twisted from the ribs of falsehood.
 As if it was close to its eyes and its altar... from its snout and from its beards was a barrel.
 Dates are like the honeycomb of a bee when it harvests... in the cave of Zalm, the marshes betray it.
 Qur’an in its freedom for one who sees it... a clear emancipation and ease in the cheeks.
 It will be taken on ease, and it will follow... A rain that has touched the earth. Analysis
 Letter: Her father, her brother, is from a muhjana family... and her paternal uncle is her maternal uncle, Quda Shamlil.
 Old women will leave behind the rash... as soon as their piety is as great as the sleeve is made of sandals.
 One day the hump of the earth will continue to raise it... from the sparks of confusion and shifting
 He was covering her hands after she came to the rescue... and the Asaqeel was covered with cloth.
 One day the chameleon remained hunted... he was surrounded by the sun, bored
 We started to eat skewered meat... She responded to it with heavy skewers.
 The soft wailing of the two hyenas has no meaning... When her firstborn mourned, the wailing one is reasonable.
 The traitors seek to go around and tell them...O son of Abi Salma, you will be killed.
 Leave the way to her hands, you have no father... for everything that the Most Gracious has destined is an effect.
 Every son of a female, even if his safety lasts for a long time... a day on a portable humpback machine.
 I was informed that the Messenger of God made a promise to me... and forgiveness is hoped for by the Messenger of God.
 I came to the Messenger of God apologizing... and the excuse is accepted by the Messenger of God.
 Wait, Messenger of the One who gave you a voluntary prayer... The Qur’an contains exhortations and details.
 Do not take me for the words of informers, and I have not committed a crime, even if there are many rumors about me.
 I stand where no elephant can stand... I see and hear what an elephant hears.
 He would continue to thunder unless he had... with the Messenger, God willing. Tanweel
 Until I placed my right hand so that I would not dispute it...in a palm full of vengeance that was said to be said.
 So it was my fear when he spoke to him... since it was said that you are attributed and responsible.
 From a pupa with sharp fangs... he obeyed him with a stomach without which a generation stumbled.
 He goes in the morning and welds two sides of mine...flesh of the people scattered with mustards.
 Wild donkeys remain weak from it... and hookahs do not walk through its valley.
 And there is still a trustworthy brother in his valley... Where the place of clothing and clothing is eaten
 The Messenger is a light to be illuminated... and a sharpened sword of God drawn.
 Concerning a group of young men from Quraysh, their speaker said... In the heart of Mecca, when they embraced Islam, they disappeared.They disappeared, but the cup remained, and there was no revelation... at the meeting, and there was no inclination of comforters.
 The smell of the naked men is their robes... of the robes woven by David in the Hijah
 Contaminated eggs have become rounded... as if the neck of the neck is braided.
 They walk with the gait of camels, and blossoms protect them...a beating when black people smell spices.
 They do not rejoice when their spears fail... They are a people who do not fight when they are defeated.
 The stab does not occur except in their throats... and they have nothing to do with the depths of death."
"6478","Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, Maan bin Issa told me, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told me Al-Awqas, on the authority of Ibn Jud’an, said: Ka’b bin Zuhair bin Abi Salma recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque: “
 [Simple Sea]
 Souad declared, “My heart is wet today... I am in love, and then there is no need for anything that is shackled.”"
"6479","Al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad bin Falih narrated to me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sang Ka’b ibn Zuhayr’s bant Sa’ad in his mosque in Medina, and when he reached his statement:
 [Simple Sea]
 Indeed, the Messenger is a sword with which to seek guidance... and a sharpened sword of God drawn.
 Concerning a group of young men from Quraysh, their speaker said: “In the heart of Mecca, when they embraced Islam, they disappeared.”
 The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed his sleeve to the people so that they could hear from him. He said: Bujayr ibn Zuhayr wrote to his brother Ka’b ibn Zuhair bin Abi Salma intimidated him and called him to Islam, and he said verses about it:
 [Long Sea]
 Whoever reaches the Ka'b level, will it be yours in that for which you are falsely blamed, and it is more decisive?
 To God, not Al-Uzza or Al-Lat alone...so you will be saved if there is salvation and be safe.
 There is a day when no one will escape from the Fire except the pure and Muslim of heart.
 The debt of Zuhair, which is nothing, is void...and the debt of Abu Salma Ali is forbidden.
 This is a hadith with chains of transmission that were collected by Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami. As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Fulayh, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba and the hadith Al-Hajjaj ibn Dhu al-Ruqaybah, they are both authentic, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi mentioned them briefly in al-Maghazi.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6479 - Al-Hakim said this and the hadith of Ibn Dhul-Ruqaybah are authentic"
"6480","As Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, H. Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ali ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Aqeel al-Jarrahi informed us, and the wording for them is that they said: He informed. Abu Shuaib Al-Harrani, Abu Ja’far Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He surrendered Medina on his way out of Taif, and Bujayr bin Zuhayr bin Abi Salma wrote to his brother Ka’b bin Zuhair bin Abi Salma, informing him that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “killed men in Mecca who used to satirize him and harm him,” and that he was one of the remaining poets of Quraysh, Ibn al-Zabar’a. Hubayra bin Abi Wahb have fled in every direction, so if you have a need, go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for he He does not kill anyone who comes to him repentant, and if you do not do so, then save yourself until you are saved. Ka’b used to say: verses in which he attained salvation from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until it was narrated on his authority, and it was known, and he was the one who said:
 [Long Sea]
 Didn't they deliver a message about me with a generous message... and would you be destroyed for what I said? Woe to you.
 So you told me if I was not effective...For anything, woe to someone else, that is
 On a creation, you did not assign a mother or a father... upon him, and you did not assign a father to him.
 If you do not do it, you are not sorry... nor will anyone say, “Why did you stumble?”
 Al-Ma'mun gave you a slow cup to drink...so Al-Ma'mun consumed some of it and gave you gum.
 He said: Ka'b only said: Al-Ma'mun, based on what the Quraysh said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they used to say it. When Ka'b reached that, she became upset with him. The earth, and he felt pity for himself and caused the enemy who was present with him to tremble, so they said: He has been killed. When he did not find anything, he appeared. His poem in which he praises the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentions his fear and the trembling of being told off by him, then he went out until he came Medina, and he went down to a man with whom he had an acquaintance from Juhayna, as was mentioned to me, and he took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he prayed. In the morning, he prayed with the people, then he pointed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so go to him. So I trusted him, and he mentioned to me that he stood up to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he put his hand in his hand. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “No.” He knows him,”He said: O Messenger of God, Ka’b bin Zuhayr came to seek protection from you as a repentant and Muslim man. Will you accept it if I bring him to you? The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Yes.” He said: O Messenger of God, I am Ka’b bin Zuhayr.
 Ibn Ishaq said: Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told me, he said: A man from the Ansar jumped up on him and said: O Messenger of God, leave me and my enemy. By God, I beheaded him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Leave him alone, for he has come repentant and departing.” Ka’b became angry with this neighborhood. Among the supporters of what their friend did to him, and that is because no man among the immigrants spoke of it except well, so he said his poem that was Suad came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned the poem until the end and added to it:
 [Simple Sea]

 You throw the glass in the eyes of a single person, gasping... If sadness ignites, then the incline
 Huge, imitating her, so uncle, restricting her... in her character from the daughters of a stallion, a preference
 It falls upon easy places while it is restless... cripples that fall to the ground.
 And he said to the people, “Guide to them, and I have made... the leaves of the grasshoppers run over the gravel.” It was said
 When I saw the hump of the earth raising it...with the lights, mixing and shifting
 And every friend I was hoping for said... I will not meet you, I will be busy with you.“If he marries a horn, it is not permissible for him... to leave the horn unless it is loose.”
 Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada said: When he said: When the blacks prepared spices, and he only meant the company of the Ansar, since he had made their companion and singled out The emigrants from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Quraysh. By praising him, the Ansar became angry with him, so he said: After he converted to Islam while he was He praises the Ansar and mentions their ordeal with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and their situation in Yemen, so he said:
 [full sea]

 Whoever is pleased with the generosity of life will remain...in the rank of the righteous of the Ansar.
 They inherited good deeds from generation to generation... Indeed, the good ones are the children of the good people.
 Those who sacrifice their souls for their Prophet... during the turmoil and the attack of the Titan.
 And those who look with reddened eyes... like burning coals, without their eyes dull.
 The Samaritan oppressors, with arms like the Indians' paws, are not short.
 And for them, when the stars fade and become hidden... for the wanderers who go to their places.
 Those who turn people away from their religions... by honor and by keeping us in danger.
 Until they stood upright while spears were crushing them... in every unknown place and every choice.
 For the truth, God is the supporter of his religion...and his prophet with the truth and warnings.
 And those who feed the guest, when he takes their place... from the fat of a heap, like the hills, a tax collector.And those who advance when the clouds gather... and those who strike people in the hurricane.
 They seek to attack the enemy with every effort... and the mild night is coming at the airport.
 Aged, hoarse, and formidable... like a sword striking his throat with a bracelet.
 They trained as I trained, with bare stomachs...the necks of the lions were defeated by predators.
 And sincere old people like lions, with strings... and with all the dust that touches the strings.
 And with mixtures like thujaf, the weak ones... He cures the cruelty of the ungodly with them.
 They struck a blow against us on the Day of Badr... and the crowds of Nizar condemned it for its attack.
 They do not complain of death if it befalls them... a war with caves and shelters
 They purify themselves as if it were a ritual for them... with the blood of the infidels who were hanged.
 And when you come to them to seek their help... you will find yourself between Ma'afir and Ghafar.
 They protect the religion of God. Indeed, His religion has... a right for every deceitful person.
 If the people knew all my knowledge... those who command me would have believed me.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6480 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6481","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Qurrah bin Iyas bin Hilal bin Rabab bin Ubayd Allah bin Dhu’ayb bin Aws bin Sawwarah bin Amr bin Sariya bin Tha’labah bin Dinar bin Sulaiman bin Aws bin Othman Ibn Amr is Abu Muawiyah Ibn Qurra. He had a house in Basra in the presence of Al-Awfa. The Azariqa killed him along with Ibn Ubais in the year four. ""sixty"""
"6482","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ahmad bin Bishr Al-Marthadi narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Ja’d narrated to us, Adi bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurra, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I will take the sheep to slaughter it and have mercy on it. He said: “And the sheep, if May God have mercy on her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6482 - Adi bin Al-Fadl perished"
"6483","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Tabbaa’, Abu Sufyan Al-Maamari told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurra, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over all other foods. We did not write about it except about him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6483 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6484","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told me, in Nishapur, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki told us, Ibrahim ibn Zakaria al-Abdisi told us, Fudayk ibn Suleiman, Khalifa bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah bin Qurrah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever says “Allahu Akbar” at sunset on the seashore, raising his voice, God will give him a reward equal to the number of each drop in the water. “The sea has ten good deeds, erased from it ten bad deeds, and raised for it ten levels, with each two levels being a hundred-year journey for a galloping horse.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6484 - This is very objectionable"
"6485","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Aidh bin Amr bin Hilal bin Ubaid bin Rawaha bin Labiba bin Adi bin Amer bin Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Hadmah bin Latim bin Uthman bin Amr, nicknamed Abu Hubayra died under the rule of Ibn Ziyad, and he had a famous house in Basra.”"
"6486","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Zaid bin Al-Harish told us, Hashraj bin Abdullah bin Hashraj, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, who said: I was hit in the face by a throw, and I was fighting in the hands of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Hunayn, when the blood ran down my face, beard, and chest, “the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took food, and the blood ran down my face and chest.” To Thandawti, then he prayed for me.” Hashraj said: “A’idh used to tell us about this during his lifetime, so when he died and we washed him, we looked at what had happened.” He describes to us from the trace of the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the end of what he was telling us from his chest, and behold, a flowing bang like the bang of a horse.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6486 - Its chain of transmission is unknown"
"6487","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, they said: Ismail bin Iyas said: I heard Amr bin Sulaym Al-Muzani saying: I heard Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Muzani, may God Almighty have mercy on him, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The rock and the stick are from Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6487 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6488","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “In Naming one of the Ansar from the Banu Khazraj who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Ubayy Ibn Salul,” Urwah said: “He is Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Malik bin Salem bin Ghanam bin Awf bin Al-Khazraj.”"
"6489","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul was martyred on the Day of Al-Yamamah in the year twelve.”"
"6490","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Ubayy Ibn Salul, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, kill my father. He said: “Do not kill your father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6490 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6491","Abu Abdullah told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Khazen told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sari Al-Asqalani told us, Abdah bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul, that “he asked permission of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, wanted to kill his father, but he forbade him from doing so."
"6492","Abu Abdullah told me, Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sari Al-Asqalani told us, Asim bin Suleiman Al-Kuri told us, Hisham told us Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ubayy Ibn Salul, that two of his teeth were injured on the day of Uhud with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to"
"6493","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, in Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Ubayy Ibn Salul mentioned. Ibn Ishaq said: Salul is a woman, and she is my father’s mother, and they are Banu al-Ahbala.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6492 - Asim bin Suleiman Al-Kuri is a liar"
"6494","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Al-Nu’man Bin Qawqal, and Qawqal's name is Malik bin Tha’labah bin Da’ad bin Fahm bin Tha’labah bin Ghanim bin Salem bin Awf bin Amr bin Awf bin Al-Khazraj, and Al-Qawaqil: They are the group of Ubadah bin Al-Samit.”"
"6495","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told me, Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid told us, my father told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu al-Aswad told us, about Urwah, “In naming one of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Numan ibn Malik ibn Tha’labah ibn Asram, and he is the one who is called Qawqul.” Jabir bin Abdullah narrated on the authority of Al-Numan bin Qoqal"
"6496","Abu Al-Hussein bin Tamim Al-Hanthali told us, Abu Ismail told us, Abu Al-Aswad Al-Nadr bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Qawqal, that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, Have you seen that if I pray the obligatory prayers, fast Ramadan, perform what is permissible, and prohibit what is forbidden, and do nothing more than that, I will enter Paradise? He said: “Yes.” He said: By God, I will not add anything to that."
"6497","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Salih told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwah, “In naming one of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, ‘Itban ibn Malik,” he said: Some thing occurred to me in my sight, so I sent to the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace."
"6498","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Arim Abu Al-Nu’man told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Ali told us Ibn Zaid, he said: “We were with Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, and he said: To his son.”"
"6499","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “In Naming the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Ziyad bin Labid bin Tha’labah bin Sinan bin Amir bin Adi bin Umayyah bin Bayda bin Amer bin Zurayq, his mother was the daughter of Abd Mudharib bin Al Harith bin Zaid bin Ubaid bin Amr bin Awf, and he died in the first of Muawiyah’s caliphates in my hearing. From the history of youth”"
"6500","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Yahya bin Ishaq al-Silahini told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ziyad bin Labid Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted his companions while he was saying: “The time of knowledge has passed.” I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, how can the time of knowledge pass while we are We read the Qur’an and teach it to our children, and our children teach it to their children until the Hour comes? He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Labid. If I were to see you as one of the most learned scholars of the people of Medina, do not the Jews and Christians read the Torah? And the Gospel, and they do not benefit from it at all? This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"6501","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming The Ansar who witnessed Badr and Aqaba were Amara bin Hazm bin Zayd bin Luthan bin Amr bin Abd Awf bin Ghanim bin Malik Ibn Al-Najjar, and he was martyred on the Day of Al-Yamamah from among the Ansar, then from Banu Malik Ibn Al-Najjar, Amara Ibn Hazm.”"
"6502","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Bakr bin Sawadah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Nuaym al-Hadrami, on the authority of Amara bin Hazm, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me sitting on a grave. He said: “Come down from the grave.” “Do not harm the companion of the grave, and he will not harm you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6502 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6503","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Yazid bin Thabit bin Al-Dahhak bin Zaid bin Luzan bin Amr bin Awf bin Ghanim bin Malik bin Al-Najjar, his mother and the mother of his brother Zaid bin Thabit Al-Nawar bint Malik bin Amer bin Adi bin Al-Najjar witnessed Badr and was martyred on the Day of Al-Yamamah.”"
"6504","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Uthman bin Hakim told us, On the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of his uncle Yazid bin Thabit, that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions. A funeral, and when they saw it, “he revolted and his companions revolted, and they did not stop standing until I returned, and I do not consider him to be anyone but a Jew or a Jewish woman.”"
"6505","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Ibn Salih told us Lahi’ah, Othman bin Hakim told us, Kharijah bin Zaid bin Thabit informed me, on the authority of his uncle Yazid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, that they They went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day with a funeral until they reached Al-Baqi. He said: What is this? They said: This is so-and-so, the servant of so-and-so, and he knew her, so he said: “Will you not inform me of her?” They said: We buried her at noon, and I was asleep, but I did not say that. We would like to announce it to you. So he stood up and described the people behind him and said the takbir over it four times. Then he said: “None of you dies unless you announce it to me. My prayer is mercy for them.”"
"6506","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Busur bin Abi Artaat, and the name of Abi Artaat is Umayr bin Amr bin Awaymir bin Imran bin Al-Halbas bin Sayyar bin Nizar bin Mu’iz Bin Amir bin Luay"
"6507","Ahmed bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Busr bin Abi Artaat died, may God have mercy on him. May God protect him during the caliphate of Muawiyah. He had grown old until he became senile, and he was nicknamed Abu Abd al-Rahman. He died in Medina and his son. In Basra"
"6508","Ibrahim bin Firas Al-Faqih told us, about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Souri told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Shayban, Yazid bin Ubaidah bin Abi Al-Muhajir told me, Yazid, the client of Busr bin Abi Artaat, told me, on the authority of Busr Ibn Abi Artaat, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to “pray, O God, grant us the best punishment in all matters and protect us from our disgrace.” This world and the torment of the Hereafter.”"
"6509","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Al-Mustarid bin Shaddad bin Amr bin Hasal bin Al-Ahbab bin Habib bin Amr bin Shayban bin Muharib bin Fahr bin Malik died. In Egypt in the state of Muawiyah”"
"6510","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Zuhr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Mustaridah ibn Shaddad, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “There is nothing like this world in the hereafter except that when a man inserts his finger and what does it come back with?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6510 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6511","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Muammar bin al-Muthanna told us, he said: “Khafaf bin Ima bin Rahdha bin Harbah bin Khafaf bin Haritha bin Ghaffar. His father, Ima bin Rahdha, converted to Islam and was one of the leaders of his people. He witnessed Khafaf bin Imaa Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6512","Ibrahim bin Asmat Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, about Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, said: Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: “We came to our people forgiving, but some of them converted to Islam before That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, and Ima bin Rahdha was their leader, and he was their master.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6512 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6513","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ismail told me, Abdullah bin Saleh told me, Laith told me, Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Ali, on the authority of Khafaf bin Ima Al-Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said the following prayer in the morning prayer: “O God, curse the Banu Lahyan and Ar’al, and they are rebellious and disobedient, they disobeyed God and His Messenger, and be forgiving, may God forgive them. And he became Muslim, may God bless her."
"6514","It was narrated on the authority of Abu Basra, a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The God, Blessed and Almighty, has increased the number of prayers for you, so pray them between the evening prayer and the morning prayer, which is the Witr prayer. And he is Abu Nusra al-Ghaffari. He said: Abu Tamim, so I and Abu Dharr were sitting, so Abu Dharr took my hand, and we went to Abu Basra and found him at the door that At Amr's house, Abu Dharr said to him, O Abu Basra, you heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, God is Blessed and Most High. He added more prayer for you, so pray it between the evening prayer and the Witr prayer in the morning? He said: Yes"
"6515","Professor Abu Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, told me: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Basra bin Abi Basra Al-Ghafari, who said: I got married A virgin woman found her pregnant, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for the child, he is your slave. When she gives birth, flog her with a hundred lashes.” And she gets the dowry based on what was permissible from her private parts.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6515 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6516","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Abu Rahm, whose name is Kulthum ibn Husayn ibn Ubaid bin Khaled bin Muaysir bin Badr bin Ahmas bin Ghaffar, and it is also said that Kulthum bin Husayn bin Ubaid bin Khaled was appointed by the Messenger of God as his successor. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him upon Medina when he set out to conquer Mecca.”"
"6517","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Shuaib Al-Harrani told us, Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to conquer Mecca, he succeeded Abu Rahm Kulthum ibn Husayn al-Ghifari in charge of Medina.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6517 - True"
"6518","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told me in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told me, Muammar told me, about Al-Zuhri, my nephew Abu Rahm told me that he heard Abu Rahm Kulthum ibn Husayn, one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who They pledged their allegiance under the tree. He said: I went on a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the battle of Tabuk, and I marched one night with him while we were near the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made us drowsy and I woke up when my mount approached the mount of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I started up. I pushed my mount away from him until my eyes overtook me on some part of the road while we were at night, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The dearest of my family “I must leave behind me the immigrants from Quraysh and the Ansar, and Aslam and Ghafar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6518 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6519","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Hudhayfah bin Usayd bin Al-Aghwas bin Waqi’ah bin Haram bin Ghaffar, and it was said: Ibn Usayd bin Khalid bin Al-Aghwas, nicknamed Abu Sariha He moved from Medina to Kufa and died there.”"
"6520","Ismail bin Ali Al-Hatbi told me, Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Muaddeb told us, Ubaid bin Ishaq Al-Attar told us, Muhammad bin Al-Fadil told us, about Ash'ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysara, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Asid al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The wind will come in which God takes the soul of every believer, then the rising of the sun from the west. This is the sign that God mentioned.” Glory be to Him in His Book of Hadith"
"6521","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqiqi told me, Hamdan told me, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, Yahya bin Nasr bin Hajib told us, Abdullah bin Shubrumah, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Asid, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to offer two salted rams and slaughter them. One of them says: “O God, this is on the authority of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,” and he brings the other closer together and says: “O God, this is on the authority of my nation, who bears witness to your monotheism.” And I have the right to deliver the message.”"
"6522","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Attab bin Usayd bin Abi Al-Ais bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf, Umm Attab bin Usayd, and Khaled bin Usayd Zainab, daughter of Abu Amr bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams used the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to reproach Mecca, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. Ettab was his governor in Mecca, and Ettab bin Usayd died in Mecca in Jumada al-Akhir in the year thirteen.”"
"6523","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar Al-Qadi told us, Hussein bin Sa`id bin Hashim bin Sa`id, from Banu Qais bin Tha`labah. Yahya bin Sa`id bin Salim al-Qaddah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the night he approached Mecca on the battle Al-Fath: “Indeed, in Mecca there are four people from the Quraysh whom he keeps away from polytheism and desires for them to embrace Islam.” It was said: Who are they, O Messenger? God? He said: “Attab bin Usayd, Jubayr bin Mutim, Hakim bin Hazzam, and Suhail bin Amr.”"
"6524","Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Karazi told me, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Harami bin Hafs Al-Atki told us, Khaled bin Abi Uthman told us, about Ayoub bin Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Aqrab, said: I heard Attab bin Usayd, may God be pleased with him, while he was leaning his back. To the House of God, he says: “By God, I have not done well in this work of mine, which I have appointed as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except two knotted garments, and I covered them with two bags.” “My lord”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6524 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6525","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Khalid bin Nizar Al-Ayli told us, Muhammad bin Salih al-Tamar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Attab ibn Usayd, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said regarding the zakat on vineyards: “It is to be harvested just as palm trees are harvested, then the zakat on it is paid with raisins, just as the zakat on palm trees is paid with dates.”"
"6526","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “And among the allies of Banu Hashim other than the people of Badr Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, and Shaddad was an ancestor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had Salma bint Umays after whom he succeeded Hamza bin Abd. Al-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6527","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: He informed me Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Shaddad bin Al-Had, that a Bedouin man believed in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I will emigrate With you? So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recommended it to his companions, and when the Battle of Khaybar or Hunn took place, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took some sheep, so he divided He swore to him, and he gave his companions what he had sworn to him, and he looked after them. When he came, they pushed him to him, and he said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, distributed it to you. So he took it and brought it to him and said: O Muhammad, I did not follow you on this, but I followed you on the condition that He was shot here, and he pointed to his throat with an arrow, so I will die and enter Paradise. He said: “If you believe God, He will believe you.” They stayed for a short time, then they were denied. Fighting the enemy, he was brought carrying an arrow that had hit him wherever he pointed, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is it him?” They said: Yes, he said: “God spoke the truth, so He spoke the truth to him.” So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, shrouded him, then presented him and prayed over him, and among what appeared to be his prayers over him were: “Oh God, this is your servant who went out as a migratory in your cause and was killed as a martyr, so I am a witness against him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6527 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6528","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “Usama bin Zayd bin Haritha bin Sharahil bin Ka’b bin Abd al-Uzza bin Yazid bin Imru’ al-Qays al-Kalbi, may God bless him. And His Messenger” and he informed me of this lineage: Ahmad bin Yaqoub, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Shabab told us, and he added to it, and his mother, Umm Ayman, his servant. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “died in Medina at the end of the caliphate of Muawiyah when he was sixty years old, and his nickname was Abu Muhammad.”"
"6529","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Mu’la bin Mahdi al-Mawsili told us, Abu Awanah told us, On the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: Usama bin Zaid, may God be pleased with them, told me: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The most beloved of my family is those upon whom God has bestowed favors and upon whom I have bestowed blessings.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6529 - Omar bin Abi Maslamah is weak"
"6530","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan told us, Affan and Hajjaj told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Osama is the most beloved of people to me.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions Muslim, and they did not produce it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6530 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6531","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Qurrah bin Khalid told me, Muhammad bin Sirin said: During the reign of Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, the palm tree amounted to a thousand dirhams, so Usama bin Zaid went to the palm tree and tapped it. And he brought out her coals and fed them to his mother, and he said to him: What made you do this? And you see that the palm tree has reached a thousand, so he said: “My mother asked for it, and she does not ask me for anything that I am capable of unless I give it to her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6531 - The hadith contains transmission"
"6532","Ahmad bin Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Ja`far al-Hadrami told us, Sa`id bin Amr al-Ash’athi told us, Abu Bakr bin Shuaib bin Al-Ahhabab said: I heard our sheikhs say: The inscription on the ring of Usama bin Zayd was “Love of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6533","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about"
"6534","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Hussein bin Yazid Al-Tahan told us, Aidh bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, who said: “I was the buttocks of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him at Arafat."
"6535","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, Khaled al-Harrani told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Urayb, on the authority of Khallad bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I went to see Usama bin Zayd and he praised me in my face, saying: He made me feel comfortable. I praise you to your face. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If a believer is praised to his face, then there is faith in his heart.”"
"6536","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, he said: “Abu Rafi’ was a client of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib. When Al-Abbas converted to Islam, may God be pleased with him, he gave it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his name was He converted to Islam, and it is said that Ibrahim converted to Islam before Badr, but he was residing in Mecca with Abbas, and he died after killing Uthman in the year thirty-five.”"
"6537","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told me, Ahmed bin Najda told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Abdul Hamid told us, we told him Qais bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Khaled, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, Ali’s servant, on the authority of Abu Rafi’ May God be pleased with him. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Ali, may God be pleased with him, to Yemen, and he held a banner for him. When he departed, he said: “O Abu Rafi’, follow him and do not let him behind him, and let him stand and not turn around until I come to him.” So he came to him and instructed him to do some things, and he said: “O Ali, because May God guide you to a man who is better for you than anything the sun has risen upon.”"
"6538","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, that Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told him, that Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’ told him, that Abu Rafi’ told him He received a letter from the Quraysh to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: When I delivered the letter, Islam was placed in my heart, and I said: Oh Messenger of God, by God, I will never return to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will not be dishonest in my covenant, nor will I be afraid of the cold. But go back to them, and if what is in your heart now is in your heart, then go back.” He said: So I returned to them, then I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said hello and I said hello
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6538 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6539","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: And Salman Al-Farisi He was nicknamed Abu Abdullah. His loyalty was to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Salman is from among us, the People of the House.”"
"6540","Ahmed bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Shihab told us, he said: “Salman Al-Farisi died in the year thirty-seven.”"
"6541","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, and Ismail bin Abi Uwais, they said: Ibn Abi Fudaik narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He line the trench in the year of the war of the parties until he reached Al-Madhahij, so he cut forty cubits for every ten, so the immigrants protested, Salman of us, and she said Al-Ansar: Salman is from us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Salman is from us, the People of the House.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6541 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"6542","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Mu’la bin Mahdi al-Mawsili told us, Imran bin Khalid told us Al-Khuza’i Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: Salman Al-Farisi entered upon Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them both, while he was leaning on A pillow and he threw it to him, and Salman said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Omar said: Tell us, O Abu Abdullah. He said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was leaning on a pillow. He threw it to me and then said to me: “O Salman, no Muslim enters upon his Muslim brother and throws something to him.” A pillow out of his honor unless God forgives him.”"
"6543",""
"6544","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Jallab told us, saying: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Quddus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Al-Muttab, Abu Tufail told me, Salman Al-Farisi told me, He said: I was a man from the people of Ji, and the people of my village worshiped mule horses, so I knew that they were not upon anything, so I was told: The religion What you are looking for is in Morocco. So I went out until I came to Mosul. I asked about the best people there, and was directed to a man in a hermitage. So I came to him and said to him: I am a man from the people of Ji and I have come to ask for work and to learn knowledge, so bring me to you and I will serve you and be your companion. And teach me something of what God has taught you. He said: Yes, so I accompanied him and he applied to me the same thing that was done to him, and he used to apply vinegar and oil to him. And the pills. I did not stay with him until death befell him, and I sat at his head crying for him. He said: What makes you cry? So I said: I cry because I left my country seeking goodness, and God blessed me with your company, and you taught me, and you treated me well, but then death befell you, and I do not know. Where do I go? He said: I have a brother on the island in such-and-such a place, and he is upon the truth, so come to him and extend my greetings to him.And tell him that I advised him and I advised you to keep him company. When the man was arrested, I went out and went to the man who described him to me and told him. With the news, and I read him greetings from his friend and told him that he had died and he ordered me to accompany him, so he included me with him and dealt with me as he used to do. Ali was with the other, and I accompanied him as long as God willed, and then death befell him. When death befell him, I sat by his head crying, and he said to me: What makes you cry? I said: I left my country in search of goodness, and God blessed me with the company of so-and-so, and he was a good companion to me, taught me, and advised me of you upon his death, and he revealed Death awaits you, and I do not know where to go. He said: You come to a brother of mine on the path of the Romans, for he is on the right path, so come to him and extend my greetings to him and accompany him."
"6545","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Saeed bin Muhammad told us. Al-Warraq, on the authority of Musa Al-Juhani, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.” And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The people who are longest satisfied in this world are the ones who are most “Hunger on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a strange hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"6546","Abd Al-Baqi bin Qani’ Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Muaddeb told us, Ubaid bin Ishaq Al-Attar told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim Al-Rummani, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: “O Messenger of God, I read in the Torah the blessing of food and ablution “Before and after”"
"6547","Da'laj bin Ahmad al-Sijzi told me, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ali al-Abar told us, Muhammad bin Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani told us, al-Walid told us Bin Muslim, Muhammad bin Hamza bin Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: When God, Blessed and Most High, wanted to guide Zayd ibn Sa’nah, Zayd ibn Sa’nah said: There is nothing among the signs of prophecy that did not I recognized it in the face of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I looked at him, except for two things that I did not tell about him. Does his dream precede his ignorance and does not increase it? “The severity of ignorance is for him, except for a dream,” so I used to be kind to him by mingling with him and learning his dream from his ignorance. Zayd bin Sa’nah said, so the Messenger of God came out One day, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was from the chambers, and with him was Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and a man came to him on his mount like a Bedouin, and he said: O Messenger of God, Busra, a village of the Banu So-and-so, have embraced Islam and entered into Islam, and I told them that if they embraced Islam, provision would come to them in abundance, and it would A year of hardship and drought has befallen them, and I fear, O Messenger of God, that they will leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed.So if you decide to send them something to help them with, then you will do so. A man looked at me and next to him I saw Ali, may God be pleased with him, and he said: Oh. Messenger of God, nothing remained of it. Zayd ibn Sa`nah said: So I approached him and said: O Muhammad, can you sell me known dates from the wall of Bani? So-and-so for such-and-such a term, and he said: “No, Jew, but I will sell you a known date for such-and-such a term, and I will not name my son’s family.” “So-and-so” and I said: Yes, so he pledged allegiance to me, so I let go and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for a specified date for such-and-such and such-and-such a term. So the man gave it to her and said: Be fair to them and help them with it. Zayd bin Sa’na said: When it was two or three days before the deadline, I came to him, took the girdles of his shirt and robe, looked at him with a harsh face, and said to him: O Muhammad, will you not give me my rights, for by God there is no You are aware, O Banu Abdul Muttalib, that bad judgment is often overlooked, and I had knowledge through your interactions with you, and I looked at Omar and saw that his eyes were darting around... His face was like a round sphere, then he looked at me,He said: O enemy of God, do you tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what I hear and do with it what I see? And by the One who sent him with the truth, had I not been careful? I would have struck your head with my sword while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was looking at Omar calmly and calmly and smiling, then he said: “O Omar, he and I We were in need of something other than this, that you command me to perform well, and order him to follow well. Go with him, O Omar, and give him his due, and increase it. “Twenty saa’ of dates.” So I said: “What is this increase, O Omar?” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to give you some place.” I cursed you. I said: Do you know me, O Omar? He said: No, who are you? I said: Zayd ibn Sa`na. He said: Al-Habir. I said: Al-Habir. He said: So what made you do what you did to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what you said to him? Did you say? I said to him: O Omar, he did not have any of the signs of prophethood that I recognized in the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I looked at him. Except for two things I did not tell about him: “Does his forbearance precede his ignorance?And the severity of his ignorance only adds to him a dream.” I have tested them both, and I bear you as witness, O Umar, that I have accepted God as my Lord and Islam as my religion. And Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is a prophet, and I bear witness to you that half of my wealth - for I have the most wealth among them - is a charity for the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said Omar, may God be pleased with him: Or against some of them, for you cannot help them. I said: Or against some of them. Then Zaid returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Zaid said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is his servant and messenger, and he believed in him, believed him, pledged allegiance to him, and testified with him. Many scenes, then Zaid died in the Battle of Tabuk, advancing without retreating, and may God have mercy on Zaid, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it while he was From the deceptions of the hadith, and Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sirri Al-Asqalani is trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6547 - What he denies and rejects"
"6548","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani informed us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he informed us Ali bin Abdul Aziz, they said: Abu Nu’aym told us, Hashraj bin Nabatah told us, he said: I asked Safina about his name, and he said: “I will inform you.” In my name, my name was Qais, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me Safina. I said: Why did he name you Safina? He said: He went out with his companions, and their luggage was heavy on them, so he said: Spread your cloak. So I spread it out and he put their luggage in it, then he carried it on me and said: “Load, you are nothing but a vessel.” He said: “If I had carried a camel’s calf that day, or two, or five, or six, it would not have been heavy on me.” “Sahih.” The chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6548 - True"
"6549","And Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us the name of the ship of Abu Al-Abbas, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ismail bin Maslama bin Qa'nab, on the authority of his father, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hafs Saeed bin Juman, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman's ship, he said: “Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, freed me, and she stipulated that I serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as he lives.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6549 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6550","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me, that Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Uthman told him, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, that Safina, the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ I sailed on the sea, and my ship that I was in was broken, so I mounted one of its planks, and the plank cast me into a thicket wherein was a lion, and it came up to me. He wanted me, so I said: O Abu Al-Harith, I am the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He lowered his head and came to me and pushed me with his shoulder. Until he brought me out of the thicket and put me on the road and hummed, so I thought he was bidding me farewell, and that was my last covenant with him.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6550 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6551","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “In Naming the Muslims who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Aqaba from among the Ansar, from Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj bin Al-Harith Saad Ibn al-Rabi’, who is a captain and witnessed Badr.”"
"6552","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin al-Mundhir told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, “In naming those of the Ansar who were martyred on the Day of Uhud from the Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, Saad bin Al-Rabi’.”"
"6553","Musa bin Ismail bin Al-Qadi told us, my father told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubairi told us, Ismail bin Qays told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Narrated by Ibn Zayd Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Umm Sa’d bint Sa’d Ibn al-Rabi’, that she went to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and he threw his garment to her until I sat on it, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, came in and said: O successor of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who is this? He said: “This is the daughter of someone better than me and you.” He said: And who is better than me and you except the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Abu Bakr said: “A man who was arrested during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his seat in Paradise, and you and I remained.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6553 - Rather, Ismail is weak"
"6554","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told us. Al-Humaidi, Abdul Rahman bin Ammar bin Saad Al-Qardh, the muezzin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He commanded Bilal to insert his finger into his ear and said: ‘Indeed, your voice is louder,’” and Bilal’s call to prayer was two by two. His iqama was single, and the prayer was performed once in a while, and he used to call the call to prayer on Friday during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he was Fa’i is like a trap, and when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would go out to the two Eids, he would go to the house of Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, then on the people of the pavilions, then he begins to pray before the sermon, then he says “Allahu Akbar” in the first seven times before the recitation, and in the afterlife Five times before the recitation, then he addressed the people, then he left the other way, from the path of Banu Zurayk, and slaughtered a sacrifice at the edge of the wafer in his hand with a razor. Then he went out to the house of Ammar bin Yasser and the house of Abu Hurairah in the court, and he used to go out to the two Eids walking and return walking, and he used to say “Allahu Akbar” between He multiplied the sermon and used to say “Allahu Akbar” in the sermon and deliver the sermon on a stick.” And when Bilal used to say “Allahu Akbar” with the call to prayer, he would face the Qiblah, then He says: God is great, God is great, I bear witness that there is no god but God twice, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God twice, and he faces the Qiblah. Then he turns away from the qiblah and says: Hail to the prayer twice, then he turns away from the left of the qiblah and says: Hail to the farmer twice, then He faces the Qiblah and says: “God is great, God is great, there is no god but God.”"
"6555","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us, Ibn Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Musfa told us, Baqiyya, Al-Zubaidi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hafs bin Omar bin Saad Al-Qardh, that his father and his paternal uncles told him that Saad Al-Qardh was A muezzin to the people of Quba, then Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, moved him and made him a muezzin for the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6555 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6556","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Jannadah ibn Abi Umayyah ibn Nizar ibn Ka’b bin Al-Harith bin Ka’b bin Abdullah bin Malik bin Nasr Al-Azdi died in the year eighty.”"
"6557","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Hudhafa Al-Azdi, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a group of Azd on Friday, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invited us to He had food in his hands. We said: We are fasting. He said: Did you fast yesterday? We said: No. He said: “Will you fast tomorrow?” We said: No. He said: Then break your fast. Then he said: “Do not fast on Friday alone.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6557 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6558","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, dictating to us Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqqi told us, Othman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Waqqasi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi said: While Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was sitting in the mosque when a man passed at the back of the mosque and said: A man: O Commander of the Faithful, do you know this passerby? He said: No, so who is he? He said: Sawad bin Qarib, and he is a man from the people of Yemen from a family in which there is honor and position, and he is the one whose vision came to him with the appearance of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so Omar said to me about him, so he was called by him, and he said: You are Sawad bin Qarib. He said: Yes, he said: You are the one whose opinion came to you with the appearance of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. He said: You are as you used to be of priesthood. He became very angry and said: O Prince. Believers, no one has greeted me with this since I converted to Islam. Omar said: O Glory be to God, by God, the polytheism we were upon is greater than what you were upon. From your soothsaying, he informed me that you had brought your opinion regarding the appearance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful, I am there. One night between sleeping and being awake, a visionary came to me and struck me with his foot.And he said, “Arise, O Sawad bin Qarib, and understand and reason if you understand. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent from Luay bin Ghalib He calls to God and to His worship, then he proceeds to say:
 [Fast Sea]
 I marveled at the jinn and their spying... and how the misery tugged at them with their senses.
 She descends to Mecca seeking guidance... How good are the jinn as their impurities.
 So go to the elite of Hashem... and raise the name with your eyes to its head.
 He said: I did not raise my head when he said that and said, “Let me sleep, for I was sleepy in the evening. When the second night came, he came to me and hit me.” with his foot and said, “Did I not say, ‘O Sawad bin Qarib, arise, understand and understand?’” If you understand, the Messenger of God sent Luay bin Ghalib calling to God and to worshiping Him, then he created the genie, saying:
 I marveled at the jinn and their pursuit... and the darkness tightened them with their wings.
 You descend to Mecca seeking guidance... No jinn is as truthful as its liars.
 So go to the elite of Hashem... between its narratives and its veil,
 He said: I did not raise my head, so when the third night had come, he came to me and hit me with his foot and said: Did I not tell you, Sawad bin Qarib, understand? And understand, if you can understand, that the Messenger of God was sent by Luay bin Ghalib to call to God and to His worship, and then he established, saying:
 I marveled at the jinn and their news...And Al-Easa bound it with its ropes
 You descend to Mecca seeking guidance... The believers of the jinn are not like their disbelievers.
 So go to the elite of Hashem... not before her like her tails,
 He said: Then I fell in love with Islam and desired it, so when I got up in the morning, I packed on my mount and set off, heading for Mecca. When I was Somehow, I was informed that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had migrated to Medina. So I came to Medina and asked about the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I was told: In the mosque. I reached the mosque, tied my camel and entered, and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people around him, so I said: Listen. My article, O Messenger of God. Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: Come closer to him, and he continued until I was in his hands. He said: Come and tell me. By following your opinion, he said:
 [Long Sea]
 A rescuer came to me after I had calmed down... and it was not while I had been afflicted with a liar.
 Three nights, he said, every night... The Messenger of God came to you from Luay bin Ghalib
 So I rolled up the hem of my garment and placed...the fox and forehead between my fingers.
 So I bear witness that there is no Lord other than Him...and that you are secure over every conqueror.
 And you are the closest of the messengers as a means to God, O son of the most generous, the best of the best.
 So tell us what comes to you, O best of those who walk...And if the gray hairs came,
 And be my intercessor on the Day when there is no one to intercede... except you with Mughni, on the authority of Sawad bin Qarib.”
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions rejoiced so much over my conversion to Islam that it was seen on their faces. He said: Then Omar jumped up and stuck to him and said: I would love to hear this from you
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6558 - The chain of transmission is interrupted"
"6559","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Salman bin Amer bin Aws bin Amr bin Hujr bin Amr bin Al-Harith bin Taim bin Dhuhal bin Malik bin Bakr bin Saad bin Dabbah settled in Basra and had a house in Hazrat Al-Jami Mosque, where he died during the Caliphate of Uthman, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6560","Abu Asim told us, Abu Naama Al-Adawi Amr bin Issa told us, Bashir bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Salman bin Amer Al-Dhabi, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my father used to uphold ties of kinship, honor guests, and fulfill his obligation, but he did not realize Islam, does he have any reward for that? He said: “No.” When I took over, he said: “I have to go to the old man.” So he said to me: “It will be after you. They will never be humiliated, they will never be disgraced, and they will never be poor.” ""Never"""
"6561","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Muammar bin al-Muthanna told us, he said: “Sa`sa`ah bin Najiya bin Aqal bin Muhammad bin Sufyan bin Mujashi bin Darim, the grandfather of Al-Farzadq bin Ghalib, a delegation to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6562","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Ghallabi told us, Al-Ala’ bin Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Malik bin Abu Swayya Al-Manqari, Ubadah bin Kurayb told us, Al-Tufayl bin Omar Al-Rubi’i told me, on the authority of Sa’saa bin Najiya Al-Mujashi’i, and he is a grandfather Al-Farzadq bin Ghalib said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he proposed to me Islam, so I converted to Islam and he taught me verses from the Qur’an, so I said: Oh Messenger of God, I did deeds during the pre-Islamic era. Will I have a reward for them? He said: “And I did not do them.” So I said: Two she-camels of my companions have gone astray, so I went out. I followed them on a camel of mine, and two houses were raised for me in a clearing of the earth. I went to them and found in one of them an old old man, and I said: Have you felt that? Two she-camels, so I called them and said: Miqsam bin Darim, we have captured your two she-camels and sold them, and God has blessed the people of two families with them. Your people are Arabs from Mudar. While he was speaking to me, a woman from the other house called to him: “She has given birth. She has given birth.” He said: “And she has not given birth, if that.” A boy, as we have become a partner among our people. And if it is a slave girl, bury her. The slave woman said, so I said: What is this newborn? He said: A daughter of mine, so I said: I will buy her from you. He said: O brother of Banu Tamim, I will sell your daughter, and I am an Arab man from Mudar, so I said: I I do not buy her neck from you, but rather I buy her soul from you, lest you kill her. He said: What will you buy her for? I said: For these two she-camels. And their son. He said: And you will add to me this camel of yours. I said: Yes, provided that you send a messenger with me. When I reach my family, I will return the camel to him. When he was in Some night I thought to myself that this is a place where none of the Arabs had preceded me, and Islam appeared and I was greeted by three hundred people."
"6563","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Abdullah bin Harb Al-Laythi told us, Ibrahim bin Asaad narrated to me, Aqal bin Shibah bin Aqal bin Sa’saa bin Najiya Al-Mujashi’i told me, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of His father, Sa'sa'ah bin Najiya, said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, perhaps the surplus has been given to me. I hid it for the far-flung and wayfarer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your mother and father, your sister and your brother, the lowest of the two of you.”"
"6564","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: Qais bin Asim bin Sinan bin Khalid bin Munqar bin Ubaid bin Muqais bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Saad bin Zayd Manat bin Tamim, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “This is the master of the people of piety.”"
"6565","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Asadi, al-Hafiz Hamdan, told us, Muhammad ibn Zakaria al-Ghallabi told us, Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Swayya Al-Manqari, Abi Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Malik told me, on the authority of his father, Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suwayya Al-Manqari, he said: I witnessed Qais bin Asim when he died as he was leaving his will, and he gathered his sons, who were thirty-two males, and he said: O my son, then I am dead, so prevail upon the eldest among you and succeed your fathers, and do not prevail over the youngest of you, lest that be disgraced by you in the eyes of your equals, and do not rise up to mourn over me, for I I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “he forbade wailing,” and you must put the money in order, for it is a reminder to the generous person and it dispenses with it. mean, and do not give the necks of camels to others than they are entitled to, and do not deprive them of their right, and beware of every evil race, for no matter how much it pleases you one day, it will not Your evil is greater, and beware of the sons of your enemies, for they are your enemies in the manner of their fathers. And when I die, bury me in a place He is looking at this neighborhood from Bakr bin Wael, for there were disputes between me and them during pre-Islamic times, so I fear that they will dig me up from my grave. So spoil their worldly life for them and spoil your hereafter for you. Then he called his kinan and ordered his eldest son, and his name was Ali, and he said: He took out an arrow from my quiver, so he took it out and said: Break it. He broke it, then he said: Take out two arrows, so he took them out and said: Break them. So he broke them, but he was not able to break them, so he said, “My sons, this is how you are when gathered together, and so are you in a group.” Then he set out, He says:
 [light sea]

 Glory is only what the father of truth built... and its creator brought to life the newborn.
 Glory, courage, and dream are enough... if they are adorned with chastity and presence.
 And thirty, my sons, if you... make appointments with the female representatives of the covenants.
 Thirty cups of mug, if... a heavy knot stretches it for a long period of time.
 It was not broken, even if the shares were divided... putting them together would result in dissipation.
 Those of age and skill are better... even if there are among you, they will have
 And you must memorize the minor ones until... the minor breaking of the vow reaches the level of effort.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6565 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6566","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Wasiti told us, Ziyad told us Al-Jassass, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Qays bin Asim Al-Manqari, may God be pleased with him, told me: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he saw me I heard him say: “This is the master of the people of Al-Wabar.” When I got down, I went to him and started talking to him, and I said: O Messenger of God, what is the wealth that I do not have? Is there a burden from a guest who has welcomed me and a large family? So he said: “What a good wealth the forty had, and even more so the sixty, and woe to the owners of the hundred, except for the one who gave in its messengers and in its generosity, and became poorer.” Its back, and feed the contented one, and the one who is free.” I said: O Prophet of God, how honorable and good are these manners. O Prophet of God, they are not permissible. In the valley in which I am with an abundance of camels, he said: So what do you do? I said: You can outnumber camels and outnumber people. Whoever wants can take the head of a camel and take it away, and say: “What do you do with the poor parts of its back?” I said: I do not impoverish the young nor the neglected one. He said: “Then your wealth is more beloved to you or the wealth of your masters.” I said: My wealth is more beloved to me than the wealth of my masters. He said: “Then yours is yours, whatever you eat and use, or wear and use, or give and carry on, otherwise it belongs to your masters.” So I said: By God, if I stay Al-Hasan said: So he did, by God. When Qays’s death approached, he advised his sons. He said: Beware of the question, for it will be the last. A person’s earning is that no one asks except that he abandons his earning."
"6567","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq al-Usayli told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Abi Ubaida Muammar bin Al-Muthanna said: “Amr bin Al-Ahtam bin Sumayy bin Sinan bin Khaled bin Munqar bin Ubaid bin Muqais bin Amr Ibn Ka'b Ibn Sa'd Ibn Zayd Manat Ibn Tamim, whose name is Al-Ahtam, Sinan, whose folds will be torn on the Day of Killing."
"6568","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ubaidah Al-Wabari told us, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Idris al-Muqali told us, they said: Ali bin Harb al-Mawsili told us, Abu Saad told us Al-Haytham bin Mahfouz, on the authority of Abu Al-Muqawam Al-Ansari, Yahya bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utbah, on the authority of Muqassam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, May God be pleased with them both. He said: Qais bin Asim, Al-Zabarqan bin Badr, and Amr bin Al-Ahtim Al-Tamimi sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Al-Zabarqan became proud and said: O Messenger of God, I am the master of Tamim, and the one who is obeyed among them and the one who is answered in their regard. I will protect them from injustice and I will take for them. With their rights, and this one knows that, meaning Amr bin Al-Ahtam, and he said: Amr bin Al-Ahtam: By God, O Messenger of God, he is very disobedient. He is obstructed by his side, obeyed in his club. Al-Zabarqan said: By God, O Messenger of God, he learned from me other than what he said, and what prevented him from speaking about it. Except envy. Amr said: I envy you. By God, you are mean to your uncle, greedy of money, foolish of birth, and wasteful in your family. By God, oh Messenger of God, you were truthful in what you said at the beginning, and you did not lie in what you said last, but I am a man. I was satisfied and said the best of what I knew, and I was angry and said the ugliest. I did not find anything, and by God, you were correct in both matters. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, part of the statement is magic. “For magic.” It was narrated on the authority of Abu Bakra Al-Ansari that he attended this council."
"6569","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Ali Al-Farisi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulayman Al-Qusayti told us, Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman bin Jawshan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a delegation from the Banu Tamim included Qais bin Asim, Amr bin Al-Ahtam, and Al-Zabarqan bin Badr. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Amr bin Al-Ahtam: What It says about Al-Zabarqan bin Badr. He said: O Messenger of God, he is obedient to his caller, very disobedient, and refrains from doing what is behind his back. Al-Zabarqan said: O Messenger of God, by God, he knew more from me than what he described me, but he envied me. Amr said: By God, O Messenger of God, he is remorseful. Chivalry, narrow-minded, mean-spirited, foolish of birth, and by God, you did not lie at first, and you told the truth at the end, but I was satisfied and said what is best. I knew, and I became angry, so I said, “The ugliest thing I have ever known.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, some of the rhetoric is magic, and some of poetry is wisdom.”"
"6570","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin al-Muthanna told us, he said: “Sa’sa’a bin Muawiyah bin Husayn bin Umair bin Ubadah bin Al-Nazzal bin Murrah bin Ubaid bin Muqais bin Amr bin Ka’b bin Saad Ibn Zayd Manat Ibn Tamim, uncle of Al-Ahnaf Ibn Qais.”"
"6571","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Hadba bin Khalid told us, Jarir told us Ibn Hazim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sa’sa’a ibn Muawiyah, the uncle of Al-Ahnaf, said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him reciting this. Verse: “{So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it} [Al-Zalzalah: 8] So I said: I don’t care if I don’t hear anything else. ""Suffice me, suffice me"""
"6572","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Ahnaf bin Qais bin Husayn bin Al-Nazzal bin Ubaidah is a veteran who followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and guided the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and said: “The name of Al-Ahnaf is Al-Dahhak, and it is also called Sakhr bin Qais bin Muawiyah bin Husayn. He was born with Ahnaf.” Then his mother said: By God, had it not been for the club in his leg, there would not have been a boy like him in the neighborhood, and he was the most formidable of the Arabs."
"6573","Tell us about the accuracy of what Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq mentioned, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Al-Ahnaf Ibn Qais said: I was circumambulating the Kaaba during the time of Uthman Ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, when a man from Banu Layth came and took my hand and said: Shall I not bring you good tidings? I said: Yes, so he said: Do you remember when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me? And he greeted your people, the Banu Sa’d, and I began to introduce Islam to them and invite them to it, and I said: You, you call to goodness and command With goodness, I conveyed that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O God, forgive Al-Ahnaf bin Qais.” Al-Ahnaf, may God be pleased with him, was He says: There is nothing I hope for in my work.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6573 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6574","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Al-Aswad bin Saree bin Himyar bin Ubadah ibn al-Nazzal ibn Murrah ibn Ubaidah had a house in Basra in the presence of the mosque, one of the following Banu Tamim. He died during the reign of Muawiyah, may God be pleased with him. about him"
"6575","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Abdullah bin Suwar told us, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told us Al-Muzani, narrated by Al-Hasan, said: Al-Aswad bin Saree’ said: O Messenger of God, should I not adjure you with praises with which I have praised my Lord, Blessed and Most High? So he said: “Indeed, your Lord, Blessed and Most High, loves praise, and He has not added anything to that.” It is an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6575 - True"
"6576","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz, in Kufa, told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman told us, Muammar bin Bakkar Al-Saadi told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Sari’ Al-Tamimi, he said: I came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Prophet of God, I recited a poem in which I praised God, Blessed and Most High, and I praised you. He said: “As for what you praised God? “Give it and whatever you have praised me with, leave it.” So I started singing it, and a tall, short-haired man came in and said to me: “Hold on.” When he left, he said: “Give it.” So I started to sing to him, but it was not long before he came back and said to me: Hold on. When he came out, he said: Bring me, so I said: Who is this, O Prophet of God, who, when he entered, said: Hold it and when he came out you said bring it? He said: “This is Omar Ibn Al-Khattab and he is not of falsehood in anything.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6576 - Muammar bin Bakkar has many evil deeds"
"6577","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Shabab told me, he said: “Jariyah ibn Qudamah ibn Zuhayr ibn Husayn ibn Rabah ibn Saad bin Yahya bin Rabi’ah bin Ka’b, nicknamed Abu Al-Walid and Abu Yazid. He has a house in Basra on the Bahariyya road.”"
"6578","Ali bin Ahmad bin Qarqoub Al-Tamar told us about Hamdan, Muhammad bin Muadh Al-Halabi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah Al-Qanabi told us, My father told me, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, on the authority of Jariyah ibn Qudamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said, Messenger of God, say something to me that will benefit me, and say something to me that I may understand it. So he said: “Do not get angry.” And he repeated it to me several times, saying: “Do not get angry.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6578 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6579","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubair, he said: When the people came for Hajj in the year nine, Urwa bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi, the uncle of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked permission to return to his people. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I fear that They will kill you.” He said: “If they find me sleeping, they will wake me up.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission, and he returned to his people as a Muslim, and he provided dinner. Then Thaqif came to him and called them to Islam, but they accused him, disobeyed him, and made him listen to what he did not expect, then they left him until when They had eaten dawn and dawn had come. Urwa stood up in his house and called for prayer and recited the tashahhud. Then a man from Thaqif shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The likeness of Urwa is like the companion of Yasin who called his people to God Almighty, and they killed him.”"
"6580","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Mujashi’ ibn Masoud ibn Tha’labah ibn Wahb ibn Aidh, nicknamed Abu Suleiman, and his mother and his brother’s mother was Mujalid Malika bint Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Labid bin Khuzaymah. Mujashi’ was killed on the day Al-Jamal Al-Asghar in the year thirty-six, and he was buried in his home in Bani Sulaym, Hazrat Bani Sudus. He had no other home in Basra, including his home in Hazrat Al-Jami Mosque »"
"6581","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah told us, Asim Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, Mujasha bin Masoud told us, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my brother Mujalid after the conquest, and I said: O Messenger By God, I have brought my brother Mujalid to you so that you may pledge allegiance to him on the emigration. He said: “The people of the emigration have gone with what is in it.” So I said: So, for what will you pledge allegiance to him, oh? The Messenger of God, he said: “I pledge my allegiance to him on Islam, faith, and jihad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6581 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6582","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Amr bin Abasa bin Aamir bin Khaled bin Ghadira bin Attab bin Imru’ al-Qais, his mother was Ramla bint al-Waqi’ah, from Banu Hizam, and he is the brother of Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, from his mother, a resident of the Levant, nicknamed Abu Yahya.”"
"6583","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Abdullah bin Al-Alaa bin Zuhr, that he heard Abu Salam Al-Aswad say: I heard Amr bin Absa, may God be pleased with him, saying: He prayed with us The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to a camel of spoils. When he greeted him, he took some hair from the camel’s side and said: “It is not permissible for me to do any of this.” “The spoils are like these, except for the fifth, and the fifth will be returned to you.”"
"6584","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told us, Muhammad bin Muhajir told us, Al-Abbas bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, may God be pleased with him, he said: I came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the first to be sent, and at that time he was in disdain. I said: Are you what you are? He said: “I am a prophet.” I said: What is a prophet? He said: “The Messenger of God.” I said: “God has sent you.” He said: “Yes.” I said: With what did he send you? He said: “By worshiping God, destroying idols, and maintaining ties of kinship.” I said: Well done, He sent you. Who followed you in this? He said: “Free and slave,” meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. Then Amr ibn Absa used to say: You saw me when I was a quarter of Islam, so I converted to Islam and then I said, “Should I follow you, O Messenger of God?” He said, “No, but pursue the land of your people, and when you appear, come to me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They go out
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6584 - True"
"6585","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Jabir bin Samra Al-Sawai’i was nicknamed Abu Khaled, and it is said that Abu Abdullah died during the rule of Bishr ibn Marwan.”"
"6586","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Yusuf bin Yaqoub, they said: Abu Rabi’ al-Zahrani told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of al-Mughirah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, may God be pleased with him, he said: I was With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: “The affairs of this nation will continue to prevail until twelve caliphs arise.” And he said a word. It was hidden from me, and my father was sitting closer to him than me, so I said: What did he say? He said: “They are all from Quraysh.” Jabir bin Samra narrated another hadith on the authority of his father."
"6587","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud Al-Shadhakuni told us, we told him Ismail bin Ubaid Allah bin Muhib, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, on the authority of his father Samurah bin Amr Al-Sawai’i, may God be pleased with him, he said: I asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: We are the people of a desert country and livestock, so should we perform ablution from sheep’s meat and milk? He said: “No.”"
"6588","Ahmed bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa told us, he said: “Abu Juhayfa Wahb bin Abdullah Al-Sawai’i died in the state of Bishr bin Marwan»"
"6589","Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Najda al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Yunus bin Abi Yafour told us, on the authority of Aun bin Abi Juhayfa, on the authority of his father, said: I was with my uncle with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “The affairs of my nation will continue to be sound until twelve caliphs pass away.” Then he said a word and lowered his voice, so I said to my uncle while he was in front of me: What did he say, uncle? He said: He said, my son: “They are all from Quraysh.”"
"6590","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas bin Kathir told us Bin Dahman bin Abdullah bin Hammam bin Aban bin Yasar bin Malik, nicknamed Abu Abdullah. He died in the year fifty.”"
"6591","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Hammam Al-Dallal told us, Saeed bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Taifi told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Iyad, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “commanded him to He will make the Taif Mosque where their tyrant was.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6591 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6592","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Amer Ibn Wathilah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Jahsh Ibn Hayyan Ibn Saad Ibn Laith was born in the year of Uhud and came of age from the life of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He remained in peace for eight years. He settled in Kufa, then resided in Mecca until he died. He was the last of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to die. He died in the year ""One hundred and two""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6592 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6593","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, Thabit ibn al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Juma’, My father told me, he said: Abu Tufayl said: “I lived eight years in the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was born in the year of Uhud.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6593 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6594","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Shabab al-Asfari told me, he said: “Abu al-Tufayl Aamir ibn Wathilah died in the year A hundred."
"6595","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ja’far bin Yahya told me, my uncle told me Amara bin Thawban, that Abu Tufayl told him, saying: I was a boy carrying a camel’s organ, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was dividing meat with a ji’ranah, and a woman came to him and he spread out his cloak for her.” So I said: Who is this? They said: His mother who breastfed him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6595 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6596","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Suraqa bin Malik bin Jasham From the Banu Mudlij Ibn Murrah Ibn Abd Manat Ibn Ali Ibn Kinanah.” Muhammad Ibn Umar said: Suraqa Ibn Malik lived recently and died in the year Twenty-four"
"6597","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abdullah bin Saleh, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Suraqa bin Malik bin Jasham, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said to him: “Oh Suraqa, shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise and the people of Hell?” So I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “As for the people of Hellfire, for every oppressor is arrogant and arrogant, but as for the people of Paradise, they are the weak and defeated.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6597 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6598","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, al-Hasan bin al-Abbas al-Muqri al-Razi told us, Sahl bin Othman al-Askari told us, Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ataba, on the authority of Idris Al-Awdi, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Maysara Al-Zarraad, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Suraqa Ibn Malik Ibn Jasham said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us at Batha’ and said: “Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the day of The Resurrection” Suraqa bin Malik is the brother of Ka’b bin Malik
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6598 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6599","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us that this was true, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh al-Sahmi told us, Hassan bin Ghalib told us, Ibn For a while, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his brother Suraqa bin Malik, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a lost woman who returns to his basin. Will he have a reward if Did he satisfy her? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In every freed liver there is a reward.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6599 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6600","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Al-Mughirah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his uncle Suraqa bin Malik that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “In every Hira’s liver there is a reward.”"
"6601","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Dirar bin Al-Azwar, and the name of Al-Azwar is Malik bin Aws bin Khuzaymah bin Rabi’ah bin Malik bin Tha’labah bin Dudan bin Usayd bin Khuzaymah bin Mudarika bin Ilyas bin Mudar lived in Kufa and died there.”"
"6602","Abd al-Baqi ibn Qa’i al-Hafiz told us, Hisham ibn Ali al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sa’id al-Athram told us, Salam Abu Al-Mundhir Al-Qaari told us, Asim bin Bahdala told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Dirar bin Al-Azwar, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him, so I said to him: Extend your hand and I pledge my allegiance to you on Islam. So I pledged allegiance to him, then I said:
 [The Converging Sea]

 I left off the cup and playing the qāyān...and wine as a prayer and supplication.
 And fill the ink in the depths... and burden the Muslims with fighting.
 O Lord, I will not deceive me in my sale... I have sold my family and my wealth in vain.
 Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How unfair your pledge of allegiance is, O Dirar.”"
"6603","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Dirar ibn al-Azwar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was milking, and he said: “Leave my supplicant milk
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6603 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6604","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Shabab Al-Asfari told us, he said: “Wabisa bin Ma’abad bin Qays bin Ka’b bin Fahd bin Munqidh bin Al-Harith bin Tha’labah bin Dudan bin Asad bin Khuzaymah went down to Kufa, then moved to the island and died there.”"
"6605","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hussein bin Abdullah Al-Raqi told us, Ali bin Ma’abad Al-Raqi told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, On the authority of Mubashir bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat, on the authority of Al-Fudayl bin Amr, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Wabisa bin Ma’abad May God be pleased with him. He said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Do not take the backs of animals as pulpits, and the worst of these animals is the mule.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6605 - A weak hadith"
"6606","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Shabab told me, he said: “Khuraym ibn Fatik ibn Lakhram ibn Shaddad ibn Amr lioness"
"6607","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sakouni told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Tasnim Al-Hadrami told us, Muhammad bin Khalifa Al-Asadi told us, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said one day to Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both: He narrated to me a hadith that I like. He said: Khurraym bin Fatik Al-Asadi narrated to me. He said: I went out with my camels and they were struck by lightning. So I hung it up and covered a camel’s arm with it, and that was two of the events of the emergence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then I said: I seek refuge in the greatness of this. Valley, he said: And this is what they used to do in the pre-Islamic era, so suddenly a phone called me, shouting about me and saying:
 [The sea of rage]

 Woe to you, seek refuge in God, the Majestic... the Revealer of the forbidden and the lawful.
 And unite God and do not care... What a terror is Dhu Al-Hazm?
 When they remembered God for miles around... and in the plains of the earth and the mountains.
 And the agent of truth is not a fool... except he is pious and does good deeds.
 He said: So I said:
 [The sea of rage]

 O you who call for something that is impossible... is it apparent to you that you are guided or misguided?
 He said:

 This is the Messenger of God, the owner of good deeds... He came with springs and rivers.
 In Surah after detail... forbidden and permissible.
 He enjoins fasting and prayer...and rebukes people from indignities.
 There were terrible things in those days
 He said: So I said: Who are you, may God have mercy on you? He said: I am Malik bin Malik. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me from the land of the people of Najdah. He said: So I said: If I had someone to suffice me with these camels, I would go to him until I believe in him. He said: I will suffice for them until I return them to your family. She was safe, God Almighty willing, so I captured a camel of hers, then I came to Medina and met the people on Friday while they were praying, and I said: Make up the prayer. Then I entered, and I was going to finish my mount when Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, came out and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says to you. He said: “Come in.” So I entered, and when he saw me, he said: What did the sheikh who guaranteed you that your camels would be delivered to your family safely? May your family be safe. I said, “May God have mercy on him.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “Yes, may God have mercy on him.” He said, “Khuraym, I bear witness that there is no god but God.” And his Islam was good
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6607 - It is not valid"
"6608","Abu al-Qasim al-Sakouni told us, Abu Ja`far al-Hadrami told us, Yahya bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Maan al-Saadi told us. Al-Masoudi, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiya, on the authority of Khuraym ibn Fatik, may God be pleased with him, that He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Khuraym bin Fatik, if it were not for two qualities in you, you would be the man. So he said: What is the matter with my father? Messenger of God? He said: “Grow your hair and let your garment loose.” So Khuraim went off and cut his hair and shortened his garment.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6608 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"6609","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Shabab Al-Asfari told us, he said: “Usama bin Umair bin Asim bin Ubaid Allah bin Hanif bin Yasar bin Najiya bin Amr bin Al-Harith bin Tabha bin Lahyan bin Hudhayl, who is Abu Abi Al-Malih, settled in Basra."
"6610","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Azhari told us, Ishaq bin Daoud Al-Sawwaf told us about a cover-up, Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamil Al-Aruqi told us, Abd told us Al-Wahhab bin Isa Al-Wasiti, Yahya bin Abi Zakaria Al-Ghassani told us, Maysarah bin Abi Al-Malih bin Usama told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, Osama bin Umair, said that he prayed two rak’ahs of Fajr with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he prayed close to him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs. Then he heard him say: “O God, Lord of Gabriel, Michael, Israfil, and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, I seek refuge in You from the Fire three times.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6610 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6611","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin al-Muthanna told us, he said: “My father The meat’s name is Abdullah bin Abdul Malik bin Abdullah bin Affan, and he was an honorable poet, and he witnessed the conquest of Hunayn, and Umair, his master, was with him.” Abu Ubaidah said: “He was named Abi Lahm because he refused to eat meat.”"
"6612","Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Shabab told us, and he mentioned this lineage and said: “Muhammad bin Omar used to eat meat.” The yellow ones were on three of the city, and Umair, his master, was camping with him.”"
"6613","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Hatem bin Ismail told us, Yazid bin Abi Ubaid told us, He said: I heard Umair, the master of my father’s meat, saying: My master commanded me to prepare meat for him, and a poor man came to me, so I fed him some of it, and he struck me. My lord, I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned it to him. He called him and said: Why did you hit him? He said: He feeds me my food without my ordering him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The reward is between you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6613 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6614","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Muhammad bin Zaid bin told us Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud, on the authority of Umair, Abi al-Lahm’s servant, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the oil stones, drawing water, raising water. ""His palms"""
"6615","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Amr bin Umayyah Bin Khuwailid bin Abdullah bin Iyas bin Ubaid bin Nashirah bin Ka'b bin Jadi bin Damrah bin Bakr bin Abd Manat bin ""Kenana"""
"6616","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hatim bin Ismail told us, Ya’qub bin Amr told us Ibn Abdullah Ibn Umayyah Al-Damri, on the authority of Ja’far Ibn Amr Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of his father Amr Ibn Umayyah Al-Damri, may God be pleased with him, that he He said: O Messenger of God, send my mount and put my trust. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, tie it and put my trust.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6616 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"6617","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Umayr bin Salamah bin Muntab bin Talha bin Jadi bin Damra"
"6618","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, and Ziyad bin Al-Khalil Al-Tustari told us, they said: Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us. Al-Hazami, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Issa bin Talha bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Umair bin Salama al-Dhamri, may God be pleased with him, said: While we were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was Ihram in some aspects of the spirit, since we were with a crippled donkey. So I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Leave him,” and his owner came to him. The one who sterilized him was a man from Bahz, and he said: O Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, what is your concern with this donkey? So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered He asked Abu Bakr to divide it among the companions, then he passed by, and when he was about to receive the reward, he passed by a gazelle standing in the shade of a tree that had an arrow in it, so the Prophet ordered “A man, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” called out that no one should take him, so the people ran out and left him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6618 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"6619","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abu Al-Ja'd al-Dhamri Amr bin Bakr bin Junada bin Murad bin Ka'b bin Damra»"
"6620","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah informed us, about Ubaidah bin Sufyan al-Hadrami said: I heard Abu al-Ja`d al-Dhamri saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever neglects Friday prayers... Three things that he neglected, God put a seal on his heart.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6620 - Hasan"
"6621","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: “Al-Saab bin Jathama bin Qais bin Abdullah bin Wahb bin Yamar bin Awf bin Ka’b bin Salma bin Laith, and Umm al-Saab Zainab bint Harb bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf, the sister of Abu Sufyan, and her name was Fakhta Bint Harb. He used to stay in Wadan.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6621 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6622","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Amr bin Dinar told me that Ibn Shihab told him, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was told that horses had raided at night and killed some of the sons of the polytheists. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They are from their fathers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6622 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6623","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr bin Rakha told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Omar bin Abi Bakr told us Al-Muamili, on the authority of Zakaria bin Issa Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: “Qabath bin Ashim bin Amir bin Al-Mulawh bin Yamar bin Awf bin Ka'b bin Amir bin Laith Al-Dhababi»"
"6624","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Al-Zubayr bin Musa told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwayrith said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan saying to al-Qabbath ibn Ashaym: O Qubath, you are the greatest mother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: “Rather, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is older than me, and I am older than him.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was born in the year of the elephant. And he prophesied on the head of forty elephants.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6624 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6625","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Amr bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Zurayq told us, Asbagh bin Abdul Aziz told us, my father told me Abd al-Aziz bin Asbagh bin Aban bin Suleiman, on the authority of his grandfather Aban, on the authority of his father Suleiman, who said: Qabbath bin Ashim’s conversion to Islam was that Some men from his people and other Arabs came to him and said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Muttalib has gone out calling for a religion other than Our religion, so Qabath stood until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he entered upon him, he said to him: “Sit down, O Qabath.” So Qabbath frowned, so the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Are you the one who said that if the women of Quraysh went out as much as possible, they would repel Muhammad and his companions?” Then Qabath said: By the One who sent you with the truth, my tongue did not speak it, nor did my lips purse it, nor did anyone hear it from me, and it is nothing but an obsession. In my soul, I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that you are His servant and Messenger, and that what you have brought is true."
"6626","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas Al-Faqih told us about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Saleh, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Yunus bin Saif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Qabath bin Ashim al-Laythi, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The prayer of two men, one of them being led by the other, is purer in the sight of God than the prayer of forty in succession. The prayer of four people, one of them leading a companion, is purer in the sight of God than the prayer of eighty people, and the prayer of eight, one of them leading a companion, is purer. In the sight of God Almighty, it is one hundred prayers repeated.”"
"6627","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, He said: “Umair bin Qatada bin Saad bin Amir bin Junda’ bin Laith Al-Laythi.”"
"6628","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Salamah al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Khunnis, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: There was an issue in my mind that made me sad that I did not ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not hear anyone asking him about it, so I was waiting for him, so one day I entered upon him while he was performing ablution, so I agreed with him. On two occasions I would have liked to agree with him. I found him calm and good-natured, so I said: O Messenger of God, do you permit me to ask you? He said: “Yes, ask whatever seems to you.” I said: “O Messenger of God, what is faith?” He said: “Gorgement and patience.” I said: Which of the believers has the best faith? He said: “The best of them in character.” I said: Which of the Muslims is the best in Islam? He said: “The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.” I said: Which jihad is better? He lowered his head and was silent for a long time until I was afraid that I had upset him, and I wished that I had not asked him when I had heard him yesterday. He says: “The greatest sin among Muslims is the one who asks about something that was not forbidden to them, so it was forbidden to them because of his asking for it.” So I said: I seek refuge in By God, because of the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, he raised his head and said: “How did you say?” I said: Which jihad is better? He said: “A word of justice from an unjust imam.” Abu Badr the narrator, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair. His name is Bashar bin Al-Hakam, a sheikh from Basra. It was narrated on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani without a hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6628 - Al-Hakim reported to him a weak hadith meaning this hadith"
"6629","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Shaddad bin Al-Had bin Amr bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Numayr bin Atwara bin Amer bin Laith bin Bakra, and the name of Hadi Osama, and he is Abu Abdullah bin Shaddad Ibn al-Hadi moved to Kufa."
"6630","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, so he mentioned this lineage and said that he was named The guide, because he was guided to the path."
"6631","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub, narrating on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is upon us in one of the daytime prayers, noon or afternoon, while he was carrying Al-Hasan or Al-Hussein, so he came forward and placed him at His right foot, “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated for a long time, so I raised my head among the people, and behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace prostrating, and behold, the boy was riding on his back. I sat down and prostrated. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, some people said: O Messenger of God, I have Did you prostrate in this prayer of yours a prostration that you had not previously prostrated? Is it something that you were commanded to do or that was revealed to you? He said: “No, it was not, but my son left me, and I hated to hasten him until he had fulfilled his need.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6631 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"6632","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: “Al-Harith Ibn al-Barasa is Al-Harith bin Malik bin Qais bin Uwaid bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Abd Manaf bin Ashja’ bin Amer bin Laith, and his mother Al-Barsa’ The daughter of Abdullah bin Rabi’ah Al-Hilaliyya. He stayed in Mecca and then went to Kufa."
"6633","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Zakaria bin told us. Abu Zaida, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik bin Al-Barsa’, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying The day of the conquest of Mecca: “Mecca will never be invaded after this year.” Sufyan said: I heard it from Zechariah, his interpretation of disbelief.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6633 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6634","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Malik bin Al-Huwaith bin Hashish bin Awf Bin Junda`, nicknamed Abu Sulayman, and some of the Banu Layth told me that he is Malik bin al-Huwayrith bin Ashim bin Zabalah bin Hashish bin Abd Yalil bin Nashib bin Ghayrah bin Saad bin Laith bin Bakr»"
"6635","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told us, Ubaid bin Aqeel Al-Muqri told us, Sulayman Abu Muhammad Al-Qaflani, on the authority of Asim Al-Jahdari, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, may God be pleased with him: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He recited it: “On that day, His punishment will not punish anyone, nor will it be bound.” [Al-Fajr: 26]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6635 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6636","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Fadalah bin Wahb bin Buhra bin Buhaira bin Malik bin Qais bin Amir bin Laith, his mother was the daughter of Kaysan bin Amir Al-Awari, and he was Abu Abdullah Fadalah bin Wahb moved to Basra."
"6637","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun Al-Wasiti told us, Khaled bin Abdul told us God, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Fadalah Al-Laythi, on the authority of his father, Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me, and it was while he taught me that he said: “Guard the prayers,” so I said: These are my hours. There are tasks in it, so give me a comprehensive command. If I do it, it will be sufficient for me. He said: “Preserve the two eras.” I said: What are the two eras? He said: “Prayer before sunrise and prayer before sunset.”"
"6638","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Mus’ab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Mus’ab Al-Habir is the son of Umair bin Ubaid bin Hashim bin Abdul Manaf bin Abdul Dar bin Qusayy is the reciter whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to The Ansar were reciting the Qur’an in Medina before the arrival of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and many people embraced Islam with him and he witnessed a full moon.”"
"6639","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, said: “The first of the immigrants to come to us was Mus’ab bin Umair, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6640","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Musa bin Ubaidah told us, on the authority of His brother Abdullah bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting In Quba, a group of people were with him, then Musab bin Umair stood up, wearing a cloak that barely concealed him, and the people turned their backs, so he came and greeted them, and they responded to him, so the Prophet said about him, “Pray.” May God bless him and grant him peace, and praised him, then he said: “I saw this man with his parents in Mecca, honoring him and giving him good deeds. Quraysh is like him, then he left that seeking the pleasure of God and the support of His Messenger. However, nothing will come upon you except such-and-such until Persians and the Romans will attack you, and one of you will go in the morning dressed and go out dressed, and he will have lunch for you with a bowl and rest for you with a bowl.” They said: Oh. Messenger of God, are we better today or that day? He said: “Rather, today you are better than that day. If only you knew of the world’s “I do not know that your souls will find rest from it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6640 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6641","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abu Salamah Abdullah bin Abdul-Assad bin Hilal bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzum bin Yaqtah bin Murrah bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fahr bin Malik, and he was one of the immigrants from Abyssinia. He migrated to Medina and witnessed Badr, and Umm Salamah was with him. Abu Salamah died in Shawwal of the year Four of the Hijra”"
"6642","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit told us Al-Bunani, Omar bin Abi Salamah bin Abdul-Assad told me, on the authority of his mother, Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that his father, Abu Salamah, may God be pleased with her On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: To God we belong and to Him we shall return, O God.” With you I consider my calamity.” And he mentioned the hadith in its length. This is a hadith that was narrated in the two Sahih books, but I narrated it because I did not find a safe hadith for my father on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated a hadith with a chain of transmission other than this.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6642 - Take it out"
"6643","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Suhail Ibn Bayda is Suhail bin Wahb bin Rabi’ah bin Hilal bin Ahab bin Dabbah bin Al-Harith bin Fahr bin Malik bin Al-Nadr. And his mother’s name is White, and her name is Da’ad bint Sa’id bin Sahm.”"
"6644","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, “In naming Whoever immigrated to the land of Abyssinia, the first migration before the emergence of Ja`far ibn Abi Talib, Suhail ibn Bayda, and in naming those who witnessed Badr came from Quraysh, then from Banu Al-Harith bin Fahr, Suhail bin Bayda.”"
"6645","Ali bin Issa told me, Ahmad bin Najdah told me, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Fulayh bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Salih bin Ajlan, and Muhammad bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God did not pray May God’s blessings and peace be upon Suhail Ibn Bayda, except in the mosque.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6645 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6646","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth told me, Yazid bin Abdullah told me Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Al-Salt, on the authority of Suhail Ibn Bayda, may God be pleased with him, who said: While the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Suhail Ibn Bayda, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and with him on a camel. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Suhail Ibn Bayda.” He raised his voice two or three times, and Suhail answered all of this. The people heard the voice of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they knew He wanted them, so the one who was in front of him sat down, and the one behind him followed him until when they gathered, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever bears witness “There is no god but God. God has forbidden him from Hell and made Paradise necessary for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6646 - Its chain of transmission is good and has a transmission"
"6647","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria al-Tustari told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Iyad ibn Zuhayr ibn Abi Shaddad ibn Rabia bin Hilal bin Wahib bin Dabbah bin Al Harith bin Fahr Al Fihri witnessed Badr, and died in the Levant in the year thirty.”"
"6648","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Abd Allah bin Hudhafa bin Qais bin Adi bin Saeed bin Sahm”"
"6649","Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Prophet sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Alqamah bin Mahrez was on a mission. When we reached the head of our raids, he gave permission for a group of the army and gave Abdullah bin command over them. Hudhafa bin Qais Al-Sahmi, who was from the people of Badr and had a sense of humor, as he used to ride the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Some of his travels to make him laugh, and the Romans had captured him during the time of Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, so they wanted him to commit disbelief, so he protected him. God Almighty even saved him, Blessed and Most High, from them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6649 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6650","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told us, Qurrah bin Abdul Rahman bin Huwail, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hudhafah Al-Sahmi, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me May God bless him and grant him peace, I announce to the people of Mina that no one should fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.”"
"6651","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Bayhaqi told us, they said: Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, he reported Hushaym, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Wael, that Abdullah bin Hudhafah bin Qais said: O Messenger of God, who is my father? He said: “Your father is a fool. The child is for the bed and the stone is for the whore.” He said: “If you had called me for an Ethiopian, I would have followed him.” His mother said to him: “You have exposed me.” He said: I liked to rest.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6651 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6652","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Burdah Hani ibn Nayyar ibn Amr ibn Ubaid ibn Kilab ibn Dahman ibn Ghanim ibn Dhubyan ibn Humaym ibn Kahil ibn Dahlah bin Bala bin Amr bin Al-Harith bin Al-Haf bin Quda’ah”"
"6653","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “In Naming the one who witnessed Badr, Abu Burdah ibn Nayyar."
"6654","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Utba Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Abdullah bin Musa told us, And Abu Ghassan said: Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I met my uncle Abu Burdah and he had a flag, so I said: Where do you want? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a man who had married his father’s wife.” After him, I will behead him and take his money.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6654 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6655","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “In mentioning Whoever witnessed Badr and Aqaba, Uwaim bin Sa`idah bin Aish bin Qays bin Qays bin Zayd bin Umayyah bin Zaid bin Malik from The Ansar, then from Banu Umayyah Ibn Zaid. It is said that he is an ally of Banu Amr Ibn Awf, and it was said that he is from among themselves."
"6656","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Muhammad bin Talha Al-Taymi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Salem told me. Bin Utba bin Uwaim bin Sa`idah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Uwaim bin Sa`idah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him And he said: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, chose me and chose companions for me, and made for me ministers, supporters, and in-laws among them. So whoever reviles them... The curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind will be upon him. On the Day of Resurrection, no act of negligence or justice will be accepted from him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. He takes him out
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6656 - True"
"6657","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubayr, Abu Lubaba Bashir bin Abdul-Mundhir and Al-Harith bin Hatib “went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and went out with him to Badr So he returned them, and appointed Abu Lubabah over the city, and shot them with two arrows along with the people of Badr.”"
"6658","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Al-Sa’ib bin Abi Lubaba, on the authority of his father, he said: When God turned to my father Lubaba, Abu Lubaba said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I am abandoning the home of my people in which I was afflicted. sin and give up all of my wealth as charity to God Almighty and to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Lubaba, a third is sufficient for you. He said: So I gave a third in charity.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6658 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6659","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Abu Habba Thabit bin Al-Numan bin Umayyah bin Tha’labah bin Amr bin Awf bin Malik bin Al-Aws, and he was martyred on Uhud.”"
"6660","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani, Al-Hafiz, told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin told us Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yusuf, the servant of Uthman, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, informing that he heard Abu Habbat al-Badri, he gives fatwas to the people that there is nothing wrong with a man throwing pebbles into stones. He said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Othman, so I mentioned that. To Abdullah bin Omar, he said: “Abu Hibbah spoke the truth, but Abu Hibbah was bad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6660 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6661","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, Yunus bin Yazid told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, Ibn Hazm told me that Ibn Abbas and Abu Hibbah Al-Ansari told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “He took me until I passed a level where I could hear the squeaking of pens.”"
"6662","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada'ah bin Sabra bin Sa'id bin Sa'd bin Sahm bin Amr bin Husays bin Ka'b bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fahr bin Malik converted to Islam on the day of the conquest.”"
"6663","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed me, my father informed me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Muammar informed me, about Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada’ah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “He prostrated in the star,” he said: So the people prostrated with him. Al-Muttalib said: And I did not prostrate with them on that day, and he was a polytheist on that day. Request: I will never let myself prostrate in it ever again.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6663 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6664","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Juzz bin Maadi Karib bin Amr bin Usaym bin Amr bin Uwaij bin Amr bin Zubaid died in the year eighty-six.”"
"6665","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Salih told us, Hassan bin Ghalib told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah. Amr bin Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Juzz’, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “He will be after me.” The rulers of temptations are at their doorsteps, like those who bless camels. They will not give anything to anyone unless they take from his religion the like of it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6665 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in Al-Talkhees, and Al-Dhahabi said in Al-Mizan, Al-Hakim said to him on the authority of Malik, fabricated hadiths"
"6666","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “The name Ibn Umm Maktum, may God be pleased with him, Amr bin Qais.”"
"6667","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Khaled bin Nizar told us, Omar bin Qais told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went around during his Hajj on his camel, Al-Jada’, and Abdullah Ibn A mute mother whose snout is beginning to tremble.”"
"6668","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah Ibn Umm Maktum, his mother is Umm Maktum, and her name is Atika bint Abdullah bin Ankatha bin Amir bin Makhzum, and he is Amr bin Qais bin Zaida bin Al-Asam bin Haram bin Rawaha bin Abd Muais bin Aamir bin Luay. What Musab said is difficult, so I came to him for it. By both names.”"
"6669","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with them, said: “The first of the immigrants to come was Musab bin Umair, then Amr bin Umm came to us after him.” The blind man is muffled.”"
"6670","Ja`far bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, may God Almighty have mercy on him, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Quddus bin Bakr bin Khunnis, narrated by Mas’ar, on the authority of Abul-Balad, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I went to see Aisha and she had a mother’s son who was concealed, and she was cutting pieces for him. He ate the citron with honey, and she said: “This has been his from the family of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ever since God blamed his Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about it. The Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, only wanted the revelation of Surat ‘Abs and turned away."
"6671","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, they said: Abu Musa, Ahmad bin Bashir Al-Hamdani told us, Abu Al-Bilad told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, he said: I entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her. There was a blind man with her, and she was cutting the citron for him and feeding it with honey. So I said: Who is this, O Mother of the Believers? She said: “This is Ibn Umm Maktum, who God Almighty blamed his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” She said: “He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Ibn Umm Maktoum, who had a gray hair, greeted him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them, and Abs descended and turned away until he came to him. “The blind man is the son of Umm Maktum.”"
"6672","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told me about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad al-Khazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman al-Razi told us, Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktum, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out on a In the morning, he said: “Fire has been kindled for the people of Hell, and temptations have come like pieces of a dark night. If you knew what I know, you would have laughed a little and cried.” ""a lot"""
"6673","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shairi told us, Muhammad bin Asim Al-Adl told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Amr ibn Umm Maktum, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I An old man who is blind and whose house is vast, and I have no guide to suit me, and between me and the mosque there are trees and rivers. Do I have any excuse to pray in Betty, he said, “Do you hear the call?” I said: Yes. He said: “Then bring it.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: I do not know anyone. He said: In this chain of transmission, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zurr other than Ibrahim bin Tahman, and it was narrated by Zaida, Shayban the grammarian, Hammad bin Salamah, Abu Awanah and others, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin Other than Ibn Umm Maktum, as for the hadith of Zaydah"
"6674","So Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, and Amma, the hadith of Shayban."
"6675","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Asheeb told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, As for the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah"
"6676","So Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Awanah told us, and Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin"
"6677","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Al-Hadrami Abu Al-Ala’ His name is Abdullah bin Abbad bin Akbar bin Rabia bin Malik bin Arif bin Malik bin Al-Khazraj bin Iyad bin Al-Sadaf bin Hadramaut Ibn Kindah Al-Ala’ died on his return from Bahrain in the year twenty-one.”"
"6678","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Abdan told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Azdi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Hayyan Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me in the two mixtures to be One of them is a Muslim and the other is a polytheist, to take a tithe from the Muslim, and from the polytheist the poll tax.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6678 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6679","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, “He wrote to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began with himself.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6679 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6680","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Abdullah Ibn Jahsh Ibn Rabab Ibn Ya`mar Ibn Sabra Ibn Kabir Ibn Ghanam Ibn Dudan Ibn Asad Ibn Khuzaymah, and his mother Umaymah Ibn Abd Al-Muttalib is the paternal aunt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6681","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “And Abdullah bin Jahsh He mentioned this lineage in naming one of the Muslims who witnessed Badr, and added that he was an ally of the Banu Umayyad ibn Abd Shams."
"6682","Abu Ja`far Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, “In Naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Banu Umayyad. Abdullah bin Jahsh is an ally of them and he is from the Banu Umayyad. Asad bin Khuzaymah"
"6683","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Zakaria told me, Shabab told us, he said: “Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh bin Rabab bin Yamar I found him bin Sabra bin Kabir bin Ghanam bin Dudan bin Asad bin Khuzaimah bin Mudarika bin Ilyas bin Mudar, an ally of the Umayyads. His father’s mother was Umaima bint Abdul Muttalib, the aunt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his paternal aunt was Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6684","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Abi told us Kathir, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman informed me, Abu Kathir, the servant of Muhammad bin Abdan bin Jahsh, informed me on the authority of his master Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he passed by Muammar, and he was sitting at his house in the market with his thighs exposed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cover your thigh, O Muammar, for the thigh is private.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6684 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6685","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “And Yazid bin Abdullah Bin Saad bin Al-Aswad bin Thumama bin Yaqzan bin Al-Harith bin Amr bin Muawiyah bin Al-Harith, an ally of Banu Mu’aqib, and he was The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to go to Al-Yamamah.”"
"6686","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib Ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “None of you should take the belongings of his companion, whether playfully or seriously. And if one of you finds his friend’s stick, let him return it to him.” And his son, Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, recognized the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and narrated a hadith from him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6686 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6687","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated to us, Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, said: “My father performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Farewell Hajj, and I was seven years old.”"
"6688","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: “And Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid died in the year ninety-one.”"
"6689","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, Muhammad bin Bakkar told me, Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Yaqoub, On the authority of Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid, may God be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bring Abdullah bin Khatal out from between curtains. The Kaaba, so he killed him patiently, then said: “No one from Quraysh will be killed patiently after this.”"
"6690","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abu Hashim bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams bin Abd Manaf, his mother was Khunas bint Malik bin Al-Mudarib bin Hajr bin Abd Ibn Ma’is Ibn Amir Ibn Luayy. He was one-eyed and his eye was gouged out on the Day of Yarmouk. Abu Hashim died in the time of Muawiyah.”"
"6691","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, Khaled told me Ibn Dahqan, on the authority of Khaled Ibn Sablan, on the authority of Kuhail Ibn Harmala, he said: Abu Hurairah came to Damascus, and descended upon Abu Kulthum al-Sadoosi, so we came to him. So we remembered the middle prayer and disagreed about it. Abu Hurairah said: “You disagreed about it just as we disagreed about it, while we were in Quba, at the house of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and among us is the righteous man Abu Hashim bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah. He got up and entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was bold in doing so, then he came out to us and told us that it was afternoon.”"
"6692","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, in Hamdan, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Masry told us, about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Muawiyah entered upon Abu Hashim bin Utba while he was He was crying, so he said: Uncle, what makes you cry? Is there pain or sadness for this world? He said: No, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with me that I did not keep. He said to me: “O Abu Hashim, you will gain money.” It will be given to people”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6692 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6693","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, he said: “Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’ is the husband of a daughter The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and her cousin. His mother was Hala bint Khuwaylid, Khadija’s sister. Abu Al-Aas’s name was Mahsham, and he was nicknamed Jaroo. Al-Bathaa, and Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave birth to Abi Al-Aas Ali bin Abi Al-Aas and Umamah bint Abi Al-Aas, and Abu Al-Aas died. Al-Aas in the eleventh year of the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6694","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zur’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, responded to Zainab to Abu Al-Aas. With the first marriage, but nothing happened.” This is an authentic chain of narration based on Muslim’s condition, and it has been narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned her to him. With a new marriage
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6694 - Incorrect"
"6695","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Humaid bin Ahmad told me Abu Ruman, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Zainab, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, converted to Islam. He converted to Islam a year before her husband, Abu Al-Aas, and then Abu Al-Aas converted to Islam. “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned her with a new marriage.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6695 - This is false, and perhaps he meant that she migrated a year before him."
"6696","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told us, Al-Zubayr bin Bakkar told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Amir told us Ibn Kariz Ibn Rabi’ah Ibn Habib Ibn Abd Shams Ibn Abd Manaf, and his mother was Dajjah bint Asma’ Ibn Al-Salt Ibn Habib Ibn Jariyah Ibn Hilal Ibn Hazzam was appointed by Uthman Ibn Affan in charge of Basra and he removed Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari. Then Abu Musa said: “A young man has come to you from Quraysh were generous to mothers, paternal aunts, and paternal aunts. He said this and that about your wealth, or he was of many virtues, and he was the one who conquered Khurasan. He entered ihram from Neyshabur, out of gratitude to God Almighty, and made watering cans at Arafat.”"
"6697","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told me, Mus’ab bin Abdullah told me, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather Mus’ab bin Thabit. Bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir bin Kuraiz, and Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, may God be pleased with them, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed for his money is a martyr.”
 Musab said: It was mentioned with this chain of transmission that Abdullah bin Aamir bin Kuraiz was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was young, and he said: This is our likeness, and he made the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spit on him and sought refuge in him. So he made Abdullah use the saliva of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, he is an irrigator.” So he would not till the land except that water would appear to him, and he would have the barking that is said: with barking. Amer, and he owns Al-Juhfa, and he has the orchard of Ibn Amer with its palm trees one night from Mecca, and he has many wells in the land, and Muawiyah was the husband of a servant. Allah bin Amir’s daughter was Hind, and Hind bint Muawiyah was the most kind to Abdullah bin Amir, and she came to him one day with a mirror. And the comb, and she was in charge of servicing it herself. So he looked in the mirror, and his face met hers. He saw her youth and beauty, and he saw The gray hairs in his beard made him feel old, so he raised his head to her and said, “Follow your father.” So she went and went to her father and told him. Muawiyah said: Can a free woman be divorced? She said: He did not come before me, so she told him her news, and Muawiyah sent to him, and said: I honored you with my daughter, then you returned her to me, and he said: I will tell you about that, that God, Blessed and Most High, has bestowed upon me His bounty and made me generous, and I love nothing but generous. I do not like anyone to be generous to me. And your daughter failed me in rewarding her for her good company, so I looked, and behold, I am old and she is young, with no wealth or honor to give her. It was her honor, so I decided to return her to you so that she could be married to one of your young men, as if his face was the leaf of the Qur’an.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6697 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6698","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “Hind bin Abu Hala bint Malik, one of the Banu Usayd bin Amr bin Tamim, an ally of the Banu Abd al-Dar, and he is the son of Khadija.”"
"6699","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Muhammad bin Salam told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: “Abu Hala, Khadija’s husband, his name is Hind bin al-Nabash bin Zurarah and his two sons Hind and Hala. Hind witnessed Uhud."
"6700","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Juma bin Omar Al-Ijli told me, A man, on the authority of Abu Hala Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, he said: “I asked my uncle Hind bin Abi Hala Al-Tamimi, and he was a gentleman. On the authority of Hilyat the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned the hadith in its length."
"6701","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Ali bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Tamim told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Hala, on the authority of his father, that he entered The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was lying asleep. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up and hugged Hala to his chest and said: “Hala, Hala, Hala.” “It is as if he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was pleased with him because of his closeness to Khadija, may God be pleased with her.”"
"6702","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Abdullah bin Zum'ah bin Al-Aswad bin Al-Muttalib bin Asad bin Abdul-Uzza bin Qusayy, and his mother was Qariba bint Abi Umayyah bin Abdullah bin Omar. Ibn Makhzum, and her mother was Atika bint Abd al-Muttalib.”"
"6703","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Al-Zuhri told me, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zamaa ibn Al-Aswad bin Al-Muttalib bin Asad said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was comforted, and I was with him with a group of Muslims, he called Bilal. To the prayer, and he said: “Bring on someone who will lead the people in prayer.” So I went out and found Omar, may God be pleased with him, among the people, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was absent. So I said: O Omar, stand up and lead the people. So he stood up, and when he said the takbir, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard his voice. Omar was a loud man, so the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “So where is Abu Bakr? God and the Muslims refuse that.” So he sent for Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he came after Omar prayed that prayer and led the people in prayer, Abdullah bin Zam’a said. Then Omar said: Woe to you, what have you done to me, O Ibn Zam’a? By God, when you ordered me to do so, I only thought that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had ordered that, and had it not been for that, I would not have led the people in prayer. I said: By God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not command me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw that you were more deserving of the one who attended the prayer with the people. This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6703 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6704","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Zakaria told us, Khalifa bin Khayyat told us, he said: “Abu Umamah Siddi bin Ajlan bin Wahb Ibn Urayb Ibn Wahb Ibn Rabah Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Wahb Ibn Ma'n Ibn Malik Ibn Asar Ibn Saad Ibn Qays Aylan Ibn Mudar came down The Levant, Khalifa said: “His lineage is Abd al-Malik ibn Qarib al-Asma’i, who said: Bahila is the wife of Ma’an ibn Malik ibn Asar ibn Sa’d. Ibn Qais Aylan, her children are attributed to her, and she is Bahila bint Saad, the clan bin Malik bin Adad bin Zaid bin Yashjub bin Ya’rab bin Qahtan. Shabab bin Khayyat said: Abu Umamah died in the year eighty-six."
"6705","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abdullah bin Salamah bin Ayyash Al-Amiri told me, Sadaqa bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God sent me to my people to invite them to God Blessed and Most High, and I presented to them the laws of Islam, so I came to them and they had watered their camels, milked them, and drank, and when they saw me, They said: Welcome Al-Sadi bin Ajlan, then they said: We have been informed that you have sought out this man. I said: “No, but I believe in God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to you to introduce to you Islam and its laws, while we were like that when they brought a piece of blood. So they laid it down and gathered around it to eat it. They said: Come, Siddiqui. So I said: Woe to you! I have only come to you from someone who makes this forbidden to you. God sent it down to him. They said: What is that? I said: “This verse was revealed to him {Forbidden to you are dead animals, blood, and the flesh of swine} [Al-Ma’idah: 3] up to His saying: {Except what you have purified} [Al-Ma’idah: 3] So I began to invite them to Islam, but they refused, so I said to them: Bring me some water, for I am very thirsty. They said: No, but we will leave you. Dying of thirst, he said: “So I was covered and covered my head with a turban, and I slept in the heat of the day in extreme heat. Then he came to me in my dream with a glass mug that people had not seen.” Better than it, and in it is a drink that people have never seen more delicious than it, so he gave me some of it, so I drank it, and when I finished my drink I woke up, and by God I was not thirsty. And I did not know anyone thirsty after that drink.” So I heard them saying: A man from among the tribes of your people came to you and you did not give him a taste, so come to me. With their taste, I said: “I have no need for it. God, Blessed and Most High, fed me and gave me drink, so I showed them my stomach, and they submitted to the rest of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6705 - Sadaqa bin Hurmuz was deemed weak by Ibn Ma’in"
"6706","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub told me, Musa ibn Zakaria told me, Khalifa ibn Khayyat told me, he said: “Muawiyah ibn Haidah ibn Muawiyah ibn Qusayr ibn Ka’b bin Rabi’ah bin Aamer, his lineage goes back to Abdullah bin Al-Jaroud.”"
"6707","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm, Al-Hafiz, in Kufa, told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib told us, Bishr bin Adam told us, Azhar bin Saad, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Bahz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Muawiyah ibn Haidah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger God, who is righteous? He said: “Your mother,” and he mentioned the hadith. We did not write it down from the hadith of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Bahz, except on his authority."
"6708","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah bin Haidah, on the authority of his father, that he said to his brother Malik bin Haidah: Go with us to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He knows you but he does not know me. He imprisoned some of my neighbors. We went to him and Malik bin Haidah said: O Messenger of God, I have I converted to Islam and my neighbors converted to Islam, so he left them and did not answer him, then he returned and did not answer him, so he got up angrily and said: “If I do that, they will claim You call for one matter and differ from something else.” So I started to rebuke him, and he forbade him, so he said: What is he saying? They said: He is saying such-and-such, so he said: “If I do that, then that one is upon me, and they are not responsible for anything from him. Leave his neighbors to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6708 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6709","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Abu Al-Jamahir told us, Saeed bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his uncle, Mikhmar bin Haidah, said: I said: O Messenger of God, I will be away from water for months, and my family is with me. Will I catch them? He said: “Yes, even if I am absent for twenty years.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6709 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6710","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Umamah Abdullah bin Osama Al-Halabi told us, in Aleppo, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married twelve chaste Arab women.” Follow him Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, according to that
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6710 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6711","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih informed us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married twelve women.” Qatada disagreed with them in this regard. Ibn Di'amah and other imams, as for Qatada's statement about it:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6711 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6712","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Imam Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Ala told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Ala told us. Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married fifteen women, six of whom were from Quraysh. And one of the allies of Quraysh, and seven Arab women, and one of the Children of Israel, and he did not marry except one during the pre-Islamic era. Abu Ubaidah Muammar bin Al-Muthanna disagreed with them, and what he said, may God have mercy on him, is closer to the truth.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6712 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6713","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Ubaid Al-Qasim bin Salam told us, may God have mercy on him, he said: “It has been proven and authentic with us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married eighteen women, seven of whom were from the Quraysh tribe. And one of the allies of Quraysh, and nine of the other Arab tribes, and one of the children of Israel from the children of Harun bin Imran, the brother of Musa bin Imran.” Abu Ubaidah said: “The first one of his wives, may God bless him and grant him peace, to marry in pre-Islamic times was Khadija, then he married after Khadija.” Sawda bint Zamaa in Mecca in Islam, then he married Aisha two years before the Hijra, then he married in Medina after an incident Badr in the year two years of history, Umm Salamah, then he married Hafsa bint Umar also in the year two years of history. These five were from Quraysh. Then he married in the third year of history, Zainab bint Jahsh, then in the fifth year of history, he married Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, then he married In the sixth year of history, he married Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, then in the seventh year of history he married Safiyya bint Huyay, then he married Maymunah bint Al-Harith, then he married Fatima bint Shurayh, then he married Zainab bint Khuzaymah, then he married Hind bint Yazid, then he married Asma bint Al-Numan, then he married Qutaylah bint Qais, sister of Al-Ash’ath, then he married Sana’ bint Al-Salt Al-Sulamiyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6713 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6714","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Ibrahim Al-Asadi, Al-Hafiz Hamdan, told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told me, Abu Mushar told us. Abdul-Ala bin Mushar, Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, on the authority of his uncle Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Aisha, may God be pleased with her, when she was seven years old, and he consummated his marriage with her when she was nine years old, and he took her away when she was eight years old. Ten years, and she died, may God be pleased with her, at the time of Muawiyah in the year fifty-seven.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6714 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6715","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, Abdullah bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa: Urwa wrote to Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik bin Marwan, “And the Messenger of God married May God’s prayers and peace be upon him when Khadija Aisha died, may God be pleased with her, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, showed her in a dream three times. It will be said: This is your wife Aisha, and Aisha was six years old on the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her. Then he married her and brought her She was nine years old in Medina, and Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, died on Tuesday night after the Witr prayer, and was buried that night in Al-Baqi’. For fifteen nights before Ramadan, Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, prayed over her, while Marwan was absent, and Abu Hurairah was He will succeed him"
"6716","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar, he said: “Aisha bint Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with her, her mother, Umm Ruman bint Amer bin Uwaimir bin Abd Shams bin Attab bin Udhaynah bin Subay bin Dahman bin Al-Harith bin Ghanam bin Malik bin Kinanah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her in Shawwal. The tenth year of the Prophet, three years before the Hijra, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, celebrated his wedding there in Shawwal at the beginning of eight months. From the Hijra, and it was the day he married a nine-year-old girl.”
 Ibn Omar said: Musa bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Rayta, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she She was asked: When did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, build a relationship with you? She said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, migrated to Medina, he and his daughters left behind. When he came to Medina, he sent Zayd bin Haritha to us. He sent his master Abu Rafi’ with him and gave them two camels and five hundred dirhams, which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had taken from Medina. Abu Bakr used it to buy what they needed from Dhahr.Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, sent with them Abdullah bin Uriqat al-Dili with two or three camels, and he wrote to Abdullah bin Abi Bakr. He ordered him to bring his family, Umm Ruman, and me and my sister Asma, the wife of Al-Zubayr. They went out accompanied, and when they reached Qudayd, he bought Zaid bin Haritha with those five hundred dirhams for three camels, then they all entered Mecca and came across Talha bin Ubaid Allah who wanted to emigrate. With the family of Abu Bakr, we all went out, and Zaid bin Haritha and Abu Rafi’ went out with Fatima, Umm Kulthum, and Sawda bint Zam’a, and Zaid carried Umm Ayman, Usama bin Zaid, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr went out with Umm Ruman and his two sisters, and Talha bin Ubaid Allah went out and accompanied us all. Until we were in the white from Mina, my camel set out while I was in a blanket with my mother in it, then my mother started saying: And his two daughters and his brides, until our camel overtook He descended from Lift and greeted him. Then we approached Medina, and I camped with Abu Bakr’s family, and the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, camped while he was On that day, he would build the mosque and verses around the mosque, so his family stayed there and we stayed for days in the house of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,What prevents you from building with your family? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Al-Zadaq,” so Abu Bakr gave him twelve ounces and a pound, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent it to him. He greeted us and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lived with me in this house that I am in, and it is the one in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. He was buried in it, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a door for himself in the mosque, facing Aisha’s door. She said: And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, built He greeted Sawda in one of the three houses next to me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was there. He said: “And Aisha died.” May God be pleased with her in the year fifty-eight, in the month of Ramadan.
 Ibn Umar said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Maimun, the client of Urwa, told me on the authority of Habib, the client of Urwa, who said: When Khadija died, he was sad for her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then Gabriel, peace be upon him, brought Aisha to him in a cradle, and said: O Messenger of God, this takes away some of your sadness. In this case, Khadija succeeded, then he returned it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go to Abu Bakr’s house and say: “O Umm Ruman!Treat Aisha well and protect me from her.” Because of this, Aisha had a low status with her family and they were not aware of God’s command regarding her, so he came to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would sometimes come to them, and not a single day would miss him unless he came to the house of Abu Bakr. He became a Muslim until he migrated, and he found Aisha hidden at Abu Bakr’s door, crying sadly. He asked her, but her mother became suspicious and stated that she Tola’, and tears came to the eyes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he went to Umm Ruman and said: “O Umm Ruman, did I not command you to protect me from Aisha?” She said: O Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, she informed the truthful about us and made him angry with us. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And if So she did.” Umm Ruman said: “No offense, I will never harm her.” And Aisha, may God be pleased with her, was born in the fourth year of the Prophet’s life. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her in the tenth year of Shawwal, when she was six years old at that time. He married her after Sawda In a month
 Ibn Umar said: Ibn Abi Sabra told me, on the authority of Musa bin Maysara, on the authority of Salem Sablan, who said: “Aisha died on the night of the seventeenth of Ramadan after Witr, so she was ordered to be buried that night.The Ansar gathered and attended, and no night saw more people than her. The people of Al-Awali came down, and she was buried in Al-Baqi’.
 Ibn Umar said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: “I witnessed Abu Hurairah praying for Aisha, may God be pleased with her, in Al-Baqi’” and Ibn Omar, among the people, people do not deny him. “And Marwan did ‘Umrah that year, and he appointed Abu Hurairah as his successor.”"
"6717","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, On the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said, and she was telling herself to be buried in her house with the Messenger of God, may God bless her. He and Abu Bakr, peace be upon him, and she said: “I committed an incident after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bury me with his wives.” So she was buried. In Al-Baqi’ “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6717 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6718","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ziyad Al-Asadi, who said: I heard Ammar bin Yasser “swearing by God that it “His wife, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this world and the hereafter.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6718 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6719","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Habib bin Muhammad al-Hafiz told us, Ubayd Allah bin Omar al-Qawariri told us, Harami bin Amara, Al-Harish bin Al-Harith narrated to me, Ibn Abi Mulaika narrated to me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died.” Peace be upon him, in my house, on my day and night, and between my dawn and my dawn, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr entered with a piece of fresh arak. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at it and I said: O Abdul Rahman, bite it from that place. So he handed it to me and I handed it to him and he spread it out. To me, so I bit it off and flattened it, so I gave it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took care of it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6719 - True"
"6720","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, Ismail ibn Ulayya informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died in my house and on my day, between my dawn and my sacrifice, and he entered Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr was wearing it, and he had a fresh siwak. He looked at it until I thought he had a need for it, so I took it and chewed it. I bit it and flavored it, then I pushed it to him and he reclined like the best I have ever seen him recline, then he went to raise it to me, and his hand fell. So I started praying for him with a supplication that Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, used to pray for him, and he used to pray with it when he was sick, but he did not pray with it during his illness. Then he raised his gaze to the sky and said: “The Most High Companion,” and his soul, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, overflowed. Praise be to God who combined my saliva with his saliva in The last day of the world “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6720 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6721","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “I was entering the house where Omar was buried with them, and by God, I did not enter unless I had my clothes tied up, out of shame. Omar, may God be pleased with him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6721 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6722","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abu Ammar told us, Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Wasiti told us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Aisha said to me: I saw Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, standing in my room. This one, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was speaking to him. When he entered, I said: O Messenger of God, who is this? He said: “Who have you compared him to?” I said: With Dihya al-Kalbi, he said: “You have seen much good. That is Gabriel, peace be upon him.” I only stayed for a short while until he said: “Oh Aisha, this is Gabriel reciting peace to you.” She said: I said: And peace be upon him, may God reward him with goodness from an intruder.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6722 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6723","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Affan Al-Amiri told me, Asbat bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Mutarrif told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, he said: Omar’s allotment for the mothers of the believers is ten thousand, and he added two thousand for Aisha, and he said: “She is the beloved of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he greeted
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6723 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6724","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Sufyan bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, he said: “The giving of the people of Badr was six thousand six thousand, and the giving of their mothers was The believers are ten thousand, ten thousand for each woman among them, other than three women: Aisha, for Omar said: I prefer her to two thousand for the love of the Messenger May God bless him and grant him peace, as well as Safiya and Juwayriyah, seven thousand, seven thousand. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” To send Mutarrif bin Tarif to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6724 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6725","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Omar bin Saeed told us Ibn Abi Husayn Al-Makki, Abdullah Ibn Abi Mulaika narrated to me, Dhakwan Abu Amr, Aisha’s client, narrated to me that a staircase was brought to Omar, from Iraq, had a gem in it, so he said to his friends: Do you know what its price is? They said: No, and they did not know how to divide it, so he said: Do you have permission that I send it to Aisha because of the love of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: Yes, so he sent it to her, and she opened it and said: “What was revealed to Ibn al-Khattab after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Oh God, no “You will spare me for his gift to the one who met him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, if it is authentic that he heard the dhikwan of Abu Amr and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6725 - There is a transmission"
"6726","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: Ibn Abbas came to ask permission to see Aisha, may God be pleased with her, during her illness, but she refused to give him permission, so the sons of Her brother: Give me permission for him, for he is one of the best of your sons. She said: Leave me alone from recommending him. They did not stop with her until she gave him permission. When he entered upon her, he said Ibn Abbas: “You were named Mother of the Believers so that you might be happy, and it was your name before you were born. You were one of the most beloved wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not love anything except that which was good, and there is nothing between you and meeting your loved ones except the separation of the soul. The body, and your necklace fell off on the night of the Apocalypse, so God granted the Muslims a choice in that, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed the verse about tayammum. And verses from the Qur’an were revealed about you, and there is not a mosque among the Muslim mosques in which your excuse is not recited at night and during the day.” So she said: Leave me alone. Your recommendation for me, O Ibn Abbas, I wished I had been forgotten. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6726 - True"
"6727","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Sa’id bin Al-Marzban, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, said: Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not marry me until Gabriel brought me my picture.” And he said: This is your wife. He married me while I was a slave girl. So when he married me, God bestowed on me modesty even though I was young. Sufyan said: Al-Zuhri said: “The edges are fences that are in the middle of them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6727 - True"
"6728","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, Hisham told us Ibn Urwa, on the authority of Awf Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Al-Tufayl, on the authority of Rumaytha, Umm Abdullah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Abi Atiq, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with On her authority, she said: My companions told me that I should speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to order the people to give gifts to him wherever he is, for the people are anxious. With their gifts on the day of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and we love goodness just as Aisha loves it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent and did not He came to me, and my companions came to me and I told them that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had not spoken to me. They said: By God, do not invite him, and this is not the case when you invite him. She said: So he turned around and I spoke to him and said: My companions told me to speak to you and order the people so that they will give you gifts wherever you are, so I told him something like the article. The first time, two or three times, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about it. Then he said: “O Umm Salamah, do not trouble me about Aisha. By God, the revelation did not descend upon me while I was in the clothing of any of my women other than Aisha.” She said: So I said: I seek refuge in God from causing you harm in Aisha: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6728 - True"
"6729","Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Shaybani told us, Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Shuaib, the women’s jurist in Egypt, told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi, my father told me, Abu Al-Anbas Saeed bin Kathir told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told us that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned Fatima, may God be pleased with her. She said: Then I spoke and he said: “Aren’t you content to be my wife in this world?” And the afterlife? I said: Yes, by God. He said: “You are my wife in this world and the hereafter.” This Abu Al-Anbas: Sa’id bin Kathir Madani, trustworthy and the hadith “It is true and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6729 - True"
"6730","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Hasani told us, Malik told us Ibn Sa`ir, Ismail Ibn Abi Khaled told us, Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Dahhak informed us that Abd Allah Ibn Safwan came to Aisha and another with him. Aisha said to one of them: Did you hear the hadith of Hafsa, so-and-so? He said: Yes, O Mother of the Believers. Then Abdullah bin Safwan said to her: What is that, O Mother of the Believers? She said: “During my nine days, none of the women before me had any, except that God Almighty brought Maryam bint Imran. By God, I am not saying this. I am prouder than any of my companions.” Abdullah bin Safwan said to her: What are they, O Mother of the Believers? She said: “The king brought my picture to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me when I was seven years old. I was given it as a gift to him when I was nine years old, and he married me as a virgin like none of the people, and the revelation used to come to him while he and I were in a blanket. One, and I was one of the people most beloved to him, and verses from the Qur’an were revealed to me in which the nation almost perished, and I saw Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, but he did not see him. “One of his wives other than me, and he was arrested in my house, and no one took care of him except the king except me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6730 - True"
"6731","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab informed me, about Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women} [An-Nour: 23] He said: “It was revealed in Aisha in particular: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6731 - True"
"6732","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, informed us that Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, and Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, saying: Ali told us Ibn Asim, Khaled Al-Hadha narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf Ibn Qais, who said: “I heard the sermon of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, Othman bin Affan, and Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them and the caliphs, until this day of mine, and I have not heard the words. From the mouth of a created being more luxurious and more beautiful than that of Aisha, may God be pleased with her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6732 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6733","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Abu Sa`id ibn Shazan told me, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told me, Issa ibn Yunus informed me, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, said: “I have not seen anyone more knowledgeable about what is permissible and what is forbidden, knowledge, poetry and medicine than Aisha, the Mother of the Believers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6733 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6734","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “If the knowledge of all people were gathered together, then knowledge Of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Aisha would have been the most knowledgeable of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6734 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6735","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, Abd told us Al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, said: “I have never seen anyone more eloquent than Aisha, may God be pleased with her.”"
"6736","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, On the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, that he was told: Did Aisha perform the religious duties well? He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw the sheikhs of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking them about the religious duties.”"
"6737","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musabbih bin Hatim Al-Ukli told me, in Basra, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Hafs Al-Qurashi told me, Hammad Al-Arqat, a righteous man, told me on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, Khayra’s husband, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: I said to Aisha: What do you say? Poetry, and you are the daughter of a friend and you do not care, and you say medicine, so what is your knowledge in it? She said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was falling ill, and Arab delegations came to him and treated him well, so I will remember that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6737 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6738","Ali bin Isa Al-Hiri told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Aisha, that she and her parents, Abu Bakr and Umm Ruman, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: We would like to She prayed for Aisha and we listened, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, forgive Aisha, the daughter of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq. Forgiveness is obligatory, apparent and hidden.” Her parents were astonished at the good supplication of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for her. He said: “You are astonished by this my supplication to whom? He bore witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6738 - It is objectionable despite the quality of its chain of transmission"
"6739","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abd Al-A'la Al-San'ani says: I found in a book that I heard from Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was asked: Who is the most beloved person to you? He said: “Aisha.” It was said: We do not mean your family. He said: “Abu Bakr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it and it has a chain of transmission. It is true according to their conditions and by it it is known.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6739 - Very strange"
"6740","It was narrated to me by Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri, Musaddad bin Qatan narrated to us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to an army that included Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them. When I returned, I said: Oh Messenger of God, who is the most beloved person to you? He said, “What do you want to do with that?” I said: O Messenger of God, I want to know that. He said: Aisha. I said: I mean, who are the men? He said: “Her father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6740 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6741","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani and Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Khasib al-Sufi told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hadrami told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban, Waki’, and Abu Usama told us, they said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, that Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him He said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he returned from the Battle of Dhat al-Silasal: O Messenger of God, who is the most beloved to you? He said: “Aisha.” He said: “Who are the men?” He said: “Her father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6741 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6742","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Ali bin Asim told us, he informed us Bayan bin Bishr, Amer Al-Sha’bi said to me: A man came to me and said to me: All the mothers of the believers are more beloved to me than Aisha. I said: “As for you, She disobeyed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Aisha was the most beloved of them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6742 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6743","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, and Muhammad bin Bakkar told us, They said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Majishun told us, my father told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, who among your wives will be in Paradise? He said: “But you are one of them.” She said: “It seems to me that this is because he did not marry a virgin other than me.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6743 - True"
"6744","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya and Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, told us Qutayba bin Saeed, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said to me: “Indeed, I saw On a hill and around me cows are being slaughtered.” So I said to her: “If your visions come true, there will be a battle of slaughter around you.” She said: “I seek refuge in God from your polytheism, how miserable it is.” “I said,” so I said to her: “Perhaps if it is something that will harm you,” she said: “By God, because something else from heaven is more beloved to me than doing that.” When it was later reported that Ali, may God be pleased with him, had killed the mammal, she said to me: “If you come to Kufa, write for me people from Some of the people of the town that you know witnessed this. When I came, I found the people in factions, so I wrote to them, from each faction, ten who had witnessed this. He said: So I brought her their testimony, and she said: “May God curse Amr ibn Al-Aas, for he claimed to me that he killed him in Egypt.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6744 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6745","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan sent a hundred thousand to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she divided them until she did not leave anything of them, so she said Barira: You are fasting, so can you buy us meat for a dirham? Aisha said: “If I had been reminded, I would have done so.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6745 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6746","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zamaa bin Salih told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, that Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, heard the cry for Aisha and said to a maid: Go and look. She came and said: It is obligatory. Umm Salamah said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, she was the most beloved of people to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except her father.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6746 - In it is Zam’ah bin Salih, and no one narrated it except Muslim, coupled with another one with him."
"6747","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Abu Muslim Al-Mustamli told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: He said: Muawiyah: O Ziyad, which of the people is more knowledgeable? He said: “You, O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “Should I decide on you?” He said: “But if you decide to marry me, then Aisha.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6747 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6748","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Harashi told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, al-Mu’affa bin Imran told us, al-Mughirah bin Ziyad told us, On the authority of Ataa, he said: “Aisha was the most knowledgeable of the people, the most knowledgeable of the people, and the best of people’s opinions regarding the common people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6748 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6749","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Hafsa bint Omar bin Al-Khattab bin Nufayl bin Abdul-Uzza bin Rabah bin Abdullah bin Qurt bin Razah bin Adiy bin Ka’b bin Luay bin Ghalib, and her mother was Zainab bint Mad’un bin Habib bin Wahb bin Hudhafa bin Jumah, and she was one of the emigrants.”"
"6750","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “Then The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Hafsa, the daughter of Omar ibn Al-Khattab, and she was before him the servant of Khunays ibn Hudhafa al-Sahmi.”"
"6751","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: Hafsa, the daughter of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, was given maids by her husband, and Othman by Ruqayyah, so Omar passed by Othman and said: Do you have any Hafsa? So he turned away from me and did not tell me anything. Then Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and complained about him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is better than that. “Shall I marry Hafsa, and Othman will marry Umm Kulthum?” So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Hafsa, and Othman married Umm Kulthum, a daughter. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6751 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6752","So Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, that Usama bin Zaid bin Aslam, he told him on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Hafsa was born and the Quraysh were building the house before the Prophet was sent, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God grant him peace for five years.”
 Ibn Umar said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabrah told me, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Hassan, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Peace be upon him, Hafsa in Sha`ban, on top of thirty months before Uhud.”
 Ibn Umar said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “Hafsa died in Sha’ban of the year forty-five, so he prayed. It was owned by Marwan bin Al-Hakam, who was a worker in the city at that time.”
 Ibn Umar said: Ali bin Muslim Al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw Marwan carrying Hafsa’s bed between the pillars of the family’s house. He packed bundles to the house of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, and Abu Hurairah carried her from the house of Al-Mughirah to her grave.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Nafi’ told me, saying: “Abdullah, Asim, Ibn Omar, Salim, and Abdullah descended in the grave of Hafsa. And Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar.”"
"6753","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Imran al-Juniy told us, about Qais bin Zaid: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, divorced Hafsa bint Omar, and her two maternal uncles, Qudamah and Uthman, son of Mad’un, entered upon her, and she cried. She said: By God, he did not divorce me when he was satisfied, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to me: Go back to Hafsa, for she is “Sawmah is a staunch faster, and she will be your wife in Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6753 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6754","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hasan bin Abi Jaafar told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, divorced Hafsa, so Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Muhammad, you divorced me.” Hafsa, she is a fasting and steadfast woman, and she will be your wife in Paradise, so go back to her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6754 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6755","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: “Umm Salamah, the first female emigrant.”"
"6756","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, about Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “And of those who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, who first emigrated to the land of Abyssinia, then Abu Salamah Abdullah bin Abdul-Asad and his wife Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah migrated to Medina.”"
"6757","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Umm Salamah’s name was Ramla, and she was the first woman to enter Medina as an immigrant, and she was with Abu Salamah before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abdullah bin Abdul-Assad bin Hilal bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzoum. He was the first to immigrate to the land of Abyssinia and witnessed Badr, and he died during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to Abu Salamah she bore Salamah, Omar, Durra, and Zainab. Their mother, Umm Salama, husband The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, succeeded her after Abu Salamah. Her son, Omar bin Abi Salamah, narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted"
"6758","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of a brother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you attend the dead or the sick, say goodness, for the angels They believe in what you say.” When Abu Salamah died, I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How should I say? He said: “Say, O God, forgive us and him, and follow me from him with a righteous deed.” So I said it, and God followed me with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6758 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, if they did not narrate it"
"6759","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit informed us, about Ibn Umar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it strikes If one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him say: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. Oh God, I consider my calamity to be with You, so reward me for it. I say, and give me in exchange for her something better than her. I said: Who is better than Abu Salamah? So I did not stop until I said it. When her waiting period was over, Abu Bakr proposed to her. She sent him back, and Omar proposed to her. She sent him back, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to her to propose to her. She said: Welcome to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And by His Messenger, go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and tell him that I am a young woman other than myself, and that he is not one of my guardians. Witness, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to her: “As for your saying: I am a young woman, God will suffice you for your children. As for your saying: I am jealous, so I will pray to God to remove your jealousy. As for the saints, none of them is a witness or an absent person, but he will please me.” So she said to her son: Get up, O Omar, and marry the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to her. He married her to him and said to her: I will not deprive you of what I gave your sister, so-and-so, for two liters. And two palms and a pillow made of human beings stuffed with fiber. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to her while she was breastfeeding Zainab. Whenever the Prophet came She, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took her and placed her in her lap, breastfeeding her. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was a living and generous person, and he would return. Then Ammar bin Yasser, who was her breast-brother, became aware of her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to come to her one day, so he came. Ammar entered upon her, and Zainab rose from her lap and said: Leave this disgusting, disgusting woman with whom you have harmed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and entered, looking around the house and saying: “Where is a dungeon? Why do I not see a dungeon?” She said: Ammar came and took her away, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, built with his family, and said: “If you want me to take seven to you, I can do seven to the women.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He said: “Ibn Umar bin Abi Salamah: The one whom Hammad bin Salamah did not name in this hadith was named by someone else Sa’id bin Umar. Ibn Abi Salamah, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6759 - True"
"6760","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her, took With his garment preventing her from leaving her house, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you wish, I can add more to you and I will call you to the virgin for seven. And the thiba has three “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6760 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6761","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Umm Salamah’s name is Hind bint Abi Umayyah, and the name of Abi Umayyah: Suhail bin Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzum, and her mother was Atika bint Amer bin Rabia bin Malik bin Khuzaymah bin Alqamah bin Firas bin Ghanam bin Malik bin Kinanah. Abu Salama Abdullah bin Abd al-Assad ibn Hilal, and he immigrated with her to the land of Abyssinia during both migrations, and she bore him there Zainab and she bore him after “That is Salamah, ‘Umar, and Durrat Banu Abi Salamah.”
 Ibn Umar said: Umar bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yarubu`, on the authority of Umar bin Abi Salamah bin Abdul-Assad said: My father went out to Uhud, and Abu Usama al-Jashmi shot him in the arm with an arrow. He stayed for a month healing his wound, then The wound healed, “and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent my father to Qatan in Muharram for thirty-five months,” and he was absent for twenty-nine. One night, then he returned and entered the city for eight days of Safar in the year four, while the wound had healed, and he died there for eight days of Jumada al-Akhira. In the fourth year of the Hijra, “So my mother prepared for the waiting period and was married for the remaining ten nights of Shawwal in the year four, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her.” He greeted him on the last few nights of Shawwal in the year the fourth. Then the people of Medina said: The most prominent Arabs entered upon the master of Islam and the Muslims. At the beginning of the evening, a bride was given dinner, and she got up at the end of the night, grinding. She is the mother of the believers, Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her.
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Nafi’ told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “Umm Salamah recommended that the governor of Medina not pray over her while he was Al-Walid bin Utba bin Abi Sufyan, she died when she entered the year fifty-nine, and her nephew Abdullah bin Abdullah prayed over her. Ibn Abi Umayyah”"
"6762","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd informed me Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hind bint Al-Harith Al-Farasiyya, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Indeed, Aisha has a part of me that no one has revealed.” He said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Umm Salamah, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked. Peace be upon him, and it was said: O Messenger of God, what did the division do? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, and he learned that Umm Salamah had stayed with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6762 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6763","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad, the judge in Baghdad, told me. Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me. Muhammad bin Suhail told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah. Muammar bin Al-Muthanna said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Umm Salamah before the Battle of Badr in the year two of history. Hind bint Abi Umayyah bin Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Makhzoum, and the first of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Zainab. The last of them to die was Umm Salamah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6763 - He said this in the year two, but it is a mistake"
"6764","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sakouni told me, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Khalid told us Al-Ahmar, Razin told me, Salma told me, she said: I went in to see Umm Salamah, and she was crying, so I said: What makes you cry? She said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a dream crying with dust on his head and beard, so I said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God? He said: “I witnessed the killing of Hussein just before.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6764 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6765","Abu Abdullah al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Mihran informed us, Abdullah ibn Musa informed us, Ismail ibn Nashet informed us, he said: I heard Shahr bin Hawshab said: “I came to Umm Salamah to console her for the killing of Al-Hussein bin Ali.”"
"6766","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, he informed me Ibn Jurayj, Habib bin Abi Thabit told me that Abd al-Hamid bin Abi Amr and al-Qasim bin Muhammad told him that they heard Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham tells that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that when she came Medina told them that she was the daughter of Abu Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, so they denied her and said: How deceitful are strange things until people started to Hajj, so it was said to her: You write to your family, so she wrote to them, and they returned to Medina, and they believed her and increased her dignity. Umm Salamah said: “When Zainab gave birth, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6766 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6767","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Afsi told me, Muhammad bin Othman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Khalid told us, Jarir, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, said: We were sitting with Muharib bin Dathar, and he said: Ibn Sa’id bin Zayd told me, “Umm Salamah, She recommended that Saeed bin Zaid pray over her, fearing that Marwan bin Al-Hakam would pray over her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6767 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6768","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abdullah bin Abi Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, He said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, and before him she was under Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh al-Asadi. Asad of Khuzaymah, and he died on her behalf in the land of Abyssinia, where he had left Mecca as an emigrant, then he was tempted and converted to Christianity, so he died while he was a Christian. And God confirmed Islam for Umm Habiba and immigration, then her husband became a Christian and died while he was a Christian, and Umm Habiba bint Abi refused. Sufyan wanted her to become a Christian, and God Almighty completed her conversion to Islam and migration until she came to Medina and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to her. So Othman bin Affan married her to him.” Al-Zuhri said: “They claimed that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote to the Negus, so he married her to him and gave him forty uqiyahs on his behalf.”"
"6769","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, may God have mercy on him. Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Mus’ab bin Abdullah told us. Al-Zubairi, said: “Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan bin Harb, her name is Ramla bint Abi Sufyan, and it is said: Her name is Hind, and her name is Ramla. Her mother was Safiyya bint Abi Al-Aas bin Umayyah, and it is also said: Amina bint Abd al-Uzza bin Harban bin Awf bin Ubaid bin Awayj bin Adi bin Ka'b and she died a year before Muawiyah.”"
"6770","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Masqala told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Umm Habiba Her name is Ramla bint Abi Sufyan bin Harb, and her mother is Safiya bint Abi Al-Aas bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams, the paternal aunt of Uthman bin Affan. Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh ibn Rabab, Halib Harb ibn Umayyah, married her. She bore him a beloved, and I was nicknamed her. He married David’s beloved. بْنُ عُرْوَةَ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ الثَّقَفِيُّ»
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Zuhair told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, who said: Umm Habibah said: I saw in a dream that Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh appeared to my husband in the worst and most disfigured way, so I was terrified, so I said: He has changed, by God, what is his condition? He said in the morning: O Umm Habiba, I looked at religion and did not see a religion better than Christianity, and I had embraced it, then I entered into a religion. Muhammad, then I returned to Christianity, and I said: By God, it is not good for you. I told him about the vision that I had seen of him, but he did not celebrate it and fell into a state of grief. On the wine until he died, then I saw in my sleep as if someone was coming and saying to me: O Mother of the Believers. I was terrified and interpreted it as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. يَتَزَوَّجُنِي، قَالَتْ: فَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا أَنِ انْقَضَتْ عِدَّتِي،All I felt was the messenger of the Negus at my door asking for permission. Then I saw a maid of his called Abraha. She was looking after his clothes and oil. So she came to me and said: The king says to you: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has written to me to marry you. So I said: May God give you good tidings. She said: The king says to you: Appoint someone to marry you. So she sent to Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas and appointed him and gave Abraha two bracelets. Of silver, and two rings that were on her feet, and silver rings that were on the toes of her feet, out of joy about what I had given her good tidings, and when evening came, he commanded Al-Najashi Jaafar bin Abi Talib and some of the Muslims who attended, so Al-Najashi delivered a speech and said: Praise be to God, the Holy King, peace and faith. The Dominant, the Mighty, the Mighty, praise be to God as He deserves His praise, and I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that He is the One Jesus, son of Mary, peace and blessings be upon him, gave good tidings about him, but after that, the Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wrote to me to marry him to Umm Habiba. The daughter of Sufyan, so I responded to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for, and I gave her four hundred dinars in charity. Then he poured out the dinars between يَدَيِ الْقَوْمِ،Then Khalid bin Saeed spoke and said: Praise be to God, I praise Him, seek His help and seek His help, and I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He sent him with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all other religions, even if the polytheists disliked it. But after that, I have responded to what The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invited him and his wife, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, so God blessed His Messenger and gave the dinars to Khalid. Bin Saeed grabbed her, then they wanted to get up, so he said: Sit down, for it is the Sunnah of the Prophets, may the peace and blessings of God be upon them, that if they get married, they will be eaten. He called for food and they ate, then dispersed. Umm Habiba said: When the money reached me, I sent for Abraha who gave me good news. So I said to her: I had given you what I gave you on that day, and I had no money in my hand, and these are fifty shekels, so take them and seek help from me. So she left. She returned it to me and said, “The king has determined that I will not dispose of you at all while I am the one who is in charge of his clothes.” And I have followed the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I have submitted to God, and the king has ordered his wives to send to you everything عِنْدَهُنَّ مِنَ"
"6771","So Mukhlid bin Ja’far Al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad bin Jarir Al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Ishaq bin Muhammad told me, Ja’far bin Muhammad told me Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Amr Ibn Umayyah Al-Damri to Al-Najashi to propose to him Umm Habibah bint Abu Sufyan, and she was the wife of Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh, so he married her to him, and Al-Najashi made her truthful from him on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he handed over four hundred dinars. ""Except for that"""
"6772","So Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told me, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, On the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that he asked Aisha, the wife of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: How much the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave in charity to his wives. She said: “His charity for his wives was twelve uqiyahs.” And half, that is five hundred dirhams. This is the dowry of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his wives. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Indeed, the Negus gave Umm Habiba four hundred dinars in exchange for using the morals of kings to exaggerate in deeds to seek the Prophet’s help. May God bless him and grant him peace in that.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6772 - True"
"6773","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: “Al-Najashi prepared Umm Habibah to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and sent her with Sharhabeel bin “good”
 Ibn Umar said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told me, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Abi Aoun, he said: When Abu Sufyan bin Harb reached the age of marriage, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his daughter: “That stallion does not peck his nose.”
 Ibn Umar said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabrah told me, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail, on the authority of Awf bin Al-Harith, he said: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, saying: Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called me when she died and said: “He was among us.” Whatever happens between co-wives, God has forgiven all of that and has forgiven you, and I have absolved you from all of that.” Aisha said: I am pleased with your pleasure, may God make you happy. She sent a message to Umm Salamah and told her the same thing. She died in the year forty-four in the emirate of Muawiyah, may God be pleased with them both."
"6774","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Zainab was the daughter of Jahsh bin Rabab bin Yamar bin Sabra bin Murrah bin Kathir bin Ghanam bin Dudan bin Asad bin Khuzaymah. Her mother was Umaima bint Abd al-Muttalib bin Hashim bin Amr bin Abd Manaf, and Zainab was with Zaid bin Haritha, so he left her. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married her.” And in it was revealed: “And when Zaid had finished with her, We made her in marriage to you.” [Al-Ahzab: 37] He said: “So it was.” She takes pride in the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God gave me in marriage to His Messenger, and your fathers and your relatives and Hamnah bint Jahsh gave you in marriage. “She was the woman who had to undergo menstruation. She was married to Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and she was the sister of Zainab bint Jahsh.”"
"6775","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, explaining these stories. Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, He said: “Zainab bint Jahsh bin Rabab is the sister of Abd al-Rahman bin Jahsh.”
 Omar bin Othman Al-Jahshi told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina, and Zainab bint Jahsh was among those who migrated with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She was a beautiful woman, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to her to Zayd ibn Haritha, and she said: No. He pleased him, and she was the most beloved of the Quraysh. He said: “I have satisfied him for you.” So Zaid married her.
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came The house of Zaid bin Haritha was looking for him, and Zaid was only called: Zaid bin Muhammad, so perhaps the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost him at that time. He says: “Where is Zaid?” So he came to his house looking for him, but he did not find him. Then Zainab came to him and said to him: Here, O Messenger of God. So he left and continued to worry about hardly anything. It can only be understood as Glory be to God the Great, Glory be to God, the Converter of hearts.Then Zaid came to his house, and his wife told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to his house. Zaid said: Didn’t you tell him: He enters. She said: I suggested that to him and he refused. He said: I heard him say something. She said: I heard him speak something I did not understand when he left. And I heard him say: “Glory be to God the Great, Glory be to God, the Converter of hearts.” He said: So Zaid went out until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: Oh Messenger of God, I have been informed that you have come to my house, so will you come in with my father and mother, O Messenger of God? Perhaps Zainab likes you so I can separate from her. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Keep your husband safe from you.” Zayd was unable to find a way to her after that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. And he greets him, and he informs him, and he says: “Retain your husband.” He says: O Messenger of God, then I separate from her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Imprison your husband.” Then Zayd left her and separated from her and she left. He said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting and talking with Aisha, he was pleased with her. God on her behalf when a cloud took over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.Then he walked away from him, smiling, and saying: “Whoever goes to Zainab and gives her the good news that God Almighty has married her to her from heaven,” and he recited: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: {And when you said to him whom God had bestowed, and you had bestowed good upon him} [Al-Ahzab: 37] The whole story was said by Aisha Radi God said about her: “So it took me from what was near and after what had reached me of its beauty and other things, which are the greatest and most noble of things, what God had done for it.” God Almighty married her to her from heaven.” Aisha said: “She is proud of us about this.” Aisha said: “So Salma, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out May God bless him and grant him peace, she became distressed, so I told her about that and he gave her clarifications.”
 Ibn Umar said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabrah told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi said: “Zainab bint Jahsh commanded that she be carried on the bed of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that a coffin be made over him.” It was said that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, was blamed for it. “And Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, passed by diggers digging Zainab’s grave on the day of Sayyaf and he said: “If only I had set up a camp over them.” And it was the first camp set up over a grave in Al-Baqi’.Ibn Umar said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Sabrah told me, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salit, he said: I saw Abu Ahmad ibn Jahsh carrying Zainab’s bed while he was blind and crying, and I heard Omar saying: Oh Abu Ahmad, Step down from the bed, and people will not bother you on her bed. Abu Ahmad said: “This is the one by which we have attained all goodness, and this cools my heat to the extent that I feel.” Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Commitment, commitment.
 He said: Omar bin Othman Al-Jahshi told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “Zainab bint Jahsh never left behind a dinar or a dirham. She used to give everything in charity.” She took possession of it, and it was a shelter for the poor, and she left her house, so they sold it to Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik when the mosque was demolished for fifty thousand. A dirham
 He said: Omar bin Othman Al-Jahshi told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The mother of Okasha bint Muhsin was asked how old Zainab bint Jahsh was on the day of her death. She died? She said: “We came to Medina for migration when she was thirty-odd years old, and she died in the year twenty.” Omar bin Uthman said: My father used to say: “Zainab bint Jahsh died when she was fifty-three years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6775 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6776","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told me, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, he told me Ibrahim bin Abi Uwais Al-Madani, my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his wives: “The quickest you are to catch up with me, the longest of you.” Aisha said: When we gathered in a house One of us, after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached out to the wall with our hands, and we did not stop doing that until Zainab died. Bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She was a short woman and not the tallest of us. We knew then that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He only meant charity by the length of the hand. He said: “Zainab was a handicraftswoman, and she used to tan and bead and give alms in the cause of God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6776 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6777","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama narrated to us, Ali bin Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud. Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Amer, said: Zainab bint Jahsh used to say to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I am the greatest of your wives over you in right. The best of them in marriage, the most faithful of them to cover, and the closest of them in kinship, then you say: The Most Gracious, the Mighty and Sublime, has made you in marriage from above His throne, and Gabriel was He, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, is the ambassador of that, and I am your paternal aunt’s daughter and you have no relatives of your women other than me. “I mentioned at the beginning of the translation that Umm Zainab bint Jahsh, Umaima bint Abd al-Muttalib bin Hashim, and she is the paternal aunt of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6777 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6778","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulayman al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb al-Mawsili told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Your wives are proud of me, saying: He did not marry you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did I not honor your dowry? Did I not emancipate forty?” A slave from your people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6778 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6779","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar Bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Urwa Bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, captured the captives of the Banu... Al-Muttaliq: Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith bin Abi Dirarar fell in the arrow of Thabit bin Qais bin Al-Shammas, so she recorded it on herself and it was A sweet and gentle woman, hardly anyone saw her unless she took his breath away.” He said: “So she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking his help in Writing it down
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6779 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6780","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith bin Abi Dharar bin Habib bin Aidh bin Malik bin Jadhimah bin Al-Mustaliq, from Khuza’ah, who was married to Musafa’ bin Safwan. So he was killed on the day of Marsa’."
"6781","So Yazid bin Ubayd Allah bin Qusayt told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, captured the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, so he took out a fifth of it, then divided it among the people and gave the knight Two arrows, and the man one arrow, so Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith bin Abi Dirar fell into the arrow of Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, and it was under the name of a cousin of hers called Safwan bin Malik bin Judhaymah, who was killed on her authority, so Thabit bin Qays wrote it on the authority of Her soul was nine ounces long, and she was a beautiful woman. Hardly anyone saw her unless she took his breath. While the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was with me. Then Juwayriyah entered and asked him about her letter. By God, it was not until I saw her that I hated her entering upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I knew that he would see in her the same as I saw, so she said: O Messenger of God, I am Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, the master of his people, and something has befallen me. You did not know that I fell into the arrow of Thabit ibn Qays, so he wrote me down for nine awqiqs in my redemption.He said: “Or better than that.” She said: What is it? He said: “I will fulfill your obligation and marry you.” She said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “I have done so.” Then the news spread to the people, and they said: “In-laws.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were seeking enslavement, so they freed whoever was in their hands from the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, and their emancipation amounted to a hundred members of the family. By his marrying her, Aisha said: I do not know of a woman who was a greater blessing to her people than her, and that was his departure from the battle. Al-Muraisi
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Abyad, the client of Juwayriyah, told me on the authority of his father. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the Banu Al-Muttaliq: Juwayriyah fell into captivity, her father came and ransomed her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her afterward. As for the hadith of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq is close to the wording of Al-Waqidi, and the meanings are all the same.”
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Abyad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. He greeted her in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal in the year fifty-six in the emirate of Muawiyah, and Marwan bin al-Hakam, who was at that time the governor of Medina, prayed over her.
 Ibn Omar said: Muhammad bin Yazid told me about his grandmother, and she was the servant of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith.On the authority of Juwayriyah, may God be pleased with her, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me when I was twenty years old.” She said: “And she died.” Juwayriyah in the year fifty, and she was sixty-five years old at that time, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam prayed over her.”
 Ibn Omar said: Hazzam bin Hisham told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith said: “I saw before the arrival of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace For three nights, it was as if the moon had set, and he walked from Yathrib until he fell on my lap. I disliked telling it to any of the people until a messenger came. God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When we were taken captive, I hoped for a vision. When he freed me and married me, by God, I did not speak to him among my people until the Muslims were the only ones. Those who sent them, and I felt nothing but a slave girl from among my cousins tell me the news, so I thanked God Almighty.”"
"6782","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And Juwayriyah Al-Harith’s daughter, her name was Barrah bint Al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar ibn Habib ibn Aidh ibn Malik ibn Jadhimah, from Khuza’ah. She was with A cousin of hers called: Musafa bin Safwan bin Dhul-Shifar."
"6783","Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata told me, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith “that her name was Barrah, and he changed it, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, called her Juwayriyah, and he hated to be said: He came out from a land, “correct according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not bring him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6783 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6784","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck Juwayriyah al-Hijab, and it was He divides to her as he divides to his wives.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6784 - True"
"6785","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Saeed bin Kathir bin told us Ufair, Sa’id bin Abi Maryam, and Abu Salih said: Al-Layth bin Sa’d told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq told him about Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, may God be pleased with her, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered her and said: “Is there any food?” She said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, we have no food except a bone from a sheep which I gave to my mistress as charity. He said: “Bring it to me, for it has reached the age of “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6785 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6786","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told me, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, that he heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, say: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, opened Khaybar chose Safiya bint Huyay for himself, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took her out, following her behind him. Then he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, placed his foot so that it could stand on it and ride. When he reached the red-haired dam, he latched onto it and made a cage in a place, and he ordered me and I prayed for him. Those around him, that was the feast of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Mus’ab said: “She was Safiyya bint Huyyay bin Akhtab bin Sa’id bin Tha'labah ibn Ubaid ibn al-Khazraj ibn Abi Habib ibn al-Nadr ibn al-Nahham ibn Nahum, from the children of Israel, from the tribe of Moses, may peace be upon him. Peace be upon her, and her mother was Barrah bint al-Samawal. She perished in the time of Muawiyah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6786 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6787","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, he informed us Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Peace and blessings of God be upon him. With Safiyya, Abu Ayyub spent the night at the door of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when he saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said “Allahu Akbar” and said: Abu Ayoub saw the sword and said: O Messenger of God, she was a newly married slave girl, and I had killed her father, her brother, and her husband, so I did not protect her. On you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed and said to him: “Good.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6787 - True"
"6788","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Issa bin Tahman told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fed Safiyya bint Huyyay bread and meat.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6788 - Indeed, it is a mistake, but it is Dhi Zainab"
"6789","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm bin Masqala told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Muhammad told me Bin Musa, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Aminah bint Abi Qays Al-Ghafariyya, who said: I am one of the women who married Safiyya, may God be pleased with her. On her authority to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I heard her say: “I have not yet reached the age of seventeen, and my effort is to reach the age of seventeen one night. “I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: “Safiya died in the year fifty-two in the time of Muawiyah and was buried in Al-Baqi’.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6789 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6790","Da'laj bin Ahmad al-Sijzi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muawiyah al-Basri told us, Shadh bin Fayyad Abu Ubaidah told us, Hashim bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Kinanah, on the authority of Safiyya, may God be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while I was crying, and he said: “O daughter of Hayy! Makes you cry? I said: I have heard that Hafsa and Aisha are harassing me and saying: We are better than her, we are the cousins of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And his wives said: “Didn’t you say: How can you be better than me and my father Aaron and my uncle Musa and my husband Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6790 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6791","Bukayr bin Ahmad bin Sahl al-Sufi told me, in Mecca, and he wrote it for me in his own handwriting. Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abu Thawr told us. Ibrahim bin Khalid Al-Kalbi, Abu Qatn narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah told me: Mas’ar bin Kadam told me: “The wife of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me. Maymunah bint Al-Harith bin Hazn bin Bujayr bin Al-Haram bin Ruwaiba bin Abdullah bin Hilal bin Amer bin Sa’sa’ah, upon him be peace and blessings be upon him. Her mother was Hind bint Awf bin Zuhair bin Al-Harith bin Hamata bin Harith, from Himyar.”"
"6792","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Maymunah bint Al-Harith Bin Hamata bin Harith, she is the maternal aunt of Abdullah bin Abbas, and the sister of Umm Al-Fadl bint Al-Harith. She was married in pre-Islamic times. Masoud bin Amr bin Umair Al-Thaqafi, then he left her and Abu Rahm bin Abdul-Uzza bin Abi Qais from Banu Malik bin Hasal succeeded her. Ibn Aamir Ibn Luayy, and he died on her behalf, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her. Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib married her to him. He was in charge of her, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built there lavishly, ten miles from Mecca, and she was the last woman he married. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that was in the seventh year of the Umrah of the affair.” Ibn Umar said: “Maymunah, may God be pleased with her, died in the year Sixty-one, and she was the last of the Prophet’s wives, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was eighty or eighty-one years old on the day she died. Because of her old age, she was flogged.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6792 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6793","Israel, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “My aunt’s name was Maimuna Barrah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named her Maymunah, peace and blessings be upon him. “Sahih”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6793 - Al-Dhahabi said it is authentic"
"6794","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Maymunah’s name was Barrah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named her Maymunah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6794 - True"
"6795","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Muhammad bin Falih told us, about Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out the previous year in the year of Hudaybiyyah, performing Umrah in Dhul-Qa’dah. In the year seven, which is the month in which the polytheists repelled him from the Sacred Mosque, until when he reached Yagg he sent Jafar bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he went to Maimuna bint Al-Harith bin Hazan Al-Amiriyah, so he proposed to her, and she left her affairs with Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib. Her sister, Umm Al-Fadl, was under him, so Al-Abbas, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her off. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed with honor after That was for a while, until Maimuna came and he built extravagantly with her. God Almighty destined that the death of Maimuna bint Al-Harith, may God be pleased with her, would occur after That was after a while, and she died where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built a building there.”"
"6796","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Ibn Abi told me Najih, on the authority of Ata’, and Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimuna bint Al-Harith May God be pleased with her. He stayed in Mecca for three days, and Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza came to him with a group of Quraysh on the third day. They said to him: He has died. Your time has passed, so depart from us. He said: “And what is the matter with you if you leave me alone and I arrange a wedding among you and prepare food for you and you prepare it?” They said: We have no need of your food, so leave us. So he left with Maimuna bint Al-Harith, may God be pleased with her, so that I can marry with her in an extravagant manner. “This is a hadith.” It is valid according to the condition of a Muslim, but they did not take it out.” What is amazing about God’s decree and destiny is that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built Maimunah bint Al-Harith extravagantly brought it back to Medina when he left the Umrah to perform the judiciary, and it remained with him until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left. He greeted the conquest of Mecca, and he took her with him until he conquered Taif, and he departed to return to Medina, and Maimunah died lazily in the place. “which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built with her when she was married.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6796 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6797","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us that what I mentioned was true, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us. My father, he said: I heard Abu Fazara, narrating on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Maimunah, may God be pleased with her: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He married her lawfully, and built lawful marriage with her. He built with her extravagantly, and she died extravagantly on the night he built the marriage. She was my aunt, so I stayed in I and Ibn Abbas's grave was in her grave. When we placed her in the grave, her head was turned, so I took my cloak, gathered it, and placed it at her head. So Ibn Abbas took it, threw it away, and placed a headpiece by her head. And Mecca is twelve miles away.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “This authentic chain of transmission was based on the fact that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace It was lawful for him to marry her. As for the narrations of Ikrimah on the authority of Ibn Abbas, they speak of the fact that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married her while he was “Forbidden”"
"6798","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, Abu al-Sha’a’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got married while he was Muharram.” Amr said: I mentioned it to Al-Zuhri, then he said: O Amr, who do you see? I said: They say: Auspicious. Ibn Shihab said: Yazid bin Al-Asam told me, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her while it was lawful.” He said: Amr told Ibn Shihab: “You make a Bedouin urinate on his heels like Ibn Abbas.” Ibn Shihab said: She is his maternal aunt. Amr said: “She is my maternal aunt.” Ibn Abbas also said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6798 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6799","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Kathir bin Hisham told us, Ja’far bin Burqan said: We told us Yazid bin Al-Asam, the son of Maimunah’s sister, said: I met Aisha, who was coming from Mecca, and I and Ibn Talha bin Ubaidullah, who is the son of Her sister. We had fallen into one of the walls of the city and were hit by it. This was reported to her, so she went to her sister’s son and blamed him. And she excused him, and she came to me and gave me a eloquent sermon, then she said: “Did you not know that God Almighty led you until he placed you among the Ahlul Bayt? Nabih, you have gone, and by God, it is auspicious, and throw your cloak on your strangers, but it was from our fear of God Almighty and brought us to the womb.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6799 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6800","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad, the servant of Khuza’ah, on the authority of Salih ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Durrah, on the authority of Maimunah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out One night, he came from me and I closed for him. He came and asked to open, but I refused to open. He said: “You swore that you would not open for me.” So I said to him: You go to your husbands one night and he said: “I didn’t do that, but I found a lump of urine.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6800 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6801","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the martyr, may God have mercy on him, told us Abdullah bin Abdul told us Al-Wahhab Al-Hajabi, Abdul Aziz Al-Darawardi told us, and Ibrahim bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sisters are believers: Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and her sister Umm al-Fadl, daughter of Al-Harith, and her sister Salma bint Al-Harith, Hamza’s wife, and Asma bint Umays, their maternal sister. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim.” And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6801 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6802","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, On the authority of Ataa, he said: We attended with Ibn Abbas an extravagant funeral for Maimunah, and Ibn Abbas said: “This is Maimunah. If you raise her coffin, there will be no You may disturb her, but do not disturb her, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had nine wives. He used to divide among eight, and one did not He swears by her.” Ata’ said: “She is Safiyya.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"6803","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Kathir bin Hisham told us, and Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Ala’ Al-Abdi told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada Ibn Di'amah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimuna bint Al-Harith bin Farwa, who is the sister of Umm Al-Fadl, the wife of Al-Abbas. Ibn Abdul-Muttalib, when he performed Umrah in Mecca, and she presented herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and about it was revealed: {And a believing woman, if she gives She herself is for the Prophet if the Prophet wanted to marry her exclusively for you and not for the believers.} [Al-Ahzab: 50], then she was taken with him to Medina and was Before him, at Farwa bin Abdul-Uzza bin Asad, from Banu Tamim bin Dudan.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6803 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6804","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Zainab bint Khuzaymah, one of the Banu Hilal bin Amir, and she was with Abdullah bin Jahsh before him. So he was killed on her behalf on the day of Uhud.”"
"6805","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Musa ibn Harun told us, Abu Hammam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab said: “Zainab bint Khuzaymah bin Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Abd Manaf bin Hilal bin Amer bin Sa’sa’a passed away. She is the Mother of the Poor. She was called by that name in pre-Islamic times. She died in Medina after the Hijra during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6805 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6806","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, may God Almighty have mercy on him, informed me: Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Alaa, Saeed bin Abi Arouba narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, who said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Zainab bint Khuzaymah, and she was the mother of The poor women from Banu Amir bin Sa’sa’ah, and before him she was with Tufail bin Al-Harith, so she died in the presence of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she did not stay there for long. With Him is only a little.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6806 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6807","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Al-Aliyah, a woman from Banu Bakr bin Kilab.”"
"6808","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Yahya bin Yusuf Al-Ruqi told us, Abu Muawiyah Al-Dareer, on the authority of Jamil bin Zaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Zayd bin Ka’b bin Ujrah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married A woman from Banu Ghifar. When she entered upon him and put on her clothes, he saw that her face was white, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Put on your clothes.” “And join your family,” and he ordered her to make friends. “These are not the names of the Kilabiyah, but rather they are the names of the daughter of Nu’man al-Ghafariyyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6808 - Ibn Mu’in Zayd is not trustworthy"
"6809","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Ala told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Qatada, he said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married one of the people of Yemen, Asma bint al-Nu’man al-Ghafariyya, and she was the daughter of Al-Numan bin Al-Harith bin Sharahil bin Al-Numan. When he consummated the marriage with her, he invited her and she said: “Come, you.” So he divorced her.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6809 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6810","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Zuhayr bin Al-Ala told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Qatada, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Umm Sharik Al-Ansariya from Banu Al-Najjar, and he said: “I would love to get married in... The Ansar.” Then he said: “I hate their jealousy.” He did not enter into it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6810 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6811","Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih told us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: Hafs ibn al-Nadr al-Sulami and Abd al-Qahir claimed Ibn Al-Sirri Al-Salami: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Sana’, the daughter of Asma’ Ibn Al-Salt Al-Salami, and she died before he consummated the marriage with her.”"
"6812","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: As for Al-Kalabiyya, there was disagreement about her name. Some of them said: She is Fatima bint Al-Dahhak bin Sufyan Al-Kalabi, and some of them said: She is Amra. Bint Zaid bin Ubaid bin Rawas bin Kilab bin Amer, and some of them said: She is Saba bint Sufyan bin Awf bin Ka’b bin Ubaid bin Ubayy. Bakr ibn Kilab, and some of them said: She is Al-Aaliyah bint Dhabyan, and some of them said: There was only one Kilabiyah, but there is a difference of opinion regarding “Her name,” and some of them said: “Rather, they are all of them, but each one of them has a story different from the story of its owner.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6812 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6813","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Zahid told us, Abdullah told us Bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told us, Ya’qub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of my nephew Ibn Shihab, on the authority of his uncle Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Al-Kalabiyya, and when she entered upon him, he approached her. She said: “I seek refuge in God from you.” He said: “You have sought refuge with a great burden on your family.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6813 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6814","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Asad Al-Harashi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Al-Awza’i said: I asked Al-Zuhri: Which of the Prophet’s wives, may God bless him and grant him peace, did she seek refuge from him? He said: Urwah told me, on the authority of Aisha, that when the daughter of Abi Al-Jun entered upon him and he approached her, she said: I seek refuge in God from you. He said: “You have been greatly distressed by your right to your family.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6814 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6815","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married a woman from Kindah, the wretched woman who had asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to To return her to her people and to separate from her, so he did and returned her with a man from the Ansar called: Abu Usayd al-Sa’idi.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6815 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6816","Abu Abdullah Al-Ansari told us an explanation of this story, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Utbah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Abi Awn al-Dawsi, who said: Al-Nu’man bin Abi John al-Kindi came and was He and his father's sons were going to find something that followed the drink, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Shall I not marry you to the most beautiful woman among the Arabs? She was a cousin of hers, and he died on her behalf, so she became orphaned, and she desired you and was engaged to you. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married her for twelve ounces and an inch, and he said: O Messenger of God, do not be short of her dowry. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I have not believed any of my women above this man, and I do not believe any of my daughters above this.” Al-Nu’man ibn Abi said John: You are sad, so he said: So, O Messenger of God, send to your family someone who will carry them to you, for I am going out with your messenger, and I will send your family. With him, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Abu Usayd al-Sa’idi, and when they came to her, she sat in her house and allowed him to enter, and Abu said Usayd: The wives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do not bet with men.Abu Usayd said - and that was after the veil was revealed and I sent for him and he made my matter easy for me - he said: There is a veil between you and the men with whom you speak, except One of your mahrams came and I accepted. Abu Usayd said: I stayed there for three days, then I carried myself with the woman on a camel in a palanquin, so I accepted her until I came to Medina and settled it in Bani Sa`idah, and the women of the neighborhood entered it and welcomed it and made it easy, and they left from it and mentioned its beauty. This spread throughout the city, and they talked about its arrival. Abu Usayd al-Saadi said: I returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was with Banu Amr ibn Awf, so I informed him, and a group of women entered her. When they heard of her beauty and she was one of the most beautiful women, she said: You are one of the kings, so if you want to be with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace be upon him, so seek refuge from him, for you will be happy with him and he desires you.
 Ibn Omar said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aoun, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married a Canadian woman in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal, the ninth year of the Hijra.”
 He said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father,Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik wrote to him asking him whether the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married the sister of Al-Ash’ath bin Qais? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never married her, nor did he marry a Canadian woman, except the sister of the Banu al-Jun. He owned her, and when he brought her “And the city came, and he looked at it and divorced her, and did not rebuild there.”
 He said: Hisham bin Muhammad mentioned that Ibn al-Ghasil narrated to him on the authority of Hamza bin Abi Usayd al-Sa’idi, on the authority of his father, and he was Badri. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Asma bint al-Nu’man al-Juniyah, so he sent me to bring her, and Hafsa said to Aisha: You brush it and I will comb it. They did so, then one of them said to her: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, likes a woman when she enters. She must say, “I seek refuge in God from you.” When she entered upon him, and he closed the door and lowered the curtain, he extended his hand to her, and she said, “I seek refuge in God from you.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, put his sleeve over his face, so he covered himself with it and said: “I sought refuge with Ma’adh three times.”Abu Usayd said: Then he came out to me and said: “O Abu Usayd, attach her to her family and provide her with providers” - meaning, as handlers - and she was She says: Call me the wretched one. Ibn Omar said: Hisham bin Muhammad said: Zuhayr bin Muawiyah Al-Ja’fi told me, “She died of an aggravation.”
 Hisham said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He succeeded Asma’ bint al-Nu’man al-Muhajir ibn Abi Umayyah, so he wanted Omar wanted to punish her, and she said: “By God, the veil was not imposed on me, nor was I called the Mother of the Believers.” So he stopped her.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6816 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"6817","Mukhlid ibn Ja`far al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad ibn Jarir told me, he said: Abu Ubaidah Muammar ibn al-Muthanna said: “Then the Messenger of God married May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the Kindah delegation came to him from Qitaila bint Qais, sister of Al-Ash’ath bin Qais, in the year ten, then he complained in the middle of Zero, then he was arrested on Monday, two days ago in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal, and she had not approached him nor had he entered into her. And some of them spent time. At the time of his marriage to her, he claimed that he married her a month before his death. Others claimed that he married her during his illness, and others claimed He recommended that a dead woman be given the choice, and if she wished, she chose marriage, so he married her to Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl in Hadramaut, so he informed Abu Bakr, and he said: I intended to burn a sacrifice for them. Omar bin Al-Khattab said: She is not one of the mothers of the believers, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not enter into marriage with her. He greeted her and did not impose the veil on her, and some of them claimed that she had apostatized."
"6818","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sought the help of Maria the Coptic, and she bore him Abraham.”"
"6819","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Mariah, daughter of Shimon, and she was the one whom he had given as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Al-Muqawqis, the companion of Alexandria, and he presented with her her sister Sirin and a eunuch called Mabur. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Sirin to Hassan ibn Thabit, and the Muqawqis are from the Copts, who are Christians. Maria gave birth to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abraham, in Dhul-Hijjah in the year eight of Hijra, and Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him, died in Medina when he was eighteen months old."
"6820","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Mahan told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, On the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, may God be pleased with him, he said: When Ibrahim, son of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, he said: “Indeed, he has Breastfeeding in Paradise”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6820 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6821","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Abar told me, Al-Hasan bin Hammad Sajjada told me, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told me, Abu Muadh Sulaiman bin Al-Arqam Al-Ansari narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Maria was given a gift. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with her was a cousin of hers. She said: Then a misfortune happened to her and she continued to be pregnant. She said: So he kept her alone with his son. Her paternal uncle, she said: Then the people of immorality and falsehood said: Because of his need for a child, he claimed someone else’s child, and his mother was low on milk, so she bought him A fertile woman, so he was fed with her milk, and his meat was good for him. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Then he brought it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. One day he greeted and said: “How do you see?” So I said: Whoever is fed with the meat of lamb, his meat is good. He said: “Not even the resemblance.” She said: Then I felt the jealousy that makes women feel when I said: I don’t see it. She said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard what the people were saying, so he said to Ali: “Take this sword and go and strike the neck of a cousin.” Maria is where I found him.” She said: So he went off and behold, he was at a wall on a palm tree with a patch of water. He said: Then when he looked at Ali, who had the sword. A trembling greeted him. He said: Then the cloth fell, so if God Almighty and Majestic did not create for him, men have nothing to wipe with.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6821 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6822","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, said: “Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, used to spend on Maria until he died, then Omar, may God be pleased with him, became May God spend on her behalf until she died during his caliphate.” Ibn Umar said: “And Maria, the mother of Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died.” In Muharram, the sixteenth year of the Hijra, Omar was seen bringing people to witness it, so Omar prayed over her and buried her in Al-Baqi’."
"6823","I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, mentioning a proven hadith on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The mother of Ibrahim was accusing a man, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that his neck be beheaded. They looked, and it was him.” Answered. I said to Yahya: Who spoke to you? He said: Affan, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah"
"6824","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli, Muhammad bin Ghalib Al-Dhabi, and Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, they said, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that a man was being accused of killing the mother of Abraham, the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: “Go and behead him.” Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, came to him, and he found himself in a saddle. He was cooling down there, so Ali said to him: Get out, so he gave him his hand and took him out, and behold, he was summoned and had no male. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that A Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6824 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6825","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took upon him and greeted him with my hand, so I went with him to his son Ibrahim while he was helping himself, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him in his lap until His soul came out. He said: So he put it down and cried. He said: So I said: Are you crying, O Messenger of God, and you forbid crying? He said: “I did not forbid him from crying.” Crying, but I have forbidden two foolish and immoral voices, a voice at the tune of amusement and play and the psalms of the devil, and a voice at the time of calamity and blows. Faces and slits of pockets, and this is mercy, and whoever does not have mercy will not have mercy, and had it not been a sincere promise and a true word, and that the first of us should join the last of us. We grieve for you more than this, and we are sad because of you, O Abraham. The eye weeps and the heart grieves, and we do not say anything that will displease the Lord.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6825 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6826","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mihran told us, Ubi told us, Muhammad ibn Musfa told us, Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, walked barefoot behind the funeral of his son Ibrahim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6826 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6827","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “I was informed that Maria, the mother of the Prophet’s son, may God bless him and grant him peace, died in Medina in the year seventeen, and the Commander of the Faithful, Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and she was buried in Al-Baqi’."
"6828","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb read to me, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi informed you Al-Mawali, on the authority of Faid, the freed slave of Ubayd Allah bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his grandmother Salma, his slave The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his maid said: Rarely did a person come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and complain to him of pain except that he said: He said to him: “Have cupping,” and there was no pain in his legs except that He told him: “Dye them with henna.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6828 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6829","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Yazid Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Maimuna bint Saad, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the child of adultery. He said: “Two sandals with which I strive to fight are dearer to me than freeing the child of illegitimate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6829 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6830","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Sinan Abu Farwa Al-Rahwi, Abu Yahya Al-Kala’i told us, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, who said: I entered upon Umaima, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: One day I was washing his hands while he was performing ablution when a man entered and said: O Messenger of God, I want to return to my family, so advise me. With a commandment that he memorized, he said: “Do not associate anything with God, even if you are cut up and burned with fire, and do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to leave So be separated from your family and your worldly life, and do not neglect a prayer intentionally, for whoever abandons it intentionally will be freed from the protection of God Almighty and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him be peace, and do not drink alcohol, for it is the beginning of every sin, and do not exceed your limits, for you will come on the Day of Resurrection with a stone on your neck. Seven lands, and do not flee on the day of the advance, for whoever flees on the day of the advance has incurred the wrath of God, and his abode is Hell, and a wretched destination. And spend on your family from your best, and do not lift your staff from them, but hide them in the name of God Almighty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6830 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"6831","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Abu Usama Al-Halabi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was pleased. May God bless him and grant him peace. Rayhana was from Banu Qurayza and she joined her family."
"6832","Abu Ubaidah Muammar ibn al-Muthanna said: One of the concubines of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Rayhana bint Zayd ibn Sam’un, from the Banu al-Nadir. Some of them said: From the Banu Qurayzah, and she used to live among the palm trees. “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to rest with her sometimes, and she was captured captive.” In Shawwal of the fourth year. Abu Ubaidah said: There are four of them: Maria al-Qibtiyya, Rayhana, and Jamila. He captured her during captivity, and his wives were almost afraid that He defeated them, and he had another valuable maid whom Zainab bint Jahsh had given him, and he abandoned her in connection with Safiyya bint Jahsh. He revived Dhul-Hijjah, Muharram, and Safar. “So when the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal came in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was pleased with Zainab. He entered upon her and she said: I do not know how to reward you, so she gave it to him, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6832 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6833","Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Ataki narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani narrated to me, Abu Salih narrated to me, al-Layth narrated to me, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: “The eldest daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Zainab, daughter of Khadija.”"
"6834","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi informed me, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Suleiman Al-Hashimi, saying: “Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born in the thirtieth year of the birth of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, and she died in the eighth year of Immigration"
"6835","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah told me Ibn Abi Bakr Ibn Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Hazm said: I narrated on the authority of Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “While I I am preparing for Mecca to my father. Hind bint Utbah bin Rabi’ah followed me and said: O daughter of Muhammad, did I not hear that you want to join With your father? She said: So I said: I did not want that, and she said: O cousin, do not do that if you need any luggage that will accompany you on your travel. And you convey it to your father, for I have your need.” Zainab said: “By God, I do not see her saying that except to do it.” She said: “But I feared her. I denied that I wanted that, so I prepared myself, and when I had finished preparing, my father-in-law, Kinanah ibn al-Rabi’, my brother-in-law, came and brought me a camel. So I rode him, and he took his bow and his quiver and went out with me during the day, leading her while she was in her howdah. The men of Quraysh spoke of that, so they went out in He sought it until they reached Dhū Tuwa, and the first to precede it were Habbar ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza and Nafi’. Ibn Abd Qais Al-Fihri, a relative of the Banu Abi Ubaid in Africa, was terrorized by a warrior with a spear while she was in her howdah.The woman was pregnant, according to what they claim, and when she was fed up, she threw her womb out, and her father-in-law was blessed and his body was destroyed. Then he said: He will not come near me. A man, except that I put an arrow in him, but the people hesitated from him, and Abu Sufyan came with a group of Quraysh and said: O man, refrain from destroying us until We will talk to you, so he stopped, so Abu Sufyan came and stood over him and said: You were not injured, you went out with the woman in front of the people in public and you knew Our calamity, our calamity, and what entered upon us from Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. People think that his daughter was brought out to him publicly, in front of the people of We have shown that this was due to a humiliation that befell us due to the calamity that occurred, and that this is a weakness and weakness in us, and by my life we have no right to detain her. On the authority of her father, there is a need, but bring the woman back, so that when the voice calms down and the people say, “We have returned her,” then be happy with her secretly and join her. With her father. He said: So he did so, so he returned and she remained for several nights until, when the sound had subsided, he took her out at night until he handed her over to Zayd ibn Harithah and his companion, and they came forward. with it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is a hadith in which there was a message between Abdullah bin Abi Bakr and Zainab, may God be pleased with them, and had it not been for him I would have ruled on the condition of a Muslim,It was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission, according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, in brief.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6835 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6836","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Muqri in Baghdad told us, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Maryam, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Yazid bin Al-Hadi told us, and Omar bin Abdullah bin Urwa told me, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, his daughter Zainab left Mecca with Kinanah or Ibn Kinanah, so they went out after her, and Habbar ibn Al-Aswad overtook her, and he continued stabbing her camel with his spear until it struck her. She vomited what was in her stomach and shed blood, and she became pregnant. Banu Hashim and Banu Umayyah quarreled over her, and Banu Umayyah said: We have more right to her. She was with their cousin Abu Al-Aas, and she was with Hind bint Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Hind used to say to her: This is because of Your father. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Zayd bin Haritha: “Will you not go and bring me Zainab?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Take my ring and give it to her.” So Zaid went off and left his camel, and he continued to be gentle until he met a shepherd and said: Who do you care for? He said: By Abi Al-Aas. He said: Who are these sheep? He said: To Zainab bint Muhammad, so he went with him about something, then he said to him: May I give you something that you can give to her and not mention to anyone? He said: Yes, So he gave him the ring, and the shepherd went off and brought his sheep in and gave them the ring, and she recognized it and said: Who gave this to you? He said: A man. She said: Where did you leave him? He said: In such-and-such a place. He said: So she remained silent until when night came, she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her: Ride. She said: No, but You ride in my hands, so he rode and she rode after him until she came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “She is the best of my daughters.” This was reported to Ali bin Al-Hussein, so he went to Urwa and said: There is no hadith that I have heard from you that you narrate that would diminish Fatima’s right. Urwa said: “By God, I do not like to have what is between the East and the West, and I deprive Fatima, may God be pleased with her, of a right that is hers. And as for what follows: “It is permissible for you that I never narrate it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"6837","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl informed us, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ibn Abi told us Maryam - the hadith is immoral. Imam Abu Bakr said at the end of this word: The best of my daughters means: that is, one of the best of my daughters, because the news It is authenticated and authentic on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that Fatima, peace be upon her, is the mistress of the women of this nation - and likewise it is proven on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Fatima is the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise, except Maryam bint Imran.” And I assumed from this type that the Arabs would You say better: you mean better, and in my book there is what is rich and sufficient, God willing, the Almighty, and Imam Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, healed May God narrate from him in explaining this word, and we will not add more to what he says, since he is truly the leading Imam, but under this word there is a letter that denotes To another meaning other than what he said, which is that knowledge surrounds that Zainab is older than Fatima, may God be pleased with her, in age and was born before her. It can be said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meant better when he said: that is, the eldest and oldest of my children, and God knows best."
"6838","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Hazm, he said: “Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. “Eighth year of the Hijra”
 Muhammad bin Omar said: Hisham bin Muhammad al-Kalbi told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, He said: “The oldest son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Al-Qasim, then Zainab. Zainab married Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’, and she bore him Ali. And Umamah, about which Abu Al-Aas says:
 [Simple Sea]
 I mentioned Zainab when she bequeathed my land... so I said, “Irrigation for someone who lives in the sanctuary.”
 The daughter of Al-Amin, may God reward her, is righteous...And every Baal will praise what they know"
"6839","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, He said: “Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the eldest of his daughters, and the reason for her death was that when she left Mecca for The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Habbar bin Al-Aswad and another man overtook her, and one of them pushed her, according to what was said, and she fell on a rock. So she miscarried when she was pregnant, and she shed blood, and her pain did not go away until she died from it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6839 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6840","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: When the people of Mecca were sent to ransom their captives Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to ransom Abu Al-Aas with a necklace, and Khadija had brought it to Abu Al-Aas when he built Upon her, when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw her, he was very kind to her and said: “If you decide to release her prisoner and respond to her... “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6840 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6841","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz told me, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, Abdullah bin Al-Samh told us, On the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: Zainab, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Abu Al-Aas’s wife as a neighbor. She married her to Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’, “so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted her to be close to her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6841 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6842","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, Abdullah bin Shabib told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Abu Bakr told me Ibn Abi Uwais, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: Yahya Ibn Sa`id, and Salih Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: When he was captured Abu Al-Aas Zainab said: Indeed, I have rewarded Abu Al-Aas, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have rewarded whoever Zainab has rewarded, for he gives protection to “The Muslims are the lowest.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6842 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6843","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, On the authority of Musa bin Jubayr Al-Ansari, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik Al-Ghifari, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to her Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’ to ask me to get some protection from your father, so she went out. So she raised her head from the door of her room while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in the morning prayer. She said: O people, I am Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I have rewarded Abu Al-Aas. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, finished praying, he said: “O people, I have no knowledge.” With this until you heard him. Indeed, he bestows the reward upon the lowest of Muslims.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6843 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6844","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail, the jurist in Al-Ray, told us, Abu Hatim told us, Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Ruqi told us, Issa told us Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, and Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I saw on Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “And he handed over a silk shirt to Sira.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6844 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6845","Abu Omar Ahmad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Omar bin Hafs told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Shazan told us, Saeed bin Al-Salt told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: Zainab, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he went out with her funeral and we went out with him, and we saw him sad and sad. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered her grave, he came out radiant. Color and we asked him about that, and he said: “She was a sick woman, and I remembered the severity of death and the congestion of the grave, so I prayed to God to lighten About her
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6845 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6846","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, Dawud bin Al-Husayn told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned his daughter Zainab divorced her husband, Abu Al-Aas, two years after her first marriage, but he did not make a marriage.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6846 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6847","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah, Abu Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Urwa, in naming those who went out the first time to migrate to Abyssinia before the departure Jafar and his companions: “Uthman bin Affan with his wife Ruqaya, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6848","I heard Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya saying: I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq saying: I heard Abdullah bin Muhammad Bin Suleiman bin Jaafar bin Suleiman Al-Hashimi, says: “Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born in the year thirty-three of the birth of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6849","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told me, Salit bin Muslim Al-Amiri, from Bani Amir bin Luay, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, he said: Saad told me, he said: When Othman wanted Ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him, went to the land of Abyssinia. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Take a telegram with you.” He said: Akhal One of you is patient with his friend, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them, and said: “Come to me.” With their news.” Asmaa returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was with him. She said: O Messenger of God, come out. A donkey was saddled, so he loaded it on him and took it toward the sea. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Bakr, they are the first to He migrated after Lot and Abraham, peace and blessings be upon them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6849 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6850","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “She lived Ruqayya, may God be pleased with her, until Othman, may God be pleased with him, married her, and from Ruqayyah a boy named Abdullah was born, and he died when he was young. After that, Othman was nicknamed Abu Abdullah.” Ibn Ishaq said: “And some people of knowledge told me that a young man from Abyssinia They saw Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was there with Uthman. She was one of the best of people, and they went to see her. They would be amazed at its beauty until God killed them in the battle when the Negus marched against his enemy. Ibn Ishaq said: It is said that Abdullah bin Uthman died in Jumada al-Awwal in the year four when he was six years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6850 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6851","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Salamah told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “Behind the Prophet, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Othman and Usama bin Zaid visited Ruqayyah during her illness, and he went out to Badr while she was in pain, so Zaid bin Haritha came to Al-Udhaibah. With the good news, Ruqayyah, may God be pleased with her, had died, so we heard the cry, and by God, we did not believe the good news until we saw the captives.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6851 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6852","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, Radi On his authority, he said: When Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No man who neglects to enter the grave.” “His family tonight.” Othman did not enter the grave. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6852 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6853","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Falayh told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali bin Osama, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I witnessed the burial of the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting on the grave. And I saw his eyes filling with tears, so he said: “Is there a man among you who did not have intercourse with his family tonight?” Abu Talha said: I, O Messenger of God, said: “So descend into her grave.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6853 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6854","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, and Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Saeed Al-Razi told us, dictating in Al-Jami’, Abu Zur’ah al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Al-Mu’affa bin Sulaiman Al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Zaid Bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Muhammad Abdullah bin Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Othman’s wife, with a comb in her hand, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out of Just then, I shook his head, and he said to me: “How do you find Abu Abdullah?” I said: Fine. He said: “Honor him, for he is one of my companions most similar to me in character.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is the text, as Ruqayyah died. In the third year of the Hijra, at the conquest of Badr, and Abu Hurairah only converted to Islam after the conquest of Khaybar, and God knows best, and we have recorded it with a chain of transmission. ""another""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6854 - Sahih Munkar Al-Matn"
"6855","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I entered upon Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with her in her hand. A comb, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just left me, so I shook his head and he said to me: “How do you find Othman?” She said: So I said: Fine. He said: “Honor him, for he is one of my companions most similar to me in character.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “And I have no doubt that the father of Huraira, may God Almighty have mercy on him, narrated this hadith on the authority of an early companion of the Companions, who entered upon Ruqayyah, may God be pleased with her, but I had asked for him. I tried my best, but I did not find him in time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6855 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6856","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Nasr al-Muzaki and al-Hasan ibn Halim al-Maruzian informed me that it had passed, saying: Abu al-Mawjih reported, Abdan informed, Abdullah, Yunus bin Yazid told me, he said: And Ibn Shihab said: And it has reached us, and God knows best, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore an oath on the day Badr was given to Uthman by his share. He had left behind his wife Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was afflicted with measles, so Zaid came. Ibn Haritha was giving good tidings of the conquest, and he had a camel with him, and Othman was at the grave of Ruqayyah, may God be pleased with her, burying it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6856 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6857","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “The name of Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Umayyah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her to Uthman after Ruqayyah in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal, and she entered upon him in Jumada al-Akhira in the year eight, and she died while she was with Uthman in Sha`ban in the year nine. She was the mother of Atiyya. “The Ansar woman who bathed her in the presence of women from the Ansar.”"
"6858","Musa bin Ismail Al-Qadi told us, my father told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Saeed Al-Musahaqi told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, He said: “Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and Uthman married Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6858 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6859","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Munadi told us, Dawud bin Muhabbar told us, Jisr bin Farqad told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: When Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, Omar passed by Uthman and said: Do you have Hafsa, the daughter of Omar? He did not answer him anything, so Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Perhaps God Almighty, O Omar, will bring you a son-in-law who is better for you than Othman.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Omar’s daughter. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Umm Kulthum to Uthman, and before that Abu Bakr had proposed to her and Omar, may God be pleased with him, had proposed to her. On their behalf, he did not marry her off, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best intercessor for Uthman is that I do not marry off my daughters, but God Almighty makes them in marriage.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6859 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6860","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told me, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Masry told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, he told me Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him: That the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When he greeted, he found Othman bin Affan while he was distressed, and he said: “What is the matter with you, O Othman?” He said: May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, and my mother. Did he enter upon any of the people as he entered upon me? The daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. May God have mercy on her, and the relationship between you and me was severed forever. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you say that, O Uthman, and this Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, commands me, by the command of God Almighty, to marry her sister Umm Kulthum to you, on the basis of her friendship and on the basis of Her waiting period.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her to her.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6860 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6861","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah told us, Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, H. Abu Abdullah told us Al-Saffar, Ahmad bin Mahdi told us, Hajjaj bin Abi Mani’ told us, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ziyad said: I asked Al-Zuhri, Regarding silk, do women wear it or not? He claimed that Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, told him that he “saw a silk dress wearing Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “Sira” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording, rather they narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Jarir and Yunus bin Yazid on the authority of Al-Zuhri. ""abbreviated""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6861 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6862","Abu Al-Abbas Ismail bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Mikaal told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Musa Al-Hafiz Abdan told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Musa Al-Hafiz Abdan told us, Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan, Al-Walid bin Al-Walid told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thuban told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she said: O Messenger of God, my husband is good. Or Fatima's husband? She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, then he said: “Your husband is one who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him.” So she turned and he said to her: “Come on, what did I say?” She said: I said: My husband is one of those who love God and His Messenger and whom God and His Messenger love. He said: “Yes, and I will add to you that I entered Paradise and saw his abode but did not I saw one of my friends climbing it in his house.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6862 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6863","Abu Jafar Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Amr bin Khalid told us, Abi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, said: None of Abdul Muttalib’s daughters embraced Islam except Safiyya. He said: “And he contributed to her.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, two shares,” and she was the sister of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib on his father’s and his mother’s side."
"6864","Muhammad bin Muzaffar Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Sufyan told me Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Muawiyah Al-Utbi in Egypt, my father told me, Saeed told us Ibn Katheer Ibn Ufayr said: “Safiyya bint Abd al-Muttalib, the mother of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, died in the year twenty, which was the same day she died. And seventy, and Omar bin Al-Khattab prayed over her and buried her in Al-Baqi’."
"6865","Abu Abdullah Al-Isfahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Wasfiyya, the daughter of Abd al-Muttalib bin Hashim and her mother was Hala bint Wahib bin Abd Manaf bin Zahra bin Kilab, and she was the sister of Hamza bin Abd. Al-Muttalib to his mother. He had married her in pre-Islamic times to Al-Harith ibn Harb ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams, and she bore him Safiyya, then he left her in charge. Al-Awwam bin Khuwaylid bin Usayd, and she bore him Al-Zubayr, Al-Sa’ib, and Abdul-Kaaba. She converted to Islam and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She migrated to Medina and lived after him until the caliphate of Omar bin Al-Khattab, and she narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6866","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Asadi al-Hafiz, in Hamadan, told us: Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Farawi told us, Umm Farwah bint Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr narrated to us, on the authority of her father, on the authority of Her grandfather, Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his mother Safiyya bint Abdul Muttalib: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the ditch, he put his wives in a dugout. He was called Fa'ri', and he put Hassan bin Thabit with them, so the Jews came to Al-Atm, seeking the forelocks of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he advanced. A man who had a crush on us, so I said to him: O Hassan, go to him and kill him. He said: By God, that would not have been in me, and if that had been in me, I would have been with him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said to him: Strap this sword on my arm. So he tied it, so I got up to him and struck his head until I cut it off, so I said To him: Take his ears and throw him at them, and he said: By God, what is wrong with me? So I took his head and threw him at them, and they stumbled while they were there. They say: “We know that Muhammad would not leave his family behind when no one was with them.” She said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Hassan fought hard against the polytheists with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was with us in the fort. When he returned, he would follow him as he returned. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then Saad bin Muadh passed by us and he had taken a saffra while he was at a wedding a few days before that. He shudders
 [The sea of rage]

 A little time for the camel to catch up with the excitement... There is no harm in death if the time comes.”
 Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “I did not see a more beautiful man than him on that day.” This is a large, strange hadith with this chain of transmission. It was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6866 - Strange and it was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission"
"6867","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abd al-Muttalib - Urwah said: And I heard her say: “I am the first woman to kill a man. I was in Farea’ Hisn.” Hassan bin Thabit, and Hassan was with us among the women and children when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrenched. Safiyya said: “Then a man from... Jews, so he started going around the fort, so I said to Hassan: This Jew is in the fort as you see, and he is not safe from pointing out our private parts, and he has been busy. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions, go to him and kill him. He said: May God forgive you, O daughter of Abdul Muttalib, and God has “You know what kind of owner I am.” Safiyya said: “When he said that and I did not see anything with him, I detained myself and took a pillar from the fort, then I descended from the fort to him.” So I struck him with the pillar until I killed him, then I returned to the fort and said: O Hassan, come down and seize him, for he did not prevent me from “I rob him, but he is a man.” He said: “I have no need to rob him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6867 - Urwa did not catch Safiyya"
"6868","Just as Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Salamah bin Bakht, on the authority of Amira bint Ubayd Allah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Umm Durrah, on the authority of Barrah bint Abi Tajarah, who said: The Quraysh did not deny the Duha prayer. You only deny the time, “And when the time of the afternoon prayer came, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would disperse to the paths and pray, singly and in pairs.” So he walked. Talib bin Umair and Hatib bin Abd Shams were praying in a group of soldiers, some of them looking at each other, when Ibn al-Asidi attacked them. And Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, and they were indecent, so they threw stones at them for an hour until they came out and left while they were getting stronger, and they came to Abu Jahl. And Abu Lahab and Uqba bin Abi Muayt, so they reported the news to them, so they set out for them in the morning, and they used to leave in the early afternoon. So they performed ablution and prayed, but while they were in a village, Abu Jahl, Uqba, Abu Lahab, and a number of their fools attacked them. So they oppressed them, and they attacked them, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, demonstrated Islam, spoke of it, called on them, and defended themselves, and Talib bin Umair went to Abu Jahl and hit him, wounding him. They took him and tied him up, then Abu Lahab stood up to him until he unbuckled him. He was his brother’s son, so it was said to Arwa bint Abd al-Muttalib: Don’t you see that your son Tulayb has followed Muhammad and become his servant? Arwa was She converted to Islam, so she said: The best of days for Tulayb is the day he sacrifices himself on behalf of his cousin, and he has brought the truth from God Almighty. So they said: Have you followed Muhammad? She said: Yes, so some of them went out to Abu Lahab and informed him. He went back and entered upon her and said: It is amazing for you and for your following Muhammad and you left. The religion of Abdul Muttalib, she said: That has happened, so stand up without your brother’s son, and help him and prevent him. If his matter becomes apparent, you have the choice if you wish. To join him or to follow your religion, and if you had not excused your nephew, he said: And we have power over all the Arabs. Then they say: He came with a new religion. He said: Then Abu Lahab left.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6868 - I did not find her conversion to Islam except from Al-Waqidi"
"6869","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, he said: “Umm Hani’ bint Abi Talib, her name is Hind, and her mother is Fatima bint Asad bin Hashim. This is how Imam Abu Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, mentioned the name of Umm Hani. News circulated that her name was Fatah."
"6870","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, H. Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Murrah, on the authority of Fakhta, who is the mother of Hani, the daughter of Abu Talib, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He prayed the Fajr prayer on the day of the conquest in one garment, with eight rak'ahs separated between its two ends.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6870 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6871","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: And in what was mentioned The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed Umm Hani to his uncle Abu Talib before he was inspired, and Hubayra ibn Abi addressed her to him. He gave her in marriage to Hubayra, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Umar, you married off Hubayra and left me.” So he said: O son of my brother, I have married To them, and the generous rewards the generous. Then she converted to Islam, and Islam separated her from Hubayra, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to her. herself and said: By God, I would have loved you in pre-Islamic times, so how could I do in Islam? But I am a young woman, so I hate that they would harm you. Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6871 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6872","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, may God be pleased with her, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to me, and I apologized to him and he excused me.” Then God Almighty revealed: {O Prophet, indeed We have made lawful for you your wives to whom you have received their wages} [Al-Ahzab: 50] - to His saying - {those who emigrated with you} [Al-Ahzab: 50] She said: “I was not permissible for him because I did not immigrate with him. I was one of the freedmen.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6872 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6873","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub and Abu Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, saying: Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab told us. Ibn Ata’, Saeed Ibn Abi Arouba reported, on the authority of Ayyub Ibn Safwan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, that Ibn Abbas did not pray the noon prayer until We brought him to Umm Hani, and I said to her: Tell Ibn Abbas what you told us. Umm Hani said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered.” He greeted my house and prayed the Duha prayer, eight rak’ahs. Then Ibn Abbas came out, saying: “I read what was between the two tablets, and I did not recognize the sunrise prayer.” Except for the Hour” {They glorify the evening and sunrise} [p. 18], then Ibn Abbas said: “This is the sunrise prayer.” Abdullah bin Abbas narrated On the authority of Umm Hani, another hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6873 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6874","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Iyad bin Abdullah told me, On the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, told him She said: O Messenger of God, my mother’s son Ali claims that he killed the one whom I rewarded, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have rewarded whomever I rewarded.” She paid"
"6875","A third hadith by Abdullah bin Abbas on the authority of Umm Hani: “Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr Al-Hamdani, Sa’dan bin Al-Walid, Baya’ Al-Sabiri, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, may God be pleased with her. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Do you have any food that I can eat?” He was hungry, so I said, “I have some dried crumbs, and I am ashamed to bring them to you.” So he said, “Come to them,” so I broke them and scattered them on them. salt and said: “Is there any Edam?” She said: O Messenger of God, I only have some vinegar. He said: “Come to it.” When I brought it to him, he poured it over his food, and he ate some of it, then thanked God. God Almighty, then He said: “How good is vinegar, O Umm Hani, no house will be deserted in which there is vinegar.” Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, narrated On their authority, on the authority of Umm Hani’"
"6876","Muhammad bin Issa Al-Razi, the merchant in Baghdad, told me. Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’affa bin Sulayman told us, Hakim bin Hakim told us. Nafi’, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon Umm Hani’ And a hanging water bottle, so he drank while standing.” A hadith was narrated by the sons of Umm Hani on the authority of their fathers, on the authority of her."
"6877","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid, Al-Hafiz Al-Asadi in Hamadan, told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Abi Musab told us, and Muhammad bin Abd. Allah bin Rawad, they said: Uthman bin Abdullah bin Abi Atiq told us, Sa`id bin Amr bin Ja`dah bin Hubayra told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, Ja`dah bin Hubayra, he said: I heard my mother, Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God God Almighty favored the Quraysh with seven qualities that He did not give to anyone before them and will not give to anyone after them. Among them is prophecy, among them is veiling, and among them is Al-Saqaya, and their victory over the elephant, while they worshiped none but God, and they worshiped God for ten years when no one else worshiped Him, and a Surah was revealed about them that did not He will involve others in it in order to unite the Quraysh.” It was narrated on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah bin Hubayra, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Hani’."
"6878","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar, the ascetic and just, told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Ibn Nu’aym told us, Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ Al-Abdi, who is Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah bin Hubayra, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Hani, who said: “If I could hear the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night while I was on my family’s throne.”"
"6879","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm bin Masqala Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Arwa bint Abdul Muttalib had converted to Islam. Salama bin Bakht told me, on the authority of Umairah bint Ubayd Allah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Umm Durrah, on the authority of Barrah bint Abi Tajarah, who said: “The Quraysh Do not deny the Duha prayer, you are only denying the time.” I said: The hadith is as mentioned above, so we will not repeat it here, so ponder. Al-Hakim said: This is a hadith. It was narrated by Al-Madani with this chain of narration, and Al-Waqidi is presented in this knowledge, and he ruled on it, and Hisham bin Urwa denied that it had been “The most peaceful of the daughters of Abdul Muttalib other than Safiyya, Umm al-Zubayr, and God knows best.”"
"6880","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told me about the validity of this lineage, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abd told us. “God Al-Zubairy”"
"6881","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Abi told me Al-Zinad, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: I went to Marwan ibn al-Hakam and told him: A woman from your family was divorced, so I passed away. As she was moving, I blamed that on her, so they said: Fatima bint Qays commanded us, and she informed us that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He ordered her to move to the son of Umm Maktum when her husband divorced her.” Marwan said: Yes, she ordered them to do that. Urwa said: So I said: By God, Aisha was severely criticized for that, and she said: “Fatima was with her husband in a brutal place, so there was fear for “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6881 - True"
"6882","Muhammad bin Ali al-Sana'ani told me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq told me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ataa told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Asim bin Thabit told me that Fatima bint Qais, the sister of al-Dahhak bin Qais, told him that she was with a man from Bani Qays. Makhzum - and he mentioned the length of the hadith and said at the end - When her waiting period had ended, Abu Jahm and Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan proposed to her. So she consulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “As for Muawiyah, he is a tramp who has no money, and as for Abu Jahm, I fear for you his discord.” So he ordered me to marry Osama bin Zaid, so I married Osama bin Zaid. Jabir bin Abdullah narrated on the authority of Fatima bint Qays
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6882 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6883","Ismail bin Ali Al-Khatbi told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal, and Muhammad bin Abdoos bin Kamil told us, saying: Wahb bin Baqiyya al-Wasiti told us, Ja`far bin Sulaiman al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, She said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the woman suffering from menstruation, and he said: “She stays for the days of her period, then she bathes and prays when she is pure.” Aisha and Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with them, narrated on the authority of Fatima bint Qais
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6883 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6884","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Salem Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: Fatima bint Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless her. And she said: I am menstruating. He said: “That is not menstruation, rather it is a sweat so that she may sit for days of menstruation, then she should bathe, then “You put on a piece of clothing and pray.”"
"6885","So Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Sulaiman al-Tustari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi`, Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that Fatima bint Qays asked for a fatwa The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: I have menstruation but have not become pure, should I give up prayer? He said: “This is a sweat that is not menstruation, and one wash is more complete than ablution.”"
"6886","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And among the women of Quraysh who accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Al-Shifa bint Abdullah, who was the mother of Sulayman bin Abi Hathamah Al-Qurashi and my father’s grandmother. Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah»"
"6887","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Al-Shifa’ is a daughter.” Abdullah converted to Islam before the conquest, and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6888","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad told us that Abu Bakr bin Sulaiman bin Abi Hathamah Al-Qurashi told him that a man from the Ansar An ant came out with it, which indicated that Al-Shifa’ bint Abdullah was ruqyah from the ant. He came to her and asked her to perform ruqyah for him, and she said: By God, I did not perform ruqyah. Since I converted to Islam, the Ansari went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him what Shefa said, so he called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Show it to me.” So I showed it to him, and he said: “Perform ruqyah for him and teach her to Hafsa just as you taught her the Book.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs, and Abu Bakr bin Suleiman heard it from his grandmother.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6888 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6889","As Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, Al-Jarrah bin Al-Dahhak Al-Kindi, on the authority of Kurayb bin Sulaiman Al-Kindi, who said: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, took me by the hand until he set out I was brought to a man from the Quraysh, one of the Banu Zahra, called Ibn Abi Hathamah. He was praying close to him until Ibn Abi Hathamah finished praying. Then he turned to us with his face, and Ali bin Al-Hussein said to him: The hadith you mentioned on the authority of your mother regarding ruqyah, and he said: Yes, you told me. My mother, she used to recite a ruqyah in pre-Islamic times, and when Islam came she said: I will not recite ruqyah until I consult the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “Perform the incantation as long as it does not involve any association with God Almighty.”"
"6890","Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Matar al-Zahid al-Adl narrated to us the hadith in its authentic form, dictating in the year thirty-seven and thirty-seven. One hundred, Mahmoud bin Muhammad al-Wasiti told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Abu Ishaq al-Harawi told us, Othman bin Omar bin Othman told me Ibn Sulaiman Ibn Abi Hathama Al-Qurashi Al-Adawi, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, Othman Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother Al-Shifa’ bint Abd By God, she used to perform ruqa in pre-Islamic times, and when she migrated to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she came to him and said: O Messenger By God, I used to perform ruqa in the pre-Islamic era, and I decided to show it to you. He said: “Show it,” so I showed it to him, and it was one of them. The ant’s ruqyah, and he said: “Run with it and teach it to Hafsa: In the name of God, it is crucified when it returns from their mouths and does not harm anyone. Oh God, reveal Bravery is the Lord of mankind.” He said: “You should recite it on a stick of vines seven times and put it in a clean place, then rub it on a stone and paint it in the light.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6890 - Ibn Ma’in was asked about Uthman but he did not know him"
"6891","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan told me, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told me, Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: Al-Asma’i said: “An ant is a sore that comes out In junub and other things.”"
"6892","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told me, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, On the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Shifa’, the daughter of Abdullah, she said: “One day I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I asked him and complained to him. He started to apologize to me and I blamed him,” she said: “Then It was time for the first prayer, so I entered my daughter’s house while she was at Sharhabeel Ibn Hassana’s house. I found her husband in the house, so I started blaming him and said: You are here. Praying while you are here. He said: O aunt, do not blame me. I had two dresses, one of which was borrowed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, I blame him and this. Likewise, Sharhabeel said: “One of them was a shield, so we patched it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6892 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6893","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “And among those who Amer bin Rabi’ah immigrated to Abyssinia, and with him was his wife Laila bint Abi Hathamah bin Ghanim bin Awf bin Ubaid bin Awayj bin Adi. Ibn Ka'b"
"6894","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: He told me Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, who said: “No female emigrants came to Medina more first than Laila bint Abi Hathamah.” With my father, her husband is Amer bin Rabia.”"
"6895","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abdul told me Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Ubaid Allah bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Amer bin Rabia, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother, Umm Abdullah bint Abi Hathamah said: “By God, we are going to travel to the land of Abyssinia, for Amer went to attend to some of our needs, as Omar came Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, until he stopped me while he was following his polytheism, and we were facing trials and hardship from him, and he said: This is the beginning, mother. Abdullah? I said: Yes, by God, we will leave in God’s land. You have harmed us and oppressed us, until God makes a way out for us. He said: May God be with you, and I saw him. Raqqa, but I did not see her. Then he left, and seeing our departure made him sad.” He said: “Amer ibn Rabi’ah came from that need of his, and I said: “O Abu. Abdullah, if you saw Omar just now and his tenderness and sadness for us, he said: Do you hope for his conversion to Islam? I said: Yes. He said: What you saw will not be delivered until the speech is delivered. He said, despairing of what he saw of his harshness and cruelty towards “Islam”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6895 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6896","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Among them is Fatima bint Al-Khattab bin Nufayl, the wife of Sa’id bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, and she had converted to Islam before Omar, and she was “One of the first pledges of allegiance in Mecca.”"
"6897","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Omar Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mustamli told us, Ali bin Khashram told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Uthman Abi Al-Ala’ Al-Basri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him: “Indeed, a man from Banu Zahra He met Omar, before he converted to Islam, wearing a sword, and said: Where are you going? He said: I want to kill Muhammad. He said: Shall I not point out to you the wonder, O Omar, that your circumcised Saeed and your sister have become righteous and abandoned the religion they followed? He said: Then Omar walked towards them, complaining, until he approached the door. He said: There was with them a man called Khabab, who was reciting Surat Taha to them. When he heard Khabbab, with the name of Omar, entered under their bed, and Omar entered and said: What is this beauty that I saw with you? They said: Except for a conversation that we talked between us. He said: Perhaps you have become patient and abandoned the religion that you are following. Then his circumciser, Sa`id bin Zaid, said to him: O Omar, what do you think if the truth is not in your religion? Then he went to circumcise him and had intercourse with him severely. He said: Then his sister pushed him away from her husband, so he struck He turned to her face, and her face bled, so she said while she was angry: O Omar, what do you think if the truth is in something other than your religion, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah? I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: When Omar despaired, he said: Give me this book that you have so that I can read it. His sister said: You It is an abomination and only the purified should touch it. Arise and wash or perform ablution” - Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6897 - It has been dropped"
"6898","We told him Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab, about Hamdan, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Burd al-Antaki told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. Al-Hunaini, Osama bin Zayd bin Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When my sister opened the door to me, I said: O enemy. Did she get sick? She said, and he raised something and said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, whatever you are doing, do it, for I have converted to Islam. He said: So I went in and sat on the bed, and suddenly there was a newspaper in the middle of the house. I said: What is this newspaper here? She said: Leave it alone, Ibn Al-Khattab. You do not perform ghusl due to ritual impurity, nor do you purify yourself, and only the purified can touch this.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6898 - It was dropped from it and it was weak and disconnected"
"6899","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ubayd Allah bin Saeed bin Katheer bin Ufayr told us, Ubayy told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Abu Thafal Al-Marri, said: I heard Rabah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Sufyan, saying: My grandmother, Asma bint Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr, told me, She heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no prayer for the one who does not perform ablution, and there is no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of God Almighty over him. He who does not believe in me and does not love the Ansar does not believe in God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6899 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary in this place"
"6900","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he informed us Abd al-Malik bin Qudamah bin Ibrahim al-Jumahi, Omar bin Shuaib, Amr bin Shuaib’s brother in the Levant, told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: Umm Nabih, daughter of Al-Hajjaj, the mother of Abdullah bin Amr, was a woman who used to give gifts to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and used to please him. One day, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a visitor came and said: “How are you, Umm Abdullah?” She said: My father and mother are fine, O Messenger of God. He said: “And how is Abdullah?” She said: You and my mother are fine, and Abdullah is a man who has renounced the world. He said: “How?” She said: He forbade sleep, so he does not sleep, nor does he break his fast, and meat was forbidden, so he does not eat meat, and does not give his family their due. He said: “Where is he?” She said: He left just now and is about to return, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he comes to you, detain him for me.” He did not tarry. Abdullah came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Yourself has a right over you, and your family has a right over you.”"
"6901","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And among the women of Banu Amir bin Luayy are Sahlah bint Suhail bin Amr bin Abd Shams bin Abd Wad bin Nasr bin Malik bin Hasal. She was among those who migrated with her husband, Abu Hudhayfah, to the land of Abyssinia, and she gave birth to him in Abyssinia, Muhammad ibn Abi Hudhayfah."
"6902","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sahlah, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah, that she mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she was safe. Abu Hudhayfah’s servant and his intercourse with her, so she claimed that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her to breastfeed him,” so she breastfed him while he was a man. After he witnessed a full moon
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6902 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6903","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed and Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded Sahlah, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah To breastfeed Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah, until the jealousy of Abu Hudhayfah goes away. She breastfed him while he was a man.” Rabi’ah said: And it was a concession for Salim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6903 - True"
"6904","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “And among the women of Quraysh Umm Habibah, and her name is Hamnah bint Jahsh, the sister of Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she is from Asad bin Khuzaymah, an ally of Banu “sun slave”"
"6905","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Abu Al-Nu’man Arim told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw in the mosque a rope stretched between two posts and said: “What is this rope?” It was said: O Messenger of God, Hamnah bint Jahsh prays, and when she becomes tired she clings to the rope. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let her pray as long as she can.” She has the strength to endure, so when she is tired, let her sit.” Ali told me, Ismail told us, Abu al-Nu’man told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, By the same token
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6905 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6906","Abu Ja`far bin Ubaid al-Hafiz and Abdan bin Yazid al-Daqqaq told us about Hamdan, saying: Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Ishaq bin told us. Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Farawi, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of his brother Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hamnah bint Jahsh, that she was told: Your brother has been killed. She said: May God have mercy on him. To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. Then she was told: Your uncle Hamza was killed. She said: To Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return. Then it was said to her: Your husband was killed. She said: We made him sad. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed To marry a woman to a branch that is for nothing.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6906 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6907","Abdul Aziz bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dabbas informed me, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Sayegh told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us. Al-Hazami, Omar bin Othman Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Urwa told me that Aisha told him that Umm Habiba Bint Jahsh, the wife of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and she is the sister of Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She told him that she had had her menstruation seven years, so she asked him for a fatwa about that. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is not the case.” With menstruation, but this is a sweat, so wash yourself and then pray.” She would wash in a place until the water rose to the redness of the blood, then she would get up and pray."
"6908","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Hafiz told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, that his paternal aunt, Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh, came to Aisha and said: I fear that I will be among the people of Hell, I had not prayed for about two years, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Let you stop praying every month on the days you recite it, and then perform ablution.” For every prayer, it is only a sweat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6908 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6909","Abu al-Nadr, the jurist, told us about al-Tabaran, and Abu Yahya al-Khatan, the jurist in Bukhara, told us: Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Baghdadi, then Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti, Abdul-Rahman bin Othman bin Ibrahim told us, my father told us, on the authority of my grandfather Muhammad bin Hatib, on the authority of his mother, Umm Jamil, She said: I came with you to the point that when I was out of the city a night or two later, I cooked something for you, then the firewood was cut off, so I went out to ask for firewood. So I took the pot and leaned on your arm. I approached Medina and brought you to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib, who was the first to be named after you, wiped your head and called for blessings, then spit in you and spit on your hand and said: “Go.” Wretched, Lord of people, heal you, you are the healer. There is no cure except your healing, a healing that does not leave behind an illness.” She said: “I did not leave you until your hand was healed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6909 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6910","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And among them was a mother Ayman, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his custodian, whose name is Baraka. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inherited five total. And a piece of sheep, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, freed Umm Ayman when he married Khadija, so he married her to Ubaid bin Yazid from the Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and she bore him Ayman, and he was killed as a martyr on the Day of Khaybar. Zaid bin Harithah was Khadija’s wife, so she gave him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, freed him and married him to Umm Ayman after the prophethood, and she bore him Usama bin Zaid.”"
"6911","Yahya bin Saeed bin Dinar told me, on the authority of a sheikh, from Banu Saad bin Bakr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to Umm Ayman: “Oh, his mother.” And when he looked at her, he said: “These are the rest of my household.”"
"6912","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah told us, Abu Malik Al-Nakhi told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anzi, on the authority of Umm Ayman, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose during the night to bring pottery to me near the house. So he urinated in it, so I woke up during the night thirsty and drank from the pot without realizing it. When morning came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh Umm Ayman, lead my people to that pottery and throw away what is in it. I said: By God, I have drunk what is in it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed until his molars became visible, then he said: “As for you, your stomach will never grieve after him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6912 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6913","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “The mother of Ayman, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his custodian, died at the beginning of the caliphate of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him.”"
"6914","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Rumaih told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told me, my father told me, he said: Khasim Ibn Abi Al-Furat, the client of Usama. Ibn Zaid Al-Hasan Ibn Umayyah and disputed with him, and Ibn Abi Al-Furat said to him in his speech: O Ibn Baraka, you want Umm Ayman, so Al-Hasan said: Bear witness, and he raised it to Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, who was the judge of the city at that time, told him the story. Abu Bakr said to Ibn Abi Al-Furat: What did you mean when you said to him, Ibn Baraka? He said: I called her by her name. Abu Bakr said: By this you meant to belittle her and her state of Islam, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Oh His mother, O mother of Ayman, God Almighty will not tell me if I tell you to die.” So he struck him with seventy lashes.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6914 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6915","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Arwa bint Kariz bin Rabi’ah bin Habib bin Abd Shams converted to Islam and migrated to Medina and died during the caliphate of Uthman, may God be pleased with him.” about him"
"6916","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And the names of the daughter of Abu Bakr, her mother was Qutaylah bint Abd al-Uzza bin As’ad bin Jabir bin Malik bin Hasal bin Amer bin Luay, and she was Abdullah’s sister. Ibn Abi Bakr, from his father and his mother. She converted to Islam in the past in Mecca and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She was married to Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam. So Abdullah, Urwa, Asim, Al-Muhajir, Khadija the eldest, Umm Al-Hasan, and Aisha bint Al-Zubayr bore him seven.”"
"6917","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Dawud bin Al-Muhabbir told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them, that she took up a dagger in the time of Sa’id bin Al-Aas. During the temptation, she placed it under her elbow, and it was said to her: What are you doing with this? She said: “If a thief comes in to me, I will destroy his stomach.” She was blind.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6917 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6918","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “Asma’ bint Abu Bakr died. A few nights after the killing of her son Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, and he was killed on Tuesday, seventeen nights before Jumada Al-Awwal of the year seventy-three”"
"6919","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “ Duba'ah bint Al-Zubayr bin Abdul Muttalib bin Hashim was married by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Al-Miqdad bin Amr bin Alopecia and she bore him Abdullah and Karima. Abdullah was killed on the Day of the Camel with Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and Ali passed by him killed. He said: “How miserable is the sister’s son.”"
"6920","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abd told us The heir, narrated to us by Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his grandmother Umm Al-Hakam, on the authority of her sister Daba’ah bint Al-Zubayr, “She gave meat to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he bitten some of it and then prayed without performing ablution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6920 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6921","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Umm Al-Hakam was the daughter of Al-Zubayr bin Abdul Muttalib bin Hashim. He married her to Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, and she bore him Muhammad and Abbas. And Abd al-Shams, Abd al-Muttalib, Umayyah, and Arwa al-Kubra.”"
"6922","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Nawfal, on the authority of Umm al-Hakam bint al-Zubayr, that she “handed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a shoulder of meat.” So he ate from it and then prayed but did not perform ablution.” Hammad bin Salamah, may God be pleased with him, misunderstood this name and said: Umm Hakim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6922 - Hammad bin Salamah narrated on the authority of Qatada on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah on the authority of her, but it was not authentic."
"6923","As Ibrahim bin Ismat Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ammar, Mawla Bani Hashim, on the authority of Umm Hakim, daughter of Abdul Muttalib, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate a bone in my presence, and Bilal came and gave him permission.” With prayer, he prayed but did not perform ablution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6923 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6924","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Umama bint Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib bin Hashim, and her mother was Salma bint Umays bin Ma`d bin Taim, the sister of Asma bint Umays. She lived after the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she narrated on his authority.”"
"6925","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Bakr bin Abdul Rahman told us, Issa bin Al-Mukhtar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who is the maternal brother of Umamah bint Hamzah. On the authority of his sister, Umamah bint Hamzah, that a servant of hers died leaving behind only one daughter. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that To his daughter Al-Nisf and to Hamza’s daughter Al-Nisf.”"
"6926","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Umm Kulthum bint Uqba bin Abi Mu’ayt. Her mother was Arwa bint Kuraiz. Umm Kulthum converted to Islam and pledged allegiance before the Hijra, and she was the first to A number of women emigrated after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6927","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “It is not known A Quraysh woman left her parents’ house as a Muslim, migrating to God and His Messenger, except for Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, who left Mecca alone. She accompanied a man from Khuza’ah until she came to the city during the truce of Hudaybiyyah, then her two brothers Al-Walid and Amara went out after her, and they arrived at the same time. Its arrival, and they said: O Muhammad, our condition and what you covenanted upon us, and in it was revealed: {When the believing women come to you as migrants} [Al-Mumtahana: 10] the verse, She did not have a husband in Mecca, so when she came to Medina, Zaid bin Haritha married her, and he was killed on her behalf, so Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam married her. Zainab bore him, and he divorced her. Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married her, and she bore him Ibrahim and Hamid, and he died on her behalf, so he married her. Amr bin Al-Aas, and she died on his behalf.”"
"6928","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Khaled’s mother’s name was Umma bint Khaled bin Sa’id bin Al-Aas bin Umayyah, and Khaled bin Sa’id had migrated to the land of Abyssinia with him. His wife, Humina bint Khalaf, bore him there Ummah bint Khalid, and he remained in the land of Abyssinia until they came with the people of the two ships. Ummah reached puberty and became sensible, and Al-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam married her, and she bore him Omar and Khalid, the sons of Al-Zubayr. She lived and lived and narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him”"
"6929","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid told us, Musa bin Uqba said: I heard Umm Khaled, daughter of Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, saying: “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking refuge from the torment of"
"6930","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, my grandfather told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, my brother Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Fatima bint Utba “that Abu Hudhayfah took her and her sister Hind to pledge allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he stipulated for them, Hind said: Do you know of any of these infirmities and infirmities among the women of your people? Then Abu Hudhayfah said to her: “Pledge your allegiance to him, for this is what he stipulates.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6930 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6931","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Hamnah"
"6932","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah bin Al-Faraj told us, Zayd bin Yahya bin Ubaid told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Hamnah, may God be pleased with her, that she heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, the world is sweet.” Green, for perhaps a person who is delving into this world for the wealth of God and His Messenger will have nothing on the Day of Resurrection but Hell.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6932 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6933","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: «"
"6934",""
"6935","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Judhamah bint Jandal bin Wahb Al-Asadiyya converted to Islam in Mecca in the past, pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and migrated to Medina. With its people"
"6936","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Amr bin Othman told us Al-Jahshi, on the authority of his father, said: “The Banu Ghanim bin Dudan forced their men and women into the migration to the point that their doors were closed, so he left. Among the women in the migration were Zainab, Umm Habibah, Hamnah the daughters of Jahsh, Aminah bint Ruqish, Umm Habibah bint Bananah, and Judhamah bint Jandal, and Judhama bint Jandal was under Unays bin Qatada bin Rabi’ah from Aws. He witnessed Badr and was killed on the day of Uhud as a martyr. Judama lived after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she narrated on his authority, and Aisha narrated on the authority of Judama.”"
"6937","Abu Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Sa’id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, and Malik Ibn Anas, they said: Abu Al-Aswad Muhammad Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Nawfal told us, Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, on the authority of Judama bint Wahb Al-Asadiya, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he intended to forbid the use of wild animals. He said: So I looked and saw that Persia and the Romans were committing violence, but that would not harm their children. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about isolation? He said: “It is the hidden valley.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed to narrate the hadith of Malik bin Anas on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad without “The increase belongs to Yahya bin Ayyub.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6937 - They took out the first part"
"6938","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ja`far bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Abi Thawr, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah bin Uthman, she said: “By God, it is as if I Look at the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that morning when he entered the Kaaba, then left it, and stood at its door, and in his hand was a dove from... “There were sticks that were in the Kaaba, so he broke them and took them out until, when he was at the door of the Kaaba, he threw them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6938 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6939","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, he said: “Fatima is the daughter of my father. Hubaysh bin Al-Muttalib bin Asad bin Abdul-Uzza married her to Abdullah bin Jahsh bin Rayab, and she bore him Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh lived and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and narrated on his authority."
"6940","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “And Busra bint Safwan Ibn Nawfal Ibn Asad Ibn Abd al-Uzza Ibn Qusayy, and she is the maternal sister of Uqba Ibn Abi Muayt, and he is the grandfather of Abd al-Malik Ibn Marwan, and the mother of Abdul-Malik Aisha bint Muawiyah bin Al-Mughirah bin Abi Al-Aas bin Umayyah, she lived in Busra after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and the news was narrated from him: “Ablution for one who touches the penis is well known.”"
"6941","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “And Barrah bint Abu Tijarah, the client of Banu Abd al-Dar. They say that we are from Yemen, from the Azd, allies of Banu Abd al-Dar, and he has many descendants among them, as does Abu Tajara. Ibn Abi Fakihah, whose name is Yasar, and it was narrated by Barrah on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6942","Muhammad bin Omar told me, Ali bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Amri told me, Mansour bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of his mother Safiyya, on the authority of Barrah bint Abi Tijarah said: “When God intended to honor him and initiate prophecy, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would Because of his need, he went further until he did not see a house, and he went to the paths and the bottoms of valleys, and he did not pass by a stone or a tree without it saying: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, and he used to look to his right and to his left and behind him and did not see anyone.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6942 - This hadith is not authentic"
"6943","Mukhlid bin Jaafar told me, Muhammad bin Jarir told me, Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told me, Al-Khalil bin Omar told me, he said: I heard Ibn Abu Nabih, narrating on the authority of his grandmother Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Habiba bint Abi Tajarah, who said: We had a characteristic in pre-Islamic times that said: So I looked out of a window between Safa and Marwah and supervised the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, he was running and saying to his companions: “Strive.” For God Almighty has ordained for you to strive.” She said: I saw him, in the intensity of the effort, turning the garment around his stomach until I saw the whites of his armpits and thighs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6943 - It is not authentic"
"6944","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ma’mal told us. Al-Makki, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Rahman bin Muhsin, Ata bin Abi Rabah narrated to me, on the authority of Habiba bint Abi Tajarat, who said: I entered upon Abu Hussein went to see women from the Quraysh while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked between Safa and Marwah as he ran, wrapping his garment around it. The intensity of striving as he said to his companions: “Strive, for God Almighty has decreed for you to strive.”"
"6945","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: “And the mother of Farwa, the daughter of my father Quhafa, sister of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, paternal aunt of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and her mother Hind bint Nufail bin Bujayr bin Ubaid bin Qusayy, whom he married Abu Bakr Al-Ash’ath ibn Qais, and she bore him Muhammad, Ishaq, Hubabah, and Qaribah.”"
"6946","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Ruqiqa Al-Tamimiyyah, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among the Muslim women, so we said to him: We have come to you, O Messenger of God, to pledge allegiance to you on the condition that we will not associate anything with God, nor will we steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill our children, nor come We fabricate slander between our hands and our feet, and we do not disobey you in what is right. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As much as you are able.” We said: God and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. So we said: Give us your pledge of allegiance, O Messenger. God. He said: “Go, I have pledged allegiance to you. My words to one woman are the same as my words to a hundred women.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not shake hands with us. Sunday"
"6947","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: “Umaima bint Raqiqa and Raqiqa, her mother and father were Abdullah bin Bijad bin Umair bin Al-Harith bin Harithah bin Saad bin Taym bin Murrah, and her mother Raqiqa bint Khuwaylid bin Asad bin Abd al-Uzza, sister of Khadija, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Umaima was celibate, so Habib married her Ibn Ka’b Ibn Utair Al-Thaqafi, and she bore him Al-Nahdiyyah, and Umaima Bint Ruqayqa lived after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and narrated on his authority.” So he told us of the authenticity of what Abu Abdullah Al-Waqidi mentioned.”"
"6948","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Issa bin Abdullah Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima, the aunt of Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I heard her saying: “We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Peace be upon him, so he enjoined upon us not to associate anything with God.” He said: “Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Ibn Ishaq on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir.”"
"6949","On the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Barira, may God be pleased with her, that she said: There are three things of the Sunnah regarding me: You give me meat as charity, so I gave it as a gift to Aisha, the hadith, “I owed nine uqiyahs, so Aisha said: If your masters wish, we can return it to them, in full remembrance of loyalty.”"
"6950","Mukhlid bin Jaafar told me, Muhammad bin Jarir told us, Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Al-Minhal told us Ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of those who mentioned him, on the authority of Layla, Aisha’s servant, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered to perform a judgment. I needed it, so I went in and did not see anything, but I smelled musk. So I said: O Messenger of God, I have not seen anything. He said: “Indeed, the earth has been commanded to be sufficient of us for the people of the prophets.” Al-Hakim, may God have mercy on him, said. God Almighty: “A group of female companions, may God be pleased with them, remained with me whom I did not mention out of fear of simplification and fear of lengthening the book. I translated the book of the Companions for virtues, and I did not find any virtues after the wives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for some of them, so I sought God Almighty has made the last book a book of the virtues of the Companions, may God be pleased with them all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6950 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6951","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Azhar, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “A man from Quraysh has as much strength as two men from Quraysh.” Al-Zuhri said: “It means gaining opinion.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6951 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6952","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: “O Omar, gather your people for me.” He gathered them together and then entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, have you gathered them? Will they come in to you, or will you go out to them? He said: “Rather, I will go out to them.” The Muhajireen and Ansar heard about that, and they said: A revelation has come among the Quraysh, and the observer and listener were present with what It was said to them, so he stood between them and said: “Are there anyone else among you?” They said: Yes, among us are our allies, the sons of our brothers, and our loyalists. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Our allies are among us and our loyalists are among us.” Then he said: “Have you not heard My friends from among you who are pious? If they are, then that is it. If not, then see and then see, for people will not come.” And you bring burdens, and they will be turned away from you.” Then he called out and raised his voice and said: “Indeed, the Quraysh are trustworthy people who desire misfortunes.” “God made him prostrate to his nostrils.” He said it three times. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6952 - True"
"6953","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Hammad told us Ibn Waqid Al-Saffar, Muhammad Ibn Dhakwan told us, maternal uncle of the son of Hammad Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a woman passed by, and a man from the people said: This is the daughter of Muhammad. Abu Sufyan said: The likeness of Muhammad among the Banu Hashim is like the basil in the middle of the figs. So the woman went off and told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out with anger evident on his face and said: “What is the matter with statements that inform me about people that God, Blessed and Most High, created The heavens, so He chose the highest and inhabited it whomsoever He wished from among His creation. Then He created creation and chose from among the creation the children of Adam and chose from among the children of Adam the Arabs. He chose from among the Arabs Mudar, and from among Mudar he chose Quraysh, and from among Quraysh he chose Banu Hashim, and he chose me from Banu Hashim, for I am from Banu Hashim of choice. To a choice, for whoever loves the Arabs will love them because of my love, and whoever hates the Arabs will love them because I hate them.” It was said in this chain of transmission about Muhammad bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar,"
"6954","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, and Muhammad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, they said: Abdullah bin Al-Fadl told us Bakr Al-Sahmi, Yazid bin Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Dhakwan, Abdullah bin Bakr said: I do not think that Muhammad is the only one who narrated it to me. On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, So he mentioned the hadith in its entirety, like it."
"6955","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ja’far Al-Muzaki told us, and in others, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad bin Hafs bin Omar bin Musa bin Abdullah bin Muammar Al-Taymi, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard my uncle Ubaid Allah bin Omar bin Musa, saying: Rabi’ah bin Abi Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr bin Othman bin Affan, he said: He told me My father: O my son, if you are appointed to do any of the people’s affairs, then honor the Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever insults the Quraysh is insulted by him.” God Almighty”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6955 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6956","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Muzaki told me, through passages from the origin of his book, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us. Al-Hashimi, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Saleh bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Sufyan bin Al-Ala bin Jariyah. Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yusuf bin Al-Hakam, Abu Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever seeks dishonor from Quraysh, God has insulted him.” This hadith was narrated by Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah. Ibn Usamah Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Saad, and it is from the deception of the hadith in what the elders narrated on the authority of the younger ones.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6956 - True"
"6957","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Qari, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi told us, they said: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Salih, and Yahya Ibn Abdullah Ibn Bukayr, Al-Layth Ibn Saad told us, Ibn Al-Hadi told me, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Saad, on the authority of Salih Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Yusuf Ibn Abi Aqeel, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever seeks humiliation from Quraysh, God Almighty has insulted him.” Yusuf bin Abi Aqeel is: Ibn Al-Hakam Without a doubt, the narration has been authenticated from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a son does not commit injustice against his father.”"
"6958","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqashi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Hamza bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the pulpit: “What is the matter with people who say that my kinship is of no use? Indeed, by God, my kinship is connected in This world and the hereafter. O people, I will leave you at the basin. When I come, some men stand up and say this: O Messenger of God, I am so-and-so, and he said This one: O Messenger of God, I am so-and-so, and this one said: O Messenger of God, I am so-and-so, so I say, “I knew you,” but you spoke after me and returned. Al-Qahqari “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6958 - True"
"6959","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, in what I read to him from the original of his book, Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Al-Walid Al-Karabisi reported, In Baghdad, Ishaq bin Saeed bin Al-Arqun Al-Dimashqi told us, Khalid bin Da’laj told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas Radi God said about them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The security of the people of the earth from discord is loyalty to the Quraysh, and the Quraysh are the people of God.” If an Arab tribe disobeys it, it becomes the party of Satan.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6959 - It is weak and its chain of transmission is weak"
"6960","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Muhammad ibn Tarif told us. Al-Bajli, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sabrah Al-Nakhi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abd Al-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, said: We used to meet a group of Quraysh while they were talking, and they would stop talking, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “What is the matter with people who talk? When they see a man from my family, they stop their conversation, and God does not enter the heart of a man.” “Faith is such that it loves them for God Almighty and for my kinship.” This hadith is known from the hadith of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Abbas, so if this evidence comes from the hadith of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-A’mash, we will rule it to be authentic. As for the hadith of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad.”"
"6961","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger By God, when the Quraysh faced each other, they met each other with joy, and when they met us, they met us with faces we did not know. He said: Then he became extremely angry. Then he said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of God and for His Messenger.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6961 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6962","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, in Hamdan, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, al-Fayd bin al-Fadl al-Bajli told us, Mas’ar bin Kadam, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The imams of Quraysh, the righteous, are the princes of the righteous, and the unrighteous are the princes of the wicked, and each has a right, so they were given Every person has his right, and if I command over you an Abyssinian slave who has been mutilated, then listen to him and obey him as long as none of you has a choice between his conversion to Islam and the beheading of him. If he has a choice between his conversion to Islam and beheading, let him put his neck forward, for he has neither this world nor the hereafter after his conversion to Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6962 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6963","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that Al-Tufayl bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do you have a fort? And the fortress of Dos, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a shelter for the Ansar and said: Then Tufayl emigrated and a man from his people emigrated with him. Then the man became ill - he said: he became bored or something similar - so he came to Qarn, took a pair of scissors, cut off his sides, and he died. Al-Tufayl saw him in a dream. He said: What did God do to you? He said: He forgave me for my migration to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: What is the matter with your hands? He said: I was told: We will never fix what you have done wrong with yourself. He said: Tufayl related it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Oh God And his hands, so forgive.” He raised his hands. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6963 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6964","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {You are the best nation raised for mankind} [Al Imran: 110] He said: “They are the ones who migrated with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6964 - True"
"6965","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad, Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb told me, my uncle told me, he told me Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Kathir bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The immigrants will have pulpits of gold on which they will sit on the Day of Resurrection. They will be safe from terror.” He said: Then Abu Sa’id says: “By God, if I loved anyone with it, I would love my people with it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6965 - Ahmed bin Abdul Rahman Wah"
"6966","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamami told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, Abu Zumail told us, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah wrote to the people of Mecca, so God Almighty informed his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent Ali and Al-Zubayr to follow the letter, and they found a woman riding a camel. So they extracted it from one of its horns, and brought it to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was read to him. He sent it to Hatib, and he said: “O Hatib, You wrote this book? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: What made you do that? He said: O Messenger of God, by God I am sincere to God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I was a stranger among the people of Mecca and my family was among them. They appeared to me, so I feared for them, so I wrote a letter that would not harm God and His Messenger in the least, and perhaps it would be of benefit to my family. Omar said: So I chose My sword and I said: O Messenger of God, free me from him, for he has disbelieved, so I beheaded him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ibn Al-Khattab, How do you know, perhaps God has looked at the people of this group of the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it like this, rather they agreed on the hadith of Abdullah bin Abi Rafi’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of Ali The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me, Abu Marthad, and Al-Zubayr to Rawdat Khakh without this word.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6966 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6967","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi in Hamadan told me, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told me, Adam ibn Abi Iyas told me, Muhammad ibn Ismail told me. Ibn Abi Fudaik Al-Madani, Abdul-Malik Ibn Zayd told us, on the authority of Mus’ab Ibn Mus’ab, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: Talha bin Ubaid Allah spoke to Amer bin Fuhayra about something, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Wait, O Talha, for he witnessed Badr as you witnessed, and the best of you is the best to his loyal ones.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6967 - True"
"6968","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told me, about Asim bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God Almighty looked at the people of Badr. He said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it with this wording, with the certainty that God looked at them. So He forgave them, but they brought it out based on suspicion, and how do you know? Perhaps God Almighty looked at the people of Badr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6968 - True"
"6969","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the imam of the prophets, their preacher, and the one who intercedes for them, without any pride.”
 Then I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If it had not been for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar, even if the Ansar had taken a valley or People, I would have been with the Ansar.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6969 - True"
"6970","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father Ka’b bin Malik, that he said: The last sermon we gave was delivered by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “O community of the Emigrants, you have begun to increase, and the Ansar have finished, and they are my defect that I shelter.” To it, so honor their doers of good and overlook their transgressors.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6970 - True"
"6971","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Sulaiman bin Al-Ghaseel, told by Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, left during his illness. He tied a rag around his head and said: “The people are increasing and the supporters are few and far, until they become to the people like salt is to the food. So who is my guardian? “If any of you does any deed, let it accept it from their doers of good, and ignore their wrongdoers.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6971 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"6972","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb, Abu Sakhr told you, that Yahya ibn al-Nadr al-Ansari told him that he heard Abu Qatada say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the pulpit: To the Ansar: “Indeed, the people are my covering, and the Ansar are my banner. And if the people were to take a valley and the Ansar were to take a path, I would certainly follow a path.” The Ansar, so whoever is in charge of the Ansar, let him do good to those who do good to them and overlook those who do wrong to them, and whoever frightens them has frightened those who are between them. These two - and he pointed to himself - had it not been for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6972 - True"
"6973","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, And Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, Muhammad bin Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Talha, that he entered upon The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the pain in which he died, and he said: “Convey your greetings to your people, for I have never known anyone to be chaste and patient.” Authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6973 - True"
"6974","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Asim bin Suwayd told us, Yahya told me Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, who said: Usayd Ibn Hudayr Al-Ashhli came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was dividing food, so he mentioned He has a family of the Ansar from Banu Zafar, among whom there is a need. He said: And most of the people of that house are women. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “You have left us, O Usayd, until what is in our hands is gone. So if you hear of something that has come to us, mention to me the people of that house.” He said: After that, food came to him from Khaybar, barley and dates. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided it among the people, and he divided it among the Ansar and gave generously. He took an oath among the people of that household and was generous, he said: Then Usayd bin Hudair said to him: Thank you, may God reward you, that is, the Prophet of God on our behalf, with the best reward - or He said: Good - so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And you, O people of Ansar, may God reward you with the best reward - and he said good - for you are what I know someone to be chaste and patient, and after me you will see an impact in the matter and the oath, so be patient until you meet me at the basin.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6974 - True"
"6975","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Abdul-Warith bin Abdul-Samad told me, my father told me, Abdullah bin Abu Yazid, on the authority of Musa ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Ansar gathered stones against them, so they came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “You will not ask me for anything today unless you will be given it.” When they heard what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, they said: Pray to God for forgiveness for us. He said: “O God, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar.” “And to the sons of the sons of the Ansar.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6975 - True"
"6976","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, received young men from the Ansar, female slaves and male servants, and he said: “By God, I “I love you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6976 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6977","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Al-Hayyan prided themselves among the Ansar, the Aws and the Khazraj, and the Aws said: ‘From us. Whose death shook the throne of the Most Gracious, Saad bin Muadh, and among us who was protected by the back of Asim bin Thabit bin Al-Aflah, and among us who was washed by The angels are Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib, and among us is one whose testimony was approved by the testimony of two men, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and the Khazrajis said: among us. Four compiled the Qur’an, and no one compiled it except them: Ubayy bin Ka’b, Muadh bin Jabal, Zayd bin Thabit, and Abu Zayd. “This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6977 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6978","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Sufyan told me Al-Thawri, on the authority of Suleiman Al-A’mash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khutami, Abdul-Rahman bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Abd May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The immigrants and the Ansar are one another’s guardians in this world.” And the Hereafter, and the freedmen from Quraysh and the unmarried people from Thaqif, some of them are guardians of one another in this world and the hereafter.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6978 - True"
"6979","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh al-Azdi, on the authority of Amr ibn Abbasa al-Sulami, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, may God bless him and grant him peace, was showing horses, and with him was Uyaynah bin Badr al-Fazari. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “I know horses better than you.” . Uyaynah said: I know the men better than you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is the best of men?” He said: Men of Najd who carry their swords on their shoulders and their spears on the hilts of their horses. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You lied. Rather, the best of men are the men of Yemen, and faith is Yemen to the point of leprosy and leprosy, and eating donkeys is better than eating them, and Hadhramaut is better than Banu Al-Harith, by God, I do not care if all of Al-Harith perish. God has cursed the four kings: Jammad, Makhos, Ibadha, and their sister. Then he said: “My Lord commanded me to curse the Quraysh twice, so I cursed them, and He commanded me to pray over them, so I prayed over them twice.” Then he said: “God cursed Tamim bin Murrah five times, and Bakr bin Wael seven times, and God cursed two of the tribes of Banu Tamim, Muqais and Maladis.” Then he said: “A disobedient person who disobeyed God and His Messenger, Abdul Qais, Ja`dah, and Ismat.” Then he said: “Aslam, Ghafar, and Muzainah, and their allies from Juhayna are better.” From Banu Asad, Tamim, and Ghatafan, and they will be considered lowly in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said: “The two worst tribes among the Arabs are Najran and Banu Taghlib. “And most of the tribes in Paradise will be mixed.” This is a strange hadith with a strange text, with a sound chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6979 - Sahih Gharib"
"6980","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Malik informed us Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I accept Islam. Ghaffar, Ashja’, Muzainah, Juhaynah, and whoever is from Banu Ka’b, a loyalist to the exclusion of the people. Allah and His Messenger are their friend.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6980 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"6981","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Rizmah told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Khuthaym bin Arak, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Forgiving, may God forgive her. May God bless her and grant her peace. As for me, I did not say it, but God said it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this addition. To add to this, there is another witness with a valid chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6981 - True"
"6982","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Humaidi told us, Ali told us Ibn Yazid Ibn Abi Hakim Al-Aslami, Iyas Ibn Salamah Ibn Al-Akwa’ told me, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to stand in prayer and pray against some Arab tribes, saying: “May God curse Ra’al, Dhakwan, and the disobedient woman who disobeyed God and His Messenger. And Bani Lahyan.” And he says: “Forgiving, may God forgive her, and may God protect her. It was not me who said it, but God Almighty said it.” Then he says “Allahu Akbar.” After he supplicates against whomever he supplicates
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6982 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6983","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubair Al-Humaidi told us, Ali bin Yazid told us Ibn Abi Hakim, on the authority of his father, and others, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Al-Akwa’, that Aamir Ibn Al-Tufayl did not enter Medina except with the protection of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “O Amer, become a Muslim.” He said: Yes, as long as I have The lint is yours. He said: “This will not be safe.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Amer, go so that we can look into your situation until tomorrow.” So he sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to the Ansar and said: “What do you see? Indeed, I have called this man, but he refused to embrace Islam unless he has the robe, and I have the right to do so.” They said: “Whatever God wills.” Then you wish, O Messenger of God. They never took one iqal from us but we took two from them, for God and His Messenger know best. So Amer returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: “Peace be upon you, O Aamer.” He said: Nothing else, so he refused except to have the rain, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had the mud, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, refused. May God bless him and grant him peace. Amer said: By God, I will fill it for you with horses and men. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God refuse that to you and the people of the Aws and Khazraj tribe.” Then Amer left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, protect him from me.” So God slaughtered him before his family came, and Amer said when the slaughter took hold of him: Oh, my family. Amir, this is the gland like the gland of a virgin, so he perished when it took him away from his family.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6983 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6984","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, Qurra bin Khalid told us, Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever climbs the ditch of Al-Marar For it will be erased from him what was removed from the Children of Israel.” The horses of the Khazraj tribe were the first to ascend it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of you will be forgiven, except the one with the red camel.” He said: And when he was a Bedouin seeking a lost one, we said to him: Come, he will ask forgiveness for you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Because I find what I seek is more beloved to me than for your companion to ask forgiveness for me.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition that Muslim
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6984 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"6985","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What is harmful is a woman who revealed “Between two Ansar slave girls, or she stayed between her parents.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6985 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6986","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told me, Mansour told us, Maslamah bin Alqamah Al-Mazni told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Three things I heard from Banu Tamim from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I will hate Tamim forever after them. Aisha had a vow made by the descendants of Ishmael, and some of the Banu al-Anbar were taken captive, so he said to Aisha: It would please you to fulfill your vow. So he freed a freed man from among them and made them among the descendants of Ishmael. He brought one of the blessings of charity to Banu Saad. When he saw it, he was amazed and said: This is it. Yes, my people, so he made them his people, and said: They are the hardest fighting people in the epics. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6986 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6987","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed me, he informed me Muammar, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the words of God Almighty: {You are the best of nations brought forth to mankind} [Al Imran: 110] He said: “You will complete seventy nations, of which you are the best and most honorable in the eyes of God Almighty.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri followed this, in a narration on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, and brought an addition. In the text
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6987 - True"
"6988","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi told us, Sa`id ibn Masoud told us, and Abu Abdullah al-Saffar informed us, Muhammad ibn Salamah, they said: Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri reported, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “You will give the reward of seventy nations. You are the most honorable of them before God Almighty and the best of them.”"
"6989","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, saying: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Maysara Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: “You are the best of people raised for mankind” [Al Imran: 110] “You will drag them with chains and bring them into Islam.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6989 - True"
"6990","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamza, speaking on the authority of Zayd Ibn Arqam, he said: The Ansar said: O Messenger of God, every prophet has followers “And indeed, we have followed you, so pray to God to make our followers among us.” So he prayed for them to make their followers among them. He said: So I extended that to Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, and he said: “Zayd bin Arqam claimed that.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6990 - True"
"6991","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Abu Isma Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told us, Amr bin Abi Amr told us, Suhail bin Abi Salih told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, people from my nation will come after me, one of whom would like to buy my vision with his family and money.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. The correct interpreter hadith in this regard is his saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The best of people is my generation, then “Those who follow them have agreed to bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6991 - True"
"6992","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf bin Sufyan Al-Tai told us, in Homs, Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Al-Awza’i, Usayd bin Abdul-Rahman told us, Saleh bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Abu Jumah, he said: We had lunch with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah was with us. He said: So we said: O Messenger of God, is anyone better than us? We accepted Islam with you and fought with you? He said: “Yes, there will be people after you who will believe in me but have not seen me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6992 - True"
"6993","Abu Ubayd Allah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zahid told us, Ahmad ibn Mahdi ibn Rustum told us, Abu Amir al-Aqdi told us, Muhammad ibn Abu Humaid, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you know which people of faith have the best faith?” They said, O Messenger of God, the angels? He said: “They are like that, and that is right for them, and what prevents them, and God has sent them down to the position in which He sent them down, rather, others.” They said: Oh Messenger of God, then the prophets whom God Almighty honored with prophecy and message? He said: “They are like that, and it is their right to do that, and what prevents them is that God has sent them down to the status in which He sent them down, rather than others.” He said: We said: Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “People will come after me in the loins of men, and they will believe in me and have not seen me, and they will find the hanging paper, and they will work with what is in it. “The best of the people of faith in faith.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6993 - Rather, Muhammad bin Abi Hamid is weak"
"6994","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim told us, Yahya bin Salih Al-Wahazi told us, Jami’ bin Thawb, Abdullah bin Busr, the companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Blessed is he who sees me, and blessed is he who sees me.” He who has seen me has seen it, and for he who has seen it has seen he who has seen me and believed in me.” This hadith was narrated with close chains of narration on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him. Of the chains of transmission we have mentioned, and the closest of these narrations to authenticity are what we have mentioned.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6994 - Jamil bin Thawb is weak"
"6995","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid, Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “O Salman, do not hate me or abandon your religion. I said: O Messenger of God, how can I hate you when God Almighty has guided me? He said: “You hate the Arabs, so they hate me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6995 - Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan spoke about it"
"6996","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad al-Mahrajani told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muawiya told us, Abu Sufyan Ziyad bin Sahl al-Harithi told us, Amara bin Mihran Al-Ma'awali told us, Amr bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When God created creation, He chose the Arabs, then He chose from the Arabs Quraysh, then He chose from Quraysh Banu Hashim, then He chose me from Banu Hashim, for I am better than the best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6996 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"6997","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Yazid bin Awanah told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Dhakwan, the maternal uncle of the son of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him Likewise, “The narration has been authentic on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, so if it is on the authority of Salem then it is strange and authentic, and if it is on the authority of Ibn Umar then Amr heard it.” Ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6997 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"6998","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Abu Muslim told Ibrahim bin Abdullah, that Maqil bin Malik told them, he said: Thana Al-Haytham Bin Hammad, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loving the Arabs is faith, and hating them is hypocrisy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6998 - Al-Haytham bin Hammad is abandoned"
"6999","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani and Abu Sa`id al-Thaqafi told us, about others who said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulayman al-Hadrami told us, Al-Alaa bin Amr al-Hanafi, Yahya bin Yazid al-Ash’ari told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Love the Arabs for three reasons: Because I am an Arab, the Qur’an is Arabic, and the speech of the people of Paradise is Arabic.” Muhammad bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj"
"7000","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria told us, Ismail bin Amr told us, Ismail bin Amr told us Muhammad bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Preserve me in the Arabic language for three qualities, because I am an Arab, the Qur’an is Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is Arabic.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “The hadith of Yahya bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, is an authentic hadith. The Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, is an Arabic language that neglects God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, for its evidence warns of a threat. From him, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to those who choose Persian over Arabic in speech and writing, and we have narrated hadiths in that regard, including:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7000 - I think the hadith is fabricated"
"7001","Abu Amr Saeed bin Al-Qasim bin Al-Alaa Al-Mutawa’i did not tell me, Ahmad bin Al-Layth bin Al-Khalil told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. Al-Jariri, in Balkh, Amr bin Harun told us, Usama bin Zaid Al-Laythi told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is better than you at speaking Arabic should not speak Persian, for he will inherit hypocrisy.” Among them are
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7001 - Amr bin Harun was lied to by Ibn Ma’in and abandoned by the group."
"7002","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Bayruti did not tell us, Abu Farwa told us, my father told me, Talha bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He spoke Persian, which increased his wickedness and diminished his chivalry.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7002 - It is not authentic and its chain of transmission is completely weak"
